/* GENERATED by lib/ — do not hand-edit; edit exams/<id>/research/q*.json then run lib/merge.py */
window.EXAM_DATA=window.EXAM_DATA||{};window.EXAM_DATA["scs-c03"]=[{"id":1,"question_en":"A security engineer needs to implement a solution to create and control the keys that a company uses for cryptographic operations. The security engineer must create symmetric keys in which the key material is generated and used within a custom key store that is backed by an AWS CloudHSM cluster. The security engineer will use symmetric and asymmetric data key pairs for local use within applications. The security engineer also must audit the use of the keys. How can the security engineer meet these requirements?","question_zh":"安全工程师需要实施一项解决方案，用于创建和管理公司用于加密操作的密钥。该安全工程师必须在由 AWS CloudHSM 集群支持 的自定义密钥存储中生成并使用对称密钥的密钥材料。安全工程师将使用对称和非对称数据密钥对，在应用程序内部进行本地使 用。此外，安全工程师还必须对密钥的使用情况进行审计。 安全工程师如何满足这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"To create the keys, use AWS Key Management Service (AWS KMS) and the custom key stores with the CloudHSM cluster. For auditing, use Amazon Athena.","B":"To create the keys, use Amazon S3 and the custom key stores with the CloudHSM cluster. For auditing, use AWS CloudTrail.","C":"To create the keys, use AWS Key Management Service (AWS KMS) and the custom key stores with the CloudHSM cluster. For auditing, use Amazon GuardDuty.","D":"To create the keys, use AWS Key Management Service (AWS KMS) and the custom key stores with the CloudHSM cluster. For auditing, use AWS CloudTrail."},"options_zh":{"A":"创建密钥时，使用 AWS 密钥管理服务（AWS KMS）以及与 CloudHSM 集群配合的自定义密钥存储。用于审计时，使用 Amazon Athena。","B":"创建密钥时，使用 Amazon S3 和与 CloudHSM 集群配合的自定义密钥存储。用于审计时，使用 AWS CloudTrail。","C":"创建密钥时，使用 AWS 密钥管理服务（AWS KMS）以及与 CloudHSM 集群配合使用的自定义密钥存储。用于审计时，使用 Amazon GuardDuty。","D":"创建密钥时，请使用 AWS 密钥管理服务（AWS KMS）以及与 CloudHSM 集群配合使用的自定义密钥存储。用于审计时，请 使用 AWS CloudTrail。"},"answer":["D"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Security/IAM","Storage","Monitoring/Ops","Analytics"],"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選","research":{"verdict":["D"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"AWS KMS is the service for creating and controlling cryptographic keys, and its custom key store feature (an AWS CloudHSM key store) lets you create symmetric encryption KMS keys whose non-extractable key material is generated and stored in a CloudHSM cluster that you own and manage, with cryptographic operations performed inside those HSMs. KMS also provides the GenerateDataKey and GenerateDataKeyPair operations to issue symmetric data keys and asymmetric data key pairs for local cryptographic use within applications (note: GenerateDataKeyPair specifically requires a symmetric KMS key in the default key store, but this fine print does not change which option is viable, since no option pairs KMS with a non-CloudHSM key store). For auditing, AWS KMS is natively integrated with AWS CloudTrail, which records every KMS API call — key management operations like CreateKey as well as cryptographic operations such as Encrypt, Decrypt, and GenerateDataKey — providing a complete audit trail of key use. Therefore option D (KMS + CloudHSM-backed custom key store + CloudTrail) is the only option that satisfies key creation/control, CloudHSM-backed key material, and auditing. Athena only queries logs that something else (CloudTrail) must first capture, GuardDuty is a threat-detection service rather than an API audit log, and Amazon S3 cannot create cryptographic keys.","explanation_zh":"AWS KMS 是用來建立與控管加密金鑰的服務，其 custom key store（AWS CloudHSM key store）功能可讓你建立對稱加密 KMS key，其不可匯出的金鑰材料由你自有並管理的 CloudHSM cluster 產生與存放，加密運算也在該 cluster 的 HSM 內執行。KMS 亦提供 GenerateDataKey 與 GenerateDataKeyPair 操作，可發出對稱 data key 及非對稱 data key pair 供應用程式在本地端使用（註：GenerateDataKeyPair 依 API 文件須使用預設 key store 中的對稱 KMS key，但此細節不影響哪個選項可行，因為沒有任何選項是「KMS 搭配非 CloudHSM key store」）。稽核方面，AWS KMS 原生整合 AWS CloudTrail，會記錄所有 KMS API 呼叫——包含 CreateKey 等金鑰管理操作，以及 Encrypt、Decrypt、GenerateDataKey 等加密操作——提供完整的金鑰使用稽核軌跡。因此選項 D（KMS + CloudHSM custom key store + CloudTrail）是唯一同時滿足建立/控管金鑰、CloudHSM 支援的金鑰材料與稽核三項需求的選項。Athena 只能查詢已由 CloudTrail 等機制先行擷取的日誌，GuardDuty 是威脅偵測服務而非 API 稽核日誌，Amazon S3 則根本無法建立加密金鑰。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"Amazon Athena is a query engine for data already stored in S3; it does not itself capture or record KMS key-usage events. Without CloudTrail there is nothing for Athena to query, so it cannot satisfy the auditing requirement on its own.","why_zh":"Amazon Athena 只是查詢 S3 中既有資料的查詢引擎，本身不會擷取或記錄 KMS 金鑰使用事件。若沒有 CloudTrail，Athena 根本無資料可查，無法單獨滿足稽核需求。"},{"letter":"B","why_en":"Amazon S3 is object storage and cannot create or manage cryptographic keys; key creation with a CloudHSM-backed custom key store is an AWS KMS capability, not an S3 capability.","why_zh":"Amazon S3 是物件儲存服務，無法建立或管理加密金鑰；搭配 CloudHSM custom key store 建立金鑰是 AWS KMS 的功能，並非 S3 的功能。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"Amazon GuardDuty is a threat-detection service that analyzes sources like CloudTrail, VPC Flow Logs, and DNS logs to produce findings; it does not provide an audit log of every KMS key-usage API call, which is what CloudTrail delivers.","why_zh":"Amazon GuardDuty 是威脅偵測服務，分析 CloudTrail、VPC Flow Logs、DNS logs 等來源以產生 findings；它不會提供每次 KMS 金鑰使用 API 呼叫的稽核日誌，該功能由 CloudTrail 提供。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/kms/latest/developerguide/key-store-overview.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/kms/latest/developerguide/keystore-cloudhsm.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/kms/latest/developerguide/logging-using-cloudtrail.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/kms/latest/developerguide/create-cmk-keystore.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/kms/latest/APIReference/API_GenerateDataKeyPair.html"]}},{"id":2,"question_en":"A company is using AWS Organizations with nested OUs to manage AWS accounts. The company has a custom compliance monitoring service for the accounts. The monitoring service runs as an AWS Lambda function and is invoked by Amazon EventBridge Scheduler. The company needs to deploy the monitoring service in all existing and future accounts in the organization. The company must avoid using the organization ' s management account when the management account is not required. Which solution will meet these requirements?","question_zh":"一家公司正在使用带有嵌套组织单元（OUs）的 AWS Organizations 来管理 AWS 账户。该公司为 这些账户提供了一项自定义的合规性监控服务，该监控服务以 AWS Lambda 函数的形式运行， 并由 Amazon EventBridge 调度器触发。 公司需要在组织内所有现有和未来的账户中部署监控服务。当不需要时，公司必须避免使用组织的管 理账户。 哪种解决方案能满足这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Create a CloudFormation stack set in the organization ' s management account and manually add new accounts.","B":"Configure a delegated administrator account for AWS CloudFormation. Create a CloudFormation StackSet in the delegated administrator account targeting the organization root with automatic deployment enabled.","C":"Use Systems Manager delegated administration and Automation to deploy the Lambda function and schedule.","D":"Create a Systems Manager Automation runbook in the management account and share it to accounts."},"options_zh":{"A":"在组织的管理账户中创建一个 CloudFormation 堆栈集，并手动添加新账户。","B":"为 AWS CloudFormation 配置一个委托管理员账户。在该委托管理员账户中创建一个目标 为组织根目录的 CloudFormation StackSet，并启用自动部署功能。","C":"使用 Systems Manager 的委派管理与自动化功能来部署 Lambda 函数并设置计划任务。","D":"在管理账户中创建 Systems Manager 自动化运行手册，并将其共享给其他账户。"},"answer":["B"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Organizations/Governance","Compute","Serverless/Integration","Monitoring/Ops"],"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選","research":{"verdict":["B"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"The requirements are: (1) deploy the Lambda function plus its EventBridge Scheduler schedule to ALL existing AND future accounts in an organization that uses nested OUs, and (2) avoid using the management account when it is not strictly required. CloudFormation StackSets with service-managed permissions is the AWS-native mechanism built exactly for this: a StackSet can target the organization root (which automatically includes all nested child OUs and their accounts), and enabling automatic deployment makes CloudFormation deploy new stack instances the moment a new account joins the targeted organization/OU — satisfying the 'future accounts' requirement with zero manual steps. On the management-account constraint, AWS documentation is explicit: 'In addition to your organization's management account, member accounts with delegated administrator permissions can create and manage StackSets with service-managed permissions for the organization,' and 'For StackSets with service-managed permissions, the administrator account is either the organization's management account or a delegated administrator account. You can manage a StackSet by signing in to the AWS administrator account that created the StackSet.' This means once a delegated administrator is registered, all day-to-day StackSet creation, updates, and monitoring happen from that delegated account — the management account is touched only once, to activate trusted access with Organizations and to register the delegated administrator (a step docs confirm only the management account can perform). That one-time, unavoidable step is precisely the 'when required' exception the question allows. Option A also uses CloudFormation StackSets but runs everything from the management account and requires manually adding each new account (no automatic-deployment/future-account coverage), directly violating both stated constraints. Option C describes Systems Manager Automation with delegated administration, which is a real feature (multi-account/multi-Region Automation execution against Organizations targets) but it is a task-execution/runbook-orchestration mechanism, not a declarative, continuously-reconciled infrastructure-provisioning mechanism with native 'deploy to organization root, auto-onboard new accounts' semantics — achieving persistent Lambda + EventBridge Scheduler deployment with automatic new-account coverage would require substantial custom orchestration on top of it, so it is not the best fit. Option D creates and shares the runbook from the management account (violating the avoid-management-account requirement) and sharing alone deploys nothing — each account still needs a separate mechanism to execute it, with no automatic coverage of future accounts. Therefore B is confirmed as the best answer.","explanation_zh":"題目要求：(1) 將 Lambda 函數及其 EventBridge Scheduler 排程部署到含巢狀 OU 的組織內所有現有與未來帳戶；(2) 非必要時避免使用 management account。CloudFormation StackSets 的 service-managed permissions 模式正是為此設計：StackSet 可鎖定 organization root 為目標（會自動涵蓋所有巢狀子 OU 及其帳戶），啟用 automatic deployment 後，只要有新帳戶加入被鎖定的組織／OU，CloudFormation 就會自動部署新的 stack instance——完全不需手動操作即可滿足「未來帳戶」的要求。關於 management account 的限制，AWS 官方文件明確指出：「除了組織的 management account 外，具備 delegated administrator 權限的成員帳戶也能為組織建立並管理 service-managed permissions 的 StackSets」，且「對於 service-managed permissions 的 StackSets，administrator account 可以是組織的 management account，也可以是 delegated administrator account；你可以透過登入建立該 StackSet 的 AWS administrator account 來管理它」。這代表一旦註冊了 delegated administrator，日常的 StackSet 建立、更新、監控都能在該委派帳戶完成——management account 只需被觸碰一次，用於啟用與 Organizations 的 trusted access，以及註冊 delegated administrator（文件確認此步驟僅 management account 能執行）。這個一次性且無法避免的步驟，正符合題目「非必要時避免」的例外情況。選項 A 雖然也用 CloudFormation StackSets，但一切都在 management account 執行，且需手動逐一加入新帳戶（無自動部署／未來帳戶涵蓋能力），直接違反兩項限制。選項 C 描述的 Systems Manager Automation 搭配 delegated administration 確實存在（可對 Organizations 目標執行跨帳戶／跨區域的 Automation），但它本質是任務執行／runbook 編排機制，而非具備「鎖定 organization root、新帳戶自動加入」語意的宣告式、持續調和的基礎設施佈建機制；要用它達成 Lambda 與 EventBridge Scheduler 的持續部署並自動涵蓋新帳戶，需要大量額外的自訂編排，並非最佳解。選項 D 在 management account 建立並分享 runbook（違反避免使用 management account 的要求），且單純分享 runbook 本身不會部署任何資源，各帳戶仍需另外的機制執行它，也無法自動涵蓋未來帳戶。因此確認 B 為最佳答案。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"Operates entirely from the management account (which the company must avoid when not required) and relies on manually adding new accounts to the StackSet, so future accounts are not covered automatically — service-managed permissions with a delegated administrator plus automatic deployment exist precisely to eliminate both of these problems.","why_zh":"完全在 management account 操作（題目要求非必要時避免），且需手動將新帳戶加入 StackSet，無法自動涵蓋未來帳戶——service-managed permissions 搭配 delegated administrator 與 automatic deployment 正是為了消除這兩個問題。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"Systems Manager Automation (even with delegated administration for multi-account/multi-Region targets) executes operational runbooks on demand; it is not a declarative provisioning mechanism with organization-root targeting and native automatic deployment to newly joined accounts, so keeping the Lambda + EventBridge Scheduler stack deployed in every existing and future account would require substantial custom orchestration on top of it.","why_zh":"Systems Manager Automation（即使搭配 delegated administration 對多帳戶／多區域目標執行）是隨需執行維運 runbook 的機制，並不具備鎖定 organization root、對新加入帳戶原生自動部署的宣告式佈建能力；要讓 Lambda 與 EventBridge Scheduler 持續部署到所有現有與未來帳戶，需在其上額外建置大量自訂編排。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"Creating and sharing a runbook from the management account violates the requirement to avoid the management account when not required, and sharing a runbook does not by itself deploy anything — each account would still need a separate trigger/mechanism to execute it, with no automatic coverage of future accounts.","why_zh":"在 management account 建立並分享 runbook，違反非必要時避免使用 management account 的要求；且分享 runbook 本身並不會部署任何資源，各帳戶仍需另外的觸發機制去執行它，也無法自動涵蓋未來帳戶。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AWSCloudFormation/latest/UserGuide/stacksets-orgs-delegated-admin.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AWSCloudFormation/latest/UserGuide/stacksets-orgs-associate-stackset-with-org.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AWSCloudFormation/latest/UserGuide/stacksets-concepts.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AWSCloudFormation/latest/UserGuide/stacksets-orgs-manage-auto-deployment.html"]}},{"id":3,"question_en":"A company has AWS accounts in an organization in AWS Organizations. The organization includes a dedicated security account. All AWS account activity across all member accounts must be logged and reported to the dedicated security account. The company must retain all the activity logs in a secure storage location within the dedicated security account for2 years.No changes or deletions of the logs are allowed. Which combination of steps will meet these requirements with theLEAST operational overhead? (Select TWO.)","question_zh":"一家公司在 AWS Organizations 中拥有一个组织内的 AWS 账户。该组织包含一个专用的安全账户。 所有成员账户的AWS账户活动必须被记录并上报至专用的安全账户。公司必须在专用安全账户内的安全存储位置保留所 有活动日志两年，且不得对日志进行任何修改或删除。 哪两种步骤组合能够以最少的操作开销满足这些要求？（选择两项。）","options_en":{"A":"In the dedicated security account, create an Amazon S3 bucket. Configure S3 Object Lock incompliance modewith a retention period of 2 years. Set the bucket policy to allow the organization’ smanagement accountto write to the S3 bucket.","B":"In the dedicated security account, create an Amazon S3 bucket. Configure S3 Object Lock incompliance modewith a retention period of 2 years. Set the bucket policy to allow the organization’ smember accountsto write to the S3 bucket.","C":"In the dedicated security account, create an Amazon S3 bucket with an S3 Lifecycle configuration that expires objects after 2 years. Allow member accounts to write to the bucket.","D":"Create anAWS CloudTrail organization trail. Configure logs to be delivered to the Amazon S3 bucket in the dedicated security account.","E":"Turn on AWS CloudTrail in each account and forward logs to the dedicated security account by using AWS Lambda and Amazon Data Firehose."},"options_zh":{"A":"在专用的安全账户中创建一个 Amazon S3 存储桶。配置 S3 对象锁定为合规模式，保留期为 2 年。设置存储桶策 略，允许组织的管理账户向该 S3 存储桶写入数据。","B":"在专用的安全账户中创建一个 Amazon S3 存储桶。配置 S3 对象锁定为合规模式，并设置保留期为 2 年。将存储桶 策略设置为允许组织内的成员账户向该 S3 存储桶写入数据。","C":"在专用的安全账户中创建一个 Amazon S3 存储桶，并配置 S3 生命周期策略，使对象在 2 年后过期。允许成员账户 向该存储桶写入数据。","D":"创建一个 AWS CloudTrail 组织级跟踪，将日志配置为发送至专用安全账户中的 Amazon S3 存储桶。","E":"在每个账户中启用 AWS CloudTrail，并使用 AWS Lambda 和 Amazon Data Firehose 将日志转发至专用的安全账户。"},"answer":["A","D"],"multi":true,"vote":{},"tags":["Organizations/Governance","Storage","Compute","Monitoring/Ops"],"difficulty":2,"diff_why":"複選","research":{"verdict":["A","D"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"both","explanation_en":"The requirement combines two things: (1) centralized, all-account activity logging with LEAST operational overhead, and (2) an immutable 2-year retention store where no one can change or delete logs. For (1), a single AWS CloudTrail organization trail (D) is purpose-built for this: created once by the management account (or a delegated administrator), it automatically logs management-account and all member-account events — current and future accounts included — and delivers every log file to one S3 bucket in the designated security account. No per-account CloudTrail configuration or custom log-forwarding pipeline is needed. For (2), S3 Object Lock in compliance mode with a 2-year retention period (A) is the only option that actually enforces 'no changes or deletions': per AWS documentation, compliance mode is 'the strictest level of protection,' preventing any user — including the AWS account root user — from shortening or removing the retention period or deleting the protected object versions. Between A and B, the AWS CloudTrail documentation for organization-trail S3 bucket policies confirms that member accounts never need or receive direct write access to the bucket: log delivery is performed by the cloudtrail.amazonaws.com service principal, and the bucket policy's aws:SourceArn condition 'must be a trail ARN that is owned by the management account, and uses the management account ID' (docs: create-s3-bucket-policy-for-cloudtrail.html, 'Create or update an Amazon S3 bucket to use to store the log files for an organization trail'). So the bucket policy is scoped to the management account's trail, matching option A, not option B's 'allow member accounts to write' model, which is both unnecessary and would needlessly widen the attack surface of an otherwise immutable log archive. C fails outright because an S3 Lifecycle expiration rule only deletes objects after 2 years — it provides zero protection against changes or deletions during the retention window. E (per-account CloudTrail plus a custom Lambda/Firehose forwarding pipeline) is exactly the high-overhead, bespoke approach the organization trail (D) is designed to replace.","explanation_zh":"題目要求同時滿足兩件事:(1) 以最低營運負擔對所有帳號活動做集中式記錄,(2) 一個任何人都無法變更或刪除、保留 2 年的不可變儲存區。對於 (1),單一 AWS CloudTrail organization trail(D)正是為此設計:由 management account(或委派管理員)建立一次,即可自動記錄 management account 與所有現有及未來成員帳號的事件,並將所有日誌檔統一投遞到 security account 的單一 S3 bucket,不需要逐帳號設定 CloudTrail 或自建轉送管線。對於 (2),S3 Object Lock 搭配 compliance mode、保留期 2 年(A)是唯一真正強制「不得變更或刪除」的選項:依 AWS 文件,compliance mode 是「最嚴格層級的保護」,可防止任何使用者——包括 AWS 帳號 root user——縮短或移除保留期,或刪除受保護的物件版本。在 A 與 B 之間,AWS CloudTrail 關於 organization trail 的 S3 bucket policy 文件證實成員帳號從不需要、也不會取得對 bucket 的直接寫入權限:日誌投遞是由 cloudtrail.amazonaws.com 服務主體執行,且 bucket policy 的 aws:SourceArn 條件「必須是 management account 擁有的 trail ARN,並使用 management account ID」(文件出處:create-s3-bucket-policy-for-cloudtrail.html,「Create or update an Amazon S3 bucket to use to store the log files for an organization trail」段落)。因此 bucket policy 的授權範圍是 management account 的 trail,對應選項 A,而非選項 B「開放成員帳號寫入」的模式——後者既不必要,也會無謂擴大這個原本不可變的日誌保存區的攻擊面。C 直接不符合要求,因為 S3 Lifecycle 到期規則只會在 2 年後刪除物件,對保留期內的變更或刪除完全沒有防護。E(逐帳號開啟 CloudTrail 並用 Lambda/Firehose 自建轉送管線)正是 organization trail(D)設計來取代的高營運負擔、客製化做法。","distractors":[{"letter":"B","why_en":"With an organization trail, member accounts never write to the bucket directly — CloudTrail's cloudtrail.amazonaws.com service principal delivers the logs, and per AWS docs the bucket policy's aws:SourceArn condition must reference the trail ARN owned by the management account (using the management account ID). Granting every member account direct write access is unnecessary and unnecessarily widens the attack surface of the immutable log archive.","why_zh":"使用 organization trail 時,成員帳號從不直接寫入 bucket——是由 CloudTrail 的 cloudtrail.amazonaws.com 服務主體投遞日誌,且依 AWS 文件,bucket policy 的 aws:SourceArn 條件必須參照 management account 擁有的 trail ARN(使用 management account ID)。讓所有成員帳號都取得直接寫入權限並非必要,反而不必要地擴大了這個不可變日誌保存區的攻擊面。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"An S3 Lifecycle expiration rule only deletes objects after the 2-year period elapses; it provides no protection at all against modification or deletion during those 2 years, so it fails the 'no changes or deletions' requirement. Only Object Lock in compliance mode enforces true WORM (write-once-read-many) protection.","why_zh":"S3 Lifecycle 到期規則只會在 2 年期滿後刪除物件,對這 2 年期間內的變更或刪除完全沒有防護,因此不符合「不得變更或刪除」的要求。只有 Object Lock 的 compliance mode 能強制真正的 WORM(一次寫入、多次讀取)保護。"},{"letter":"E","why_en":"Enabling CloudTrail individually in every account and building a custom Lambda + Amazon Data Firehose forwarding pipeline to the security account is exactly the high-operational-overhead, bespoke approach the question rules out. An organization trail achieves the same centralized delivery natively with a single configuration and automatically covers new accounts, with no custom code to build or maintain.","why_zh":"在每個帳號各自啟用 CloudTrail,再自行建置 Lambda + Amazon Data Firehose 轉送管線到 security account,正是題目要排除的高營運負擔、客製化做法。Organization trail 只需一次設定即可原生達成相同的集中投遞效果,並自動涵蓋新加入的帳號,無需自行開發或維運程式碼。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/awscloudtrail/latest/userguide/creating-trail-organization.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/awscloudtrail/latest/userguide/create-s3-bucket-policy-for-cloudtrail.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonS3/latest/userguide/object-lock.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonS3/latest/userguide/batch-ops-compliance-mode.html"]}},{"id":4,"question_en":"A security engineer received an Amazon GuardDuty alert indicating a finding involving the Amazon EC2 instance that hosts the company ' s primary website. The GuardDuty finding received read: UnauthorizedAccess:IAMUser/InstanceCredentialExfiltration. The security engineer confirmed that a malicious actor used API access keys intended for the EC2 instance from a country where the company doesnot operate. The security engineer needs to deny access to the malicious actor. What is the first step the security engineer should take?","question_zh":"一名安全工程师收到一条Amazon GuardDuty告警，提示发现与托管公司主要网站的Amazon EC2实例相关的异常情况。该 GuardDuty告警内容为：UnauthorizedAccess:IAMUser/InstanceCredentialExfiltration。安全工程师确认，有恶意行为者使用了 本应用于EC2实例的API访问密钥，且访问来源国家为该公司未开展业务的地区。安全工程师需要阻止该恶意行为者的访问 权限。 安全工程师应采取的第一步是什么？","options_en":{"A":"Open the EC2 console and remove any security groups that allow inbound traffic from 0.0.0.0/0.","B":"Install the AWS Systems Manager Agent on the EC2 instance and run an inventory report.","C":"Install the Amazon Inspector agent on the host and run an assessment with the CVE rules package.","D":"Open the IAM console and revoke all IAM sessions that are associated with the instance profile."},"options_zh":{"A":"打开 EC2 控制台，移除所有允许来自 0.0.0.0/0 的入站流量的安全组。","B":"在 EC2 实例上安装 AWS Systems Manager Agent 并运行清单报告。","C":"在主机上安装 Amazon Inspector 代理，并使用 CVE 规则包运行一次评估。","D":"打开 IAM 控制台，撤销与该实例配置文件关联的所有 IAM 会话。"},"answer":["D"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Security/IAM","Compute","Monitoring/Ops"],"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選","research":{"verdict":["D"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"The finding UnauthorizedAccess:IAMUser/InstanceCredentialExfiltration.OutsideAWS fires when the temporary security credentials (an ASIA-prefixed access key, secret key, and session token) that AWS STS issued to the EC2 instance's role via its instance profile are being used from an IP address outside AWS — here, from a country the company does not operate in. Per AWS's own guidance for compromised credentials (docs.aws.amazon.com/guardduty/latest/ug/compromised-creds.html), the response depends on whether the key is a long-term AKIA key (IAM user) or a short-term ASIA key (STS/role): ASIA credentials 'cannot be viewed or managed' and cannot simply be deactivated like an access key. The AWS-documented way to immediately cut off a live session created from a role is the 'Revoke active sessions' action in the IAM console for that role (docs.aws.amazon.com/IAM/latest/UserGuide/id_roles_use_revoke-sessions.html): it attaches an inline AWSRevokeOlderSessions policy that denies all actions to any session whose aws:TokenIssueTime is before the revoke action, instantly invalidating every credential the attacker holds while leaving the EC2 instance unaffected (it just fetches fresh, unrevoked credentials from the instance metadata service on its next request). Because the attacker is calling AWS service endpoints directly over the internet using stolen IAM credentials, no network- or host-level control can intercept those calls — security groups (A) only filter traffic to/from the instance's ENI, not calls the attacker makes straight to AWS APIs from their own network; installing SSM (B) or Inspector (C) are investigative/inventory actions that touch the host, not the stolen credential, and do nothing to deny the attacker. Only revoking the IAM role's active sessions (D) directly denies the malicious actor, making it the correct first step.","explanation_zh":"GuardDuty 的 UnauthorizedAccess:IAMUser/InstanceCredentialExfiltration.OutsideAWS 發生於：EC2 執行個體透過 instance profile 取得的角色 STS 臨時憑證（ASIA 開頭的 access key、secret key、session token）被人從 AWS 之外的 IP 位址使用——本題中是從公司未營運的國家。依 AWS 官方對憑證外洩的處理指引（docs.aws.amazon.com/guardduty/latest/ug/compromised-creds.html），處理方式取決於金鑰型態：長期 AKIA 金鑰（IAM user）可直接停用／刪除，但 ASIA 這類短期臨時憑證『無法在主控台檢視或管理』，也無法像一般 access key 那樣直接停用。AWS 文件記載的立即阻斷方式，是在 IAM 主控台對該角色執行『Revoke active sessions』（docs.aws.amazon.com/IAM/latest/UserGuide/id_roles_use_revoke-sessions.html）：此動作會附加內嵌的 AWSRevokeOlderSessions 政策，對所有 aws:TokenIssueTime 早於撤銷時間點的工作階段拒絕全部動作，立即讓攻擊者手上的所有憑證失效，而 EC2 執行個體本身完全不受影響（下一次請求時會從 instance metadata service 自動取得全新、未被撤銷的憑證）。由於攻擊者是直接透過網際網路呼叫 AWS 服務端點、使用竊得的 IAM 憑證，因此網路層或主機層的控制都攔不到這些呼叫：security group（A）只能過濾進出該執行個體 ENI 的流量，攔不住攻擊者從自己網路直接打向 AWS API 的呼叫；安裝 SSM（B）或 Inspector（C）屬於針對主機的調查／盤點動作，並不作用在已外洩的憑證上，無法阻止攻擊者。只有撤銷該 IAM 角色的作用中工作階段（D）才能直接拒絕該惡意行為者存取，因此是正確的第一步。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"Security groups control network traffic to and from the instance's network interface. The attacker is calling AWS APIs directly from an external country using stolen IAM credentials; those calls go to AWS service endpoints over the internet, not through the instance's security group, so removing 0.0.0.0/0 inbound rules does nothing to deny the actor.","why_zh":"Security group 只控制進出執行個體網路介面的流量。攻擊者是在境外用竊取的 IAM 憑證直接呼叫 AWS API，這些呼叫透過網際網路送往 AWS 服務端點，不會經過該執行個體的 security group，因此移除 0.0.0.0/0 入站規則無法阻斷攻擊者。"},{"letter":"B","why_en":"Installing the SSM Agent and running an inventory report is an asset-visibility/investigation task focused on what is installed on the host. It does not revoke or invalidate the exfiltrated STS credentials and does nothing to stop the attacker's ongoing API calls.","why_zh":"安裝 SSM Agent 並執行清查報告，是聚焦於主機上安裝了哪些軟體的資產盤點／調查動作，並不會撤銷或使外洩的 STS 憑證失效，無法阻止攻擊者持續呼叫 API。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"Amazon Inspector's CVE assessment package scans the host for known software vulnerabilities. That might help explain how the instance was compromised, but it is not a containment action and has no effect on the already-issued, exfiltrated temporary credentials.","why_zh":"Amazon Inspector 的 CVE 評估套件是掃描主機上已知的軟體弱點，或許有助於事後了解執行個體如何被入侵，但這不是圍堵動作，對已經簽發並外洩的臨時憑證沒有任何作用。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/guardduty/latest/ug/guardduty_finding-types-iam.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/guardduty/latest/ug/compromised-creds.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/IAM/latest/UserGuide/id_roles_use_revoke-sessions.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/IAM/latest/UserGuide/id_credentials_temp_control-access_disable-perms.html"]}},{"id":5,"question_en":"A company that builds document management systems recently performed a security review of its application on AWS. The review showed that uploads of documents through signed URLs into Amazon S3 could occur in the application without encryption in transit. A security engineer must implement a solution that prevents uploads that are not encrypted in transit. Which solution will meet this requirement?","question_zh":"一家开发文档管理系统的企业最近对其在AWS上的应用程序进行了安全审查。审查发现，通过签名 URL将文档上传至Amazon S3时，数据在传输过程中可能未加密。安全工程师必须实施一项解决方案， 以防止未加密传输的上传行为。 哪种解决方案能满足这一要求","options_en":{"A":"Ensure that all client implementations are using HTTPS to upload documents into the application.","B":"Configure the s3-bucket-ssl-requests-only managed rule in AWS Config.","C":"Add an S3 bucket policy that denies all S3 actions for condition “aws:SecureTransport”: “false”.","D":"Add an S3 bucket ACL with a grantee of AllUsers, a permission of WRITE, and a condition of secureTransport."},"options_zh":{"B":"在 AWS Config 中配置 s3-bucket-ssl-requests-only 管理规则。","C":"添加一个S3存储桶策略，拒绝所有S3操作，条件SecureTransport”：“false”。","D":"添加一个S3存储桶ACL，授权对象为AllUsers，权限为WRITE，并设置条件 secureTransport。","A":"确保所有客户端实现均使用 HTTPS 将文档上传至应用程序。"},"answer":["C"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Organizations/Governance","Security/IAM","Storage"],"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選","research":{"verdict":["C"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"The requirement is to PREVENT (not merely detect) uploads that are not encrypted in transit. AWS's S3 'Protecting data in transit with encryption' documentation explicitly states that enforcing HTTPS-only communication is done through policy mechanisms such as bucket policies (also SCPs, RCPs, or VPC endpoint policies) using the aws:SecureTransport condition key. An explicit Deny on all S3 actions with the condition \"aws:SecureTransport\": \"false\" makes Amazon S3 itself reject every plain-HTTP request — including PUTs via presigned URLs — no matter how the client behaves. This is the only option that is a server-side preventive control enforced by the service. Option B's s3-bucket-ssl-requests-only AWS Config managed rule (identifier S3_BUCKET_SSL_REQUESTS_ONLY) is explicitly documented as checking whether a bucket policy requiring SSL/TLS exists and flagging the bucket NON_COMPLIANT if not — it is a detective control that reports after the fact and does not itself block an HTTP request. Option A is an unenforceable client-side convention — a presigned URL still works over HTTP unless the bucket denies it server-side. Option D is invalid because S3 bucket ACLs do not support condition elements at all (grants are simply to a grantee with a permission, no 'secureTransport' condition exists), and granting WRITE to the AllUsers group would make the bucket publicly writable — a severe security regression, not a fix.","explanation_zh":"題目要求「防止」（prevent）未加密傳輸的上傳，而不只是偵測。AWS 的 S3「Protecting data in transit with encryption」官方文件明確指出：要強制 HTTPS-only，是透過 policy 機制（bucket policy，或 SCP、RCP、VPC endpoint policy）搭配 aws:SecureTransport condition key 來實現。在 bucket policy 中對所有 S3 action 加入明確 Deny、條件為 \"aws:SecureTransport\": \"false\"，S3 服務端就會直接拒絕所有純 HTTP 請求，包含透過 presigned URL 的上傳，無論客戶端如何實作。這是唯一屬於服務端強制執行的預防性控制選項。選項 B 的 s3-bucket-ssl-requests-only 是 AWS Config 受管規則（識別碼 S3_BUCKET_SSL_REQUESTS_ONLY），官方文件明確說明它只是檢查 bucket policy 是否要求 SSL/TLS，若無則標記 NON_COMPLIANT——屬於事後偵測性控制，本身不會阻擋 HTTP 請求。選項 A 只是客戶端約定，無法強制——只要 bucket 本身沒有伺服器端 Deny，presigned URL 仍可走 HTTP。選項 D 無效：S3 bucket ACL 完全不支援 condition 元素（授權只是 grantee + permission，並無 secureTransport 這種條件），且授予 AllUsers WRITE 會讓 bucket 可被公開寫入，是嚴重的安全倒退，而非修補。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"Relying on client implementations is not enforcement; any holder of the presigned URL can still send the request over plain HTTP unless the bucket itself denies non-TLS requests server-side.","why_zh":"依賴客戶端實作並非強制手段；只要 bucket 本身未在伺服器端拒絕非 TLS 請求，持有 presigned URL 的任何人仍可用純 HTTP 送出請求。"},{"letter":"B","why_en":"s3-bucket-ssl-requests-only is a detective AWS Config managed rule (S3_BUCKET_SSL_REQUESTS_ONLY): it only evaluates whether the bucket policy requires SSL/TLS and reports the bucket NON_COMPLIANT if not; it does not itself block or reject an HTTP upload.","why_zh":"s3-bucket-ssl-requests-only 是偵測性的 AWS Config 受管規則（S3_BUCKET_SSL_REQUESTS_ONLY）：只評估 bucket policy 是否要求 SSL/TLS，不符合就回報 NON_COMPLIANT，本身並不會阻擋或拒絕 HTTP 上傳請求。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"S3 ACLs do not support condition elements (there is no 'secureTransport' concept in ACL grants), and granting WRITE to the AllUsers group would open the bucket to public writes — the opposite of a security fix.","why_zh":"S3 ACL 授權完全不支援 condition 元素（ACL 沒有 secureTransport 這種條件），且授予 AllUsers WRITE 等於開放公開寫入，與安全修補背道而馳。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonS3/latest/userguide/UsingEncryptionInTransit.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/config/latest/developerguide/s3-bucket-ssl-requests-only.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonS3/latest/userguide/security_iam_service-with-iam.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonS3/latest/userguide/acl-overview.html"]}},{"id":6,"question_en":"A company’s security team needs to receive a notification whenever an AWS access key has not been rotated in 90 or more days. A security engineer must develop a solution that provides these notifications automatically. Which solution will meet these requirements with the LEAST amount of effort?","question_zh":"每当AWS访问密钥超过90天未轮换时，公司的安全团队都需要收到通知。安全工程师必须开发一个 能够自动提供此类通知的解决方案。 哪种解决方案能在最少的努力下满足这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Deploy an AWS Config managed rule to run on a periodic basis of 24 hours. Select the access-keys- rotated managed rule, and set the maxAccessKeyAge parameter to 90 days. Create an Amazon EventBridge rule with an event pattern that matches the compliance type of NON_COMPLIANT from AWS Config for the managed rule. Configure EventBridge to send an Amazon SNS notification to the security team.","B":"Create a script to export a .csv file from the AWS Trusted Advisor check for IAM access key rotation. Load the script into an AWS Lambda function that will upload the .csv file to an Amazon S3 bucket. Create an Amazon Athena table query that runs when the .csv file is uploaded to the S3 bucket. Publish the results for any keys older than 90 days by using an invocation of an Amazon SNS notification to the security team.","C":"Create a script to download the IAM credentials report on a periodic basis. Load the script into an AWS Lambda function that will run on a schedule through Amazon EventBridge. Configure the Lambda script to load the report into memory and to filter the report for records in which the key was last rotated at least 90 days ago. If any records are detected, send an Amazon SNS notification to the security team.","D":"Create an AWS Lambda function that queries the IAM API to list all the users. Iterate through the users by using the ListAccessKeys operation. Verify that the value in the CreateDate field is not at least 90 days old. Send an SNS notification to the security team if the value is at least 90 days old. Create an EventBridge rule to schedule the Lambda function to run each day."},"options_zh":{"A":"部署一个 AWS Config 管理规则，以每 24 小时定期运行一次。选择 access-keys-rotated 管理规则，并将 maxAccessKeyAge 参数设置为 90 天。创建一个 Amazon EventBridge 规则，其事件模式匹配 AWS Config 中该管理 规则的 NON_COMPLIANT 合规类型。配置 EventBridge 将 Amazon SNS 通知发送给安全团队。","B":"创建一个脚本，从 AWS Trusted Advisor 的 IAM 访问密钥轮换检查中导出 .csv 文件。将该脚本加载到 AWS Lambda 函数中，用于将 .csv 文件上传至 Amazon S3 存储桶。创建一个 Amazon Athena 表格查询，当 .csv 文件上传至 S3 存 储桶时自动执行。通过调用 Amazon SNS 通知将超过 90 天的密钥结果发送给安全团队。","C":"创建一个脚本，定期下载 IAM 凭据报告。将该脚本加载到 AWS Lambda 函数中，并通过 Amazon EventBridge 按计划 执行。配置 Lambda 脚本将报告加载到内存中，并筛选出密钥上次轮换时间超过 90 天的记录。若发现任何符合条 件的记录，则向安全团队发送 Amazon SNS 通知。","D":"创建一个 AWS Lambda 函数，调用 IAM API 列出所有用户。通过使用 ListAccessKeys 操作遍历每个用户，检查 CreateDate 字段的值是否已超过 90 天。如果该值超过 90 天，则向安全团队发送 SNS 通知。创建一个 EventBridge 规则，每天定时触发该 Lambda 函数运行。"},"answer":["A"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Organizations/Governance","Security/IAM","Storage","Compute","Serverless/Integration","Analytics"],"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選","research":{"verdict":["A"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"The key qualifier is LEAST effort, which points to a fully managed, configuration-only pipeline rather than any custom code. AWS Config's managed rule access-keys-rotated (identifier ACCESS_KEYS_ROTATED, resource type AWS::IAM::User, trigger type Periodic) checks whether active IAM access keys have been rotated within the number of days set by the maxAccessKeyAge parameter (default 90) and marks the key NON_COMPLIANT if not. AWS Config emits a 'Config Rules Compliance Change' event to Amazon EventBridge whenever a rule's evaluation result changes compliance state; an EventBridge rule can match on complianceType NON_COMPLIANT for this specific Config rule and target an SNS topic to notify the security team. The entire solution is enable-the-managed-rule-and-wire-EventBridge-to-SNS — zero custom code, zero infrastructure to maintain. Option B requires a custom script, an S3 bucket, and an Athena query pipeline just to replicate what one Config rule already does, and Trusted Advisor's IAM access key rotation check additionally requires a Business or Enterprise Support plan. Option C requires writing and maintaining a Lambda function that downloads and parses the IAM credentials report (which does contain access_key_1/2_last_rotated fields) on an EventBridge schedule. Option D requires custom Lambda code that paginates through ListUsers/ListAccessKeys and compares CreateDate manually. B, C, and D are all technically workable but each demands building and operating custom code, which is strictly more effort than A's managed-rule + EventBridge + SNS chain.","explanation_zh":"題目關鍵字是 LEAST effort（最少工作量），指向完全託管、純設定即可完成的方案，而非任何自訂程式碼。AWS Config 的受管規則 access-keys-rotated（識別碼 ACCESS_KEYS_ROTATED，資源類型 AWS::IAM::User，觸發類型 Periodic）會依 maxAccessKeyAge 參數（預設 90 天）檢查作用中的 IAM access key 是否在期限內完成輪替，逾期則標記為 NON_COMPLIANT。AWS Config 只要規則的合規狀態改變，就會發出 'Config Rules Compliance Change' 事件到 Amazon EventBridge；建立一條比對該規則 complianceType 為 NON_COMPLIANT 的 EventBridge 規則，並以 SNS topic 為目標，即可自動通知安全團隊。整個方案就是「啟用受管規則＋設定 EventBridge 到 SNS」——零自訂程式碼、零基礎設施維護。選項 B 需要自訂腳本、S3 儲存桶與 Athena 查詢管線，只為重現一條 Config 規則已經能做到的事，而且 Trusted Advisor 的 IAM access key 輪替檢查還需要 Business 或 Enterprise Support 方案。選項 C 需要撰寫並維護一個 Lambda 函式，依 EventBridge 排程下載並解析 IAM credentials report（雖然報告確實含 access_key_1/2_last_rotated 欄位）。選項 D 需要自訂 Lambda 程式碼分頁列舉 ListUsers/ListAccessKeys 並手動比對 CreateDate。B、C、D 技術上都可行，但都需要建置與維運自訂程式碼，工作量明顯高於 A 的「受管規則＋EventBridge＋SNS」鏈路。","distractors":[{"letter":"B","why_en":"Requires custom scripting, Lambda, S3, and an Athena query pipeline — a multi-service build to replicate what a single managed Config rule already does; Trusted Advisor's IAM access key rotation check also requires a Business or Enterprise Support plan, and Athena does not natively fire queries on S3 object upload without additional Lambda/Step Functions glue. Far more effort than A.","why_zh":"需要自訂腳本、Lambda、S3 與 Athena 查詢管線，只為重現一條受管 Config 規則就能做到的事；且 Trusted Advisor 的 IAM access key 輪替檢查需要 Business 或 Enterprise Support 方案，Athena 也無法在沒有額外 Lambda/Step Functions 膠合邏輯下原生於 S3 檔案上傳時自動觸發查詢。工作量遠高於 A。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"Technically workable (the IAM credential report includes access_key_1/2_last_rotated fields), but requires writing, testing, and maintaining custom Lambda code to download and parse the report plus an EventBridge schedule — more build-and-operate effort than enabling a managed rule.","why_zh":"技術上可行（IAM credential report 含 access_key_1/2_last_rotated 欄位），但必須撰寫、測試並維護自訂 Lambda 下載與解析程式，再加上 EventBridge 排程，建置與維運工作量高於直接啟用受管規則。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"Also technically workable (ListAccessKeys returns CreateDate), but requires custom Lambda code that iterates all IAM users with pagination and manual date-comparison logic — again more build-and-maintain effort than the managed Config rule + EventBridge + SNS chain.","why_zh":"技術上同樣可行（ListAccessKeys 回傳 CreateDate），但需自寫 Lambda 程式分頁列舉所有 IAM 使用者並手動比對日期邏輯，建置與維護成本仍高於受管 Config 規則＋EventBridge＋SNS 的方案。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/config/latest/developerguide/access-keys-rotated.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/config/latest/developerguide/monitor-config-with-cloudwatchevents.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/config/latest/developerguide/evaluate-config_use-managed-rules.html"]}},{"id":7,"question_en":"A company needs to detect unauthenticated access to its Amazon Elastic Kubernetes Service (Amazon EKS) clusters. The solution must require no additional configuration of the existing EKS deployment. Which solution will meet these requirements with the LEAST operational effort?","question_zh":"一家公司需要检测对其 Amazon 弹性 Kubernetes 服务（Amazon EKS）集群的未授权访问。该解决方案必须无需对现有的 EKS 部署进行额外配置。 哪种解决方案能在最少的操作投入下满足这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Install a third-party security add-on.","B":"Enable AWS Security Hub and monitor Kubernetes findings.","C":"Monitor CloudWatch Container Insights metrics for EKS.","D":"Enable Amazon GuardDuty and use EKS Audit Log Monitoring."},"options_zh":{"A":"安装第三方安全插件。","B":"启用 AWS Security Hub 并监控 Kubernetes 的检测结果。","C":"监控 EKS 的 CloudWatch 容器洞察指标。","D":"启用 Amazon GuardDuty 并使用 EKS 审计日志监控。"},"answer":["D"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Security/IAM","Compute","Monitoring/Ops","Containers"],"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選","research":{"verdict":["D"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"GuardDuty EKS Protection (which includes EKS Audit Log Monitoring) is purpose-built for this requirement. Per AWS docs, when you enable EKS Protection, GuardDuty uses its own independent stream to collect and analyze EKS audit logs — 'no additional configuration is required.' It works even if the customer has not turned on Amazon EKS control plane logging to CloudWatch, since GuardDuty ingests the audit log stream directly and separately from that feature. It also does not require installing any agent or add-on into the cluster. This satisfies both the 'no additional configuration of the existing EKS deployment' constraint and the LEAST-operational-effort qualifier, since it's just a toggle on the GuardDuty detector (or is on by default via the 30-day trial when GuardDuty is enabled). It generates findings specifically for unauthenticated access — e.g. Discovery:Kubernetes/SuccessfulAnonymousAccess, Persistence:Kubernetes/SuccessfulAnonymousAccess, CredentialAccess:Kubernetes/SuccessfulAnonymousAccess, DefenseEvasion:Kubernetes/SuccessfulAnonymousAccess, and Impact:Kubernetes/SuccessfulAnonymousAccess — all of which fire when the system:anonymous (unauthenticated) Kubernetes user successfully invokes an API. The other options either require installing/maintaining software inside the cluster, merely aggregate findings that GuardDuty itself produces, or monitor performance rather than security events, none of which directly detect unauthenticated access with less effort.","explanation_zh":"GuardDuty EKS Protection（包含 EKS Audit Log Monitoring）正是為此需求設計。根據 AWS 官方文件，啟用 EKS Protection 後，GuardDuty 會用自己獨立的串流來收集並分析 EKS audit logs——「不需要額外設定」。即使客戶未開啟 Amazon EKS control plane logging 傳送到 CloudWatch，這項功能也能運作，因為 GuardDuty 是直接、獨立地擷取 audit log 串流，與該功能無關；也完全不需要在叢集內安裝任何 agent 或 add-on。這同時滿足「不需對現有 EKS 部署做額外設定」與「最少維運工作量」兩項要求，只需在 GuardDuty detector 上開關一次（或啟用 GuardDuty 時透過 30 天試用預設開啟）。它會針對未驗證存取產生專屬 findings，例如 Discovery:Kubernetes/SuccessfulAnonymousAccess、Persistence:Kubernetes/SuccessfulAnonymousAccess、CredentialAccess:Kubernetes/SuccessfulAnonymousAccess、DefenseEvasion:Kubernetes/SuccessfulAnonymousAccess 與 Impact:Kubernetes/SuccessfulAnonymousAccess，這些都在 system:anonymous（未驗證）使用者成功呼叫 Kubernetes API 時觸發。其他選項不是需要在叢集內安裝並維護軟體，就是只彙整 GuardDuty 本身產生的 findings，或是監控效能而非安全事件，都無法以更低的維運成本直接偵測未驗證存取。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"A third-party security add-on must be installed and maintained inside the cluster — that is additional configuration of the EKS deployment and clearly more operational effort than a one-click GuardDuty toggle that requires no changes to EKS itself.","why_zh":"第三方安全 add-on 必須安裝並維護在叢集內——這正是對 EKS 部署的額外設定，維運工作量明顯高於完全不需變更 EKS 本身、一鍵開啟的 GuardDuty。"},{"letter":"B","why_en":"Security Hub is a findings aggregator and compliance-check service; it does not itself analyze EKS audit logs or detect unauthenticated access to the cluster. The Kubernetes threat findings that could appear in Security Hub are generated by GuardDuty in the first place, so GuardDuty must be enabled regardless — Security Hub alone detects nothing and adds an unnecessary extra layer.","why_zh":"Security Hub 是 findings 彙整與合規檢查服務，本身不會分析 EKS audit logs 或偵測對叢集的未驗證存取；會出現在 Security Hub 的 Kubernetes 威脅 findings 本來就是由 GuardDuty 產生的，因此仍須啟用 GuardDuty——單靠 Security Hub 偵測不到任何東西，反而多了一層不必要的設定。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"CloudWatch Container Insights collects performance metrics (CPU, memory, network) and requires deploying the CloudWatch agent/add-on to the cluster; it is an observability tool, not a threat-detection service, and cannot identify unauthenticated Kubernetes API access.","why_zh":"CloudWatch Container Insights 收集的是效能指標（CPU、記憶體、網路），且需要在叢集部署 CloudWatch agent/add-on；它是可觀測性工具而非威脅偵測服務，無法識別未驗證的 Kubernetes API 存取。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/guardduty/latest/ug/kubernetes-protection.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/guardduty/latest/ug/guardduty-finding-types-eks-audit-logs.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/guardduty/latest/ug/eks-protection-enable-standalone-account.html"]}},{"id":8,"question_en":"AWS Config cannot deliver configuration snapshots to Amazon S3. Which TWO actions will remediate this issue?","question_zh":"AWS Config 无法将配置快照传递到 Amazon S3。 哪两项操作可以解决此问题？","options_en":{"A":"Verify the S3 bucket policy allows config.amazonaws.com.","B":"Verify the IAM role has s3:GetBucketAcl and s3:PutObject permissions.","C":"Verify the S3 bucket can assume the IAM role.","D":"Verify IAM policy allows AWS Config to write logs.","E":"Modify AWS Config API permissions."},"options_zh":{"A":"验证S3存储桶策略是否允许config.amazonaws.com。","B":"验证 IAM 角色是否具有 s3:GetBucketAcl 和 s3:PutObject 权限。","C":"验证S3存储桶能否承担IAM角色。","D":"验证 IAM 策略是否允许 AWS Config 写入日志。","E":"修改 AWS Config API 权限。"},"answer":["A","B"],"multi":true,"vote":{},"tags":["Organizations/Governance","Security/IAM","Storage"],"difficulty":2,"diff_why":"複選","research":{"verdict":["A","B"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"AWS Config delivers configuration snapshots to S3 through two permission layers, and a failure in either one blocks delivery. First, the S3 bucket policy must grant the AWS Config service principal (config.amazonaws.com) access — the documented bucket policy grants s3:GetBucketAcl, s3:ListBucket, and s3:PutObject to that principal — so option A is correct. Second, the IAM role assigned to the configuration recorder must have S3 permissions; the documented IAM role policy for AWS Config includes s3:PutObject on the bucket's AWSLogs prefix and s3:GetBucketAcl on the bucket — so option B is correct. These are exactly the two checks AWS troubleshooting guidance lists for 'Config is not delivering to S3'. S3 buckets are resources, not principals, so they cannot assume IAM roles (C); the issue is snapshot delivery to S3, not log writing (D); and there is no 'AWS Config API permissions' setting to modify (E).","explanation_zh":"AWS Config 將 configuration snapshot 交付到 S3 需要兩層權限，任一層缺失都會導致交付失敗。第一，S3 bucket policy 必須授權 AWS Config 服務主體（config.amazonaws.com）——官方文件的 bucket policy 就是授予該主體 s3:GetBucketAcl、s3:ListBucket 與 s3:PutObject——因此選項 A 正確。第二，指派給 configuration recorder 的 IAM role 必須具備 S3 權限；官方文件的 IAM role policy 包含對 bucket AWSLogs 前綴的 s3:PutObject 及對 bucket 的 s3:GetBucketAcl——因此選項 B 正確。這正是 AWS 針對「Config 無法交付到 S3」列出的兩項檢查。S3 bucket 是資源而非主體，無法 assume IAM role（C）；本題是 snapshot 交付到 S3 的問題，與寫入 logs 無關（D）；也不存在可修改的「AWS Config API permissions」設定（E）。","distractors":[{"letter":"C","why_en":"S3 buckets are resources, not IAM principals — a bucket cannot assume an IAM role. It is AWS Config (the service) that assumes the role, so this option is conceptually invalid.","why_zh":"S3 bucket 是資源而非 IAM 主體，bucket 無法 assume IAM role。是 AWS Config 服務去 assume 該 role，此選項在概念上就不成立。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"The problem is delivering configuration snapshots to S3, not writing logs (e.g., to CloudWatch Logs). A generic 'write logs' permission has no bearing on S3 snapshot delivery.","why_zh":"問題在於將 configuration snapshot 交付到 S3，而非寫入 logs（例如 CloudWatch Logs）。籠統的「寫 logs」權限與 S3 snapshot 交付無關。"},{"letter":"E","why_en":"There is no configurable 'AWS Config API permissions' setting; access is controlled via the IAM role/service principal and the S3 bucket policy, not by modifying Config's API.","why_zh":"不存在可設定的「AWS Config API permissions」；存取是透過 IAM role／服務主體與 S3 bucket policy 控制，而非修改 Config 的 API。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/config/latest/developerguide/s3-bucket-policy.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/config/latest/developerguide/iamrole-permissions.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/config/latest/developerguide/gs-cli-prereq.html"]}},{"id":9,"question_en":"A company runs its microservices architecture in Kubernetes containers on AWS by using Amazon Elastic Kubernetes Service (Amazon EKS) and Amazon Aurora. The company has an organization in AWS Organizations to manage hundreds of AWS accounts that host different microservices. The company needs to implement a monitoring solution for logs from all AWS resources across all accounts. The solution must include automatic detection of security-related issues. Which solution will meet these requirements with theLEAST operational effort?","question_zh":"该公司使用 Amazon Elastic Kubernetes Service（Amazon EKS）和 Amazon Aurora，在 AWS 上通过 Kubernetes 容器运行其微服 务架构。该公司在 AWS Organizations 中创建了一个组织，用于管理托管不同微服务的数百个 AWS 账户。 公司需要为所有账户中的所有AWS资源的日志实施监控解决方案，该方案必须包含对安全相关问题的自动检测功能。 哪种解决方案能在最少的操作投入下满足这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Designate an Amazon GuardDuty administrator account in the organization’s management account. Enable GuardDuty for all accounts. Enable EKS Protection and RDS Protection in the GuardDuty administrator account.","B":"Designate a monitoring account. Share Amazon CloudWatch Logs from all accounts. Use Amazon Inspector to evaluate the logs.","C":"Centralize CloudTrail logs in Amazon S3 and analyze them with Amazon Athena.","D":"Stream CloudWatch Logs to Amazon Kinesis and analyze them with custom AWS Lambda functions."},"options_zh":{"A":"在组织的管理账户中指定一个 Amazon GuardDuty 管理员账户。为所有账户启用 GuardDuty，并在 GuardDuty 管理员账户 中启用 EKS 保护和 RDS 保护。","B":"指定一个监控账户。共享所有账户的 Amazon CloudWatch 日志，并使用 Amazon Inspector 对日志进行评估。","C":"将 CloudTrail 日志集中存储在 Amazon S3 中，并使用 Amazon Athena 进行分析。","D":"将 CloudWatch 日志流式传输到 Amazon Kinesis，并使用自定义的 AWS Lambda 函数进行分析。"},"answer":["A"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Organizations/Governance","Security/IAM","Storage","Compute","Database","Serverless/Integration","Monitoring/Ops","Analytics","Containers"],"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選","research":{"verdict":["A"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"The qualifier is LEAST operational effort for monitoring logs across hundreds of accounts with automatic detection of security issues. Amazon GuardDuty is a fully managed threat detection service that integrates natively with AWS Organizations: from the management account you designate a delegated GuardDuty administrator account, which can then auto-enable GuardDuty for all existing and new member accounts (up to 50,000 members) with no log-shipping pipelines to build. GuardDuty automatically analyzes foundational data sources (CloudTrail management events, VPC Flow Logs, DNS logs) across every account, and its optional protection plans extend detection to the exact workloads in this scenario: EKS Protection analyzes EKS audit logs from the cluster control plane to detect malicious or unauthorized Kubernetes activity, and RDS Protection profiles login activity on Amazon Aurora databases (MySQL- and PostgreSQL-compatible) to flag anomalous or brute-force access attempts. Enabling these protection plans from the delegated administrator account applies them organization-wide with no custom code, no manual querying, and no infrastructure to operate. All other options require building or operating analysis logic manually and therefore fail the least-operational-effort test.","explanation_zh":"本題關鍵字是「最少營運工作量」(LEAST operational effort)：需跨數百個帳戶監控日誌並「自動」偵測安全問題。Amazon GuardDuty 是全代管的威脅偵測服務，原生整合 AWS Organizations——從管理帳戶指定 GuardDuty 委派管理員帳戶後，該帳戶可自動為所有現有及新加入的成員帳戶啟用 GuardDuty（最多可管理 50,000 個成員帳戶），完全不需自建日誌傳輸管線。GuardDuty 會自動分析基礎資料來源（CloudTrail 管理事件、VPC Flow Logs、DNS 日誌），而其可選的保護方案正好對應本情境的工作負載：EKS Protection 分析 EKS 控制平面的 audit logs 以偵測惡意或未授權的 Kubernetes 活動；RDS Protection 則分析 Amazon Aurora（MySQL/PostgreSQL 相容版）的登入活動，以偵測異常存取或暴力破解嘗試。在委派管理員帳戶啟用這些保護方案即可套用到整個組織，完全免寫程式、免手動查詢、免自行維運基礎設施。其餘選項都需要自行建置或維運分析邏輯，不符合最少營運工作量的要求。","distractors":[{"letter":"B","why_en":"Amazon Inspector is a vulnerability management service that scans EC2 instances, container images in ECR, and Lambda functions for software vulnerabilities and unintended network exposure — it does not ingest or evaluate CloudWatch Logs at all, so this design is technically invalid, not merely higher-effort.","why_zh":"Amazon Inspector 是弱點管理服務，掃描 EC2、ECR 容器映像與 Lambda 的軟體漏洞及非預期網路暴露——它完全不會擷取或評估 CloudWatch Logs，此設計在技術上根本不成立，而不只是工作量較高。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"Centralizing CloudTrail logs in S3 and querying with Athena only covers API activity (not EKS audit logs or Aurora login activity) and provides no automatic security detection — someone must write and run Athena queries manually against each new dataset, which is significant ongoing operational effort.","why_zh":"將 CloudTrail 日誌集中到 S3 再用 Athena 查詢只涵蓋 API 活動（不含 EKS audit logs 或 Aurora 登入活動），且沒有任何自動安全偵測——必須有人針對每批新資料手動撰寫並執行 Athena 查詢，營運負擔沉重。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"Streaming CloudWatch Logs to Kinesis and analyzing with custom Lambda functions means building, maintaining, and scaling bespoke detection logic yourself across hundreds of accounts — the opposite of least operational effort, with no managed threat intelligence behind it.","why_zh":"把 CloudWatch Logs 串流到 Kinesis 並用自製 Lambda 函式分析，代表要在數百個帳戶自行建置、維護並擴展客製偵測邏輯——與最少營運工作量背道而馳，且背後沒有代管的威脅情資支援。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/guardduty/latest/ug/guardduty_organizations.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/guardduty/latest/ug/kubernetes-protection.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/guardduty/latest/ug/rds-protection.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/guardduty/latest/ug/maintaining-guardduty-organization-delegated-admin.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/inspector/latest/user/what-is-inspector.html"]}},{"id":10,"question_en":"A company detects bot activity targeting Amazon Cognito user pool endpoints. The solution must block malicious requests while maintaining access for legitimate users. Which solution meets these requirements?","question_zh":"一家公司发现有针对 Amazon Cognito 用户池端点的机器人活动。解决方案必须在阻止恶意请求的同时，确保合法用户仍可 正常访问。 哪种解决方案符合这些要求","options_en":{"A":"Enable Amazon Cognito threat protection.","B":"Restrict access to authenticated users only.","C":"Associate AWS WAF with the Cognito user pool.","D":"Monitor requests with CloudWatch."},"options_zh":{"B":"仅允许已认证用户访问。","C":"将 AWS WAF 与 Cognito 用户池关联。","D":"使用 CloudWatch 监控请求。","A":"启用 Amazon Cognito 威胁防护。"},"answer":["A"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Security/IAM","Monitoring/Ops"],"difficulty":2,"diff_why":"題庫與社群皆錯","research":{"verdict":["C"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"neither","explanation_en":"The scenario is bot traffic hitting the user pool's public endpoints (hosted UI/managed login and unauthenticated API operations like InitiateAuth, RespondToAuthChallenge, sign-up), and the requirement is to block malicious requests while still letting legitimate users through. AWS's documented mechanism for exactly this is associating an AWS WAF web ACL with the Cognito user pool: per AWS docs, 'AWS WAF web ACLs inspect incoming traffic to your user pool endpoints and authentication API for unwanted activity at the network and application layers,' and 'you can protect your user pool from unwanted requests to your classic hosted UI, managed login, and Amazon Cognito API service endpoints.' A web ACL using the AWS WAF Bot Control managed rule group, rate-based rules, and CAPTCHA/Challenge actions can detect and block automated/bot requests while allowing normal users to proceed. Amazon Cognito threat protection (formerly 'advanced security features,' option A) is a materially different control: AWS describes it as monitoring sign-in for indicators of risk (compromised-credentials detection, adaptive authentication based on location/device) and applying MFA or blocking a sign-in — it scores individual authentication events for account-takeover/credential-stuffing risk, not raw HTTP request/bot traffic patterns at the endpoint level, and it has no bot-detection or rate-limiting capability comparable to WAF Bot Control. B (restrict to authenticated users) is self-defeating because the very endpoints under bot attack (sign-in, sign-up) must accept unauthenticated requests by design. D (CloudWatch monitoring) is observability only and blocks nothing. So C is correct; the dump's suggested answer A conflates credential-risk scoring with bot/request-level blocking.","explanation_zh":"情境是機器人（bot）流量攻擊 Cognito user pool 的公開端點（hosted UI／managed login，以及 InitiateAuth、RespondToAuthChallenge、註冊等未驗證 API），要求是「阻擋惡意請求、同時讓合法使用者維持存取」。AWS 文件針對這種情境的機制正是將 AWS WAF web ACL 與 Cognito user pool 關聯：官方文件寫明「AWS WAF web ACLs 會在網路與應用層檢查送往 user pool 端點與驗證 API 的流量，找出不想要的活動」，且「可保護 user pool 免於送往 classic hosted UI、managed login 與 Amazon Cognito API 端點的不想要請求」。搭配 AWS WAF Bot Control 受管規則群組、rate-based rules 與 CAPTCHA/Challenge 動作，可偵測並阻擋自動化 bot 請求，同時放行正常使用者。Amazon Cognito threat protection（舊稱 advanced security features，選項 A）是本質不同的控制：AWS 文件說明它是監控登入事件的風險指標（外洩憑證偵測、依地點/裝置的 adaptive authentication）並套用 MFA 或封鎖該次登入——它評分的是單一驗證事件的帳號接管/憑證填充風險，而非端點層級的原始 HTTP 請求或 bot 流量型態，也沒有類似 WAF Bot Control 的機器人偵測或速率限制能力。B（僅限已驗證使用者存取）自相矛盾，因為正被 bot 攻擊的端點（登入、註冊）本質上就必須接受未驗證請求。D（用 CloudWatch 監控）只是可觀測性，不會阻擋任何請求。因此正確答案是 C；題庫給的 A 把「憑證風險評分」與「bot／請求層級阻擋」混為一談。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"Cognito threat protection (advanced security) does per-sign-in risk scoring — compromised-credentials detection and adaptive authentication based on location/device — driving block/MFA decisions on individual authentication events. It does not inspect or rate-limit raw HTTP traffic at the endpoint level and has no bot-detection engine, so it cannot address a volumetric bot-traffic problem the way an AWS WAF web ACL (with Bot Control) does.","why_zh":"Cognito threat protection（advanced security）是對「單一登入事件」做風險評分——外洩憑證偵測、依地點/裝置的 adaptive authentication——並依此決定封鎖或要求 MFA。它不會檢查或限速端點層級的原始 HTTP 流量，也沒有機器人偵測引擎，因此無法像搭配 Bot Control 的 AWS WAF web ACL 那樣處理大量 bot 流量問題。"},{"letter":"B","why_en":"Sign-in and sign-up endpoints must by nature accept unauthenticated requests — that is how a new or not-yet-signed-in user reaches Cognito. Restricting the user pool to 'authenticated users only' would block legitimate users trying to sign in, defeating the stated goal of preserving access for them.","why_zh":"登入與註冊端點本質上必須接受未驗證的請求——這正是新使用者或尚未登入的使用者接觸 Cognito 的方式。把 user pool 限制為「僅限已驗證使用者」會連合法使用者的登入請求都一併擋下，違背題目要求保留合法使用者存取的目標。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"CloudWatch monitoring provides visibility/metrics and alarming, but on its own it does not block or filter any request; it fails the core requirement to actively block malicious bot traffic.","why_zh":"CloudWatch 監控只提供可觀測性／指標與告警，本身並不會阻擋或過濾任何請求，無法滿足「主動阻擋惡意 bot 流量」的核心要求。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/cognito/latest/developerguide/user-pool-waf.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/cognito/latest/developerguide/managing-security.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/cognito/latest/developerguide/cognito-user-pool-settings-threat-protection.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/waf/latest/developerguide/waf-bot-control.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/waf/latest/developerguide/aws-managed-rule-groups-bot.html"]}},{"id":11,"question_en":"A company uses Amazon EC2 instances to host frontend services behind an Application Load Balancer. Amazon Elastic Block Store (Amazon EBS) volumes are attached to the EC2 instances. The company uses Amazon S3 buckets to store large files for images and music. The company has implemented a security architecture on AWS to prevent, identify, and isolate potential ransomware attacks. The company now wants to further reduce risk. A security engineer must develop a disaster recovery solution that can recover to normal operations if an attacker bypasses preventive and detective controls. The solution must meet an RPO of1 hour. Which solution will meet these requirements?","question_zh":"一家公司使用 Amazon EC2 实例在 Application Load Balancer 后面托管前端服务，EC2 实例上挂载了 Amazon 弹性块存储（Amazon EBS）卷。该公司使用 Amazon S3 存储桶来保存图像和音乐等大文件。 目前，公司已在 AWS 上实施了安全架构，以预防、检测并隔离潜在的勒索软件攻击。现在，公司 希望进一步降低风险。安全工程师需要设计一个灾难恢复方案，以便在攻击者绕过预防和检测控制 措施时，能够将系统恢复到正常运行状态。该方案必须满足 1 小时的恢复点目标（RPO）。 哪种解决方案能满足这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Use AWS Backup to create backups of the EC2 instances and S3 buckets every hour. Create AWS CloudFormation templates that replicate existing architecture components. Use a Git repository to store the CloudFormation templates alongside application configuration code.","B":"Use AWS Backup to create backups of the EBS volumes and S3 objects every day. Use Amazon Security Lake to create a centralized data lake for AWS CloudTrail logs and VPC flow logs. Use the logs for automated response.","C":"Use Amazon Security Lake to create a centralized data lake for AWS CloudTrail logs and VPC flow logs. Use the logs for automated response. Enable AWS Security Hub to establish a single location for recovery procedures. Create AWS CloudFormation templates that replicate existing architecture components. Use a Git repository to store the CloudFormation templates alongside application configuration code.","D":"Create EBS snapshots every 4 hours. Enable Amazon GuardDuty Malware Protection. Create automation to immediately restore the most recent snapshot for any EC2 instances that produce an Execution:EC2/MaliciousFile finding in GuardDuty."},"options_zh":{"A":"使用 AWS Backup 每小时对 EC2 实例和 S3 存储桶创建备份。创建 AWS CloudFormation 模板以 复制现有的架构组件，并使用 Git 仓库将 CloudFormation 模板与应用程序配置代码一同存储。","B":"每天使用 AWS Backup 对 EBS 卷和 S3 对象创建备份。使用 Amazon Security Lake 为 AWS CloudTrail 日志和 VPC 流日志创建集中式数据湖，并利用这些日志实现自动化响应。","C":"使用 Amazon Security Lake 创建用于 AWS CloudTrail 日志和 VPC 流日志的集中式数据湖，并 利用这些日志实现自动化响应。启用 AWS Security Hub，以建立统一的恢复流程管理位置。 创建可复制现有架构组件的 AWS CloudFormation 模板，并使用 Git 仓库将 CloudFormation 模板与应用程序配置代码一同存储。","D":"每4小时创建一次EBS快照。启用Amazon GuardDuty恶意软件防护功能。设置自动化流程， 当任何EC2实例在GuardDuty中产生“执行：EC2/恶意文件”告警时，立即恢复最新的快 照。"},"answer":["A"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Networking/DNS","Disaster Recovery/HA","Security/IAM","Storage","Compute","Monitoring/Ops","Analytics"],"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選","research":{"verdict":["A"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"The scenario asks for a disaster-recovery (last-resort) solution that restores normal operations even if an attacker bypasses every preventive and detective control, with an RPO of 1 hour. Because the attacker is assumed to have gotten past detective controls, the recovery mechanism itself must not depend on a detection event firing — it must be an independent, schedule-driven backup/rebuild capability. AWS Backup natively supports both Amazon EC2 instances (which includes their attached EBS volumes) and Amazon S3 buckets as protected resource types (docs.aws.amazon.com/aws-backup/latest/devguide/backup-feature-availability.html, working-with-supported-services.html, s3-backups.html). Backup rule frequency in a backup plan can be set to 'every hour' from the console, or even more finely via a cron expression, and the AWS Backup CLI can schedule snapshot backups as frequently as hourly (docs.aws.amazon.com/aws-backup/latest/devguide/plan-options-and-configuration.html) — so hourly AWS Backup jobs directly satisfy the 1-hour RPO for all in-scope data (EC2/EBS and S3). Combining this with AWS CloudFormation templates that replicate the existing architecture, version-controlled in Git alongside application configuration, lets the team redeploy the entire known-good environment from code and restore data from the most recent (≤1-hour-old) recovery points — a complete, detection-independent recovery path. Option B backs up only once per day, giving a 24-hour RPO (fails the 1-hour requirement), and pairs it with Security Lake, which is a detective/analytics capability, not a recovery mechanism. Option C has no backup or snapshot mechanism at all — Security Lake and Security Hub are detective/governance tools and CloudFormation alone can rebuild infrastructure but cannot recover lost data, so it cannot meet any RPO. Option D takes EBS snapshots only every 4 hours (a 4-hour RPO, failing the 1-hour bar) and covers only EBS, not the S3 objects in scope; worse, its 'automation' to restore is triggered by a GuardDuty Execution:EC2/MaliciousFile finding (docs.aws.amazon.com/guardduty/latest/ug/findings-malware-protection.html) — exactly the kind of detective control the question says the attacker may have bypassed, so it is not a reliable last-line-of-defense recovery plan, and restoring the 'most recent' snapshot could reintroduce already-compromised data if the finding fires late. Only option A meets the 1-hour RPO across all in-scope resources with a detection-independent, schedule-based recovery design.","explanation_zh":"題目要求的是「即使攻擊者繞過所有預防與偵測控制，仍能恢復正常營運」的災難復原（最後防線）方案，且 RPO 為 1 小時。既然假設攻擊者已繞過偵測控制，復原機制本身就不能依賴某個偵測事件觸發，而必須是獨立、依排程執行的備份／重建能力。AWS Backup 原生支援 Amazon EC2 執行個體（含其掛載的 EBS 磁碟區）與 Amazon S3 儲存貯體作為受保護的資源類型（見 backup-feature-availability.html、working-with-supported-services.html、s3-backups.html）。備份計畫的備份規則頻率在主控台可設定為「每小時」，透過 cron 運算式甚至能更細緻設定，AWS Backup CLI 最短可排程到每小時執行一次快照備份（見 plan-options-and-configuration.html）——因此每小時執行的 AWS Backup 工作可直接滿足範圍內所有資料（EC2/EBS 與 S3）的 1 小時 RPO。再搭配複製現有架構的 AWS CloudFormation 範本、與應用程式設定一起以 Git 做版本控管，團隊便能以程式碼重新部署整個已知良好的環境，並從最近（不超過 1 小時前）的復原點還原資料——形成一條完全不依賴偵測的完整復原路徑。選項 B 每天只備份一次，RPO 為 24 小時（不符 1 小時要求），且搭配的 Security Lake 屬於偵測／分析能力而非復原機制。選項 C 完全沒有任何備份或快照機制——Security Lake 與 Security Hub 屬偵測／治理工具，單靠 CloudFormation 只能重建基礎設施，無法救回遺失的資料，因此無法滿足任何 RPO。選項 D 每 4 小時才做一次 EBS 快照（RPO 為 4 小時，不符 1 小時門檻），且只涵蓋 EBS、未涵蓋範圍內的 S3 物件；更嚴重的是，其還原「自動化」是由 GuardDuty 的 Execution:EC2/MaliciousFile 偵測發現（見 findings-malware-protection.html）觸發——這正是題目假設攻擊者可能已繞過的偵測控制類型，因此不是可靠的最後防線復原計畫，且若發現觸發得太晚，還原「最新」快照也可能重新引入已受感染的資料。只有選項 A 能以不依賴偵測、依排程執行的復原設計，對範圍內所有資源都滿足 1 小時 RPO。","distractors":[{"letter":"B","why_en":"Daily AWS Backup jobs give a 24-hour RPO, far exceeding the required 1-hour RPO; Amazon Security Lake centralizing CloudTrail/VPC Flow Logs for automated response is a detective capability, not a data-recovery mechanism, so it cannot compensate for the insufficient backup frequency.","why_zh":"每日執行的 AWS Backup 工作 RPO 為 24 小時，遠超過所需的 1 小時 RPO；Amazon Security Lake 集中 CloudTrail／VPC Flow Logs 供自動化回應使用，屬於偵測能力而非資料復原機制，無法彌補備份頻率不足的問題。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"This option contains no backup or snapshot mechanism at all for EC2/EBS or S3 data, so it cannot meet any RPO; Security Lake and Security Hub are detective/governance tools, and CloudFormation templates alone can rebuild infrastructure but not recover the actual lost data.","why_zh":"此選項完全沒有針對 EC2/EBS 或 S3 資料的任何備份或快照機制，因此無法達成任何 RPO；Security Lake 與 Security Hub 屬於偵測／治理工具，單靠 CloudFormation 範本只能重建基礎設施，無法復原實際遺失的資料。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"EBS snapshots every 4 hours yield a 4-hour RPO (fails the 1-hour requirement) and cover only EBS volumes, not the S3 buckets in scope; the restore automation is triggered by a GuardDuty Execution:EC2/MaliciousFile finding, which is itself a detective control the question says the attacker may bypass, undermining reliability as a last-resort recovery plan, and restoring the 'most recent' snapshot risks restoring already-compromised data if detection is delayed or evaded.","why_zh":"每 4 小時拍攝一次 EBS 快照的 RPO 為 4 小時（不符 1 小時要求），且只涵蓋 EBS 磁碟區、未涵蓋範圍內的 S3 儲存貯體；還原自動化是由 GuardDuty 的 Execution:EC2/MaliciousFile 發現觸發，而這本身正是題目假設攻擊者可能繞過的偵測控制，作為最後防線的復原計畫並不可靠，且若偵測延遲或被規避，還原「最新」快照也可能連同已受感染的資料一併還原。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/aws-backup/latest/devguide/backup-feature-availability.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/aws-backup/latest/devguide/working-with-supported-services.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/aws-backup/latest/devguide/s3-backups.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/aws-backup/latest/devguide/creating-a-backup.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/aws-backup/latest/devguide/plan-options-and-configuration.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/guardduty/latest/ug/findings-malware-protection.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/managedservices/latest/userguide/ams-disaster-recovery.html"]}},{"id":12,"question_en":"A security team manages a company’s AWS Key Management Service (AWS KMS) customer managed keys. Only members of the security team can administer the KMS keys. The company ' s application team has a software process that needs temporary access to the keys occasionally. The security team needs to provide the application team ' s software process with access to the keys. Which solution will meet these requirements with the LEAST operational overhead?","question_zh":"安全团队负责管理公司 AWS 密钥管理服务（AWS KMS）中的客户托管密钥。只有安全团队成员才 能管理这些 KMS 密钥。公司的应用团队有一个软件流程，偶尔需要临时访问这些密钥。安全团队需 要为应用团队的软件流程提供密钥访问权限。 哪种解决方案能在最少的操作开销下满足这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Export the KMS key material to an on-premises hardware security module (HSM). Give the application team access to the key material.","B":"Edit the key policy that grants the security team access to the KMS keys by adding the application team as principals. Revert this change when the application team no longer needs access.","C":"Create a key grant to allow the application team to use the KMS keys. Revoke the grant when the application team no longer needs access.","D":"Create a new KMS key by generating key material on premises. Import the key material to AWS KMS whenever the application team needs access. Grant the application team permissions to use the key."},"options_zh":{"A":"将KMS密钥材料导出到本地硬件安全模块（HSM），并授予应用团队访问该密钥材料的权限。","B":"编辑授予安全团队访问KMS密钥权限的关键策略，将应用团队添加为授权主体。当应用团队不 再需要访问权限时，撤销此更改。","C":"创建一个密钥授权，允许应用团队使用KMS密钥。当应用团队不再需要访问权限时，撤销 该授权。","D":"在本地生成密钥材料，创建新的KMS密钥。当应用团队需要访问时，将密钥材料导入AWS KMS，并授予应用团队使用该密钥的权限。"},"answer":["C"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Security/IAM"],"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選","research":{"verdict":["C"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"The requirement is temporary, occasional access to KMS keys with the LEAST operational overhead. AWS KMS grants are purpose-built for exactly this scenario. The AWS KMS Developer Guide states directly: \"Grants are often used for temporary permissions because you can create one, use its permissions, and delete it without changing your key policies or IAM policies.\" The security team can create a grant scoping the application team's process to only the cryptographic operations it needs (e.g., Encrypt, Decrypt, GenerateDataKey), and later retire or revoke that grant when access is no longer needed — all without ever touching the key policy that only the security team manages. This is a self-service, API-driven, reversible mechanism with minimal ongoing administration. Option B works but requires the security team to manually edit and then revert a security-critical key policy document every time access is needed, which is more error-prone and higher-overhead than creating/revoking a grant. Option A is not even feasible: AWS KMS never allows customer managed key material to be exported (there is no export API for KMS key material), so handing key material to an on-premises HSM is impossible. Option D describes the BYOK (import key material) workflow, which is a heavyweight process (generate material on-premises, wrap and import it, track expiration) meant for key origin/control requirements — not for granting temporary access — and repeating the import cycle whenever access is needed is the opposite of low overhead.","explanation_zh":"需求是以「最少維運負擔（LEAST operational overhead）」提供對 KMS keys 的暫時性、偶發存取。AWS KMS 的 grant 機制正是為此設計：KMS 開發者指南明確指出「Grants are often used for temporary permissions because you can create one, use its permissions, and delete it without changing your key policies or IAM policies.」安全團隊可以建立一個 grant，僅授予應用團隊流程所需的加解密操作（例如 Encrypt、Decrypt、GenerateDataKey），用畢後再 retire 或 revoke 該 grant，全程不需碰觸僅由安全團隊管理的 key policy。這是一種可透過 API 自助操作、可逆、維運負擔極低的機制。選項 B 雖然技術上可行，但每次需要存取時都得手動編輯再還原這份安全關鍵的 key policy 文件，比建立／撤銷 grant 更容易出錯、負擔更高。選項 A 根本不可行：AWS KMS 從不允許匯出 customer managed key 的金鑰材料（KMS 沒有金鑰材料匯出 API），因此無法把金鑰材料交給地端 HSM。選項 D 描述的是 BYOK（匯入金鑰材料）流程，這是為金鑰來源／控制權需求設計的重量級流程（需在地端產生材料、包裝並匯入、管理到期時間），並非用來授予暫時存取，而且每次要存取就重複匯入循環，正好與「低維運負擔」背道而馳。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"AWS KMS never permits exporting the key material of a standard customer managed key (there is no such export operation); handing raw key material to the application team would also break the security boundary the security team is meant to maintain.","why_zh":"AWS KMS 從不允許匯出標準 customer managed key 的金鑰材料（沒有這樣的匯出操作）；把原始金鑰材料交給應用團隊也會破壞安全團隊原本應維持的安全邊界。"},{"letter":"B","why_en":"Adding and later removing the application team as principals in the key policy works, but it requires manual edits to a sensitive, security-critical document each time access is needed and reverted — higher operational overhead and risk than issuing/revoking a scoped grant.","why_zh":"在 key policy 中加入應用團隊為 principal、事後再移除的做法可行，但每次都要手動修改這份敏感且安全關鍵的文件，維運負擔與風險都高於發放／撤銷範圍受限的 grant。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"Creating a key with imported (BYOK) key material and re-importing it whenever access is needed is a heavy, manual process aimed at controlling key origin/lifecycle, not at granting temporary access — it adds far more operational overhead than a grant.","why_zh":"建立使用匯入（BYOK）金鑰材料的金鑰，並在每次需要存取時重新匯入，是針對金鑰來源／生命週期控制設計的繁重手動流程，並非用來授予暫時存取，其維運負擔遠高於使用 grant。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/kms/latest/developerguide/grants.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/kms/latest/developerguide/grant-manage.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/kms/latest/developerguide/importing-keys.html"]}},{"id":13,"question_en":"A company’s security policy requires all Amazon EC2 instances to use the Amazon Time Sync Service. AWS CloudTrail trails are enabled in all of the company’s AWS accounts. VPC Flow Logs are enabled for all VPCs. A security engineer must identify any EC2 instances that attempt to use Network Time Protocol (NTP) servers on the internet. Which solution will meet these requirements?","question_zh":"公司的安全策略要求所有 Amazon EC2 实例必须使用 Amazon 时间同步服务。AWS CloudTrail 跟踪已 在公司所有的 AWS 账户中启用，且所有 VPC 均已启用 VPC 流日志。 安全工程师必须识别任何尝试使用互联网上网络时间协议（NTP）服务器的EC2实例。 哪种解决方案能满足这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Monitor CloudTrail logs for API calls to non-standard time servers.","B":"Monitor CloudTrail logs for API calls to the Amazon Time Sync Service.","C":"Monitor VPC Flow Logs for traffic to non-standard time servers.","D":"Monitor VPC Flow Logs for traffic to the Amazon Time Sync Service."},"options_zh":{"A":"监控 CloudTrail 日志中对非标准时间服务器的 API 调用。","B":"监控 CloudTrail 日志中对 Amazon 时间同步服务的 API 调用。","C":"监控VPC流量日志，以检测流向非标准时间服务器的流量。","D":"监控 VPC 流日志，以检测流向 Amazon 时间同步服务的流量。"},"answer":["C"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Compute","Monitoring/Ops"],"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選","research":{"verdict":["C"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"NTP is plain network traffic over UDP port 123, not an AWS API call, so CloudTrail (which records API activity) can never reveal which time server an instance talks to — options A and B are irrelevant to the requirement. VPC Flow Logs capture IP traffic to and from instance network interfaces, so filtering flow log records for UDP port 123 traffic whose destination is an internet (non-standard) time server directly identifies instances violating the policy. Option D fails for a documented reason: the Amazon Time Sync Service is reached at the link-local address 169.254.169.123 (or via the instance's local endpoint), and AWS explicitly lists 'traffic to and from 169.254.169.123 for the Amazon Time Sync Service' as traffic that VPC Flow Logs do NOT capture. Therefore the only workable detection is monitoring VPC Flow Logs for traffic to non-standard time servers (C).","explanation_zh":"NTP 是走 UDP 123 埠的純網路流量，不是 AWS API 呼叫，因此記錄 API 活動的 CloudTrail 無法看出執行個體連到哪個時間伺服器——選項 A、B 與需求無關。VPC Flow Logs 會擷取進出執行個體網路介面的 IP 流量，因此過濾流向網際網路（非標準）時間伺服器的 UDP 123 流量，就能直接找出違反政策的執行個體。選項 D 有官方文件明載的致命傷：Amazon Time Sync Service 使用 link-local 位址 169.254.169.123，而 AWS 明確列出「往返 169.254.169.123 的 Amazon Time Sync Service 流量」屬於 VPC Flow Logs 不會記錄的流量類型。因此唯一可行的偵測方式是監控 VPC Flow Logs 中流向非標準時間伺服器的流量（C）。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"CloudTrail records AWS API calls only; an instance syncing time with an internet NTP server generates no API call, so nothing would appear in CloudTrail.","why_zh":"CloudTrail 只記錄 AWS API 呼叫；執行個體與網際網路 NTP 伺服器對時不會產生任何 API 呼叫，CloudTrail 裡不會有紀錄。"},{"letter":"B","why_en":"Using the Amazon Time Sync Service is also plain NTP traffic (to 169.254.169.123), not an API call, so CloudTrail contains no such events — and monitoring compliant usage would not identify violators anyway.","why_zh":"使用 Amazon Time Sync Service 同樣是純 NTP 流量（連到 169.254.169.123），不是 API 呼叫，CloudTrail 不會有相關事件；而且監控合規行為也無法找出違規者。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"VPC Flow Logs explicitly do not capture traffic to/from 169.254.169.123 (Amazon Time Sync Service), so there is nothing to monitor; and even if visible, watching compliant traffic would not reveal instances using internet NTP servers.","why_zh":"官方文件明載 VPC Flow Logs 不會擷取往返 169.254.169.123（Amazon Time Sync Service）的流量，根本無資料可監控；即使看得到，監控合規流量也無法找出使用網際網路 NTP 的執行個體。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/vpc/latest/userguide/flow-logs-limitations.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AWSEC2/latest/UserGuide/set-time.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/awscloudtrail/latest/userguide/cloudtrail-user-guide.html"]}},{"id":14,"question_en":"A company hosts its public website on Amazon EC2 instances behind an Application Load Balancer (ALB). The website is experiencing a global DDoS attack by a specific IoT device brand that has a unique user agent. A security engineer is creating an AWS WAF web ACL and will associate the web ACL with the ALB. The security engineer must implement a rule statement as part of the web ACL to block the requests. The rule statement must mitigate the current attack and future attacks from these IoT devices without blocking requests from customers. Which rule statement will meet these requirements?","question_zh":"一家公司将其公共网站托管在 Amazon EC2 实例上，并置于应用负载均衡器（ALB）之后。该网站正 遭受某个特定物联网设备品牌发起的全球性 DDoS 攻击，该品牌具有唯一的用户代理标识。 安全工程师正在创建一个 AWS WAF 网站访问控制列表（web ACL），并将其与应用负载均衡器 （ALB）关联。该安全工程师必须在 web ACL 中实现一条规则语句，以阻止相关请求。该规则语句 需能够缓解当前及未来来自这些物联网设备的攻击，同时不阻断客户正常的请求。 哪条规则语句能满足这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Use an IP set match rule statement that includes the IP address for IoT devices from the user agent.","B":"Use a geographic match rule statement. Configure the statement to block countries that the IoT devices are located in.","C":"Use a rate-based rule statement. Set a rate limit that is equal to the number of requests that are coming from the IoT devices.","D":"Use a string match rule statement that includes details of the IoT device brand from the user agent."},"options_zh":{"A":"使用包含用户代理中物联网设备IP地址的IP集合匹配规则语句。","B":"使用地理匹配规则语句。配置该语句以阻止物联网设备所在国家的访问。","C":"使用基于速率的规则语句。设置一个等于物联网设备请求数量的速率限制。","D":"使用包含用户代理中物联网设备品牌详细信息的字符串匹配规则语句。"},"answer":["D"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Networking/DNS","Security/IAM","Compute"],"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選","research":{"verdict":["D"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"The attack traffic is uniquely identifiable by a distinctive User-Agent string tied to one IoT device brand, not by IP, geography, or volume. AWS WAF's string match (byte match) rule statement is built for exactly this: the official documentation states you can search \"as an exact match for the request's User-agent header,\" and the statement lets you choose a match condition (exactly matches, starts with, ends with, contains string/word) plus a Block action. Because the rule keys on the device brand's user-agent value rather than on network-layer attributes, it mitigates the current attack and any future traffic from the same IoT devices worldwide, while leaving legitimate customer requests (which carry different user agents) untouched. This matches ByteMatchStatement in the WAF API. The other three options either cannot target the identifying attribute or would collaterally block legitimate customers.","explanation_zh":"攻擊流量的可識別特徵是某 IoT 裝置品牌獨有的 User-Agent 字串,而非 IP、地理位置或流量大小。AWS WAF 的 string match（byte match）rule statement 正是為此設計:官方文件明確指出可「exact match for the request's User-agent header」,此 statement 可選擇比對條件（exactly matches、starts with、ends with、contains string/word）並搭配 Block action。由於規則是鎖定該裝置品牌的 user-agent 值,而非網路層屬性,因此能同時緩解目前攻擊,也能防範未來這些 IoT 裝置從全球各地發起的攻擊,同時不影響帶有不同 user agent 的合法客戶請求。此對應 WAF API 中的 ByteMatchStatement。其餘三個選項都無法鎖定此識別特徵,或會誤傷合法客戶。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"An IP set match statement matches source IP addresses/CIDR ranges. A user agent is an HTTP header, not an IP address; globally distributed IoT devices behind a DDoS attack constantly rotate/expand IPs, so an IP set requires perpetual manual updates and cannot reliably mitigate future attacks, while also risking collateral blocking of legitimate customers sharing those IP ranges (e.g., NAT/CGNAT/ISP-shared IPs).","why_zh":"IP set match statement 比對的是來源 IP 位址／CIDR 範圍。User agent 是 HTTP header,不是 IP;全球分散發動 DDoS 的 IoT 裝置 IP 會不斷變動或擴增,IP set 需要持續手動更新,無法可靠防範未來攻擊,還可能誤擋共用同一 IP 範圍（如 NAT／CGNAT／ISP 共用 IP）的合法客戶。"},{"letter":"B","why_en":"A geographic match statement blocks traffic by the request's country of origin. The attack is described as global, so blocking on geography would require blocking many/all countries where the IoT devices are located — which would also block legitimate customers in those same countries, directly violating the requirement to not block customer requests.","why_zh":"Geographic match statement 依請求來源國家封鎖流量。題目描述攻擊是全球性的,若依地理位置封鎖,就需封鎖 IoT 裝置所在的多個（甚至全部）國家,連帶會封鎖同一國家的合法客戶,直接違反「不得封鎖客戶請求」的要求。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"A rate-based rule statement aggregates and counts requests (by default per client IP) and rate-limits when a threshold is exceeded within a rolling evaluation window — it keys on request volume/rate, not on device identity. Setting the limit \"equal to the number of requests coming from the IoT devices\" is an arbitrary, hard-to-tune threshold: distributed low-and-slow IoT traffic could stay under it and evade blocking, while legitimate high-traffic customers sharing IPs (e.g., behind NAT) could be throttled — it does not specifically target the identifying user-agent attribute.","why_zh":"Rate-based rule statement 是依滾動評估視窗內的請求量／速率（預設以每個來源 IP 聚合）計數並限流,鎖定的是流量速率而非裝置身分。把上限設為「IoT 裝置的請求數量」是武斷且難以調校的門檻:分散且低速的 IoT 流量可能低於門檻而躲過封鎖,而共用 IP（如 NAT 後）的高流量合法客戶反而可能被限流——它並未針對識別特徵 user agent 本身進行比對。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/waf/latest/developerguide/waf-rule-statement-type-string-match.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/waf/latest/developerguide/waf-rule-statement-type-ipset-match.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/waf/latest/developerguide/waf-rule-statement-type-geo-match.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/waf/latest/developerguide/waf-rule-statement-type-rate-based.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/waf/latest/APIReference/API_ByteMatchStatement.html"]}},{"id":15,"question_en":"An ecommerce website was down for 1 hour following a DDoS attack. Users were unable to connect to the website during the attack period. The ecommerce company ' s security team is worried about future potential attacks and wants to prepare for such events. The company needs to minimize downtime in its response to similar attacks in the future. Which steps would help achieve this? (Select TWO.)","question_zh":"一家电子商务网站在遭受DDoS攻击后中断了1小时，用户在攻击期间无法访问该网站。该公司安全 团队担心未来可能再次遭遇此类攻击，希望提前做好应对准备。公司需要在未来类似攻击发生时尽 量减少停机时间。 哪些步骤有助于实现这一目标？","options_en":{"A":"Enable Amazon GuardDuty to automatically monitor for malicious activity and block unauthorized access.","B":"Subscribe to AWS Shield Advanced and reach out to AWS Support in the event of an attack.","C":"Use VPC Flow Logs to monitor network traffic and an AWS Lambda function to automatically block an attacker’s IP using security groups.","D":"Set up an Amazon EventBridge rule to monitor the AWS CloudTrail events in real time, use AWS Config rules to audit the configuration, and use AWS Systems Manager for remediation.","E":"Use AWS WAF to create rules to respond to such attacks."},"options_zh":{"B":"订阅 AWS Shield Advanced，并在发生攻击时联系 AWS 支持。","C":"使用 VPC 流日志监控网络流量，并通过 AWS Lambda 函数利用安全组自动阻断攻击者的 IP 地址。","D":"设置 Amazon EventBridge 规则以实时监控 AWS CloudTrail 事件，使用 AWS Config 规则进行配置审计，并使用 AWS Systems Manager 进行修复。","E":"使用 AWS WAF 创建规则以应对此类攻击。","A":"启用 Amazon GuardDuty 以自动监控恶意活动并阻止未经授权的访问。"},"answer":["B","E"],"multi":true,"vote":{},"tags":["Organizations/Governance","Security/IAM","Compute","Serverless/Integration","Monitoring/Ops"],"difficulty":2,"diff_why":"複選","research":{"verdict":["B","E"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"The goal is to minimize downtime in future DDoS attacks, which requires a service purpose-built for DDoS mitigation plus expert-backed incident response — not detection-only or config-audit tooling. AWS Shield Advanced is AWS's managed DDoS protection service; subscribers can contact the AWS Support Center (Shield Advanced customers get critical/urgent DDoS cases routed directly to DDoS experts) and escalate to the Shield Response Team (SRT) — security engineers who specialize in DDoS event response, who can analyze AWS WAF logs, apply mitigating web ACL changes (with customer approval), build custom network mitigations, and even work with AWS networking teams to reroute traffic during an active attack. This directly cuts time-to-mitigation (B). AWS WAF is the mechanism used to actually stop application-layer (layer 7) attack traffic: you (or the SRT) create rate-based rules and custom rules in a web ACL to block or throttle malicious requests, and Shield Advanced's automatic application layer DDoS mitigation feature itself operates by deploying and tuning AWS WAF rules on your behalf (E). GuardDuty (A) only produces detection findings — it has no mechanism to block traffic, so it does not reduce downtime during an attack. VPC Flow Logs plus a custom Lambda function that edits security groups (C) is a slow, DIY, reactive pipeline, and security groups only support allow rules (no explicit deny), so they cannot 'block an attacker's IP' — and this approach cannot scale to a distributed attack from many source IPs. EventBridge + CloudTrail + Config + Systems Manager (D) is a configuration-compliance and remediation pattern for API activity/resource drift, not a DDoS traffic-mitigation mechanism. Therefore B and E are the correct pair.","explanation_zh":"題目要求將未來 DDoS 攻擊造成的停機時間降到最低，這需要專為 DDoS 緩解打造的服務，再加上有專家後援的事件回應機制——而非純偵測或組態稽核工具。AWS Shield Advanced 是 AWS 的託管式 DDoS 防護服務：訂閱者可聯繫 AWS Support Center（Shield Advanced 客戶的緊急 DDoS 案件會直接轉給 DDoS 專家），並可升級至 Shield Response Team（SRT）——專精 DDoS 事件回應的安全工程師，可分析 AWS WAF 記錄、（經客戶同意後）修改 web ACL 進行緩解、建立自訂網路層緩解措施，攻擊期間甚至可與 AWS 網路團隊合作重新導向流量，直接縮短緩解時間（B）。AWS WAF 則是實際攔阻應用層（第 7 層）攻擊流量的機制：你（或 SRT）可在 web ACL 中建立 rate-based rules 與自訂規則來封鎖或限速惡意請求，Shield Advanced 的自動應用層 DDoS 緩解功能本身也是透過部署與調整 AWS WAF 規則來運作（E）。GuardDuty（A）只會產生偵測 findings，沒有封鎖流量的機制，無法在攻擊期間減少停機時間。VPC Flow Logs 加上自訂 Lambda 修改 security groups（C）是緩慢、自建、被動反應的管線，且 security groups 只支援 allow 規則（沒有明確的 deny），無法「封鎖攻擊者 IP」，也無法應付來自大量分散來源 IP 的攻擊。EventBridge + CloudTrail + Config + Systems Manager（D）是針對 API 活動／資源組態偏移的合規稽核與修復模式，並非 DDoS 流量緩解機制。因此正確答案為 B 與 E。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"GuardDuty is a threat-detection service that only generates findings from analyzed logs/events; it has no enforcement capability to block unauthorized access or DDoS traffic, so enabling it alone cannot reduce downtime during an attack.","why_zh":"GuardDuty 是威脅偵測服務，只會根據分析的日誌／事件產生 findings；它沒有封鎖未授權存取或 DDoS 流量的執行能力，單獨啟用無法在攻擊期間減少停機時間。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"Security groups are stateful, allow-only firewalls with no explicit deny rules, so a Lambda function cannot use them to 'block an attacker's IP'; a custom VPC Flow Logs + Lambda pipeline is also too slow and cannot realistically scale to block the many distributed source IPs typical of a DDoS attack.","why_zh":"Security groups 是有狀態、僅支援 allow 規則的防火牆，沒有明確的 deny 規則，Lambda 無法用它來「封鎖攻擊者 IP」；自建的 VPC Flow Logs + Lambda 管線反應也太慢，且難以應付 DDoS 攻擊中常見的大量分散來源 IP。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"EventBridge + CloudTrail + Config + Systems Manager form a configuration-drift detection and remediation workflow for API/resource activity; it addresses compliance auditing, not the mitigation of volumetric or application-layer DDoS traffic.","why_zh":"EventBridge + CloudTrail + Config + Systems Manager 是針對 API／資源活動的組態偏移偵測與修復流程，處理的是合規稽核，並非緩解大流量或應用層 DDoS 流量的機制。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/waf/latest/developerguide/ddos-srt-support.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/waf/latest/developerguide/ddos-responding-contact-support.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/waf/latest/developerguide/ddos-app-layer-rbr.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/waf/latest/developerguide/ddos-automatic-app-layer-response.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/waf/latest/developerguide/what-is-aws-waf.html"]}},{"id":16,"question_en":"A company has a large fleet of Amazon Linux 2 Amazon EC2 instances that run an application. The application processes sensitive data and has the following compliance requirements: • No remote access management ports to the EC2 instances can be exposed internally or externally. • All remote session activity must be recorded in an audit log. • All remote access to the EC2 instances must be authenticated and authorized by AWS IAM Identity Center. The company ' s DevOps team occasionally needs to connect to one of the EC2 instances to troubleshoot issues. Which solution will provide remote access to the EC2 instances while meeting the compliance requirements?","question_zh":"一家公司拥有大量运行应用程序的 Amazon Linux 2 Amazon EC2 实例。该应用程序处理敏感数据，并具有以下合规性 要求： • 任何EC2实例的远程管理端口均不得在内部或外部暴露。 • 所有远程会话活动必须记录在审计日志中。 所有对EC2实例的远程访问必须通过AWS IAM Identity Center进行身份验证和授权。 公司的 DevOps 团队偶尔需要连接到某个 EC2 实例以排查问题。 哪种解决方案可以在满足合规要求的同时，提供对EC2实例的远程访问？","options_en":{"A":"Grant access to the EC2 serial console at the account level.","B":"Enable EC2 Instance Connect and configure security group rules.","C":"Assign an EC2 instance role that allows access to AWS Systems Manager. Create an IAM policy that grants access to Systems Manager Session Manager. Assign the policy to an IAM role of the DevOps team.","D":"Use AWS Systems Manager Automation runbooks to open remote access ports."},"options_zh":{"A":"在账户级别授予访问 EC2 串行控制台的权限。","B":"启用 EC2 实例连接并配置安全组规则。","C":"分配一个允许访问 AWS Systems Manager 的 EC2 实例角色。创建一个 IAM 策略，授予对 Systems Manager Session Manager 的访问权限，并将该策略分配给 DevOps 团队的 IAM 角色。","D":"使用 AWS Systems Manager Automation 运行手册来打开远程访问端口。"},"answer":["C"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Security/IAM","Compute","Monitoring/Ops"],"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選","research":{"verdict":["C"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"both","explanation_en":"AWS Systems Manager Session Manager satisfies every requirement in the question. Per AWS docs, Session Manager 'provides secure node management without the need to open inbound ports, maintain bastion hosts, or manage SSH keys' — the SSM Agent on the instance initiates an outbound HTTPS connection to the Systems Manager service, so no inbound remote-management port (SSH/RDP) is ever exposed, internally or externally. Access control is 'centralized access control to managed nodes using IAM policies': an administrator grants ssm:StartSession (and related) permissions via an IAM policy attached to a role, and the instance needs an instance profile role with SSM permissions (e.g., AmazonSSMManagedInstanceCore) so the agent can register with the service. Because IAM Identity Center provisions its permission sets as IAM roles that users federate into, routing the DevOps team's access through an Identity Center-assigned IAM role with a Session Manager policy directly satisfies the 'authenticated and authorized by IAM Identity Center' requirement. Session logging closes the audit-log requirement: Session Manager can stream/store full session activity (commands and output) to Amazon CloudWatch Logs and/or Amazon S3, and session start/stop/termination API calls are recorded in AWS CloudTrail. This exactly matches option C's description of an instance role with Systems Manager access plus an IAM policy/role for the DevOps team granting Session Manager access. The other options each fail at least one hard requirement: the EC2 serial console (A) is a low-level, IAM Identity Center-agnostic emergency console, not routed through Identity Center and not logging session content as an audit trail; EC2 Instance Connect (B) still requires an inbound security group rule allowing SSH on TCP port 22 (either from the EC2 Instance Connect service range or the user's IP), directly violating the 'no remote access management ports exposed' requirement; and using Systems Manager Automation to open remote access ports (D) is the opposite of the required posture — it deliberately opens management ports rather than eliminating them.","explanation_zh":"AWS Systems Manager Session Manager 完全滿足題目的每一項要求。根據 AWS 官方文件，Session Manager「提供安全的節點管理，不需開放任何 inbound 連接埠、維護 bastion host 或管理 SSH 金鑰」——EC2 上的 SSM Agent 會主動對 Systems Manager 服務發起對外 HTTPS 連線，因此不論內部或外部都不需暴露任何遠端管理連接埠（SSH/RDP）。存取控制方面，Session Manager 提供「透過 IAM 政策集中管控受管節點的存取權限」：管理者透過附加於角色的 IAM 政策授予 ssm:StartSession 等權限，EC2 執行個體則需要具備 SSM 權限（如 AmazonSSMManagedInstanceCore）的執行個體設定檔角色，讓 Agent 能向服務註冊。由於 IAM Identity Center 會將其 permission set 佈建為使用者聯合登入的 IAM 角色，讓 DevOps 團隊透過 Identity Center 指派的 IAM 角色（附加 Session Manager 政策）取得存取權限，正好滿足「須經 IAM Identity Center 驗證與授權」的要求。稽核日誌要求則由 Session Manager 的工作階段記錄功能滿足：可將完整的工作階段活動（指令與輸出）串流／儲存到 Amazon CloudWatch Logs 及／或 Amazon S3，且工作階段的啟動／停止／終止 API 呼叫會記錄於 AWS CloudTrail。這正對應選項 C 所描述的「賦予 EC2 執行個體角色存取 Systems Manager 的權限，並建立授予 Session Manager 存取權的 IAM 政策給 DevOps 團隊的 IAM 角色」。其餘選項皆未能滿足至少一項硬性要求：EC2 序列主控台（A）是與 IAM Identity Center 無關的底層緊急主控台，不經過 Identity Center 授權，也不會將工作階段內容記錄為稽核日誌；EC2 Instance Connect（B）仍需在安全群組中開放 TCP 22 埠的 inbound SSH 規則（無論是給 EC2 Instance Connect 服務的 IP 範圍或使用者的 IP），直接違反「不得暴露遠端管理連接埠」的要求；而使用 Systems Manager Automation runbook 開放遠端存取連接埠（D）恰恰與要求的安全態勢相反——它是主動開啟管理連接埠，而非消除它們。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"The EC2 serial console is a low-level, out-of-band console mainly for troubleshooting boot/network misconfiguration; access is controlled at the account/instance level via IAM, but it is not integrated with IAM Identity Center per-user federation, and it does not produce a recorded audit log of session activity — only the act of enabling/using serial console access appears in CloudTrail as an API call, not the session content.","why_zh":"EC2 序列主控台是低階、頻外（out-of-band）的主控台，主要用於排除開機或網路設定問題；存取雖可透過 IAM 在帳戶/執行個體層級控管，但並未與 IAM Identity Center 的使用者聯合驗證整合，也不會產生工作階段活動的稽核記錄——CloudTrail 只會記錄啟用/使用序列主控台這個 API 呼叫本身，而非工作階段內容。"},{"letter":"B","why_en":"EC2 Instance Connect (whether the classic in-browser method or via an EC2 Instance Connect Endpoint) still relies on an underlying SSH connection, and the target instance's security group must allow inbound TCP port 22 (from the EC2 Instance Connect service IP range or the connecting principal), which directly violates the requirement that no remote access management ports be exposed internally or externally; it also lacks Session Manager-style command/output audit logging.","why_zh":"EC2 Instance Connect（無論是傳統瀏覽器方式或透過 EC2 Instance Connect Endpoint）底層仍依賴 SSH 連線，且目標執行個體的安全群組必須允許 inbound TCP 22 埠（來自 EC2 Instance Connect 服務的 IP 範圍或連線端），直接違反「內部或外部皆不得暴露遠端存取管理連接埠」的要求；它也缺乏如 Session Manager 般的指令/輸出稽核記錄功能。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"Using Systems Manager Automation runbooks to open remote access ports is the opposite of the required control: it deliberately (even if temporarily) exposes a remote-management port for direct SSH/RDP access, which violates the first compliance requirement outright, regardless of any Identity Center integration used elsewhere.","why_zh":"使用 Systems Manager Automation runbook 開放遠端存取連接埠，與要求的控管方向完全相反：它會（即便是暫時性地）主動暴露遠端管理連接埠以供直接 SSH/RDP 存取，這已直接違反第一項合規要求，無論其他環節是否整合了 Identity Center。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/systems-manager/latest/userguide/session-manager.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/systems-manager/latest/userguide/session-manager-logging.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/systems-manager/latest/userguide/session-manager-auditing.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/systems-manager/latest/userguide/getting-started-restrict-access-quickstart.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AWSEC2/latest/UserGuide/ec2-instance-connect-prerequisites.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AWSEC2/latest/UserGuide/eice-security-groups.html"]}},{"id":17,"question_en":"A company has an organization with all features enabled in AWS Organizations. In the management account, the company configures AWS IAM Identity Center for the organization in the eu-west-2 Region. The company configures IAM Identity Center with a SAML-based identity provider. The company needs to configure an AWS managed application that integrates with IAM Identity Center in a new AWS account in the us-east-1 Region. Most of the users that will authenticate to the AWS managed application are external third-party users who cannot be added to the company’s identity provider. A security engineer needs to configure authentication for the third-party users. The solution must provide isolation from the company’s identity provider. Which solution will meet these requirements?","question_zh":"一家公司使用启用了所有功能的 AWS Organizations 组织。该公司在管理账户中为位于 eu-west-2 区域的组织配置了 AWS IAM Identity Center，并使用基于 SAML 的身份提供商来设置 IAM Identity Center。 该公司需要在 us-east-1 区域的新 AWS 账户中配置一个与 IAM Identity Center 集成的 AWS 托管应用 程序。大多数将对该 AWS 托管应用程序进行身份验证的用户是外部第三方用户，无法添加到公司 的身份提供商中。 安全工程师需要为第三方用户配置身份验证。该解决方案必须与公司的身份提供商实现隔离。 哪种解决方案能满足这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Create a SAML identity provider in IAM in the management account that connects to the third-party users’ identity provider. Create IAM roles in the management account that allow access to the AWS managed application.","B":"Deploy Amazon Cognito into the new AWS account in us-east-1. Configure an identity pool for a SAML-based identity provider. Configure an IAM role that uses the sts:AssumeRole action to allow access to the AWS managed application from Amazon Cognito.","C":"Enable account instances in IAM Identity Center. Deploy an IAM Identity Center account instance in the new AWS account in us-east-1. Configure the AWS managed application to use the new instance. Configure users in the new account instance directory.","D":"Create a new identity provider for the third-party users. Configure a second identity source in IAM Identity Center in the organization’s management account to use the new identity provider. Create a new permission set that gives access to the AWS managed application in the new account."},"options_zh":{"A":"在管理账户的 IAM 中创建一个 SAML 身份提供商，用于连接第三方用户的身份提供商。在 管理账户中创建 IAM 角色，以允许访问 AWS 托管的应用程序。","B":"在 us-east-1 区域的新 AWS 账户中部署 Amazon Cognito。为基于 SAML 的身份提供商配置一 个身份池，并设置一个 IAM 角色，使用 sts:AssumeRole 操作允许从 Amazon Cognito 访问 AWS 托管应用程序。","C":"在 IAM Identity Center 中启用账户实例。在位于 us-east-1 区域的新 AWS 账户中部署 IAM Identity Center 账户实例。配置 AWS 托管应用程序以使用该新实例。在新账户实例的目录中 配置用户。","D":"为第三方用户创建一个新的身份提供商。在组织的管理账户中，于 IAM Identity Center 配置 第二个身份源以使用该新的身份提供商。创建一个新的权限集，以便在新账户中访问 AWS 托管的应用程序。"},"answer":["C"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Organizations/Governance","Security/IAM"],"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選","research":{"verdict":["C"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"Account instances of IAM Identity Center exist precisely for this scenario. AWS documentation lists as an explicit use case: 'You have an organization instance of IAM Identity Center, but you want to deploy a supported AWS managed application to an isolated set of users that are distinct from users in your organization instance.' An account instance is bound to a single AWS account and Region (so it can live in the new account in us-east-1 while the organization instance stays in eu-west-2), has its own Identity Center directory in which the third-party users can be created directly, and supports select AWS managed applications — providing complete isolation from the company's SAML identity provider and its organization-instance users. Because the organization instance was created after Nov 15, 2023 (implied by 'all features enabled' modern setup), its administrator can permit account-instance creation in member accounts; this is the 'enable account instances' step in option C. Options A and B fail because AWS managed applications that integrate with IAM Identity Center authenticate through an Identity Center instance (organization or account), not through IAM SAML federation roles/console access or Amazon Cognito identity pools, which grant AWS credentials for custom application code, not sign-in to a managed application's Identity Center-driven access portal. Option D is impossible because IAM Identity Center supports only one identity source per organization at a time ('You can have only one identity source per organization in AWS Organizations') — you cannot add a second identity source alongside the SAML IdP already configured for the organization instance — and even if it were possible, mixing the third-party users into the organization instance would violate the required isolation from the company's identity provider; account instances also do not use permission sets, so the premise of option D is doubly flawed.","explanation_zh":"IAM Identity Center 的 account instance 正是為此情境設計。AWS 文件明確列出此使用案例：「你已有 organization instance，但想將支援的 AWS managed application 部署給一組與 organization instance 使用者完全隔離的獨立使用者」。Account instance 綁定於單一 AWS 帳號與 Region（因此可建立在 us-east-1 的新帳號，而 organization instance 留在 eu-west-2），擁有自己的 Identity Center directory 可直接建立第三方使用者，並支援特定 AWS managed applications，與公司的 SAML identity provider 及 organization instance 使用者完全隔離。Organization instance 管理員可允許成員帳號建立 account instance（enable account instances），這正是選項 C 的第一步。A 與 B 不可行：與 IAM Identity Center 整合的 AWS managed application 是透過 Identity Center instance（organization 或 account）驗證，而非 IAM SAML federation role／主控台存取，也不是 Amazon Cognito identity pool（後者是核發 AWS 憑證給自訂應用程式碼用，並非登入 Identity Center 驅動的 managed application access portal）。D 不可行，因為每個 organization 的 IAM Identity Center 同時只能有一個 identity source（「You can have only one identity source per organization in AWS Organizations」），無法在已設定 SAML IdP 的 organization instance 上再加一個 identity source；即使可行，把第三方使用者混入 organization instance 也違反隔離需求，而且 account instance 本來就不支援 permission set，選項 D 的前提本身即有誤。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"IAM SAML identity providers and IAM roles federate access to the AWS Management Console/APIs via sts:AssumeRoleWithSAML; they do not provide sign-in to AWS managed applications that integrate with IAM Identity Center, and placing third-party users' access configuration in the management account is also contrary to the isolation and least-privilege intent of the requirement.","why_zh":"IAM 的 SAML identity provider 與 IAM role 是透過 sts:AssumeRoleWithSAML 聯合存取 AWS Management Console／API，無法讓使用者登入與 IAM Identity Center 整合的 AWS managed application；且把第三方使用者的存取設定放在 management account 也違反題目要求的隔離與最小權限精神。"},{"letter":"B","why_en":"Amazon Cognito identity pools exchange a SAML assertion for temporary AWS credentials so custom application code can call AWS services directly; Cognito is not a recognized identity source for IAM Identity Center and cannot drive sign-in to an Identity Center-integrated AWS managed application's access portal.","why_zh":"Amazon Cognito identity pool 是把 SAML assertion 換成臨時 AWS 憑證，供自訂應用程式碼直接呼叫 AWS 服務；Cognito 並非 IAM Identity Center 認可的 identity source，無法驅動使用者登入與 Identity Center 整合的 AWS managed application access portal。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"An IAM Identity Center instance supports only one identity source at a time per AWS documentation, so configuring a 'second identity source' on the organization instance is not possible; even hypothetically, doing so would mix third-party users into the corporate organization instance, breaking the required isolation, and account instances (the actual mechanism needed here) do not use permission sets at all.","why_zh":"依 AWS 文件，每個 IAM Identity Center instance 同時只能有一個 identity source，因此無法在 organization instance 上設定「第二個 identity source」；即便假設可行，也會把第三方使用者混入公司的 organization instance，違反題目要求的隔離，而且真正該用的 account instance 機制本來就不支援 permission set。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/singlesignon/latest/userguide/account-instances-identity-center.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/singlesignon/latest/userguide/identity-center-instances.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/singlesignon/latest/userguide/manage-your-identity-source.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/singlesignon/latest/userguide/awsapps-that-work-with-identity-center.html"]}},{"id":18,"question_en":"A company has security requirements for Amazon Aurora MySQL databases regarding encryption, deletion protection, public access, and audit logging. The company needs continuous monitoring and real-time visibility into compliance status. Which solution will meet these requirements?","question_zh":"一家公司对 Amazon Aurora MySQL 数据库在加密、删除保护、公共访问和审计日志方面有安全要 求。该公司需要持续监控并实时掌握合规状态。 哪种解决方案能满足这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Use AWS Audit Manager with a custom framework.","B":"Enable AWS Config and use managed rules to monitor Aurora MySQL compliance.","C":"Use AWS Security Hub configuration policies.","D":"Use EventBridge and Lambda with custom metrics."},"options_zh":{"A":"使用 AWS 审计管理器配合自定义框架。","B":"启用 AWS Config 并使用托管规则来监控 Aurora MySQL 的合规性。","C":"使用 AWS Security Hub 配置策略。","D":"使用 EventBridge 和 Lambda 配合自定义指标。"},"answer":["B"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Organizations/Governance","Security/IAM","Compute","Database","Serverless/Integration"],"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選","research":{"verdict":["B"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"AWS Config is the purpose-built service for continuously assessing resource configurations against desired settings and showing compliance status in near real time. There are AWS-managed Config rules covering every stated Aurora MySQL requirement: rds-storage-encrypted (encryption at rest), rds-cluster-deletion-protection-enabled / rds-instance-deletion-protection-enabled (deletion protection), rds-instance-public-access-check (public accessibility), and rds-logging-enabled (audit/log exports enabled). Config evaluates resources on configuration changes, flags them COMPLIANT/NON_COMPLIANT, and provides a live compliance dashboard — exactly the 'continuous monitoring and real-time visibility into compliance status' the question asks for, with no custom code. Audit Manager (A) automates evidence collection for audits and itself pulls findings from Config/Security Hub; it is for audit reporting, not real-time compliance monitoring. Security Hub configuration policies (C) are a central-configuration feature for enabling Security Hub standards/controls across an organization, not a monitoring mechanism for these specific database settings (and Security Hub's RDS controls are backed by Config rules anyway). EventBridge + Lambda with custom metrics (D) would work but reinvents Config with far more operational overhead.","explanation_zh":"AWS Config 正是為「持續評估資源設定是否符合期望組態，並即時呈現合規狀態」而生的服務。題目列出的每一項 Aurora MySQL 要求都有對應的 AWS 受管 Config 規則：rds-storage-encrypted（靜態加密）、rds-cluster-deletion-protection-enabled / rds-instance-deletion-protection-enabled（刪除保護）、rds-instance-public-access-check（公開存取）、rds-logging-enabled（稽核日誌）。Config 會在組態變更時觸發評估，標記 COMPLIANT/NON_COMPLIANT 並提供即時合規儀表板，完全符合「持續監控＋即時合規可見性」的需求，且無需自寫程式。Audit Manager（A）是自動蒐集稽核證據用，底層還是依賴 Config/Security Hub 的資料，屬稽核報告而非即時監控。Security Hub configuration policies（C）是用來在組織內集中啟用 Security Hub 標準/控制項的設定功能，本身不是針對這些資料庫設定的監控機制（Security Hub 的 RDS 控制項底層也是 Config 規則）。EventBridge + Lambda 自訂指標（D）雖可行，但等於重造 Config，維運負擔最大。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"Audit Manager automates evidence collection and report assembly for audits; it is not a real-time compliance monitoring tool and largely sources its evidence from AWS Config and Security Hub. A custom framework adds work without providing the continuous resource-level evaluation Config gives natively.","why_zh":"Audit Manager 用於自動蒐集稽核證據與產出稽核報告，並非即時合規監控工具，其證據來源大多還是 AWS Config 與 Security Hub。自訂框架只是增加工作量，無法取代 Config 原生的持續資源評估。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"Security Hub configuration policies are used with central configuration to enable/disable Security Hub, standards, and controls across an organization — they configure Security Hub itself, they are not a mechanism to monitor specific Aurora settings; the underlying RDS checks are AWS Config rules anyway.","why_zh":"Security Hub configuration policies 是搭配 central configuration，用來在組織內集中啟用/停用 Security Hub、標準與控制項——它設定的是 Security Hub 本身，並非監控特定 Aurora 設定的機制；其底層 RDS 檢查本來就是 AWS Config 規則。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"EventBridge + Lambda with custom metrics could be built to detect these settings, but it is custom code that reimplements what AWS Config managed rules already provide out of the box, with far more operational overhead and no built-in compliance dashboard.","why_zh":"EventBridge + Lambda 自訂指標雖然做得到，但等於自寫程式重造 AWS Config 受管規則現成的功能，維運負擔遠高於 Config，且沒有內建的合規儀表板。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/config/latest/developerguide/rds-storage-encrypted.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/config/latest/developerguide/rds-cluster-deletion-protection-enabled.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/config/latest/developerguide/rds-instance-public-access-check.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/config/latest/developerguide/rds-logging-enabled.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/config/latest/developerguide/evaluate-config.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/audit-manager/latest/userguide/what-is.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/securityhub/latest/userguide/central-configuration-intro.html"]}},{"id":19,"question_en":"A company runs critical workloads in an on-premises data center. The company wants to implement an AWS based disaster recovery (DR) solution that will achieve an RTO of less than 1 hour. The company needs to continuously replicate physical and virtual servers. The company must optimize costs for data storage and bandwidth usage. The DR solution must be automated. Which solution will meet these requirements?","question_zh":"一家公司在本地数据中心运行关键业务负载。该公司希望实施基于 AWS 的灾难恢复（DR）解决方 案，以实现少于 1 小时的恢复时间目标（RTO）。公司需要持续复制物理和虚拟服务器，并且必须 优化数据存储和带宽使用的成本。灾难恢复解决方案必须实现自动化。 哪种解决方案能满足这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Use AWS Backup to directly replicate the on-premises servers to AWS. Enable cross-Region backup copying and data vaulting. Configure recovery points to match the defined RTO. Use AWS Step Functions to automate recovery steps.","B":"Configure an AWS Storage Gateway Volume Gateway to use Amazon Elastic Block Store (Amazon EBS) snapshots for recovery. Configure AWS Backup to manage the snapshots. Create automated recovery procedures.","C":"Enable AWS Elastic Disaster Recovery. Configure replication agents to continuously replicate each on- premises server. Enable the default staging area subnet configuration.","D":"Create an AWS Direct Connect connection between the on-premises data center and AWS. Configure Amazon EventBridge to monitor for failures and to invoke AWS Lambda functions that launch preconfigured Amazon EC2 instances from AMIs in the event of an incident."},"options_zh":{"A":"使用 AWS Backup 将本地服务器直接复制到 AWS，启用跨区域备份复制和数据归档功能。配 置恢复点以满足定义的 RTO 要求，并使用 AWS Step Functions 自动化恢复步骤。","B":"配置 AWS 存储网关卷网关，使用 Amazon 弹性块存储（Amazon EBS）快照进行恢复。配置 AWS Backup 来管理这些快照，并创建自动化的恢复流程。","C":"启用 AWS 弹性灾难恢复。配置复制代理，持续复制每台本地服务器。启用默认的暂存区域子网 配置。","D":"在本地数据中心与 AWS 之间创建 AWS Direct Connect 连接。配置 Amazon EventBridge 以监 控故障，并在发生事件时调用 AWS Lambda 函数，从预配置的 AMI 启动预先设置好的 Amazon EC2 实例。"},"answer":["C"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Networking/DNS","Disaster Recovery/HA","Storage","Compute","Cost Optimization","Serverless/Integration"],"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選","research":{"verdict":["C"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"both","explanation_en":"AWS Elastic Disaster Recovery (DRS) is purpose-built for exactly this scenario: it uses lightweight replication agents to perform continuous block-level replication of on-premises physical and virtual servers into a low-cost staging area subnet in your AWS account. The official AWS documentation states this design 'reduces costs by using affordable storage and minimal compute resources to maintain ongoing replication,' directly satisfying the cost-optimization requirement for storage and bandwidth. When a disaster occurs, DRS automatically converts servers to boot natively on AWS and lets you 'launch recovery instances on AWS within minutes,' easily meeting an RTO of under 1 hour, and the entire replication/conversion/launch workflow is automated by the managed service (configured and monitored via the console). Option A is wrong because AWS Backup is a point-in-time backup service, not continuous replication, and it cannot directly replicate arbitrary on-premises physical servers. Option B (Storage Gateway Volume Gateway + EBS snapshots) protects storage volumes via periodic snapshots, not whole-server continuous replication, and cannot reliably recover an entire physical/virtual server within the RTO. Option D is a costly custom build (Direct Connect plus EventBridge/Lambda launching pre-built AMIs) that provides no continuous data replication—AMIs would go stale—so it fails both the RPO/RTO and cost requirements, and it is not a managed automated DR solution.","explanation_zh":"AWS Elastic Disaster Recovery (DRS) 正是為此情境設計：透過輕量 replication agent 對地端實體與虛擬伺服器進行持續的區塊層級複寫，資料寫入你 AWS 帳戶中低成本的 staging area subnet。AWS 官方文件明確指出此設計「使用低價儲存與最少的運算資源維持持續複寫以降低成本」，直接滿足儲存與頻寬成本最佳化需求。災難發生時，DRS 會自動將伺服器轉換為可在 AWS 原生開機，並可「在數分鐘內於 AWS 上啟動 recovery instance」，輕鬆達成 RTO 小於 1 小時，且整個複寫／轉換／啟動流程都由受管服務自動化處理（透過主控台設定與監控）。選項 A 錯誤：AWS Backup 是時間點備份服務，非持續複寫，也無法直接複寫任意地端實體伺服器。選項 B（Storage Gateway Volume Gateway 加 EBS snapshot）只透過週期性 snapshot 保護儲存磁碟區，並非整台伺服器的持續複寫，無法在 RTO 內可靠復原整台實體/虛擬伺服器。選項 D 是昂貴的自建方案（Direct Connect 加 EventBridge/Lambda 啟動預建 AMI），沒有持續資料複寫——AMI 會過時——同時不符 RPO/RTO 與成本要求，也不是受管的自動化 DR 解決方案。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"AWS Backup is a point-in-time backup service, not continuous replication; it cannot 'directly replicate' arbitrary on-premises physical/virtual servers, and restoring from backups plus Step Functions orchestration is slower and more complex than DRS's built-in recovery.","why_zh":"AWS Backup 是時間點備份服務而非持續複寫；它無法「直接複寫」任意地端實體/虛擬伺服器，從備份還原再加上 Step Functions 編排也比 DRS 內建復原更慢、更複雜。"},{"letter":"B","why_en":"Storage Gateway Volume Gateway protects storage volumes only, not entire servers (OS, applications, configuration); EBS snapshots are periodic, not continuous replication, so it cannot recover whole physical/virtual servers within the RTO.","why_zh":"Storage Gateway Volume Gateway 只保護儲存磁碟區，不含整台伺服器（作業系統、應用程式、設定）；EBS snapshot 是週期性而非持續複寫，無法在 RTO 內復原整台實體/虛擬伺服器。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"Direct Connect plus EventBridge/Lambda launching pre-built AMIs provides no continuous data replication—AMIs go stale, causing large data loss—and Direct Connect is expensive, contradicting the cost-optimization requirement; it is also a fragile custom build rather than a managed automated DR solution.","why_zh":"Direct Connect 加 EventBridge/Lambda 啟動預建 AMI 沒有持續資料複寫——AMI 會過時導致大量資料遺失——且 Direct Connect 昂貴，違背成本最佳化要求；這也是脆弱的自建方案，而非受管的自動化 DR 解決方案。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/drs/latest/userguide/what-is-drs.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/drs/latest/userguide/Network-diagrams.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/drs/latest/userguide/agent-installation.html"]}},{"id":20,"question_en":"An AWS Lambda function was misused to alter data, and a security engineer must identify who invoked the function and what output was produced. The engineer cannot find any logs created by the Lambda function in Amazon CloudWatch Logs. Which of the following explains why the logs are not available?","question_zh":"一个AWS Lambda函数被滥用以篡改数据，安全工程师需要确定是谁调用了该函数以及产生了什么输 出。但工程师在Amazon CloudWatch Logs中找不到任何由Lambda函数生成的日志。 以下哪一项解释了日志不可用的原因？","options_en":{"A":"The execution role for the Lambda function did not grant permissions to write log data to CloudWatch Logs.","B":"The Lambda function was invoked by using Amazon API Gateway, so the logs are not stored in CloudWatch Logs.","C":"The execution role for the Lambda function did not grant permissions to write to the Amazon S3 bucket where CloudWatch Logs stores the logs.","D":"The version of the Lambda function that was invoked was not current."},"options_zh":{"A":"Lambda 函数的执行角色未授予将日志数据写入 CloudWatch Logs 的权限。","B":"该 Lambda 函数是通过 Amazon API Gateway 调用的，因此日志未存储在 CloudWatch Logs 中。","C":"Lambda 函数的执行角色未被授予向 CloudWatch Logs 存储日志的 Amazon S3 存储桶写入权限。","D":"被调用的 Lambda 函数版本不是最新的。"},"answer":["A"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Storage","Compute","Serverless/Integration","Monitoring/Ops"],"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選","research":{"verdict":["A"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"AWS Lambda documentation states that Lambda automatically captures invocation logs and sends them to CloudWatch Logs \"provided your function's execution role has the necessary permissions\": logs:CreateLogGroup, logs:CreateLogStream, and logs:PutLogEvents, normally granted via the AWSLambdaBasicExecutionRole managed policy. If the execution role lacks these permissions, Lambda cannot create the /aws/lambda/<function-name> log group or log stream and no log events are written at all — which is exactly the symptom described (no logs found anywhere in CloudWatch Logs for the function). This is the single most common root cause of \"missing Lambda logs\" and is documented as a prerequisite, not an optional add-on. The distractors describe mechanisms that don't exist or don't affect logging: invoking via API Gateway does not redirect or suppress the function's own CloudWatch logs; CloudWatch Logs is a fully managed service and never stores log data in a customer S3 bucket (exporting logs to S3 is a separate, opt-in subscription-filter feature, not the default log destination); and invoking a non-current version/alias still logs to the same function log group, so version currency is irrelevant to whether logs exist.","explanation_zh":"AWS Lambda 官方文件明確指出，Lambda 只有在函數的 execution role 具備必要權限時，才會自動把呼叫日誌送到 CloudWatch Logs，所需權限為 logs:CreateLogGroup、logs:CreateLogStream、logs:PutLogEvents，通常透過 AWSLambdaBasicExecutionRole 受管政策授予。若 execution role 缺少這些權限，Lambda 就無法建立 /aws/lambda/<function-name> 的 log group 或 log stream，也完全不會寫入任何日誌事件——這正好對應題目描述的症狀（在 CloudWatch Logs 中完全找不到該函數的日誌）。這是「Lambda 日誌遺失」最常見、文件中明訂為前提條件（而非選用項目）的根本原因。其餘選項描述的機制不是不存在、就是與日誌無關：透過 API Gateway 呼叫不會改變或抑制函數自身的 CloudWatch 日誌；CloudWatch Logs 是全受管服務，從不會把日誌資料存到客戶的 S3 bucket（把日誌匯出到 S3 是另一項需另外設定的 subscription-filter 選用功能，不是預設的日誌目的地）；呼叫非最新版本或 alias 仍會寫入同一個函數的 log group，因此版本是否最新與日誌是否存在無關。","distractors":[{"letter":"B","why_en":"Invoking a Lambda function through API Gateway does not change the logging destination; the function's own execution logs still go to CloudWatch Logs at /aws/lambda/<function-name> as long as the execution role permits it. (API Gateway has its own separate access-logging feature, but that does not explain missing Lambda function logs.)","why_zh":"透過 API Gateway 呼叫 Lambda 不會改變日誌目的地；只要 execution role 有權限，函數本身的執行日誌仍會寫入 CloudWatch Logs 的 /aws/lambda/<function-name>。（API Gateway 有自己獨立的存取日誌功能，但這無法解釋 Lambda 函數日誌遺失的問題。）"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"CloudWatch Logs is its own managed storage service and does not store Lambda logs in a customer-owned S3 bucket by default; exporting logs to S3 requires an explicit, separately configured subscription filter, so S3 write permissions are irrelevant to whether Lambda logs appear in CloudWatch Logs.","why_zh":"CloudWatch Logs 是自有的受管儲存服務，預設不會把 Lambda 日誌存到客戶的 S3 bucket；要把日誌匯出到 S3 需要另外明確設定 subscription filter，因此 S3 寫入權限與 Lambda 日誌是否出現在 CloudWatch Logs 無關。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"Every invoked version or alias of a Lambda function logs to the same /aws/lambda/<function-name> log group; invoking an older (non-current) version still produces CloudWatch logs, so version currency does not explain missing logs.","why_zh":"Lambda 函數的任何版本或 alias 被呼叫時，都會寫入同一個 /aws/lambda/<function-name> log group；呼叫舊版（非最新）版本仍會產生 CloudWatch 日誌，因此版本是否為最新無法解釋日誌遺失。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/lambda/latest/dg/monitoring-cloudwatchlogs.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/lambda/latest/dg/security-iam-awsmanpol.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/lambda/latest/dg/lambda-intro-execution-role.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/lambda/latest/dg/logging-with-s3.html"]}},{"id":21,"question_en":"A company wants to use a suite of AWS Lambda functions to automatically remediate noncompliant resources. The company packages the suite of Lambda functions into an AWS CloudFormation template. The company wants to deploy the suite of Lambda functions to all AWS Organizations accounts. However, the company cannot use the Organizations management account for deployment. Which solution provides centralized deployment of the Lambda function suite to all accounts in the organization?","question_zh":"一家公司希望使用一组 AWS Lambda 函数来自动修复不符合合规要求的资源。该公司将这组 Lambda 函数打包成一个 AWS CloudFormation 模板，并希望将其部署到所有 AWS Organizations 账户中。但 该公司无法使用 Organizations 的管理账户进行部署。 哪种解决方案可将Lambda函数套件集中部署到组织中的所有账户？","options_en":{"A":"Register a delegated administrator for CloudFormation. Deploy the template to every account in the organization by using StackSets.","B":"Create a cross-account IAM role with a unique external ID in each AWS account. Assume the cross- account role to deploy the template.","C":"Package the template as an AWS Service Catalog product. Log in to each account and provision the product to each account.","D":"Set up AWS CodePipeline in each account. Configure a pipeline to pull the template from an Amazon S3 bucket in the Organizations management account."},"options_zh":{"A":"为 CloudFormation 注册一个委派管理员。使用 StackSets 将模板部署到组织中的每个账户。","B":"在每个 AWS 账户中创建一个带有唯一外部 ID 的跨账户 IAM 角色，并通过假设该跨账户角 色来部署模板。","C":"将模板打包为 AWS 服务目录产品。登录每个账户，并在每个账户中部署该产品。","D":"在每个账户中设置 AWS CodePipeline，并配置一个管道，从 Organizations 管理账户中的 Amazon S3 存储桶拉取模板。"},"answer":["A"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Organizations/Governance","Security/IAM","Storage","Compute","Monitoring/Ops"],"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選","research":{"verdict":["A"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"The requirement is centralized deployment of a CloudFormation template to ALL accounts in the organization, without using the Organizations management account for the deployment itself. AWS CloudFormation StackSets with service-managed permissions integrates directly with AWS Organizations, and AWS explicitly documents that member accounts can be registered as delegated administrators: 'In addition to your organization's management account, member accounts with delegated administrator permissions can create and manage StackSets with service-managed permissions for the organization,' and 'Delegated administrators can choose to deploy to all accounts in your organization or specific OUs.' Once registered, the delegated administrator (a non-management member account) creates and operates the StackSet, which CloudFormation automatically deploys — and keeps deployed to new accounts — across the whole organization from that single account. This is a single, centralized, org-integrated mechanism operated from outside the management account, exactly matching the question's constraints. Option A is therefore correct.","explanation_zh":"題目要求在「部署本身不使用 Organizations management account」的前提下，將 CloudFormation 範本集中部署到組織內所有帳號。AWS CloudFormation StackSets（service-managed permissions）與 AWS Organizations 直接整合，且官方文件明確支援將成員帳號註冊為 delegated administrator：「除了 management account 之外，具 delegated administrator 權限的成員帳號也能為組織建立與管理 service-managed StackSets」，並且「delegated administrator 可選擇部署到組織內所有帳號或特定 OU」。註冊完成後，該 delegated administrator（非 management account 的成員帳號）即可建立並操作 StackSet，CloudFormation 會自動將其部署（並持續涵蓋新帳號）到整個組織——這是從 management account 之外、單一集中且與 Organizations 整合的部署機制，完全符合題目限制，故 A 正確。","distractors":[{"letter":"B","why_en":"Assuming a manually-created cross-account role in every account is the self-managed StackSets permission model at best, or a fully manual pattern at worst: it requires per-account role setup, repeated per-account deployments, and has no automatic coverage of new accounts joining the organization. It is not a single centralized org-wide mechanism, and the external ID detail (meant for third-party confused-deputy scenarios) adds nothing here.","why_zh":"在每個帳號手動建立並 assume cross-account role，充其量只是 StackSets 的 self-managed 權限模型，甚至是純手動做法：需逐帳號建立角色、逐帳號重複部署，且新加入組織的帳號不會自動涵蓋。這並非單一、集中且與組織整合的機制；external ID（用於第三方 confused-deputy 情境）在此也無實質意義。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"Logging in to each account and provisioning an AWS Service Catalog product manually is the direct opposite of centralized deployment — it does not scale, requires per-account human action, and has no organization-wide automatic rollout.","why_zh":"登入每個帳號並手動 provision AWS Service Catalog 產品，正好與「集中部署」相反——無法規模化、需逐帳號人工操作，也沒有組織層級的自動佈署。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"Setting up AWS CodePipeline separately in each account is decentralized per-account infrastructure that must be built and maintained account-by-account. It also has the pipeline pull the template from an S3 bucket in the Organizations management account, which conflicts with the requirement that deployment not use the management account.","why_zh":"在每個帳號各自建立 AWS CodePipeline 屬於去中心化的逐帳號基礎設施，需要逐一建置與維護；且此方案讓 pipeline 從 management account 的 S3 bucket 拉取範本，與「部署不得使用 management account」的限制相衝突。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AWSCloudFormation/latest/UserGuide/stacksets-orgs-delegated-admin.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AWSCloudFormation/latest/UserGuide/stacksets-orgs-activate-trusted-access.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AWSCloudFormation/latest/UserGuide/stacksets-orgs-associate-stackset-with-org.html"]}},{"id":22,"question_en":"A company needs to build a code-signing solution using an AWS KMS asymmetric key and must store immutable evidence of key creation and usage for compliance and audit purposes. Which solution meets these requirements?","question_zh":"一家公司需要使用 AWS KMS 的非对称密钥构建代码签名解决方案，并且必须存储密钥创建和使用的不可篡改证据，以 满足合规性和审计要求。 哪种解决方案符合这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Create an Amazon S3 bucket with S3 Object Lock enabled. Create an AWS CloudTrail trail with log file validation enabled for KMS events. Store logs in the bucket and grant auditors access.","C":"Capture KMS API calls using EventBridge and store them in DynamoDB.","D":"Track KMS usage with CloudWatch metrics and dashboards.","B":"Log application events to Amazon CloudWatch Logs and export them."},"options_zh":{"A":"创建一个启用S3对象锁定功能的Amazon S3存储桶。创建一个启用日志文件验证功能的AWS CloudTrail追踪，用于KMS 事件。将日志存储在该存储桶中，并授予审计人员访问权限。","B":"将应用程序事件记录到 Amazon CloudWatch Logs 并导出。","C":"使用 EventBridge 捕获 KMS API 调用并将其存储在 DynamoDB 中。","D":"使用 CloudWatch 指标和仪表板跟踪 KMS 的使用情况。"},"answer":["A"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Security/IAM","Storage","Database","Serverless/Integration","Monitoring/Ops"],"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選","research":{"verdict":["A"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"AWS KMS is fully integrated with AWS CloudTrail: every KMS API call — including CreateKey (evidence of key creation) and Sign/Verify (evidence of asymmetric-key usage during code signing) — is recorded as a CloudTrail event with caller identity, timestamp, and request parameters (docs.aws.amazon.com/kms/latest/developerguide/logging-using-cloudtrail.html). To turn that record into immutable, audit-grade evidence, two complementary controls apply: (1) CloudTrail log file integrity validation, which hashes each delivered log file with SHA-256 and signs hourly digest files with SHA-256-with-RSA, making it 'computationally infeasible to modify, delete, or forge CloudTrail log files without detection' (docs.aws.amazon.com/awscloudtrail/latest/userguide/cloudtrail-log-file-validation-intro.html); and (2) S3 Object Lock, which enforces WORM storage on the destination bucket so the log/digest objects cannot be overwritten or deleted before the retention period expires (docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonS3/latest/userguide/object-lock.html). Together these give both cryptographic proof of integrity and physical immutability — exactly the compliance/audit requirement in the question. None of the other options provide both a complete, authoritative event record and immutability.","explanation_zh":"AWS KMS 與 AWS CloudTrail 完整整合：每一次 KMS API 呼叫——包括 CreateKey（金鑰建立的證據）與 Sign/Verify（程式碼簽章時使用非對稱金鑰的證據）——都會被記錄為 CloudTrail 事件，內含呼叫者身分、時間戳與請求參數（docs.aws.amazon.com/kms/latest/developerguide/logging-using-cloudtrail.html）。要把這份紀錄變成不可竄改的稽核級證據，需搭配兩項互補控制：(1) CloudTrail log file integrity validation——對每個交付的日誌檔以 SHA-256 雜湊，並以 SHA-256-with-RSA 對每小時的 digest file 簽章，使得「在不被偵測的情況下修改、刪除或偽造 CloudTrail 日誌檔在運算上不可行」（docs.aws.amazon.com/awscloudtrail/latest/userguide/cloudtrail-log-file-validation-intro.html）；(2) S3 Object Lock——對目的地儲存桶啟用 WORM（一寫多讀）儲存，使日誌／digest 物件在保留期內無法被覆寫或刪除（docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonS3/latest/userguide/object-lock.html）。兩者合一，同時提供加密完整性證明與實體不可變性，正好滿足題目要求的合規／稽核證據。其餘選項都無法同時提供完整、權威的事件紀錄與不可變性。","distractors":[{"letter":"C","why_en":"EventBridge can react to KMS events sourced from CloudTrail, but writing them into DynamoDB gives no immutability — items can be updated or deleted via normal API calls or IAM-permitted access — and there is no cryptographic integrity validation of the stored records, so it fails the 'immutable evidence' requirement.","why_zh":"EventBridge 可以對來自 CloudTrail 的 KMS 事件做出反應，但寫入 DynamoDB 不具不可變性——項目可透過一般 API 呼叫或具權限的存取被更新或刪除——且沒有對儲存紀錄做加密完整性驗證，無法滿足『不可變證據』的要求。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"CloudWatch metrics are aggregated numeric time-series data points (e.g., call counts), not individual event records; they cannot show who created or used a specific key, with what parameters, and provide no immutability guarantee at all.","why_zh":"CloudWatch metrics 是彙總後的數值時間序列資料（例如呼叫次數），並非個別事件紀錄；無法顯示是誰、以何種參數建立或使用了特定金鑰，也完全沒有不可變性保證。"},{"letter":"B","why_en":"Application-level logging to CloudWatch Logs only captures whatever the application chooses to emit, not the authoritative KMS control-plane/data-plane record that CloudTrail provides; CloudWatch Logs entries (exported or not) can be deleted and have no built-in log file integrity validation mechanism.","why_zh":"把應用程式事件記錄到 CloudWatch Logs，只能取得應用程式自行選擇輸出的內容，並非 CloudTrail 提供的權威 KMS 控制層／資料層紀錄；CloudWatch Logs 項目（無論是否匯出）可被刪除，也沒有內建的日誌檔完整性驗證機制。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/kms/latest/developerguide/logging-using-cloudtrail.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/awscloudtrail/latest/userguide/cloudtrail-log-file-validation-intro.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonS3/latest/userguide/object-lock.html"]}},{"id":23,"question_en":"A company has hundreds of AWS accounts in an organization in AWS Organizations. The company operates out of a single AWS Region. The company has a dedicated security tooling AWS account in the organization. The security tooling account is configured as the organization ' s delegated administrator for Amazon GuardDuty and AWS Security Hub. The company has configured the environment to automatically enable GuardDuty and Security Hub for existing AWS accounts and new AWS accounts. The company is performing control tests on specific GuardDuty findings to make sure that the company ' s security team can detect and respond to security events. The security team launched an Amazon EC2 instance and attempted to run DNS requests against a test domain,example.com, to generate a DNS finding. However, the GuardDuty finding was never created in the Security Hub delegated administrator account. Why was the finding not created in the Security Hub delegated administrator account?","question_zh":"一家公司在 AWS Organizations 中拥有数百个 AWS 账户，且所有业务均在一个 AWS 区域内运行。 该公司在组织中设有专门用于安全工具的 AWS 账户，并将该账户配置为组织在 Amazon GuardDuty 和 AWS Security Hub 方面的委托管理员。公司已将环境设置为自动为现有和新创建的 AWS 账户启 用 GuardDuty 和 Security Hub。 该公司正在对特定的 GuardDuty 检测结果执行控制测试，以确保其安全团队能够检测并响应安全事 件。安全团队启动了一个 Amazon EC2 实例，并尝试向测试域名 example.com 发送 DNS 请求，以生 成一条 DNS 检测记录。然而，该 GuardDuty 检测结果从未在 Security Hub 的委派管理员账户中创建。 为什么该发现结果未在安全中心的委派管理员账户中创建？","options_en":{"A":"VPC flow logs were not turned on for the VPC where the EC2 instance was launched.","B":"The VPC where the EC2 instance was launched had the DHCP option configured for a custom OpenDNS resolver.","C":"The GuardDuty integration with Security Hub was never activated in the AWS account where the finding was generated.","D":"Cross-Region aggregation in Security Hub was not configured."},"options_zh":{"A":"启动 EC2 实例的 VPC 未启用 VPC 流日志。","B":"启动EC2实例的VPC配置了自定义OpenDNS解析器的DHCP选项。","C":"生成该发现的AWS账户中从未启用GuardDuty与Security Hub的集成。","D":"安全中心未配置跨区域聚合。"},"answer":["B"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Networking/DNS","Organizations/Governance","Security/IAM","Compute"],"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選","research":{"verdict":["B"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"GuardDuty's DNS-based findings are generated from Route 53 Resolver DNS query logs, and GuardDuty can only access these logs when EC2 instances use the AWS-provided DNS resolvers (the default AmazonProvidedDNS setting). The GuardDuty foundational data sources documentation states this explicitly: 'If you use AWS DNS resolvers for your Amazon EC2 instances (the default setting), then GuardDuty can access and process your request and response Route53 Resolver DNS query logs through the internal AWS DNS resolvers. If you use another DNS resolver, such as OpenDNS or GoogleDNS, or if you set up your own DNS resolvers, then GuardDuty cannot access and process data from this data source.' Because the VPC's DHCP option set pointed instances at a custom OpenDNS resolver, the test DNS queries to example.com bypassed the internal AWS DNS resolvers entirely, so GuardDuty never generated the DNS finding — and with no finding generated, there was nothing to forward to the Security Hub delegated administrator account. The other options do not explain the missing finding: (A) GuardDuty consumes VPC Flow Logs through an independent, duplicated stream and does not require the customer to enable VPC Flow Logs — this data source is also unrelated to DNS-based findings; (C) the GuardDuty-to-Security Hub integration is enabled automatically whenever both services are enabled (which the scenario confirms via org-wide auto-enable), so a broken integration is not the cause; (D) the company operates in a single AWS Region, so cross-Region aggregation in Security Hub is irrelevant — the finding would surface in the home Region if it had ever been generated.","explanation_zh":"GuardDuty 的 DNS 類 findings 是由 Route 53 Resolver DNS query logs 產生，而 GuardDuty 只有在 EC2 執行個體使用 AWS 提供的 DNS 解析器（預設的 AmazonProvidedDNS 設定）時才能存取這些日誌。GuardDuty foundational data sources 文件明確指出：『If you use AWS DNS resolvers for your Amazon EC2 instances (the default setting), then GuardDuty can access and process your request and response Route53 Resolver DNS query logs through the internal AWS DNS resolvers. If you use another DNS resolver, such as OpenDNS or GoogleDNS, or if you set up your own DNS resolvers, then GuardDuty cannot access and process data from this data source.』由於該 VPC 的 DHCP option set 指向自訂的 OpenDNS 解析器，對 example.com 的測試 DNS 查詢完全繞過了 AWS 內部 DNS 解析器，因此 GuardDuty 從未產生該 DNS finding；既然沒有 finding 產生，自然也就沒有東西可以轉發到 Security Hub 委派管理員帳戶。其他選項都無法解釋 finding 消失的原因：(A) GuardDuty 透過獨立且複製的資料串流取用 VPC Flow Logs，客戶不需自行啟用 Flow Logs，而且此資料來源與 DNS 類 findings 無關；(C) 只要 GuardDuty 與 Security Hub 都啟用，兩者的整合就會自動開啟（本題情境中組織已全面 auto-enable），因此整合未啟用並非根因；(D) 公司僅在單一 AWS Region 營運，Security Hub 的跨 Region 彙總與此無關——若 finding 真的產生，也會出現在該 home Region 中。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"GuardDuty consumes VPC Flow Logs through an independent, duplicated stream — customers do not need to enable VPC Flow Logs for GuardDuty to analyze traffic. More importantly, DNS-based findings come from Route 53 Resolver DNS query logs, not flow logs, so this option does not address the actual failure mode.","why_zh":"GuardDuty 透過獨立複製的資料串流取用 VPC Flow Logs，客戶不需自行開啟 Flow Logs，GuardDuty 就能分析流量。更重要的是，DNS 類 findings 是由 Route 53 Resolver DNS query logs 產生，與 flow logs 無關，因此此選項並未點出真正的故障原因。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"AWS documentation states that when both GuardDuty and Security Hub are enabled, the GuardDuty-to-Security Hub integration is enabled automatically and findings are sent immediately. Since the org already auto-enables both services for member accounts, the integration was active; the root cause is that no GuardDuty finding was ever generated in the first place.","why_zh":"AWS 文件指出，只要 GuardDuty 與 Security Hub 都啟用，GuardDuty 與 Security Hub 的整合就會自動開啟並立即傳送 findings。由於組織已對成員帳戶全面 auto-enable 兩項服務，整合本身是啟用的；真正的根因是 GuardDuty 根本沒有產生該 finding。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"Cross-Region aggregation only affects whether findings generated in linked Regions are replicated to a home Region. The company operates in a single Region, so this setting is irrelevant — and even without it, a finding generated in that Region would still appear there.","why_zh":"跨 Region 彙總只影響已連結 Region 中產生的 findings 是否被複製到 home Region。公司只在單一 Region 營運，此設定與本題無關；即使沒有設定，該 Region 產生的 finding 仍會顯示在該 Region 中。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/guardduty/latest/ug/guardduty_data-sources.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/guardduty/latest/ug/securityhub-integration.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/securityhub/latest/userguide/finding-aggregation.html"]}},{"id":24,"question_en":"A company uses an organization in AWS Organizations to manage its 250 member accounts. The company also uses AWS IAM Identity Center with a SAML external identity provider (IdP). IAM Identity Center has been delegated to a member account. The company ' s security team has access to the delegated account. The security team has been investigating a malicious internal user who might be accessing sensitive accounts. The security team needs to know when the user logged into the organization during the last 7 days. Which solution will quickly identify the access attempts?","question_zh":"一家公司使用 AWS Organizations 中的组织来管理其 250 个成员账户。该公司还使用 AWS IAM Identity Center，并配置了 SAML 外部身份提供商（IdP）。IAM Identity Center 已被委派给一个成员 账户，公司的安全团队有权访问该委派账户。 安全团队正在调查一名可能访问敏感账户的恶意内部用户。安全团队需要了解该用户在过去7天内登 录组织的时间。 哪种解决方案能快速识别访问尝试？","options_en":{"A":"In the delegated account, use Amazon CloudWatch Logs to search for events that match the user details for all successful attempts.","B":"In each member account, use the IAM Identity Center console to search for events that match the user details for all attempts.","C":"In the external IdP, use Amazon EventBridge to search for events that match the user details for all attempts.","D":"In the organization ' s management account, use AWS CloudTrail to search for events that match the user details for all successful attempts."},"options_zh":{"A":"在委托账户中，使用 Amazon CloudWatch Logs 搜索与所有成功尝试的用户信息相匹配的事件。","B":"在每个成员账户中，使用 IAM Identity Center 控制台搜索与所有尝试的用户信息相匹配的事件。","C":"在外部身份提供商中，使用 Amazon EventBridge 搜索与所有尝试的用户信息相匹配的事件。","D":"在组织的管理账户中，使用 AWS CloudTrail 搜索与所有成功尝试的用户信息相匹配的事件。"},"answer":["D"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Organizations/Governance","Security/IAM","Serverless/Integration","Monitoring/Ops"],"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選","research":{"verdict":["D"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"IAM Identity Center emits sign-in activity as CloudTrail events, and the definitive \"user logged in\" event is UserAuthentication — it is only logged once a user has completed every required credential check, so a successful sign-in is unambiguous in the log. AWS documentation confirms that for the federated sign-in flow (an external SAML IdP, as used here), IAM Identity Center 'doesn't invoke the internal MFA authentication sequence... because an external, federated identity provider is responsible for all user credential authentication' — meaning the CredentialChallenge/CredentialVerification events that native or AD-sourced sign-ins generate for failed attempts don't apply here, so the meaningful, searchable signal for this scenario is the successful UserAuthentication event, exactly as option D frames it ('all successful attempts'). Crucially, these events are recorded in the AWS account where the IAM Identity Center action actually occurs, and per AWS docs an organization instance of IAM Identity Center is always enabled in, and remains bound to, the AWS Organizations management account; registering a member account as delegated administrator only grants that account's admins permission to perform IAM Identity Center administrative tasks (such as assigning users/groups to accounts), it does not relocate the instance, its identity store, or its CloudTrail footprint. So even though the security team's day-to-day access is in the delegated account, the sign-in events they need live in the management account's CloudTrail Event history — which requires no setup, retains 90 days of management events by default, and is searchable by the 'User name' lookup attribute — making a management-account CloudTrail search the fastest way to answer 'when did this user log in during the last 7 days.'","explanation_zh":"IAM Identity Center 的登入活動會以 CloudTrail 事件記錄，其中真正代表「使用者已登入」的關鍵事件是 UserAuthentication——只有在使用者完成所有必要的憑證驗證後才會記錄此事件，因此成功登入在日誌中是明確可辨的。AWS 官方文件證實，在使用外部 SAML IdP 的聯合登入（federated sign-in）流程中，IAM Identity Center「不會執行內部 MFA 驗證流程……因為外部聯合身分提供者負責所有使用者憑證驗證」——也就是說，原生使用者或 AD 來源登入失敗時會產生的 CredentialChallenge／CredentialVerification 事件在此情境下並不適用，因此此情境下真正有意義、可搜尋的訊號就是成功的 UserAuthentication 事件，這正好對應選項 D 所描述的「所有成功嘗試（all successful attempts）」。更關鍵的是，這些事件記錄在 IAM Identity Center 動作實際發生的那個 AWS 帳戶中；根據 AWS 文件，IAM Identity Center 的 organization instance 永遠是在 AWS Organizations 的 management account 中啟用並歸屬於該帳戶——將某個成員帳戶註冊為 delegated administrator，只是授予該帳戶的管理者執行 IAM Identity Center 管理工作（例如指派使用者／群組給各帳戶）的權限，並不會把 instance、其身分存放區或其 CloudTrail 記錄搬到別的帳戶。因此，儘管security team日常存取的是委派帳戶，他們需要的登入事件其實存在於 management account 的 CloudTrail Event history 中——這無需任何事前設定、預設保留 90 天的管理事件，並可用「User name」這個 lookup 屬性搜尋——所以在 management account 中搜尋 CloudTrail 是回答「此使用者過去 7 天何時登入」最快的方法。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"This gets the right idea (search for successful sign-in events) but the wrong location and wrong service: IAM Identity Center doesn't stream sign-in activity to CloudWatch Logs on its own (that requires an explicitly configured CloudTrail trail with a CloudWatch Logs integration), and even if it did, the sign-in events are generated in the management account where the organization instance lives — not in the delegated administrator account — so searching CloudWatch Logs in the delegated account would find nothing.","why_zh":"這個選項方向正確（要找成功登入事件），但服務和帳戶位置都錯了：IAM Identity Center 本身不會自動把登入活動串流到 CloudWatch Logs（那需要額外設定帶有 CloudWatch Logs 整合的 CloudTrail trail）；而且就算設定了，登入事件也是在 organization instance 所在的 management account 產生，而不是在 delegated administrator account——因此在委派帳戶的 CloudWatch Logs 中搜尋不會有結果。"},{"letter":"B","why_en":"An IAM Identity Center organization instance lives in one account (the management account); ordinary member accounts don't each have their own Identity Center console with sign-in event search. Even if something were visible per account, manually checking 250 member accounts is neither quick nor how AWS designed centralized IAM Identity Center auditing to work.","why_zh":"IAM Identity Center 的 organization instance 只存在於一個帳戶（management account）；一般成員帳戶並沒有各自的 Identity Center 主控台可搜尋登入事件。就算真的每個帳戶都能看到東西，逐一檢查 250 個成員帳戶既不快速，也不是 AWS 設計集中式 IAM Identity Center 稽核的方式。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"EventBridge is an AWS service, not a capability of the external IdP, so 'in the external IdP, use EventBridge' doesn't correspond to any real architecture. EventBridge is also built for near-real-time event routing/matching as events occur, not for retroactively searching 7 days of historical sign-in activity.","why_zh":"Amazon EventBridge 是 AWS 的服務，並非外部 IdP 本身具備的功能，所以「在外部 IdP 中使用 EventBridge」並不對應任何真實架構。EventBridge 設計用於即時事件路由／比對，而非回溯搜尋過去 7 天的歷史登入活動。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/singlesignon/latest/userguide/understanding-sign-in-events.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/singlesignon/latest/userguide/sso-info-in-cloudtrail.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/singlesignon/latest/userguide/identity-center-instances.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/singlesignon/latest/userguide/delegated-admin-how-to-register.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/awscloudtrail/latest/userguide/view-cloudtrail-events.html"]}},{"id":25,"question_en":"A company is using AWS Organizations with the default SCP. The company needs to restrict AWS usage for all AWS accounts that are in a specific OU. Except for some desired global services, the AWS usage must occur only in theeu-west-1Region for all accounts in the OU. A security engineer must create an SCP that applies the restriction to existing accounts and any new accounts in the OU. Which SCP will meet these requirements?","question_zh":"一家公司正在使用带有默认服务控制策略（SCP）的 AWS Organizations。该公司需要限制特定组织单元（OU）内所有 AWS 账 户的 AWS 使用权限，除了一些指定的全局服务外，该 OU 内所有账户的 AWS 使用必须仅限于 eu-west-1 区域。安全工程师必 须创建一个 SCP，以对现有账户以及该 OU 中未来创建的新账户应用此限制。 哪个SCP能满足这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Deny with NotAction, but uses StringEquals for aws:RequestedRegion = eu-west-1","B":"Allow with Action, scoped to desired global services in eu-west-1","C":"Deny with NotAction for desired global services, and StringNotEquals aws:RequestedRegion = eu-west- 1","D":"Allow with NotAction and StringNotEquals aws:RequestedRegion = eu-west-1"},"options_zh":{"A":"使用 NotAction 拒绝，但对 aws:RequestedRegion = eu-west-1 使用 StringEquals","B":"允许操作，作用范围限定为 eu-west-1 区域中的指定全局服务","C":"对所需的全局服务使用 NotAction 拒绝，并且 StringNotEquals aws:RequestedRegion = eu-west-1","D":"允许，条件为 NotAction 且 StringNotEquals aws:RequestedRegion = eu-west-1"},"answer":["C"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Organizations/Governance"],"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選","research":{"verdict":["C"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"both","explanation_en":"The requirement — restrict all AWS usage to eu-west-1 except a short list of exempted global services, applied uniformly to existing and future accounts in an OU — matches AWS's published 'DenyAllOutsideRequestedRegions' pattern exactly: a Deny-effect statement using NotAction to list the exempted global-service actions (e.g., cloudfront:*, iam:*, organizations:*, route53:*, support:*), combined with a Condition of StringNotEquals on aws:RequestedRegion set to eu-west-1. This denies every action not in the exemption list whenever the request targets any Region other than eu-west-1 — exactly option C. Because it is a Deny, AWS Organizations' SCP evaluation model guarantees enforcement across the whole subtree: a Deny attached at the OU applies to every account under that OU, present and future, and it works alongside the default FullAWSAccess policy (no need to replace it). AWS Control Tower's 'Region deny' guardrail (AWS-GR_REGION_DENY / CT.MULTISERVICE.PV.1) and the IAM documentation's own example use this identical Deny + NotAction + StringNotEquals construction. Options A, B, and D fail on logic, not on syntax: contrary to the first-pass reasoning, the AWS Organizations SCP syntax reference explicitly lists Condition and NotAction as supported for BOTH Allow and Deny effects, so an Allow statement CAN legally carry NotAction/Condition — the reason those options are wrong is what they compute, not that they are malformed. Option A inverts the Region test (StringEquals blocks the wanted Region and leaves every other Region open). Per the SCP evaluation model, a permission is allowed only if every SCP along the account's path in the hierarchy explicitly allows it, so an Allow-only SCP behaves as an allow-list: option B's Allow scoped only to the global services in eu-west-1 would permit just those calls and implicitly leave everything else denied everywhere, including ordinary (non-global) service usage inside eu-west-1 itself — far more restrictive than required. Option D's Allow with NotAction plus StringNotEquals aws:RequestedRegion=eu-west-1 grants the non-global actions specifically when the Region is NOT eu-west-1 (and grants nothing for eu-west-1), the exact inverse of the desired outcome — it would authorize usage outside eu-west-1 while leaving eu-west-1 itself without a matching Allow.","explanation_zh":"需求是：把所有 AWS 用量限制在 eu-west-1，只豁免少數 global services，且要同時套用到 OU 內現有及未來的所有帳號——這正好對應 AWS 官方發布的 'DenyAllOutsideRequestedRegions' 樣式：Deny 效果的陳述式用 NotAction 列出豁免的 global service 動作（例如 cloudfront:*、iam:*、organizations:*、route53:*、support:*），搭配 Condition 的 StringNotEquals 比對 aws:RequestedRegion 是否等於 eu-west-1。只要請求鎖定的 Region 不是 eu-west-1，任何不在豁免清單內的動作都會被拒絕——正是選項 C。由於這是 Deny，AWS Organizations 的 SCP 評估模型能保證整個子樹都受管：掛在 OU 上的 Deny 會套用到該 OU 下現有與未來的每一個帳號，且可與預設的 FullAWSAccess policy 並存（不需替換它）。AWS Control Tower 的 'Region deny' 護欄（AWS-GR_REGION_DENY / CT.MULTISERVICE.PV.1）以及 IAM 官方文件本身的範例都採用同樣的 Deny + NotAction + StringNotEquals 結構。選項 A、B、D 的問題出在邏輯，而非語法：與第一輪分析不同，AWS Organizations 的 SCP 語法參考文件明確列出 Condition 與 NotAction 對 Allow 與 Deny 兩種效果都支援，所以 Allow 陳述式合法地可以帶 NotAction/Condition——這幾個選項錯的原因是它們算出來的結果不對，而不是寫法不合法。選項 A 把 Region 判斷反過來了：StringEquals 會封鎖想要的 Region，其餘 Region 反而不受限。依照 SCP 評估模型，某個權限要被允許，必須是帳號階層路徑上『每一個』SCP 都明確允許，所以只有 Allow 陳述式的 SCP 其實是一種允許清單（allow-list）：選項 B 的 Allow 只涵蓋 eu-west-1 的 global services，結果只有那些呼叫被允許，其餘所有動作在所有地方（包含 eu-west-1 內部一般服務的用量）都會被隱含拒絕——比需求嚴格太多。選項 D 的 Allow 搭配 NotAction 及 StringNotEquals aws:RequestedRegion=eu-west-1，恰好在 Region『不是』eu-west-1 時才授予非 global service 的動作（而 eu-west-1 本身完全沒有對應的 Allow），邏輯正好相反——會變成允許在 eu-west-1 以外使用，卻讓 eu-west-1 本身無權可用。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"StringEquals aws:RequestedRegion = eu-west-1 inverts the intended logic: the Deny fires only when the request IS in eu-west-1, so it blocks the desired Region and leaves all other Regions unrestricted — the opposite of a single-Region restriction.","why_zh":"StringEquals aws:RequestedRegion = eu-west-1 把邏輯反過來了：Deny 只在請求位於 eu-west-1 時才生效，反而封鎖了想用的 Region，其他 Region 卻完全不受限——與『只限單一 Region』的需求相反。"},{"letter":"B","why_en":"An Allow SCP scoped only to Action = the global services in eu-west-1 acts as an allow-list under the SCP intersection model: it permits just those global-service calls and implicitly denies everything else everywhere, including ordinary (non-global) service usage inside eu-west-1 — far more restrictive than the requirement, which needs general usage to work fine in eu-west-1.","why_zh":"把 Action 只限定在 eu-west-1 的 global services 的 Allow SCP，在 SCP 交集模型下會變成允許清單：只允許那些 global service 呼叫，其餘所有動作在所有地方（包含 eu-west-1 內部的一般服務用量）都被隱含拒絕——比需求嚴格太多，因為題目要求一般用量在 eu-west-1 要能正常運作。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"An Allow with NotAction (global services) plus StringNotEquals aws:RequestedRegion=eu-west-1 grants the non-global actions precisely when the Region is NOT eu-west-1, and grants nothing when the Region IS eu-west-1 — the exact inverse of the desired restriction, since it would authorize usage outside eu-west-1 while leaving eu-west-1 itself without an Allow for ordinary services.","why_zh":"Allow 搭配 NotAction（global services）與 StringNotEquals aws:RequestedRegion=eu-west-1，恰好在 Region『不是』eu-west-1 時才授予非 global service 動作，Region 是 eu-west-1 時反而沒有對應授權——邏輯正好相反，會變成允許在 eu-west-1 以外使用，eu-west-1 本身的一般服務卻無權可用。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/IAM/latest/UserGuide/reference_policies_examples_aws_deny-requested-region.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/organizations/latest/userguide/orgs_manage_policies_scps_syntax.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/organizations/latest/userguide/orgs_manage_policies_scps_evaluation.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/controltower/latest/userguide/region-deny.html"]}},{"id":26,"question_en":"A company has a compliance requirement to encrypt all data in transit. The company recently discovered an Amazon Aurora cluster that does not meet this requirement. How can the company enforce encryption for all connections to the Aurora cluster?","question_zh":"一家公司有合规要求，必须对传输中的所有数据进行加密。该公司最近发现了一个不符合此要求的 Amazon Aurora 集群。 公司如何强制对所有连接到 Aurora 集群的通信实施加密？","options_en":{"A":"In the Aurora cluster configuration, set therequire_secure_transportDB cluster parameter toON.","B":"Use AWS Directory Service for Microsoft Active Directory to create a user directory and to enforce Kerberos authentication with Aurora.","C":"Configure the Aurora cluster to use AWS Certificate Manager (ACM) to provide encryption certificates.","D":"Create an Amazon RDS proxy. Connect the proxy to the Aurora cluster to enable encryption."},"options_zh":{"A":"在 Aurora 集群配置中，将 require_secure_transport 数据库集群参数设置为 ON。","B":"使用 AWS Directory Service for Microsoft Active Directory 创建用户目录，并与 Aurora 强制实施 Kerberos 认证。","C":"配置 Aurora 集群使用 AWS 证书管理器（ACM）来提供加密证书。","D":"创建一个 Amazon RDS 代理，将该代理连接到 Aurora 集群以启用加密。"},"answer":["A"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Security/IAM","Database"],"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選","research":{"verdict":["A"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"To enforce encryption in transit for every connection to an Aurora MySQL cluster, you set the require_secure_transport DB cluster parameter to ON in a custom DB cluster parameter group. AWS documentation states: \"You can require that all user connections to your Aurora MySQL DB cluster use TLS by using the require_secure_transport DB cluster parameter,\" and once it is ON, any client that cannot establish an encrypted connection is rejected with MySQL Error 3159 (\"Connections using insecure transport are prohibited\"). The change takes effect without a reboot. This is the only option that actually enforces (not merely enables) TLS at the cluster level. (For Aurora PostgreSQL the equivalent is rds.force_ssl, but that is not offered here, so A is the intended enforcement mechanism.)","explanation_zh":"要強制所有連到 Aurora MySQL 叢集的連線都加密傳輸，需在自訂 DB cluster parameter group 中將 require_secure_transport 這個 DB cluster 參數設為 ON。AWS 官方文件明確說明：可以透過 require_secure_transport DB cluster 參數要求所有使用者連線都使用 TLS；設為 ON 後，無法建立加密連線的用戶端會被拒絕並收到 MySQL Error 3159（Connections using insecure transport are prohibited）。此變更不需重啟叢集即可生效。這是唯一能在叢集層級「強制」（而非僅支援）TLS 的選項。（Aurora PostgreSQL 對應參數為 rds.force_ssl，但本題選項未列出，故 A 為正解。）","distractors":[{"letter":"B","why_en":"AWS Managed Microsoft AD with Kerberos provides authentication for Aurora, not encryption of data in transit; Kerberos verifies identities and does not force TLS on client connections.","why_zh":"AWS Managed Microsoft AD 搭配 Kerberos 提供的是 Aurora 的「身分驗證」，不是傳輸加密；Kerberos 驗證身分，並不會強制用戶端連線使用 TLS。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"Aurora database endpoints use RDS-managed certificates (e.g., rds-ca-rsa2048-g1) installed automatically by RDS; you cannot attach ACM certificates to an Aurora cluster, and having a certificate does not by itself enforce that clients connect with TLS.","why_zh":"Aurora 資料庫端點使用 RDS 自動安裝與管理的憑證（如 rds-ca-rsa2048-g1），無法把 ACM 憑證掛到 Aurora 叢集上；而且有憑證本身也不代表強制用戶端必須用 TLS 連線。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"RDS Proxy is for connection pooling/failover; it does not enforce encryption for all connections to the cluster — clients could still connect directly to the cluster unencrypted, and TLS enforcement on the proxy is itself a separate setting.","why_zh":"RDS Proxy 用於連線池與容錯移轉，並不會強制所有連到叢集的連線加密——用戶端仍可直接以未加密方式連到叢集；且 Proxy 本身要強制 TLS 也是另外的設定。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonRDS/latest/AuroraUserGuide/AuroraMySQL.Security.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonRDS/latest/AuroraUserGuide/AuroraPostgreSQL.Security.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonRDS/latest/AuroraUserGuide/UsingWithRDS.SSL.html"]}},{"id":27,"question_en":"A company is storing data in Amazon S3 Glacier. A security engineer implemented a new vault lock policy for 10 TB of data and called the initiate-vault-lock operation 12 hours ago. The audit team identified a typo in the policy that is allowing unintended access to the vault. What is the MOST cost-effective way to correct this error?","question_zh":"一家公司正在 Amazon S3 Glacier 中存储数据。安全工程师为 10 TB 的数据实施了新的保险库锁定策略，并于 12 小时前执行了 initiate-vault-lock 操作。审计团队发现策略中存在拼写错误，导致保险库被意外访问。 纠正此错误的最经济有效的方法是什么？","options_en":{"A":"Call the abort-vault-lock operation. Update the policy. Call the initiate-vault-lock operation again.","B":"Copy the vault data to a new S3 bucket. Delete the vault. Create a new vault with the data.","C":"Update the policy to keep the vault lock in place.","D":"Update the policy. Call the initiate-vault-lock operation again to apply the new policy."},"options_zh":{"A":"调用中止保险库锁定操作。更新策略。再次调用启动保险库锁定操作。","B":"将保险库数据复制到新的 S3 存储桶中，删除原保险库，然后使用该数据创建一个新的保险库。","C":"更新策略以保持保险库锁定状态。","D":"更新策略。再次调用 initiate-vault-lock 操作以应用新策略。"},"answer":["A"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Storage","Cost Optimization"],"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選","research":{"verdict":["A"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"Locking a Glacier vault is a two-step process: initiate-vault-lock attaches the Vault Lock policy to the vault and sets the lock to an InProgress state, returning a lock ID; you then have 24 hours to validate the policy and call complete-vault-lock with that lock ID to move it to the immutable Locked state. Since initiate-vault-lock was called only 12 hours ago, the lock is still within its 24-hour InProgress window and has NOT been completed — the policy is not yet locked/immutable. AWS's Vault Lock overview explicitly states: 'If the Vault Lock policy doesn't work as expected, you can stop the Vault Lock process and restart from the beginning,' and the AbortVaultLock API reference confirms this operation 'stops the vault locking process if the vault lock is not in the Locked state' and removes the in-progress policy (it returns AccessDeniedException only if the lock is already Locked). Therefore the correct and most cost-effective fix is: call abort-vault-lock to delete the flawed in-progress policy, correct the typo, and call initiate-vault-lock again (A) — this requires no data movement and no retrieval cost. Option C leaves the unintended-access typo in place, which does not solve the audit finding. Option D is not viable/is redundant: you cannot usefully call initiate-vault-lock again to 'apply' a new policy while a lock is already InProgress without first removing the existing in-progress policy via abort-vault-lock. Option B (copy 10 TB out of Glacier to a new S3 bucket, delete the vault, recreate it) would incur very large retrieval and transfer costs and is far from cost-effective given the InProgress lock can simply be aborted for free.","explanation_zh":"鎖定 Glacier vault 是兩步驟流程：initiate-vault-lock 會將 Vault Lock policy 附加到 vault 並使鎖定進入 InProgress 狀態，同時回傳一組 lock ID；之後有 24 小時可驗證政策，並用該 lock ID 呼叫 complete-vault-lock 使其轉為不可變的 Locked 狀態。題目中 initiate-vault-lock 僅在 12 小時前呼叫，仍在 24 小時的 InProgress 視窗內、尚未完成，代表政策還不是鎖定/不可變狀態。AWS 的 Vault Lock 官方文件明確指出：「若 Vault Lock policy 運作不如預期，可以中止 Vault Lock 流程並從頭開始」；而 AbortVaultLock API 文件也證實此操作「會在 vault lock 尚未處於 Locked 狀態時停止鎖定流程」並移除進行中的政策（只有當鎖定已是 Locked 狀態時才會回傳 AccessDeniedException）。因此最正確且最具成本效益的做法是：呼叫 abort-vault-lock 刪除有錯字的進行中政策、修正錯字，再重新呼叫 initiate-vault-lock（A）——完全不需搬移資料、也沒有取回成本。選項 C 讓有錯字（造成非預期存取）的政策繼續存在，並未解決稽核團隊發現的問題。選項 D 不可行也是多餘的：鎖定已處於 InProgress 狀態時，不能直接再呼叫 initiate-vault-lock 來「套用」新政策，必須先透過 abort-vault-lock 移除現有進行中的政策。選項 B（將 10 TB 資料從 Glacier 複製到新 S3 bucket、刪除 vault、用資料重建新 vault）會產生非常高額的取回與傳輸費用，相較於可直接免費中止的 InProgress 鎖定，完全稱不上具成本效益。","distractors":[{"letter":"B","why_en":"Retrieving and copying 10 TB out of Glacier to rebuild the vault incurs significant retrieval and data-transfer costs and is entirely unnecessary, since the lock is still InProgress and can simply be aborted at no cost.","why_zh":"從 Glacier 取回並複製 10 TB 資料以重建 vault，會產生高額的取回與資料傳輸費用，且完全沒必要——鎖定仍處於 InProgress 狀態，直接免費中止即可。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"Keeping the flawed policy in place leaves the unintended access that the audit team flagged; it does not remediate the issue, it merely accepts it.","why_zh":"保留有錯字的政策等於保留稽核團隊發現的非預期存取權限；這並未修正問題，只是接受了風險。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"A vault lock that is already InProgress cannot simply be overwritten by updating the policy and calling initiate-vault-lock again; the existing in-progress policy must first be removed via abort-vault-lock before a corrected policy can be initiated.","why_zh":"已處於 InProgress 狀態的 vault lock 無法只靠更新政策、再次呼叫 initiate-vault-lock 就直接覆蓋；必須先用 abort-vault-lock 移除現有進行中的政策，才能重新 initiate 修正後的政策。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/amazonglacier/latest/dev/vault-lock.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/amazonglacier/latest/dev/api-AbortVaultLock.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/amazonglacier/latest/dev/vault-lock-how-to-cli.html"]}},{"id":28,"question_en":"A company finds that one of its Amazon EC2 instances suddenly has a high CPU usage. The company does not know whether the EC2 instance is compromised or whether the operating system is performing background cleanup. Which combination of steps should a security engineer take before investigating the issue? (Select THREE.)","question_zh":"一家公司发现其某台Amazon EC2实例的CPU使用率突然升高，但不清楚该EC2实例是否已被入侵， 还是操作系统正在进行后台清理。 安全工程师在调查问题之前应采取哪些步骤组合？（选择三项。）","options_en":{"A":"Disable termination protection for the EC2 instance if termination protection has not been disabled.","B":"Enable termination protection for the EC2 instance if termination protection has not been enabled.","C":"Take snapshots of the Amazon Elastic Block Store (Amazon EBS) data volumes that are attached to the EC2 instance.","D":"Remove all snapshots of the Amazon Elastic Block Store (Amazon EBS) data volumes that are attached to the EC2 instance.","E":"Capture the EC2 instance metadata, and then tag the EC2 instance as under quarantine.","F":"Immediately remove any entries in the EC2 instance metadata that contain sensitive information."},"options_zh":{"A":"如果尚未禁用终止保护，请为EC2实例禁用终止保护。","B":"如果尚未启用终止保护，请为EC2实例启用终止保护。","C":"对附加到 EC2 实例的 Amazon 弹性块存储（Amazon EBS）数据卷进行快照。","D":"删除所有与EC2实例关联的Amazon弹性块存储（Amazon EBS）数据卷的快照。","E":"获取EC2实例的元数据，然后将该EC2实例标记为隔离状态。","F":"立即删除EC2实例元数据中包含敏感信息的任何条目。"},"answer":["B","C","E"],"multi":true,"vote":{},"tags":["Storage","Compute"],"difficulty":2,"diff_why":"複選","research":{"verdict":["B","C","E"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"This is an evidence-preservation / containment question. Before investigating a possibly compromised EC2 instance, official AWS incident-response guidance is to contain and preserve the resource without destroying it, not to alter or erase potential evidence. (B) Enable termination protection so the instance cannot be accidentally or maliciously terminated while it is being investigated — this keeps the resource (and its volatile state, logs, and attached volumes) intact for the responder. (C) Take point-in-time EBS snapshots of the attached data volumes to preserve a forensic copy of disk state; this is literally what AWS's own SSM automation runbook AWS-QuarantineEC2Instance does — its documented steps are: gather instance details, verify the instance is not in an Auto Scaling group, create a snapshot of the root volume, wait for the snapshot to complete, and only then apply an isolating security group. (E) Capture the instance metadata (instance ID, AMI, IPs, launch time, IAM role, etc.) and tag the instance as 'under quarantine' so responders can identify it, apply restrictive controls, and avoid it being touched by automation (e.g., Auto Scaling replacement) during the investigation — AWS's own compromised-resource remediation guidance shows this exact tagging pattern (e.g., tagging a resource with values like Investigation=Malware, DoNotDelete=True) to mark evidence as protected. AWS's Security Incident Response 'Contain' documentation explicitly states that containment actions 'isolate compromised resources without destroying them' and are designed to be reversible, preserving the resource for later forensic review. Options A, D, and F do the opposite of this principle — they remove protection, destroy potential evidence, or alter evidence before it can be examined — so none of them belong in a pre-investigation checklist.","explanation_zh":"這是一題「證據保全／圍堵（containment）」題。在調查疑似被入侵的 EC2 instance 之前，AWS 官方事件回應指引要求先圍堵並保全該資源、而不是破壞或竄改任何可能的證據。(B) 啟用 termination protection，避免調查期間 instance 被意外或惡意終止——讓資源（含其揮發性狀態、日誌與掛載的 volume）維持完整供回應人員檢視。(C) 對掛載的資料 volume 建立時間點 EBS 快照，保留磁碟狀態的鑑識副本；這正是 AWS 自家 SSM 自動化 runbook AWS-QuarantineEC2Instance 實際執行的步驟：先蒐集 instance 詳細資訊、確認該 instance 不在 Auto Scaling group 中、對 root volume 建立快照、等待快照完成，最後才套用隔離用的 security group。(E) 擷取 instance metadata（instance ID、AMI、IP、啟動時間、IAM role 等）並將 instance 標記（tag）為「隔離中」，讓回應人員能識別該資源、套用限制性控制，並避免它在調查期間被自動化機制（例如 Auto Scaling 替換）動到——AWS 自家對受入侵資源的補救指引就示範了這種標記模式（例如打上 Investigation=Malware, DoNotDelete=True 之類的 tag）來標示證據需受保護。AWS Security Incident Response 的「Contain」文件明確指出，圍堵動作會「在不破壞資源的前提下隔離受影響資源」，且設計上是可逆的，目的就是保留資源供後續鑑識檢視。選項 A、D、F 恰好違反此原則——分別是移除保護、銷毀潛在證據、或在檢視前竄改證據——因此都不屬於調查前應執行的步驟。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"Disabling termination protection makes it easier for the instance to be terminated (accidentally, or by an attacker who still has valid credentials), which would destroy volatile evidence and attached-volume state before investigation — the opposite of the containment principle of isolating a resource 'without destroying it'.","why_zh":"停用 termination protection 會讓 instance 更容易被終止（意外，或攻擊者仍持有有效憑證時惡意為之），導致調查前揮發性證據與掛載 volume 狀態被銷毀，正好違反圍堵原則中「隔離資源但不破壞它」的要求。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"Removing existing EBS snapshots destroys potential forensic evidence and historical restore points. AWS's own quarantine runbook does the opposite — it creates a new snapshot of the root volume as one of its first actions, not deletes existing ones.","why_zh":"移除既有 EBS 快照會銷毀潛在的鑑識證據與歷史還原點。AWS 自家的隔離 runbook 做的正好相反——它最早執行的動作之一就是為 root volume 建立新快照，而不是刪除既有快照。"},{"letter":"F","why_en":"Immediately removing entries from instance metadata alters potential evidence before it has been examined and breaks chain of custody. The correct action is to capture/preserve metadata as-is (as in option E), not scrub or modify it.","why_zh":"在檢視前就立即移除 instance metadata 中的項目，等於在證據還沒被檢查前就竄改它，破壞監管鏈（chain of custody）。正確做法是原樣擷取並保存 metadata（如選項 E 所述），而不是清除或修改它。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/security-ir/latest/userguide/contain.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/systems-manager-automation-runbooks/latest/userguide/aws-quarantineec2instance.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/guardduty/latest/ug/compromised-ec2.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/guardduty/latest/ug/compromised-ec2-recoverypoint.html"]}},{"id":29,"question_en":"A company needs to migrate several applications to AWS. This will require storing more than 5,000 credentials. To meet compliance requirements, the company will use its existing password management system for key rotation, auditing, and integration with third-party secrets containers. The company has a limited budget and is seeking the most cost-effective solution that is still secure. How should the company accomplish this at the LOWEST cost?","question_zh":"一家公司需要将多个应用程序迁移到 AWS，这将涉及存储超过 5,000 个凭据。为满足合规要求， 该公司将使用现有的密码管理系统来实现密钥轮换、审计以及与第三方密钥容器的集成。由于 预算有限，公司正在寻求一种既安全又最具成本效益的解决方案。 公司应如何以最低的成本实现这一目标？","options_en":{"A":"Configure the company’s key management solution to integrate with AWS Systems Manager Parameter Store.","B":"Configure the company’s key management solution to integrate with AWS Secrets Manager.","C":"Use an Amazon S3 encrypted bucket to store the secrets and configure the applications with the appropriate roles to access the secrets.","D":"Configure the company’s key management solution to integrate with AWS CloudHSM."},"options_zh":{"A":"配置公司的密钥管理解决方案，以与 AWS Systems Manager 参数存储集成。","B":"配置公司的密钥管理解决方案，以与 AWS Secrets Manager 集成。","C":"使用 Amazon S3 加密存储桶来存储密钥，并为应用程序配置相应的角色以访问这些密钥。","D":"配置公司的密钥管理解决方案，以与 AWS CloudHSM 集成。"},"answer":["A"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Migration","Security/IAM","Storage","Cost Optimization","Monitoring/Ops"],"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選","research":{"verdict":["A"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"The scenario's decisive constraint is LOWEST cost for storing 5,000+ credentials, given that key rotation, auditing, and third-party secrets-container integration are already provided by the company's existing password/key management system — AWS only needs to be the storage backend. AWS Systems Manager Parameter Store standard-tier parameters (including SecureString parameters encrypted with AWS KMS) incur no additional charge and support up to 10,000 standard parameters per AWS account per Region with values up to 4 KB — confirmed on the official 'Managing tiers' page, which states the standard tier has 'No additional charge' versus the advanced tier where 'Charges apply.' This comfortably covers 5,000+ credentials at zero incremental storage cost, while KMS encryption and IAM policies still provide security. Parameter Store's usual gap versus Secrets Manager — no built-in automatic rotation — is irrelevant here because rotation is explicitly handled by the existing external system, and the company's key management solution can integrate with Parameter Store's API/SecureString parameters just as it would with Secrets Manager. AWS Secrets Manager (option B) offers the same integration capability but bills roughly $0.40 per secret per month (about $2,000+/month for 5,000 secrets) plus API charges — its differentiating value (managed rotation, resource policies) is redundant when rotation is already externally managed, so it fails the cost qualifier despite being technically valid. Amazon S3 (option C) is generic object storage, not a purpose-built secrets/parameter service, and lacks the native parameter hierarchy, versioning, and secrets-tooling integration that Parameter Store/Secrets Manager provide, making it a less appropriate and non-standard choice for this use case. AWS CloudHSM (option D) is a dedicated, single-tenant hardware security module billed per HSM-hour (with a highly-available production cluster requiring multiple HSMs) — it is designed for cryptographic key storage and crypto operations, not for storing thousands of application credentials, and is by far the most expensive of the four options. Therefore, configuring the existing key management solution to integrate with Parameter Store (standard tier) is the correct, lowest-cost, still-secure answer.","explanation_zh":"本題的決定性限制是「LOWEST cost」，且輪替（rotation）、稽核與第三方 secrets container 整合皆已由公司既有的密碼／金鑰管理系統負責——AWS 只需要充當儲存後端。AWS Systems Manager Parameter Store 標準層參數（含以 AWS KMS 加密的 SecureString）完全不額外收費，且每個 AWS 帳號、每個 Region 可存放最多 10,000 個標準參數、每筆最大 4 KB——這在官方「Managing tiers」文件中明確列出：標準層為「No additional charge」，進階層才「Charges apply」。這足以零額外儲存成本地容納 5,000+ 組憑證，同時仍可透過 KMS 加密與 IAM 政策維持安全性。Parameter Store 相較 Secrets Manager 常見的缺口——沒有內建自動輪替——在此情境中並不重要，因為輪替已由既有外部系統處理，且公司的金鑰管理方案同樣能與 Parameter Store 的 API／SecureString 參數整合，如同與 Secrets Manager 整合一樣。AWS Secrets Manager（選項 B）提供相同的整合能力，但每個 secret 每月約收費 $0.40（5,000 個約每月 $2,000+）外加 API 費用——其主打的差異化價值（受管輪替、資源政策）在輪替已由外部系統處理時是多餘的，因此雖然技術上可行，卻不符合成本要求。Amazon S3（選項 C）是通用物件儲存，並非專為密文／參數設計的服務，缺乏 Parameter Store／Secrets Manager 原生具備的參數階層、版本管理與密文工具整合，對此情境而言並非合適或標準的做法。AWS CloudHSM（選項 D）是單租戶專用硬體安全模組，按 HSM 小時計費（生產環境高可用叢集需要多台 HSM），設計用途是加密金鑰的儲存與加密運算，而非存放數千組應用程式憑證，是四個選項中成本最高者。因此，將既有金鑰管理方案整合至 Parameter Store（標準層）才是正確、成本最低且仍安全的答案。","distractors":[{"letter":"B","why_en":"AWS Secrets Manager works technically and can integrate with an external key management solution, but it charges roughly $0.40 per secret per month plus API request costs — over $2,000/month for 5,000+ secrets — and its key differentiator (built-in automatic rotation) is unneeded because the existing password management system already handles rotation and auditing. It fails the LOWEST-cost qualifier that the question asks for.","why_zh":"AWS Secrets Manager 技術上可行，也能與外部金鑰管理方案整合，但每個 secret 每月約收 $0.40 外加 API 請求費用（5,000+ 個每月超過 $2,000），且其主打特色（內建自動輪替）在此情境是多餘的，因為現有密碼管理系統已負責輪替與稽核。這不符合題目要求的「最低成本」。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"S3 is general-purpose object storage, not a purpose-built secrets/parameter store: it lacks Parameter Store's native parameter hierarchy, SecureString/KMS-integrated secret semantics, and direct integration with secrets tooling used by AWS services. Building custom secret distribution logic on S3 increases the risk of misconfiguration and leakage, so it is not the standard, secure option AWS documentation points to for credential storage.","why_zh":"S3 是通用型物件儲存，並非專為密文／參數設計的服務：缺少 Parameter Store 原生的參數階層、SecureString／KMS 整合的密文語意，以及與 AWS 服務所用密文工具的直接整合。在 S3 上自建密文散佈邏輯會提高設定錯誤與外洩的風險，因此並非 AWS 文件建議用來存放憑證的標準安全做法。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"CloudHSM is a dedicated, single-tenant hardware security module intended for cryptographic key storage and cryptographic operations (e.g., signing, encryption), not for storing thousands of application passwords/credentials. It is billed per HSM per hour, and a production-grade highly available cluster requires multiple HSMs, making it by far the most expensive of the four options — directly contradicting the company's limited-budget, lowest-cost requirement.","why_zh":"CloudHSM 是單租戶專用硬體安全模組，設計用途是加密金鑰的保管與加密運算（如簽章、加解密），並非用來存放數千組應用程式帳密。其計費方式為每台 HSM 每小時收費，且生產等級的高可用叢集需要多台 HSM，是四個選項中成本最高者，與公司預算有限、要求最低成本的需求直接牴觸。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/systems-manager/latest/userguide/parameter-store-advanced-parameters.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/systems-manager/latest/userguide/systems-manager-parameter-store.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/secretsmanager/latest/userguide/integrating_parameterstore.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/systems-manager/latest/userguide/integration-ps-secretsmanager.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/secretsmanager/latest/userguide/intro.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/cloudhsm/latest/userguide/pricing.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/cloudhsm/latest/userguide/introduction.html"]}},{"id":30,"question_en":"A company uses AWS IAM Identity Center with SAML 2.0 federation. The company decides to change its federation source from one identity provider (IdP) to another. The underlying directory for both IdPs is Active Directory. Which solution will meet this requirement?","question_zh":"一家公司使用 AWS IAM Identity Center 配合 SAML 2.0 联邦身份验证。该公司决定将其联邦身份源从 一个身份提供商（IdP）更改为另一个。两个 IdP 的底层目录均为 Active Directory。 哪种解决方案能满足这一要求？","options_en":{"A":"Disable all existing users and groups within IAM Identity Center that were part of the federation with the original IdP.","B":"Modify the attribute mappings within the IAM Identity Center trust relationship to match information that the new IdP sends.","C":"Reconfigure all existing IAM roles in the company ' s AWS accounts to explicitly trust the new IdP as the principal.","D":"Confirm that the Network Time Protocol (NTP) clock skew is correctly set between IAM Identity Center and the new IdP endpoints."},"options_zh":{"A":"禁用 IAM Identity Center 中所有曾属于与原始身份提供商（IdP）联合的现有用户和组。","B":"修改 IAM Identity Center 信任关系中的属性映射，以匹配新的身份提供商发送的信息。","C":"重新配置公司所有 AWS 账户中的现有 IAM 角色，明确信任新的身份提供商作为主体。","D":"确认 IAM Identity Center 与新的身份提供商（IdP）端点之间的网络时间协议（NTP）时钟 偏差已正确设置。"},"answer":["B"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Security/IAM"],"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選","research":{"verdict":["B"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"AWS's official guidance has a section titled 'Changing from one external IdP to another external IdP' (in Considerations for changing your identity source) that maps directly onto this scenario. It states: 'IAM Identity Center preserves all of your assignments. The user assignments, group assignments, and group memberships continue to work as long as the new IdP sends the correct assertions (for example, SAML nameIDs). These assertions must match the user names in IAM Identity Center when your users authenticate through the new external IdP.' Because both the old and new IdP are backed by the same Active Directory, the underlying users/groups and their IAM Identity Center assignments are unaffected by the switch — nothing needs to be recreated. The only real configuration work is making sure what the new IdP's SAML assertions carry (NameID/Subject and any additional claims) lines up with what IAM Identity Center expects for each user, which is exactly the attribute-mapping configuration under the IAM Identity Center identity-source (SAML trust) settings — option B. Option A is actively harmful: disabling users/groups would break SSO rather than complete the migration, and the docs explicitly warn that changing sources incorrectly 'will lose single sign-on access.' Option C misunderstands the trust model: the IAM roles IAM Identity Center auto-creates for permission sets trust the IAM Identity Center SAML provider/service itself (an AWS-internal principal), never the external IdP directly, so no role trust policy references the IdP and none need to change. Option D (NTP/clock skew) is a SAML-assertion troubleshooting check (assertions have tight NotBefore/NotOnOrAfter validity windows), not a step required to migrate the federation source. Therefore B is the correct solution, confirming the first analyst.","explanation_zh":"AWS 官方文件在「變更身分來源的考量事項」中有專門一節「Changing from one external IdP to another external IdP」，正對應此情境。文件寫道：IAM Identity Center 會保留所有指派；只要新 IdP 傳送正確的 assertion（例如 SAML nameID），使用者指派、群組指派與群組成員資格就會持續生效，且這些 assertion 必須與 IAM Identity Center 中的使用者名稱相符。由於新舊兩個 IdP 底層都是同一個 Active Directory，使用者/群組本身與其在 IAM Identity Center 的指派並不受切換影響，不需要重建。真正需要做的設定，就是確保新 IdP 傳來的 SAML assertion（NameID/Subject 及其他宣告）與 IAM Identity Center 對每個使用者的期望值一致——也就是在 IAM Identity Center 身分來源（SAML 信任關係）設定中調整屬性對應（attribute mappings），也就是選項 B。選項 A 反而有害：停用使用者/群組只會中斷 SSO，文件明確警告錯誤變更會導致「失去單一登入存取權」。選項 C 誤解了信任模型：IAM Identity Center 為權限集自動建立的 IAM 角色信任的是 IAM Identity Center 的 SAML 提供者（AWS 內部主體），從不直接信任外部 IdP，因此角色信任政策不需要異動。選項 D（NTP/時鐘偏移）只是 SAML assertion 疑難排解的檢查項目（assertion 有嚴格的 NotBefore/NotOnOrAfter 有效期），並非切換聯合來源所必需的步驟。因此 B 為正確答案，與第一位分析者的結論一致。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"Unnecessary and actively harmful: per AWS docs, IAM Identity Center preserves users, groups, and assignments when switching between external IdPs backed by the same directory; disabling them breaks SSO access instead of completing the new federation.","why_zh":"既不必要又有害：根據 AWS 文件，在底層目錄相同的外部 IdP 之間切換時，IAM Identity Center 會保留使用者、群組與指派；停用它們只會中斷 SSO 存取，無法完成新的聯合設定。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"The auto-generated permission-set IAM roles trust the IAM Identity Center SAML provider itself (an AWS-managed principal), not the external IdP directly — no IAM role trust policy references the customer's IdP, so nothing there needs to change when the IdP is swapped.","why_zh":"權限集自動產生的 IAM 角色信任的是 IAM Identity Center 本身的 SAML 提供者（AWS 內部主體），而非直接信任外部 IdP；沒有任何 IAM 角色信任政策會引用客戶的 IdP，因此更換 IdP 時不需要修改角色信任。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"Clock skew between endpoints can cause SAML assertion timestamp validation failures, but confirming NTP sync is a troubleshooting/health check, not the configuration change required to point IAM Identity Center's identity source at a new IdP.","why_zh":"端點間的時鐘偏移可能導致 SAML assertion 時間戳記驗證失敗，但確認 NTP 同步只是疑難排解／健康檢查項目，並不是把 IAM Identity Center 身分來源指向新 IdP 所需的設定變更。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/singlesignon/latest/userguide/manage-your-identity-source-considerations.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/singlesignon/latest/userguide/attributemappingsconcept.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/singlesignon/latest/userguide/manage-your-identity-source-change.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/singlesignon/latest/userguide/how-to-change-idp-metadata.html"]}},{"id":31,"question_en":"A company is using Amazon Macie, AWS Firewall Manager, Amazon Inspector, and AWS Shield Advanced in its AWS account. The company wants to receive alerts if a DDoS attack occurs against the account. Which solution will meet this requirement?","question_zh":"一家公司正在其AWS账户中使用Amazon Macie、AWS Firewall Manager、Amazon Inspector和AWS Shield Advanced。该公司希望在账户遭受DDoS攻击时收到警报。 哪种解决方案能满足这一要求？","options_en":{"A":"Use Amazon Macie to detect an active DDoS event and create Amazon CloudWatch alarms that respond to Macie findings.","B":"Use Amazon Inspector to review resources and invoke Amazon CloudWatch alarms for any resources that are vulnerable to DDoS attacks.","C":"Create an Amazon CloudWatch alarm that monitors AWS Firewall Manager metrics for an active DDoS event.","D":"Create an Amazon CloudWatch alarm that monitors AWS Shield Advanced metrics for an active DDoS event."},"options_zh":{"A":"使用 Amazon Macie 检测活跃的 DDoS 事件，并创建 Amazon CloudWatch 警报以响应 Macie 的发现结果。","B":"使用 Amazon Inspector 检查资源，并对任何易受 DDoS 攻击的资源触发 Amazon CloudWatch 警报。","C":"创建一个 Amazon CloudWatch 警报，用于监控 AWS Firewall Manager 的指标，以检测正在进行的 DDoS 事件。","D":"创建一个 Amazon CloudWatch 警报，用于监控 AWS Shield Advanced 的指标，以检测正在进行的 DDoS 事件。"},"answer":["D"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Security/IAM","Monitoring/Ops"],"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選","research":{"verdict":["D"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"AWS Shield Advanced publishes near-real-time Amazon CloudWatch metrics in the AWS/DDoSProtection namespace for every resource it protects, including DDoSDetected — which 'indicates whether a DDoS event is underway for a particular ARN' and is non-zero during an event — plus DDoSAttackBitsPerSecond, DDoSAttackPacketsPerSecond, and DDoSAttackRequestsPerSecond. AWS's own 'AWS Shield Advanced metrics' documentation explicitly recommends, as a starting point, creating a CloudWatch alarm for each protected resource that fires when DDoSDetected is non-zero, and Shield Advanced increases its metric-reporting frequency to once a minute during an active event so the alarm reflects near-real-time status. Option C fails because the companion 'Monitoring with Amazon CloudWatch' page states outright, in a dedicated note, that 'CloudWatch metrics and alarms are not enabled for Firewall Manager' — Firewall Manager centrally manages WAF/Shield/security-group policies across accounts but emits no metrics of its own to alarm on. Option A fails because Amazon Macie only discovers and classifies sensitive data in S3 and has no DDoS-detection capability or findings type for it. Option B fails because Amazon Inspector scans EC2/ECR/Lambda workloads for software vulnerabilities (CVEs) and unintended network exposure — it does not detect active DDoS traffic or flag resources as 'DDoS-vulnerable.' Therefore D is the only solution that satisfies the requirement, confirming the first analyst's answer.","explanation_zh":"AWS Shield Advanced 會在 AWS/DDoSProtection 命名空間下，為每個受保護資源發布近即時的 Amazon CloudWatch 指標，其中 DDoSDetected 這項指標「代表某個 ARN 上是否正在發生 DDoS 事件」，事件發生時該值會非零；另外還有 DDoSAttackBitsPerSecond、DDoSAttackPacketsPerSecond、DDoSAttackRequestsPerSecond 等指標。AWS 官方「AWS Shield Advanced metrics」文件明確建議，最基本的作法是為每個受保護資源建立 CloudWatch alarm，於 DDoSDetected 非零時觸發；而且 Shield Advanced 在事件發生期間會把回報頻率提高到每分鐘一次，讓警報能反映近即時狀態。選項 C 不成立，因為同系列的「Monitoring with Amazon CloudWatch」文件中有專門一則附註明白寫著「CloudWatch metrics and alarms are not enabled for Firewall Manager」——Firewall Manager 只是跨帳號集中管理 WAF/Shield/安全群組政策的服務，本身不會發出可供建立警報的指標。選項 A 不成立，因為 Amazon Macie 僅用於探索與分類 S3 中的敏感資料，完全不具備偵測 DDoS 的能力或對應的 finding 類型。選項 B 不成立，因為 Amazon Inspector 掃描的是 EC2/ECR/Lambda 工作負載的軟體弱點（CVE）與非預期網路暴露，並不會偵測進行中的 DDoS 流量，也不會將資源標記為「易受 DDoS 攻擊」。因此只有 D 能滿足題目需求，確認第一位分析師的答案正確。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"Amazon Macie discovers and classifies sensitive data (e.g., PII) in Amazon S3 using machine learning and pattern matching; it has no DDoS-detection capability and produces no findings related to network-layer or application-layer DDoS activity.","why_zh":"Amazon Macie 使用機器學習與模式比對來探索並分類 Amazon S3 中的敏感資料（例如個資），完全不具備偵測 DDoS 攻擊的能力，也不會產生與網路層或應用層 DDoS 活動相關的 findings。"},{"letter":"B","why_en":"Amazon Inspector automatically scans EC2 instances, container images in ECR, and Lambda functions for software vulnerabilities (CVEs) and unintended network exposure; it does not classify resources as 'vulnerable to DDoS' nor can it detect an active DDoS event in progress.","why_zh":"Amazon Inspector 會自動掃描 EC2 執行個體、ECR 中的容器映像及 Lambda 函式，找出軟體弱點（CVE）與非預期的網路暴露；它不會將資源歸類為「易受 DDoS 攻擊」，也無法偵測正在進行中的 DDoS 事件。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"AWS's 'Monitoring with Amazon CloudWatch' documentation explicitly states 'CloudWatch metrics and alarms are not enabled for Firewall Manager.' Firewall Manager centrally administers AWS WAF rules, Shield Advanced protections, and security groups across accounts/OUs, but it emits no metrics of its own that a CloudWatch alarm could monitor for a DDoS event.","why_zh":"AWS 的「Monitoring with Amazon CloudWatch」文件明確指出「CloudWatch metrics and alarms are not enabled for Firewall Manager」。Firewall Manager 負責跨帳號／OU 集中管理 AWS WAF 規則、Shield Advanced 保護與安全群組，但它本身不會發出任何指標，因此無法讓 CloudWatch alarm 監控 DDoS 事件。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/waf/latest/developerguide/monitoring-cloudwatch.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/waf/latest/developerguide/shield-metrics.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/waf/latest/developerguide/ddos-get-started-create-alarms.html"]}},{"id":32,"question_en":"A security engineer wants to create a new AWS KMS customer managed key. The KMSAdmin IAM role will create and disable this key. The KMSUser IAM role will use this key for decryption. Which key policy will meet these requirements?","question_zh":"安全工程师希望创建一个新的 AWS KMS 客户管理密钥。KMSAdmin IAM 角色将负责创建并禁用该密钥，而 KMSUser IAM 角色将使 用此密钥进行解密操作。 哪项关键政策能够满足这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"A key policy that grants KMSAdmin only kms:Create and kms:Disable*, and grants KMSUser kms: Decrypt.","B":"A key policy that grants KMSAdmin kms:Create* and kms:Disable*, and grants KMSUser kms: Decrypt.","C":"A key policy that grants KMSAdmin and KMSUser kms:CreateGrant, but does not grant KMSUser kms:Decrypt.","D":"A key policy that grants both KMSAdmin and KMSUser only kms:Decrypt*."},"options_zh":{"A":"一项关键策略，仅授予KMSAdmin kms:Create和kms:Disable*权限，并授予KMSUser kms:Decrypt权限。","B":"一项关键策略，授予KMSAdmin kms:Create* 和 kms:Disable* 权限，并授予KMSUser kms:Decrypt 权限。","C":"一项关键策略，授予 KMSAdmin 和 KMSUser kms:CreateGrant 权限，但不授予 KMSUser kms:Decrypt 权限。","D":"一项关键策略，仅授予 KMSAdmin 和 KMSUser kms:Decrypt* 权限。"},"answer":["B"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Security/IAM"],"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選","research":{"verdict":["B"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"both","explanation_en":"AWS KMS's own documented default key policy is the authoritative template here. Its key-administrators statement grants exactly the wildcarded actions \"kms:Create*\", \"kms:Describe*\", \"kms:Enable*\", \"kms:List*\", \"kms:Put*\", \"kms:Update*\", \"kms:Revoke*\", \"kms:Disable*\", \"kms:Get*\", \"kms:Delete*\", etc., while its key-users statement grants cryptographic-operation actions including \"kms:Decrypt\". Option B mirrors this exactly: KMSAdmin gets \"kms:Create*\" (which AWS docs confirm resolves to kms:CreateAlias and kms:CreateGrant — note kms:CreateKey itself is only ever granted via an IAM identity policy, never a resource-based key policy, since the key doesn't exist yet when it's being created) and \"kms:Disable*\" (which resolves to kms:DisableKey, and kms:DisableKeyRotation for symmetric keys), satisfying the \"create and disable\" requirement; KMSUser gets \"kms:Decrypt\", satisfying the decryption requirement. Option A fails because \"kms:Create\" (no wildcard, no suffix) is not a valid IAM/KMS action name — the real actions are kms:CreateKey, kms:CreateAlias, kms:CreateGrant — so that statement is a no-op and grants KMSAdmin nothing. Option C never grants KMSUser kms:Decrypt, so KMSUser cannot perform the required decryption. Option D grants only kms:Decrypt* to both roles, so KMSAdmin never receives any create or disable permission at all. B is the only option whose action set is both syntactically valid and functionally matches the stated requirements.","explanation_zh":"AWS KMS 官方文件記載的預設 key policy 就是這題的權威範本：其 key administrators 敘述句授予的正是萬用字元動作 \"kms:Create*\"、\"kms:Describe*\"、\"kms:Enable*\"、\"kms:List*\"、\"kms:Put*\"、\"kms:Update*\"、\"kms:Revoke*\"、\"kms:Disable*\"、\"kms:Get*\"、\"kms:Delete*\" 等；而 key users 敘述句則授予加解密操作，包含 \"kms:Decrypt\"。選項 B 與此完全吻合：KMSAdmin 取得 \"kms:Create*\"（AWS 文件證實此會匹配 kms:CreateAlias 與 kms:CreateGrant——注意 kms:CreateKey 本身只能透過 IAM identity policy 授予，永遠不會出現在資源型的 key policy 裡，因為建立當下該金鑰資源尚不存在）與 \"kms:Disable*\"（匹配 kms:DisableKey，對稱金鑰還包含 kms:DisableKeyRotation），滿足「建立與停用」的需求；KMSUser 則取得 \"kms:Decrypt\"，滿足解密需求。選項 A 錯在 \"kms:Create\"（無萬用字元、無後綴）根本不是有效的 IAM/KMS 動作名稱——實際動作是 kms:CreateKey、kms:CreateAlias、kms:CreateGrant——因此該敘述句形同虛設，KMSAdmin 什麼都拿不到。選項 C 從未授予 KMSUser kms:Decrypt，KMSUser 無法執行所需的解密操作。選項 D 讓兩個角色都只拿到 kms:Decrypt*，KMSAdmin 完全沒有任何建立或停用權限。只有 B 的動作集合既語法有效、又確實符合題目需求。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"\"kms:Create\" without a wildcard or suffix is not a valid IAM/KMS action name at all (valid ones are kms:CreateKey, kms:CreateAlias, kms:CreateGrant), so this policy statement is a no-op and grants KMSAdmin no create-related permission.","why_zh":"\"kms:Create\"（不帶萬用字元或後綴）根本不是有效的 IAM/KMS 動作名稱（有效的是 kms:CreateKey、kms:CreateAlias、kms:CreateGrant），因此這條敘述句形同虛設，KMSAdmin 拿不到任何 create 相關權限。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"Granting only kms:CreateGrant to both roles gives neither the required abilities: KMSAdmin still cannot disable the key, and explicitly withholding kms:Decrypt means KMSUser cannot decrypt with the key at all.","why_zh":"只授予兩個角色 kms:CreateGrant 完全無法滿足需求：KMSAdmin 仍然無法停用金鑰，而明確不授予 kms:Decrypt 代表 KMSUser 完全無法用該金鑰解密。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"Granting only kms:Decrypt* to both roles leaves KMSAdmin with zero administrative permissions (no create, no disable), so the admin requirement is completely unmet even though KMSUser's decrypt need happens to be covered.","why_zh":"兩個角色都只給 kms:Decrypt* 代表 KMSAdmin 完全沒有任何管理權限（無法建立、無法停用），即使 KMSUser 的解密需求恰好被滿足，管理需求依然完全落空。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/kms/latest/developerguide/key-policy-default.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/kms/latest/developerguide/deleting-keys-adding-permission.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/kms/latest/developerguide/kms-api-permissions-reference.html"]}},{"id":33,"question_en":"A company needs a solution to protect critical data from being permanently deleted. The data is stored in Amazon S3 buckets. The company needs to replicate the S3 objects from the company ' s primary AWS Region to a secondary Region to meet disaster recovery requirements. The company must also ensure that users who have administrator access cannot permanently delete the data in the secondary Region. Which solution will meet these requirements?","question_zh":"一家公司需要一种解决方案，以防止关键数据被永久删除。这些数据存储在 Amazon S3 存储桶中。该公司需要将 S3 对象从 主 AWS 区域复制到次要区域，以满足灾难恢复要求。同时，公司还必须确保拥有管理员权限的用户无法永久删除次要区域 中的数据。 哪种解决方案能满足这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Configure AWS Backup to perform cross-Region S3 backups. Select a backup vault in the secondary Region. Enable AWS Backup Vault Lock in governance mode for the backups in the secondary Region.","B":"Implement S3 Object Lock in compliance mode in the primary Region. Configure S3 replication to replicate the objects to an S3 bucket in the secondary Region.","C":"Configure S3 replication to replicate the objects to an S3 bucket in the secondary Region. Create an S3 bucket policy to deny the s3:ReplicateDelete action on the S3 bucket in the secondary Region.","D":"Configure S3 replication to replicate the objects to an S3 bucket in the secondary Region. Configure S3 object versioning on the S3 bucket in the secondary Region."},"options_zh":{"A":"配置 AWS Backup 执行跨区域的 S3 备份。选择次要区域中的一个备份存储库，并为该区域的备份启用治理模式下的 AWS Backup 存储库锁定功能。","B":"在主区域以合规模式启用 S3 对象锁定功能，并配置 S3 复制，将对象复制到次级区域的 S3 存储桶中。","C":"配置 S3 复制，将对象复制到次要区域的 S3 存储桶中。创建一个 S3 存储桶策略，拒绝在次要区域的 S3 存储桶上执行 s3: ReplicateDelete 操作。","D":"配置 S3 复制，将对象复制到次要区域的 S3 存储桶中，并在该次要区域的 S3 存储桶上启用 S3 对象版本控制。"},"answer":["B"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Disaster Recovery/HA","Storage"],"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選","research":{"verdict":["B"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"The requirements are: (1) cross-Region replication of S3 objects for DR, and (2) even administrators must be unable to permanently delete the data in the secondary Region. Per AWS docs, S3 Object Lock compliance mode is the only listed mechanism that satisfies (2): 'a protected object version can't be overwritten or deleted by any user, including the root user in your AWS account... The only way to delete an object under compliance mode before its retention date expires is to delete the associated AWS account.' Object Lock is explicitly designed to work with S3 Replication: locked objects and their retention metadata are copied to the destination, and AWS states 'if the source bucket has Object Lock enabled, the destination buckets must also have Object Lock enabled' — so the replicated copies in the secondary Region inherit the same compliance-mode WORM protection, satisfying both requirements together. Option A fails because AWS Backup Vault Lock in governance mode 'can have the lock removed by users with sufficient IAM permissions' — an administrator can remove it and then delete backups; only Vault Lock compliance mode is truly immutable, and the option specifies governance mode. Option C's bucket-policy deny of s3:ReplicateDelete only blocks replication of delete markers from the primary Region (protecting against an accidental delete on the source propagating to the secondary copy); it does nothing to stop a user from directly and permanently deleting object versions in the secondary bucket, and an administrator can simply edit or remove that bucket policy at will. Option D's versioning alone does not make data immutable — any principal with s3:DeleteObjectVersion (which administrators have) can still permanently purge specific versions. Therefore B is correct.","explanation_zh":"題目有兩個要求：（1）將 S3 物件跨 Region 複寫以符合 DR，（2）連管理員都無法永久刪除次要 Region 的資料。根據 AWS 文件，S3 Object Lock 的 compliance mode 是選項中唯一能滿足（2）的機制：「受保護的物件版本無法被任何使用者（含 AWS 帳戶的 root 使用者）覆寫或刪除⋯在保留期限到期前，唯一能刪除 compliance mode 物件的方法是刪除該關聯的 AWS 帳戶。」Object Lock 明確設計為可與 S3 Replication 搭配使用：鎖定的物件及其保留中繼資料會被複製到目的地，AWS 文件也指出「若來源儲存桶啟用 Object Lock，目的地儲存桶也必須啟用 Object Lock」——因此次要 Region 的複本會繼承相同的 compliance-mode WORM 保護，同時滿足兩項需求。選項 A 不成立，因為 AWS Backup Vault Lock 的 governance mode「可被具足夠 IAM 權限的使用者移除鎖定」——管理員可解除鎖定後刪除備份；只有 Vault Lock compliance mode 才是真正不可變的，但選項指定的是 governance mode。選項 C 在儲存桶政策中拒絕 s3:ReplicateDelete，只會阻擋來源刪除標記被複寫到次要 Region（防止來源端的意外刪除傳播過去），並不能阻止使用者直接在次要儲存桶永久刪除物件版本，而且管理員本來就能任意修改或移除該儲存桶政策。選項 D 僅靠版本控管無法讓資料不可變——任何擁有 s3:DeleteObjectVersion 權限的人（管理員必然具備）仍可永久清除特定版本。因此答案為 B。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"AWS Backup Vault Lock in governance mode can be managed, changed, or deleted by users with sufficient IAM permissions — an administrator could remove the lock and then delete the backups. Only Vault Lock compliance mode is immutable and cannot be removed by any user, including admins and AWS itself; the option specifies the wrong mode.","why_zh":"AWS Backup Vault Lock 的 governance mode 可由具足夠 IAM 權限的使用者管理、變更或移除——管理員可解除鎖定後刪除備份。只有 Vault Lock compliance mode 是不可變的，任何人（含管理員與 AWS 本身）都無法移除；此選項指定的模式並不符合需求。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"Denying s3:ReplicateDelete only blocks replication of delete markers from the source (i.e., stops a source-side delete from propagating); it does nothing to stop a user from directly and permanently deleting object versions already in the secondary bucket, and an administrator can simply edit or remove the bucket policy anyway.","why_zh":"拒絕 s3:ReplicateDelete 只會阻擋刪除標記從來源被複寫過來（防止來源端刪除動作傳播過去），無法阻止使用者直接在次要儲存桶永久刪除已存在的物件版本；而且管理員本來就能直接修改或移除該儲存桶政策。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"Versioning protects against accidental overwrites/deletes surfacing as data loss but does not make data immutable — any user with s3:DeleteObjectVersion (which an administrator has) can still permanently delete specific object versions.","why_zh":"版本控管只能防止意外覆寫/刪除造成的資料遺失，並不能讓資料不可變——任何擁有 s3:DeleteObjectVersion 權限的使用者（管理員必然有）仍可永久刪除特定物件版本。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonS3/latest/userguide/object-lock.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonS3/latest/userguide/object-lock-managing.html#object-lock-managing-replication","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/aws-backup/latest/devguide/vault-lock.html"]}},{"id":34,"question_en":"A security engineer wants to forward custom application-security logs from an Amazon EC2 instance to Amazon CloudWatch. The security engineer installs the CloudWatch agent on the EC2 instance and adds the path of the logs to the CloudWatch configuration file. However, CloudWatch does not receive the logs. The security engineer verifies that the awslogs service is running on the EC2 instance. What should the security engineer do next to resolve the issue?","question_zh":"安全工程师希望将自定义应用程序安全日志从 Amazon EC2 实例转发到 Amazon CloudWatch。该工程师在 EC2 实例上安 装了 CloudWatch 代理，并将日志路径添加到 CloudWatch 配置文件中。 然而，CloudWatch 没有接收到日志。安全工程师确认 awslogs 服务正在 EC2 实例上运行。 安全工程师接下来应该采取什么措施来解决该问题？","options_en":{"A":"Add AWS CloudTrail to the trust policy of the EC2 instance. Send the custom logs to CloudTrail instead of CloudWatch.","B":"Add Amazon S3 to the trust policy of the EC2 instance. Configure the application to write the custom logs to an S3 bucket that CloudWatch can use to ingest the logs.","C":"Add Amazon Inspector to the trust policy of the EC2 instance. Use Amazon Inspector instead of the CloudWatch agent to collect the custom logs.","D":"Attach the CloudWatchAgentServerPolicy AWS managed policy to the EC2 instance role."},"options_zh":{"A":"将 AWS CloudTrail 添加到 EC2 实例的信任策略中，将自定义日志发送到 CloudTrail 而不是 CloudWatch。","B":"将 Amazon S3 添加到 EC2 实例的信任策略中。配置应用程序将自定义日志写入 S3 存储桶，以便 CloudWatch 可以 从中摄取日志。","C":"将 Amazon Inspector 添加到 EC2 实例的信任策略中。使用 Amazon Inspector 而不是 CloudWatch 代理来收集自定 义日志。","D":"将 CloudWatchAgentServerPolicy AWS 管理策略附加到 EC2 实例角色。"},"answer":["D"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Storage","Compute","Monitoring/Ops"],"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選","research":{"verdict":["D"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"The CloudWatch agent is installed, its configuration file already lists the custom log path, and the awslogs/CloudWatch agent service is confirmed running — so the install and config steps are not the problem. AWS's official prerequisites page for the CloudWatch agent states that before the agent can send data (including custom logs) from an EC2 instance, you must create an IAM role with the CloudWatchAgentServerPolicy AWS managed policy attached and then attach that role to the instance; without it, the agent runs but every logs:CreateLogGroup/CreateLogStream/PutLogEvents call is denied, so nothing ever reaches CloudWatch Logs — exactly the symptom in the question. That makes attaching CloudWatchAgentServerPolicy to the EC2 instance role (option D) the correct next troubleshooting step. Options A, B, and C all discard the working CloudWatch Logs pipeline in favor of an unrelated service (CloudTrail records AWS API activity, not app log files; Inspector is a vulnerability-assessment service; routing through S3 is not how the CloudWatch agent ships logs), and all three also misuse 'trust policy' — a trust policy defines which principals may assume a role, not what data sources or destinations the instance can reach.","explanation_zh":"CloudWatch agent 已安裝、設定檔已包含自訂日誌路徑，且確認 awslogs／CloudWatch agent 服務正在執行——所以問題不在安裝或設定步驟。AWS 官方 CloudWatch agent 前置條件文件說明：EC2 執行個體要讓 agent 傳送資料（含自訂日誌）到 CloudWatch 之前，必須建立一個附加 CloudWatchAgentServerPolicy 這個 AWS 受管政策的 IAM role，並將該 role 附加到執行個體；若缺少此步驟，agent 雖正常執行，但每次呼叫 logs:CreateLogGroup／CreateLogStream／PutLogEvents 都會被拒絕，導致 CloudWatch Logs 完全收不到任何資料——正是題目描述的症狀。因此正確的下一步是把 CloudWatchAgentServerPolicy 附加到 EC2 執行個體的 IAM role（選項 D）。選項 A、B、C 都放棄了原本可行的 CloudWatch Logs 管線，改用不相干的服務（CloudTrail 記錄的是 AWS API 活動而非應用程式日誌檔；Inspector 是弱點評估服務；CloudWatch agent 本身也不是透過 S3 中繼來傳送日誌），而且三者都誤用了「trust policy」一詞——trust policy 只定義哪些主體可以 assume 該 role，與執行個體能存取哪些資料來源或目的地無關。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"CloudTrail records AWS API/management activity, not arbitrary application log files, so you cannot 'send custom logs to CloudTrail' as a substitute for CloudWatch Logs. The described action of adding a service to a role's trust policy is also a misuse of the term — trust policies control which principals can assume the role, not which AWS services the instance can send data to.","why_zh":"CloudTrail 記錄的是 AWS API／管理活動，並非任意的應用程式日誌檔，因此無法把「自訂日誌」改送到 CloudTrail 來取代 CloudWatch Logs。此選項描述的「把服務加進 trust policy」也是誤用——trust policy 控制的是哪些主體可以 assume 該 role，而不是執行個體可以把資料送到哪個 AWS 服務。"},{"letter":"B","why_en":"The CloudWatch agent ships log file contents directly to CloudWatch Logs via the Logs API; there is no supported workflow where CloudWatch 'ingests' arbitrary application logs from an S3 bucket. Rerouting through S3 abandons the intended, already-configured pipeline instead of fixing the missing IAM permission that is actually blocking delivery.","why_zh":"CloudWatch agent 是直接透過 CloudWatch Logs API 把日誌檔內容傳送出去；並沒有一套受支援的流程讓 CloudWatch 從 S3 bucket「擷取」任意應用程式日誌。改繞道 S3 等於放棄了本來已設定好的管線，而不是修正真正阻擋日誌送達的 IAM 權限缺口。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"Amazon Inspector is an automated vulnerability-management service that scans workloads for software vulnerabilities and network exposure — it does not collect, tail, or forward custom application log files to CloudWatch, so it cannot substitute for the CloudWatch agent here. The trust-policy wording is again incorrect.","why_zh":"Amazon Inspector 是自動化弱點管理服務，用來掃描工作負載的軟體弱點與網路暴露面，並不會收集、追蹤或轉送自訂應用程式日誌到 CloudWatch，因此無法在此取代 CloudWatch agent。trust policy 的用法在此同樣不正確。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonCloudWatch/latest/monitoring/prerequisites.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonCloudWatch/latest/monitoring/Solution-EC2-Health.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonCloudWatch/latest/logs/QuickStartEC2Instance.html"]}},{"id":35,"question_en":"A security engineer is designing a solution that will provide end-to-end encryption between clients and Docker containers running in Amazon Elastic Container Service (Amazon ECS). This solution must also handle volatile traffic patterns. Which solution would have the MOST scalability and LOWEST latency?","question_zh":"安全工程师正在设计一种解决方案，以在客户端与运行于 Amazon 弹性容器服务（Amazon ECS） 中的 Docker 容器之间提供端到端加密。该方案还必须能够应对波动的流量模式。 哪种方案具有最高的可扩展性和最低的延迟？","options_en":{"A":"Configure a Network Load Balancer to terminate the TLS traffic and then re-encrypt the traffic to the containers.","C":"Configure a Network Load Balancer with a TCP listener to pass through TLS traffic to the containers.","D":"Configure Amazon Route 53 to use multivalue answer routing to send traffic to the containers.","B":"Configure an Application Load Balancer to terminate the TLS traffic and then re-encrypt the traffic to the containers."},"options_zh":{"A":"配置网络负载均衡器以终止 TLS 流量，然后重新加密流量发送到容器。","B":"配置一个应用负载均衡器，用于终止 TLS 流量，然后重新加密流量发送到容器。","C":"配置一个带有 TCP 监听器的网络负载均衡器，以将 TLS 流量转发到容器。","D":"配置 Amazon Route 53 使用多值应答路由，将流量发送到容器。"},"answer":["C"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Networking/DNS","Security/IAM","Compute","Containers"],"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選","research":{"verdict":["C"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"The requirements are end-to-end encryption between clients and the ECS containers, plus MOST scalability and LOWEST latency under volatile traffic. A Network Load Balancer configured with a plain TCP listener passes the TLS session through untouched — the TLS handshake and encrypted bytes flow straight to the container, which terminates TLS itself. That is genuine end-to-end encryption, with no decrypt/re-encrypt step at the load balancer. Per AWS docs, NLB operates at OSI Layer 4, can handle millions of requests per second, and is built to scale automatically to volatile, spiky traffic with ultra-low added latency, since it only forwards TCP packets rather than parsing HTTP. Options A and B both terminate TLS at the load balancer (NLB with a TLS listener, or ALB with an HTTPS listener) and then re-encrypt to the target — the AWS Elastic Beanstalk docs for TCP Passthrough explicitly contrast this 'relay without decrypting' behavior against listeners that terminate and offload TLS, and note the trade-off that termination lets the LB inspect traffic but breaks strict end-to-end encryption and adds cryptographic processing overhead. B (ALB) is additionally a Layer 7 HTTP(S) proxy, so it always terminates TLS and carries higher per-request processing overhead than a Layer 4 NLB. D (Route 53 multivalue answer routing) is explicitly documented as 'not a substitute for a load balancer': it returns at most eight healthy IP records per DNS query and relies on DNS caching, so it reacts poorly to volatile traffic and provides no connection-level distribution or encryption termination/passthrough behavior at all. Therefore C is the best fit for end-to-end encryption with maximum scalability and minimum latency.","explanation_zh":"題目要求客戶端與 ECS 容器之間端到端加密，並且在流量劇烈波動下要有「最高擴展性」與「最低延遲」。將 Network Load Balancer 設定為純 TCP listener，會讓 TLS 交握與加密位元組原封不動地轉發到容器，由容器自行終止 TLS——這才是真正的端到端加密，負載平衡器完全沒有解密／重新加密的步驟。根據 AWS 文件，NLB 運作在 OSI 第 4 層，每秒可處理數百萬個請求，且專為自動因應劇烈、突發流量而設計，因為它只轉送 TCP 封包、不解析 HTTP，額外延遲極低。選項 A、B 都會在負載平衡器上終止 TLS（NLB 用 TLS listener，或 ALB 用 HTTPS listener）再重新加密到後端——AWS Elastic Beanstalk 的 TCP Passthrough 文件明確將這種『不解密即中繼』的行為，與終止並卸載 TLS 的 listener 做對比，並指出終止 TLS 雖然讓 LB 能檢視流量，但會破壞嚴格的端到端加密，也會增加加解密處理開銷。選項 B（ALB）更是第 7 層 HTTP(S) 代理，必定終止 TLS，且單一請求的處理開銷比第 4 層 NLB 更高。選項 D（Route 53 multivalue answer routing）官方文件明確寫著『並非負載平衡器的替代方案』：每次 DNS 查詢最多只回傳 8 筆健康 IP 記錄，且依賴 DNS 快取，因此對劇烈流量變化反應遲鈍，完全沒有連線層級的分流，也不具備任何加密終止或穿透行為。因此 C 最符合端到端加密＋最高擴展性＋最低延遲的需求。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"Terminating TLS at the NLB (via a TLS listener) and re-encrypting to the containers means the load balancer decrypts the traffic mid-path, which is not strict end-to-end encryption, and the decrypt/re-encrypt cycle adds cryptographic processing latency compared with pure TCP passthrough.","why_zh":"在 NLB 上用 TLS listener 終止 TLS 再重新加密到容器，代表流量在負載平衡器上被解密，並非嚴格的端到端加密；解密／重加密的過程也比純 TCP passthrough 增加加解密延遲。"},{"letter":"B","why_en":"An ALB is a Layer 7 HTTP(S) proxy that always terminates TLS at the listener, so encryption is broken at the LB rather than carried end-to-end to the container; Layer 7 request parsing also adds more per-request latency and generally offers less raw connection throughput than a Layer 4 NLB under volatile traffic.","why_zh":"ALB 是第 7 層 HTTP(S) 代理，一定會在 listener 終止 TLS，加密在負載平衡器就被中斷，而非一路延伸到容器；第 7 層解析請求也比第 4 層 NLB 增加單請求延遲，在劇烈流量下原生連線吞吐量通常也較低。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"Route 53 multivalue answer routing is explicitly documented as 'not a substitute for a load balancer': it returns at most eight healthy DNS records per query and depends on DNS caching by resolvers, so it reacts slowly to volatile traffic shifts, offers no connection-level load distribution, and does nothing to terminate or pass through TLS — it does not address the scalability, latency, or encryption requirements at all.","why_zh":"Route 53 multivalue answer routing 官方文件明確指出『並非負載平衡器的替代方案』：每次查詢最多回傳 8 筆健康 DNS 記錄，且依賴 resolver 端的 DNS 快取，對流量劇烈變化反應緩慢，也沒有連線層級的負載分流機制，更完全不處理 TLS 終止或穿透，因此無法滿足擴展性、延遲或加密的需求。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/elasticloadbalancing/latest/network/introduction.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/elasticloadbalancing/latest/network/load-balancer-listeners.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/elasticbeanstalk/latest/dg/https-tcp-passthrough.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/elasticbeanstalk/latest/dg/environments-cfg-nlb.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/Route53/latest/DeveloperGuide/routing-policy-multivalue.html"]}},{"id":36,"question_en":"A public subnet contains two Amazon EC2 instances. The subnet has a custom network ACL. A security engineer is designing a solution to improve the subnet security. The solution must allow outbound traffic to an internet service that uses TLS through port 443. The solution also must deny inbound traffic that is destined for MySQL port 3306. Which network ACL rule set meets these requirements?","question_zh":"一个公共子网包含两台 Amazon EC2 实例。该子网配置了自定义的网络 ACL。安全工程师正在设计一种解决方案以提升子网的安全性。 该方案必须允许通过 443 端口使用 TLS 协议向互联网服务发送出站流量，同时必须拒绝目标端口为 MySQL 的 3306 端口的入站流量。 哪个网络ACL规则集符合这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Use inbound rule 100 to allow traffic on TCP port 443. Use inbound rule 200 to deny traffic on TCP port 3306. Use outbound rule 100 to allow traffic on TCP port 443.","B":"Use inbound rule 100 to deny traffic on TCP port 3306. Use inbound rule 200 to allow traffic on TCP port range 1024-65535. Use outbound rule 100 to allow traffic on TCP port 443.","C":"Use inbound rule 100 to allow traffic on TCP port range 1024-65535. Use inbound rule 200 to deny traffic on TCP port 3306. Use outbound rule 100 to allow traffic on TCP port 443.","D":"Use inbound rule 100 to deny traffic on TCP port 3306. Use inbound rule 200 to allow traffic on TCP port 443. Use outbound rule 100 to allow traffic on TCP port 443."},"options_zh":{"A":"使用入站规则100允许TCP端口443的流量。使用入站规则200拒绝TCP端口3306的流量。使用出站规则100允许TCP端口443 的流量。","B":"使用入站规则100拒绝TCP端口3306的流量。使用入站规则200允许TCP端口范围1024-65535的流量。使用出站规则100允许 TCP端口443的流量。","C":"使用入站规则100允许TCP端口范围1024-65535的流量。使用入站规则200拒绝TCP端口3306的流量。使用出站规则100允许 TCP端口443的流量。","D":"使用入站规则100拒绝TCP端口3306的流量。使用入站规则200允许TCP端口443的流量。使用出站规则100允许TCP端口443的 流量。"},"answer":["B"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Compute"],"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選","research":{"verdict":["B"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"Network ACLs are stateless, so the return traffic of the outbound TLS (port 443) connection arrives inbound on ephemeral ports (AWS's documented example uses 1024-65535) and must be explicitly allowed by an inbound rule — see the ephemeral-port outbound example in AWS's own NACL walkthrough. NACL rules are evaluated starting with the lowest rule number, and the first matching rule is applied regardless of any higher-numbered contradicting rule. Because MySQL port 3306 falls inside the ephemeral range 1024-65535, the deny rule for 3306 must have a LOWER number than the allow rule for the ephemeral range — the AWS docs explicitly state: 'You might want to add a deny rule in a situation where you must open a wide range of ports, but there are certain ports within the range that you want to deny. Be sure to give the deny rule a lower number than the rule that allows the wider range of port traffic.' Option B does exactly this: inbound rule 100 denies TCP 3306, inbound rule 200 allows TCP 1024-65535 (return traffic for the outbound TLS session), and outbound rule 100 allows TCP 443. Options A and D only add an inbound allow for port 443 itself (not the ephemeral range), so the outbound HTTPS connection's replies — which arrive on a random high-numbered destination port, not 443 — are dropped by the implicit deny; option C evaluates the broad ephemeral allow (rule 100) before the 3306 deny (rule 200), so traffic to 3306 matches the allow first and the deny never takes effect. This confirms the first analyst's answer.","explanation_zh":"Network ACL 是無狀態（stateless）的，因此對外 TLS（port 443）連線的回應流量會以入站方向落在暫時性連接埠（ephemeral ports，AWS 官方範例採用 1024-65535），必須用入站規則明確允許——可參考 AWS 官方 NACL 教學中出站方向允許 ephemeral 埠回應的範例。NACL 規則由最小編號開始評估，第一條符合的規則即生效，後面編號較大的矛盾規則不再作用。由於 MySQL port 3306 落在 1024-65535 範圍內，拒絕 3306 的規則編號必須小於允許整個 ephemeral 範圍的規則——AWS 文件明確指出：「當你需要開放較大範圍的埠、但範圍內有特定埠想要拒絕時，請確保 deny 規則的編號比允許較大埠範圍的規則小」。選項 B 正是如此：入站規則 100 拒絕 TCP 3306、入站規則 200 允許 TCP 1024-65535（對外 TLS 連線的回應流量）、出站規則 100 允許 TCP 443。選項 A 和 D 只允許入站 port 443 本身（而非 ephemeral 範圍），但對外 HTTPS 連線的回應會落在隨機的高位目的地埠（而非 443），因此仍會被隱含拒絕擋下；選項 C 先評估寬鬆的 ephemeral 允許（規則 100），3306 的流量會先命中允許規則，之後編號較大的拒絕規則（規則 200）永遠不會生效。此結論與第一位分析者一致。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"Inbound allow on port 443 does not cover the return traffic of an outbound 443 connection, which arrives on the ephemeral port range (1024-65535) as the destination port; with no ephemeral allow rule, responses hit the implicit deny and the TLS connection never completes.","why_zh":"入站允許 port 443 並不涵蓋對外 443 連線的回應流量（回應的目的地埠落在 ephemeral 範圍 1024-65535）；沒有允許 ephemeral 埠的規則，回應會被隱含拒絕擋下，TLS 連線無法完成。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"Rule 100 (allow 1024-65535) is evaluated before rule 200 (deny 3306); since 3306 is within 1024-65535, inbound MySQL traffic matches the allow rule first and the lower-priority deny rule never takes effect — the exact anti-pattern AWS's NACL docs warn against.","why_zh":"規則 100（允許 1024-65535）先於規則 200（拒絕 3306）評估；3306 落在該範圍內，入站 MySQL 流量會先命中允許規則，優先順序較低的拒絕規則永遠不會生效——這正是 AWS NACL 文件明確警告要避免的反模式。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"Like option A, it only allows inbound port 443 and never allows the ephemeral port range, so return traffic for the outbound TLS connection (destined for a random high port, not 443) is dropped by the implicit deny.","why_zh":"與選項 A 相同，只允許入站 port 443、未允許 ephemeral 埠範圍，對外 TLS 連線的回應流量（目的地是隨機高位埠而非 443）會被隱含拒絕丟棄。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/vpc/latest/userguide/nacl-rules.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/vpc/latest/userguide/vpc-network-acls.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/vpc/latest/userguide/nacl-examples.html"]}},{"id":37,"question_en":"A company has a web application that reads from and writes to an Amazon S3 bucket. The company needs to use AWS credentials to authenticate all S3 API calls to the S3 bucket. Which solution will provide the application with AWS credentials to make S3 API calls?","question_zh":"一家公司有一个网络应用程序，用于读取和写入 Amazon S3 存储桶。该公司需要使用 AWS 凭据对所有针对该 S3 存储桶的 S3 API 调用进行身份验证。 哪种解决方案能为应用程序提供 AWS 凭据以进行 S3 API 调用？","options_en":{"A":"Integrate with Cognito identity pools and use GetId to obtain AWS credentials.","B":"Integrate with Cognito identity pools and use AssumeRoleWithWebIdentity to obtain AWS credentials.","C":"Integrate with Cognito user pools and use the ID token to obtain AWS credentials.","D":"Integrate with Cognito user pools and use the access token to obtain AWS credentials."},"options_zh":{"A":"与 Cognito 身份池集成，并使用 GetId 获取 AWS 凭据。","B":"与 Cognito 身份池集成，并使用 AssumeRoleWithWebIdentity 获取 AWS 凭据。","C":"与 Cognito 用户池集成，并使用 ID 令牌获取 AWS 凭据。","D":"与 Cognito 用户池集成，并使用访问令牌获取 AWS 凭据。"},"answer":["B"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Security/IAM","Storage"],"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選","research":{"verdict":["B"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"Amazon Cognito identity pools (federated identities) are the mechanism that vends temporary AWS credentials capable of signing S3 API calls; Cognito user pools alone never issue AWS credentials, only OIDC/OAuth tokens for authenticating users. AWS's own documentation on the identity pools authentication flow lays out two flows: in the enhanced flow, the app calls GetId (returns only an identity ID) and then GetCredentialsForIdentity (returns AWS credentials); in the basic (classic) flow, the app calls GetId, then GetOpenIdToken (returns an OIDC token issued by the identity pool), then presents that token to AWS STS's AssumeRoleWithWebIdentity, which returns the temporary AWS credentials used to sign S3 requests. Option B names the API call that actually returns AWS credentials, so it is correct. Option A (GetId) only returns a Cognito identity ID -- a required input to the later credential-vending calls, but not credentials itself. Options C and D invoke Cognito user pools directly: a user pool's ID token or access token are bearer tokens for authenticating/authorizing a user against the user pool (and OAuth-scoped resources); they are not AWS credentials and cannot sign SigV4 S3 requests unless first exchanged through an identity pool.","explanation_zh":"Amazon Cognito identity pools（federated identities）才是能發放可簽署 S3 API 呼叫之臨時 AWS credentials 的機制；Cognito user pools 本身完全不會核發 AWS credentials，只會核發用於驗證使用者身分的 OIDC/OAuth tokens。AWS 官方文件描述 identity pools 的驗證流程有兩種：enhanced flow 中，應用程式呼叫 GetId（只回傳 identity ID）後再呼叫 GetCredentialsForIdentity（回傳 AWS credentials）；basic（classic）flow 中，應用程式呼叫 GetId，再呼叫 GetOpenIdToken（回傳由 identity pool 核發的 OIDC token），最後把該 token 交給 AWS STS 的 AssumeRoleWithWebIdentity，由其回傳可用於簽署 S3 請求的臨時 AWS credentials。選項 B 所指名的 API 呼叫確實會回傳 AWS credentials，因此正確。選項 A（GetId）只回傳 Cognito identity ID——雖然是後續取得 credentials 呼叫所需的輸入之一，但本身並非 credentials。選項 C、D 則是直接使用 Cognito user pools：user pool 的 ID token 或 access token 只是用來對 user pool（及 OAuth scope 資源）驗證／授權使用者身分的 bearer tokens，並非 AWS credentials，若未先透過 identity pool 交換，就無法用來簽署 SigV4 的 S3 請求。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"GetId only returns a Cognito identity ID; per AWS's documented enhanced and basic authentication flows, credentials come from a subsequent GetCredentialsForIdentity (enhanced flow) or GetOpenIdToken + AssumeRoleWithWebIdentity (basic flow) call, not from GetId itself.","why_zh":"GetId 只回傳 Cognito identity ID；依 AWS 文件所述的 enhanced 與 basic 驗證流程，credentials 是由後續的 GetCredentialsForIdentity（enhanced flow）或 GetOpenIdToken + AssumeRoleWithWebIdentity（basic flow）呼叫取得，而非 GetId 本身。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"A Cognito user pool ID token is an OIDC token containing identity claims about the authenticated user; it is only an artifact accepted BY an identity pool, and cannot be used directly as AWS credentials without that identity-pool exchange, which this option omits.","why_zh":"Cognito user pool 的 ID token 是含有已驗證使用者身分 claims 的 OIDC token；它只是 identity pool 所接受的其中一種輸入 artifact，若無 identity pool 的交換過程，不能直接當作 AWS credentials 使用，而此選項並未包含該交換步驟。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"A Cognito user pool access token authorizes calls to user pool self-service APIs and OAuth-scoped resources; it is not an AWS credential and cannot sign SigV4 S3 API calls without first being exchanged via an identity pool.","why_zh":"Cognito user pool 的 access token 用於授權呼叫 user pool 自助服務 API 與 OAuth scope 保護的資源；它並非 AWS credential，若未先透過 identity pool 交換，無法用來簽署 SigV4 的 S3 API 呼叫。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/cognito/latest/developerguide/authentication-flow.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/STS/latest/APIReference/API_AssumeRoleWithWebIdentity.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/cognitoidentity/latest/APIReference/API_GetId.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/cognitoidentity/latest/APIReference/API_GetCredentialsForIdentity.html"]}},{"id":38,"question_en":"A company needs to securely deploy resources and workloads across AWS accounts. The accounts are in an organization in AWS Organizations. The company needs to use AWS CloudFormation for infrastructure as code (IaC) management of approved architectural patterns. The company also must enforce tagging requirements and specific guidelines for resource and workload configuration and creation. Which solution will meet these requirements?","question_zh":"一家公司需要在 AWS 账户之间安全地部署资源和工作负载。这些账户位于 AWS Organizations 中的一个组织内。 公司需要使用 AWS CloudFormation 对已批准的架构模式进行基础设施即代码（IaC）管理，同时 还必须强制执行资源和工作负载配置及创建的标签要求和具体规范。 哪种解决方案能满足这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Use CloudFormation stack policies to prevent the creation of resources that do not meet the tagging or configuration requirements. Use Amazon EventBridge rules to detect API calls that attempt to create resources outside of CloudFormation.","B":"Use an AWS CodePipeline pipeline to test and deploy IaC-defined workloads through CloudFormation into the accounts. Use AWS Config rules to enforce the tagging requirements. Apply an SCP to prevent the creation of misconfigured resources in all OUs.","C":"Create an IAM permissions boundary to prevent the creation of misconfigured resources through CloudFormation and to enforce the tagging requirements. Apply the permissions boundary to all account roles. Use AWS Config rules to identify existing resources that are in a misconfigured state.","D":"Use AWS Service Catalog with CloudFormation to manage access to approved architecture configurations. Provision Service Catalog portfolios to the accounts across the organization. Use AWS Config rules to enforce the tagging requirements and other resource configuration policies across accounts."},"options_zh":{"A":"使用 CloudFormation 堆栈策略来阻止创建不符合标签或配置要求的资源。使用 Amazon EventBridge 规则来检测试图在 CloudFormation 之外创建资源的 API 调用。","B":"使用 AWS CodePipeline 管道，通过 CloudFormation 将 IaC 定义的工作负载测试并部署到各账户 中。使用 AWS Config 规则强制执行标签要求，并在所有组织单元（OU）上应用服务控制策 略（SCP），以防止创建配置错误的资源。","C":"创建一个 IAM 权限边界，以防止通过 CloudFormation 创建配置错误的资源，并强制执行标 签要求。将该权限边界应用于所有账户角色。使用 AWS Config 规则识别当前处于配置错 误状态的现有资源。","D":"使用 AWS 服务目录与 CloudFormation 来管理对已批准架构配置的访问。将服务目录产品集提 供给组织内的各个账户。使用 AWS Config 规则在各账户中强制执行标签要求及其他资源配 置策略。"},"answer":["D"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Organizations/Governance","Security/IAM","Serverless/Integration","Monitoring/Ops"],"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選","research":{"verdict":["D"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"The requirement has three parts: (1) IaC via CloudFormation, (2) restrict deployments to approved architectural patterns, and (3) enforce tagging and configuration guidelines across an organization. AWS Service Catalog is the purpose-built service for exactly this: per the Service Catalog admin guide, administrators publish approved CloudFormation-based products into portfolios and 'end users can quickly deploy only the approved IT services they need, following the constraints set by your organization' — standardization is achieved by restricting where/how a product can be launched. With AWS Organizations integration, those portfolios can be shared to all accounts in the organization (imported portfolios appear automatically in member accounts), so users across the org can only launch vetted, pre-approved architectures, with launch constraints controlling exactly how they are provisioned. AWS Config managed rules such as required-tags then evaluate tagging and other resource-configuration compliance across accounts (deployable organization-wide via organization conformance packs/aggregators). Option D combines the governed-provisioning layer (Service Catalog + CloudFormation) with the compliance layer (Config rules), matching every stated requirement. The other options misuse features: stack policies only protect existing stack resources from unintended updates (not creation-time validation), permissions boundaries merely cap the maximum permissions an IAM identity can be granted rather than validate resource configurations or tags, and SCPs act on IAM/API actions and condition keys, not on detailed resource configuration content, so they cannot 'prevent the creation of misconfigured resources' in the way the option claims; none of A/B/C provides a mechanism to limit users to approved architectural patterns the way Service Catalog does.","explanation_zh":"題目有三個需求：(1) 以 CloudFormation 做 IaC、(2) 只允許部署「已核准的架構模式」、(3) 在整個 Organization 強制標籤與資源組態規範。AWS Service Catalog 正是為此而生：依官方 admin guide 所述，管理員把核准的 CloudFormation 範本發佈為 portfolio 中的 products，「end users can quickly deploy only the approved IT services they need, following the constraints set by your organization」，標準化即透過限制 product 可在何處、如何被啟動來達成。搭配與 AWS Organizations 的整合，portfolio 可分享到組織內所有帳戶（成員帳戶會自動看到 imported portfolio），使組織內使用者只能啟動經審核的架構，並可用 launch constraints 精確控管佈建方式。再以 AWS Config 受管規則（如 required-tags）跨帳戶稽核標籤與其他資源組態合規（可用 organization conformance packs 全組織部署）。選項 D 同時涵蓋「受控佈建」（Service Catalog + CloudFormation）與「合規稽核」（Config rules），完整符合需求。其他選項都誤用功能：stack policy 只在堆疊「更新」時保護既有資源不被誤改，並非建立時驗證；permissions boundary 只是設定 IAM 身分可被授予的權限上限，並不會驗證資源組態或標籤；SCP 作用於 IAM/API 動作與條件鍵，無法檢查細部資源組態內容，因此無法如選項所述「阻止建立錯誤設定的資源」；A/B/C 都沒有像 Service Catalog 那樣把使用者限制在核准架構模式內的機制。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"CloudFormation stack policies only protect resources in an existing stack from unintentional changes during stack UPDATE operations; they cannot validate tags or configurations at creation time, and EventBridge detection of out-of-band API calls is detective, not preventive, and does not deliver approved architectural patterns.","why_zh":"CloudFormation stack policy 只在堆疊「更新」時保護既有資源不被誤改，無法在建立時驗證標籤或組態；EventBridge 偵測繞過 CloudFormation 的 API 呼叫屬於事後偵測而非預防，也無法提供「核准架構模式」的機制。"},{"letter":"B","why_en":"AWS Config rules are detective (they flag non-compliant tags, they don't enforce/prevent at creation), and SCPs act on API actions/condition keys, not on detailed resource configurations, so an SCP cannot broadly 'prevent the creation of misconfigured resources'; a CodePipeline alone also doesn't restrict users to approved architectural patterns across accounts.","why_zh":"AWS Config rules 屬偵測性（標記不合規標籤，無法在建立時強制阻擋）；SCP 只能針對 API 動作與條件鍵，無法檢查細部資源組態，因此無法泛泛地「阻止建立錯誤設定的資源」；單靠 CodePipeline 也無法把各帳戶使用者限制在核准的架構模式內。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"IAM permissions boundaries set the maximum permissions an identity can have; they cannot inspect resource configurations or reliably enforce tagging across all resource types (tag condition-key support is inconsistent), and they provide no mechanism for distributing approved CloudFormation patterns.","why_zh":"IAM permissions boundary 只是設定身分的權限上限，無法檢查資源組態，也無法對所有資源類型可靠地強制標籤（tag 條件鍵支援度不一），更沒有分發「核准 CloudFormation 架構模式」的機制。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/servicecatalog/latest/adminguide/introduction.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/servicecatalog/latest/adminguide/catalogs_portfolios_sharing.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/organizations/latest/userguide/services-that-can-integrate-servicecatalog.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/config/latest/developerguide/required-tags.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AWSCloudFormation/latest/UserGuide/protect-stack-resources.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/IAM/latest/UserGuide/access_policies_boundaries.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/organizations/latest/userguide/orgs_manage_policies_scps.html"]}},{"id":39,"question_en":"A security administrator is setting up a new AWS account. The security administrator wants to secure the data that a company stores in an Amazon S3 bucket. The security administrator also wants to reduce the chance of unintended data exposure and the potential for misconfiguration of objects that are in the S3 bucket. Which solution will meet these requirements with the LEAST operational overhead?","question_zh":"安全管理员正在设置一个新的AWS账户。该管理员希望保护公司存储在Amazon S3存储桶中的数据， 并降低因意外数据泄露以及S3存储桶内对象配置错误所带来的风险。 哪种解决方案能在最少的操作开销下满足这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Configure the S3 Block Public Access feature for the AWS account.","B":"Configure the S3 Block Public Access feature for all objects that are in the bucket.","C":"Deactivate ACLs for objects that are in the bucket.","D":"Use AWS PrivateLink for Amazon S3 to access the bucket."},"options_zh":{"A":"为 AWS 账户配置 S3 块公共访问功能。","B":"为存储桶中的所有对象配置 S3 块公共访问功能。","C":"禁用存储桶中对象的访问控制列表（ACL）。","D":"使用 AWS PrivateLink for Amazon S3 来访问存储桶。"},"answer":["A"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Networking/DNS","Storage"],"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選","research":{"verdict":["A"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"both","explanation_en":"AWS docs confirm Amazon S3 Block Public Access (BPA) at the account level is the correct, lowest-overhead control here. The S3 User Guide states BPA lets administrators 'easily set up centralized controls to limit public access... enforced regardless of how the resources are created,' overriding any ACL, bucket policy, or access-point policy that would otherwise grant public access — and AWS recommends turning on all four settings. Critically, the account-level configuration page states: 'Account level settings override settings on individual objects. Configuring your account to block public access will override any public access settings made to individual objects within your account' — this is the exact mechanism that reduces 'the potential for misconfiguration of objects' named in the question, and it is applied once, account-wide, covering all current and future buckets (least operational overhead). Option B is not a real configuration path: the same doc explicitly says 'Amazon S3 doesn't support block public access settings on a per-object basis' — BPA is only settable at the organization, account, bucket, or access-point level, never per object, so B misdescribes the feature. Option C (disabling ACLs via S3 Object Ownership 'Bucket owner enforced') is a valid, AWS-recommended hardening step, but it is configured per bucket, only removes the ACL path to exposure, and does nothing to stop a misconfigured public bucket policy — narrower coverage and more recurring setup work than one account-level BPA toggle. Option D (S3 PrivateLink) only changes the network path for legitimate access from a VPC; it does not evaluate or restrict ACLs/bucket policies at all, so it does not address unintended exposure from misconfiguration, and stands up extra interface-endpoint infrastructure. Net: A uniquely satisfies both stated goals with a single, one-time, account-wide setting.","explanation_zh":"AWS 官方文件證實，在帳戶層級啟用 Amazon S3 Block Public Access(BPA) 正是本題維運負擔最低的正確做法。S3 使用者指南指出，BPA 讓管理員可以「輕鬆建立集中式控制來限制公開存取……無論資源如何建立都會強制執行」，會覆蓋任何原本授予公開存取的 ACL、bucket policy 或 access point policy，且 AWS 建議四項設定全部開啟。關鍵是帳戶層級設定頁面明確寫道：「帳戶層級設定會覆蓋個別物件上的設定；將帳戶設為封鎖公開存取，會覆蓋帳戶內任何物件層級的公開存取設定」——這正好對應題目所說「降低物件設定錯誤（misconfiguration of objects）風險」的需求，而且只需在帳戶層級設定一次，即可涵蓋現有與未來所有 bucket，維運負擔最低。選項 B 描述的其實不是真實存在的設定方式：同一份文件明確指出「Amazon S3 不支援以逐一物件（per-object）為單位設定 Block Public Access」——BPA 只能設定在 organization、帳戶、bucket 或 access point 層級，從未有「物件層級」，因此 B 對此功能的描述有誤。選項 C（透過 S3 Object Ownership 的「Bucket owner enforced」停用 ACL）確實是 AWS 建議的強化措施，但需要逐一 bucket 設定，且只能消除經由 ACL 造成公開的途徑，對於設定錯誤而公開的 bucket policy 完全無效——涵蓋範圍較窄，且需要重複維運設定，負擔高於單一帳戶層級的 BPA 開關。選項 D（S3 PrivateLink）只改變合法存取從 VPC 出發時的網路路徑，完全不會檢查或限制 ACL／bucket policy，因此無法解決設定錯誤導致的意外外洩問題，還需額外建置 interface endpoint 基礎設施。綜合以上，只有 A 能以單次、帳戶層級的設定同時滿足題目兩項需求，故選 A。","distractors":[{"letter":"B","why_en":"Not a real feature: the S3 docs explicitly state 'Amazon S3 doesn't support block public access settings on a per-object basis' — BPA is only configurable at the organization, account, bucket, or access-point level, so this option misdescribes how the control works and, even generously reinterpreted per-bucket, requires far more recurring configuration than the single account-wide setting in A.","why_zh":"此為不存在的設定方式：S3 官方文件明確指出「Amazon S3 不支援以逐一物件為單位設定 Block Public Access」——BPA 只能在 organization、帳戶、bucket 或 access point 層級設定，因此此選項對功能的描述有誤；即便寬鬆解讀為 bucket 層級設定，也遠比 A 的單一帳戶層級設定需要更多重複維運工作。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"Disabling ACLs (S3 Object Ownership: Bucket owner enforced) is a genuine AWS best practice, but it must be configured per bucket, only removes the ACL path to public exposure, and provides no protection against a misconfigured public bucket policy — narrower scope and more recurring setup than the single account-level Block Public Access toggle.","why_zh":"停用 ACL（S3 Object Ownership 的 Bucket owner enforced）確實是 AWS 建議的做法，但必須逐一 bucket 設定，且只能消除經由 ACL 造成的公開途徑，對設定錯誤而公開的 bucket policy 毫無防護——涵蓋範圍較窄，且比單一帳戶層級的 Block Public Access 開關需要更多重複設定工作。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"AWS PrivateLink for S3 only provides private network connectivity from a VPC to S3 over the AWS network instead of the public internet; it does not evaluate, override, or restrict ACLs or bucket policies at all, so it does nothing to reduce unintended exposure from misconfiguration, and it adds the ongoing operational overhead of provisioning and managing interface VPC endpoints.","why_zh":"AWS PrivateLink for S3 只是讓來自 VPC 的存取改走 AWS 私有網路而非公開網際網路，完全不會檢查、覆蓋或限制 ACL 或 bucket policy，因此對降低設定錯誤造成的意外外洩毫無幫助，還會增加建置與維護 interface VPC endpoint 的額外維運負擔。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonS3/latest/userguide/access-control-block-public-access.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonS3/latest/userguide/configuring-block-public-access-account.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonS3/latest/userguide/ensure-object-ownership.html"]}},{"id":40,"question_en":"A company creates AWS Lambda functions from container images that are stored in Amazon Elastic Container Registry (Amazon ECR). The company needs to identify any software vulnerabilities in the container images and any code vulnerabilities in the Lambda functions. Which solution will meet these requirements?","question_zh":"一家公司使用存储在 Amazon 弹性容器注册表（Amazon ECR）中的容器镜像来创建 AWS Lambda 函数。该公司需 要识别容器镜像中的软件漏洞以及 Lambda 函数中的代码漏洞。 哪种解决方案能满足这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Enable Amazon GuardDuty. Configure Amazon ECR scanning and Lambda code scanning in GuardDuty.","B":"Enable Amazon GuardDuty. Configure Runtime Monitoring and Lambda Protection in GuardDuty.","C":"Enable Amazon Inspector. Configure Amazon ECR enhanced scanning and Lambda code scanning in Amazon Inspector.","D":"Enable AWS Security Hub. Configure Runtime Monitoring and Lambda Protection in Security Hub."},"options_zh":{"A":"启用 Amazon GuardDuty。在 GuardDuty 中配置 Amazon ECR 扫描和 Lambda 代码扫描。","B":"启用 Amazon GuardDuty，并在 GuardDuty 中配置运行时监控和 Lambda 保护。","C":"启用 Amazon Inspector。在 Amazon Inspector 中配置 Amazon ECR 增强扫描和 Lambda 代码扫描。","D":"启用 AWS Security Hub。在 Security Hub 中配置运行时监控和 Lambda 保护功能。"},"answer":["C"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Security/IAM","Compute","Containers"],"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選","research":{"verdict":["C"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"The requirement is vulnerability identification in two places: software vulnerabilities in ECR container images and code vulnerabilities in the Lambda function code. Both are Amazon Inspector capabilities. Amazon ECR enhanced scanning is the integration between ECR and Amazon Inspector that continuously scans container images for vulnerable OS and programming-language packages, generating package vulnerability findings. Amazon Inspector Lambda code scanning analyzes the custom application code in Lambda functions and layers using automated reasoning and machine learning to detect code vulnerabilities such as injection flaws, data leaks, missing encryption, and weak cryptography. GuardDuty is a threat-detection service (its Lambda Protection feature monitors Lambda network activity logs for malicious behavior, not code or image vulnerabilities), and Security Hub is a findings-aggregation/compliance service with no native scanning engine — and Runtime Monitoring/Lambda Protection are GuardDuty features, not Security Hub features, making option D internally inconsistent. Therefore enabling Amazon Inspector with ECR enhanced scanning and Lambda code scanning (option C) is the only solution that meets both requirements.","explanation_zh":"題目要求兩種弱點識別：ECR container image 中的軟體弱點，以及 Lambda function 程式碼中的程式碼弱點，這兩者都是 Amazon Inspector 的功能。Amazon ECR enhanced scanning 是 ECR 與 Amazon Inspector 的整合，會持續掃描 container image 中有弱點的作業系統與程式語言套件，產生 package vulnerability findings；Amazon Inspector Lambda code scanning 則使用自動推理與機器學習分析 Lambda function 與 layer 中的自訂應用程式程式碼，找出程式碼弱點（例如注入漏洞、資料外洩、缺少加密、弱加密演算法）。GuardDuty 是威脅偵測服務（其 Lambda Protection 功能只監控 Lambda 的網路活動日誌以偵測惡意行為，不做程式碼或 image 弱點掃描）；Security Hub 是安全發現彙整／合規檢查服務，本身沒有掃描引擎，而且 Runtime Monitoring 與 Lambda Protection 其實是 GuardDuty 的功能而非 Security Hub 的功能，使選項 D 的敘述本身就自相矛盾。因此只有選項 C（啟用 Amazon Inspector 並設定 ECR enhanced scanning 與 Lambda code scanning）能同時滿足兩項需求。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"GuardDuty is a threat-detection service that analyzes logs and runtime activity for malicious behavior; it has no ECR image vulnerability scanning or Lambda code scanning feature. Those are Amazon Inspector features, not GuardDuty features.","why_zh":"GuardDuty 是威脅偵測服務，分析日誌與執行期活動中的惡意行為；它沒有 ECR image 弱點掃描或 Lambda code scanning 功能，這些是 Amazon Inspector 的功能，而非 GuardDuty 的功能。"},{"letter":"B","why_en":"GuardDuty Runtime Monitoring and Lambda Protection detect active threats (e.g., suspicious network activity from Lambda invocations, runtime compromise of container/EC2 workloads); they do not identify software vulnerabilities in images or code vulnerabilities in function code — that is Amazon Inspector's job.","why_zh":"GuardDuty Runtime Monitoring 與 Lambda Protection 偵測的是進行中的威脅（例如 Lambda 呼叫時的可疑網路活動、容器/EC2 工作負載執行期被入侵），不會識別 image 中的軟體弱點或 function 程式碼中的程式碼弱點——這是 Amazon Inspector 的工作。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"Security Hub aggregates and normalizes findings from other services and runs configuration compliance checks; it performs no vulnerability scanning itself, and Runtime Monitoring/Lambda Protection are actually GuardDuty features, not Security Hub features — the option describes a nonexistent configuration.","why_zh":"Security Hub 只彙整並標準化其他服務的安全發現並執行組態合規檢查，本身不做弱點掃描；而且 Runtime Monitoring 與 Lambda Protection 其實是 GuardDuty 的功能，不是 Security Hub 的功能——此選項描述的組態並不存在。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/inspector/latest/user/scanning_resources_lambda_code.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/inspector/latest/user/scanning-ecr.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonECR/latest/userguide/image-scanning-enhanced.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/guardduty/latest/ug/lambda-protection.html"]}},{"id":41,"question_en":"A company ' s security team wants to receive email notification from AWS about any abuse reports regarding DoS attacks. A security engineer needs to implement a solution that will provide a near-real-time alert for any abuse reports that AWS sends for the account. The security engineer already has created an Amazon Simple Notification Service (Amazon SNS) topic and has subscribed the security team ' s email address to the topic. What should the security engineer do next to meet these requirements?","question_zh":"一家公司的安全团队希望接收来自 AWS 的电子邮件通知，以便及时了解有关 DDoS 攻击的滥用报告。安全工程师需要实 施一个解决方案，以实现对 AWS 发送给该账户的任何滥用报告进行近乎实时的告警。安全工程师已创建了一个 Amazon Simple Notification Service（Amazon SNS）主题，并将安全团队的电子邮件地址订阅到该主题。 安全工程师接下来应采取什么措施来满足这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Use the AWS Trusted Advisor API and a scheduled Lambda function to detect AWS_ABUSE_DOS_REPORT notifications.","B":"Create an Amazon EventBridge rule that uses AWS Health and identifies a specific event for AWS_ABUSE_DOS_REPORT. Configure the rule action to publish a message to the SNS topic.","C":"Use the AWS Support API and a scheduled Lambda function to detect abuse report cases.","D":"Use AWS CloudTrail logs with metric filters to detect AWS_ABUSE_DOS_REPORT events."},"options_zh":{"A":"使用 AWS Trusted Advisor API 和一个定时的 Lambda 函数来检测 AWS_ABUSE_DOS_REPORT 通知。","B":"创建一个 Amazon EventBridge 规则，使用 AWS Health 并识别特定的 AWS_ABUSE_DOS_REPORT 事件。将规则操作 配置为向 SNS 主题发布消息。","C":"使用 AWS 支持 API 和定时触发的 Lambda 函数来检测滥用举报案例。","D":"使用 AWS CloudTrail 日志配合指标过滤器来检测 AWS_ABUSE_DOS_REPORT 事件。"},"answer":["B"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Compute","Serverless/Integration","Monitoring/Ops"],"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選","research":{"verdict":["B"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"AWS delivers abuse reports (including DoS abuse reports) as AWS Health events, identified by the event type code AWS_ABUSE_DOS_REPORT (service field ABUSE). AWS Health natively integrates with Amazon EventBridge: AWS Health publishes events to EventBridge on a durable, at-least-once basis, and EventBridge rules can match on detail.eventTypeCode and route matching events to targets including Amazon SNS topics. This is exactly the AWS-documented pattern - the EventBridge IAM conditions reference page literally uses \"AWS_ABUSE_DOS_REPORT\" as its canonical example value for events:detail.eventTypeCode (with events:detail.service = \"ABUSE\"), confirming this is a real, named AWS Health event type intended to be matched by an EventBridge rule. Since the security engineer already created the SNS topic and subscribed the security team's email, the only remaining step is to build the EventBridge rule (source aws.health, detail.eventTypeCode = AWS_ABUSE_DOS_REPORT) with the SNS topic as the target - option B. The 'near-real-time' requirement rules out any scheduled/polling approach: option A (Trusted Advisor API polled by a scheduled Lambda) does not surface AWS Health abuse events and introduces polling latency; option C (Support API polled by a scheduled Lambda) likewise polls on an interval and requires a Business/Enterprise support plan; option D is wrong because CloudTrail records API calls, not AWS Health/abuse notifications, so no AWS_ABUSE_DOS_REPORT event would appear in CloudTrail logs, and CloudWatch Logs metric filters are unrelated to this event stream.","explanation_zh":"AWS 濫用報告（包含 DoS 濫用報告）是以 AWS Health 事件的形式發出，事件類型代碼為 AWS_ABUSE_DOS_REPORT（service 欄位為 ABUSE）。AWS Health 原生整合 Amazon EventBridge：AWS Health 會以持久、至少一次送達的方式將事件發佈到 EventBridge，EventBridge 規則可比對 detail.eventTypeCode 並將符合的事件路由到包含 Amazon SNS topic 在內的目標。這正是 AWS 官方文件所記載的模式——EventBridge IAM 條件參考頁面明確以 \"AWS_ABUSE_DOS_REPORT\" 作為 events:detail.eventTypeCode 的標準範例值（對應 events:detail.service = \"ABUSE\"），證實這是一個真實、具名的 AWS Health 事件類型，設計上就是要讓 EventBridge 規則來比對。由於安全工程師已建立 SNS topic 並訂閱了安全團隊的信箱，剩下唯一要做的就是建立 EventBridge 規則（來源 aws.health、detail.eventTypeCode = AWS_ABUSE_DOS_REPORT），並將該 SNS topic 設為目標——也就是選項 B。題目強調「近即時」，排除了任何排程輪詢方案：選項 A（以排程 Lambda 輪詢 Trusted Advisor API）不會呈現 AWS Health 濫用事件，且會產生輪詢延遲；選項 C（以排程 Lambda 輪詢 Support API）同樣是定期輪詢，還需要 Business/Enterprise 支援方案；選項 D 錯誤是因為 CloudTrail 記錄的是 API 呼叫，而非 AWS Health／濫用通知，CloudTrail 日誌中不會出現 AWS_ABUSE_DOS_REPORT 事件，且 CloudWatch Logs 的 metric filter 與此事件串流無關。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"Trusted Advisor checks do not surface AWS Health abuse events, and a scheduled Lambda polls on an interval, which is not near-real-time.","why_zh":"Trusted Advisor 檢查不會呈現 AWS Health 濫用事件，且排程 Lambda 是定期輪詢，並非近即時。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"Polling the AWS Support API on a schedule introduces detection delay (not near-real-time) and requires a Business/Enterprise Support plan; abuse notices are natively delivered via AWS Health/EventBridge instead.","why_zh":"以排程輪詢 AWS Support API 會產生偵測延遲（非近即時），且需 Business/Enterprise 支援方案；濫用通知本來就透過 AWS Health/EventBridge 原生傳遞。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"CloudTrail records AWS API calls; AWS abuse reports are not API activity, so no AWS_ABUSE_DOS_REPORT event appears in CloudTrail logs, and metric filters belong to CloudWatch Logs anyway.","why_zh":"CloudTrail 記錄的是 AWS API 呼叫；AWS 濫用報告並非 API 活動，CloudTrail 日誌中不會出現 AWS_ABUSE_DOS_REPORT 事件，且 metric filter 是 CloudWatch Logs 的功能。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/eventbridge/latest/userguide/eb-use-conditions.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/health/latest/ug/cloudwatch-events-health.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/health/latest/ug/aws-health-events-eventbridge-schema.html"]}},{"id":42,"question_en":"A company runs a public web application on an Amazon EKS cluster. The company uses an Amazon CloudFront distribution to deploy the application. An Application Load Balancer (ALB) is configured as an origin for the distribution. A security engineer needs to implement a monitoring solution that sends notifications to an existing Amazon SNS topic. The solution must send a notification to the SNS topic when the application receives 10,000 requests from the same end-user IP address during any 5-minute period. Which solution will meet these requirements?","question_zh":"一家公司在 Amazon EKS 集群上运行一个公共网络应用。该公司使用 Amazon CloudFront 分发来部署该应用，并将 Application Load Balancer（ALB）配置为分发的源站。 安全工程师需要实现一个监控解决方案，将通知发送到现有的 Amazon SNS 主题。该解决方案必须在任意 5 分钟内检测到应用程序 从同一终端用户 IP 地址收到 10，000 次请求时，向 SNS 主题发送通知。 哪种解决方案能满足这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Configure CloudFront standard logging. Send logs to an Amazon CloudWatch Logs log group. Create a log group metric filter to send a notification to the SNS topic when the request threshold is breached.","B":"Configure VPC Flow Logs to send logs for the VPC that contains the EKS cluster to an Amazon CloudWatch Logs log group. Create a log group metric filter to send a notification to the SNS topic when the request threshold is breached.","C":"Configure an AWS WAF web ACL with an Autonomous System Number match rule. Associate the web ACL with the ALB. Create an Amazon CloudWatch metric alarm to send a notification to the SNS topic when the ASN match rule request threshold is breached.","D":"Configure an AWS WAF web ACL with a rate-based rule. Associate the web ACL with the CloudFront distribution. Create an Amazon CloudWatch metric alarm to send a notification to the SNS topic when the rate-based rule request threshold is breached."},"options_zh":{"A":"配置 CloudFront 标准日志记录，将日志发送到 Amazon CloudWatch Logs 日志组。创建日志组的 指标筛选器，当请求阈值被超出时，向 SNS 主题发送通知。","B":"配置VPC流量日志，将包含EKS集群的VPC的日志发送到Amazon CloudWatch Logs日志组。 创建日志组的指标过滤器，当请求阈值被超出时，向SNS主题发送通知。","C":"配置一个带有自治系统编号（ASN）匹配规则的 AWS WAF 网站访问控制列表（web ACL）， 并将该 web ACL 与应用负载均衡器（ALB）关联。创建一个 Amazon CloudWatch 指标告警， 当 ASN 匹配规则的请求阈值被超出时，向 SNS 主题发送通知。","D":"配置一个基于速率的 AWS WAF 网站访问控制列表（web ACL），并将该 web ACL 与 CloudFront 分发关联。创建 Amazon CloudWatch 指标告警，当基于速率的规则请求阈值被超出 时，向 SNS 主题发送通知。"},"answer":["D"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Networking/DNS","Security/IAM","Compute","Serverless/Integration","Monitoring/Ops","Containers"],"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選","research":{"verdict":["D"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"AWS WAF rate-based rules are purpose-built for this exact requirement: they count requests aggregated by originating IP address over an evaluation window, and the default window is 300 seconds (5 minutes) with a configurable rate limit (minimum 10). Setting the limit to 10,000 directly implements 'more than 10,000 requests from the same IP in any 5-minute period.' Because CloudFront sits in front of the ALB, the web ACL must be associated with the CloudFront distribution so WAF evaluates the true end-user (viewer) IP; a web ACL on the ALB would see CloudFront edge locations as the source IP. Every WAF rule publishes CloudWatch metrics (AllowedRequests, BlockedRequests, CountedRequests), so a CloudWatch alarm on the rate-based rule's metric can notify the existing SNS topic when the rule starts matching. The other options either cannot aggregate request counts per client IP in a rolling 5-minute window (metric filters count pattern occurrences, not per-IP rates) or match on the wrong attribute (ASN, network flows).","explanation_zh":"AWS WAF rate-based rule 正是為此需求而設計：它以來源 IP address 為彙總鍵，在 evaluation window 內計算請求數，預設視窗即為 300 秒（5 分鐘），rate limit 可自訂（最低 10）。將 limit 設為 10,000 即直接實作「同一 IP 在任意 5 分鐘內超過 10,000 個請求」。由於 CloudFront 位於 ALB 前方，web ACL 必須關聯到 CloudFront distribution 才能看到真正的終端使用者（viewer）IP；若掛在 ALB 上，來源 IP 會是 CloudFront edge 節點。每條 WAF rule 都會發佈 CloudWatch metrics（AllowedRequests、BlockedRequests、CountedRequests），因此可對該 rate-based rule 的 metric 建立 CloudWatch alarm，觸發時通知既有的 SNS topic。其他選項不是無法以每個 client IP 做 5 分鐘滾動視窗的計數（metric filter 只能計算 log pattern 出現次數，無法按 IP 分組計速率），就是比對錯誤的屬性（ASN、網路流量）。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"A CloudWatch Logs metric filter counts log events matching a static pattern; it cannot group by client IP and evaluate a per-IP threshold over a rolling 5-minute window, so it cannot detect '10,000 requests from the same IP'. This would require custom log analytics, far more overhead than a native rate-based rule.","why_zh":"CloudWatch Logs metric filter 只能計算符合固定 pattern 的 log 事件次數，無法按 client IP 分組並在 5 分鐘滾動視窗內針對每個 IP 評估門檻，因此偵測不到「同一 IP 10,000 個請求」，需要額外自建 log 分析，遠比原生 rate-based rule 複雜。"},{"letter":"B","why_en":"VPC Flow Logs capture layer-3/4 network flow metadata inside the VPC; traffic reaching the EKS VPC comes from CloudFront edge IPs, not end-user IPs, and flow logs do not represent HTTP request counts. A metric filter also cannot do per-IP rate aggregation.","why_zh":"VPC Flow Logs 只記錄 VPC 內第 3/4 層網路流量中繼資料；到達 EKS VPC 的流量來源是 CloudFront edge IP 而非終端使用者 IP，且 flow logs 不代表 HTTP 請求數。metric filter 同樣無法做每 IP 的速率彙總。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"An ASN match statement matches requests by the autonomous system number of the source network — it does not count requests per individual IP over a time window. Additionally, associating the web ACL with the ALB (behind CloudFront) means WAF sees CloudFront edge IPs as the source, not end-user IPs.","why_zh":"ASN match statement 是依來源網路的 autonomous system number 比對，並不會在時間視窗內按單一 IP 計數。此外把 web ACL 掛在 CloudFront 後方的 ALB 上，WAF 看到的來源 IP 是 CloudFront edge IP，而非終端使用者 IP。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/waf/latest/developerguide/waf-rule-statement-type-rate-based-high-level-settings.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/waf/latest/developerguide/waf-rule-statement-type-rate-based.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/waf/latest/developerguide/monitoring-cloudwatch.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/waf/latest/developerguide/cloudfront-features.html"]}},{"id":43,"question_en":"A company uses infrastructure as code (IaC) to create AWS infrastructure. The company writes the code as AWS CloudFormation templates to deploy the infrastructure. The company has an existing CI/CD pipeline that the company can use to deploy these templates. After a recent security audit, the company decides to adopt a policy-as-code approach to improve the company’s security posture on AWS. The company must prevent the deployment of any infrastructure that would violate a security policy, such as an unencrypted Amazon EBS volume. Which solution will meet these requirements?","question_zh":"一家公司使用基础设施即代码（IaC）来创建 AWS 基础设施，通过编写 AWS CloudFormation 模板 来部署基础设施。该公司已拥有现成的 CI/CD 流水线，可用于部署这些模板。 在最近的一次安全审计后，该公司决定采用“策略即代码”的方法，以提升其在 AWS 上的安全 防护水平。公司必须防止部署任何违反安全策略的基础设施，例如未加密的 Amazon EBS 卷。 哪种解决方案能满足这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Turn on AWS Trusted Advisor. Configure security notifications as webhooks in the preferences section of the CI/CD pipeline.","B":"Turn on AWS Config. Use the prebuilt rules or customized rules. Subscribe the CI/CD pipeline to an Amazon SNS topic that receives notifications from AWS Config.","C":"Create rule sets in AWS CloudFormation Guard. Run validation checks for CloudFormation templates as a phase of the CI/CD process.","D":"Create rule sets as SCPs. Integrate the SCPs as a part of validation control in a phase of the CI/CD process."},"options_zh":{"A":"启用 AWS Trusted Advisor，并在 CI/CD 管道的首选项部分将安全通知配置为 webhook。","B":"启用 AWS Config，使用预置规则或自定义规则。将 CI/CD 管道订阅到一个 Amazon SNS 主题，该主题接收来自 AWS Config 的通知。","C":"在 AWS CloudFormation Guard 中创建规则集，并将 CloudFormation 模板的验证检查作为 CI/CD 流程的一个阶段来运行。","D":"将规则集创建为SCP，并将其作为CI/CD流程某个阶段中验证控制的一部分进行集成。"},"answer":["C"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Organizations/Governance","Storage","Serverless/Integration","Monitoring/Ops"],"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選","research":{"verdict":["C"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"Two requirements decide this question: 'policy-as-code' and 'prevent the deployment' (a preventive, shift-left control, not a detective one) of CloudFormation-defined infrastructure that violates a security policy such as unencrypted EBS volumes. AWS's own CloudFormation best-practices guide has a dedicated section, 'Implement policy as code with AWS CloudFormation Guard,' describing cfn-guard as an open-source CLI tool that provides a policy-as-code language to validate CloudFormation templates against organization policy rules — and explicitly recommends embedding this validation into CI/CD pipelines to check templates before deployment. You author rule sets in Guard's declarative DSL (e.g., requiring Encrypted: true on AWS::EC2::Volume) and run 'cfn-guard validate' as a pipeline stage; a non-compliant template fails the build and never reaches CloudFormation, which is exactly the preventive control the audit demands. By contrast, AWS Config (option B) — including its managed 'encrypted-volumes' rule — evaluates resources only after they are created or changed, so the unencrypted volume would already exist before any SNS notification fires; this is a detective, not preventive, control. Trusted Advisor (option A) is likewise a detective/advisory service with no template-evaluation or pipeline-blocking capability, and 'webhook notifications in pipeline preferences' is not a real Trusted Advisor feature. SCPs (option D) are AWS Organizations account-level guardrails that restrict IAM API actions; they cannot parse or validate CloudFormation template resource properties and are not 'run' as a CI/CD validation phase. Therefore C is the only option that satisfies both the policy-as-code and preventive-deployment-blocking requirements.","explanation_zh":"本題由兩個要求決定答案：'policy-as-code' 以及『阻止部署』（預防性、左移控制，而非偵測性控制）違反安全政策（例如未加密 EBS volume）的 CloudFormation 基礎設施。AWS 官方 CloudFormation 最佳實務文件有專門章節「Implement policy as code with AWS CloudFormation Guard」，說明 cfn-guard 是一款開源 CLI 工具，提供 policy-as-code 語言，用以依組織政策規則驗證 CloudFormation 模板，並明確建議把此驗證嵌入 CI/CD pipeline，在部署前檢查模板。做法是用 Guard 的宣告式 DSL 撰寫規則集（例如要求 AWS::EC2::Volume 必須 Encrypted: true），再於 pipeline 階段執行 'cfn-guard validate'；不合規的模板會讓建置失敗，永遠不會被送到 CloudFormation 部署，正是稽核要求的預防性控制。相對地，AWS Config（選項 B，包括其受管規則 encrypted-volumes）只在資源建立或變更『之後』才評估，未加密的 volume 早在 SNS 通知發出前就已部署完成，屬於偵測性而非預防性控制。Trusted Advisor（選項 A）同樣是偵測/建議型服務，無法評估模板或阻擋 pipeline 部署，且『在 pipeline 偏好設定中設定 webhook 通知』並非真實的 Trusted Advisor 功能。SCP（選項 D）是 AWS Organizations 帳戶層級的護欄，限制的是 IAM API 動作，無法解析或驗證 CloudFormation 模板的資源屬性，也不是能在 CI/CD 中『執行』的驗證階段。因此只有 C 同時滿足 policy-as-code 與『阻止部署』兩項要求。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"Trusted Advisor is a detective/advisory service that checks existing resources and best practices; it cannot evaluate CloudFormation templates or block a pipeline deployment, and it is not policy-as-code. 'Security notification webhooks in pipeline preferences' is not a real Trusted Advisor integration.","why_zh":"Trusted Advisor 是偵測/建議型服務，只檢查已存在的資源與最佳實務，無法評估 CloudFormation 模板或阻擋 pipeline 部署，也不是 policy-as-code；所謂在 pipeline 偏好設定裡設安全通知 webhook 並非真實的 Trusted Advisor 整合。"},{"letter":"B","why_en":"AWS Config (including its managed 'encrypted-volumes' rule) evaluates resources after they are created or changed, so a non-compliant unencrypted EBS volume would already be deployed before any SNS notification fires — a detective control that fails the 'prevent deployment' requirement.","why_zh":"AWS Config（包括其受管規則 encrypted-volumes）是在資源建立或變更之後才評估合規性，未加密的 EBS volume 早已部署完成才會發出 SNS 通知，屬偵測性控制，無法滿足『阻止部署』的要求。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"SCPs are Organizations-level guardrails that restrict IAM API actions on accounts; they are not written as validation rule sets for CloudFormation template contents and cannot be 'run' as a validation phase inside a CI/CD pipeline. They also cannot express fine-grained resource-property checks like 'EBS volume must be encrypted' as template policy-as-code.","why_zh":"SCP 是 AWS Organizations 帳戶層級的 IAM API 動作護欄，不是針對 CloudFormation 模板內容撰寫的驗證規則集，無法在 CI/CD pipeline 中作為驗證階段『執行』，也難以以 policy-as-code 方式表達『EBS volume 必須加密』這類資源屬性層級的模板檢查。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AWSCloudFormation/latest/UserGuide/best-practices.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/cfn-guard/latest/ug/what-is-guard.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/cfn-guard/latest/ug/setting-up.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/config/latest/developerguide/encrypted-volumes.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/organizations/latest/userguide/orgs_manage_policies_scps.html"]}},{"id":44,"question_en":"A security engineer needs to implement AWS IAM Identity Center with an external identity provider (IdP). Which THREE steps from the following list are required to meet this requirement? (Select THREE.)","question_zh":"安全工程师需要使用外部身份提供商（IdP）来实施 AWS IAM Identity Center。以下列表中哪三个步骤是满足此要求所必需的？（选择三项。）","options_en":{"A":"Configure the external IdP as the identity source in IAM Identity Center.","B":"Create an IAM role that has a trust policy that specifies the IdP's API endpoint.","C":"Enable automatic provisioning in IAM Identity Center settings.","D":"Enable automatic provisioning in the external IdP.","E":"Obtain the SAML metadata from IAM Identity Center.","F":"Obtain the SAML metadata from the external IdP."},"options_zh":{"A":"在 IAM Identity Center 中将外部身份提供商配置为身份源。","B":"创建一个 IAM 角色，并为其设置信任策略，以指定身份提供商（IdP）的 API 端点。","C":"在 IAM Identity Center 设置中启用自动配置。","D":"在外部身份提供商中启用自动配置。","E":"从 IAM Identity Center 获取 SAML 元数据。","F":"从外部身份提供商获取 SAML 元数据。"},"answer":["A","E","F"],"multi":true,"vote":{},"tags":["Security/IAM"],"difficulty":2,"diff_why":"複選","research":{"verdict":["A","E","F"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"Per AWS's official procedure for connecting IAM Identity Center to an external IdP (Settings > Identity source > Change identity source), three actions are required: (1) configure External identity provider as the identity source in IAM Identity Center (A); (2) download the IAM Identity Center service-provider SAML metadata file — AWS states this file 'is required by your external identity provider' to configure the trust relationship on the IdP side (E); and (3) obtain the SAML metadata file from the external IdP and upload it into IAM Identity Center, since 'this metadata file contains the necessary public x509 certificate used to trust messages that are sent from the IdP' (F). Automatic (SCIM) provisioning, covered by options C and D, is a separate, optional layer documented in 'Using SAML and SCIM identity federation with external identity providers' — IAM Identity Center federation and sign-in work with manually provisioned users, so enabling SCIM on either side is not a required step to 'implement' the IdP connection itself. Option B describes IAM SAML federation (an IAM role trust policy referencing a SAML provider ARN), which is an entirely different, unrelated mechanism from IAM Identity Center's external-IdP metadata exchange, and no such role or 'IdP API endpoint' trust policy appears anywhere in the Identity Center setup flow.","explanation_zh":"依 AWS 官方將 IAM Identity Center 連接外部 IdP 的步驟（Settings > Identity source > Change identity source），需要三個動作：(1) 在 IAM Identity Center 中把 identity source 設定為 External identity provider（A）；(2) 下載 IAM Identity Center 的 service provider SAML metadata 檔——AWS 文件明言此檔「外部 IdP 端建立信任關係時是必需的」（E）；(3) 從外部 IdP 取得其 SAML metadata 檔並上傳到 IAM Identity Center，因為「這份 metadata 檔包含用來信任 IdP 傳來訊息所需的 x509 憑證」（F）。選項 C、D 所涉及的自動（SCIM）佈建，屬於「Using SAML and SCIM identity federation with external identity providers」文件中另外描述的選配層——IAM Identity Center 的聯合登入即使使用者是手動佈建也能正常運作，所以在任一端啟用 SCIM 都不是「建立」IdP 連線本身的必要步驟。選項 B 描述的其實是 IAM SAML federation（IAM role trust policy 中引用 SAML provider ARN），這與 IAM Identity Center 的外部 IdP metadata 交換是完全不同、不相關的機制；Identity Center 的設定流程中，從未出現需要建立指向「IdP API endpoint」的 IAM role trust policy 這種步驟。","distractors":[{"letter":"B","why_en":"No such step exists in the IAM Identity Center external-IdP flow. IAM Identity Center manages trust purely via the SAML metadata exchange (download SP metadata, upload IdP metadata); it never requires creating an IAM role, and IAM SAML role trust policies reference a SAML provider ARN — never an 'IdP API endpoint', which is not a real construct in either IAM or Identity Center federation.","why_zh":"IAM Identity Center 的外部 IdP 連接流程中不存在此步驟。IAM Identity Center 純粹透過 SAML metadata 互換（下載 SP metadata、上傳 IdP metadata）來管理信任，完全不需要建立 IAM role；且 IAM 的 SAML role trust policy 引用的是 SAML provider ARN，從來不是「IdP 的 API endpoint」——這在 IAM 或 Identity Center 聯合登入中都不是真實存在的概念。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"SCIM automatic provisioning is an optional, separate feature documented alongside SAML in 'Using SAML and SCIM identity federation with external identity providers'. IAM Identity Center federation and sign-in function correctly with manually provisioned/assigned users, so enabling automatic provisioning is not required to implement the IdP connection.","why_zh":"SCIM 自動佈建是與 SAML 並列、另外記載於「Using SAML and SCIM identity federation with external identity providers」文件中的選配功能。即使使用者是手動佈建／指派，IAM Identity Center 的聯合登入仍可正常運作，因此啟用自動佈建並非建立 IdP 連線的必要步驟。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"Same reasoning as C: enabling automatic (SCIM) provisioning on the external IdP side is optional tooling for keeping users/groups in sync, not a prerequisite for the SAML trust/identity-source configuration that actually 'implements' the IdP integration.","why_zh":"與 C 同理：在外部 IdP 端啟用自動（SCIM）佈建，只是用來同步使用者/群組的選配工具，並非真正「實作」IdP 整合所需的 SAML 信任／identity source 設定的前提條件。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/singlesignon/latest/userguide/how-to-connect-idp.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/singlesignon/latest/userguide/other-idps.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/singlesignon/latest/userguide/manage-your-identity-source-idp.html"]}},{"id":45,"question_en":"A security team manages a company ' s AWS Key Management Service (AWS KMS) customer managed keys. Only members of the security team can administer the KMS keys. The company ' s application team has a software process that needs temporary access to the keys occasionally. The security team needs to provide the application team’s software process with access to the keys. Which solution will meet these requirements with the LEAST operational overhead?","question_zh":"安全团队负责管理公司 AWS 密钥管理服务（AWS KMS）中的客户托管密钥。只有安全团队的成员才能管理这些 KMS 密钥。 公司的应用团队有一个软件流程，偶尔需要临时访问这些密钥。安全团队需要为应用团队的软件流程提供密钥访问权限。 哪种解决方案能在最少的操作开销下满足这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Export the KMS key material to an on-premises hardware security module (HSM). Give the application team access to the key material.","B":"Edit the key policy that grants the security team access to the KMS keys by adding the application team as principals. Revert this change when the application team no longer needs access.","C":"Create a key grant to allow the application team to use the KMS keys. Revoke the grant when the application team no longer needs access.","D":"Create a new KMS key by generating key material on premises. Import the key material to AWS KMS whenever the application team needs access. Grant the application team permissions to use the key."},"options_zh":{"A":"将KMS密钥材料导出到本地硬件安全模块（HSM），并授予应用团队访问该密钥材料的权限。","B":"编辑授予安全团队访问KMS密钥权限的关键策略，将应用团队添加为授权主体。当应用团队不再需要访问权限时，撤销此 更改。","C":"创建一个密钥授权，允许应用团队使用KMS密钥。当应用团队不再需要访问权限时，撤销该授权。","D":"在本地生成密钥材料，创建新的KMS密钥。当应用团队需要访问时，将密钥材料导入AWS KMS，并授予应用团队使用该 密钥的权限。"},"answer":["C"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Security/IAM"],"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選","research":{"verdict":["C"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"The qualifier is LEAST operational overhead for giving temporary, occasional access to KMS keys. AWS KMS grants are the purpose-built mechanism for exactly this scenario: the AWS KMS Developer Guide states plainly that \"grants are often used for temporary permissions because you can create one, use its permissions, and delete it without changing your key policies or IAM policies.\" A grant is a policy instrument, separate from the key policy, that lets a specified grantee principal (here, the application team's software process) call specific cryptographic operations on the key; when the process no longer needs access, the security team simply retires or revokes the grant, instantly removing all permissions the grant allowed — with no policy editing, no drafting/reverting IAM or key-policy JSON, and no risk of leaving stale principals in the key policy. This cleanly separates key administration (security team via key policy) from key usage (application team via grant), which is the recommended AWS pattern. By contrast, option B requires the security team to manually edit and later revert the key policy every time access is needed, which is more error-prone and higher-touch. Option A is not a supported operation for standard KMS keys — AWS KMS does not allow exporting the key material of AWS-KMS-generated customer managed keys to an external HSM, and even where limited export exists (e.g., certain custom key store scenarios) it is a heavyweight, security-sensitive workflow, not a temporary-access mechanism. Option D describes creating an entirely new key with imported key material and re-importing/expiring it on each access cycle, which manages a different key altogether and carries far more ongoing operational burden. Therefore C is correct.","explanation_zh":"題目關鍵是以「最少營運負擔（LEAST operational overhead）」提供暫時性、偶發性的 KMS key 存取。AWS KMS 的 grant（授權）正是為此情境設計的機制：AWS KMS Developer Guide 明確指出「grants 常用於暫時性權限，因為你可以建立 grant、使用其權限，然後刪除它，而不需更改 key policy 或 IAM policy」。grant 是獨立於 key policy 的政策工具，可讓指定的 grantee principal（此處為應用團隊的軟體程序）對該 key 執行指定的加密操作；當程序不再需要存取時，安全團隊只需 retire 或 revoke 該 grant，就能立即移除該 grant 所賦予的所有權限——完全不必編輯政策、不必撰寫再還原 IAM 或 key policy 的 JSON，也不會在 key policy 中殘留過期的 principal。這使金鑰管理權（安全團隊透過 key policy）與金鑰使用權（應用團隊透過 grant）清楚分離，是 AWS 建議的做法。相較之下，選項 B 要求安全團隊每次需要授權時都手動編輯並之後還原 key policy，更繁瑣也更容易出錯。選項 A 對標準 KMS key 而言並非受支援的操作——AWS KMS 不允許將 AWS-KMS 產生的 customer managed key 之金鑰材料匯出到外部 HSM，即使在少數有限的匯出情境（例如特定 custom key store 場景）中，那也是一套沉重且高度安全敏感的流程，而非暫時存取機制。選項 D 描述的是建立一把全新的、以匯入金鑰材料為來源的 key，且每次存取循環都要重新匯入／處理到期，等於在管理另一把完全不同的 key，營運負擔遠高於使用 grant。因此正確答案為 C。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"AWS KMS does not support exporting the key material of standard AWS-KMS-generated customer managed keys to an on-premises HSM; handing raw key material to another team also completely bypasses KMS's grant/policy-based access control — this is not a supported temporary-access pattern and carries maximal security and operational risk.","why_zh":"AWS KMS 不支援將標準、由 AWS-KMS 產生金鑰材料的 customer managed key 匯出到地端 HSM；把原始金鑰材料交給另一個團隊，也完全繞過 KMS 以 grant／policy 為基礎的存取控制——這不是受支援的暫時存取模式，且安全與營運風險最高。"},{"letter":"B","why_en":"Adding and later removing the application team as principals in the key policy works technically, but it requires the security team to manually edit and revert the key policy JSON every time access is granted or revoked — more error-prone and higher operational overhead than creating/revoking a scoped grant.","why_zh":"在 key policy 中新增應用團隊為 principal、之後再移除，技術上可行，但每次授權與收回都需要安全團隊手動編輯並還原 key policy 的 JSON——比建立／撤銷範圍明確的 grant 更容易出錯、營運負擔也更高。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"This describes creating and repeatedly re-importing key material into a brand-new KMS key rather than granting temporary access to the existing keys the security team already administers — it manages a separate key lifecycle (import, expiration, re-import) and does not solve the stated requirement with anywhere near the same efficiency.","why_zh":"此選項描述的是建立一把全新的 KMS key 並反覆重新匯入金鑰材料，而非對安全團隊已在管理的現有 key 授予暫時存取權——這等於要管理另一套金鑰生命週期（匯入、到期、再匯入），效率遠不如使用 grant，也未真正解決題目需求。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/kms/latest/developerguide/grants.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/kms/latest/developerguide/grant-manage.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/kms/latest/developerguide/key-policies.html"]}},{"id":46,"question_en":"A company has a web application that reads from and writes to an Amazon S3 bucket. The company needs to authenticate all S3 API calls with AWS credentials. Which solution will provide the application with AWS credentials?","question_zh":"一家公司有一个网络应用程序，用于读取和写入 Amazon S3 存储桶。该公司需要使用 AWS 凭据对所有 S3 API 调用进行身份验 证。 哪个解决方案将为应用程序提供 AWS 凭据？","options_en":{"A":"Use Amazon Cognito identity pools and the GetId API.","B":"Use Amazon Cognito identity pools and AssumeRoleWithWebIdentity.","C":"Use Amazon Cognito user pools with ID tokens.","D":"Use Amazon Cognito user pools with access tokens."},"options_zh":{"A":"使用 Amazon Cognito 身份池和 GetId API。","B":"使用 Amazon Cognito 身份池和 AssumeRoleWithWebIdentity。","C":"使用 Amazon Cognito 用户池和 ID 令牌。","D":"使用 Amazon Cognito 用户池和访问令牌。"},"answer":["B"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Security/IAM","Storage"],"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選","research":{"verdict":["B"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"both","explanation_en":"The app needs actual AWS credentials (access key, secret key, session token) to SigV4-sign S3 API calls, and only Amazon Cognito identity pools (federated identities) vend AWS credentials — user pools authenticate users but hand back OIDC JWTs, not AWS credentials. AWS's own 'Identity pools authentication flow' doc describes two flows: the enhanced flow (GetId -> GetCredentialsForIdentity) and the basic/classic flow (GetId -> GetOpenIdToken -> AssumeRoleWithWebIdentity), and states plainly that in the classic flow 'AWS Security Token Service (AWS STS) returns AWS credentials' after the AssumeRoleWithWebIdentity call, which the app then uses to sign AWS API requests. Of the two identity-pool options given, GetId (option A) is only step 1 of either flow and returns nothing but an identity ID — no credentials — whereas AssumeRoleWithWebIdentity (option B) is the STS call that actually returns temporary AWS credentials, making B the mechanism that delivers usable AWS credentials to the app. Options C and D name user pool tokens (ID token and access token respectively); per 'Common Amazon Cognito scenarios,' user pool tokens must first be exchanged through an identity pool before any AWS credentials are obtained, so by themselves they cannot authenticate S3 API calls.","explanation_zh":"應用程式需要真正的 AWS credentials（access key、secret key、session token）才能以 SigV4 簽署 S3 API 呼叫，而只有 Amazon Cognito identity pools（federated identities）會發放 AWS credentials——user pools 只負責驗證使用者身分，回傳的是 OIDC JWT，不是 AWS credentials。AWS 官方文件《Identity pools authentication flow》說明 identity pools 有兩種流程：enhanced flow（GetId -> GetCredentialsForIdentity）以及 basic（classic）flow（GetId -> GetOpenIdToken -> AssumeRoleWithWebIdentity），並明確指出在 classic flow 中，呼叫 AssumeRoleWithWebIdentity 之後「AWS Security Token Service (AWS STS) returns AWS credentials」，應用程式再用這組 credentials 簽署 AWS API 請求。在題目給出的兩個 identity pool 選項中，GetId（選項 A）只是任一流程的第一步，只回傳 identity ID、不含 credentials；而 AssumeRoleWithWebIdentity（選項 B）才是向 STS 取得臨時 AWS credentials 的呼叫，因此 B 才是真正能交付可用 AWS credentials 給應用程式的機制。選項 C、D 提到的是 user pool 的 token（ID token 與 access token）；根據《Common Amazon Cognito scenarios》文件，user pool token 必須先透過 identity pool 交換才能取得 AWS credentials，本身無法用來驗證 S3 API 呼叫。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"GetId is only step 1 of either identity-pool authflow and returns solely a unique identity ID from the identity pool — no AWS credentials are issued at this step; credentials require a further GetCredentialsForIdentity (enhanced flow) or GetOpenIdToken+AssumeRoleWithWebIdentity (classic flow) call.","why_zh":"GetId 只是任一 identity pool 驗證流程的第一步，只會回傳 identity pool 中唯一的 identity ID，這一步並不會發出 AWS credentials；credentials 需要再呼叫 GetCredentialsForIdentity（enhanced flow）或 GetOpenIdToken 加上 AssumeRoleWithWebIdentity（classic flow）才能取得。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"User pool ID tokens are OIDC JWTs carrying user identity claims for the user pool itself (or back-end resource authorization); they are not AWS credentials and cannot SigV4-sign S3 calls unless first exchanged for credentials through an identity pool.","why_zh":"User pool 的 ID token 是攜帶使用者身分 claims 的 OIDC JWT，用於 user pool 本身或後端資源授權，並非 AWS credentials，若未先透過 identity pool 交換，就無法用來對 S3 進行 SigV4 簽署呼叫。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"User pool access tokens authorize OAuth scopes and calls to the user pool's own API (e.g., GetUser); like ID tokens they are not AWS credentials and cannot authenticate SigV4-signed AWS API requests on their own.","why_zh":"User pool 的 access token 用於授權 OAuth scopes 以及呼叫 user pool 本身的 API（例如 GetUser），與 ID token 一樣並非 AWS credentials，無法單獨用來驗證 SigV4 簽署的 AWS API 請求。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/cognito/latest/developerguide/authentication-flow.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/STS/latest/APIReference/API_AssumeRoleWithWebIdentity.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/cognito/latest/developerguide/cognito-scenarios.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/cognitoidentity/latest/APIReference/API_GetId.html"]}},{"id":47,"question_en":"A company ' s security engineer receives an abuse notification from AWS. The notification indicates that someone is hosting malware from the company ' s AWS account. After investigation, the security engineer finds a new Amazon S3 bucket that an IAM user created without authorization. Which combination of steps should the security engineer take toMINIMIZE the consequencesof this compromise? (Select THREE.)","question_zh":"一家公司的安全工程师收到AWS发出的滥用通知，提示有人正通过该公司的AWS账户托管恶意软件。经调查后，安全工 程师发现一名IAM用户未经授权创建了一个新的Amazon S3存储桶。 安全工程师应采取哪些步骤组合来最小化此次泄露事件的后果？（选择三项。）","options_en":{"A":"Encrypt all AWS CloudTrail logs.","B":"Turn on Amazon GuardDuty.","C":"Change the password for all IAM users.","D":"Rotate or delete all AWS access keys.","E":"Take snapshots of all Amazon Elastic Block Store (Amazon EBS) volumes.","F":"Delete any resources that are unrecognized or unauthorized."},"options_zh":{"A":"加密所有 AWS CloudTrail 日志。","B":"启用 Amazon GuardDuty。","C":"更改所有 IAM 用户的密码。","D":"旋转或删除所有 AWS 访问密钥。","E":"对所有 Amazon 弹性块存储（Amazon EBS）卷进行快照。","F":"删除任何无法识别或未经授权的资源。"},"answer":["B","D","F"],"multi":true,"vote":{},"tags":["Security/IAM","Storage","Monitoring/Ops"],"difficulty":3,"diff_why":"複選・題庫與社群皆錯","research":{"verdict":["C","D","F"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"neither","explanation_en":"An abuse notification from AWS plus an unauthorized S3 bucket created by an unrecognized IAM user indicates that IAM credentials (and/or the console sign-in) have been compromised, so the task is containment and eradication of what has already happened, not future detection. AWS's own remediation guidance for this exact scenario is the AWS re:Post Knowledge Center article 'Resolve issues with unauthorized activity in AWS accounts' (formerly 'What do I do if I notice unauthorized activity in my AWS account?'), which the Amazon GuardDuty documentation ('Remediating potentially compromised AWS credentials') also points to for suspected credential compromise. That article's remediation steps are: (1) change the passwords of the IAM users you created, to cut off console access obtained with stolen credentials; (2) rotate or delete the AWS access keys of the affected account, to cut off programmatic/API access (deactivate first, verify apps still work, then delete); and (3) delete any resources you don't recognize or didn't authorize (unsanctioned EC2 instances, IAM users/roles, access keys, policies, and here specifically the rogue S3 bucket hosting malware), which stops the abuse and the ongoing cost/liability. That is exactly options C, D, and F. Turning on GuardDuty (B) is a detective control for finding future or ongoing threats — it does not revoke the attacker's already-obtained credentials or remove the malicious bucket, so it does not minimize the consequences of a compromise that has already been identified and reported by AWS. Encrypting CloudTrail logs (A) is a data-protection hardening measure unrelated to containment. Taking EBS snapshots (E) is an evidence-preservation/forensics step for EC2, irrelevant to an S3-bucket/IAM-credential incident and does not reduce impact. The dump's suggested answer (B, D, F) incorrectly substitutes a detective control (GuardDuty) for the essential credential-lockdown step (changing IAM passwords), so the first analyst's C/D/F is correct and the dump's B/D/F is wrong.","explanation_zh":"收到 AWS 的濫用通知，且發現一個由未經授權的 IAM user 建立的 S3 bucket，代表 IAM 憑證（及／或 console 登入）已遭入侵，此時的任務是圍堵（containment）與根除（eradication）已發生的事件，而非偵測未來威脅。AWS 官方針對此情境的補救指引，正是 AWS re:Post Knowledge Center 文章「Resolve issues with unauthorized activity in AWS accounts」（舊稱「What do I do if I notice unauthorized activity in my AWS account?」），Amazon GuardDuty 文件「Remediating potentially compromised AWS credentials」在懷疑憑證遭入侵時也會指向這篇文章。該文章列出的補救步驟為：(1) 更改你所建立的 IAM users 的密碼，切斷以被竊憑證取得的 console 存取；(2) 輪換或刪除受影響帳號的 AWS access keys，切斷程式化／API 存取（先停用、確認應用程式仍正常運作，再刪除）；以及 (3) 刪除任何無法辨識或未經授權的資源（未經批准的 EC2 執行個體、IAM users/roles、access keys、policies，此處具體就是那個散布惡意軟體的 S3 bucket），以停止濫用及後續的成本與責任風險。這正好對應選項 C、D、F。開啟 GuardDuty（B）屬於偵測性控制，用於發現未來或進行中的威脅，並不能撤銷攻擊者已取得的憑證，也不能移除惡意 bucket，因此對於 AWS 已經確認並通報的入侵事件，無法降低其後果。加密 CloudTrail 日誌（A）是與圍堵無關的資料保護強化措施。對 EBS volumes 建立 snapshot（E）是針對 EC2 的證據保存／鑑識步驟，與 S3 bucket／IAM 憑證事件無關，無法降低影響。題庫給出的建議答案（B、D、F）錯誤地以偵測性控制（GuardDuty）取代了關鍵的憑證鎖定步驟（更改 IAM 密碼），因此第一位分析師提出的 C/D/F 才是正確答案，題庫的 B/D/F 是錯的。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"Encrypting CloudTrail logs is a data-protection hardening measure for audit trail confidentiality; it does nothing to revoke the compromised credentials or remove the malicious S3 bucket, so it does not minimize the consequences of this specific incident.","why_zh":"加密 CloudTrail 日誌是為了稽核軌跡機密性所做的資料保護強化措施，無法撤銷已遭入侵的憑證，也無法移除惡意 S3 bucket，對降低本次事件的後果沒有幫助。"},{"letter":"B","why_en":"GuardDuty is a detective control aimed at finding future or ongoing threats via threat intelligence and anomaly detection; the compromise here has already been identified (AWS itself reported it), and enabling GuardDuty neither revokes the attacker's IAM access nor deletes the malware-hosting bucket, so per AWS's own KC remediation article it is not one of the containment/eradication actions that minimize consequences.","why_zh":"GuardDuty 是透過威脅情報與異常偵測來發現未來或進行中威脅的偵測性控制；本案的入侵已被確認（AWS 已主動通報），開啟 GuardDuty 既不能撤銷攻擊者的 IAM 存取權，也不能刪除散布惡意軟體的 bucket，依 AWS 官方 KC 補救文章，這並非能降低後果的圍堵／根除動作之一。"},{"letter":"E","why_en":"Taking EBS snapshots is an evidence-preservation/forensics step relevant to compromised EC2 instances; this incident involves an S3 bucket and IAM credentials, not EBS volumes, and merely preserving data does not reduce or contain the impact of the compromise.","why_zh":"建立 EBS snapshot 是與遭入侵 EC2 執行個體相關的證據保存／鑑識步驟；本次事件涉及的是 S3 bucket 與 IAM 憑證，並非 EBS volumes，單純保存資料並不能降低或圍堵入侵造成的影響。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/guardduty/latest/ug/compromised-creds.html","https://repost.aws/knowledge-center/potential-account-compromise","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/IAM/latest/UserGuide/id_credentials_access-keys.html","https://github.com/aws-samples/aws-customer-playbook-framework/blob/main/docs/Compromised_IAM_Credentials.md"]}},{"id":48,"question_en":"A company allows users to download its mobile app onto their phones. The app is MQTT based and connectsto AWS IoT Core to subscribe to specific client-related topics. Recently, the company discovered that some malicious attackers have been trying to get a Trojan horse onto legitimate mobile phones. The Trojan horse poses as the authentic application and uses a client ID with injected special characters to gain access to topics outside the client ' s privilege scope. Which combination of actions should the company take to prevent this threat? (Select TWO.)","question_zh":"一家公司允许用户将移动应用程序下载到手机上。该应用基于MQTT协议，连接至AWS IoT Core，用于订阅与特定客户端相 关的主题。最近，该公司发现一些恶意攻击者试图将木马程序植入合法的手机中。该木马伪装成正版应用程序，并使用包含 注入特殊字符的客户端ID，从而访问超出客户端权限范围的主题。 公司应采取哪些措施的组合来防止这一威胁？（选择两项。）","options_en":{"A":"In the application, use an IoT thing name as the client ID to connect the device to AWS IoT Core.","B":"In the application, add a client ID check. Disconnect from the server if any special character is detected.","C":"Apply an AWS IoT Core policy that allows \" AWSIoTWirelessDataAccess \" with the principal set to \" client/${iot:Connection.Thing.ThingName} \" .","D":"Apply an AWS IoT Core policy to the device to allow \" iot:Connect \" with the resource set to \" client /${iot:ClientId} \" .","E":"Apply an AWS IoT Core policy to the device to allow \" iot:Connect \" with the resource set to \" client /${iot:Connection.Thing.ThingName} \" ."},"options_zh":{"A":"在应用程序中，使用物联网设备名称作为客户端ID，将设备连接到AWS IoT Core。","B":"在应用程序中添加客户端ID检查，若检测到任何特殊字符，则断开与服务器的连接。","C":"应用一个 AWS IoT Core 策略，允许“AWSIoTWirelessDataAccess”权限，并将主体设置为“client/${iot:Connection. Thing.ThingName}”。","D":"为设备应用一个 AWS IoT Core 策略，允许“iot:Connect”操作，并将资源设置为“client/${iot:ClientId}”。","E":"为设备应用一个 AWS IoT Core 策略，允许“iot:Connect”操作，并将资源设置为“client/${iot:Connection.Thing. ThingName}”。"},"answer":["A","E"],"multi":true,"vote":{},"tags":["Uncategorized"],"difficulty":2,"diff_why":"複選","research":{"verdict":["A","E"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"This is a classic MQTT client-ID injection attack against an AWS IoT Core policy that relies on the raw ${iot:ClientId} variable. The AWS IoT Core developer guide explicitly warns: 'Using the policy variable ${iot:ClientId} with Connect is not recommended. There is no check on the value of ClientId... Because any ClientId is allowed, setting a random client ID can bypass thing group policies' — and gives the concrete example that a client can connect using a wildcard/special character (e.g. '+') as the client ID to gain access outside its intended scope. This confirms option D is exactly the vulnerable pattern being exploited, not the fix. The safe alternative is the thing policy variable iot:Connection.Thing.ThingName (option E): per the 'Thing policy variables' guide, this variable 'resolves to the name of the thing in the AWS IoT Core registry for which the policy is being evaluated' — AWS IoT Core determines the thing from the X.509 certificate the device presents at authentication, not from the untrusted client-supplied ClientId string, so an attacker cannot forge it merely by injecting characters into the client ID. For this substitution to work, the docs state a prerequisite: 'the value of clientId in the MQTT connect message or the TLS connection must exactly match the thing name' — meaning the legitimate app must connect using its registered IoT thing name as its MQTT client ID (option A). Together, A (app uses the thing name as client ID) + E (policy keyed off the registry-verified thing name rather than the raw client-supplied ID) closes the injection vector at the server-side authorization layer, which is the only place a Trojan horse impersonating the app cannot bypass the control.","explanation_zh":"這是針對倚賴原始 ${iot:ClientId} 變數的 AWS IoT Core policy 的典型 MQTT client ID 注入攻擊。AWS IoT Core 開發人員指南明確警告：『不建議在 Connect 中使用 policy 變數 ${iot:ClientId}。系統不會檢查 ClientId 的值……因為任何 ClientId 都被允許，設定隨機 client ID 可繞過 thing group policy』，並舉出具體範例：client 可用萬用字元/特殊字元（如 '+'）作為 client ID 連線，藉此取得超出其預期範圍的存取權。這證實選項 D 正是被攻擊者利用的漏洞寫法，而非修補方式。安全的替代做法是使用 thing policy 變數 iot:Connection.Thing.ThingName（選項 E）：根據『Thing policy variables』文件，此變數『解析為正在評估 policy 之 thing 在 AWS IoT Core registry 中的名稱』——AWS IoT Core 是依裝置驗證時所出示的 X.509 憑證來判斷對應的 thing，而非依賴不可信、由 client 端提供的 ClientId 字串，因此攻擊者無法僅靠在 client ID 中注入字元來偽造它。要讓此替換生效，文件明載前提條件：『MQTT connect 訊息或 TLS 連線中的 clientId 值必須與 thing name 完全相符』——也就是說合法 App 必須使用其在 registry 中註冊的 IoT thing name 作為 MQTT client ID（選項 A）。A（App 用 thing name 當 client ID）＋ E（policy 以經 registry 驗證的 thing name、而非原始 client 提供的 ID 為依據）兩者合併，才能在伺服器端授權層徹底封住此注入途徑——這也是冒充 App 的木馬程式唯一無法繞過的控制點。","distractors":[{"letter":"B","why_en":"A client-side check inside the app is useless here: the threat is a Trojan horse impersonating the app, so the attacker controls the client code entirely and simply omits or bypasses the check. Security controls that matter must be enforced server-side in the AWS IoT Core policy/authorization layer, not in code the attacker can rewrite.","why_zh":"在 App 內做 client 端檢查在此毫無作用：威脅本身就是冒充正版 App 的木馬程式，攻擊者完全掌控 client 端程式碼，可直接省略或繞過該檢查。真正有效的安全控管必須在伺服器端的 AWS IoT Core policy/授權層強制執行，而不是放在攻擊者能重寫的程式碼裡。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"AWSIoTWirelessDataAccess is an AWS managed IAM policy that grants permission to send data to LoRaWAN/Sidewalk devices via the SendDataToWirelessDevice API (AWS IoT Core for LoRaWAN / IoT Wireless) — it has nothing to do with MQTT client-ID authorization. It is also nonsensical as described: 'client/${iot:Connection.Thing.ThingName}' is IoT policy Resource-ARN syntax, not something you set as a 'principal' for an IAM managed policy.","why_zh":"AWSIoTWirelessDataAccess 是 AWS 受管 IAM 政策，授予透過 SendDataToWirelessDevice API 向 LoRaWAN/Sidewalk 裝置傳送資料的權限（屬於 AWS IoT Core for LoRaWAN／IoT Wireless），與 MQTT client ID 授權完全無關。且描述本身也不合理：『client/${iot:Connection.Thing.ThingName}』是 IoT policy 的 Resource ARN 語法，並非可設定給 IAM 受管政策的『principal』。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"This is the vulnerable pattern itself, not a fix. AWS docs explicitly state that using ${iot:ClientId} with iot:Connect is not recommended because there is no check on the ClientId value — an attacker's client with an injected/wildcard client ID still satisfies 'client/${iot:ClientId}' and connects successfully, which is exactly the flaw the attacker in this scenario is exploiting.","why_zh":"這正是漏洞本身的寫法，而非修補方式。AWS 文件明確指出不建議在 iot:Connect 中使用 ${iot:ClientId}，因為系統不會檢查 ClientId 的值——攻擊者以注入/含萬用字元的 client ID 連線時，依然能滿足 'client/${iot:ClientId}'，因而成功連線，這正是題目情境中攻擊者所利用的漏洞。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/iot/latest/developerguide/basic-policy-variables.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/iot/latest/developerguide/thing-policy-variables.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/iot-wireless/latest/developerguide/security-iam-awsmanpol.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/iot/latest/developerguide/pub-sub-policy.html"]}},{"id":49,"question_en":"A company has two AWS accounts: Account A and Account B. Each account has a VPC. An application that runs in the VPC in Account A needs to write to an Amazon S3 bucket in Account B. The application in Account A already has permission to write to the S3 bucket in Account B. The application and the S3 bucket are in the same AWS Region. The company cannot send network traffic over the public internet. Which solution will meet these requirements?","question_zh":"一家公司拥有两个 AWS 账户：账户 A 和账户 B。每个账户都有一个 VPC。运行在账户 A 的 VPC 中 的应用程序需要向账户 B 中的 Amazon S3 存储桶写入数据。该应用程序已具备向账户 B 的 S3 存储 桶写入数据的权限。应用程序和 S3 存储桶位于同一 AWS 区域。该公司无法通过公共互联网传输网 络流量。 哪种解决方案能满足这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"","B":"Deploy a software VPN appliance in Account A. Create a VPN connection between the software VPN appliance and a virtual private gateway in Account B.","C":"Create a VPC peering connection between the VPC in Account A and the VPC in Account B. Update the VPC route tables, network ACLs, and security groups to allow network traffic between the peered IP ranges.","D":"In Account A, create a gateway VPC endpoint for Amazon S3. Update the VPC route table in Account"},"options_zh":{"A":"在两个账户中，为每个可用区的子网创建一个传输网关和VPC连接，并更新VPC路由表。","B":"在账户A中部署一个软件VPN设备，并在该软件VPN设备与账户B中的虚拟私有网关之间创建 VPN连接。","C":"在账户A的VPC与账户B的VPC之间创建VPC对等连接，并更新VPC路由表、网络ACL和安全 组，以允许对等IP范围之间的网络流量。","D":"在账户A中，为Amazon S3创建一个网关型VPC端点，并更新账户A中的VPC路由表。"},"answer":["D"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Networking/DNS","Storage"],"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選","research":{"verdict":["D"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"Amazon S3 buckets are not resources inside any VPC — S3 is a regional service reachable via its public service endpoints or, privately, via a VPC endpoint. The fact that the bucket is owned by Account B is a red herring for the network path: what matters is that the application's VPC (in Account A) and the bucket are in the same Region, and the application already has IAM/bucket-policy permission to write to it. Creating a gateway VPC endpoint for S3 in Account A and adding it to Account A's route table sends all S3-bound traffic over AWS's private network with no internet gateway, NAT device, or extra cost, and it works regardless of which account owns the target bucket, since authorization is handled separately by IAM and the bucket policy. Per AWS's own docs, 'endpoint connections cannot be extended out of a VPC' and gateway endpoints cannot be used across a VPN connection, VPC peering connection, or transit gateway. That single fact eliminates B (software VPN to Account B's VPC), C (VPC peering to Account B's VPC), and A (transit gateway attachments across both accounts): all three only wire the two VPCs together, but S3 is not a resource inside Account B's VPC, so none of them creates a private path to the bucket, and none of them even provisions an S3 endpoint. D is the only option that correctly recognizes the fix belongs entirely within Account A's VPC.","explanation_zh":"Amazon S3 bucket 並不是任何 VPC 內的資源——S3 是區域級服務，可透過公開的 service endpoint，或透過 VPC endpoint 私有存取。bucket 屬於 Account B 這件事其實是網路路徑上的煙霧彈：真正重要的是 Account A 的應用程式所在 VPC 與 bucket 同屬一個 Region，且應用程式已經具備 IAM／bucket policy 授予的寫入權限。在 Account A 建立 S3 的 gateway VPC endpoint 並加進 Account A 的路由表後，所有往 S3 的流量都會走 AWS 私有網路，不需要 internet gateway、NAT device，也不額外收費；且不論目標 bucket 屬於哪個帳戶都適用，因為授權是由 IAM 與 bucket policy 另外處理的。根據 AWS 官方文件，『endpoint 連線無法延伸到 VPC 之外』，gateway endpoint 也無法跨 VPN 連線、VPC peering 連線或 transit gateway 使用。這一點就足以排除 B（連到 Account B VPC 的軟體 VPN）、C（與 Account B VPC 的 VPC peering）、A（兩帳戶間的 transit gateway attachment）：這三個選項都只是把兩個 VPC 接在一起，但 S3 並不是 Account B VPC 內的資源，因此都無法建立到 bucket 的私有路徑，而且三者都完全沒有建立任何 S3 endpoint。只有 D 正確辨識出解法完全落在 Account A 的 VPC 內部即可完成。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"Creating a transit gateway with VPC attachments in both accounts only builds private connectivity between VPC A and VPC B's subnets; it provisions no S3 endpoint at all. Since S3 is not a resource inside Account B's VPC, this never gives the application a private path to the bucket, and AWS docs additionally note that S3 gateway endpoints cannot be used across a transit gateway.","why_zh":"在兩個帳戶建立 transit gateway 並附加 VPC，只是替 VPC A 與 VPC B 的子網路建立私有連線，並未建立任何 S3 endpoint。由於 S3 並非 Account B VPC 內的資源，這樣做永遠無法讓應用程式取得通往 bucket 的私有路徑；AWS 文件也另外指出 S3 gateway endpoint 無法跨 transit gateway 使用。"},{"letter":"B","why_en":"A software VPN between Account A and a virtual private gateway in Account B only provides VPC-to-VPC connectivity; S3 is not inside Account B's VPC, so the VPN tunnel never reaches the bucket, and AWS docs state gateway endpoint connections cannot be extended across a VPN connection.","why_zh":"在 Account A 與 Account B 的 virtual private gateway 之間建立軟體 VPN，只提供 VPC 對 VPC 的連線；S3 並不在 Account B 的 VPC 裡，VPN 隧道根本到不了 bucket，且 AWS 文件指出 gateway endpoint 連線無法延伸到 VPN 連線的另一端。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"VPC peering connects the private IP ranges of the two VPCs, but the S3 bucket has no presence in Account B's VPC; traffic over peering cannot reach S3, and AWS docs explicitly state gateway endpoints cannot be extended across a VPC peering connection.","why_zh":"VPC peering 只連接兩個 VPC 的私有 IP 範圍，但 S3 bucket 並不存在於 Account B 的 VPC 中；經 peering 的流量到不了 S3，且 AWS 文件明確指出 gateway endpoint 無法跨 VPC peering 連線延伸使用。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/vpc/latest/privatelink/vpc-endpoints-s3.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonS3/latest/userguide/privatelink-interface-endpoints.html"]}},{"id":50,"question_en":"A company hosts a web application on an Apache web server. The application runs on Amazon EC2 instances that are in an Auto Scaling group. The company configured the EC2 instances to send the Apache web server logs to an Amazon CloudWatch Logs group that the company has configured to expire after 1 year. Recently, the company discovered in the Apache web server logs that a specific IP address is sending suspicious requests to the web application. A security engineer wants to analyze the past week of Apache web server logs to determine how many requests that the IP address sent and the corresponding URLs that the IP address requested. What should the security engineer do to meet these requirements with the LEAST effort?","question_zh":"一家公司在一个 Apache 网络服务器上托管了一个网络应用程序。该应用程序运行在 Amazon EC2 实例上，这些实例属于一个自 动扩展组。该公司已将 EC2 实例配置为将 Apache 网络服务器日志发送到一个 Amazon CloudWatch Logs 组，该日志组被设置为 一年后过期。 最近，该公司在 Apache 网络服务器日志中发现某个特定 IP 地址正在向网络应用发送可疑请求。安全工程师希望分析过去一周 的 Apache 服务器日志，以确定该 IP 地址发送了多少次请求，以及其请求的具体 URL。 安全工程师应采取什么措施，才能以最少的努力满足这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Export the CloudWatch Logs group data to Amazon S3. Use Amazon Macie to query the logs for the specific IP address and the requested URLs.","B":"Configure a CloudWatch Logs subscription to stream the log group to an Amazon OpenSearch Service cluster. Use OpenSearch Service to analyze the logs for the specific IP address and the requested URLs.","C":"Use CloudWatch Logs Insights and a custom query syntax to analyze the CloudWatch logs for the specific IP address and the requested URLs.","D":"Export the CloudWatch Logs group data to Amazon S3. Use AWS Glue to crawl the S3 bucket for only the log entries that contain the specific IP address. Use AWS Glue to view the results."},"options_zh":{"A":"将 CloudWatch Logs 组的数据导出到 Amazon S3，并使用 Amazon Macie 查询特定 IP 地址和请求的 URL 日志。","B":"配置 CloudWatch Logs 订阅，将日志组流式传输到 Amazon OpenSearch Service 集群。使用 OpenSearch Service 分析日志中 的特定 IP 地址和请求的 URL。","C":"使用 CloudWatch Logs Insights 和自定义查询语法，分析特定 IP 地址和请求 URL 的 CloudWatch 日志。","D":"将 CloudWatch Logs 组的数据导出到 Amazon S3。使用 AWS Glue 爬取 S3 存储桶，仅获取包含特定 IP 地址的日志条目， 并使用 AWS Glue 查看结果。"},"answer":["C"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Security/IAM","Storage","Compute","Monitoring/Ops","Analytics"],"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選","research":{"verdict":["C"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"The logs are already in a CloudWatch Logs group (retained 1 year), so the past week of Apache access logs is directly queryable in place — nothing needs to be exported or moved. CloudWatch Logs Insights is the AWS-documented, purpose-built feature to \"interactively search and analyze your log data in Amazon CloudWatch Logs\": the engineer selects the log group, sets the time range to the last 7 days, and runs a query such as filter @message like /<IP>/ | parse @message for the URL | stats count(*) by URL. This requires zero new infrastructure, zero data movement, and no additional services — clearly the LEAST effort. Every other option requires exporting/streaming the data first and/or misuses a service for this job: Amazon Macie only discovers sensitive data (PII/credentials) in S3 and cannot count requests by IP or extract URLs; AWS Glue crawlers infer schema into the Data Catalog and are not an ad-hoc query/viewing tool (you would still need Athena on top); and per AWS's own documentation, a CloudWatch Logs subscription is a mechanism for \"real-time processing of log data\" that delivers events \"soon after being ingested\" (usually under three minutes) — it only forwards logs generated from the moment the subscription is created onward, so it would not retroactively contain the prior week's historical Apache logs, on top of the added effort of standing up and managing an OpenSearch Service cluster.","explanation_zh":"日誌已經存放在保留 1 年的 CloudWatch Logs log group 中，過去一週的 Apache 存取日誌可以直接就地查詢，完全不需要匯出或搬移資料。CloudWatch Logs Insights 是 AWS 官方文件所定義、專為「互動式搜尋與分析存放在 CloudWatch Logs 的日誌資料」而設計的功能：工程師只需選取 log group、把時間範圍設為過去 7 天，執行類似 filter @message like /<IP>/ | parse @message 取出 URL | stats count(*) by URL 的查詢即可。不需建立任何新基礎設施、不需搬移資料、也不需啟用額外服務，顯然是「最少工作量（LEAST effort）」。其他選項都必須先匯出或串流資料，且/或誤用服務來完成這項工作：Amazon Macie 只能探索 S3 中的敏感資料（PII/憑證），無法依 IP 統計請求數或取出請求的 URL；AWS Glue crawler 只會推斷 schema 並寫入 Data Catalog，本身並非臨時查詢/檢視工具（仍需搭配 Athena 才能查詢）；而根據 AWS 文件，CloudWatch Logs subscription 是用於「即時處理日誌資料」的機制，事件會在攝入後「很快」（通常少於 3 分鐘）被傳送——它只會轉送 subscription 建立之後才產生的日誌，並不會回補過去一週的歷史 Apache 日誌，還得額外佈建與維運 OpenSearch Service 叢集。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"Amazon Macie is a sensitive-data discovery service (finds PII/credentials in S3); it is not a log query/analytics tool and cannot count requests by IP or extract requested URLs. The S3 export step is also unnecessary extra effort.","why_zh":"Amazon Macie 是敏感資料探索服務（掃描 S3 中的 PII/憑證），不是日誌查詢分析工具，無法依 IP 統計請求數或取出請求的 URL；先匯出到 S3 也是多餘的工作量。"},{"letter":"B","why_en":"Per AWS docs, a CloudWatch Logs subscription is a real-time feed that delivers events soon after ingestion — it does not backfill the past week of historical logs — and provisioning/managing an OpenSearch cluster is far more effort than an in-place Logs Insights query.","why_zh":"根據 AWS 文件，CloudWatch Logs subscription 是即時傳送機制，只會傳送建立之後新攝入的日誌事件，不會回補過去一週的歷史日誌；而且佈建與管理 OpenSearch 叢集的工作量遠大於直接用 Logs Insights 就地查詢。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"AWS Glue crawlers only infer schema and populate the Data Catalog; Glue is an ETL/catalog service with no ad-hoc query viewer — you would still need Athena to query the results. Export + crawler + ETL is the opposite of least effort.","why_zh":"AWS Glue crawler 只負責推斷 schema 並建立 Data Catalog；Glue 是 ETL/目錄服務，本身沒有臨時查詢檢視功能，仍需 Athena 才能查詢。匯出＋crawler＋ETL 完全不符合最少工作量。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonCloudWatch/latest/logs/AnalyzingLogData.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonCloudWatch/latest/logs/CWL_QuerySyntax.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonCloudWatch/latest/logs/SubscriptionFilters.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonCloudWatch/latest/logs/Subscriptions.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/macie/latest/user/what-is-macie.html"]}},{"id":51,"question_en":"A healthcare company stores more than 1 million patient records in an Amazon S3 bucket. The patient records include personally identifiable information (PII). The S3 bucket contains hundreds of terabytes of data. A security engineer receives an alert that was triggered by an Amazon GuardDuty Exfiltration:S3 /AnomalousBehavior finding. The security engineer confirms that an attacker is using temporary credentials that were obtained from a compromised Amazon EC2 instance that has s3:GetObject permissions for the S3 bucket. The attacker has begun downloading the contents of the bucket. The security engineer contacts a development team. The development team will require 4 hours to implement and deploy a fix. The security engineer must take immediate action to prevent the attacker from downloading more data from the S3 bucket. Which solution will meet this requirement?","question_zh":"一家医疗保健公司将其超过100万份患者记录存储在Amazon S3存储桶中。这些患者记录包含个人身 份信息（PII）。该S3存储桶内含有数百TB的数据。 安全工程师收到一条由Amazon GuardDuty检测到的“数据外泄：S3/异常行为”告警。经确认，攻 击者正在使用从一台被入侵的Amazon EC2实例获取的临时凭证，该实例拥有对S3存储桶的s3: GetObject权限。攻击者已开始下载存储桶中的内容。安全工程师联系了开发团队，开发团队需要4 小时来完成修复方案的实施和部署。 安全工程师必须立即采取行动，防止攻击者从S3存储桶下载更多数据。 哪种解决方案能满足这一要求？","options_en":{"A":"Revoke the temporary session that is associated with the instance profile that is attached to the EC2 instance.","B":"Quarantine the EC2 instance by replacing the existing security group with a new security group that has no rules applied.","C":"Enable Amazon Macie on the S3 bucket. Configure the managed data identifiers for personally identifiable information (PII). Enable S3 Object Lock on objects that Macie flags.","D":"Apply an S3 bucket policy temporarily. Configure the policy to deny read access for all principals to block downloads while the development team address the vulnerability."},"options_zh":{"A":"撤销与附加到 EC2 实例的实例配置文件相关联的临时会话。","B":"通过将现有的安全组替换为一个没有任何规则的新安全组，对EC2实例进行隔离。","C":"在S3存储桶上启用Amazon Macie，配置用于个人身份信息（PII）的托管数据标识符， 并对Macie标记的对象启用S3对象锁定。","D":"临时应用一个S3存储桶策略。配置该策略，拒绝所有主体的读取权限，以阻止下载，直到开 发团队解决漏洞为止。"},"answer":["A"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Security/IAM","Storage","Compute"],"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選","research":{"verdict":["A"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"The compromised asset here is not the bucket itself but a specific IAM principal's temporary security credentials (the instance profile role attached to the EC2 instance). IAM lets you immediately revoke a role's temporary security credentials: choosing 'Revoke active sessions' on the role attaches an inline AWSRevokeOlderSessions policy that denies all actions for any session token issued before that moment (with ~30 seconds of propagation). Because an explicit deny always wins in policy evaluation, this instantly invalidates the exact stolen session the attacker is using for s3:GetObject, while the EC2 instance's own instance-profile credentials are auto-refreshed by IMDS and unaffected (no other reads on the bucket are disrupted). This is precisely the scenario the AWS IAM 'Revoke role's temporary security credentials' feature is documented for ('if users inadvertently expose their credentials to an unauthorized third party ... you can immediately revoke all permissions to the role's credentials issued before a certain point in time'). It is corroborated by the AWS Security Incident Response service's containment model, which maps 'IAM containment' (attach a deny-all policy to the compromised principal, revoking its ability to act) as the targeted first response when a specific IAM role/user is the compromised resource, distinct from 'EC2 containment' (network isolation via security group) and 'S3 containment' (bucket-wide deny-all-external-access) which apply when the EC2 host or the bucket itself — not a stolen credential — is the compromised asset. Option D (bucket policy denying all principals) would also stop the attacker, but it is the wrong-scoped containment action: it takes down legitimate access for every principal (application, backup job, other services) reading a bucket with over a million patient records for the full 4-hour window, which is unnecessary collateral damage when the actual compromised object is a single role's session, not the bucket. Option B (quarantine the EC2 instance's security group) does not help because the attacker is using the already-exfiltrated credentials from their own infrastructure — changing the EC2 instance's network rules has no effect on API calls the attacker makes directly to the S3 endpoint. Option C (Macie + Object Lock) is not immediate (sensitive-data discovery jobs over hundreds of terabytes take significant time) and Object Lock (WORM) only blocks deletion/overwrite, not read/download, so it does not address exfiltration at all.","explanation_zh":"本題被入侵的資產並非 bucket 本身，而是某個特定 IAM principal（掛在 EC2 上的 instance profile role）的臨時憑證。IAM 可以立即撤銷某個角色的臨時安全憑證：在該 role 上選擇「Revoke active sessions」會附加一個 inline 的 AWSRevokeOlderSessions policy，對「撤銷時間點之前」核發的所有 session token 一律 Deny 所有動作（約 30 秒內生效）。因為 policy evaluation 中 explicit deny 永遠優先，這會立即讓攻擊者手上那組被竊的 session 失效，無法再對 S3 呼叫 s3:GetObject；同時該 EC2 instance profile 會由 IMDS 自動換發新憑證繼續正常運作，也不會影響其他 principal 對該 bucket 的合法讀取。這正是 AWS IAM「撤銷角色臨時安全憑證」功能官方文件所描述的場景（「若使用者不慎將憑證外洩給未授權第三方…可立即撤銷某時間點之前核發之角色憑證的所有權限」）。AWS Security Incident Response 服務的 containment 模型也印證了這點：當被入侵的資產是特定 IAM role/user 時，對應的第一線動作是「IAM containment」（對該 principal 附加 deny-all policy、撤銷其行動能力），這與「EC2 containment」（用 security group 做網路隔離）以及「S3 containment」（對整個 bucket 全面 deny 外部存取）是三種不同、對應不同受害資產類型的動作。選項 D（bucket policy 對所有 principal deny）雖然也能擋下攻擊者，但屬於範圍錯置的圍堵動作：它會讓所有讀取這個存有百萬筆病患紀錄 bucket 的合法 principal（應用程式、備份工作、其他服務）在整整 4 小時內全部斷線，而實際上遭入侵的只是單一角色的 session，這樣的附帶損害並非必要。選項 B（隔離 EC2 的 security group）沒有幫助，因為攻擊者是在自己的基礎設施上使用已外洩的憑證直接呼叫 S3 API，更改 EC2 的網路規則對此毫無影響。選項 C（Macie + Object Lock）既不即時（對數百 TB 資料做敏感資料探索工作耗時甚鉅），Object Lock（WORM）也只防止刪除／覆寫，無法阻止讀取／下載，完全無法解決資料外洩問題。","distractors":[{"letter":"B","why_en":"Quarantining the EC2 instance via an empty security group only blocks future network traffic to/from that instance; the attacker is using the already-stolen temporary credentials from their own machine/infrastructure to call the S3 API directly, a path the instance's security group has no control over.","why_zh":"把 EC2 換成無規則的 security group 只會擋掉未來進出該 instance 的網路流量；攻擊者是在自己的機器／基礎設施上，用已竊取的臨時憑證直接呼叫 S3 API，這條路徑完全不受該 instance 的 security group 控制。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"Enabling Macie and running sensitive-data discovery over hundreds of terabytes is not an immediate action, and S3 Object Lock only enforces WORM (no delete/overwrite) — it does not block s3:GetObject reads, so ongoing downloads would continue unaffected.","why_zh":"啟用 Macie 並對數百 TB 資料執行敏感資料探索並非立即可完成的動作，而 S3 Object Lock 只強制 WORM（禁止刪除／覆寫），無法阻擋 s3:GetObject 讀取，攻擊者仍可繼續下載不受影響。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"A bucket policy denying read access to all principals does stop the attacker, but it is an over-broad, wrong-scoped containment: it also blocks every legitimate consumer of the 1-million-record PII bucket for the full 4-hour window, whereas the actual compromised asset is a single IAM role's session, which can be revoked without any collateral impact on other principals.","why_zh":"對所有 principal deny 讀取的 bucket policy 確實能擋下攻擊者，但屬於範圍過廣、圍堵層級錯置的做法：它會在整整 4 小時內連帶擋掉所有合法存取這個百萬筆 PII bucket 的使用者，而實際遭入侵的資產其實只是單一 IAM role 的 session，可以在不影響其他 principal 的情況下單獨撤銷。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/IAM/latest/UserGuide/id_roles_use_revoke-sessions.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/IAM/latest/UserGuide/id_credentials_temp_control-access_disable-perms.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/guardduty/latest/ug/compromised-s3.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/guardduty/latest/ug/compromised-creds.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/security-ir/latest/userguide/contain.html"]}},{"id":52,"question_en":"A recent security audit identified that a company’s application team injects database credentials into the environment variables of an AWS Fargate task. The company’s security policy mandates that all sensitive data be encrypted at rest and in transit. Which combination of actions should the security team take to make the application compliant with the security policy? (Select THREE.)","question_zh":"最近的一次安全审计发现，某公司的应用团队将数据库凭据注入到 AWS Fargate 任务的环境变量中。该公司的安全策略 要求所有敏感数据在静态存储和传输过程中均需加密。 安全团队应采取哪些操作组合来使应用程序符合安全策略？（选择三项。）","options_en":{"A":"Store the credentials securely in a file in an Amazon S3 bucket with restricted access to the application team IAM role. Ask the application team to read the credentials from the S3 object instead.","B":"Create an AWS Secrets Manager secret and specify the key-value pairs to be stored in this secret.","C":"Modify the application to pull credentials from the AWS Secrets Manager secret instead of the environment variables.","D":"Add a policy statement to the container instance IAM role that allows ssm:GetParameters, secretsmanager:GetSecretValue, and kms:Decrypt for the required secret and KMS key.","E":"Add a policy statement to the task role or task execution role that allows ssm:GetParameters, secretsmanager:GetSecretValue, and kms:Decrypt for the required secret and KMS key.","F":"Log in to the AWS Fargate instance, create a script to read the secret value from AWS Secrets Manager, and inject the environment variables. Ask the application team to redeploy the application."},"options_zh":{"A":"将凭据安全地存储在 Amazon S3 存储桶中的文件里，并限制应用程序团队的 IAM 角色访问权限。请应用程序团队从 S3 对象中读取凭据。","B":"创建一个 AWS Secrets Manager 密钥，并指定要存储在此密钥中的键值对。","C":"修改应用程序，使其从 AWS Secrets Manager 密钥中获取凭据，而不是从环境变量中获取。","D":"为容器实例的 IAM 角色添加策略声明，允许对所需的密钥和 KMS 密钥执行 ssm:GetParameters、secretsmanager:GetSecretValue 和 kms:Decrypt 操作。","E":"为任务角色或任务执行角色添加策略声明，允许对所需的密钥和 KMS 密钥执行 ssm:GetParameters、secretsmanager:GetSecretValue 和 kms:Decrypt 操作。","F":"登录 AWS Fargate 实例，创建一个脚本从 AWS Secrets Manager 读取密钥值并注入环境变量，然后请求应用团队重新部署应用程序。"},"answer":["B","C","E"],"multi":true,"vote":{},"tags":["Security/IAM","Storage","Compute","Database","Monitoring/Ops","Containers"],"difficulty":2,"diff_why":"複選","research":{"verdict":["B","C","E"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"both","explanation_en":"Storing plaintext database credentials in Fargate task environment variables violates the encrypt-at-rest/in-transit policy: env vars are visible via 'docker inspect', task descriptions, and logs. The AWS-documented remediation is: (B) create an AWS Secrets Manager secret holding the key-value credential pairs — Secrets Manager encrypts secrets at rest with AWS KMS and secrets are only retrievable over TLS (in transit); (C) modify the application to call Secrets Manager (GetSecretValue) directly at runtime instead of reading the value from a plaintext environment variable — this is one of the AWS-recommended patterns in 'Pass sensitive data to an Amazon ECS container'; and (E) attach an IAM policy statement granting ssm:GetParameters, secretsmanager:GetSecretValue, and kms:Decrypt on the required secret/key to the task role or the task execution role. The 'or' in option E matters: AWS's ECS documentation draws a hard line between the two roles — the task execution role's credentials are used only by the ECS/Fargate agent (e.g., to inject values via the container-definition 'secrets' parameter or pull images) and are 'not directly accessible by the containers in the task,' whereas the task IAM role's permissions are vended to the application code running inside the container (see 'Amazon ECS task IAM role,' task-iam-roles.html). Since option C has the application itself calling Secrets Manager, the permissions actually belong on the task role; option E's wording ('task role or task execution role') is written broadly enough to still be the correct choice among the given options, and it is the only option offering the app-facing role at all. Option D is wrong because AWS Fargate is serverless — there are no EC2 container instances and therefore no 'container instance IAM role' to attach anything to (see AWS_Fargate.html). Option F is wrong because Fargate infrastructure hosts cannot be logged into (no SSH/host access), and manually scripting the secret back into an environment variable would simply recreate the original violation. Option A (an S3 file) is a documented alternative pattern in the same ECS guide, but it is not part of a coherent 3-step combination with B/C/E, is weaker than a purpose-built secret store (no native rotation), and becomes redundant once Secrets Manager is adopted — so among a single coherent 3-action remediation, B/C/E is the correct set.","explanation_zh":"把資料庫憑證以明文放在 Fargate 工作的環境變數中，違反了靜態與傳輸加密政策：環境變數可透過 docker inspect、工作描述與日誌被看到。AWS 文件建議的補救做法是：(B) 建立 AWS Secrets Manager secret 存放 key-value 憑證——Secrets Manager 以 AWS KMS 對機密做靜態加密，且僅能透過 TLS（傳輸中加密）取回；(C) 修改應用程式在執行期直接呼叫 Secrets Manager（GetSecretValue）取得憑證，而不是讀取明文環境變數——這是 ECS 官方文件「Pass sensitive data to an Amazon ECS container」中建議的模式之一；以及 (E) 在 task role 或 task execution role 上附加允許 ssm:GetParameters、secretsmanager:GetSecretValue 與 kms:Decrypt（針對所需 secret／KMS key）的政策陳述。選項 E 中的『或』很關鍵：ECS 官方文件明確區分兩種角色——task execution role 的憑證僅供 ECS／Fargate agent 使用（例如透過容器定義的 secrets 參數注入值，或拉取映像檔），『容器內的程式無法直接存取』；而 task IAM role 的權限才會被分發給容器內執行的應用程式碼（見『Amazon ECS task IAM role』，task-iam-roles.html）。由於選項 C 是應用程式自行呼叫 Secrets Manager，理論上權限應掛在 task role 上；但選項 E 的措辭（『task role or task execution role』）涵蓋範圍夠廣，在給定選項中仍是唯一提供『應用程式端角色』的選項，因此仍是正確答案。選項 D 錯誤，因為 AWS Fargate 是無伺服器架構，沒有 EC2 container instance，因此不存在可附加政策的 container instance IAM role（見 AWS_Fargate.html）。選項 F 錯誤，因為無法登入 Fargate 底層主機（沒有 SSH／主機存取權），而且手動用指令碼把機密塞回環境變數等於重演原本的違規做法。選項 A（存放於 S3 的檔案）是同一份 ECS 文件中記載的替代方案，但它與 B/C/E 不構成一致的三步驟組合，且不如專用的祕密管理服務（缺乏原生輪換能力），一旦採用 Secrets Manager 便屬多餘——因此作為單一連貫的三動作補救方案，正確組合是 B、C、E。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"Storing a credentials file in an encrypted S3 bucket is a documented alternative in the same AWS ECS guide, but it does not form a coherent combination with B/C/E, lacks Secrets Manager's native rotation/audit features, and is unnecessary once Secrets Manager is adopted.","why_zh":"把憑證檔存放在加密的 S3 bucket 是同一份 AWS ECS 文件中記載的替代方案，但無法與 B/C/E 組成一致方案，且缺乏 Secrets Manager 原生的輪換／稽核功能，採用 Secrets Manager 後即屬多餘。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"AWS Fargate tasks run on AWS-managed serverless infrastructure with no EC2 container instances, so there is no 'container instance IAM role' to attach this policy to — that concept only exists for the EC2 launch type.","why_zh":"AWS Fargate 工作執行在 AWS 代管的無伺服器基礎設施上，沒有 EC2 container instance，因此不存在可附加此政策的 container instance IAM role——這個概念只存在於 EC2 啟動類型。"},{"letter":"F","why_en":"There is no host to log into on Fargate (no SSH/instance access to the underlying infrastructure), and re-injecting the secret into an environment variable via a manual script would simply recreate the original plaintext-env-var violation.","why_zh":"Fargate 沒有可登入的底層主機（無 SSH／執行個體存取權），而且用手動指令碼把機密重新注入環境變數，等於重演原本明文環境變數的違規做法。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonECS/latest/developerguide/specifying-sensitive-data-secrets.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonECS/latest/developerguide/specifying-sensitive-data-tutorial.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonECS/latest/developerguide/task_execution_IAM_role.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonECS/latest/developerguide/task-iam-roles.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonECS/latest/developerguide/AWS_Fargate.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/secretsmanager/latest/userguide/intro.html"]}},{"id":53,"question_en":"A company has a PHP-based web application that uses Amazon S3 as an object store for user files. The S3 bucket is configured for server-side encryption with Amazon S3 managed keys (SSE-S3). New requirements mandate full control of encryption keys. Which combination of steps must a security engineer take to meet these requirements? (Select THREE.)","question_zh":"一家公司有一个基于PHP的Web应用程序，使用Amazon S3作为用户文件的对象存储。该S3存储桶已配置为使用Amazon S3托 管密钥（SSE-S3）进行服务器端加密。新的需求要求对加密密钥拥有完全控制权。 安全工程师必须采取哪些步骤组合才能满足这些要求？（选择三项。）","options_en":{"A":"Create a new customer managed key in AWS Key Management Service (AWS KMS).","B":"Change the SSE-S3 configuration on the S3 bucket to server-side encryption with customer-provided keys (SSE-C).","C":"Configure the PHP SDK to use the SSE-S3 key before upload.","D":"Create an AWS managed key for Amazon S3 in AWS KMS.","E":"Change the SSE-S3 configuration on the S3 bucket to server-side encryption with AWS KMS managed keys (SSE-KMS).","F":"Change all the S3 objects in the bucket to use the new encryption key."},"options_zh":{"A":"在 AWS 密钥管理服务（AWS KMS）中创建一个新的客户托管密钥。","B":"将S3存储桶的SSE-S3配置更改为使用客户提供的密钥的服务器端加密（SSE-C）。","C":"在上传前配置 PHP SDK 使用 SSE-S3 密钥。","D":"在 AWS KMS 中为 Amazon S3 创建一个 AWS 管理的密钥。","E":"将S3存储桶的SSE-S3配置更改为使用AWS KMS管理密钥的服务器端加密（SSE-KMS）。","F":"将存储桶中的所有 S3 对象更改为使用新的加密密钥。"},"answer":["A","E","F"],"multi":true,"vote":{},"tags":["Security/IAM","Storage"],"difficulty":2,"diff_why":"複選","research":{"verdict":["A","E","F"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"The requirement is 'full control of encryption keys' while the objects stay server-side encrypted in S3. AWS KMS documentation states plainly that customer managed keys 'are recommended for customers who want full control over the lifecycle and usage of their keys' — full key-policy control, ability to enable/disable, rotate, and delete. So the engineer must (A) create a customer managed key in AWS KMS, and (E) change the bucket's default encryption from SSE-S3 to SSE-KMS pointing at that key (S3's own bucket-encryption docs say: 'If you need more control over your keys, such as managing key rotation and access policy grants, you can choose to use server-side encryption with AWS KMS keys (SSE-KMS)'). Changing a bucket's default encryption setting only changes the encryption applied to NEW uploads — AWS's own default-encryption FAQ confirms 'Objects that are already in an existing... bucket won't be automatically encrypted [with the new setting]' — so existing objects stay on SSE-S3 until explicitly re-encrypted (e.g., copy-in-place or S3 Batch Operations), making (F) mandatory too. B is not viable: AWS documentation explicitly states 'Server-side encryption with customer-provided keys (SSE-C) is not supported for default encryption,' so a bucket's default-encryption setting cannot be switched to SSE-C at all; SSE-C also requires the customer to generate/store the raw key entirely outside AWS and resend it on every request, which is a heavier and different mechanism than what the question is steering toward. D fails the 'full control' bar because an AWS managed key (aws/s3) cannot have its key policy edited, its rotation schedule controlled, or be deleted by the customer. C is nonsensical — SSE-S3 keys are never exposed to callers, so there is no 'SSE-S3 key' an SDK could be configured to use.","explanation_zh":"需求是在物件維持 S3 伺服器端加密的前提下，對加密金鑰擁有「完全控制權」。AWS KMS 官方文件明確指出，customer managed key「適合想要完全掌控金鑰生命週期與使用方式的客戶」——包含金鑰政策、啟用/停用、輪換與刪除的完整控制。因此工程師必須：(A) 在 AWS KMS 建立 customer managed key；(E) 將 bucket 的預設加密從 SSE-S3 改為指向該金鑰的 SSE-KMS（S3 官方文件亦寫道：「若需要更多金鑰控制，例如管理金鑰輪換與存取政策授權，可選擇 SSE-KMS」）。變更 bucket 預設加密僅影響「之後」上傳的新物件——AWS 官方 default-encryption FAQ 明確說明「既有 bucket 中已存在的物件不會自動套用新的加密設定」——因此既有物件仍維持 SSE-S3，必須另行明確重新加密（例如原地複製或 S3 Batch Operations），故 (F) 也是必要步驟。選項 B 不可行：AWS 文件明確指出「SSE-C 不支援作為 bucket 的預設加密設定」，也就是 bucket 的預設加密根本無法切換成 SSE-C；且 SSE-C 要求客戶自行產生並保管原始金鑰（完全在 AWS 之外），並在每次請求時附上金鑰，這與題目導向的機制不同、負擔更重。選項 D 不符合「完全控制」的門檻，因為 AWS managed key（aws/s3）的金鑰政策無法由客戶編輯、輪換排程無法控制、也無法刪除。選項 C 在技術上不成立——SSE-S3 的金鑰從不對外曝露，SDK 根本沒有「SSE-S3 金鑰」可設定使用。","distractors":[{"letter":"B","why_en":"AWS documentation explicitly states SSE-C 'is not supported for default encryption,' so a bucket's default (SSE-S3) setting cannot be switched to SSE-C at all. SSE-C also requires the application to generate, store, and supply the encryption key on every PUT/GET request — S3 never stores it — which is a heavier and orthogonal key-management burden, not the intended 'full control via KMS' path.","why_zh":"AWS 文件明確指出 SSE-C「不支援作為預設加密設定」，因此 bucket 的預設（SSE-S3）加密根本無法切換為 SSE-C。SSE-C 還要求應用程式自行產生、保存金鑰，並在每次 PUT/GET 請求中附帶金鑰——S3 完全不儲存——管理負擔更重，也不是題目導向的「透過 KMS 完全控制」路徑。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"SSE-S3 keys are created, managed, and rotated entirely by Amazon S3 and are never exposed to customers, so there is no 'SSE-S3 key' the PHP SDK could be configured to use. This option is technically meaningless.","why_zh":"SSE-S3 的金鑰完全由 Amazon S3 建立、管理與輪換，客戶永遠接觸不到，PHP SDK 無從設定使用「SSE-S3 金鑰」，此選項在技術上不成立。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"The AWS managed key for S3 (aws/s3) is created and managed by AWS: per AWS KMS concepts documentation, 'You cannot manage anything about the lifecycle or permissions of these keys' — no custom key policy, no controllable rotation schedule, no deletion — so it does not satisfy 'full control of encryption keys'.","why_zh":"S3 的 AWS managed key（aws/s3）由 AWS 建立與管理：依 AWS KMS 概念文件，「客戶無法管理這類金鑰的生命週期或權限的任何部分」——沒有自訂金鑰政策、輪換排程不可控、也無法刪除——因此無法滿足「完全控制加密金鑰」的需求。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonS3/latest/userguide/bucket-encryption.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonS3/latest/userguide/default-bucket-encryption.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonS3/latest/userguide/default-encryption-faq.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonS3/latest/userguide/UsingKMSEncryption.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonS3/latest/userguide/ServerSideEncryptionCustomerKeys.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/kms/latest/developerguide/concepts.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonS3/latest/userguide/batch-ops-update.html"]}},{"id":54,"question_en":"A company needs to identify the root cause of security findings and investigate IAM roles involved in those findings. The company has enabled VPC Flow Logs, Amazon GuardDuty, and AWS CloudTrail. Which solution will meet these requirements?","question_zh":"公司需要确定安全发现的根本原因，并调查与此类发现相关的IAM角色。该公司已启用VPC流量日志、Amazon GuardDuty 和AWS CloudTrail。 哪种解决方案能满足这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Use Amazon Detective to investigate IAM roles and visualize findings.","B":"Use Amazon Inspector and CloudWatch dashboards.","C":"Export GuardDuty findings to S3 and analyze with Athena.","D":"Use Security Hub custom actions to investigate IAM roles."},"options_zh":{"A":"使用 Amazon Detective 调查 IAM 角色并可视化发现结果。","B":"使用 Amazon Inspector 和 CloudWatch 仪表板。","C":"将 GuardDuty 的检测结果导出至 S3，并使用 Athena 进行分析。","D":"使用安全中心的自定义操作来调查 IAM 角色。"},"answer":["A"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Security/IAM","Storage","Monitoring/Ops","Analytics"],"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選","research":{"verdict":["A"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"Amazon Detective is purpose-built for exactly this requirement: AWS docs state it helps you \"analyze, investigate, and quickly identify the root cause of security findings or suspicious activities.\" It automatically ingests the exact data sources the company already enabled — VPC Flow Logs, AWS CloudTrail management events, and Amazon GuardDuty findings — into a behavior graph and generates interactive visualizations. Its Detective Investigation feature specifically \"investigates IAM users and IAM roles using indicators of compromise\" to determine whether a resource is involved in a security incident, and Detective finding groups provide root-cause analysis with a visual graph of related findings and entities. No other option combines root-cause analysis, IAM role investigation, and visualization out of the box.","explanation_zh":"Amazon Detective 正是為此需求而生：AWS 文件明確說明它能「分析、調查並快速找出安全發現或可疑活動的根本原因（root cause）」。它會自動擷取題目中公司已啟用的資料來源——VPC Flow Logs、AWS CloudTrail 管理事件與 Amazon GuardDuty findings——建立行為圖（behavior graph）並產生互動式視覺化。其 Detective Investigation 功能可依據入侵指標（indicators of compromise）專門「調查 IAM users 與 IAM roles」，判斷資源是否涉入安全事件；finding groups 則以視覺化圖形呈現相關 findings 與實體，支援根因分析。其他選項都無法同時提供根因分析、IAM role 調查與視覺化。","distractors":[{"letter":"B","why_en":"Amazon Inspector is a vulnerability scanner (EC2/ECR/Lambda CVEs and network exposure); it does not investigate the root cause of GuardDuty findings or analyze IAM role activity, and CloudWatch dashboards only display metrics.","why_zh":"Amazon Inspector 是弱點掃描服務（EC2/ECR/Lambda 的 CVE 與網路暴露），不會調查 GuardDuty findings 的根因，也不分析 IAM role 活動；CloudWatch dashboards 只能顯示指標。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"Exporting GuardDuty findings to S3 and querying with Athena requires building custom queries and correlation manually; it provides no behavior graph, no IAM role investigation capability, and no built-in root-cause visualization.","why_zh":"將 GuardDuty findings 匯出到 S3 再用 Athena 查詢，需要自行撰寫查詢並手動關聯資料；沒有行為圖、沒有 IAM role 調查功能，也沒有內建的根因視覺化。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"Security Hub custom actions merely send selected findings to EventBridge for downstream workflows (ticketing, remediation); they do not themselves perform root-cause analysis or investigate IAM roles.","why_zh":"Security Hub custom actions 只是把選定的 findings 送到 EventBridge 供下游工作流程（開單、修復）使用，本身並不執行根因分析，也不會調查 IAM roles。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/detective/latest/userguide/what-is-detective.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/detective/latest/userguide/detective-investigation-about.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/detective/latest/userguide/investigations-about.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/detective/latest/userguide/detective-source-data-about.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/securityhub/latest/userguide/securityhub-cwe-custom-actions.html"]}},{"id":55,"question_en":"A company is operating an open-source software platform that is internet facing. The legacy software platform no longer receives security updates. The software platform operates using Amazon Route 53 weighted load balancing to send traffic to two Amazon EC2 instances that connect to an Amazon RDS cluster. A recent report suggests this software platform is vulnerable to SQL injection attacks, with samples of attacks provided. The company ' s security engineer must secure this system against SQL injection attacks within 24 hours. The security engineer’s solution must involve the least amount of effort and maintain normal operations during implementation. What should the security engineer do to meet these requirements?","question_zh":"一家公司正在运行一个面向互联网的开源软件平台。该旧版软件平台已不再接收安全更新。该平台通 过 Amazon Route 53 的加权负载均衡，将流量分发至两个连接到 Amazon RDS 集群的 Amazon EC2 实 例。最近的一份报告指出，该软件平台存在 SQL 注入攻击漏洞，并提供了攻击样本。公司的安全工 程师必须在 24 小时内保护该系统免受 SQL 注入攻击。安全工程师的解决方案需以最小的工作量实现， 并在实施过程中保持正常运行。 安全工程师应采取哪些措施来满足这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Create an Application Load Balancer with the existing EC2 instances as a target group. Create an AWS WAF web ACL containing rules that protect the application from this attack, then apply it to the ALB. Test to ensure the vulnerability has been mitigated, then redirect the Route 53 records to point to the ALB. Update security groups on the EC2 instances to prevent direct access from the internet.","B":"Create an Amazon CloudFront distribution specifying one EC2 instance as an origin. Create an AWS WAF web ACL containing rules that protect the application from this attack, then apply it to the distribution. Test to ensure the vulnerability has been mitigated, then redirect the Route 53 records to point to CloudFront.","C":"Obtain the latest source code for the platform and make the necessary updates. Test the updated code to ensure that the vulnerability has been mitigated, then deploy the patched version of the platform to the EC2 instances.","D":"Update the security group that is attached to the EC2 instances, removing access from the internet to the TCP port used by the SQL database. Create an AWS WAF web ACL containing rules that protect the application from this attack, then apply it to the EC2 instances. Test to ensure the vulnerability has been mitigated, then restore the security group to the original setting."},"options_zh":{"A":"创建一个应用负载均衡器（ALB），并将现有的 EC2 实例作为目标组。创建一个包含防护规则的 AWS WAF 网站访问 控制列表（web ACL），以保护应用程序免受此类攻击，然后将其应用于 ALB。测试以确保漏洞已得到缓解，随后将 Route 53 记录指向该 ALB。更新 EC2 实例的安全组，防止互联网直接访问。","B":"创建一个 Amazon CloudFront 分发，指定一个 EC2 实例作为源站。创建一个 AWS WAF 网络 ACL，并包含保护应用 程序免受此类攻击的规则，然后将其应用到该分发上。测试以确保漏洞已被缓解，随后将 Route 53 记录指向 CloudFront。","C":"获取平台的最新源代码并进行必要的更新。测试更新后的代码，确保漏洞已得到缓解，然后将修复后的平台版本部署到 EC2实例上。","D":"更新附加到 EC2 实例的安全组，移除互联网对 SQL 数据库所用 TCP 端口的访问权限。创建一个包含规则的 AWS WAF 网站 ACL，以保护应用程序免受此类攻击，然后将其应用到 EC2 实例上。测试以确保漏洞已得到缓解，再将安全组恢 复至原始设置。"},"answer":["A"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Networking/DNS","Security/IAM","Compute","Database"],"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選","research":{"verdict":["A"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"AWS WAF web ACLs can only be associated with a fixed set of supported resource types — Application Load Balancer, Amazon API Gateway REST API, AWS AppSync GraphQL API, Amazon Cognito user pool, AWS App Runner, AWS Verified Access, AWS Amplify, and Amazon CloudFront — never a bare EC2 instance. That rules out option D outright: you cannot 'apply a web ACL to the EC2 instances,' and closing the database's TCP port does nothing to stop SQL injection, which travels over the normal web port (80/443) inside HTTP requests. The fastest, lowest-effort, zero-downtime fix is option A: stand up an Application Load Balancer with a single target group containing both existing EC2 instances (preserving the current two-instance, weighted-style capacity), attach a WAF web ACL with SQL injection protection (the SQLi rule statement and/or the AWSManagedRulesSQLiRuleSet / AWSManagedRulesCommonRuleSet), validate in count mode or staging that the sample attacks are blocked, then cut over by repointing the Route 53 records from the instances to the new ALB, and finally lock the EC2 security groups down to accept traffic only from the ALB. This requires no source-code changes, keeps both instances serving production traffic throughout, and can easily be completed inside 24 hours. Option B is technically similar but specifies only ONE EC2 instance as the CloudFront origin, silently cutting capacity in half and abandoning the existing two-instance distribution — it does not 'maintain normal operations.' Option C requires locating, patching, and safely rolling out fixed source code for software that no longer receives security updates (patches may not even exist), which is by far the highest-effort, highest-risk, and least realistic path to hit within 24 hours.","explanation_zh":"AWS WAF 的 web ACL 只能關聯到固定的一組支援資源類型——Application Load Balancer、Amazon API Gateway REST API、AWS AppSync GraphQL API、Amazon Cognito user pool、AWS App Runner、AWS Verified Access、AWS Amplify、以及 Amazon CloudFront——絕對不能直接關聯到單純的 EC2 執行個體。這直接排除選項 D：你無法『把 web ACL 套用到 EC2 執行個體』，而且關閉資料庫的 TCP 連接埠對阻擋 SQL injection 毫無幫助，因為 SQL injection 是透過一般的 Web 連接埠（80/443）夾帶在 HTTP 請求中傳送的。最快、工作量最小、且零停機的做法是選項 A：建立一個 Application Load Balancer，用單一 target group 涵蓋現有兩台 EC2 執行個體（保留原本兩台的容量與加權式分流），在 ALB 上套用含 SQL injection 防護規則（SQLi rule statement 及/或 AWSManagedRulesSQLiRuleSet／AWSManagedRulesCommonRuleSet）的 web ACL，先以 count 模式或在測試環境驗證範例攻擊確實被擋下，再把 Route 53 記錄從原本的執行個體改指向新的 ALB 完成割接，最後把 EC2 的 security group 收緊為只允許來自 ALB 的流量。整個過程不需要修改原始碼，兩台執行個體全程持續服務正式流量，完全能在 24 小時內完成。選項 B 技術上類似，但只將『一台』EC2 設為 CloudFront 的 origin，等於悄悄把容量砍半、放棄原本兩台的分流架構，不符合『維持正常營運』的要求。選項 C 則需要找到、修補並安全地部署已經不再收到安全更新之軟體的原始碼（修補程式甚至可能根本不存在），是工作量與風險都最高、也最不可能在 24 小時內完成的做法。","distractors":[{"letter":"B","why_en":"CloudFront with a WAF web ACL is architecturally valid, but the option specifies only ONE EC2 instance as the origin, halving effective capacity and discarding the existing two-instance traffic distribution — it fails the 'maintain normal operations' requirement.","why_zh":"CloudFront 搭配 WAF web ACL 在架構上是可行的，但此選項只把『一台』EC2 設為 origin，等於容量減半並放棄原本兩台的流量分配，不符合『維持正常營運』的要求。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"The platform is legacy and no longer receives security updates, so a vetted patched version of the source code may not even exist; sourcing, fixing, testing, and safely redeploying code is the highest-effort, highest-risk option and unrealistic within a 24-hour window.","why_zh":"此平台已是舊版且不再收到安全更新，可能根本沒有經過驗證的修補版原始碼；尋找、修改、測試並安全地重新部署程式碼是工作量與風險都最高的選項，24 小時內並不現實。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"AWS WAF web ACLs can only be associated with supported resource types (ALB, CloudFront, API Gateway, AppSync, Cognito, App Runner, Verified Access, Amplify) — never directly with an EC2 instance. Additionally, SQL injection travels over the web port (80/443) inside HTTP traffic, so blocking the database's TCP port provides no protection against it.","why_zh":"AWS WAF 的 web ACL 只能關聯到受支援的資源類型（ALB、CloudFront、API Gateway、AppSync、Cognito、App Runner、Verified Access、Amplify）——絕不能直接關聯到 EC2 執行個體。此外，SQL injection 是透過 Web 連接埠（80/443）夾帶在 HTTP 流量中傳送，封鎖資料庫的 TCP 連接埠對其毫無防護作用。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/waf/latest/developerguide/web-acl-associating-aws-resource.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/waf/latest/developerguide/web-acl-associating.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/waf/latest/developerguide/waf-rule-statement-type-sqli-match.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/waf/latest/developerguide/aws-managed-rule-groups-use-case.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/waf/latest/developerguide/aws-managed-rule-groups-list.html"]}},{"id":56,"question_en":"A security engineer needs to prepare for a security audit of an AWS account. Select the THREE AWS resources from the following list that meet these requirements: (1) Automatically collect evidence from AWS CloudTrail, AWS Config, and AWS Security Hub for an assessment report. (2) Determine which IAM principals within the AWS account have access to a specified resource. (3) Download AWS security and compliance documents on demand. (Select THREE.)","question_zh":"安全工程师需要为 AWS 账户的安全审计做好准备。从以下列表中选择满足这些要求的三项 AWS 资源：（1）自动从 AWS CloudTrail、AWS Config 和 AWS Security Hub 收集证据，用于评估报告。（2）确定 AWS 账户中哪些 IAM 主体有权访问指定资源。（3）按需下载 AWS 安全与合规文档。（选择三项。）","options_en":{"A":"AWS Artifact reports","B":"AWS Audit Manager controls","C":"AWS Config conformance packs","D":"AWS Config rules","E":"Amazon Detective investigations","F":"AWS IAM Access Analyzer internal access analyzers"},"options_zh":{"A":"AWS Artifact 报告","B":"AWS Audit Manager 控制","C":"AWS Config 合规性包","D":"AWS Config 规则","E":"Amazon Detective 调查","F":"AWS IAM Access Analyzer 内部访问分析器"},"answer":["A","B","F"],"multi":true,"vote":{},"tags":["Organizations/Governance","Security/IAM","Monitoring/Ops"],"difficulty":2,"diff_why":"複選","research":{"verdict":["A","B","F"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"Each of the three requirements maps one-to-one to a distinct AWS resource. (1) AWS Audit Manager controls define one or more data sources and automatically collect evidence from AWS CloudTrail (user activity), AWS Config (compliance-check evidence), and AWS Security Hub CSPM (compliance-check evidence) on a schedule, then assemble that evidence into an assessment report for the audit — satisfying the automatic multi-source evidence-collection requirement (B). (2) IAM Access Analyzer's internal access analyzer feature analyzes resource-based policies and other access controls to determine which principals within an AWS account or organization (a defined zone of trust) have access to a specified business-critical resource, generating internal access findings — satisfying the who-has-access requirement (F). (3) AWS Artifact is the central, on-demand resource for downloading AWS's security and compliance reports (e.g., SOC, PCI, ISO) and agreements — satisfying the compliance-document-download requirement (A). AWS Config conformance packs (C) and AWS Config rules (D) only evaluate individual resource configurations against desired rules; they are themselves just one data source that Audit Manager consumes, and they cannot on their own aggregate multi-source audit evidence into reports, analyze IAM principal access, or provide downloadable compliance documents. Amazon Detective investigations (E) are for root-cause/security-incident investigation using behavior graphs built from CloudTrail, VPC Flow Logs, and GuardDuty findings — not for pre-audit evidence collection, access analysis, or compliance document retrieval.","explanation_zh":"三個需求各自對應一項不同的 AWS 資源。(1) AWS Audit Manager controls 會定義一個或多個資料來源，並依排程自動從 AWS CloudTrail（使用者活動）、AWS Config（合規檢查證據）與 AWS Security Hub CSPM（合規檢查證據）收集證據，再彙整成稽核用的評估報告——滿足自動化多來源證據收集需求（B）。(2) IAM Access Analyzer 的 internal access analyzer 功能會分析資源型政策等存取控制設定，判斷 AWS 帳戶或組織（定義的信任區域）內哪些 principal 能存取指定的業務關鍵資源，並產生 internal access findings——滿足「誰能存取資源」的需求（F）。(3) AWS Artifact 是集中式、隨需下載 AWS 安全與合規報告（如 SOC、PCI、ISO）與各項協議的資源——滿足合規文件下載需求（A）。AWS Config conformance packs（C）與 AWS Config rules（D）僅評估個別資源組態是否符合期望規則，本身只是 Audit Manager 取用的其中一種資料來源，無法單獨彙整多來源稽核證據成報告、分析 IAM principal 存取權，或提供可下載的合規文件。Amazon Detective investigations（E）則是利用由 CloudTrail、VPC Flow Logs 與 GuardDuty findings 建構的行為圖，進行根因分析與安全事件調查，並非用於稽核前的證據收集、存取分析或合規文件取得。","distractors":[{"letter":"C","why_en":"AWS Config conformance packs bundle Config rules and remediation actions to evaluate resource configuration compliance at scale; they do not aggregate evidence from CloudTrail/Security Hub into an assessment report, analyze IAM principal access to a resource, or provide downloadable AWS compliance documents.","why_zh":"AWS Config conformance packs 只是打包 Config rules 與修復動作，用於大規模評估資源組態合規，不會將 CloudTrail/Security Hub 的證據彙整成評估報告，也無法分析哪些 IAM principal 能存取資源，或提供可下載的 AWS 合規文件。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"AWS Config rules evaluate whether individual resource configurations comply with desired settings. They are merely one evidence source that Audit Manager can consume, not the service that itself collects multi-source evidence into reports, analyzes principal access, or serves compliance documents.","why_zh":"AWS Config rules 只評估個別資源組態是否符合期望設定，本身只是 Audit Manager 可取用的其中一種證據來源，並非負責彙整多來源證據成報告、分析 principal 存取權，或提供合規文件的服務。"},{"letter":"E","why_en":"Amazon Detective investigations analyze security findings and behavior graphs (built from CloudTrail, VPC Flow Logs, and GuardDuty findings) for incident root-cause analysis; this addresses none of the three audit-preparation requirements in the question.","why_zh":"Amazon Detective investigations 是利用由 CloudTrail、VPC Flow Logs 與 GuardDuty findings 建構的行為圖，來分析安全 findings 並進行事件根因調查，與題目三項稽核準備需求皆無關。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/audit-manager/latest/userguide/how-evidence-is-collected.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/audit-manager/latest/userguide/what-is.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/audit-manager/latest/userguide/setup-recommendations.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/IAM/latest/UserGuide/what-is-access-analyzer.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/IAM/latest/UserGuide/access-analyzer-concepts.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/IAM/latest/UserGuide/access-analyzer-findings-view.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/artifact/latest/ug/what-is-aws-artifact.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/artifact/latest/ug/downloading-documents.html"]}},{"id":57,"question_en":"A company uses AWS Lambda functions to implement application logic. The company uses an organization in AWS Organizations to manage hundreds of AWS accounts. The company needs to implement a solution to continuously monitor the Lambda functions for vulnerabilities in all accounts. The solution must publish detected issues to a dashboard. Lambda functions that are being tested or are in development must not appear on the dashboard. Which combination of steps will meet these requirements? (Select TWO.)","question_zh":"一家公司使用 AWS Lambda 函数来实现应用程序逻辑，并通过 AWS Organizations 中的组织结构管理 数百个 AWS 账户。该公司需要实施一种解决方案，持续监控所有账户中的 Lambda 函数是否存在漏 洞，且该方案必须将检测到的问题发布到仪表板上。正在测试或处于开发阶段的 Lambda 函数不应显 示在仪表板中。 哪两个步骤的组合可以满足这些要求？（选择两项。）","options_en":{"A":"Designate a delegated Amazon GuardDuty administrator account in the organization’s management account. Use the GuardDuty Summary dashboard to obtain an overview of Lambda functions that have vulnerabilities.","B":"Designate a delegated Amazon Inspector administrator account in the organization’s management account. Use the Amazon Inspector dashboard to obtain an overview of Lambda functions that have vulnerabilities.","C":"Apply tags of “test” or “development” to all Lambda functions that are in testing or development. Use a suppression filter that suppresses findings that contain these tags.","D":"Enable AWS Shield Advanced in the organization’s management account. Use Amazon CloudWatch to build a dashboard for Lambda functions that have vulnerabilities.","E":"Enable Lambda Protection in GuardDuty for all accounts. Auto-enable Lambda Protection for new accounts. Apply a tag to the Lambda functions that are in testing or development. Use GuardDutyExclusion as the tag key and LambdaStandardScanning as the tag value."},"options_zh":{"A":"在组织的管理账户中指定一个委派的 Amazon GuardDuty 管理员账户。使用 GuardDuty 概述仪 表板查看存在漏洞的 Lambda 函数概览。","B":"在组织的管理账户中指定一个委派的 Amazon Inspector 管理员账户。使用 Amazon Inspector 控制台查看存在漏洞的 Lambda 函数概览。","C":"为所有处于测试或开发阶段的 Lambda 函数添加“test”或“development”标签。使用抑制过滤 器，以忽略包含这些标签的检测结果。","D":"在组织的管理账户中启用 AWS Shield Advanced，并使用 Amazon CloudWatch 为存在漏洞的 Lambda 函数创建仪表板。","E":"为所有账户启用 GuardDuty 中的 Lambda 保护功能。自动为新创建的账户启用 Lambda 保护。 对处于测试或开发阶段的 Lambda 函数添加标签，标签键使用 GuardDutyExclusion，标签 值使用 LambdaStandardScanning。"},"answer":["B","C"],"multi":true,"vote":{},"tags":["Organizations/Governance","Security/IAM","Compute","Monitoring/Ops"],"difficulty":2,"diff_why":"複選","research":{"verdict":["B","C"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"Amazon Inspector is the AWS service that continuously scans Lambda functions for software vulnerabilities: Lambda standard scanning checks application/package dependencies and Lambda code scanning checks custom code (https://docs.aws.amazon.com/inspector/latest/user/scanning-lambda.html). It integrates natively with AWS Organizations — the organization's management account designates a delegated Inspector administrator account, which gets an aggregated, organization-wide Inspector dashboard/coverage view across all member accounts (https://docs.aws.amazon.com/inspector/latest/user/designating-admin.html), satisfying the 'continuously monitor all accounts + publish to a dashboard' requirement (B). To keep test/development Lambda functions off that dashboard, Inspector suppression rules let the delegated administrator define filter criteria — including resource tags — so findings matching those criteria (e.g., a 'test' or 'development' tag) are hidden from the default findings view while scanning continues (https://docs.aws.amazon.com/inspector/latest/user/findings-managing-supression-rules.html); tag is a standard Inspector filter/criteria attribute (https://docs.aws.amazon.com/inspector/latest/user/findings-managing-filtering.html) (C). Option A is wrong because Amazon GuardDuty is a threat-detection service (it flags active malicious/anomalous behavior), not a vulnerability scanner, and its Summary dashboard does not surface Lambda software vulnerabilities. Option D is wrong because AWS Shield Advanced is DDoS protection for internet-facing resources and has no vulnerability-scanning capability for Lambda. Option E is wrong on two counts: GuardDuty Lambda Protection analyzes Lambda network-activity (VPC Flow Log-derived) events for threats, it does not scan code/dependencies for vulnerabilities, and the tag it describes is fabricated — AWS documentation confirms the real exclusion tag, key `InspectorExclusion` with value `LambdaStandardScanning`, belongs to Amazon Inspector (used to exclude a function from Inspector scanning entirely), not to GuardDuty (https://docs.aws.amazon.com/inspector/latest/user/scanning_resources_lambda_exclude_functions.html). Excluding a function from scanning is also a different mechanism than suppressing its findings from a dashboard, which is what the requirement calls for.","explanation_zh":"Amazon Inspector 是持續掃描 Lambda 函式軟體弱點的 AWS 服務：Lambda standard scanning 掃描應用程式／套件相依性，Lambda code scanning 掃描自訂程式碼（https://docs.aws.amazon.com/inspector/latest/user/scanning-lambda.html）。它原生整合 AWS Organizations——由組織的 management account 指定 delegated Inspector administrator account，該帳戶可取得跨所有成員帳戶的彙總 Inspector dashboard／涵蓋率總覽（https://docs.aws.amazon.com/inspector/latest/user/designating-admin.html），滿足題目「持續監控所有帳戶＋發布到儀表板」的需求（B）。若要讓測試／開發中的 Lambda 函式不出現在該儀表板上，delegated administrator 可建立 Inspector 的 suppression rules，依過濾條件（包含資源標籤 tag）定義規則，讓符合條件（例如帶有 'test' 或 'development' 標籤）的 findings 從預設檢視中隱藏，同時掃描仍持續進行（https://docs.aws.amazon.com/inspector/latest/user/findings-managing-supression-rules.html）；tag 本身即為 Inspector 標準的過濾／條件屬性之一（https://docs.aws.amazon.com/inspector/latest/user/findings-managing-filtering.html）（C）。選項 A 錯誤：Amazon GuardDuty 是威脅偵測服務（偵測正在發生的惡意／異常行為），並非弱點掃描工具，其 Summary dashboard 也不會顯示 Lambda 軟體弱點。選項 D 錯誤：AWS Shield Advanced 是針對面向網際網路資源的 DDoS 防護，完全不具備 Lambda 弱點掃描能力。選項 E 有兩處錯誤：GuardDuty Lambda Protection 分析的是 Lambda 的網路活動事件（源自 VPC Flow Log）以偵測威脅，並非掃描程式碼／相依套件的弱點；且題目描述的標籤是杜撰的——AWS 官方文件證實真正的排除標籤（key 為 `InspectorExclusion`、value 為 `LambdaStandardScanning`）屬於 Amazon Inspector（用於將函式完全排除在 Inspector 掃描之外），而非 GuardDuty（https://docs.aws.amazon.com/inspector/latest/user/scanning_resources_lambda_exclude_functions.html）。此外，將函式排除在掃描外，與把其發現從儀表板上抑制，本質上是不同的機制，後者才是題目真正要求的做法。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"GuardDuty is a threat-detection service focused on active malicious/anomalous activity (e.g., compromised credentials, C2 communication), not a software vulnerability scanner; its Summary dashboard does not report Lambda vulnerability findings.","why_zh":"GuardDuty 是聚焦於進行中的惡意／異常活動（例如憑證外洩、C2 通訊）的威脅偵測服務，並非軟體弱點掃描工具；其 Summary dashboard 不會回報 Lambda 弱點發現。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"AWS Shield Advanced provides DDoS protection for internet-facing resources such as CloudFront, Route 53, and ELB; it has no capability to scan Lambda function code or dependencies for vulnerabilities.","why_zh":"AWS Shield Advanced 為 CloudFront、Route 53、ELB 等面向網際網路的資源提供 DDoS 防護，不具備掃描 Lambda 函式程式碼或相依套件弱點的能力。"},{"letter":"E","why_en":"GuardDuty Lambda Protection detects threats from Lambda network-activity logs, not code/dependency vulnerabilities, so it cannot populate a vulnerability dashboard. Additionally, the tag it describes is fabricated: AWS docs confirm the exclusion tag key/value 'InspectorExclusion: LambdaStandardScanning' belongs to Amazon Inspector, not GuardDuty, and it excludes a function from scanning entirely rather than merely suppressing its findings from a dashboard.","why_zh":"GuardDuty Lambda Protection 偵測的是來自 Lambda 網路活動日誌的威脅，而非程式碼／相依套件弱點，因此無法產生弱點儀表板。此外題目所述標籤是杜撰的：AWS 文件證實排除標籤 key/value 'InspectorExclusion: LambdaStandardScanning' 屬於 Amazon Inspector，並非 GuardDuty，且該標籤是把函式完全排除於掃描之外，而非僅是把其發現從儀表板中抑制。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/inspector/latest/user/scanning-lambda.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/inspector/latest/user/findings-managing-supression-rules.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/inspector/latest/user/findings-managing-filtering.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/inspector/latest/user/designating-admin.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/inspector/latest/user/scanning_resources_lambda_exclude_functions.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/guardduty/latest/ug/lambda-protection.html"]}},{"id":58,"question_en":"A company uses an organization in AWS Organizations to manage multiple AWS accounts. The company uses AWS IAM Identity Center to manage access to the accounts. The company uses AWS Directory Service as an identity source. Employees access the AWS console and specific AWS accounts and permissions through the AWS access portal. A security engineer creates a new permissions set in IAM Identity Center and assigns the permissions set to one of the member accounts in the organization. The security engineer assigns the permissions set to a user group for developers namedDevOpsin the member account. The security engineer expects all the developers to see the new permissions set listed for the member account in the AWS access portal. All the developers except for one can see the permissions set. The security engineer must ensure that the remaining developer can see the permissions set in the AWS access portal. Which solution will meet this requirement?","question_zh":"一家公司使用 AWS Organizations 中的组织来管理多个 AWS 账户，并通过 AWS IAM Identity Center 管理对这些账户的访问 权限。该公司将 AWS Directory Service 用作身份源，员工通过 AWS 访问门户登录 AWS 控制台并访问特定的 AWS 账户和权 限。 安全工程师在 IAM Identity Center 中创建了一个新的权限集，并将其分配给组织中的一个成员账户。该安全工程师将此权 限集分配给了成员账户中名为 DevOps 的开发人员用户组。安全工程师期望所有开发人员都能在 AWS 访问门户中看到该成 员账户列出的权限集。但除了一名开发人员外，其余所有人都能看到该权限集。安全工程师必须确保剩下的这名开发人员 也能在 AWS 访问门户中看到该权限集。 哪种解决方案能满足这一要求？","options_en":{"A":"Add the remaining developer to the DevOps group in Directory Service.","B":"Remove and then re-add the permissions set in the member account.","D":"Update the permissions set to allow console access for the remaining developer.","C":"Add the service-linked role for organization to the member account."},"options_zh":{"A":"将剩余的开发人员添加到目录服务中的 DevOps 组。","B":"先移除，然后重新添加成员账户中的权限集。","C":"将组织的服务关联角色添加到成员账户。","D":"更新权限设置，以允许剩余的开发人员访问控制台。"},"answer":["A"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Organizations/Governance","Security/IAM"],"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選","research":{"verdict":["A"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"When AWS Directory Service (Active Directory) is configured as the identity source, IAM Identity Center synchronizes users, groups, and group memberships from the directory into its own identity store, and group membership continues to be managed in Active Directory rather than in IAM Identity Center itself. The AWS access portal only lists the AWS accounts and permission sets that have been assigned directly to a user or to a group that user belongs to. Because the permission set here was assigned to the DevOps group at the account level, and every developer except one already sees it, the assignment and provisioning are working correctly — the only variable that differs per user is directory group membership. AWS's own troubleshooting guidance for IAM Identity Center documents exactly this class of problem: a user's Active Directory group membership does not reliably sync into the IAM Identity Center identity store unless the user is an explicit ('member' attribute) member of that group — for example, AWS calls out that a user's AD *primary* group (such as Domain Users, or any other group set as a primary group) is not read for membership purposes by IAM Identity Center, so a user who is only associated with a group via primary-group semantics (and lacks an explicit member entry) will not show that group's assignments in the access portal even though colleagues who are explicit members do. The fix is therefore to make sure the remaining developer is added as an explicit member of the DevOps group in Directory Service, after which the AD-to-IAM-Identity-Center sync will pick up the membership and the permission set will appear for that user in the AWS access portal — exactly what option A does.","explanation_zh":"當以 AWS Directory Service（Active Directory）作為 identity source 時，IAM Identity Center 會將目錄中的使用者、群組及群組成員資格同步到自己的 identity store，而群組成員資格仍然是在 Active Directory 中管理，而非在 IAM Identity Center 本身管理。AWS access portal 只會列出直接指派給使用者本人、或指派給該使用者所屬群組的帳戶與 permission set。由於此題的 permission set 是指派給帳戶層級的 DevOps 群組，且除了一位開發人員外其他人都已經看得到，代表指派與 provisioning 本身運作正常——唯一因人而異的變數就是目錄中的群組成員資格。AWS 官方針對 IAM Identity Center 的疑難排解文件正好記載了這類問題：使用者在 Active Directory 中的群組成員資格，除非該使用者是該群組明確（'member' 屬性）成員，否則不一定能可靠同步到 IAM Identity Center 的 identity store——例如 AWS 特別指出，使用者的 AD「主要群組」（primary group，如 Domain Users，或任何被設為主要群組的群組）不會被 IAM Identity Center 讀取其成員資格，因此若某使用者只是透過主要群組語意與某群組關聯（而缺少明確的 member 項目），即使其他以明確成員身份加入的同事看得到該群組的指派，這位使用者在 access portal 中仍看不到。因此解法就是確保在 Directory Service 中把這位剩下的開發人員加入為 DevOps 群組的明確成員，之後 AD 到 IAM Identity Center 的同步就會抓到該成員資格，該 permission set 便會出現在該使用者的 AWS access portal 中——這正是選項 A 所做的事。","distractors":[{"letter":"B","why_en":"Removing and re-adding the permission set assignment operates on the account/group assignment itself, which every other developer already proves is working correctly; it does nothing to change what IAM Identity Center believes about the one affected user's directory group membership, so it would not fix a single-user visibility gap caused by AD sync.","why_zh":"移除再重新加入 permission set 指派，動的是帳戶／群組層級的指派本身，而其他所有開發人員都已證明這項指派運作正常；這個動作完全不會改變 IAM Identity Center 對那一位受影響使用者在目錄中群組成員資格的認知，因此無法修復因 AD 同步造成的單一使用者可見性問題。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"A permission set is a collection of IAM policies (and optionally a permissions boundary) that take effect after a user has already signed in and selected an account; it has no per-user 'console access' setting, and it cannot control whether the permission set tile is even displayed to a given user in the access portal.","why_zh":"Permission set 是一組 IAM 政策（可選加上 permissions boundary），只有在使用者登入並選擇帳戶「之後」才會生效；它沒有針對個別使用者的「console access」設定，也無法控制某位使用者在 access portal 中是否能看到該 permission set 的圖示。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"IAM Identity Center automatically creates and manages its own AWS-owned service-linked role/roles (e.g. AWSReservedSSO_* roles and AWSServiceRoleForSSO) in member accounts whenever an assignment is provisioned; this is not something a security engineer manually adds, and if it were somehow missing it would break access for every developer in the account, not just one.","why_zh":"IAM Identity Center 在指派被 provision 時，會自動在成員帳戶中建立並管理自己的 AWS 擁有的 service-linked role（例如 AWSReservedSSO_* 角色與 AWSServiceRoleForSSO），這不是需要工程師手動加入的東西；而且若真的缺少該角色，會導致該帳戶中所有開發人員都無法存取，而不會只影響一人。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/singlesignon/latest/userguide/troubleshooting.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/singlesignon/latest/userguide/manage-sync-configurable-ADsync.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/singlesignon/latest/userguide/using-the-portal.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/singlesignon/latest/userguide/manage-your-identity-source-ad.html"]}},{"id":59,"question_en":"A security engineer for a company wants to maintain all IAM users and roles according to the principle of least privilege. The security engineer plans to audit the IAM permissions once every 365 days. The security engineer must view the permissions that each IAM identity used in the last 365 days and must remove any unused permissions. Which solution will meet these requirements?","question_zh":"某公司的安全工程师希望根据最小权限原则维护所有IAM用户和角色。该安全工程师计划每 365天审计一次IAM权限，必须查看过去365天内每个IAM身份所使用的权限，并移除任何未 使用的权限。 哪种解决方案能满足这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Use AWS CloudTrail logs to review IAM identity actions and to remove unused permissions.","B":"Use AWS Config to review configuration changes by each IAM identity and to remove unused permissions.","C":"Use AWS Identity and Access Management Access Analyzer to review last accessed information and to remove unused permissions.","D":"Use AWS Trusted Advisor to check the IAM identities that have elevated permissions and to remove unused permissions."},"options_zh":{"A":"使用 AWS CloudTrail 日志审查 IAM 身份操作，并移除未使用的权限。","B":"使用 AWS Config 审查每个 IAM 身份的配置变更，并移除未使用的权限。","C":"使用 AWS 身份和访问管理（IAM）访问分析器查看最后访问信息，并移除未使用的权限。","D":"使用 AWS Trusted Advisor 检查具有提升权限的 IAM 身份，并移除未使用的权限。"},"answer":["C"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Organizations/Governance","Security/IAM","Monitoring/Ops"],"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選","research":{"verdict":["C"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"both","explanation_en":"IAM Access Analyzer is the purpose-built tool for this exact requirement. Its unused access analyzers continuously monitor IAM users and roles and generate three relevant finding types: unused roles, unused IAM user access keys/passwords, and unused permissions (service-level and action-level permissions that weren't used within the specified usage window). This is built on IAM's last accessed information feature, which AWS documentation states explicitly helps identify unused permissions so administrators can refine policies toward least privilege. IAM tracks last accessed information for a period of at least 400 days (since April/May 2021-2023 depending on service), so a 365-day audit window is fully covered by the data IAM retains. The last accessed data shows which AWS services and actions each IAM identity actually attempted to use, letting the engineer compare granted vs. used permissions and remove what was never exercised — exactly the workflow described in the question. CloudTrail records raw API call events but does not summarize granted-vs-used permissions per identity (and default trail/event history retention is only 90 days, far short of 365); AWS Config tracks resource configuration state/changes, not which permissions an identity invoked; Trusted Advisor's IAM-related checks (e.g., IAM use, access key rotation, root account MFA) do not include a per-identity used-vs-granted permissions report. Only IAM Access Analyzer directly delivers 'permissions used over N days, so I can remove the unused ones.'","explanation_zh":"IAM Access Analyzer 正是為此需求而設計的工具。其 unused access analyzer 會持續監控 IAM 使用者與角色，產生三類相關 findings：未使用角色（unused roles）、未使用的 IAM 使用者存取金鑰/密碼，以及未使用權限（unused permissions，指在指定期間內未被使用的服務層級與動作層級權限）。此功能建立在 IAM 的 last accessed information 之上，AWS 文件明確指出該資訊可協助找出未使用權限，讓管理者精簡政策以符合最小權限原則。IAM 追蹤 last accessed 資訊的期間至少 400 天（依服務不同，自 2021~2023 年間開始追蹤），因此 365 天的稽核週期完全涵蓋在 IAM 保留的資料範圍內。last accessed 資料會顯示每個 IAM 身分實際嘗試使用過哪些 AWS 服務與動作，讓工程師能比對「已授予 vs. 實際使用」的權限，移除從未被使用的部分——這正是題目所描述的流程。CloudTrail 只記錄原始 API 呼叫事件，不會彙總每個身分「已授予 vs. 已使用」的權限，且預設的 trail/事件歷史保留僅 90 天，遠不及 365 天；AWS Config 追蹤的是資源組態狀態/變更，而非身分實際呼叫了哪些權限；Trusted Advisor 的 IAM 相關檢查（如 IAM 使用情形、存取金鑰輪換、root 帳戶 MFA）並不包含逐身分的「已用 vs. 已授予」權限報告。只有 IAM Access Analyzer 能直接提供「N 天內使用了哪些權限，藉此移除未使用的權限」這項功能。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"CloudTrail records API activity but does not summarize which granted permissions went unused; deriving unused permissions per identity would require building custom log analysis across all events, and default CloudTrail event history retention is only 90 days — far short of the 365-day window the question requires. It is not the direct mechanism AWS provides for this task.","why_zh":"CloudTrail 記錄 API 活動，但不會彙總哪些已授予的權限未被使用；要按身分推導未使用權限需自行對所有事件建立客製化日誌分析，且 CloudTrail 預設事件歷史保留僅 90 天，遠不及題目要求的 365 天週期，並非 AWS 為此任務提供的直接機制。"},{"letter":"B","why_en":"AWS Config tracks resource configuration state and changes over time (including changes to IAM resource configurations), not which permissions an identity actually invoked/used, so it cannot identify unused permissions.","why_zh":"AWS Config 追蹤的是資源組態狀態與隨時間的變更（包含 IAM 資源組態的變更），而非身分實際呼叫/使用了哪些權限，因此無法找出未使用的權限。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"Trusted Advisor's IAM-related checks cover items like IAM use, MFA on root account, and access key rotation age; it has no check that reports last-accessed data or maps used-vs-granted permissions per IAM identity.","why_zh":"Trusted Advisor 的 IAM 相關檢查僅涵蓋 IAM 使用情形、root 帳戶 MFA、存取金鑰輪換期限等項目，沒有任何檢查能回報各 IAM 身分的 last accessed 資料或比對「已用 vs. 已授予」的權限。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/IAM/latest/UserGuide/access_policies_last-accessed.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/IAM/latest/UserGuide/access-analyzer-findings.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/IAM/latest/UserGuide/access-analyzer-findings-view.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/IAM/latest/UserGuide/what-is-access-analyzer.html"]}},{"id":60,"question_en":"A company has a large fleet of Amazon Linux 2 Amazon EC2 instances that run an application processing sensitive data. Compliance requirements include no exposed management ports, full session logging, and authentication through AWS IAM Identity Center. DevOps engineers occasionally need access for troubleshooting. Which solution will provide remote access while meeting these requirements?","question_zh":"一家公司拥有大量运行 Amazon Linux 2 的 Amazon EC2 实例，用于处理敏感数据的应用程序。 合规要求包括不得暴露管理端口、完整会话日志记录，以及通过 AWS IAM Identity Center 进 行身份验证。DevOps 工程师偶尔需要访问权限以进行故障排除。 哪种解决方案可以在满足这些要求的同时提供远程访问？","options_en":{"A":"Grant access to the EC2 serial console and allow IAM role access.","B":"Enable EC2 Instance Connect and configure security groups accordingly.","C":"Assign an EC2 instance role that allows access to AWS Systems Manager. Create an IAM policy that grants access to Systems Manager Session Manager and assign it to an IAM Identity Center role.","D":"Use Systems Manager Automation to temporarily open remote access ports."},"options_zh":{"A":"授予 EC2 串行控制台访问权限并允许 IAM 角色访问。","B":"启用 EC2 实例连接并相应地配置安全组。","C":"分配一个允许访问 AWS Systems Manager 的 EC2 实例角色。创建一个 IAM 策略，授予对 Systems Manager Session Manager 的访问权限，并将其分配给 IAM Identity Center 角色。","D":"使用 Systems Manager 自动化功能临时开放远程访问端口。"},"answer":["C"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Security/IAM","Compute","Monitoring/Ops"],"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選","research":{"verdict":["C"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"AWS Systems Manager Session Manager is the only option that satisfies all three compliance requirements simultaneously. Per the official Session Manager documentation, it provides \"secure node management without the need to open inbound ports, maintain bastion hosts, or manage SSH keys\" (no exposed management ports) and offers \"centralized access control to managed nodes using IAM policies\" — which is exactly what integrating with an IAM Identity Center permission set achieves, since a permission set is itself a collection of IAM policies attached to the role Identity Center users assume. Session Manager also supports full session logging: it records the commands entered and their output during a session, streamed to Amazon S3 and/or CloudWatch Logs, while CloudTrail separately captures the Session Manager API calls (StartSession, TerminateSession, etc.). Option C's architecture — an EC2 instance profile granting Systems Manager access (e.g., AmazonSSMManagedInstanceCore) plus an IAM policy for Session Manager Session Manager attached to an IAM Identity Center role — is precisely the supported pattern: the SSM Agent (built into Amazon Linux 2) on the managed instance talks outbound to the Systems Manager service, DevOps engineers sign in through IAM Identity Center, assume the permission-set role carrying Session Manager permissions, and start a fully logged session with zero open inbound ports.","explanation_zh":"AWS Systems Manager Session Manager 是唯一能同時滿足三項合規要求的選項。根據官方文件，Session Manager 提供「安全的 node 管理，無需開放任何 inbound port、維護 bastion host 或管理 SSH 金鑰」（滿足不暴露管理埠），並具備「透過 IAM policy 對 managed node 做集中式存取控管」的能力——這正是與 IAM Identity Center permission set 整合所達成的效果，因為 permission set 本質上就是附加在 Identity Center 使用者所扮演角色上的一組 IAM policy。Session Manager 同時支援完整的 session 記錄：會記錄 session 期間輸入的指令與其輸出，串流至 Amazon S3 及／或 CloudWatch Logs，CloudTrail 則另外記錄 Session Manager 的 API 呼叫（如 StartSession、TerminateSession）。選項 C 的架構——授予 EC2 instance profile 存取 Systems Manager 的權限（如 AmazonSSMManagedInstanceCore），再將 Session Manager 的 IAM policy 附加到 IAM Identity Center 的角色——正是官方支援的模式：Amazon Linux 2 內建的 SSM Agent 對 Systems Manager 服務發起 outbound 連線，DevOps 工程師透過 IAM Identity Center 登入、扮演帶有 Session Manager 權限的 permission-set 角色，即可在完全不開放任何 inbound 埠的情況下開啟完整記錄的 session。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"The EC2 serial console is meant for out-of-band troubleshooting of boot, network configuration, or SSH-lockout issues; it requires an OS-level user account/password (not IAM Identity Center authentication) to log in once connected, and it does not provide session command logging — it fails both the Identity Center authentication and full-session-logging requirements.","why_zh":"EC2 serial console 是用來做開機、網路設定或 SSH 被鎖死等情況的 out-of-band 疑難排解，連上之後仍需使用 OS 層級的帳號密碼登入（並非透過 IAM Identity Center 驗證），也不提供 session 指令記錄——不符合 Identity Center 驗證與完整 session 記錄兩項要求。"},{"letter":"B","why_en":"EC2 Instance Connect pushes a temporary SSH public key and still requires TCP port 22 to be open in the security group (an exposed management port); it authenticates via IAM/browser-based SSH but does not record session content — only the key-push API call appears in CloudTrail, so it fails both the no-open-ports and full-session-logging requirements.","why_zh":"EC2 Instance Connect 會推送一組臨時的 SSH 公鑰，仍必須在 security group 開放 TCP 22（等於暴露管理埠）；雖然可透過 IAM／瀏覽器式 SSH 驗證，但不會記錄 session 內容——CloudTrail 只會記錄推送金鑰的 API 呼叫，不符合不開放埠與完整 session 記錄兩項要求。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"Using Systems Manager Automation to temporarily open remote-access ports still violates the \"no exposed management ports\" requirement outright (even if temporary), adds operational and security risk from a transiently open port, and provides no inherent session-content logging or IAM Identity Center authentication layer for the actual remote-access protocol used afterward.","why_zh":"使用 Systems Manager Automation 暫時開放遠端存取埠，即便只是暫時性的，仍直接違反「不暴露管理埠」的要求，且暫時開放的埠會帶來額外的維運與安全風險，之後實際使用的遠端存取協定也沒有內建的 session 內容記錄或 IAM Identity Center 驗證層。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/systems-manager/latest/userguide/session-manager.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/systems-manager/latest/userguide/session-manager-logging.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/systems-manager/latest/userguide/getting-started-create-iam-instance-profile.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/singlesignon/latest/userguide/permissionsetsconcept.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AWSEC2/latest/UserGuide/ec2-instance-connect-set-up.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AWSEC2/latest/UserGuide/ec2-serial-console.html"]}},{"id":61,"question_en":"A company uses Amazon Cognito user pools with the hosted UI to authenticate its customers. The company’s security team has detected a surge in bot activity and suspicious traffic that targets the Amazon Cognito endpoints. A security engineer must implement a security solution to block these malicious requests. The security measures must maintain uninterrupted access for legitimate users. Which solution meets these requirements?","question_zh":"一家公司使用 Amazon Cognito 用户池和托管 UI 来对客户进行身份验证。公司的安全团队发现，针对 Amazon Cognito 端点的机器 人活动和可疑流量激增。安全工程师必须实施一项安全解决方案，以阻止这些恶意请求，同时确保合法用户能够持续访问。 哪种解决方案符合这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Use Amazon Cognito threat protection on the user pool.","B":"Configure the Amazon Cognito user pool app client settings to restrict access to only authenticated users.","C":"Associate an AWS WAF web ACL with the Amazon Cognito user pool. Define rules to filter unwanted requests and manage bot traffic.","D":"Use Amazon CloudWatch to monitor incoming Amazon Cognito requests. Create an identity pool to block suspicious user agents."},"options_zh":{"A":"在用户池中使用 Amazon Cognito 威胁防护。","B":"配置 Amazon Cognito 用户池的应用客户端设置，以限制访问权限，仅允许经过身份验证的用户访问。","C":"将 AWS WAF 网站访问控制列表（web ACL）与 Amazon Cognito 用户池关联。定义规则以过滤不需要的请求并管理机器人 流量。","D":"使用 Amazon CloudWatch 监控传入的 Amazon Cognito 请求。创建一个身份池以阻止可疑的 用户代理。"},"answer":["C"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Security/IAM","Monitoring/Ops"],"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選","research":{"verdict":["C"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"The threat is a surge of bot activity and suspicious traffic hitting the Cognito endpoints (hosted UI / API service endpoints), and the fix must block malicious requests while legitimate users keep working. AWS documentation explicitly supports associating an AWS WAF web ACL with a Cognito user pool: 'you can protect your user pool from unwanted requests to your classic hosted UI, managed login, and Amazon Cognito API service endpoints.' A web ACL gives fine-grained control over every HTTPS request the user pool responds to, and rules (rate-based rules, IP reputation lists, and the AWS Managed Rules Bot Control rule group) are purpose-built to filter unwanted requests and manage bot traffic before they ever reach Cognito, so legitimate users are unaffected. Cognito threat protection (option A, formerly advanced security features) is documented as a set of monitoring/response tools for individual authentication events — compromised-credentials detection, adaptive authentication (risk scoring on sign-in), and IP allow/deny lists tied to those risk evaluations. It does not filter or rate-limit volumetric bot/web-request traffic at the endpoint layer, which is exactly what WAF is documented to do. Therefore C is correct.","explanation_zh":"威脅是大量 bot 與可疑流量衝擊 Cognito 端點（hosted UI／API 服務端點），且必須在阻擋惡意請求的同時不影響合法使用者。AWS 官方文件明確支援將 AWS WAF web ACL 關聯到 Cognito user pool：「可保護 user pool 免受對 classic hosted UI、managed login 與 Amazon Cognito API 服務端點的不必要請求」。Web ACL 可對 user pool 回應的所有 HTTPS 請求做細緻控管，並可使用 rate-based rules、IP reputation 清單，以及 AWS Managed Rules Bot Control 規則群組，在請求到達 Cognito 前就過濾不必要的請求並管理 bot 流量，因此合法使用者不受影響。選項 A 的 Cognito threat protection（前身為 advanced security features）文件說明其為針對「個別登入事件」的監控／回應工具——外洩憑證偵測、adaptive authentication（登入風險評分）、以及與風險評估綁定的 IP allow/deny 清單——並不是在端點層過濾大量 bot／web 請求流量，那正是 WAF 文件所述的功能。因此 C 正確。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"Cognito threat protection (advanced security features) provides compromised-credentials detection, adaptive authentication, and IP allow/deny lists tied to risk scoring on individual sign-in/sign-up events. It is not a web-request filter and cannot block surges of bot traffic hitting the hosted UI endpoints; AWS documents WAF web ACLs as the mechanism for filtering unwanted requests and bot traffic to user pool endpoints.","why_zh":"Cognito threat protection（advanced security features）提供外洩憑證偵測、adaptive authentication，以及與風險評分綁定的 IP allow/deny 清單，作用於個別登入／註冊事件。它不是 web 請求過濾器，無法阻擋衝擊 hosted UI 端點的大量 bot 流量；AWS 文件指出過濾 user pool 端點的不必要請求與 bot 流量應使用 WAF web ACL。"},{"letter":"B","why_en":"There is no app client setting that restricts Cognito endpoints to 'only authenticated users' — the hosted UI/authentication endpoints exist precisely to serve unauthenticated users signing in. This option is nonsensical for the attack surface and would not stop bot traffic.","why_zh":"App client 沒有「只允許已驗證使用者存取」的設定——hosted UI／驗證端點本來就是給尚未登入的使用者使用。此選項對這個攻擊面不成立，也無法阻擋 bot 流量。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"CloudWatch only monitors metrics/logs; it cannot block requests. Identity pools issue temporary AWS credentials for authorization to AWS services — they have no capability to block suspicious user agents at the user pool endpoints.","why_zh":"CloudWatch 只能監控指標／日誌，無法阻擋請求。Identity pool 的用途是核發臨時 AWS 憑證以存取 AWS 服務，完全沒有在 user pool 端點阻擋可疑 user agent 的能力。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/cognito/latest/developerguide/user-pool-waf.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/cognito/latest/developerguide/cognito-user-pool-settings-threat-protection.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/waf/latest/developerguide/waf-bot-control.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/cognito/latest/developerguide/cognito-user-pool-settings-advanced-security.html"]}},{"id":62,"question_en":"A company has a VPC that has no internet access and has the private DNS hostnames option enabled. An Amazon Aurora database is running inside the VPC. A security engineer wants to use AWS Secrets Manager to automatically rotate the credentials for the Aurora database. The security engineer configures the Secrets Manager default AWS Lambda rotation function to run inside the same VPC that the Aurora database uses. However, the security engineer determines that the password cannot be rotated properly because the Lambdafunction cannot communicate with the Secrets Manager endpoint. What is the MOST secure way that the security engineer can give the Lambda function the ability to communicate with the Secrets Manager endpoint?","question_zh":"一家公司拥有一个无法访问互联网的VPC，并启用了私有DNS主机名选项。该VPC内运行着一个 Amazon Aurora数据库。安全工程师希望使用AWS Secrets Manager自动轮换Aurora数据库的凭据。为 此，安全工程师将Secrets Manager默认的AWS Lambda轮换函数配置为在与Aurora数据库相同的VPC 中运行。然而，安全工程师发现密码无法正常轮换，因为Lambda函数无法与Secrets Manager端点通 信。 安全工程师应采用哪种最安全的方式，使Lambda函数能够与Secrets Manager端点进行通信？","options_en":{"A":"Add a NAT gateway to the VPC to allow access to the Secrets Manager endpoint.","B":"Add a gateway VPC endpoint to the VPC to allow access to the Secrets Manager endpoint.","C":"Add an interface VPC endpoint to the VPC to allow access to the Secrets Manager endpoint.","D":"Add an internet gateway for the VPC to allow access to the Secrets Manager endpoint."},"options_zh":{"A":"为 VPC 添加 NAT 网关，以允许访问 Secrets Manager 终端节点。","B":"向 VPC 添加一个网关 VPC 终端节点，以允许访问 Secrets Manager 终端节点。","C":"向 VPC 添加一个接口型 VPC 终端节点，以允许访问 Secrets Manager 终端节点。","D":"为 VPC 添加互联网网关，以允许访问 Secrets Manager 终端节点。"},"answer":["C"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Networking/DNS","Security/IAM","Compute","Database"],"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選","research":{"verdict":["C"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"both","explanation_en":"AWS Secrets Manager documentation addresses this exact scenario directly: 'If your Lambda function runs in a VPC that doesn't have internet access, we recommend you configure Secrets Manager service private endpoints within your VPC. Your VPC can then intercept requests addressed to the public regional endpoint and redirect them to the private endpoint.' Secrets Manager private endpoints are interface VPC endpoints powered by AWS PrivateLink, which let resources in a VPC call the Secrets Manager API without an internet gateway, NAT device, VPN, or Direct Connect connection, and traffic never leaves the AWS network. The same guide notes that when automatic rotation is turned on via the console, Secrets Manager creates the Lambda rotation function in the same VPC as the database, and 'we recommend that you create a Secrets Manager endpoint in the same VPC so that requests from the Lambda rotation function to Secrets Manager don't leave the Amazon network.' Because the VPC already has private DNS hostnames enabled, enabling private DNS on the interface endpoint lets the default rotation function reach Secrets Manager at its normal regional hostname (secretsmanager.<region>.amazonaws.com) without any code changes. This makes C the MOST secure option: the AWS docs explicitly state that the NAT gateway/internet gateway alternative (A/D) 'exposes your VPC to more risk because an IP address for the gateway can be attacked from the public Internet,' and gateway VPC endpoints (B) only exist for Amazon S3 and DynamoDB — Secrets Manager is not one of the services gateway endpoints support, so B is not technically possible.","explanation_zh":"AWS Secrets Manager 官方文件直接談到這個情境：「若您的 Lambda 函數執行在沒有網際網路存取的 VPC 中，我們建議您在該 VPC 內設定 Secrets Manager 服務的私有端點。您的 VPC 便可攔截送往公開區域端點的請求，並將其重新導向至私有端點。」Secrets Manager 的私有端點是由 AWS PrivateLink 驅動的 interface VPC endpoint，讓 VPC 內資源可在不使用 internet gateway、NAT 裝置、VPN 或 Direct Connect 連線的情況下呼叫 Secrets Manager API，流量完全不離開 AWS 網路。同一份文件也指出，當透過主控台開啟自動輪替時，Secrets Manager 會在資料庫所在的同一個 VPC 建立 Lambda 輪替函數，「我們建議您在同一個 VPC 建立 Secrets Manager endpoint，使 Lambda 輪替函數對 Secrets Manager 的請求不離開 Amazon 網路。」由於該 VPC 已啟用 private DNS hostnames，只要在 interface endpoint 上啟用 private DNS，預設的輪替函數即可透過正常的區域主機名稱（secretsmanager.<region>.amazonaws.com）連到 Secrets Manager，完全不需修改程式碼。這使 C 成為「最安全」的選項：AWS 文件明確指出 NAT gateway／internet gateway 的替代方案（A／D）「會讓您的 VPC 暴露在更高風險中，因為 gateway 的 IP 位址可能遭受來自公網的攻擊」；而 gateway VPC endpoint（B）僅支援 Amazon S3 與 DynamoDB，Secrets Manager 並不在 gateway endpoint 支援的服務之列，因此 B 在技術上不可行。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"A NAT gateway would let the Lambda function reach the Secrets Manager public endpoint over the internet, but AWS docs explicitly call this riskier than a private endpoint because the gateway's public IP address can be attacked from the internet; it also contradicts the VPC's no-internet-access design.","why_zh":"NAT gateway 可讓 Lambda 函數透過網際網路連到 Secrets Manager 公開端點，但 AWS 文件明確指出這比私有端點風險更高，因為 gateway 的公有 IP 位址可能遭受網際網路攻擊；同時也違背此 VPC「無網際網路存取」的設計。"},{"letter":"B","why_en":"Gateway VPC endpoints are only available for Amazon S3 and DynamoDB. Secrets Manager requires an interface VPC endpoint (AWS PrivateLink), not a gateway endpoint, so this option is not technically achievable.","why_zh":"Gateway VPC endpoint 只提供給 Amazon S3 與 DynamoDB。Secrets Manager 需要的是 interface VPC endpoint（AWS PrivateLink），而非 gateway endpoint，因此此選項在技術上無法實現。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"An internet gateway would give the VPC public internet access to reach the Secrets Manager public endpoint, which is the least secure option and directly contradicts the requirement that the VPC has no internet access; AWS docs group this with the NAT gateway approach as exposing the VPC to more risk.","why_zh":"Internet gateway 會讓 VPC 具備公網存取以連到 Secrets Manager 公開端點，這是最不安全的選項，且直接違反該 VPC「無網際網路存取」的要求；AWS 文件將此方式與 NAT gateway 方案一併視為會讓 VPC 暴露在更高風險中。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/secretsmanager/latest/userguide/rotation-function-network-access.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/secretsmanager/latest/userguide/vpc-endpoint-overview.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/vpc/latest/privatelink/gateway-endpoints.html"]}},{"id":63,"question_en":"A security engineer is designing security controls for a fleet of Amazon EC2 instances that run sensitive workloads in a VPC. The security engineer needs to implement a solution to detect and mitigate software vulnerabilities on the EC2 instances.Which solution will meet this requirement?","question_zh":"安全工程师正在为运行在VPC中的敏感工作负载的Amazon EC2实例集群设计安全控制措施。该安全工程师需要实施一种解决 方案，以检测并缓解EC2实例上的软件漏洞。 哪种解决方案能满足这一要求？","options_en":{"A":"Scan the EC2 instances by using Amazon Inspector. Apply security patches and updates by using AWS Systems Manager Patch Manager.","B":"Install host-based firewall and antivirus software on each EC2 instance. Use AWS Systems Manager Run Command to update the firewall and antivirus software.","C":"Install the Amazon CloudWatch agent on the EC2 instances. Enable detailed logging. Use Amazon EventBridge to review the software logs for anomalies.","D":"Scan the EC2 instances by using Amazon GuardDuty Malware Protection. Apply security patches and updates by using AWS Systems Manager Patch Manager."},"options_zh":{"A":"使用 Amazon Inspector 扫描 EC2 实例，并通过 AWS Systems Manager Patch Manager 应用安全补丁和更新。","B":"在每个EC2实例上安装基于主机的防火墙和防病毒软件，并使用AWS Systems Manager运行命令来更新防火墙和防病毒软件。","C":"在 EC2 实例上安装 Amazon CloudWatch 代理，启用详细日志记录，并使用 Amazon EventBridge 检查软件日志中的异常情 况。","D":"使用 Amazon GuardDuty 恶意软件防护扫描 EC2 实例，并使用 AWS Systems Manager 补丁管理器应用安全补丁和更新。"},"answer":["A"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Security/IAM","Compute","Serverless/Integration","Monitoring/Ops"],"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選","research":{"verdict":["A"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"The requirement has two parts: detect software vulnerabilities and mitigate them. Amazon Inspector is AWS's purpose-built vulnerability management service — per AWS docs, when EC2 scanning is activated, Inspector 'scans your EC2 instances for common vulnerabilities and exposures (CVEs), network exposure issues, network reachability issues, operating system and programming language package vulnerabilities,' using either the SSM Agent or agentless EBS-snapshot scanning. AWS Systems Manager Patch Manager then automates applying OS and application security patches, directly mitigating the vulnerabilities Inspector finds — Patch Manager is the standard remediation path for Inspector findings. This Inspector-detect + Patch Manager-remediate pairing is the canonical AWS answer, so A is correct. GuardDuty Malware Protection (D) is the closest distractor, but AWS documentation defines it narrowly as a feature that 'helps you detect the potential presence of malware by scanning the Amazon EBS volumes that are attached to Amazon EC2 instances' — it identifies malicious files/infections, not unpatched CVEs or vulnerable software packages, so it does not satisfy the 'detect software vulnerabilities' requirement.","explanation_zh":"題目要求兩件事：偵測軟體弱點並加以緩解。Amazon Inspector 是 AWS 專門的弱點管理服務——根據 AWS 官方文件，啟用 EC2 scanning 後，Inspector 會「scans your EC2 instances for common vulnerabilities and exposures (CVEs), network exposure issues, network reachability issues, operating system and programming language package vulnerabilities」，透過 SSM Agent 的代理式掃描或 EBS 快照的無代理掃描完成。AWS Systems Manager Patch Manager 則自動化套用作業系統與應用程式的安全修補程式，直接緩解 Inspector 發現的弱點；Patch Manager 正是 Inspector 發現項目的標準修復途徑。這種「Inspector 偵測＋Patch Manager 修補」是 AWS 的標準答案，故 A 正確。D 的 GuardDuty Malware Protection 是最接近的干擾項，但 AWS 文件明確將其定義為「helps you detect the potential presence of malware by scanning the Amazon EBS volumes that are attached to Amazon EC2 instances」——它偵測的是惡意檔案／感染，而非未修補的 CVE 或有弱點的軟體套件，因此不符合「偵測軟體弱點」的要求。","distractors":[{"letter":"B","why_en":"Third-party host-based firewall/antivirus software detects intrusions and malware, not software vulnerabilities (unpatched CVEs); it also adds per-instance operational overhead and Run Command only updates the tools, it does not patch vulnerable software.","why_zh":"第三方主機防火牆／防毒軟體偵測的是入侵與惡意程式，而非軟體弱點（未修補的 CVE）；且每台執行個體都要維運，Run Command 只是更新這些工具本身，並不會修補有弱點的軟體。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"The CloudWatch agent collects logs and metrics; reviewing logs for anomalies is reactive monitoring and cannot enumerate vulnerable software packages, and EventBridge routes events rather than analyzing logs. Neither component detects or patches vulnerabilities.","why_zh":"CloudWatch agent 只收集日誌與指標；用日誌找異常屬於事後監控，無法列舉有弱點的軟體套件，而 EventBridge 是事件路由服務並非日誌分析工具。兩者都不能偵測或修補弱點。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"GuardDuty Malware Protection for EC2 performs agentless scans of EBS volumes to detect malware (malicious files) — typically triggered after suspicious behavior — it does not scan installed software packages for vulnerabilities/CVEs. Vulnerability detection is Amazon Inspector's job. Confirmed directly from docs.aws.amazon.com/guardduty/latest/ug/malware-protection.html.","why_zh":"GuardDuty Malware Protection for EC2 是對 EBS 磁碟區做無代理掃描以偵測惡意軟體（惡意檔案），通常在偵測到可疑行為後觸發；它不會掃描已安裝軟體套件的弱點／CVE。弱點偵測是 Amazon Inspector 的職責，已由 docs.aws.amazon.com/guardduty/latest/ug/malware-protection.html 直接確認。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/inspector/latest/user/scanning-resources.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/inspector/latest/user/scanning-ec2.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/inspector/latest/user/what-is-inspector.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/systems-manager/latest/userguide/patch-manager.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/guardduty/latest/ug/malware-protection.html"]}},{"id":64,"question_en":"A company requires a specific software application to be installed on all new and existing Amazon EC2 instances across an AWS Organization. SSM Agent is installed and active. How can the company continuously monitor deployment status of the software application?","question_zh":"一家公司需要在 AWS 组织内的所有新旧 Amazon EC2 实例上安装特定的软件应用程序。SSM Agent 已安装并处于活动状 态。 公司如何持续监控软件应用的部署状态？","options_en":{"A":"Use AWS Config organization-wide with the ec2-managedinstance-applications-required managed rule and specify the application name.","B":"Use approved AMIs rule organization-wide.","C":"Use Distributor package and review output.","D":"Use Systems Manager Application Manager inventory filtering."},"options_zh":{"A":"在整个组织中使用 AWS Config，并应用 ec2-managedinstance-applications-required 管理规则，同时指定应用程序名称。","B":"在整个组织范围内使用经批准的AMI规则。","C":"使用分发包并查看输出结果。","D":"使用 Systems Manager 应用程序管理器的库存筛选功能。"},"answer":["A"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Organizations/Governance","Compute","Monitoring/Ops"],"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選","research":{"verdict":["A"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"The requirement is to CONTINUOUSLY MONITOR whether a specific application is installed on all new and existing EC2 instances across an AWS Organization. The AWS Config managed rule ec2-managedinstance-applications-required does exactly this: per AWS docs, it 'checks if all of the specified applications are installed on the instance,' using SSM Inventory data (resource type AWS::SSM::ManagedInstanceInventory), and explicitly notes 'Ensure that SSM agent is running on the EC2 instance and an association to gather application software inventory is created' (returning NOT_APPLICABLE otherwise) — which is exactly why the question states SSM Agent is installed and active. The rule takes an applicationNames CSV parameter, has trigger type 'Configuration changes' for ongoing/continuous evaluation, and flags non-compliant instances. AWS Config also supports organization-wide deployment via PutOrganizationConfigRule (organization config rules) and organization conformance packs, satisfying the AWS Organization-wide scope for both new and existing accounts/instances. The other options either check the wrong thing (approved AMIs only validate launch-time AMI source, not currently-installed software), perform one-time deployment rather than continuous monitoring (Distributor), or require manual, non-evaluated, per-console inspection (Application Manager inventory filtering) with no automated organization-wide compliance tracking.","explanation_zh":"題目要求在整個 AWS Organization 中「持續監控」所有新舊 EC2 instance 是否安裝了特定軟體。AWS Config 受管規則 ec2-managedinstance-applications-required 正是為此設計：官方文件說明它會透過 SSM Inventory 資料（資源類型 AWS::SSM::ManagedInstanceInventory）檢查指定的應用程式是否已安裝在 instance 上，並明確指出「需確保 EC2 instance 上執行 SSM agent，且已建立收集應用程式軟體 inventory 的 association」（否則回傳 NOT_APPLICABLE）——這正是題目強調 SSM Agent 已安裝並啟用的原因。此規則接受 applicationNames（CSV）參數，觸發類型為 Configuration changes 以持續評估，並將未合規的 instance 標記出來。AWS Config 也支援透過 PutOrganizationConfigRule（organization config rules）與 organization conformance packs 在整個 Organization 範圍部署，滿足對新舊帳號/instance 的全組織涵蓋。其他選項不是檢查對象錯誤（approved AMIs 只驗證啟動時使用的 AMI 來源，不代表目前是否安裝該軟體），就是只做一次性部署而非持續監控（Distributor），或需人工、無自動評估、逐主控台檢視（Application Manager inventory 篩選），無法提供跨整個 Organization 的自動化合規追蹤。","distractors":[{"letter":"B","why_en":"The approved-amis-by-id rule only checks whether instances were launched from approved AMIs; it says nothing about whether a specific application is currently installed, and cannot monitor software added or removed after launch on existing instances.","why_zh":"approved-amis-by-id 規則只檢查 instance 是否由核准的 AMI 啟動，無法得知特定應用程式目前是否已安裝，也無法監控既有 instance 在啟動後新增或移除的軟體。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"Distributor is a deployment mechanism for installing packages; reviewing its command output only gives point-in-time installation results, not continuous, organization-wide compliance monitoring of whether the software remains installed on every instance.","why_zh":"Distributor 是安裝套件的部署機制；檢視其命令輸出只能得到當下的安裝結果，無法對整個 Organization 的所有 instance 持續監控軟體是否仍安裝。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"Filtering SSM Inventory in Application Manager is a manual, per-account/console inspection with no compliance evaluation or automatic re-checking; it does not provide continuous monitoring across an entire AWS Organization.","why_zh":"在 Application Manager 中篩選 SSM Inventory 是逐帳號、手動的主控台檢視，沒有合規評估或自動重新檢查，無法對整個 AWS Organization 提供持續監控。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/config/latest/developerguide/ec2-managedinstance-applications-required.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/config/latest/developerguide/config-rule-multi-account-deployment.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/systems-manager/latest/userguide/systems-manager-inventory.html"]}},{"id":65,"question_en":"A company uses AWS to run a web application that manages ticket sales in several countries. The company recently migrated the application to an architecture that includes Amazon API Gateway, AWS Lambda, and Amazon Aurora Serverless. The company needs the application to comply with Payment Card Industry Data Security Standard (PCI DSS) v4.0. A security engineer must generate a report that shows the effectiveness of the PCI DSS v4.0 controls that apply to the application. The company ' s compliance team must be able to add manual evidence to the report. Which solution will meet these requirements?","question_zh":"一家公司使用 AWS 运行一个管理多个国家票务销售的 Web 应用程序。该公司最近将该应用迁移至包含 Amazon API Gateway、 AWS Lambda 和 Amazon Aurora Serverless 的架构。公司要求该应用符合支付卡行业数据安全标准（PCI DSS）v4.0。安全工程 师需要生成一份报告，以展示适用于该应用的 PCI DSS v4.0 控制措施的有效性。公司的合规团队必须能够向报告中添加手动 证据。 哪种解决方案能满足这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Enable AWS Trusted Advisor. Configure all the Trusted Advisor checks. Manually map the checks against the PCI DSS v4.0 standard to generate the report.","B":"Enable and configure AWS Config. Deploy the Operational Best Practices for PCI DSS conformance pack in AWS Config. Use AWS Config to generate the report.","C":"Enable AWS Security Hub. Enable the Security Hub PCI DSS security standard. Use the AWS Management Console to download the report from the security standard.","D":"Create an AWS Audit Manager assessment that uses the AWS managed PCI DSS v4.0 standard framework. Add all evidence to the assessment. Generate the report in Audit Manager for download."},"options_zh":{"A":"启用 AWS Trusted Advisor，配置所有 Trusted Advisor 检查项，并手动将这些检查项与 PCI DSS v4.0 标准对应，以 生成报告。","B":"启用并配置 AWS Config。在 AWS Config 中部署用于符合 PCI DSS 的运营最佳实践合规包。使用 AWS Config 生成 报告。","C":"启用 AWS Security Hub。启用 Security Hub 的 PCI DSS 安全标准，并使用 AWS 管理控制台从该安全标准下载 报告。","D":"创建一个使用 AWS 管理的 PCI DSS v4.0 标准框架的 AWS 审计管理评估。将所有证据添加到该评估中，并在审计管 理中生成报告以供下载。"},"answer":["D"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Organizations/Governance","Security/IAM","Compute","Database","Serverless/Integration"],"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選","research":{"verdict":["D"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"AWS Audit Manager provides a prebuilt, AWS-managed PCI DSS v4.0 framework (40 automated controls, 240 manual controls, 15 control sets) that continuously collects evidence showing the effectiveness of controls that map to the standard. Critically, Audit Manager is the only option that lets the compliance team add manual evidence — by importing files from S3, uploading files from a browser, or entering free-text responses — alongside the automatically collected evidence, and then generate a downloadable assessment report for auditors. The requirement to 'add manual evidence to the report' is the decisive qualifier: Security Hub, AWS Config conformance packs, and Trusted Advisor only produce automated check/finding results with no mechanism for attaching manual evidence or producing an audit-style evidence report. Therefore D is correct.","explanation_zh":"AWS Audit Manager 提供 AWS 託管的預建 PCI DSS v4.0 framework（40 個自動化控制、240 個手動控制、15 個控制集），可持續收集證據以展示對應該標準之控制的有效性。關鍵在於：Audit Manager 是唯一允許合規團隊加入手動證據（manual evidence）的選項——可從 S3 匯入檔案、從瀏覽器上傳檔案或輸入文字回覆——並將其與自動收集的證據合併，最後產生可下載的 assessment report 供稽核使用。「必須能在報告中加入手動證據」是本題的決定性條件：Security Hub、AWS Config conformance pack 與 Trusted Advisor 都只產出自動化檢查／發現結果，沒有附加手動證據或產生稽核式證據報告的機制。因此 D 正確。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"Trusted Advisor provides best-practice checks (cost, performance, security, etc.), is not mapped to PCI DSS, cannot collect audit evidence, and offers no way to add manual evidence; manually mapping checks to PCI DSS v4.0 is error-prone and does not produce a compliance-effectiveness report.","why_zh":"Trusted Advisor 只提供最佳實務檢查（成本、效能、安全等），並未對應 PCI DSS，無法收集稽核證據，也沒有加入手動證據的功能；手動把檢查對應到 PCI DSS v4.0 既易錯也無法產生控制有效性報告。"},{"letter":"B","why_en":"AWS Config does offer a 'Operational Best Practices for PCI DSS 4.0' conformance pack, but a conformance pack is only a sample mapping of managed/custom Config rules to PCI DSS controls — it evaluates automated resource-configuration compliance and shows a compliance dashboard, with no way for the compliance team to attach manual evidence or produce an audit-style effectiveness report.","why_zh":"AWS Config 確實有「Operational Best Practices for PCI DSS 4.0」conformance pack，但 conformance pack 只是把 managed/custom Config rules 對應到 PCI DSS 控制的範例映射——僅評估自動化的資源組態合規性並顯示合規儀表板，合規團隊無法在其中附加手動證據，也無法產生稽核式的控制有效性報告。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"Security Hub's PCI DSS standard (v3.2.1, with v4.0.1 added later) provides automated control-check findings and a security score, but it has no manual-evidence capability and no downloadable audit report of control effectiveness with attached evidence.","why_zh":"Security Hub 的 PCI DSS 標準（v3.2.1，之後才新增 v4.0.1）只提供自動化控制檢查結果與安全分數，沒有加入手動證據的功能，也無法下載含證據的控制有效性稽核報告。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/audit-manager/latest/userguide/pci-v4.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/audit-manager/latest/userguide/upload-evidence.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/audit-manager/latest/userguide/assessment-reports.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/securityhub/latest/userguide/pci-standard.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/config/latest/developerguide/operational-best-practices-for-pci-dss-v4-including-global-resource-types.html"]}},{"id":66,"question_en":"A company has decided to move its fleet of Linux-based web server instances to an Amazon EC2 Auto Scaling group. Currently, the instances are static and are launched manually. When an administrator needs to view log files, the administrator uses SSH to establish a connection to the instances and retrieves the logs manually. The company often needs to query the logs to produce results about application sessions and user issues. The company does not want its new automatically scaling architecture to result in the loss of any log files when instances are scaled in. Which combination of steps should a security engineer take to meet these requirements MOST cost- effectively? (Select TWO.)","question_zh":"一家公司决定将其基于 Linux 的 Web 服务器实例迁移至 Amazon EC2 自动扩展组。目前，这些实例 是静态的，并且需要手动启动。当管理员需要查看日志文件时，会通过 SSH 连接到实例并手动获取 日志。 公司经常需要查询日志，以生成有关应用会话和用户问题的报告。公司不希望其新的自动伸缩架构 在实例缩减时导致任何日志文件丢失。 安全工程师应采取哪些步骤组合才能以最具成本效益的方式满足这些要求？（选择两项。）","options_en":{"A":"Configure a cron job on the instances to forward the log files to Amazon S3 periodically.","B":"Configure AWS Glue and Amazon Athena to query the log files.","C":"Configure the Amazon CloudWatch agent on the instances to forward the logs to Amazon CloudWatch Logs.","D":"Configure Amazon CloudWatch Logs Insights to query the log files.","E":"Configure the instances to write the logs to an Amazon Elastic File System (Amazon EFS) volume."},"options_zh":{"A":"在实例上配置定时任务，定期将日志文件转发到 Amazon S3。","B":"配置 AWS Glue 和 Amazon Athena 以查询日志文件。","C":"在实例上配置 Amazon CloudWatch 代理，将日志转发到 Amazon CloudWatch Logs。","D":"配置 Amazon CloudWatch Logs Insights 以查询日志文件。","E":"配置实例将日志写入 Amazon 弹性文件系统（Amazon EFS）卷。"},"answer":["C","D"],"multi":true,"vote":{},"tags":["Storage","Compute","Cost Optimization","Monitoring/Ops","Analytics"],"difficulty":2,"diff_why":"複選","research":{"verdict":["C","D"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"The two requirements are durability (no log loss when Auto Scaling terminates instances) and queryability (analyze application sessions and user issues), delivered MOST cost-effectively. Installing the CloudWatch agent (C) streams log lines to CloudWatch Logs continuously and in near real-time, so logs are preserved off-instance before a scale-in event terminates the host — this is AWS's documented pattern for collecting logs from ephemeral EC2 fleets. Once the logs are in CloudWatch Logs, CloudWatch Logs Insights (D) provides a built-in, pay-per-query interactive query capability with no additional infrastructure to provision or manage. The C+D pair works end-to-end as one pipeline. A cron-to-S3 approach risks losing logs written between the last sync and instance termination, and Glue+Athena adds crawler/catalog cost and only works on S3-resident data; EFS avoids loss but adds an always-on file-system cost and still provides no query capability.","explanation_zh":"本題兩個需求是：Auto Scaling scale-in 終止執行個體時日誌不能遺失（持久性），以及能查詢日誌分析應用工作階段與使用者問題（可查詢性），且要「最具成本效益」。在執行個體上安裝 CloudWatch agent（C）可近乎即時地把日誌串流到 CloudWatch Logs，日誌在 scale-in 終止前就已離開執行個體，這是 AWS 文件中收集短暫性 EC2 機群日誌的標準做法。日誌進入 CloudWatch Logs 後，CloudWatch Logs Insights（D）提供內建、按查詢量計費的互動式查詢功能，無需額外佈建任何基礎設施。C+D 組合構成一條完整的管線。cron 定期上傳 S3 會遺失最後一次同步到終止之間的日誌；Glue+Athena 需要日誌先在 S3 且增加 crawler/目錄成本；EFS 雖不會遺失但有常駐檔案系統費用，且本身不提供查詢能力。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"A periodic cron upload to S3 leaves a gap: any log entries written after the last cron run are lost when Auto Scaling terminates the instance during scale-in, violating the no-log-loss requirement. It also pairs with B (Athena) rather than D, and the C+D pipeline is simpler and cheaper.","why_zh":"cron 定期上傳 S3 有時間差：最後一次上傳後、執行個體被 scale-in 終止前寫入的日誌會遺失，違反不丟日誌的要求。它需搭配 B（Athena）而非 D，而 C+D 管線更簡單、更省成本。"},{"letter":"B","why_en":"Glue + Athena only queries data in Amazon S3; it cannot query logs sitting in CloudWatch Logs directly, and it adds Glue crawler/Data Catalog setup and cost. With logs streamed to CloudWatch Logs via the agent, Logs Insights is the cheaper, zero-setup query option.","why_zh":"Glue + Athena 只能查詢 Amazon S3 中的資料，無法直接查詢 CloudWatch Logs 中的日誌，且需額外建置 Glue crawler／Data Catalog 並產生費用。日誌經 agent 進入 CloudWatch Logs 後，Logs Insights 是更便宜、零建置的查詢方式。"},{"letter":"E","why_en":"Writing logs to EFS prevents loss but incurs continuous per-GB storage charges for an always-mounted file system, and EFS provides no query capability — you would still need another tool to analyze sessions and user issues. It is neither the most cost-effective nor a complete solution.","why_zh":"把日誌寫入 EFS 雖可避免遺失，但常駐掛載的檔案系統會持續按 GB 計費，且 EFS 本身沒有查詢功能，仍需其他工具分析工作階段與使用者問題，既不是最具成本效益也不是完整解法。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonCloudWatch/latest/logs/CWL_GettingStarted.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonCloudWatch/latest/monitoring/Install-CloudWatch-Agent.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonCloudWatch/latest/logs/AnalyzingLogData.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/athena/latest/ug/what-is.html"]}},{"id":67,"question_en":"A company wants to deploy an application in a private VPC that will not be connected to the internet. The company’s security team will not allow bastion hosts or methods using SSH to log in to Amazon EC2 instances. The application team plans to use AWS Systems Manager Session Manager to connect to and manage the EC2 instances. Which combination of steps should the security team take? (Select THREE.)","question_zh":"一家公司希望在不连接互联网的私有VPC中部署一个应用程序。公司的安全团队不允许使用堡垒机或通过SSH登录 Amazon EC2实例的方式。应用团队计划使用AWS Systems Manager Session Manager来连接和管理EC2实例。 安全团队应采取哪些步骤组合？","options_en":{"A":"Make sure the Systems Manager Agent is installed and running on all EC2 instances inside the VPC.","B":"Ensure the IAM role attached to the EC2 instances in the VPC allows access to Systems Manager.","C":"Create an SCP that prevents the creation of SSH key pairs.","D":"Launch a NAT gateway in the VPC. Update the routing policies to forward traffic to this NAT gateway.","E":"Ensure proper VPC endpoints are in place for Systems Manager and Amazon EC2.","F":"Ensure the VPC has a transit gateway attachment. Update the routing policies to forward traffic to this transit gateway."},"options_zh":{"B":"确保附加到VPC中EC2实例的IAM角色允许访问Systems Manager。","C":"创建一个SCP，以防止生成SSH密钥对。","D":"在VPC中启动一个NAT网关，并更新路由策略以将流量转发至该NAT网关。","E":"确保为 Systems Manager 和 Amazon EC2 配置了正确的 VPC 终端节点。","F":"确保VPC已连接至传输网关，并更新路由策略，将流量转发至该传输网关。","A":"确保在VPC内的所有EC2实例上已安装并正在运行Systems Manager代理。"},"answer":["A","B","E"],"multi":true,"vote":{},"tags":["Networking/DNS","Organizations/Governance","Security/IAM","Compute","Monitoring/Ops"],"difficulty":2,"diff_why":"複選","research":{"verdict":["A","B","E"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"Session Manager requires three things to work in a private, internet-free VPC, and they map exactly to A, B, and E. First, SSM Agent (minimum version per the Session Manager prerequisites) must be installed and running on every managed EC2 instance, because the agent is what initiates outbound communication to the Systems Manager/Session Manager service — without it the instance is not a 'managed node' at all (A). Second, each instance needs an IAM role (instance profile) that grants Systems Manager permissions — in practice the AmazonSSMManagedInstanceCore policy, which authorizes ssm:UpdateInstanceInformation and the ssmmessages/ec2messages channel actions the agent needs to register with and communicate with the service (B). Third, because the VPC has no internet gateway or NAT and the requirement explicitly forbids internet connectivity, AWS's documented solution is to create interface VPC endpoints (AWS PrivateLink) for com.amazonaws.<region>.ssm, com.amazonaws.<region>.ssmmessages, and com.amazonaws.<region>.ec2messages (plus an EC2 endpoint if EC2 API calls are needed), so that all Systems Manager/Session Manager traffic stays on the AWS network without ever reaching the internet (E). The AWS documentation states this directly: 'AWS PrivateLink restricts all network traffic between your managed nodes, Systems Manager, and Amazon EC2 to the Amazon network... you don't need an internet gateway, a NAT device, or a virtual private gateway.' Option D (NAT gateway) is a direct contradiction of the stated requirement — a NAT gateway only provides a path to the internet via an internet gateway, which the company explicitly does not want. Option F (transit gateway) solves VPC-to-VPC/on-premises routing, not private access to the regional Systems Manager service endpoints, and is not part of the documented Session Manager setup. Option C (an SCP blocking SSH key-pair creation) is a defense-in-depth guardrail against SSH usage but is not a prerequisite for Session Manager connectivity to function — the question asks what makes Session Manager work, not how to further harden against SSH. All cited sources were read and directly support A, B, and E; no better 3-option combination fits the 'no internet, no bastion/SSH' constraint.","explanation_zh":"Session Manager 要在完全不連網際網路的私有 VPC 中運作，需要三個要件，剛好對應選項 A、B、E。第一，每台受管的 EC2 執行個體都必須安裝並執行 SSM Agent（需符合 Session Manager prerequisites 所列的最低版本），因為連線是由 Agent 主動發起、向 Systems Manager／Session Manager 服務註冊與通訊；沒有 Agent，該執行個體根本不算是「managed node」（A）。第二，每台執行個體需要附加具備 Systems Manager 權限的 IAM 角色（instance profile）——實務上是 AmazonSSMManagedInstanceCore 政策，授權 ssm:UpdateInstanceInformation 以及 Agent 與服務通訊所需的 ssmmessages／ec2messages 頻道動作（B）。第三，由於此 VPC 沒有 internet gateway 或 NAT，且題目明確要求不連網際網路，AWS 文件記載的作法是建立 interface VPC endpoints（AWS PrivateLink）：com.amazonaws.<region>.ssm、com.amazonaws.<region>.ssmmessages、com.amazonaws.<region>.ec2messages（若需呼叫 EC2 API 則再加 EC2 endpoint），讓所有 Systems Manager／Session Manager 流量都留在 AWS 網路內，完全不經網際網路（E）。AWS 官方文件明確寫道：『AWS PrivateLink restricts all network traffic between your managed nodes, Systems Manager, and Amazon EC2 to the Amazon network... you don't need an internet gateway, a NAT device, or a virtual private gateway.』選項 D（NAT gateway）與題目要求直接矛盾——NAT gateway 只能透過 internet gateway 提供通往網際網路的路徑，這正是公司明確不想要的。選項 F（transit gateway）解決的是 VPC 間或與地端網路的路由問題，並非私下存取區域性 Systems Manager 服務端點的方式，也不在 AWS 記載的 Session Manager 設定步驟中。選項 C（用 SCP 禁止建立 SSH 金鑰對）是防止使用 SSH 的額外深度防禦措施，但並非讓 Session Manager 連線運作所需的前置條件——題目問的是讓 Session Manager 運作的步驟，而非如何進一步防堵 SSH。所引用的來源均已實際讀取並直接支持 A、B、E；在『不連網、不用 bastion/SSH』的限制下，找不到更合適的三選項組合。","distractors":[{"letter":"C","why_en":"An SCP blocking SSH key-pair creation is a preventive guardrail that reinforces the 'no SSH' policy, but it is not one of the steps required to make Session Manager connectivity actually work in the isolated VPC; Session Manager's prerequisites (agent, IAM role, connectivity) are entirely independent of whether SSH key pairs can be created.","why_zh":"用 SCP 禁止建立 SSH 金鑰對只是強化『禁用 SSH』政策的預防性防護，並非讓 Session Manager 在隔離 VPC 中實際運作所需的步驟；Session Manager 的前置需求（agent、IAM 角色、連線）與能否建立 SSH 金鑰對完全無關。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"A NAT gateway forwards outbound traffic to an internet gateway so instances can reach the internet — the opposite of what the company requires (a VPC 'not connected to the internet'). AWS's documented internet-free path to Systems Manager is PrivateLink interface endpoints, not a NAT gateway.","why_zh":"NAT gateway 會把出站流量轉送到 internet gateway，讓執行個體得以連上網際網路——這正好與公司要求（VPC「不連接網際網路」）相反。AWS 文件記載的無網際網路連往 Systems Manager 的方式是 PrivateLink interface endpoints，而不是 NAT gateway。"},{"letter":"F","why_en":"A transit gateway attachment is for routing between multiple VPCs or to on-premises networks; on its own it does not provide a path to the regional Systems Manager (ssm/ssmmessages/ec2messages) service endpoints, and it is not part of AWS's documented Session Manager setup for an isolated single VPC.","why_zh":"Transit gateway 連接主要用於多個 VPC 之間或與地端網路的路由，本身並不提供通往區域性 Systems Manager（ssm/ssmmessages/ec2messages）服務端點的路徑，對單一隔離 VPC 而言也不在 AWS 記載的 Session Manager 設定流程中。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/systems-manager/latest/userguide/session-manager-getting-started-privatelink.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/systems-manager/latest/userguide/setup-create-vpc.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/systems-manager/latest/userguide/session-manager-prerequisites.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/systems-manager/latest/userguide/setup-instance-permissions.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/systems-manager/latest/userguide/integrations-aws.html"]}},{"id":68,"question_en":"A security engineer needs to prepare a company ' s Amazon EC2 instances for quarantine during a security incident. The AWS Systems Manager Agent (SSM Agent) has been deployed to all EC2 instances. The security engineer has developed a script to install and update forensics tools on the EC2 instances. Which solution will quarantine EC2 instances during a security incident?","question_zh":"安全工程师需要为公司在发生安全事件时隔离其Amazon EC2实例做好准备。AWS Systems Manager代理（SSM Agent）已部署到所有EC2实例上。该安全工程师已编写脚本，用于在EC2实 例上安装和更新取证工具。 在安全事件期间，哪种解决方案会隔离EC2实例？","options_en":{"A":"Create a rule in AWS Config to track SSM Agent versions.","B":"Configure Systems Manager Session Manager to deny all connection requests from external IP addresses.","C":"Store the script in Amazon S3 and grant read access to the instance profile.","D":"Configure IAM permissions for the SSM Agent to run the script as a predefined Systems Manager Run Command document."},"options_zh":{"A":"在 AWS Config 中创建规则以跟踪 SSM Agent 版本。","B":"配置 Systems Manager 会话管理器，拒绝所有来自外部 IP 地址的连接请求。","C":"将脚本存储在 Amazon S3 中，并授予实例配置文件读取权限。","D":"配置 IAM 权限，使 SSM Agent 能够以预定义的 Systems Manager 运行命令文档形式执行脚本。"},"answer":["D"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Organizations/Governance","Security/IAM","Storage","Compute","Monitoring/Ops"],"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選","research":{"verdict":["D"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"The scenario is preparation, not execution: SSM Agent is already on every instance and a forensics script already exists, but nothing yet lets that script be invoked reliably and securely once an incident starts. AWS's Run Command setup guidance is explicit that before any principal (a responder, or the automation that triggers the response) can execute a document, it must be granted ssm:SendCommand permission scoped to that document's ARN, and the target node's instance profile must allow the SSM Agent to communicate with the Systems Manager service. Packaging the engineer's script as a (custom or AWS-provided) Run Command document and configuring the IAM permissions needed to run it supplies exactly that missing piece: a controlled, on-demand, auditable execution path through the already-deployed SSM Agent. This mirrors how AWS's own incident-response automation runbooks work — AWS-QuarantineEC2Instance (assigns an isolation security group that blocks all inbound/outbound traffic) and AWSSupport-ContainEC2Instance are Systems Manager documents invoked via an IAM-permissioned AutomationAssumeRole, not scripts sitting inert in storage. Option C only solves where the script lives and who can read it from the instance side; per AWS's remote-document guidance, even executing a script staged in S3 still requires ssm:SendCommand/ssm:GetDocument permissions and an actual Run Command invocation, so S3 read access alone defines no trigger or execution path — nothing runs the script when an incident occurs. Options A and B are unrelated to quarantine: an AWS Config rule tracking SSM Agent versions is a passive compliance check, and restricting Session Manager to deny external IP addresses only affects interactive shell sessions, not command execution. Among the four options, D is the only one that actually operationalizes running the prepared script on demand, which is the necessary precondition for using it to quarantine/contain instances during an incident.","explanation_zh":"此情境屬於「準備」而非「執行」階段:所有 instance 上都已部署 SSM Agent,forensics script 也已寫好,但目前尚無機制能在事故發生當下,可靠且安全地觸發該 script 執行。AWS 官方的 Run Command 設定文件明確指出,任何主體(不論是回應人員,或觸發回應的自動化)在執行 document 之前,都必須被授予範圍限定於該 document ARN 的 ssm:SendCommand 權限,且目標節點的 instance profile 也必須允許 SSM Agent 與 Systems Manager 服務通訊。將工程師的 script 包裝成(自訂或 AWS 提供的)Run Command document,並設定執行所需的 IAM 權限,正好補上這個缺口:透過已部署的 SSM Agent,提供一條可控、隨需、可稽核的執行路徑。這也符合 AWS 自身事件回應自動化 runbook 的運作方式——AWS-QuarantineEC2Instance(指派會阻擋所有 inbound/outbound 流量的隔離用 security group)與 AWSSupport-ContainEC2Instance,都是透過具備 IAM 權限的 AutomationAssumeRole 呼叫的 Systems Manager document,而不是靜置在儲存體中、毫無作用的 script。選項 C 只解決了 script 存放位置以及 instance 端能否讀取的問題;根據 AWS 官方的遠端 document 執行說明,即使是執行存放在 S3 的 script,仍需要 ssm:SendCommand/ssm:GetDocument 權限並實際發出 Run Command 呼叫——單純的 S3 讀取權限並未定義任何觸發機制或執行路徑,事故發生時並不會自動執行該 script。選項 A 與 B 皆與隔離無關:追蹤 SSM Agent 版本的 AWS Config rule 只是被動的合規檢查;將 Session Manager 設定為拒絕外部 IP 位址,只會影響互動式 shell 連線,與執行指令無關。在四個選項中,D 是唯一真正讓已準備好的 script 能夠隨需執行的選項,而這正是日後用它來隔離/圍堵受影響 instance 的必要前提。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"An AWS Config rule tracking SSM Agent versions only monitors compliance of the agent itself. It has no mechanism to execute a script or quarantine an instance during an incident.","why_zh":"追蹤 SSM Agent 版本的 AWS Config rule 只能監控 agent 本身的合規狀態,並沒有任何機制可以在事故發生時執行 script 或隔離 instance。"},{"letter":"B","why_en":"Restricting Session Manager connections by source IP address controls interactive shell access to instances, but it does not run the forensics script or quarantine the instance network-wise; it is unrelated to the stated requirement.","why_zh":"依來源 IP 位址限制 Session Manager 連線只能控管對 instance 的互動式 shell 存取,並不會執行 forensics script 或在網路層面隔離 instance,與題目要求無關。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"Storing the script in S3 and granting the instance profile read access only makes the script retrievable from the instance side. Per AWS's own remote-document guidance, even S3-based execution still requires ssm:SendCommand/ssm:GetDocument permissions and an actual Run Command invocation — read access alone defines no trigger, invocation path, or central control to actually run the script across instances when an incident occurs.","why_zh":"將 script 存放在 S3 並授予 instance profile 讀取權限,只是讓 instance 端可以取得該 script。根據 AWS 官方遠端 document 執行文件,即使透過 S3 執行,仍需要 ssm:SendCommand/ssm:GetDocument 權限並實際發出 Run Command 呼叫——單純的讀取權限並未定義任何觸發機制、呼叫路徑或集中控制方式,無法在事故發生時實際跨 instance 執行該 script。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/systems-manager/latest/userguide/run-command-setting-up.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/systems-manager/latest/userguide/documents-running-remote-github-s3.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/systems-manager-automation-runbooks/latest/userguide/aws-quarantineec2instance.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/systems-manager-automation-runbooks/latest/userguide/automation-awssupport-containec2instance.html"]}},{"id":69,"question_en":"A company’s application team wants to replace an internal application with a new AWS architecture that consists of Amazon EC2 instances, an AWS Lambda function, and an Amazon S3 bucket in a single AWS Region. After an architecture review, the security team mandates that no application network traffic can traverse the public internet at any point. The security team already has an SCP in place for the company’s organization in AWS Organizations to restrict the creation of internet gateways, NAT gateways, and egress- only gateways. Which combination of steps should the application team take to meet these requirements? (Select THREE.)","question_zh":"一家公司的应用团队希望用一种新的AWS架构来替换内部应用程序，该架构包括位于同一AWS区 域内的Amazon EC2实例、一个AWS Lambda函数和一个Amazon S3存储桶。在架构审查后，安全 团队要求不得有任何应用网络流量 在任何情况下都不允许访问公共互联网。安全团队已在 AWS Organizations 中为公司组织设置了 SCP，以限制创建互联网网关、 NAT 网关和出站网关。 应用团队应采取哪些步骤组合来满足这些要求？（选择三项。）","options_en":{"A":"Create an S3 endpoint that has a full-access policy for the application’s VPC.","B":"Create an S3 access point for the S3 bucket. Include a policy that restricts the network origin to VPCs.","C":"Launch the Lambda function. Enable the block public access configuration.","D":"Create a security group that has an outbound rule over port 443 with a destination of the S3 endpoint. Associate the security group with the EC2 instances.","E":"Create a security group that has an outbound rule over port 443 with a destination of the S3 access point. Associate the security group with the EC2 instances.","F":"Launch the Lambda function in a VPC."},"options_zh":{"A":"创建一个S3端点，并为应用程序的VPC配置完全访问策略。","B":"为S3存储桶创建一个S3访问点，并包含一项策略，将网络来源限制为VPC。","C":"启动 Lambda 函数。启用阻止公共访问配置。","D":"创建一个安全组，其中包含一条出站规则，允许通过端口443访问S3端点。将该安全组与EC2实例关联。","E":"创建一个安全组，其中包含一条出站规则，允许通过端口443访问S3访问点。将该安全组与EC2实例关联。","F":"在 VPC 中启动 Lambda 函数。"},"answer":["A","B","F"],"multi":true,"vote":{},"tags":["Organizations/Governance","Storage","Compute"],"difficulty":3,"diff_why":"複選・官方文件判定需斟酌・題庫與社群皆錯","research":{"verdict":["A","D","F"],"confidence":"medium","agrees_with":"neither","explanation_en":"The requirement is that literally no packet belonging to this architecture may traverse the public internet, and the org SCP has already foreclosed the 'cheat' routes (no new internet gateway, NAT gateway, or egress-only internet gateway can ever be created). That leaves two things the team must actually build: (1) a private network path from the VPC to Amazon S3, and (2) a way to force the Lambda function onto that private path instead of its internet-reachable default environment -- plus the configuration step that makes the EC2 side of that path actually work as documented. (A) A gateway VPC endpoint for S3 is the private path itself: 'Amazon S3 supports both gateway endpoints and interface endpoints. With a gateway endpoint, you can access Amazon S3 from your VPC, without requiring an internet gateway or NAT device for your VPC' (Gateway endpoints for Amazon S3, vpc-endpoints-s3.html). Creating it with a Full Access policy for the VPC wires the VPC's route tables to Amazon S3 over the AWS network instead of the internet. (F) By default 'Lambda runs your functions in an internal virtual private cloud (VPC) with connectivity to AWS services and the internet' (Lambda 'Troubleshoot networking issues', troubleshooting-networking.html). That AWS-managed environment is exactly the kind of internet-reachable path the security team is trying to eliminate. Attaching the function to the application's own VPC (Giving Lambda functions access to resources in an Amazon VPC, configuration-vpc.html) removes it from that managed environment; the same troubleshooting page then states the fix for VPC-connected functions that must reach AWS services with no internet: 'To connect a function to AWS services from a private subnet with no internet access, use VPC endpoints' -- i.e., once attached to the VPC, the function rides the same gateway endpoint created in (A). (D) The gateway-endpoint page's own 'Considerations' section spells out the companion step for the EC2 side of the path: 'The rules for the security groups for your instances that access Amazon S3 through a gateway endpoint must allow traffic to and from Amazon S3. You can reference the ID of the prefix list for Amazon S3 in security group rules.' That is precisely what D describes: an outbound HTTPS (443) rule, on the security group attached to the EC2 instances, whose destination is the (prefix-list-backed) S3 gateway endpoint. AWS's own SageMaker VPC guidance echoes the identical requirement in different words: 'you must allow outbound communication to your Amazon S3 Amazon VPC endpoints' (neo-vpc.html). Together A + D + F build and lock down one complete, AWS-documented, internet-free path: EC2 gets a route to S3 through the gateway endpoint plus a security group explicitly scoped to reach it, and Lambda is pulled out of its internet-reachable default network and onto that same VPC/route table. Why not B: an access point restricted to a VPC network origin is a real, valid feature -- 'Amazon S3 rejects any request made to the access point that doesn't originate from that VPC' (access-points-vpc.html) -- and AWS even documents pairing it with a gateway endpoint in a storage blog post. But it is an authorization control on the S3 side: it decides whether Amazon S3 will honor a request, not whether the packets that make up that request ever cross the internet. Nothing in the scenario introduces or needs an access point, and substituting it for D leaves out the security-group configuration that AWS's own gateway-endpoint documentation says instances 'must' have. Why not E: it copies D's premise but points it at the wrong object. Unlike a gateway endpoint, an S3 access point has no companion AWS-managed prefix list and no separate network footprint that a security group can reference as a destination -- there is no AWS mechanism for 'a security group rule whose destination is an S3 access point,' so E describes something that cannot be configured. Why not C: 'block public access' is exclusively an Amazon S3 (and, in a newer Lambda feature, a Lambda function-URL/resource-policy) authorization control over who may invoke or reach a resource; it has no bearing on which network path a function's own outbound calls take, and it does not touch the actual problem here, which is Lambda's internet-reachable default managed VPC. Net: the technically correct combination is A, D, F. The dump's suggested A, B, F swaps in a valid-but-tangential S3 authorization feature (B) for the AWS-documented, functionally necessary security-group/prefix-list step (D) that AWS explicitly calls a 'must' when EC2 instances use an S3 gateway endpoint.","explanation_zh":"題目要求這套架構的封包完全不能經過公有網際網路,而組織層級的 SCP 已經封死了『取巧』的路——禁止建立新的 internet gateway、NAT gateway 或 egress-only internet gateway。剩下真正需要動手做的事情有兩件:(1) 打造一條從 VPC 到 Amazon S3 的私有網路路徑;(2) 想辦法把 Lambda 函式硬拉進這條私有路徑,而不是留在它預設、可通網際網路的執行環境裡——再加上讓路徑的 EC2 端真正按官方文件運作起來的設定。(A) S3 gateway VPC endpoint 本身就是這條私有路徑:官方文件『Gateway endpoints for Amazon S3』指出:'Amazon S3 supports both gateway endpoints and interface endpoints. With a gateway endpoint, you can access Amazon S3 from your VPC, without requiring an internet gateway or NAT device for your VPC'。以 Full Access policy 為該 VPC 建立此 endpoint,會讓 VPC 的路由表把前往 S3 的流量導向 AWS 網路,而非網際網路。(F) 預設情況下,'Lambda runs your functions in an internal virtual private cloud (VPC) with connectivity to AWS services and the internet'(Lambda『Troubleshoot networking issues』文件)。這個 AWS 自行管理的環境正是安全團隊想要消除的、可通網際網路的路徑。把函式接上應用程式自己的 VPC(『Giving Lambda functions access to resources in an Amazon VPC』,configuration-vpc.html)就能讓它脫離那個受管理環境;同一份疑難排解文件接著針對『VPC 內函式需要在不使用網際網路的情況下存取 AWS 服務』給出解法:'To connect a function to AWS services from a private subnet with no internet access, use VPC endpoints'——也就是說,一旦函式接上 VPC,它就會與 EC2 共用 (A) 建立的同一個 gateway endpoint。(D) 該 gateway endpoint 官方文件的『Considerations』一節,明確寫出了路徑中 EC2 端所需的配套步驟:'The rules for the security groups for your instances that access Amazon S3 through a gateway endpoint must allow traffic to and from Amazon S3. You can reference the ID of the prefix list for Amazon S3 in security group rules.' 這正是 D 選項所描述的:在 EC2 執行個體所關聯的 security group 上,建立一條目的地指向(以 prefix list 對應的)S3 gateway endpoint 的 outbound HTTPS(443)規則。AWS 自家的 SageMaker VPC 文件也用不同措辭重申了同一項要求:'you must allow outbound communication to your Amazon S3 Amazon VPC endpoints'(neo-vpc.html)。整體而言,A + D + F 三者共同建構並鎖定了一條完整、有 AWS 官方文件依據、完全不經網際網路的路徑:EC2 透過 gateway endpoint 取得通往 S3 的路由,並搭配明確指向該 endpoint 的 security group 規則;Lambda 則被拉出其預設、可通網際網路的網路環境,接上同一個 VPC / 路由表。為何不是 B:將 access point 的 network origin 限制為 VPC 是真實且有效的功能——官方文件(access-points-vpc.html)指出 'Amazon S3 rejects any request made to the access point that doesn't originate from that VPC',AWS 甚至有一篇 storage部落格文章記載了將它與 gateway endpoint 搭配使用的做法。但這終究是 S3 端的授權控制:它決定的是 Amazon S3 是否『受理』某個請求,而不是組成該請求的封包究竟有沒有經過網際網路。本題情境完全沒有提到、也不需要 access point,若用它取代 D,反而會漏掉 AWS 官方 gateway endpoint 文件中明確指出 EC2 執行個體『必須』具備的 security group 設定。為何不是 E:E 抄了 D 的邏輯,卻套用在錯誤的物件上。與 gateway endpoint 不同,S3 access point 並沒有對應的 AWS 受管理 prefix list,也沒有可讓 security group 引用為目的地的獨立網路footprint——AWS 並不存在『security group 規則的目的地是某個 S3 access point』這種機制,所以 E 描述的是一個根本無法設定出來的東西。為何不是 C:'封鎖公開存取(block public access)' 純粹是 Amazon S3(以及較新版本中,Lambda function URL / resource policy)用來控管『誰有權限呼叫或存取某資源』的授權機制,與函式本身對外呼叫走哪一條網路路徑毫無關係,也完全沒有處理本題真正的癥結——Lambda 預設、可通網際網路的受管理 VPC。結論:技術上正確的組合是 A、D、F。題庫給出的建議答案 A、B、F,是用一個真實但與本題目標關係較邊緣的 S3 授權功能(B)取代了 AWS 官方文件明確標示為『必須』的、EC2 使用 S3 gateway endpoint 時所需的 security group / prefix list 設定步驟(D)。","distractors":[{"letter":"B","why_en":"Restricting an S3 access point's network origin to a VPC is a real feature, but it's an authorization control on the S3 side (Amazon S3 rejects requests that don't originate from the VPC) -- it governs whether a request is honored, not whether the underlying traffic crosses the internet. Nothing in the scenario introduces access points, and using B instead of D skips the security-group configuration AWS's own gateway-endpoint documentation says EC2 instances 'must' have.","why_zh":"把 S3 access point 的 network origin 限制為 VPC 是真實存在的功能,但那是 S3 端的授權控管(Amazon S3 會拒絕非來自該 VPC 的請求)——它決定的是請求會不會被受理,而不是底層流量有沒有經過網際網路。情境中完全沒有提到 access point,而且選 B 而非 D,會漏掉 AWS 官方 gateway endpoint 文件中明確指出 EC2 執行個體『必須』具備的 security group 設定。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"'Block public access' is an Amazon S3 (or, in a newer Lambda feature, a Lambda function-URL/resource-policy) authorization setting controlling who may invoke or reach a resource -- it has no effect on which network path a function's own outbound calls take, and does not address the real issue: a non-VPC Lambda function's default environment has internet connectivity.","why_zh":"『封鎖公開存取(block public access)』是 Amazon S3(或較新版本中 Lambda function URL / resource policy)用來控管『誰能呼叫或存取某資源』的授權設定,對函式本身對外呼叫要走哪條網路路徑毫無影響,也沒有解決真正的問題——未接上 VPC 的 Lambda 函式,其預設執行環境本身就具備網際網路連線能力。"},{"letter":"E","why_en":"Unlike a gateway VPC endpoint, an S3 access point has no AWS-managed prefix list and no distinct network object that a security group rule can target as a destination -- 'a security group rule whose destination is an S3 access point' is not a configurable AWS construct.","why_zh":"與 gateway VPC endpoint 不同,S3 access point 沒有對應的 AWS 受管理 prefix list,也沒有獨立的網路物件可供 security group 規則指定為目的地——『目的地為 S3 access point 的 security group 規則』並不是 AWS 上可設定出來的東西。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/vpc/latest/privatelink/vpc-endpoints-s3.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/lambda/latest/dg/troubleshooting-networking.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/lambda/latest/dg/configuration-vpc.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/lambda/latest/dg/configuration-vpc-internet.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonS3/latest/userguide/access-points-vpc.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/sagemaker/latest/dg/neo-vpc.html"]}},{"id":70,"question_en":"A company uses SAML federation with IAM to provide internal users with SSO for their AWS accounts. The company’s identity provider certificate was rotated as part of its normal lifecycle. Shortly after, users started receiving the following error when attempting to log in: “Error: Response Signature Invalid (Service: AWSSecurityTokenService; Status Code: 400; Error Code: InvalidIdentityToken)” A security engineer needs to address the immediate issue and ensure that it will not occur again. Which combination of steps should the security engineer take to accomplish this? (Select TWO.)","question_zh":"一家公司使用 SAML 联邦身份验证与 IAM 配合，为内部用户在其 AWS 账户上提供单点登录（SSO）。该公司在正常生命周期 管理过程中轮换了其身份提供商证书。不久之后，用户在尝试登录时开始收到以下错误： 错误：响应签名无效（服务：AWSSecurityTokenService；状态码：400；错误代码：InvalidIdentityToken） 安全工程师需要解决当前问题，并确保此类问题不再发生。 安全工程师应采取哪些步骤组合来完成此任务？（选择两项。）","options_en":{"A":"Download a new copy of the SAML metadata file from the identity provider. Create a new IAM identity provider entity. Upload the new metadata file to the new IAM identity provider entity.","B":"During the next certificate rotation period and before the current certificate expires, add a new certificate as the secondary certificate to the identity provider. Generate a new metadata file and upload it to the IAM identity provider entity. Perform automated or manual rotation of the certificate when required.","C":"Download a new copy of the SAML metadata file from the identity provider. Upload the new metadata to the IAM identity provider entity configured for the SAML integration in question.","D":"During the next certificate rotation period and before the current certificate expires, add a new certificate as the secondary certificate to the identity provider. Generate a new copy of the metadata file and create a new IAM identity provider entity. Upload the metadata file to the new IAM identity provider entity. Perform automated or manual rotation of the certificate when required.","E":"Download a new copy of the SAML metadata file from the identity provider. Create a new IAM identity provider entity. Upload the new metadata file to the new IAM identity provider entity. Update the identity provider configurations to pass a new IAM identity provider entity name in the SAML assertion."},"options_zh":{"A":"从身份提供商下载新的SAML元数据文件。创建一个新的IAM身份提供商实体，并将新 的元数据文件上传至该IAM身份提供商实体。","B":"在下一个证书轮换周期内，且在当前证书过期前，将新证书作为备用证书添加到身份提供商。 生成新的元数据文件并上传至IAM身份提供商实体。根据需要执行自动或手动的证书轮换。","C":"从身份提供商下载新的SAML元数据文件，并将新元数据上传至为该SAML集成配置的IAM身份 提供商实体。","D":"在下一个证书轮换周期内，且在当前证书过期前，将新证书作为备用证书添加到身份提供商。 生成新的元数据文件副本，并创建一个新的IAM身份提供商实体。将元数据文件上传至新的 IAM身份提供商实体。根据需要执行自动或手动的证书轮换。","E":"从身份提供商下载新的SAML元数据文件。创建一个新的IAM身份提供商实体。将新的元数据 文件上传至该IAM身份提供商实体。更新身份提供商配置，以便在SAML断言中传递新的 IAM身份提供商实体名称。"},"answer":["B","C"],"multi":true,"vote":{},"tags":["Security/IAM"],"difficulty":2,"diff_why":"複選","research":{"verdict":["B","C"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"both","explanation_en":"AWS's own IAM troubleshooting guide has an entry for this exact error string. Under 'Error: Response signature invalid (service: AWSSecurityTokenService; status code: 400; error code: InvalidIdentityToken)' it states: 'This error can occur when federation metadata of the identity provider does not match the metadata of the IAM identity provider. For example, the metadata file for the identity service provider might have changed to update an expired certificate. Download the updated SAML metadata file from your identity service provider. Then update it in the AWS identity provider entity that you define in IAM with the aws iam update-saml-provider cross-platform CLI command or the Update-IAMSAMLProvider PowerShell cmdlet.' That is option C word for word: download fresh metadata and upload it into the SAME existing IAM identity provider entity. Options A, D, and E all instead create a brand-new IAM identity provider entity, which the doc never prescribes for this error and which is actively harmful: a new SAML provider gets a new ARN, and every IAM role trust policy that lists the old provider ARN as Principal would stop trusting the new entity, breaking every federated role in the account until each trust policy is rewritten. E additionally invents a non-existent requirement to change the SAML assertion's issuer/provider-entity name at the IdP, which has no basis in AWS documentation. For preventing recurrence, the same IAM SAML provider page notes that IAM does not track certificate expiration itself and explicitly tells customers to plan ahead: 'we recommend monitoring certificate expiration dates and rotating certificates according to your organization's governance and security policies.' The standard way to do this without an outage window is the pattern described in option B: before the current certificate expires, add the new certificate as a secondary/second signing certificate at the identity provider (a rollover feature supported by ADFS, Okta, Azure AD, PingFederate, etc.), regenerate the IdP's SAML metadata so it now advertises the upcoming certificate, and push that updated metadata into the existing IAM identity provider entity ahead of time -- then actually cut over (retire the old certificate) whenever the rotation is scheduled. Because IAM already trusts the new certificate before the cutover, the InvalidIdentityToken error never recurs. Option D describes this same secondary-certificate rollover correctly but pairs it with creating a new IAM identity provider entity instead of updating the existing one -- the same ARN-breaking flaw as A and E -- so D is a corrupted variant of B and is wrong. The correct pair is B (proactive secondary-certificate rollover into the existing entity, preventing recurrence) and C (re-upload fresh metadata into the existing entity, fixing the immediate outage).","explanation_zh":"AWS 官方 IAM 疑難排解文件中,針對這個確切的錯誤字串有專門條目。在「Error: Response signature invalid (service: AWSSecurityTokenService; status code: 400; error code: InvalidIdentityToken)」下寫道:此錯誤發生於 identity provider 的 federation metadata 與 IAM identity provider 的 metadata 不相符時(例如 IdP 端的 metadata 檔案因憑證到期而更新),解法是「從你的 identity service provider 下載更新後的 SAML metadata 檔案,然後用 aws iam update-saml-provider 這個跨平台 CLI 指令,或 Update-IAMSAMLProvider PowerShell cmdlet,更新到你在 IAM 中定義的那個 AWS identity provider entity」。這正是選項 C 的逐字做法:下載新 metadata 並上傳到同一個既有的 IAM identity provider entity。選項 A、D、E 都改為建立全新的 IAM identity provider entity,這不僅文件從未如此建議,而且實際上有害:新的 SAML provider 會有新的 ARN,任何以舊 provider ARN 作為 Principal 的 IAM role trust policy 都會失去信任關係,導致帳號內所有聯合登入角色全部失效,直到逐一改寫 trust policy 為止。選項 E 更額外虛構了「需要在 IdP 端變更 SAML assertion 的 issuer / provider entity 名稱」這個不存在於 AWS 文件的要求。至於「避免再次發生」,同一份 IAM SAML provider 文件也提到 IAM 本身不會追蹤憑證到期時間,並明確建議客戶提前規劃:「我們建議依照貴組織的治理與安全政策,監控憑證到期日並進行憑證輪替」。要在不中斷服務的情況下做到這件事,標準做法就是選項 B 所描述的模式:在目前憑證到期前,先在 identity provider 端新增一張次要(secondary)簽章憑證(ADFS、Okta、Azure AD、PingFederate 等多數 IdP 都支援這種憑證交接功能),重新產生 IdP 的 SAML metadata(此時已同時涵蓋即將啟用的新憑證),並提前把這份更新後的 metadata 上傳到既有的 IAM identity provider entity - 等實際排定輪替時間到了,再正式切換(淘汰舊憑證)。因為 IAM 早已信任新憑證,切換當下不會再出現 InvalidIdentityToken 錯誤。選項 D 雖然同樣描述了新增次要憑證這個正確做法,卻錯誤地搭配「建立新的 IAM identity provider entity」而非更新既有 entity - 與 A、E 犯了同樣會破壞 ARN 信任關係的錯誤,因此 D 只是 B 的變質版本,是錯的。正確組合是 B(提前把次要憑證輪替進既有 entity,預防再次發生)與 C(重新上傳新 metadata 到既有 entity,修復當下的中斷)。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"Creating a brand-new IAM identity provider entity is not what the AWS troubleshooting doc prescribes for this error (it says to update the existing entity), and it changes the provider's ARN -- every IAM role trust policy that references the original SAML provider ARN as Principal would stop trusting federated logins, breaking access account-wide.","why_zh":"建立全新的 IAM identity provider entity 並非 AWS 疑難排解文件對此錯誤的建議做法(文件明言要更新既有 entity),而且會改變 provider 的 ARN - 任何以原 SAML provider ARN 作為 Principal 的 IAM role trust policy 都會失去信任關係,導致全帳號的聯合登入存取失效。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"Correctly describes the secondary-certificate rollover before rotation, but incorrectly pairs it with creating a new IAM identity provider entity instead of updating the existing one -- the same ARN-breaking flaw as A, making this a corrupted version of the correct answer B.","why_zh":"正確描述了輪替前先新增 secondary certificate 的做法,但錯誤地搭配「建立新的 IAM identity provider entity」而非更新既有的 entity - 與 A 犯了同樣會破壞 provider ARN 信任關係的錯誤,使其成為正確答案 B 的變質版本。"},{"letter":"E","why_en":"Shares A's flaw of creating a new IAM identity provider entity (breaking ARN-based trust policies) and additionally invents a requirement to reconfigure the IdP to send a new provider entity name in the SAML assertion issuer -- a step with no basis in AWS documentation for this error.","why_zh":"與 A 一樣會建立新的 IAM identity provider entity(破壞以 ARN 為基礎的 trust policy),還額外虛構了「須重新設定 IdP,在 SAML assertion 的 issuer 中傳送新 provider entity 名稱」這個步驟,此要求在 AWS 文件中對此錯誤並無任何根據。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/IAM/latest/UserGuide/troubleshoot_saml.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/IAM/latest/UserGuide/id_roles_providers_create_saml.html"]}},{"id":71,"question_en":"A company is running an application on Amazon EC2 instances in an Auto Scaling group. The application stores logs locally. A security engineer noticed that logs were lost after a scale-in event. The security engineer needs to recommend a solution to ensure the durability and availability of log data. All logs must be kept for a minimum of 1 year for auditing purposes. What should the security engineer recommend?","question_zh":"一家公司正在自动扩展组中的 Amazon EC2 实例上运行一个应用程序，该应用将日志存储在本地。安 全工程师发现，在发生缩容事件后，部分日志丢失了。安全工程师需要推荐一种解决方案，以确保日 志数据的持久性和可用性。所有日志必须至少保留一年，用于审计目的。 安全工程师应该推荐什么","options_en":{"A":"Within the Auto Scaling lifecycle, add a hook to create and attach an Amazon Elastic Block Store (Amazon EBS) log volume each time an EC2 instance is created. When the instance is terminated, the EBS volume can be reattached to another instance for log review.","B":"Create an Amazon Elastic File System (Amazon EFS) file system and add a command in the user data section of the Auto Scaling launch template to mount the EFS file system during EC2 instance creation. Configure a process on the instance to copy the logs once a day from an instance Amazon Elastic Block Store (Amazon EBS) volume to a directory in the EFS file system.","C":"Add an Amazon CloudWatch agent into the AMI used in the Auto Scaling group. Configure the CloudWatch agent to send the logs to Amazon CloudWatch Logs for review.","D":"Within the Auto Scaling lifecycle, add a lifecycle hook at the terminating state transition and alert the engineering team by using a lifecycle notification to Amazon Simple Notification Service (Amazon SNS). Configure the hook to remain in the Terminating:Wait state for 1 hour to allow manual review of the security logs prior to instance termination."},"options_zh":{"B":"创建一个 Amazon 弹性文件系统（Amazon EFS），并在自动扩展启动模板的用户数据部分添加命令，以便在创建 EC2 实 例时挂载该 EFS 文件系统。然后在实例上配置一个进程，每天将日志从实例的 Amazon 弹性块存储（Amazon EBS）卷 复制到 EFS 文件系统中的指定目录。","C":"在自动扩展组使用的 AMI 中添加 Amazon CloudWatch 代理，并配置该代理将日志发送到 Amazon CloudWatch Logs 以供查看。","D":"在自动扩展生命周期中，于终止状态转换时添加一个生命周期挂钩，并通过生命周期通知将信息发送至 Amazon Simple Notification Service（Amazon SNS）以通知工程团队。配置该挂钩在“终止：等待”状态保持 1 小时，以便在实例终止 前手动审查安全日志。","A":"在自动扩展生命周期中，添加一个挂钩，以便每次创建 EC2 实例时都创建并挂载一个 Amazon 弹性块存储（Amazon EBS） 日志卷。当实例被终止时，该 EBS 卷可重新挂载到另一台实例上以供日志审查。"},"answer":["C"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Storage","Compute","Serverless/Integration","Monitoring/Ops"],"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選","research":{"verdict":["C"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"The requirement is to make ephemeral Auto Scaling instance logs durable and available, with a minimum 1-year retention for auditing. Installing the unified CloudWatch agent in the AMI streams log files off each instance to Amazon CloudWatch Logs continuously (in near real time), so log data is already off the instance and safely stored before a scale-in event ever terminates it — no manual step is required. CloudWatch Logs stores log data durably and makes it available for query/export, and each log group's retention setting can be changed to 365 days (the console/API offer preset values such as 1, 3, 5, 7, 14, 30, 60, 90, 120, 150, 180, 365, 400, 545, 731, 1096, 1827, 2192, 2557, 2922, 3288, 3653 days, or 'Never Expire'), which directly satisfies the 1-year audit requirement. This is the AWS-recommended, fully managed pattern for centralizing instance logs from Auto Scaling groups. None of the other options actually solve durability/retention: (A) EBS volumes and manual reattachment are operationally fragile and EBS itself replicates only within a single Availability Zone; (B) a once-daily copy to EFS leaves up to 24 hours of logs on the local disk that are lost forever if the instance is terminated in between; (D) a Terminating:Wait lifecycle hook with SNS only buys up to 1 hour of human review time and does not durably store or retain logs anywhere.","explanation_zh":"需求是讓 Auto Scaling 短暫實例（ephemeral instance）上的日誌具備耐久性與可用性，並至少保留 1 年供稽核。在 AMI 中安裝 unified CloudWatch agent，可持續（近乎即時）將日誌檔從實例串流到 Amazon CloudWatch Logs，因此在 scale-in 終止實例之前，日誌早已離開該實例並安全儲存，無需任何人工步驟。CloudWatch Logs 會耐久儲存日誌資料並可供查詢／匯出，且每個 log group 的保留設定可改為 365 天（主控台／API 提供 1、3、5、7、14、30、60、90、120、150、180、365、400、545、731、1096、1827、2192、2557、2922、3288、3653 天或「Never Expire」等預設值），直接滿足 1 年稽核要求。這是 AWS 建議的全受管、用於集中管理 Auto Scaling group 實例日誌的方案。其餘選項都無法真正解決耐久性／保留問題：(A) EBS 磁碟區加人工重新掛載，作業上脆弱且容易出錯，而 EBS 本身也只在單一 Availability Zone 內複寫；(B) 每天才複製一次到 EFS，代表最多 24 小時的日誌仍留在本機磁碟，若實例在複製前被終止就永久遺失；(D) Terminating:Wait lifecycle hook 搭配 SNS 只是爭取最多 1 小時的人工檢視時間，日誌並未被耐久儲存或保留在任何地方。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"EBS volumes are replicated only within a single Availability Zone, so this does not provide the required durability/availability; reattaching volumes after every termination is a manual, error-prone, non-scalable process, and nothing in this design enforces 1-year retention.","why_zh":"EBS 磁碟區僅在單一 Availability Zone 內複寫，無法提供所需的耐久性與可用性；每次終止後重新掛載磁碟區是手動、易錯且無法擴展的流程，此設計也沒有任何機制強制 1 年保留。"},{"letter":"B","why_en":"Copying logs to EFS only once a day leaves up to 24 hours of logs on the local EBS volume that are permanently lost if a scale-in event terminates the instance before the next copy runs, so durability is not ensured.","why_zh":"每天只複製一次日誌到 EFS，代表最多 24 小時的日誌仍留在本機 EBS 磁碟區上，若 scale-in 在下次複製前終止實例，日誌就會永久遺失，無法確保耐久性。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"A Terminating:Wait lifecycle hook with an SNS notification only buys about 1 hour for manual review; it does not durably store logs anywhere, does not scale operationally, and cannot satisfy a 1-year retention requirement.","why_zh":"Terminating:Wait lifecycle hook 加 SNS 通知只是爭取約 1 小時的人工檢視時間；日誌並未被耐久儲存到任何地方，營運上也無法擴展，更不可能滿足 1 年保留要求。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonCloudWatch/latest/logs/Working-with-log-groups-and-streams.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonCloudWatch/latest/monitoring/Install-CloudWatch-Agent.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonCloudWatch/latest/logs/CWL_GettingStarted.html"]}},{"id":72,"question_en":"A company runs an internet-accessible application on several Amazon EC2 instances that run Windows Server. The company used an instance profile to configure the EC2 instances. A security team currently accesses the VPC that hosts the EC2 instances by using an AWS Site-to-Site VPN tunnel from an on-premises office. The security team issues a policy that requires all external access to the VPC to be blocked in the event of a security incident. However, during an incident, the security team must be able to access the EC2 instances to obtain forensic information on the instances. Which solution will meet these requirements?","question_zh":"一家公司在多台运行 Windows Server 的 Amazon EC2 实例上部署了一个可通过互联网访问的应用程序。该公司使用实例配置文 件对这些 EC2 实例进行了设置。目前，安全团队通过本地办公室的 AWS 站点到站点 VPN 隧道访问托管这些 EC2 实例的 VPC。 安全团队发布了一项政策，要求在发生安全事件时，必须阻止所有对 VPC 的外部访问。然而，在发生事件期间，安全团队仍 需能够访问 EC2 实例，以获取实例的取证信息。 哪种解决方案能满足这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Install EC2 Instance Connect on the EC2 instances. Update the IAM policy for the IAM role to grant the required permissions. Use the AWS CLI to open a tunnel to connect to the instances.","B":"Install EC2 Instance Connect on the EC2 instances. Configure the instances to permit access to the ec2- instance-connect command user. Use the AWS Management Console to connect to the EC2 instances.","C":"Create an EC2 Instance Connect endpoint in the VPC. Configure an appropriate security group to allow access between the EC2 instances and the endpoint. Use the AWS CLI to open a tunnel to connect to the instances.","D":"Create an EC2 Instance Connect endpoint in the VPC. Configure an appropriate security group to allow access between the EC2 instances and the endpoint. Use the AWS Management Console to connect to the EC2 instances."},"options_zh":{"A":"在 EC2 实例上安装 EC2 Instance Connect，更新 IAM 角色的 IAM 策略以授予所需的权限，并 使用 AWS CLI 建立隧道连接到实例。","B":"在 EC2 实例上安装 EC2 Instance Connect，并配置实例以允许 ec2-instance-connect 命令用户访问。 使用 AWS 管理控制台连接到 EC2 实例。","C":"在 VPC 中创建一个 EC2 实例连接端点。配置适当的网络安全组，以允许 EC2 实例与该端点之 间的访问。使用 AWS CLI 建立隧道以连接到这些实例。","D":"在 VPC 中创建 EC2 实例连接端点。配置适当的网络安全组，以允许 EC2 实例与该端点之间的 访问。使用 AWS 管理控制台连接到 EC2 实例。"},"answer":["D"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Networking/DNS","Security/IAM","Compute"],"difficulty":2,"diff_why":"題庫與社群皆錯","research":{"verdict":["C"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"neither","explanation_en":"Option C is correct; the dump's marked answer D is wrong. The official EC2 'Connect to your EC2 instance' comparison table (connect.html) shows 'EC2 Instance Connect' (classic, non-endpoint) supports Instance operating system = 'Linux' only, and 'EC2 Instance Connect Endpoint' supports 'Linux, Windows' — so for Windows Server instances, options A and B (classic EC2 Instance Connect, which is SSH/Linux-only) are ruled out immediately, and an EIC Endpoint (C or D) is the right building block. The deciding fact is in connect-using-eice.html: its 'Connection options' list for the EIC Endpoint explicitly separates 'Connect to your Linux instance using the Amazon EC2 console' (browser-based, console 'Connect' > 'EC2 Instance Connect' tab), 'Connect to your Linux instance using SSH', and 'Connect to your Linux instance with its instance ID using the AWS CLI' from a distinct, Windows-only section: 'Connect to your Windows instance using RDP.' That Windows section documents exactly one procedure: run 'aws ec2-instance-connect open-tunnel --instance-id i-1234567890abcdef0 --remote-port 3389 --local-port any-port' to open a private tunnel, then point a separate RDP client (e.g., Microsoft Remote Desktop, editing the downloaded RDP file's PC name to 'localhost:local-port') at the tunnel and log in with the administrator credentials. There is no console-based 'Connect' tab flow documented anywhere for Windows over the EIC Endpoint — the console option in that guide is explicitly scoped to Linux. Therefore, for Windows Server EC2 instances, the only AWS-documented method to reach them through an EIC Endpoint is CLI open-tunnel + a separate RDP client, which is exactly option C. Option D's claim of AWS Management Console RDP connectivity through the endpoint has no support in AWS documentation. The overall design also satisfies the scenario: EIC Endpoint traffic stays inside AWS's private network (from the VPC to the endpoint), so terminating/blocking the Site-to-Site VPN severs the on-premises path while the security team can still reach the endpoint from within AWS (e.g., via AWS CloudShell or another in-AWS network path) during an incident to pull forensic data from the instances.","explanation_zh":"正確答案是 C;dump 標示的答案 D 是錯的。EC2 官方『Connect to your EC2 instance』比較表(connect.html)顯示:『EC2 Instance Connect』(傳統版、非 endpoint)的 Instance operating system 欄位僅為『Linux』,而『EC2 Instance Connect Endpoint』則支援『Linux, Windows』— 因此對 Windows Server 執行個體而言,選項 A、B(傳統版 EC2 Instance Connect,僅限 SSH/Linux)立刻被排除,而使用 EIC Endpoint(選項 C 或 D)才是正確方向。關鍵決定性事實在 connect-using-eice.html:該頁針對 EIC Endpoint 的『Connection options』清單,明確將『Connect to your Linux instance using the Amazon EC2 console』(透過瀏覽器、主控台 Connect > EC2 Instance Connect 分頁)、『Connect to your Linux instance using SSH』、『Connect to your Linux instance with its instance ID using the AWS CLI』,與另一個獨立、僅限 Windows 的章節『Connect to your Windows instance using RDP』分開列示。該 Windows 章節僅記載一種程序:執行 `aws ec2-instance-connect open-tunnel --instance-id i-1234567890abcdef0 --remote-port 3389 --local-port any-port` 開啟私有通道,然後用另外獨立的 RDP 用戶端(例如 Microsoft Remote Desktop,將下載的 RDP 檔案中 PC name 編輯為 `localhost:local-port`)連線至該通道,並用系統管理員帳密登入。整份文件中,並不存在任何透過主控台 Connect 分頁對 Windows 執行個體進行 EIC Endpoint 連線的記載 — 該指南中的主控台選項明確僅適用於 Linux。因此,對於 Windows Server EC2 執行個體而言,AWS 文件記載的唯一透過 EIC Endpoint 連線方式,是 CLI 的 open-tunnel 指令搭配獨立的 RDP 用戶端,這正是選項 C 所描述的做法。選項 D 所稱『透過 AWS Management Console 對 endpoint 進行 RDP 連線』並無任何 AWS 文件支持。整體設計也符合題目情境:EIC Endpoint 的流量完全留在 AWS 私有網路內(從 VPC 到 endpoint),因此終止/封鎖 Site-to-Site VPN 會切斷辦公室端的外部存取路徑,而安全團隊仍可在事件發生時從 AWS 內部(例如透過 AWS CloudShell 或其他 AWS 端網路路徑)連線到該 endpoint,取得執行個體上的鑑識資訊。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"Classic EC2 Instance Connect (non-endpoint) is documented in the connect.html comparison table as supporting Instance operating system = Linux only (SSH-based). It has no Windows/RDP support, so installing it on Windows Server instances and opening a CLI tunnel is not a valid, documented procedure.","why_zh":"傳統版 EC2 Instance Connect(非 endpoint)在 connect.html 比較表中,Instance operating system 欄位僅為 Linux(基於 SSH)。它完全不支援 Windows/RDP,因此在 Windows Server 執行個體上安裝並用 CLI 開通道,並非有效且有文件記載的做法。"},{"letter":"B","why_en":"Same flaw as A: classic EC2 Instance Connect and the ec2-instance-connect command user (AuthorizedKeysCommandUser) are Linux SSH concepts documented only for Linux AMIs. There is no such mechanism, and no AWS Management Console connect option, for Windows Server instances via classic EC2 Instance Connect.","why_zh":"與選項 A 相同的問題:傳統版 EC2 Instance Connect 及 ec2-instance-connect command user(AuthorizedKeysCommandUser)是僅針對 Linux AMI 記載的 SSH 概念。Windows Server 執行個體並不存在此機制,透過傳統版 EC2 Instance Connect 主控台也沒有對應的連線選項。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"EC2 Instance Connect Endpoint does support Windows, but connect-using-eice.html's 'Connection options' list documents RDP-over-endpoint only via 'Connect to your Windows instance using RDP' — the AWS CLI open-tunnel command plus a separate RDP client. The console-based 'Connect' tab flow in that same guide is explicitly scoped to 'Connect to your Linux instance using the Amazon EC2 console' only; there is no documented console RDP path for Windows through the endpoint.","why_zh":"EC2 Instance Connect Endpoint 確實支援 Windows,但 connect-using-eice.html 的『Connection options』清單中,RDP-over-endpoint 僅記載於『Connect to your Windows instance using RDP』一節 — 也就是 AWS CLI 的 open-tunnel 指令搭配獨立的 RDP 用戶端。同一份指南中,主控台 Connect 分頁的連線流程明確僅適用於『Connect to your Linux instance using the Amazon EC2 console』;並沒有任何文件記載可透過主控台對 Windows 執行個體進行 endpoint RDP 連線。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AWSEC2/latest/UserGuide/connect.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AWSEC2/latest/UserGuide/connect-using-eice.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AWSEC2/latest/UserGuide/ec2-instance-connect-methods.html"]}},{"id":73,"question_en":"A company receives an alert from AWS Support. The alert shows a compromised access key on a single standalone AWS account. A security engineer must determine the scope of the issue. Then, the security engineer must triage and remediate the issue. Which solution will meet these requirements?","question_zh":"一家公司收到 AWS 支持发出的警报，显示某个独立的 AWS 账户中的访问密钥已被泄露。安全 工程师需要确定该问题的影响范围，然后对问题进行分类处理并实施修复措施。 哪种解决方案能满足这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Delete the IAM user that has the AWSCompromisedKeyQuarantineV3 policy attached. Review Amazon CloudWatch for suspicious activity.","B":"Review AWS CloudTrail logs. Remove any unauthorized resources. Rotate all IAM access keys for the user that has the AWSCompromisedKeyQuarantineV3 policy attached. Remove the policy from the user.","C":"Remove the AWSCompromisedKeyQuarantineV3 policy from the impacted IAM user. Review AWS CloudTrail logs. Remove any unauthorized resources.","D":"Review Amazon CloudWatch logs for suspicious activity. Remove all unauthorized resources. Rotate the impacted IAM access keys."},"options_zh":{"A":"删除已附加 AWSCompromisedKeyQuarantineV3 策略的 IAM 用户。检查 Amazon CloudWatch 是否存在可疑活动。","B":"检查 AWS CloudTrail 日志，删除任何未授权的资源。轮换所有已附加 AWSCompromisedKeyQuarantineV3 策略的用户 的 IAM 访问密钥，并从该用户移除该策略。","C":"从受影响的 IAM 用户中移除 AWSCompromisedKeyQuarantineV3 策略。检查 AWS CloudTrail 日志，并删除任何未授 权的资源。","D":"检查 Amazon CloudWatch 日志中的可疑活动，删除所有未授权的资源，并轮换受影响的 IAM 访问密钥。"},"answer":["B"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Security/IAM","Monitoring/Ops"],"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選","research":{"verdict":["B"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"both","explanation_en":"When AWS Support (or AWS's automated key-exposure detection) flags a compromised access key, AWS itself typically attaches the AWS managed policy AWSCompromisedKeyQuarantineV3 to the affected IAM identity. Its own documentation states verbatim: 'Do NOT remove this policy. Instead, please follow the instructions specified in the support case created for you regarding this event' (docs.aws.amazon.com/aws-managed-policy/latest/reference/AWSCompromisedKeyQuarantineV3.html). That means the quarantine policy must stay in place until scoping and remediation are done, not be stripped off first. AWS's own guidance for this exact scenario — the re:Post knowledge-center article 'Resolve issues with unauthorized activity in AWS accounts' (repost.aws/knowledge-center/potential-account-compromise), which the Amazon GuardDuty documentation for compromised credentials (docs.aws.amazon.com/guardduty/latest/ug/compromised-creds.html) explicitly points to as the remediation reference — instructs you to open the AWS CloudTrail console and review Event History for unsanctioned activity (new access keys, policies, roles, or temporary credentials), delete/remediate anything unauthorized, and only then finish securing the account. AWS's own sample incident playbook (github.com/aws-samples/aws-customer-playbook-framework, Compromised_IAM_Credentials.md) likewise sequences Analysis-via-CloudTrail, then Containment (rotate/disable keys), then Eradication (remove unauthorized resources), before the account is declared clean. CloudTrail — not CloudWatch — is the AWS-documented tool for scoping this kind of API/IAM-level compromise (CloudWatch is a metrics/log-monitoring service and is never the tool AWS references for this workflow); this eliminates A and D. Deleting the IAM user (A) destroys the evidence needed to scope the incident and is not a step in any AWS-documented runbook. Removing the AWSCompromisedKeyQuarantineV3 policy before completing CloudTrail review and remediation (C) directly contradicts the policy's own explicit instruction. Option B is the only option that (1) uses CloudTrail correctly for scoping, (2) remediates unauthorized resources and rotates the compromised keys before the account is considered clean, and (3) removes the quarantine policy only as the final step — matching AWS's documented process and its policy note not to remove it prematurely.","explanation_zh":"當 AWS Support(或 AWS 自動化的金鑰外洩偵測)標記出一個遭入侵的 access key 時,AWS 通常會自行將 AWS managed policy AWSCompromisedKeyQuarantineV3 附加到受影響的 IAM 身分上。其官方文件明確寫道:「請勿移除此政策。請改為遵循為此事件建立的支援案例中所指定的說明」(docs.aws.amazon.com/aws-managed-policy/latest/reference/AWSCompromisedKeyQuarantineV3.html)。這代表隔離政策必須保留到界定範圍與修復完成為止,而不是最先被移除。AWS 針對這種情境的官方指引——re:Post 知識中心文章《Resolve issues with unauthorized activity in AWS accounts》(repost.aws/knowledge-center/potential-account-compromise),此文章也被 Amazon GuardDuty 針對遭入侵憑證的官方文件(docs.aws.amazon.com/guardduty/latest/ug/compromised-creds.html)明確引用為修復參考——指示使用者開啟 AWS CloudTrail 主控台並檢閱事件歷史記錄,找出未經授權的活動(新建的 access key、政策、角色或暫時憑證),刪除/修復任何未經授權的項目,然後才完成帳戶的安全強化。AWS 官方的事件回應範例手冊(github.com/aws-samples/aws-customer-playbook-framework 的 Compromised_IAM_Credentials.md)同樣將流程排序為:先透過 CloudTrail 進行分析,再進行圍堵(輪替/停用金鑰),最後才是清除(移除未經授權的資源),之後才宣告帳戶已清理乾淨。界定此類 API/IAM 層級入侵範圍所使用的官方工具是 CloudTrail,而非 CloudWatch(CloudWatch 是指標/日誌監控服務,AWS 從未在此流程中將其列為參考工具)——這排除了選項 A 與 D。刪除 IAM 使用者(選項 A)會破壞界定事件範圍所需的證據,且不屬於任何 AWS 官方記載的處理步驟。在完成 CloudTrail 檢閱與修復之前就移除 AWSCompromisedKeyQuarantineV3 政策(選項 C),直接違反該政策本身「請勿移除」的明確說明。選項 B 是唯一(1)正確使用 CloudTrail 進行範圍界定、(2)在帳戶被視為乾淨之前先修復未經授權的資源並輪替遭入侵的金鑰、且(3)僅在最後一步才移除隔離政策的選項——完全符合 AWS 官方流程,以及該政策「請勿提前移除」的說明。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"Deleting the IAM user destroys the evidence (access history, attached policies, activity trail) needed to scope the compromise, and is not a step in any AWS-documented remediation runbook; it also relies on CloudWatch rather than CloudTrail for reviewing suspicious activity, which is not the AWS-documented mechanism for this kind of API/IAM-level investigation.","why_zh":"刪除 IAM 使用者會破壞界定入侵範圍所需的證據(存取歷史、已附加的政策、活動軌跡),且不屬於任何 AWS 官方記載的修復步驟;此外它依賴 CloudWatch 而非 CloudTrail 來檢閱可疑活動,而 CloudWatch 並非 AWS 文件中用於此類 API/IAM 層級調查的機制。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"Removing the AWSCompromisedKeyQuarantineV3 policy as the first action directly contradicts the policy's own documented guidance ('Do NOT remove this policy... follow the instructions in the support case'), and doing so before reviewing CloudTrail or remediating unauthorized resources could let the compromised credentials or residual unauthorized resources cause further damage.","why_zh":"把移除 AWSCompromisedKeyQuarantineV3 政策當作第一步,直接違反該政策官方說明(「請勿移除此政策……請遵循支援案例中的說明」);在檢閱 CloudTrail 或修復未經授權資源之前就移除政策,可能讓遭入侵的憑證或殘留的未經授權資源造成進一步損害。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"This option uses CloudWatch logs rather than CloudTrail (not the AWS-documented tool for scoping compromised-key/API-level activity) and never removes the AWSCompromisedKeyQuarantineV3 policy, which would leave the account permanently restricted from the actions the policy denies even after the incident is fully resolved.","why_zh":"此選項使用 CloudWatch 日誌而非 CloudTrail(CloudTrail 才是 AWS 文件中用於界定遭入侵金鑰/API 層級活動範圍的工具),且從未移除 AWSCompromisedKeyQuarantineV3 政策,即使事件已完全解決,帳戶仍會永久受限於該政策所拒絕的動作。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/aws-managed-policy/latest/reference/AWSCompromisedKeyQuarantineV3.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/guardduty/latest/ug/compromised-creds.html","https://repost.aws/knowledge-center/potential-account-compromise","https://repost.aws/knowledge-center/troubleshoot-iam-account-activity","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/awscloudtrail/latest/userguide/view-cloudtrail-events.html","https://github.com/aws-samples/aws-customer-playbook-framework/blob/main/docs/Compromised_IAM_Credentials.md"]}},{"id":74,"question_en":"A company is using AWS CloudTrail and Amazon CloudWatch to monitor resources in an AWS account. The company’s developers have been using an IAM role in the account for the last 3 months. A security engineer needs to refine the customer managed IAM policy attached to the role to ensure that the role provides least privilege access. Which solution will meet this requirement with the LEAST effort?","question_zh":"一家公司正在使用 AWS CloudTrail 和 Amazon CloudWatch 来监控其 AWS 账户中的资源。该公司的开发人员在过去 3 个 月中一直使用账户内的一个 IAM 角色。 安全工程师需要优化附加到该角色的客户管理的IAM策略，以确保该角色提供最小权限访问。 哪种解决方案能以最少的努力满足这一要求？","options_en":{"A":"Implement AWS IAM Access Analyzer policy generation on the role.","B":"Implement AWS IAM Access Analyzer policy validation on the role.","C":"Search CloudWatch logs to determine the actions the role invoked and to evaluate the permissions.","D":"Use AWS Trusted Advisor to compare the policies assigned to the role against AWS best practices."},"options_zh":{"A":"在角色上实施 AWS IAM 访问分析器策略生成。","B":"在角色上实施 AWS IAM 访问分析器策略验证。","C":"搜索 CloudWatch 日志，以确定该角色调用了哪些操作并评估其权限。","D":"使用 AWS Trusted Advisor 将分配给角色的策略与 AWS 最佳实践进行比较。"},"answer":["A"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Security/IAM","Monitoring/Ops"],"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選","research":{"verdict":["A"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"both","explanation_en":"AWS IAM documentation directly describes this exact scenario. The 'IAM Access Analyzer policy generation' feature analyzes an IAM entity's (user or role) AWS CloudTrail events over a specified time period of up to 90 days and generates a policy template containing only the permissions actually used. Critically, the docs state: 'You can refine an entity's permissions when you replace a broad permissions policy attached to the entity with the generated policy' - this is precisely the task described (refine the customer managed policy attached to the role). Since the role has been in use for 3 months (roughly 90+ days), there is more than enough CloudTrail history within the supported lookback window to generate an accurate usage-based policy with minimal manual effort - you specify the time range, let Access Analyzer scan CloudTrail, then review/attach the generated policy. This is far less effort than any manual alternative. Option B, IAM Access Analyzer policy validation, is a different feature entirely: it checks a policy document against IAM JSON grammar rules and AWS security best practices (unused actions, overly permissive wildcards, syntax errors) - it does not look at actual usage activity from CloudTrail, so it cannot tell you which specific permissions the role has actually exercised and cannot produce a refined least-privilege policy on its own. Option C (manually searching CloudWatch/CloudTrail logs to reconstruct which actions were invoked) could theoretically get you similar information, but it requires significant manual log analysis and correlation work that Access Analyzer automates - so it fails the 'least effort' bar. Option D, AWS Trusted Advisor, checks account-level configuration against general best practices (e.g., root account MFA, S3 bucket permissions, service limits) - it does not perform a permissions-usage analysis of a specific IAM role's custom managed policy, so it cannot produce a refined least-privilege policy for this role at all. Only option A directly and automatically produces a least-privilege policy grounded in actual CloudTrail usage data, with the least operational effort.","explanation_zh":"AWS IAM 文件直接描述了這個情境。'IAM Access Analyzer policy generation' 功能會分析某個 IAM entity(user 或 role)在指定時間範圍內(最多 90 天)的 AWS CloudTrail 事件,產生一份只包含實際使用過的權限的 policy template。文件中明確指出:「You can refine an entity's permissions when you replace a broad permissions policy attached to the entity with the generated policy」(你可以透過用產生出來的 policy 取代原本附加在該 entity 上的寬鬆權限 policy,來精簡該 entity 的權限)- 這正是題目所描述的任務(精簡附加在該 role 上的 customer managed policy)。由於該 role 已使用 3 個月(大約超過 90 天),在此功能支援的回溯期間內已有足夠的 CloudTrail 歷史紀錄,可以產生準確的、以實際使用情況為基礎的 policy,且所需人力極少 - 只要指定時間範圍,讓 Access Analyzer 掃描 CloudTrail,再檢視並附加產生出的 policy 即可。這比任何手動方式都省力得多。選項 B,IAM Access Analyzer policy validation,是完全不同的功能:它是針對 policy 文件本身檢查 IAM JSON 語法規則與 AWS 安全最佳實務(例如未使用的動作、過於寬鬆的萬用字元、語法錯誤),並不會查看 CloudTrail 中實際的使用活動,因此無法告訴你該 role 實際用過哪些權限,也無法單靠它產生出精簡的最小權限 policy。選項 C(手動搜尋 CloudWatch/CloudTrail 日誌以重建曾被呼叫的動作)理論上可以取得類似資訊,但需要大量人工日誌分析與比對工作,而這正是 Access Analyzer 自動化處理的部分,因此不符合「最少工作量」的要求。選項 D,AWS Trusted Advisor,檢查的是帳戶層級的整體設定是否符合一般最佳實務(例如 root 帳戶 MFA、S3 儲存桶權限、服務限制等),並不會針對某個 IAM role 的 custom managed policy 進行權限使用分析,因此根本無法為這個 role 產生精簡後的最小權限 policy。只有選項 A 能直接且自動地根據實際 CloudTrail 使用資料產生最小權限 policy,且所需工作量最少。","distractors":[{"letter":"B","why_en":"Policy validation checks a policy document's syntax against IAM JSON grammar and flags AWS security best-practice issues (e.g., overly permissive statements), but it does not analyze CloudTrail usage activity, so it cannot identify which permissions the role actually used and cannot generate a usage-based least-privilege policy.","why_zh":"Policy validation 只是檢查 policy 文件的語法是否符合 IAM JSON 語法規則,並標記出違反 AWS 安全最佳實務的問題(例如過於寬鬆的陳述),但它不會分析 CloudTrail 的使用活動,因此無法得知該 role 實際用過哪些權限,也無法產生以使用情況為基礎的最小權限 policy。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"Manually searching CloudWatch logs to reconstruct the actions a role invoked can work, but it requires substantial manual analysis and correlation effort that Access Analyzer automates entirely, so it does not meet the 'least effort' requirement.","why_zh":"手動搜尋 CloudWatch 日誌以重建 role 曾呼叫過的動作雖然可行,但需要大量人工分析與比對工作,而這些工作 Access Analyzer 可以完全自動化完成,因此不符合「最少工作量」的要求。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"Trusted Advisor evaluates account-wide configuration against general AWS best practices (e.g., MFA on root, service limits, S3 permissions), but it does not analyze a specific role's custom managed policy against its actual usage activity, so it cannot produce a refined least-privilege policy for the role.","why_zh":"Trusted Advisor 是評估整個帳戶的設定是否符合一般 AWS 最佳實務(例如 root 帳戶 MFA、服務限制、S3 權限等),並不會針對特定 role 的 custom managed policy 與其實際使用情況進行分析,因此無法為該 role 產生精簡後的最小權限 policy。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/IAM/latest/UserGuide/access-analyzer-policy-generation.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/IAM/latest/UserGuide/id_roles_manage.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/IAM/latest/UserGuide/getting-started_reduce-permissions-edit-policy.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/IAM/latest/UserGuide/access-analyzer-checks-validating-policies.html"]}},{"id":75,"question_en":"A security engineer needs to implement a logging solution that captures detailed information about objects in an Amazon S3 bucket. The solution must include details such as the IAM identity that makes the request and the time the object was accessed. The data must be structured and available in near real time. Which solution meets these requirements?","question_zh":"安全工程师需要实现一个日志解决方案，以捕获 Amazon S3 存储桶中对象的详细信息。该方案必须包含发出请求的 IAM 身份以 及对象被访问的时间等细节。数据必须结构化，并近乎实时地可用。 哪种解决方案符合这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Enable Amazon S3 server access logging on the S3 bucket. Create a new S3 bucket to store the logs. Analyze the logs from the logging S3 bucket.","B":"Enable AWS CloudTrail data event logging. Create a new S3 bucket to store the logs. Analyze the logs from the logging S3 bucket.","C":"Configure AWS Config rules to log access to the objects stored in the S3 bucket.","D":"Enable Amazon Macie to log access to the objects stored in the S3 bucket."},"options_zh":{"A":"在S3存储桶上启用Amazon S3服务器访问日志。创建一个新的S3存储桶用于存储日志。分析来自日志存储桶的日志。","B":"启用 AWS CloudTrail 的数据事件日志记录。创建一个新的 S3 存储桶以存储日志，并从该日志 S3 存储桶中分析日志。","C":"配置 AWS Config 规则，以记录对存储在 S3 存储桶中的对象的访问。","D":"启用 Amazon Macie 记录对存储在 S3 存储桶中的对象的访问。"},"answer":["B"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Organizations/Governance","Security/IAM","Storage","Monitoring/Ops"],"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選","research":{"verdict":["B"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"both","explanation_en":"AWS's own comparison table in the 'Logging options for Amazon S3' guide settles this directly (verified via docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonS3/latest/userguide/logging-with-S3.html). The table states 'Speed of log delivery' for CloudTrail data events is 'every 5 minutes' versus S3 server access logs 'within a few hours', and 'Log format' for CloudTrail is 'JSON' versus S3 server logs as a 'space-separated, newline-delimited' flat text file. The question requires structured, near-real-time data that includes the IAM identity making the request and the access time - that is exactly what a CloudTrail data event record for S3 contains (the userIdentity element with the principal/ARN, and the eventTime field), delivered in JSON roughly every 5 minutes. Enabling CloudTrail data event logging for the S3 bucket (option B) and sending those events to an S3 bucket for analysis meets all three requirements: object-level detail, structured format, and near-real-time delivery. Option A (S3 server access logging) fails the 'near real time' and 'structured' requirements - AWS explicitly documents delivery as best-effort, 'within a few hours', in a flat space-separated log format rather than JSON. Option C (AWS Config rules) evaluates resource configuration compliance over time and has no mechanism to capture per-object data-access events like GetObject/PutObject. Option D (Amazon Macie) is a sensitive-data discovery/classification service; it does not log object access events. Therefore B is the only option that satisfies all stated requirements, confirming the first analyst's answer.","explanation_zh":"AWS 官方文件 'Logging options for Amazon S3' 中的比較表直接解答了這題(已透過 docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonS3/latest/userguide/logging-with-S3.html 核實)。表格明確指出:CloudTrail data events 的「Speed of log delivery」為 every 5 minutes,而 Amazon S3 server access logs 則是 within a few hours;「Log format」欄位中 CloudTrail 為 JSON,S3 server logs 則是 space-separated, newline-delimited 的純文字紀錄。題目要求的是結構化、近乎即時的資料,且要包含發出請求的 IAM identity 以及存取時間 - 這正是 CloudTrail 針對 S3 的 data event 紀錄所包含的內容(userIdentity 欄位含 principal/ARN,以及 eventTime 欄位),且大約每 5 分鐘以 JSON 格式傳送。針對該 S3 bucket 啟用 CloudTrail data event logging(選項 B),並將事件送到 S3 bucket 進行分析,同時滿足了物件層級細節、結構化格式、以及近乎即時傳送這三項需求。選項 A(S3 server access logging)無法滿足「近乎即時」與「結構化」的要求 - AWS 文件明確記載它是 best-effort,傳送時間為「幾個小時內」,且格式是以空格分隔的純文字檔而非 JSON。選項 C(AWS Config rules)是用來隨時間評估資源設定是否合規,沒有機制去記錄像 GetObject/PutObject 這類物件層級的存取事件。選項 D(Amazon Macie)是資料分類與敏感資料探索服務,不會記錄物件存取事件。因此 B 是唯一能滿足所有需求的選項,確認第一位分析師的答案正確。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"S3 server access logging is explicitly documented as best-effort with delivery 'within a few hours' (not near real time), and its log records are flat space-separated, newline-delimited text files rather than structured JSON, failing both the timing and structure requirements.","why_zh":"S3 server access logging 文件明確說明它是 best-effort 傳送,通常在「幾個小時內」送達(非近乎即時),且其紀錄是以空格分隔、換行分隔的純文字檔案而非結構化 JSON,同時未滿足時效性與結構化兩項要求。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"AWS Config evaluates and tracks resource configuration state and compliance over time; it has no mechanism to log individual object-level data access requests (like GetObject) or capture the requester identity and access time for each object access.","why_zh":"AWS Config 是用來評估與追蹤資源設定狀態與合規性隨時間的變化,它沒有機制去記錄個別物件層級的資料存取請求(如 GetObject),也無法針對每次物件存取捕捉請求者身份與存取時間。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"Amazon Macie is a sensitive data discovery and classification service for data stored in S3; it does not provide access logging for individual object requests, IAM identity of the requester, or access timestamps.","why_zh":"Amazon Macie 是用於探索與分類 S3 中敏感資料的服務,它並不提供針對個別物件請求的存取紀錄,也不會記錄請求者的 IAM identity 或存取時間。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonS3/latest/userguide/logging-with-S3.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonS3/latest/userguide/ServerLogs.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/awscloudtrail/latest/userguide/how-cloudtrail-works.html"]}},{"id":76,"question_en":"A company is running a containerized application on an Amazon Elastic Container Service (Amazon ECS) cluster that uses AWS Fargate. The application runs as several ECS services. The ECS services are in individual target groups for an internet-facing Application Load Balancer (ALB). The ALB is the origin for an Amazon CloudFront distribution. An AWS WAF web ACL is associated with the CloudFront distribution. Web clients access the ECS services through the CloudFront distribution. The company learns that the web clients can bypass the web ACL and can access the ALB directly. Which solution will prevent the web clients from directly accessing the ALB?","question_zh":"一家公司正在使用 AWS Fargate 的 Amazon 弹性容器服务（Amazon ECS）集群上运行一个容器化应用程序。该应用程序 以多个 ECS 服务的形式运行，每个 ECS 服务都位于面向互联网的应用负载均衡器（ALB）的独立目标组中。该 ALB 是 Amazon CloudFront 分发的源站，且已为 CloudFront 分发关联了 AWS WAF 网络 ACL。 Web客户端通过CloudFront分发访问ECS服务。公司发现，这些Web客户端可以绕过Web ACL，直接访问ALB。 哪种解决方案可以防止网络客户端直接访问ALB？","options_en":{"A":"Create an AWS PrivateLink endpoint. Specify the existing ALB as the target. Update the CloudFront distribution by setting the PrivateLink endpoint as the origin.","B":"Create a new internal ALB. Move all the ECS services to the internal ALB. Delete the internet-facing ALB. Update the CloudFront distribution by setting the internal ALB as the origin.","C":"Modify the listener rules for the existing ALB. Add a condition to forward only the requests that come from IP addresses in the CloudFront origin prefix list.","D":"Update the CloudFront distribution by adding an X-Shared-Secret custom header for the origin. Modify the listener rules for the existing ALB to forward only the requests in which the X-Shared-Secret header has the correct value."},"options_zh":{"A":"创建一个 AWS PrivateLink 终端节点，将现有的 ALB 指定为目标。然后通过将 PrivateLink 终端节点设置为源站， 来更新 CloudFront 分发配置。","B":"创建一个新的内部ALB，将所有ECS服务迁移到该内部ALB，删除面向互联网的ALB，并通过将内部ALB设置为源 站来更新CloudFront分发配置。","C":"修改现有ALB的监听规则，添加条件，仅转发来自CloudFront源前缀列表中IP地址的请求。","D":"通过为源添加 X-Shared-Secret 自定义标头来更新 CloudFront 分发。修改现有 ALB 的监听规则，仅转发 X-Shared- Secret 标头具有正确值的请求。"},"answer":["D"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Networking/DNS","Security/IAM","Compute","Containers"],"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選","research":{"verdict":["D"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"CONFIRMED. AWS's own CloudFront documentation page 'Restrict access to Application Load Balancers' (restrict-access-to-load-balancer.html) describes this exact scenario -- internet-facing ALB origin behind CloudFront, clients bypassing CloudFront by hitting the ALB directly -- and prescribes a specific primary solution: (1) configure CloudFront to add a secret custom HTTP header (e.g., X-Shared-Secret) to every origin request, and (2) add an ALB listener rule that forwards only requests containing the correct header value, changing the default rule to return a fixed 403 response for everything else. The doc states verbatim: 'After you complete these steps, users can only access your Application Load Balancer through CloudFront.' Option D implements exactly this mechanism. I independently fetched and read the full page, including the 'Configure an Application Load Balancer to only forward requests that contain a specific header' section, which confirms the two-rule listener design (forward-if-header-matches + default 403). Option C is verifiably wrong on two counts: first, the same CloudFront doc has a distinct section, '(Optional) Limit access to origin by using the AWS-managed prefix list for CloudFront,' which explicitly says this technique works by configuring 'the security group associated with the Application Load Balancer' to accept traffic only from the CloudFront-managed prefix list at the network/transport layer -- it is an optional supplementary control applied to a security group, not to listener rules. Second, I confirmed via the ELB documentation (rule-condition-types.html / listener-rules.html) that the ALB listener 'source-ip' condition type is defined as routing 'based on the source IP address specified in CIDR format' -- it has no mechanism to reference a managed prefix list object by ID; you would have to hardcode the prefix list's current CIDR ranges, which AWS rotates and expands over time, making option C's literal claim (a listener rule condition referencing the CloudFront origin prefix list) both unsupported as described and operationally fragile even if manually approximated. Option A is invalid because AWS PrivateLink (VPC endpoint services) are fronted only by Network Load Balancers or Gateway Load Balancers, never directly by an Application Load Balancer, so an ALB cannot be the target of a PrivateLink endpoint. Option B is invalid as literally worded: CloudFront's standard custom-origin model requires a publicly reachable origin, and while AWS now offers 'VPC origins' (documented on the very same restrict-access-to-load-balancer.html page as an alternative path for internal ALBs) to let CloudFront reach a private/internal ALB, option B never configures VPC origins -- it just says to swap in a plain internal ALB as the origin, which would break connectivity entirely. Therefore exactly one option, D, matches AWS's documented and recommended approach, and the original verdict is confirmed.","explanation_zh":"確認原答案。AWS 官方 CloudFront 文件《Restrict access to Application Load Balancers》(restrict-access-to-load-balancer.html) 正是針對這個確切場景撰寫的——internet-facing ALB 作為 origin、位於 CloudFront 之後,但使用者能繞過 CloudFront 直接存取 ALB——文件給出的主要解法是:(1) 設定 CloudFront 在傳送給 origin 的請求中加入一個保密的自訂 HTTP header(例如 X-Shared-Secret),(2) 在 ALB 的 listener 新增規則,只轉發帶有正確 header 值的請求,並將預設規則改成對其餘所有請求回覆固定的 403。文件原文明確指出:「完成這些步驟後,使用者只能透過 CloudFront 存取你的 Application Load Balancer。」選項 D 正是這個實作方式。我已重新完整讀取該頁面,包括「Configure an Application Load Balancer to only forward requests that contain a specific header」段落,確認了「header 相符則轉發、否則預設回 403」的雙規則設計。選項 C 有兩個可驗證的錯誤:第一,同一份 CloudFront 文件另有獨立段落「(Optional) Limit access to origin by using the AWS-managed prefix list for CloudFront」,明確說明此技巧是透過設定「與 Application Load Balancer 關聯的 security group」,使其僅在網路/傳輸層接受來自 CloudFront managed prefix list 的流量——這是套用在 security group 上的「可選」補強措施,並非套用在 listener 規則上。第二,我透過 ELB 文件(rule-condition-types.html / listener-rules.html)確認 ALB listener 的 source-ip 條件類型的定義是「根據以 CIDR 格式指定的來源 IP 位址進行路由」,並沒有可以直接以 ID 參照 managed prefix list 物件的機制;你只能把 prefix list 當下的 CIDR 範圍手動寫死進去,而這些範圍會被 AWS 不時輪替、擴增,使得選項 C 字面所述的做法(listener 規則條件直接引用 CloudFront origin prefix list)既不受支援,即便勉強手動模擬也十分脆弱。選項 A 不成立,因為 AWS PrivateLink(VPC endpoint service)的後端只能是 Network Load Balancer 或 Gateway Load Balancer,絕不能直接以 Application Load Balancer 作為目標,因此 ALB 無法作為 PrivateLink endpoint 的 target。選項 B 依照字面描述也不成立:CloudFront 標準的自訂 origin 模式需要 origin 具備公開可達性;雖然 AWS 現在提供「VPC origins」功能(同樣記載於 restrict-access-to-load-balancer.html 頁面,作為讓 CloudFront 存取內部 ALB 的替代路徑),但選項 B 完全沒有提到要設定 VPC origins,只是單純把 origin 換成一般的內部 ALB,這樣做會直接導致連線中斷。因此只有選項 D 符合 AWS 官方文件所記載、建議的做法,原答案確認無誤。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"AWS PrivateLink (VPC endpoint services) are fronted only by Network Load Balancers or Gateway Load Balancers -- never directly by an Application Load Balancer. You cannot designate an existing ALB as the target of a PrivateLink endpoint, so this option describes an unsupported configuration.","why_zh":"AWS PrivateLink(VPC endpoint service)的後端只能是 Network Load Balancer 或 Gateway Load Balancer,絕不能直接以 Application Load Balancer 作為目標。你無法把既有的 ALB 指定為 PrivateLink endpoint 的 target,因此此選項描述的是不受支援的架構。"},{"letter":"B","why_en":"Swapping the CloudFront origin to a plain new internal ALB breaks connectivity, because CloudFront's standard custom-origin model requires a publicly reachable origin. Making an internal ALB usable as a CloudFront origin requires the separate 'VPC origins' feature, which this option never configures -- it just deletes the internet-facing ALB and points at an internal one.","why_zh":"把 CloudFront 的 origin 換成一般的新內部 ALB 會導致連線中斷,因為 CloudFront 標準的自訂 origin 模式需要 origin 具備公開可達性。要讓內部 ALB 能作為 CloudFront origin,必須額外設定獨立的「VPC origins」功能,而此選項完全沒有提到要做這項設定,只是刪除 internet-facing ALB 並指向內部 ALB。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"ALB listener 'source-ip' conditions only accept explicit, manually entered CIDR blocks -- there is no listener-rule mechanism to reference an AWS-managed prefix list object directly. AWS's own doc places the managed-prefix-list technique at the security-group layer as an optional supplement, not as a listener-rule condition, and the prefix list's IP ranges change over time, making a hardcoded listener-rule approach unreliable.","why_zh":"ALB listener 的 source-ip 條件只能填寫明確、手動輸入的 CIDR 區塊,並沒有機制可以在 listener 規則中直接引用 AWS-managed prefix list 物件。AWS 官方文件是把 managed prefix list 技巧放在 security group 層級,作為可選的補強措施,而非 listener 規則條件;且該 prefix list 的 IP 範圍會隨時間變動,若寫死在 listener 規則中將難以維持有效性。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonCloudFront/latest/DeveloperGuide/restrict-access-to-load-balancer.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/elasticloadbalancing/latest/application/rule-condition-types.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/elasticloadbalancing/latest/application/listener-rules.html"]}},{"id":77,"question_en":"A security engineer configured VPC Flow Logs to publish to Amazon CloudWatch Logs. After 10 minutes, no logs appear. The issue is isolated to the IAM role associated with VPC Flow Logs. What could be the reason?","question_zh":"安全工程师已将VPC流量日志配置为发布到Amazon CloudWatch Logs。10分钟后，仍未出现任何日志。问题仅限于与VPC流量 日志关联的IAM角色。 可能是什么原因呢？","options_en":{"A":"logs:GetLogEvents is missing.","B":"The engineer cannot assume the role.","C":"The vpc-flow-logs.amazonaws.com principal cannot assume the role.","D":"The role cannot tag the log stream."},"options_zh":{"A":"logs:GetLogEvents 缺失。","B":"工程师无法担任该角色。","C":"vpc-flow-logs.amazonaws.com 主体无法担任该角色。","D":"该角色无法标记日志流。"},"answer":["C"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Security/IAM","Monitoring/Ops"],"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選","research":{"verdict":["C"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"both","explanation_en":"AWS's official documentation, 'IAM role for publishing flow logs to CloudWatch Logs' (flow-logs-iam-role.html), states that the IAM role associated with a flow log needs two separate, independent things to work: (1) a permissions policy granting logs:CreateLogGroup, logs:CreateLogStream, logs:PutLogEvents, logs:DescribeLogGroups, and logs:DescribeLogStreams, and (2) a trust policy whose Principal is the service vpc-flow-logs.amazonaws.com, allowing that service to call sts:AssumeRole on the role. If the trust policy is missing, malformed, or scopes the wrong principal, the VPC Flow Logs service itself can never assume the role, so it can never call PutLogEvents on your behalf: log delivery never starts, and after any amount of time -- including the 10 minutes described in the question -- zero entries show up in CloudWatch Logs. That is exactly the symptom in the question, and it is a fault localized entirely to the IAM role (its trust policy), matching the question's framing that the issue is isolated to the role. This makes option C correct. Option A (logs:GetLogEvents) is a read-side CloudWatch Logs API used to retrieve existing log data for viewing/querying; it is not part of the documented publishing permissions policy and would not stop the service from writing logs even if absent. Option B is a distractor: the security engineer's personal ability to assume the role has no bearing on flow log delivery, because it is vpc-flow-logs.amazonaws.com -- not the human engineer -- that must assume the role. Option D (tagging the log stream) has no basis in the documented IAM policy at all; none of the five required actions relate to tagging, and AWS does not require the flow-log role to tag log streams. Since the only documented, role-specific failure mode that completely blocks delivery is a broken trust relationship with the vpc-flow-logs.amazonaws.com principal, C is the single correct answer.","explanation_zh":"AWS 官方文件「IAM role for publishing flow logs to CloudWatch Logs」(flow-logs-iam-role.html) 明確指出,與 flow log 關聯的 IAM role 需要兩項各自獨立的條件才能運作:(1) 權限政策(permissions policy),需授予 logs:CreateLogGroup、logs:CreateLogStream、logs:PutLogEvents、logs:DescribeLogGroups、logs:DescribeLogStreams 這五個動作;(2) 信任政策(trust policy),其 Principal 必須是 vpc-flow-logs.amazonaws.com 這個服務,允許該服務對此 role 執行 sts:AssumeRole。若信任政策缺失、設定錯誤,或指定了錯誤的 principal,VPC Flow Logs 服務本身就永遠無法 assume 該 role,因此也永遠無法代表你呼叫 PutLogEvents:日誌傳送根本不會啟動,無論經過多久(包括題目所述的 10 分鐘),CloudWatch Logs 中都不會出現任何日誌條目。這正是題目描述的現象,而且故障完全侷限在 IAM role 本身(其信任政策),與題目「問題已被隔離定位在該 IAM role」的敘述相符。因此選項 C 正確。選項 A(logs:GetLogEvents)是用來讀取、查詢既有日誌內容的 CloudWatch Logs 動作,並不屬於官方文件所列的發布權限政策,即使缺少此權限,也不會阻止服務寫入日誌。選項 B 是干擾項:安全工程師本人是否能夠 assume 該 role,與 flow log 的日誌傳送毫無關係,因為需要 assume 該 role 的是 vpc-flow-logs.amazonaws.com 這個服務,而非工程師本人。選項 D(該 role 無法標記 log stream)在官方文件記載的 IAM 政策中完全沒有依據;五個必要動作中沒有任何一個與標記(tagging)相關,AWS 也未要求 flow-log role 具備標記 log stream 的權限。由於唯一有文件依據、且專屬於該 IAM role、會完全阻斷日誌傳送的故障原因,就是與 vpc-flow-logs.amazonaws.com principal 之間的信任關係損壞,因此 C 是唯一正確答案。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"logs:GetLogEvents is a read-side CloudWatch Logs action used to retrieve existing log data for viewing/querying. It is not part of the documented permissions policy required for the flow log role to publish logs (which requires CreateLogGroup, CreateLogStream, PutLogEvents, DescribeLogGroups, and DescribeLogStreams), so its absence would not prevent log delivery.","why_zh":"logs:GetLogEvents 是用於讀取、查詢既有日誌內容的 CloudWatch Logs 動作,並非官方文件中 flow log role 發布日誌所需權限政策的一部分(該政策要求的是 CreateLogGroup、CreateLogStream、PutLogEvents、DescribeLogGroups、DescribeLogStreams),因此缺少此權限不會阻止日誌傳送。"},{"letter":"B","why_en":"The security engineer's personal ability to assume the role is irrelevant to flow log delivery. It is the vpc-flow-logs.amazonaws.com service principal, not the human engineer, that must assume the role in order to publish logs to CloudWatch Logs.","why_zh":"安全工程師本人是否能夠 assume 該 role,與 flow log 的日誌傳送無關。需要 assume 該 role 以將日誌發布到 CloudWatch Logs 的是 vpc-flow-logs.amazonaws.com 這個 service principal,而不是工程師本人。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"The documented flow log IAM permissions policy contains no tagging-related actions at all (only CreateLogGroup, CreateLogStream, PutLogEvents, DescribeLogGroups, and DescribeLogStreams). There is no AWS requirement for the flow log role to tag the log stream, so this cannot be the root cause.","why_zh":"官方文件記載的 flow log IAM 權限政策完全不包含任何與標記(tagging)相關的動作(僅有 CreateLogGroup、CreateLogStream、PutLogEvents、DescribeLogGroups、DescribeLogStreams)。AWS 並未要求 flow log role 具備標記 log stream 的權限,因此這不可能是根本原因。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/vpc/latest/userguide/flow-logs-iam-role.html"]}},{"id":78,"question_en":"A company has an Amazon RDS database. The database contains sensitive data that is shared across teams in the company. The company needs a solution to detect anomalous logins to the database. The solution must notify an existing Amazon SNS topic when anomalous logins occur. Which solution will meet these requirements?","question_zh":"一家公司拥有一个Amazon RDS数据库，该数据库包含敏感数据，并在公司各个团队之间共享。公司需要一种解决方案来检 测数据库的异常登录行为，并在发生异常登录时通知现有的Amazon SNS主题。 哪种解决方案能满足这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Use AWS Trusted Advisor security checks for Amazon RDS. Create an Amazon EventBridge rule to monitor the security checks for status changes. Configure the EventBridge rule to invoke an AWS Lambda function to publish a message to the SNS topic.","B":"Enable AWS AppFabric. Connect AWS AppFabric to the RDS DB instance. Create an Amazon Data Firehose stream as the destination for the AWS AppFabric findings. Create an AWS Lambda function that is invoked by the Firehose stream to publish a message to the SNS topic.","C":"Enable Amazon GuardDuty and configure GuardDuty RDS Protection. Create an Amazon EventBridge rule to monitor GuardDuty findings of anomalous logins. Configure the SNS topic as the target of the EventBridge rule.","D":"Enable Amazon Inspector. Create an Amazon EventBridge rule to monitor Amazon Inspector findings of anomalous logins. Configure the SNS topic as the target of the EventBridge rule."},"options_zh":{"A":"使用 AWS Trusted Advisor 的安全检查功能监控 Amazon RDS。创建一个 Amazon EventBridge 规则，用于监视安全 检查状态的变化。配置该 EventBridge 规则，使其触发一个 AWS Lambda 函数，并将消息发布到 SNS 主题。","B":"启用 AWS AppFabric。将 AWS AppFabric 连接到 RDS 数据库实例。创建 Amazon Data Firehose 流，作为 AWS AppFabric 发现结果的目标。创建一个 AWS Lambda 函数，由 Firehose 流触发，用于向 SNS 主题发布消息。","C":"启用 Amazon GuardDuty 并配置 GuardDuty RDS 保护功能。创建一个 Amazon EventBridge 规则，用于监控异常登录的 GuardDuty 发现项，并将 SNS 主题配置为该 EventBridge 规则的目标。","D":"启用 Amazon Inspector。创建一个 Amazon EventBridge 规则，用于监控 Amazon Inspector 发现的异常登录行为，并将 SNS 主题配置为该 EventBridge 规则的目标。"},"answer":["C"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Security/IAM","Compute","Database","Serverless/Integration"],"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選","research":{"verdict":["C"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"both","explanation_en":"AWS documentation confirms this directly. The GuardDuty User Guide page 'GuardDuty RDS Protection' states: 'RDS Protection in Amazon GuardDuty analyzes and profiles RDS login activity for potential access threats' to Aurora MySQL-Compatible, Aurora PostgreSQL-Compatible, and RDS for PostgreSQL databases, and that it detects things like 'a previously unseen external actor has unauthorized access to your database, or adversary attempts brute-force access by guessing the database's password.' When RDS Protection detects a suspicious or anomalous login, GuardDuty generates specific RDS Protection finding types, for example CredentialAccess:RDS/AnomalousBehavior.SuccessfulLogin and CredentialAccess:RDS/AnomalousBehavior.SuccessfulBruteForce - both explicitly named around anomalous login behavior, not SQL injection or generic data exfiltration. This directly satisfies the requirement to 'detect anomalous logins to the database.' For delivery, the GuardDuty 'Getting started' guide's own walkthrough ('Step 4: Set up GuardDuty finding alerts through SNS') and the EventBridge integration docs describe creating an Amazon EventBridge rule that matches GuardDuty finding events and forwards them straight to an Amazon SNS topic as the rule's target - no Lambda function is required for this hand-off, since SNS is a native, documented EventBridge target. So option C's architecture (enable GuardDuty RDS Protection -> EventBridge rule on GuardDuty findings -> SNS topic as target) matches the documented pattern exactly, with no extra moving parts. Option A is wrong because Trusted Advisor's RDS checks are configuration/best-practice checks (e.g., idle instances, security group exposure, backups), not login-behavior anomaly detection. Option B is wrong because AWS AppFabric is a SaaS-application data aggregation service (it connects SaaS apps like Slack, Salesforce, etc., not RDS instances) and has no RDS login-monitoring capability at all. Option D is wrong because Amazon Inspector performs vulnerability/configuration scanning of EC2, ECR container images, and Lambda functions; it does not analyze RDS authentication activity or produce anomalous-login findings. Only GuardDuty RDS Protection produces the specific finding type needed here, and only C's pipeline is a valid, documented, Lambda-free path to the existing SNS topic.","explanation_zh":"AWS 官方文件直接證實了這一點。GuardDuty 使用者指南中的 'GuardDuty RDS Protection' 頁面說明:'RDS Protection in Amazon GuardDuty 會分析並剖析 RDS 登入活動,以偵測潛在的存取威脅',適用於 Aurora MySQL-Compatible、Aurora PostgreSQL-Compatible 以及 RDS for PostgreSQL 資料庫,並能偵測諸如「先前未曾出現過的外部行為者未經授權存取你的資料庫,或是攻擊者嘗試以暴力破解方式猜測資料庫密碼」等情況。當 RDS Protection 偵測到可疑或異常登入時,GuardDuty 會產生特定的 RDS Protection finding types,例如 CredentialAccess:RDS/AnomalousBehavior.SuccessfulLogin 與 CredentialAccess:RDS/AnomalousBehavior.SuccessfulBruteForce - 這兩者的命名都明確圍繞在「異常登入行為」,而非 SQL injection 或一般性的資料外洩。這直接滿足題目要求的「偵測資料庫的異常登入」。至於通知的部分,GuardDuty 的「入門指南」中本身就有一個步驟(Step 4: Set up GuardDuty finding alerts through SNS),以及 EventBridge 整合文件都說明:建立一個 Amazon EventBridge 規則來比對 GuardDuty finding 事件,並將該規則的目標直接設為 Amazon SNS topic - 這個轉發過程完全不需要 Lambda 函數,因為 SNS 本身就是 EventBridge 官方支援的目標類型之一。因此選項 C 的架構(啟用 GuardDuty RDS Protection -> 針對 GuardDuty findings 建立 EventBridge 規則 -> 以 SNS topic 作為目標)完全符合文件所述的標準做法,且不需要額外元件。選項 A 錯誤,因為 Trusted Advisor 針對 RDS 的檢查屬於組態/最佳實務類檢查(例如閒置執行個體、安全群組暴露、備份狀況),並非登入行為異常偵測。選項 B 錯誤,因為 AWS AppFabric 是用來整合 SaaS 應用程式資料的服務(連接的是 Slack、Salesforce 等 SaaS 應用,而非 RDS 執行個體),完全沒有監控 RDS 登入的能力。選項 D 錯誤,因為 Amazon Inspector 執行的是 EC2、ECR 容器映像與 Lambda 函數的漏洞/組態掃描,並不會分析 RDS 的驗證活動,也不會產生異常登入相關的 finding。只有 GuardDuty RDS Protection 能產生題目所需的特定 finding type,而且只有 C 的流程是有文件依據、不需 Lambda 即可送達既有 SNS topic 的正確做法。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"AWS Trusted Advisor's RDS checks focus on configuration and cost/best-practice issues (idle DB instances, security group misconfigurations, backup settings), not on analyzing login activity for anomalous behavior, so it cannot detect anomalous logins at all.","why_zh":"AWS Trusted Advisor 對 RDS 的檢查著重於組態與成本/最佳實務問題(例如閒置的資料庫執行個體、安全群組設定錯誤、備份設定),並不會分析登入活動以偵測異常行為,因此根本無法偵測異常登入。"},{"letter":"B","why_en":"AWS AppFabric aggregates data from SaaS applications (e.g., Slack, Salesforce, Okta) for security and productivity insights; it does not connect to or monitor Amazon RDS instances, so it cannot generate RDS login findings, and it does not use Data Firehose as a findings destination in this manner.","why_zh":"AWS AppFabric 是用來整合 SaaS 應用程式(例如 Slack、Salesforce、Okta)資料以取得安全與生產力洞察的服務;它不會連接或監控 Amazon RDS 執行個體,因此無法產生 RDS 登入相關的 finding,也不會以此方式使用 Data Firehose 作為 findings 目的地。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"Amazon Inspector performs automated vulnerability and configuration scanning for EC2 instances, container images in ECR, and Lambda functions. It does not monitor database authentication/login activity and has no finding type for anomalous RDS logins.","why_zh":"Amazon Inspector 是針對 EC2 執行個體、ECR 中的容器映像以及 Lambda 函數進行自動化漏洞與組態掃描的服務,並不會監控資料庫的驗證/登入活動,也沒有針對 RDS 異常登入的 finding type。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/guardduty/latest/ug/rds-protection.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/guardduty/latest/ug/findings-rds-protection.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/guardduty/latest/ug/guardduty_settingup.html"]}},{"id":79,"question_en":"A company’s web application runs on Amazon EC2 instances behind an Application Load Balancer (ALB) in an Auto Scaling group. An AWS WAF web ACL is associated with the ALB. Instance logs are lost after reboots. The operations team suspects malicious activity targeting a specific PHP file. Which set of actions will identify the suspect attacker’s IP address for future occurrences?","question_zh":"一家公司的Web应用程序运行在自动扩展组中的Amazon EC2实例上，这些实例位于应用负载均衡器（ALB）之后。一个 AWS WAF网络ACL已与该ALB关联。实例日志在重启后丢失。运维团队怀疑存在针对某个特定PHP文件的恶意活动。 哪一组操作可以识别嫌疑攻击者的IP地址，以便在将来发生类似事件时使用？","options_en":{"A":"Configure VPC Flow Logs and search for PHP file activity.","B":"Install the CloudWatch agent on the ALB and export application logs.","C":"Export ALB access logs to Amazon OpenSearch Service and search them.","D":"Configure the web ACL to send logs to Amazon Kinesis Data Firehose. Deliver logs to Amazon S3 and query them with Amazon Athena."},"options_zh":{"A":"配置VPC流量日志并搜索PHP文件活动。","B":"在ALB上安装CloudWatch代理并导出应用程序日志。","C":"将 ALB 访问日志导出到 Amazon OpenSearch 服务并进行搜索。","D":"配置网络ACL，将日志发送到Amazon Kinesis Data Firehose，然后将日志传递至Amazon S3，并使用Amazon Athena进行 查询。"},"answer":["D"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Networking/DNS","Security/IAM","Storage","Compute","Serverless/Integration","Monitoring/Ops","Analytics"],"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選","research":{"verdict":["D"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"both","explanation_en":"D is correct. Verified directly against AWS docs: AWS WAF logging (docs.aws.amazon.com/waf/latest/developerguide/logging.html) states you can send web ACL logs to a CloudWatch Logs log group, an S3 bucket, or an Amazon Data Firehose delivery stream, and that logs include 'detailed information about the request' plus 'details about the rules that the request matched.' The field reference (logging-fields.html) confirms each log record carries clientIp (the requester's IP) and httpRequest metadata (including the URI), alongside the action/rule-match verdict AWS WAF applied. The logging-destinations.html page confirms Firehose is an official first-class destination (see logging-kinesis.html), and Amazon Athena has a dedicated, AWS-documented feature for this exact pipeline: 'Example queries for AWS WAF logs' (docs.aws.amazon.com/athena/latest/ug/waf-logs.html) and a ready-made 'AWS WAF logs table' schema (docs.aws.amazon.com/athena/latest/ug/create-waf-table.html) for querying WAF logs stored in S3. This is precisely option D's toolchain: configure the web ACL to send logs to Firehose, deliver to S3, and query with Athena. It solves the stated problem two ways: (1) it works despite EC2 instance logs being lost on reboot, because the data lives in S3/Firehose, entirely decoupled from the instances; and (2) because the web ACL already inspects every request for malicious patterns (SQLi, XSS, rate limits, etc.), the WAF log's action/rule-match field lets the team directly identify the clientIp tied to blocked/flagged requests against the specific PHP file, rather than just any IP that happened to request it. Checking the distractors: A (VPC Flow Logs) captures only L3/L4 metadata (IPs, ports, protocol, bytes) with no HTTP URI/path field, so it cannot identify 'PHP file' targeting at all. B is nonsensical because an ALB is a fully managed service with no OS to install a CloudWatch agent on, and ALBs don't have 'application logs' to export this way. C is not factually broken -- ALB access logs do include the client IP (client:port field) and the full request line (including the URI), as documented in load-balancer-access-logs.html -- but it demands building and operating a separate OpenSearch Service cluster and offers no native 'this is malicious' signal (no rule-match verdict), only raw request records that an analyst must manually inspect. Given a WAF web ACL is already in place specifically to evaluate malicious traffic, D's WAF-native logging pipeline is the more direct, serverless, and AWS-recommended answer. Verdict has exactly one letter: D. I confirm the first analyst's answer and their citations; no correction needed.","explanation_zh":"答案為 D。已直接對照 AWS 文件驗證:AWS WAF logging(docs.aws.amazon.com/waf/latest/developerguide/logging.html)明確指出,web ACL 的 log 可以送到 Amazon CloudWatch Logs log group、Amazon S3 bucket,或 Amazon Data Firehose delivery stream,且 log 內容包含「請求的詳細資訊」以及「請求所比對到的 rule 詳情」。欄位參考文件(logging-fields.html)確認每筆 log 都帶有 clientIp(請求端 IP)與 httpRequest metadata(含 URI),以及 AWS WAF 判定的 action/rule-match 結果。logging-destinations.html 確認 Firehose 是官方支援的一級目的地(詳見 logging-kinesis.html),而 Amazon Athena 更有專門針對此情境的官方文件功能:「Example queries for AWS WAF logs」(docs.aws.amazon.com/athena/latest/ug/waf-logs.html)以及現成的「AWS WAF logs table」schema(docs.aws.amazon.com/athena/latest/ug/create-waf-table.html),專門用來查詢存放在 S3 的 WAF logs。這正好對應選項 D 的工具鏈:將 web ACL 設定為把 log 送到 Firehose、再送到 S3,並用 Athena 查詢。此做法從兩方面解決題目情境:(1) 即使 EC2 instance 的 log 因重開機而遺失,此方案仍可運作,因為資料存放在 S3/Firehose,與 instance 完全解耦;(2) 由於 web ACL 本來就針對每個請求檢查惡意模式(SQLi、XSS、rate-based rules 等),WAF log 的 action/rule-match 欄位能讓團隊直接找出對該 PHP 檔案發動攻擊(而非只是單純請求過)的 clientIp。逐一檢視干擾選項:A(VPC Flow Logs)只記錄 L3/L4 metadata(IP、port、protocol、bytes),沒有 HTTP URI/路徑欄位,完全無法辨識「針對 PHP 檔案」的行為。B 不合理,因為 ALB 是全託管服務,沒有作業系統可安裝 CloudWatch agent,ALB 本身也沒有可用此方式匯出的「application logs」。C 在事實上並非錯誤——ALB access logs 確實包含 client IP(client:port 欄位)與完整請求列(含 URI),此點已於 load-balancer-access-logs.html 中驗證——但此方案需要額外建置並維運獨立的 OpenSearch Service cluster,且沒有原生的「此為惡意」判定訊號(沒有 rule-match 結果),只有原始請求紀錄,需要分析人員自行判讀。既然情境中已部署專門用於評估惡意流量的 WAF web ACL,D 的 WAF 原生 logging 管線更直接、無伺服器,也更符合 AWS 建議做法。正確答案恰為一個字母:D。確認第一位分析師的答案與引用來源皆正確,無需更正。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"VPC Flow Logs capture only network/transport-layer metadata (source/destination IP and port, protocol, packet/byte counts, accept/reject) and have no field for the HTTP request URI or path, so they cannot reveal that a client targeted a specific PHP file at all, regardless of the logging destination.","why_zh":"VPC Flow Logs 只記錄網路層/傳輸層 metadata(來源/目的 IP 與 port、protocol、封包/位元組數、accept/reject),沒有任何欄位記錄 HTTP 請求的 URI 或路徑,因此完全無法揭露 client 是否針對特定 PHP 檔案發動請求,無論目的地是哪裡都一樣。"},{"letter":"B","why_en":"The CloudWatch agent is software installed on an operating system (EC2, on-premises server, etc.) to collect OS/application logs and metrics; an Application Load Balancer is a fully managed AWS service with no accessible host or OS, so there is nowhere to install the agent and no 'application log' to export this way.","why_zh":"CloudWatch agent 是安裝在作業系統上(EC2、地端伺服器等)用來收集 OS/應用程式 log 與指標的軟體;Application Load Balancer 是全託管的 AWS 服務,沒有可存取的主機或作業系統,因此無處可安裝 agent,也沒有可用此方式匯出的「application log」。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"ALB access logs do genuinely contain both the client IP (client:port field) and the full request line including the URI (verified against load-balancer-access-logs.html), so this option is not factually impossible -- it could surface the IP requesting the PHP file. However, it requires standing up and operating a separate Amazon OpenSearch Service cluster (extra infrastructure/cost), and raw access log entries carry no WAF rule-match or 'malicious' verdict, so distinguishing an attacker from normal traffic must be done entirely manually. Since a WAF web ACL is already inspecting traffic for malicious patterns, the WAF-native Firehose-to-S3-to-Athena pipeline in D is the more direct and AWS-recommended fit for this scenario.","why_zh":"ALB access logs 確實同時包含 client IP(client:port 欄位)與完整請求列(含 URI,已對照 load-balancer-access-logs.html 驗證),因此此選項並非事實上不可行——確實能找出請求該 PHP 檔案的 IP。但此方案需要額外建置並維運獨立的 Amazon OpenSearch Service cluster(額外基礎設施與成本),且原始 access log 紀錄本身沒有 WAF 規則比對或「惡意」判定結果,區分攻擊者與正常流量完全要靠人工判斷。既然情境中已有 WAF web ACL 在檢查惡意流量模式,D 的 WAF 原生 Firehose 到 S3 再到 Athena 管線對此情境而言更直接,也更符合 AWS 建議做法。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/waf/latest/developerguide/logging.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/waf/latest/developerguide/logging-fields.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/waf/latest/developerguide/logging-destinations.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/waf/latest/developerguide/logging-kinesis.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/athena/latest/ug/waf-logs.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/athena/latest/ug/create-waf-table.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/elasticloadbalancing/latest/application/load-balancer-access-logs.html"]}},{"id":80,"question_en":"A security engineer needs to control access to data that is encrypted with an AWS Key Management Service (AWS KMS) customer managed key. The security engineer also needs to use additional authenticated data (AAD) to prevent tampering with ciphertext. Which solution will meet these requirements?","question_zh":"安全工程师需要控制使用 AWS 密钥管理服务（AWS KMS）客户管理密钥加密的数据的访问权限。此外，安全工程师还需 使用附加认证数据（AAD）来防止密文被篡改。 哪种解决方案能满足这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Pass the key alias to AWS KMS when calling the Encrypt and Decrypt API actions.","B":"Use IAM policies to restrict access to the Encrypt and Decrypt API actions.","C":"Use the kms:EncryptionContext condition key when defining IAM policies for the customer managed key.","D":"Use key policies to restrict access to the appropriate IAM groups."},"options_zh":{"A":"在调用 Encrypt 和 Decrypt API 操作时，将密钥别名传递给 AWS KMS。","B":"使用 IAM 策略限制对加密和解密 API 操作的访问。","C":"在为客户管理密钥定义 IAM 策略时，使用 kms:EncryptionContext 条件键。","D":"使用关键策略限制对相应 IAM 组的访问。"},"answer":["C"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Security/IAM"],"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選","research":{"verdict":["C"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"both","explanation_en":"AWS KMS documentation on encryption context states explicitly: \"AWS KMS uses the encryption context as additional authenticated data (AAD) to support authenticated encryption. The encryption context is cryptographically bound to the ciphertext so that the same encryption context is required to decrypt the data.\" This means encryption context inherently serves as tamper-detection (AAD) for ciphertext — if the ciphertext or the supplied encryption context is altered, decryption fails. The same doc page confirms encryption context can also be used to control access: you can use it 'as a condition in policy statements,' via the kms:EncryptionContext:context-key and kms:EncryptionContextKeys condition keys, in either IAM policies or key policies, to allow or deny a permission only when the request includes particular encryption context keys or key-value pairs. Using the kms:EncryptionContext condition key therefore both enforces that callers supply the correct AAD (tamper protection, inherent to how KMS handles encryption context) and restricts who can Encrypt/Decrypt with the key based on that context (access control) — satisfying both requirements in the question with one mechanism. Option C is correct.","explanation_zh":"AWS KMS 文件(Encryption context)明確指出:「AWS KMS uses the encryption context as additional authenticated data (AAD) to support authenticated encryption. The encryption context is cryptographically bound to the ciphertext so that the same encryption context is required to decrypt the data.」也就是說 encryption context 本身就是用來防止 ciphertext 被竄改的 AAD——若 ciphertext 或所提供的 encryption context 遭竄改,解密就會失敗。同一頁文件也確認可以用 encryption context 來控制存取權限:可以將其「作為 policy statement 中的 condition」使用,透過 kms:EncryptionContext:context-key 與 kms:EncryptionContextKeys 這兩個 condition key,在 IAM policy 或 key policy 中設定,只有當請求中包含特定的 encryption context key 或 key-value pair 時才允許(或拒絕)權限。因此使用 kms:EncryptionContext condition key,同時達成了「要求呼叫者提供正確的 AAD 以防止竄改」(這是 KMS 處理 encryption context 的內建行為)與「依據該 context 限制誰能使用該 key 進行 Encrypt/Decrypt」這兩項需求。答案為 C。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"Passing the key alias only identifies which KMS key to use in the API call. It has no relationship to encryption context or AAD, and does not provide tamper protection or access control based on context.","why_zh":"傳入 key alias 只是用來指定要使用哪一個 KMS key,與 encryption context 或 AAD 完全無關,也無法提供基於 context 的竄改防護或存取控制。"},{"letter":"B","why_en":"Using IAM policies to restrict the Encrypt and Decrypt actions is generic API-level access control. It does not involve encryption context at all, so it does not address the AAD/tamper-protection requirement in the question.","why_zh":"使用 IAM policy 限制 Encrypt 和 Decrypt API 動作只是一般的 API 層級存取控制,完全沒有涉及 encryption context,因此無法滿足題目中關於 AAD(防竄改)的需求。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"Key policies cannot use IAM groups as principals — AWS documentation states plainly that 'IAM groups are not valid principals in a key policy.' To grant access to a group of users you must either use an IAM role as the key policy principal, or attach an IAM policy to the group (with the key policy enabling IAM policies). This makes option D technically invalid regardless of its relevance to AAD.","why_zh":"Key policy 無法將 IAM group 設為 principal——AWS 文件明確指出「IAM groups are not valid principals in a key policy.」若要讓一群使用者存取金鑰,必須改用 IAM role 作為 key policy 的 principal,或是讓 key policy 啟用 IAM policy 後,將 IAM policy 附加到該 group。因此選項 D 在技術上就不成立,與 AAD 需求是否相關已無意義。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/kms/latest/developerguide/encrypt_context.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/kms/latest/developerguide/conditions-kms.html#conditions-kms-encryption-context","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/kms/latest/developerguide/policy-conditions.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/kms/latest/developerguide/iam-policies.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/kms/latest/developerguide/key-policies.html"]}},{"id":81,"question_en":"A company operates a web application that runs on Amazon EC2 instances. The application listens on port 80 and port 443. The company uses an Application Load Balancer (ALB) with AWS WAF to terminate SSL and to forward traffic to the application instances only on port 80. The ALB is in public subnets that are associated with a network ACL named NACL1. The application instances are in dedicated private subnets that are associated with a network ACL named NACL2. An Amazon RDS for PostgreSQL DB instance that uses port 5432 is in a dedicated private subnet that is associated with a network ACL named NACL3. All the network ACLs currently allow all inbound and outbound traffic. Which set of network ACL changes will increase the security of the application while ensuring functionality?","question_zh":"一家公司运营着一个运行在 Amazon EC2 实例上的 Web 应用程序。该应用监听 80 端口和 443 端口。公司使用带有 AWS WAF 的 应用程序负载均衡器（ALB）来终止 SSL 连接，并仅将流量转发到应用实例的 80 端口。 ALB 位于与名为 NACL1 的网络 ACL 关联的公共子网中。应用程序实例位于与名为 NACL2 的网络 ACL 关联的专用私有 子网中。一个使用端口 5432 的 Amazon RDS for PostgreSQL 数据库实例位于与名为 NACL3 的网络 ACL 关联的专用私有 子网中。目前，所有网络 ACL 都允许所有的入站和出站流量。 哪一组网络ACL更改可以在确保功能的同时提高应用程序的安全性？","options_en":{"A":"Make the following changes to NACL3: • Add a rule that allows inbound traffic on port 5432 from NACL2. • Add a rule that allows outbound traffic on ports 1024-65536 to NACL2. • Remove the default rules that allow all inbound and outbound traffic.","B":"Make the following changes to NACL3: • Add a rule that allows inbound traffic on port 5432 from the CIDR blocks of the application instance subnets. • Add a rule that allows outbound traffic on ports 1024-65536 to the application instance subnets. • Remove the default rules that allow all inbound and outbound traffic.","C":"Make the following changes to NACL2: • Add a rule that allows outbound traffic on port 5432 to the CIDR blocks of the RDS subnets. • Remove the default rules that allow all inbound and outbound traffic.","D":"Make the following changes to NACL2: • Add a rule that allows inbound traffic on port 5432 from the CIDR blocks of the RDS subnets. • Add a rule that allows outbound traffic on port 5432 to the RDS subnets."},"options_zh":{"A":"对NACL3进行以下修改： • 添加一条规则，允许来自 NACL2 的 5432 端口入站流量。 • 添加一条规则，允许端口 1024-65536 的出站流量访问 NACL2。 • 删除允许所有入站和出站流量的默认规则。","B":"对NACL3进行以下修改： • 添加一条规则，允许来自应用程序实例子网的 CIDR 块的 5432 端口入站流量。 • 添加一条规则，允许应用程序实例子网中的 1024-65536 端口的出站流量。 • 删除允许所有入站和出站流量的默认规则。","C":"对 NACL2 做如下修改： • 添加一条规则，允许从 RDS 子网的 CIDR 块向端口 5432 发出出站流量。 • 删除允许所有入站和出站流量的默认规则。","D":"对NACL2进行以下修改： • 添加一条规则，允许来自 RDS 子网 CIDR 块的 5432 端口入站流量。 • 添加一条规则，允许从 RDS 子网通过端口 5432 发出的流量。"},"answer":["B"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Networking/DNS","Security/IAM","Compute","Database"],"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選","research":{"verdict":["B"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"AWS's own network ACL documentation ('Network ACL rules', nacl-rules.html) defines the Source/Destination fields of a rule strictly as a 'CIDR range' — there is no such thing as naming another network ACL (e.g. 'NACL2') as a source or destination. That capability (referencing another object, like a security-group ID, as a source) exists only for security groups, not network ACLs, as the companion example on the same page family shows ('nacl-examples.html': the security group example uses 'sg-1234567890abcdef0' as a Source, while every network ACL rule in the same example uses a CIDR such as 172.31.1.2/32 or 0.0.0.0/0). This immediately invalidates option A, which invents rules referencing 'NACL2' as a source/destination — that is not an attribute a network ACL rule can express. That leaves B, C, and D. AWS's documented network ACL pattern ('Example: Control access to instances in a subnet') is: because network ACLs are stateless, an inbound allow rule for a service port must be paired with an outbound allow rule on the ephemeral port range (1024-65535) directed back at the client's CIDR, since the server's reply leaves from the service port but arrives at the client's OS-chosen ephemeral port. Applied to this scenario, the correct fix is on NACL3 (the RDS subnet, which is the actual target that needs to be locked down): allow inbound TCP 5432 from the CIDR blocks of the application-instance subnets (the real client, expressed as CIDR, not a NACL name), allow outbound TCP 1024-65535 back to those same subnet CIDR blocks for the stateless return traffic, and then remove the default allow-all rules so the DB tier is no longer wide open. This is exactly option B. Option C only touches NACL2: it adds an outbound rule to RDS on 5432 but removes ALL of NACL2's default allow rules — which would also strip the inbound rule needed for the ALB-to-app-instance traffic on port 80 and the ephemeral-port inbound return rule needed for the RDS response, breaking the application entirely, and it never restricts NACL3 (the DB subnet) at all, so no real security gain is achieved on the tier that matters. Option D adds an inbound rule to NACL2 allowing traffic from RDS on port 5432 — backwards, since the app instances are the client that must send outbound traffic to RDS on 5432 and receive the reply on an ephemeral port, not receive inbound traffic on 5432 — and it never removes the default allow-all rules, so it produces zero security improvement while also being functionally illogical. Only B is both syntactically valid (uses CIDR blocks, as AWS's model requires) and functionally complete (adds the correct inbound service-port rule, the mandatory ephemeral-port return rule, and removes the default allow-all) on the correct tier (NACL3/RDS subnet).","explanation_zh":"AWS 官方 network ACL 文件(nacl-rules.html「Network ACL rules」)明確定義 rule 的 Source/Destination 欄位只能是「CIDR range」——並沒有把另一個 network ACL(例如「NACL2」)當作 source 或 destination 指定的用法。能夠把其他物件(例如 security group ID)當作 source 引用的是 security group,不是 network ACL;同系列的範例頁(nacl-examples.html)也印證這點:security group 範例把 Source 設為 sg-1234567890abcdef0,而同一範例中所有 network ACL rule 的 Source/Destination 全部都是 CIDR(例如 172.31.1.2/32 或 0.0.0.0/0)。這立即排除選項 A,因為它虛構了「從 NACL2 允許進入流量」這種 network ACL rule 不存在的寫法。剩下 B、C、D 三個選項。AWS 文件所示範的 network ACL 標準做法(「Example: Control access to instances in a subnet」)是:因為 network ACL 是 stateless(無狀態),針對某服務埠的 inbound allow rule,必須搭配一條允許 outbound 到用戶端 CIDR、埠範圍為 ephemeral port(1024-65535)的 rule,因為伺服器的回應是從服務埠送出,但抵達的是用戶端作業系統挑選的 ephemeral port。套用到此情境,正確做法應該作用在 NACL3(RDS 所在、真正需要被鎖緊的子網路):新增允許 inbound TCP 5432、來源為應用程式實例子網路 CIDR(真正的用戶端,以 CIDR 表示,而非 NACL 名稱)的規則;新增允許 outbound TCP 1024-65535、目的地為同樣那些子網路 CIDR 的規則,用來處理 stateless 的回應流量;然後移除預設的全開放規則,讓資料庫層不再完全開放。這正是選項 B 的做法。選項 C 只改 NACL2:雖然新增了 outbound 到 RDS 埠 5432 的規則,但同時移除了 NACL2「所有」預設的全開放規則——這也會一併移除 ALB 對應用程式實例埠 80 流量所需的 inbound 規則,以及接收 RDS 回應所需的 ephemeral port inbound 規則,導致應用程式整個失效;而且它完全沒有限制 NACL3(資料庫子網路),因此在真正需要收緊的那一層並未帶來安全提升。選項 D 在 NACL2 新增一條允許「來自 RDS、埠 5432」的 inbound 規則——方向顛倒了,因為應用程式實例才是用戶端,應該是主動對 RDS 送出埠 5432 的 outbound 流量、並在 ephemeral port 上接收回應,而不是接收來自 RDS 埠 5432 的 inbound 流量;而且它完全沒有移除預設的全開放規則,因此完全沒有帶來安全性提升,邏輯上也不合理。只有選項 B 同時符合語法正確(以 CIDR 表示,符合 AWS 的規則模型)與功能完整(新增正確的 inbound 服務埠規則、必要的 ephemeral port 回應規則,並移除預設全開放規則),且作用在正確的一層(NACL3/RDS 子網路)。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"Network ACL rules can only specify a Source/Destination as a CIDR range (per AWS's 'Network ACL rules' documentation) — there is no mechanism to reference another network ACL (like 'NACL2') as the source or destination of a rule. This option describes a capability that does not exist in the network ACL model, unlike security groups which can reference a security-group ID as a source.","why_zh":"根據 AWS「Network ACL rules」文件,network ACL rule 的 Source/Destination 只能指定為 CIDR range,並沒有辦法把另一個 network ACL(如「NACL2」)當作規則的來源或目的地引用。這個選項描述的是 network ACL 模型中不存在的能力,不同於 security group 可以把 security-group ID 當作 source 引用。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"This option only modifies NACL2 and removes ALL of its default allow rules, which would also break the ALB-to-application-instance traffic on port 80 (inbound rule and its ephemeral-port return) since no replacement rules for that traffic are added; it also never adds an inbound ephemeral-port return rule for the RDS response, and it never restricts NACL3 (the RDS subnet) at all, so the database tier remains fully open — no real security gain where it matters.","why_zh":"此選項只修改 NACL2,並移除其所有預設的全開放規則,這會連帶破壞 ALB 到應用程式實例埠 80 的流量(因為沒有補上對應的 inbound 規則及其 ephemeral port 回應規則);同時它也沒有為 RDS 的回應新增 inbound 的 ephemeral port 規則,更完全沒有限制 NACL3(RDS 子網路),導致資料庫層依然完全開放,在真正需要加強安全的地方毫無效果。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"The direction is backwards: application instances are the client that initiates traffic to RDS on port 5432 and receives replies on an ephemeral port, so an inbound rule on NACL2 allowing traffic 'from RDS' on port 5432 does not match real traffic flow. It also never removes the default allow-all rules, so it produces no security improvement at all.","why_zh":"方向顛倒了:應用程式實例是主動對 RDS 埠 5432 發送流量、並在 ephemeral port 上接收回應的用戶端,因此在 NACL2 新增「來自 RDS」埠 5432 的 inbound 規則並不符合實際的流量方向。而且此選項完全沒有移除預設的全開放規則,因此完全沒有帶來任何安全性提升。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/vpc/latest/userguide/nacl-rules.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/vpc/latest/userguide/nacl-examples.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/vpc/latest/userguide/vpc-network-acls.html"]}},{"id":82,"question_en":"A company is planning to deploy a new log analysis environment. The company needs to analyze logs from multiple AWS services in near real time. The solution must provide the ability to search the logs and must send alerts to an existing Amazon Simple Notification Service (Amazon SNS) topic when specific logs match detection rules. Which solution will meet these requirements?","question_zh":"一家公司计划部署新的日志分析环境，需要近乎实时地分析来自多个AWS服务的日志。该解决方案必须支持日志搜索功能， 并在特定日志匹配检测规则时，向现有的Amazon Simple Notification Service（Amazon SNS）主题发送告警通知。 哪种解决方案能满足这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Analyze the logs by using Amazon OpenSearch Service. Search the logs from the OpenSearch API. Use OpenSearch Service Security Analytics to match logs with detection rules and to send alerts to the SNS topic.","B":"Analyze the logs by using AWS Security Hub. Search the logs from the Findings page in Security Hub. Create custom actions to match logs with detection rules and to send alerts to the SNS topic.","C":"Analyze the logs by using Amazon CloudWatch Logs. Use a subscription filter to match logs with detection rules and to send alerts to the SNS topic. Search the logs manually by using CloudWatch Logs Insights.","D":"Analyze the logs by using Amazon QuickSight. Search the logs by listing the query results in a dashboard. Run queries to match logs with detection rules and to send alerts to the SNS topic."},"options_zh":{"A":"使用 Amazon OpenSearch 服务分析日志，通过 OpenSearch API 搜索日志，并利用 OpenSearch 服务安全分析功能将日 志与检测规则进行匹配，然后向 SNS 主题发送告警。","B":"使用 AWS Security Hub 分析日志。在 Security Hub 的发现页面中搜索日志。创建自定义操作，将日志与检测规则匹配， 并向 SNS 主题发送警报。","C":"使用 Amazon CloudWatch Logs 分析日志。通过订阅过滤器将日志与检测规则匹配，并将告警发送到 SNS 主题。使用 CloudWatch Logs Insights 手动搜索日志。","D":"使用 Amazon QuickSight 分析日志。通过在仪表板中列出查询结果来搜索日志。运行查询以将日志与检测规 则匹配，并向 SNS 主题发送警报。"},"answer":["A"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Security/IAM","Serverless/Integration","Monitoring/Ops","Analytics"],"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選","research":{"verdict":["A"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"both","explanation_en":"Amazon OpenSearch Service is purpose-built to ingest and search logs from multiple AWS services in near real time via the OpenSearch API/Dashboards, satisfying the search requirement natively. Its Security Analytics feature adds detectors that continuously evaluate custom and prepackaged Sigma rules against ingested log events, generating findings and, when a detector matches a rule, triggering alerts. Security Analytics alerts are delivered through the OpenSearch Notifications system, and per AWS documentation (alerting.html) the supported notification channel types for an alert action are 'Slack, Amazon Chime, a custom webhook, or Amazon SNS' - so Amazon SNS is explicitly confirmed as a direct, supported alert destination, not just an internal OpenSearch mechanism. This makes A the only option delivering both near real-time multi-service log search and native detection-rule-to-SNS alerting in one integrated pipeline (identify sources -> create detector -> configure rules -> configure alerts). Option B is wrong because Security Hub aggregates findings from other AWS security services (GuardDuty, Inspector, Macie, Config, etc.), not general logs from multiple AWS services, so it fails the 'search the logs' requirement; its custom actions also route through EventBridge, not directly to SNS. Option C is wrong on a factual detail beyond just being 'manual': AWS documentation (SubscriptionFilters.html) states CloudWatch Logs subscription filters can only target Amazon Kinesis Data Streams, AWS Lambda, Amazon Data Firehose, or Amazon OpenSearch Service as destinations - SNS is not a valid subscription filter destination, so a subscription filter cannot itself 'send alerts to the SNS topic' as the option claims; an intermediate Lambda would be required, and even then, CloudWatch Logs Insights search is manual/ad hoc rather than an automated detection-rule pipeline. Option D is wrong because QuickSight is a BI/visualization tool with no near-real-time detection-rule matching against raw logs.","explanation_zh":"Amazon OpenSearch Service 天生設計來近乎即時地擷取並搜尋來自多個 AWS 服務的日誌，透過 OpenSearch API/Dashboards 就能原生滿足「搜尋日誌」的需求。其 Security Analytics 功能提供 detector，可持續套用自訂規則與內建的 Sigma 規則來評估日誌事件，產生 finding，並在 detector 比對到規則時觸發 alert。Security Analytics 的警示是透過 OpenSearch Notifications 系統發送，根據 AWS 官方文件（alerting.html），alert action 支援的通知管道類型為「Slack、Amazon Chime、自訂 webhook，或 Amazon SNS」——因此 Amazon SNS 明確被確認為受支援的直接警示目的地，而非僅是 OpenSearch 內部機制。這使得 A 是唯一能在單一整合流程中（識別來源 -> 建立 detector -> 設定規則 -> 設定警示）同時提供「近即時多服務日誌搜尋」與「偵測規則直接對接 SNS 警示」兩項能力的選項。選項 B 錯誤，因為 Security Hub 匯總的是來自其他 AWS 安全服務（GuardDuty、Inspector、Macie、Config 等）的 finding，並非一般性的多服務日誌，無法滿足「搜尋日誌」的要求；其自訂動作也是透過 EventBridge 轉送，並非直接送到 SNS。選項 C 的錯誤不只是「手動」這一點：AWS 文件（SubscriptionFilters.html）明確指出 CloudWatch Logs subscription filter 的目的地僅限 Amazon Kinesis Data Streams、AWS Lambda、Amazon Data Firehose 或 Amazon OpenSearch Service，SNS 並非合法的 subscription filter 目的地，因此 subscription filter 本身無法如選項所述「直接送出警示到 SNS 主題」，必須額外透過 Lambda 中介；而且 CloudWatch Logs Insights 的搜尋是手動、隨需查詢，並非自動化的偵測規則比對機制。選項 D 錯誤，因為 QuickSight 是 BI 視覺化工具，不具備對原始日誌進行近即時偵測規則比對的能力。","distractors":[{"letter":"B","why_en":"AWS Security Hub aggregates and displays security findings produced by other AWS security services and partner tools, not raw logs ingested from multiple AWS services in general. It has no general-purpose log search capability, so it fails the 'search the logs' requirement even though custom actions can route findings to EventBridge and onward to SNS.","why_zh":"AWS Security Hub 匯總並顯示由其他 AWS 安全服務與合作夥伴工具產生的 finding，並非一般性地擷取多個 AWS 服務的原始日誌。它不具備通用的日誌搜尋能力，因此即使自訂動作可以把 finding 透過 EventBridge 轉送到 SNS，仍無法滿足「搜尋日誌」的需求。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"CloudWatch Logs Insights only supports manual, ad hoc query-based search with no built-in 'detection rule' construct that automatically evaluates incoming logs and fires alerts. More critically, AWS documentation confirms subscription filter destinations are limited to Kinesis Data Streams, Lambda, Firehose, or OpenSearch Service - SNS is not a supported destination, so the option's claim of sending alerts directly to the SNS topic via a subscription filter is technically inaccurate without an added Lambda step.","why_zh":"CloudWatch Logs Insights 只支援手動、隨需的查詢式搜尋，沒有內建的「偵測規則」機制可自動評估進來的日誌並觸發警示。更關鍵的是，AWS 文件確認 subscription filter 的目的地僅限於 Kinesis Data Streams、Lambda、Firehose 或 OpenSearch Service，SNS 並非受支援的目的地，因此該選項所述「透過 subscription filter 直接送警示到 SNS 主題」在技術上並不正確，除非額外加上 Lambda 這一步。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"Amazon QuickSight is a business intelligence and dashboarding service for visualizing query results; it is not designed to ingest and search near real-time logs from multiple AWS services, nor does it have a native detection-rule-matching and alerting mechanism tied to SNS.","why_zh":"Amazon QuickSight 是用於視覺化查詢結果的商業智慧與儀表板服務，並非設計來近即時擷取並搜尋來自多個 AWS 服務的日誌，也沒有原生的偵測規則比對與 SNS 警示機制。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/opensearch-service/latest/developerguide/security-analytics.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/opensearch-service/latest/developerguide/alerting.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonCloudWatch/latest/logs/SubscriptionFilters.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/securityhub/latest/userguide/securityhub-cwe-custom-actions.html"]}},{"id":83,"question_en":"A company is implementing new compliance requirements to meet customer needs. According to the new requirements, the company must not use any Amazon RDS DB instances or DB clusters that lack encryption of the underlying storage. The company needs a solution that will generate an email alert when an unencrypted DB instance or DB cluster is created. The solution also must terminate the unencrypted DB instance or DB cluster. Which solution will meet these requirements in the MOST operationally efficient manner?","question_zh":"一家公司正在实施新的合规要求以满足客户需求。根据新要求，该公司不得使用任何底层存储未加密的 Amazon RDS 数据 库实例或数据库集群。公司需要一种解决方案，当创建未加密的数据库实例或数据库集群时，能够生成电子邮件警报，并 自动终止该未加密的数据库实例或数据库集群。 哪种解决方案能够以最高效的操作方式满足这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Create an AWS Config managed rule to detect unencrypted RDS storage. Configure an automatic remediation action to publish messages to an Amazon Simple Notification Service (Amazon SNS) topic that includes an AWS Lambda function and an email delivery target as subscribers. Configure the Lambda function to delete the unencrypted resource.","B":"Create an AWS Config managed rule to detect unencrypted RDS storage. Configure a manual remediation action to invoke an AWS Lambda function. Configure the Lambda function to publish messages to an Amazon Simple Notification Service (Amazon SNS) topic and to delete the unencrypted resource.","C":"Create an Amazon EventBridge rule that evaluates RDS event patterns and is initiated by the creation of DB instances or DB clusters. Configure the rule to publish messages to an Amazon Simple Notification Service (Amazon SNS) topic that includes an AWS Lambda function and an email delivery target as subscribers. Configure the Lambda function to delete the unencrypted resource.","D":"Create an Amazon EventBridge rule that evaluates RDS event patterns and is initiated by the creation of DB instances or DB clusters. Configure the rule to invoke an AWS Lambda function. Configure the Lambda function to publish messages to an Amazon Simple Notification Service (Amazon SNS) topic and to delete the unencrypted resource."},"options_zh":{"A":"创建一个 AWS Config 管理规则，用于检测未加密的 RDS 存储。配置自动修复操作，将消息发布到 Amazon Simple Notification Service（Amazon SNS）主题，该主题包含一个 AWS Lambda 函数和一个电子邮件投递目标作为订阅者。 配置 Lambda 函数以删除未加密的资源。","B":"创建一个 AWS Config 管理规则，用于检测未加密的 RDS 存储。配置手动修复操作以调用 AWS Lambda 函数。将 Lambda 函数配置为向 Amazon Simple Notification Service（Amazon SNS）主题发布消息，并删除未加密的资源。","C":"创建一个 Amazon EventBridge 规则，用于评估 RDS 事件模式，并在创建数据库实例或数据库集群时触发。将该规则配 置为向 Amazon Simple Notification Service（Amazon SNS）主题发布消息，该主题的订阅者包括一个 AWS Lambda 函 数和一个电子邮件投递目标。配置 Lambda 函数以删除未加密的资源。","D":"创建一个 Amazon EventBridge 规则，用于评估 RDS 事件模式，并在创建数据库实例或数据库集群时触发。配置该规则 以调用 AWS Lambda 函数，并将 Lambda 函数设置为向 Amazon 简单通知服务（Amazon SNS）主题发布消息，并删 除未加密的资源。"},"answer":["A"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Organizations/Governance","Security/IAM","Compute","Database","Serverless/Integration"],"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選","research":{"verdict":["A"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"both","explanation_en":"AWS Config is the AWS-native service purpose-built for continuous compliance evaluation plus automated remediation, and this is exactly the pattern AWS's own prescriptive guidance uses for unencrypted RDS instances/clusters (Config rule + Systems Manager Automation remediation, optionally with an SNS alert). This confirms A/B (Config-based) as the intended family of designs over C/D (EventBridge-based). The managed rule rds-storage-encrypted (and rds-cluster-encrypted-at-rest for clusters) has Trigger type 'Configuration changes', meaning AWS Config evaluates the resource as soon as it records the new configuration item after creation - there is no meaningful delay here that would make EventBridge's push-based model necessary for 'promptly after creation' remediation. That removes the argument that EventBridge (C/D) is required for speed. The decisive distinction is then automatic versus manual remediation, which AWS Config documentation states explicitly: with 'Auto remediation' selected, the associated Systems Manager Automation document runs automatically once the rule marks the resource NON_COMPLIANT, with no human step; 'manual remediation' instead requires a person to open the console (or call StartRemediationExecution) to explicitly trigger the remediation action before anything happens. Requiring a human in the loop to terminate a newly created unencrypted DB instance is inherently less operationally efficient and delays the required termination, which rules out B. Amazon SNS natively supports many subscription protocols on a single topic (email, Lambda, SQS, HTTPS, SMS, etc.), so one topic publish can fan out simultaneously to an email endpoint and to a Lambda function - this is the simplest, most operationally efficient way to satisfy 'send an email AND delete the resource' from a single remediation trigger, exactly as A describes. Options C and D instead build this on EventBridge rules matching RDS creation API/event patterns, which fire for every DB creation (encrypted or not) and require custom event-pattern engineering plus custom Lambda logic to independently determine encryption status, since EventBridge alone does not evaluate compliance state the way a Config managed rule does - more moving parts for an equivalent outcome. Between C and D, D additionally forces the Lambda function to do double duty (publish to SNS AND delete), which is less clean than letting SNS's native fan-out handle both subscribers as in A/C. Combining all of this, A (Config managed rule, automatic remediation, single SNS topic fanning out to email and a deleting Lambda) is the most operationally efficient solution and matches AWS's documented pattern most closely.","explanation_zh":"AWS Config 是專為持續合規性評估與自動化修復而生的原生服務,AWS 官方的 prescriptive guidance 對未加密的 RDS instance/cluster 正是採用「Config 規則 + Systems Manager Automation 修復(可選擇搭配 SNS 警示)」這種架構,這確認了 A/B(以 Config 為基礎的設計)才是本題想測試的方向,而非 C/D(以 EventBridge 為基礎)。受管規則 rds-storage-encrypted(叢集則對應 rds-cluster-encrypted-at-rest)的 Trigger type 是「Configuration changes」,代表 AWS Config 只要記錄到資源建立後的新組態項目就會立即評估 - 這裡並沒有會讓「建立後應盡快修復」這個需求非得靠 EventBridge 推播模型才能達成的明顯延遲問題,因此「EventBridge 為了速度而必要」這個論點並不成立。真正的關鍵差異在於自動修復與手動修復:AWS Config 文件明確指出,選擇「Auto remediation」後,一旦規則將資源標記為 NON_COMPLIANT,關聯的 Systems Manager Automation 文件會自動執行,無需任何人工步驟;而「manual remediation」則需要有人進入主控台(或呼叫 StartRemediationExecution)手動觸發修復動作才會執行。要求人工介入才能終止一個剛建立的未加密 DB instance,操作效率本質上較差,也會延遲必要的終止動作,因此排除 B。Amazon SNS 原生支援單一主題(topic)同時擁有多種訂閱協定(email、Lambda、SQS、HTTPS、SMS 等),因此單次發布即可同時扇出給 email 端點與 Lambda function - 這是從單一修復觸發點同時滿足「寄送 email」與「刪除資源」最簡單、操作效率最高的做法,正如選項 A 所描述。選項 C、D 則改以 EventBridge 規則比對 RDS 建立的 API/事件模式來實作,這種規則對每一次 DB 建立(不論是否加密)都會觸發,還需要額外的自訂事件模式設計,以及自訂 Lambda 邏輯去獨立判斷加密狀態(EventBridge 本身不像 Config 受管規則那樣會評估合規狀態)- 為達到相同結果卻多了更多零件。C 與 D 之間,D 又額外要求 Lambda function 同時身兼「發布 SNS」與「刪除資源」兩項工作,不如讓 SNS 原生的扇出機制直接處理兩個訂閱者(如 A、C 的做法)那麼乾淨。綜合以上,選項 A(Config 受管規則、自動修復、單一 SNS 主題同時扇出給 email 與負責刪除的 Lambda)是操作上最有效率的解決方案,也最貼近 AWS 官方文件所示範的模式。","distractors":[{"letter":"B","why_en":"AWS Config documentation is explicit that manual remediation requires a person to open the console (or call StartRemediationExecution) to explicitly trigger the remediation action before the Lambda function runs. That human-in-the-loop step delays the required termination of the unencrypted resource and is inherently less operationally efficient than the 'Auto remediation' option used in A.","why_zh":"AWS Config 文件明確指出,手動修復需要有人進入主控台(或呼叫 StartRemediationExecution)並手動觸發修復動作,Lambda function 才會執行。這個人工介入的步驟會延遲終止未加密資源的必要動作,操作效率本質上不如 A 所採用的「Auto remediation」。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"Relying on custom EventBridge event patterns for RDS creation events fires on every DB creation regardless of encryption status and requires building custom logic (typically another Lambda invocation or extra rule logic) just to determine encryption status, since EventBridge does not evaluate compliance the way a purpose-built AWS Config managed rule does. This is more custom engineering than reusing the existing rds-storage-encrypted managed rule for equivalent detection speed.","why_zh":"依賴自訂的 EventBridge 事件模式來偵測 RDS 建立事件,不論是否加密都會觸發,還需要額外建置自訂邏輯(通常是另一個 Lambda 呼叫或額外規則邏輯)才能判斷加密狀態,因為 EventBridge 並不像專為此設計的 AWS Config 受管規則那樣會評估合規性。相較於直接沿用現有的 rds-storage-encrypted 受管規則(偵測速度相當),這需要更多客製化工程。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"This combines the drawbacks of a custom EventBridge event-pattern design (instead of reusing the purpose-built rds-storage-encrypted Config rule) with making the Lambda function itself responsible for both publishing the SNS notification and deleting the resource, instead of letting a single SNS topic natively fan out to both an email subscriber and a Lambda subscriber as in A. More custom code for an equivalent outcome makes it less operationally efficient.","why_zh":"此選項結合了兩個缺點:一是採用自訂的 EventBridge 事件模式,而非直接沿用專為此設計的 rds-storage-encrypted Config 規則;二是讓 Lambda function 本身同時負責發布 SNS 通知與刪除資源,而不是像 A 一樣讓單一 SNS 主題原生扇出給 email 訂閱者與 Lambda 訂閱者。為達到相同結果卻寫了更多客製化程式碼,操作效率較低。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/config/latest/developerguide/rds-storage-encrypted.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/config/latest/developerguide/rds-cluster-encrypted-at-rest.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/config/latest/developerguide/setup-autoremediation.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/config/latest/developerguide/setup-manualremediation.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/config/latest/developerguide/remediation.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/prescriptive-guidance/latest/patterns/automatically-remediate-unencrypted-amazon-rds-db-instances-and-clusters.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonRDS/latest/UserGuide/rds-cloud-watch-events.html"]}},{"id":84,"question_en":"A company runs several applications on Amazon Elastic Kubernetes Service (Amazon EKS). The company needs a solution to detect any Kubernetes security risks by monitoring Amazon EKS audit logs in addition to operating system, networking, and file events. The solution must send email alerts for any identified risks to a mailing list that is associated with a security team. Which solution will meet these requirements?","question_zh":"一家公司在 Amazon 弹性 Kubernetes 服务（Amazon EKS）上运行多个应用程序。该公司需要一种解决方案，通过监控 Amazon EKS 审计日志以及操作系统、网络和文件事件来检测任何 Kubernetes 安全风险。该解决方案必须将识别出的风险以电子邮件形 式发送给与安全团队关联的邮件列表。 哪种解决方案能满足这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Deploy AWS Security Hub and enable security standards that contain EKS controls. Create an Amazon Simple Notification Service (Amazon SNS) topic and set the security team’s mailing list as a subscriber. Use an Amazon EventBridge rule to send relevant Security Hub events to the SNS topic.","B":"Enable Amazon Inspector container image scanning. Configure Amazon Detective to analyze EKS security logs. Create Amazon CloudWatch log groups for EKS audit logs. Use an AWS Lambda function to process the logs and to send email alerts to the security team.","C":"Enable Amazon GuardDuty. Enable EKS Protection and Runtime Monitoring for Amazon EKS in GuardDuty. Create an Amazon Simple Notification Service (Amazon SNS) topic and set the security team ' s mailing list as a subscriber. Use an Amazon EventBridge rule to send relevant GuardDuty events to the SNS topic.","D":"Install the AWS Systems Manager Agent (SSM Agent) on all EKS nodes. Configure Amazon CloudWatch Logs to collect EKS audit logs. Create an Amazon Simple Notification Service (Amazon SNS) topic and set the security team ' s mailing list as a subscriber. Configure a CloudWatch alarm to publish a message to the SNS topic when new audit logs are generated."},"options_zh":{"A":"部署 AWS Security Hub 并启用包含 EKS 控制项的安全标准。创建一个 Amazon Simple Notification Service（Amazon SNS） 主题，并将安全团队的邮件列表设置为订阅者。使用 Amazon EventBridge 规则将相关的 Security Hub 事件发送到该 SNS 主题。","B":"启用 Amazon Inspector 容器镜像扫描功能，配置 Amazon Detective 分析 EKS 安全日志，为 EKS 审计日志创建 Amazon CloudWatch 日志组，并使用 AWS Lambda 函数处理日志并向安全团队发送邮件告警。","C":"启用 Amazon GuardDuty。在 GuardDuty 中启用 Amazon EKS 的保护和运行时监控功能。创建一个 Amazon 简单通知服务 （Amazon SNS）主题，并将安全团队的邮件列表设置为订阅者。使用 Amazon EventBridge 规则将相关的 GuardDuty 事件发送到该 SNS 主题。","D":"在所有 EKS 节点上安装 AWS Systems Manager Agent（SSM Agent）。配置 Amazon CloudWatch Logs 以收集 EKS 审计日 志。创建一个 Amazon Simple Notification Service（Amazon SNS）主题，并将安全团队的邮件列表设置为订阅者。配置 CloudWatch 告警，以便在生成新的审计日志时向该 SNS 主题发布消息。"},"answer":["C"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Security/IAM","Compute","Serverless/Integration","Monitoring/Ops","Containers"],"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選","research":{"verdict":["C"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"Option C is correct and verified against AWS documentation. GuardDuty's 'EKS Protection' feature works specifically by monitoring Kubernetes audit logs from EKS clusters - the dedicated documentation page is literally titled 'EKS Protection finding types' with the description 'Security findings generated by GuardDuty when potential threats are detected through EKS audit log monitoring.' This directly satisfies the requirement to monitor EKS audit logs. Separately, GuardDuty 'Runtime Monitoring' deploys a security agent (as an EKS add-on, DaemonSet on nodes, or sidecar for Fargate) that collects OS-level process events (process name, path, PID, user, parent process, etc.), network/DNS events (socket type, remote/local IP and port, protocol, DNS payload), and file events (Open events for file access/modification, plus Mount events for filesystem mounts). This confirms Runtime Monitoring covers all three required categories: operating system, networking, and file events. Together, EKS Protection + Runtime Monitoring on EKS give full coverage of Kubernetes audit logs plus OS/network/file telemetry from the same nodes, exactly matching the question's requirements. For alerting, AWS's own documented pattern ('Set up GuardDuty finding alerts through SNS') is to create an EventBridge rule matching GuardDuty finding events and target an SNS topic with an email subscription - no Lambda function is required for this path, since SNS natively supports email as a subscription protocol and EventBridge can invoke SNS directly as a target. This confirms option C's architecture end-to-end.\n\nOption A (Security Hub) aggregates security posture findings from checks/controls (including some EKS configuration checks) but does not perform behavioral analysis of EKS audit logs, and it does not provide OS/network/file runtime telemetry - that is a GuardDuty Runtime Monitoring capability, not a Security Hub one. Option B mixes unrelated services: Amazon Inspector does vulnerability/CVE scanning of container images (not audit log or runtime behavior monitoring), and Amazon Detective is a security investigation/visualization tool for post-hoc analysis of existing findings and logs - it does not generate its own real-time threat detections from EKS audit logs, and the proposal to have Lambda parse raw CloudWatch Logs to detect 'security risks' would require building custom detection logic that GuardDuty already provides out of the box. Option D just ships EKS audit logs to CloudWatch Logs and fires an alarm whenever new log data arrives - that produces an alert on log volume/existence, not on any actual detected security risk, so it fails the core requirement of detecting risks. Only option C uses purpose-built AWS threat detection services for both the audit log and OS/network/file event requirements, with a native SNS email delivery path.","explanation_zh":"選項 C 正確,已對照 AWS 官方文件驗證。GuardDuty 的 'EKS Protection' 功能專門透過監控 EKS 叢集的 Kubernetes audit logs 來運作 - 官方文件頁面標題就是 'EKS Protection finding types',說明為「當透過 EKS audit log 監控偵測到潛在威脅時,GuardDuty 產生的安全性 finding」。這直接滿足監控 EKS audit logs 的需求。另外,GuardDuty 的 'Runtime Monitoring' 會部署安全性 agent(以 EKS add-on、節點上的 DaemonSet,或 Fargate 的 sidecar 形式),收集作業系統層級的 process 事件(process 名稱、路徑、PID、使用者、parent process 等)、網路/DNS 事件(socket 類型、遠端/本機 IP 與埠、協定、DNS payload),以及檔案事件(Open events 用於檔案存取/修改,加上 Mount events 用於檔案系統掛載)。這證實 Runtime Monitoring 涵蓋了題目要求的三大類別:作業系統、網路、檔案事件。EKS Protection 加上 EKS 的 Runtime Monitoring 兩者合併,就能完整涵蓋 Kubernetes audit logs 以及來自同一批節點的 OS/網路/檔案遙測資料,完全符合題目需求。至於告警機制,AWS 官方文件記載的做法('Set up GuardDuty finding alerts through SNS')是建立一個比對 GuardDuty finding 事件的 EventBridge 規則,並將目標設為附加 email 訂閱的 SNS 主題 - 這個流程不需要 Lambda 函式,因為 SNS 原生支援 email 作為訂閱協定,EventBridge 也能直接把 SNS 當作目標。這證實選項 C 的架構從頭到尾都是正確的。\n\n選項 A(Security Hub)彙整的是安全態勢檢查/控制項的結果(包含一些 EKS 組態檢查),但不會對 EKS audit logs 做行為分析,也不提供 OS/網路/檔案的執行時期遙測資料 - 這是 GuardDuty Runtime Monitoring 的能力,不是 Security Hub 的。選項 B 混用了不相關的服務:Amazon Inspector 做的是容器映像的漏洞/CVE 掃描(不是 audit log 或執行時期行為監控),Amazon Detective 是用於事後調查與視覺化既有 finding 與 log 的工具,本身不會從 EKS audit logs 產生即時威脅偵測;而讓 Lambda 去解析原始 CloudWatch Logs 來偵測「安全風險」,等於要自行打造 GuardDuty 已內建的偵測邏輯。選項 D 只是把 EKS audit logs 送進 CloudWatch Logs,並在有新 log 產生時觸發告警 - 這只是針對 log 量/存在與否發出警示,並非針對任何實際偵測到的安全風險,因此無法滿足偵測風險的核心需求。只有選項 C 同時針對 audit log 與 OS/網路/檔案事件需求使用了專門設計的 AWS 威脅偵測服務,並具備原生的 SNS email 傳遞路徑。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"AWS Security Hub aggregates compliance/configuration findings from security standards and integrated services; it does not analyze EKS audit logs behaviorally and does not provide OS, network, or file-level runtime telemetry from EKS nodes/containers, which is a GuardDuty Runtime Monitoring capability, not Security Hub's.","why_zh":"AWS Security Hub 彙整的是安全標準與整合服務產生的合規/組態 finding;它不會對 EKS audit logs 做行為分析,也不提供來自 EKS 節點/容器的 OS、網路或檔案層級執行時期遙測資料,這是 GuardDuty Runtime Monitoring 的能力,並非 Security Hub 具備的功能。"},{"letter":"B","why_en":"Amazon Inspector performs vulnerability/CVE scanning of container images, not audit log or runtime behavior analysis. Amazon Detective is a post-hoc investigation/visualization tool that does not natively analyze EKS audit logs to generate its own real-time findings, and using Lambda to parse raw CloudWatch Logs requires building custom threat-detection logic instead of using a purpose-built detection service.","why_zh":"Amazon Inspector 執行的是容器映像的漏洞/CVE 掃描,並非 audit log 或執行時期行為分析。Amazon Detective 是用於事後調查與視覺化的工具,本身不會原生分析 EKS audit logs 來產生即時 finding;而用 Lambda 解析原始 CloudWatch Logs,等同要自行建置威脅偵測邏輯,而非使用專門設計的偵測服務。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"This design only alerts whenever new EKS audit log data is delivered to CloudWatch Logs (a volume/existence trigger), not when an actual security risk is identified. It also does not address OS, networking, or file event monitoring at all, so it fails both core requirements of the question.","why_zh":"這個設計只會在 EKS audit logs 有新資料送進 CloudWatch Logs 時觸發告警(屬於資料量/存在性的觸發條件),並非在偵測到實際安全風險時才告警。它也完全沒有處理 OS、網路或檔案事件的監控,因此無法滿足題目的兩項核心需求。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/guardduty/latest/ug/guardduty-finding-types-eks-audit-logs.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/guardduty/latest/ug/runtime-monitoring-collected-events.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/guardduty/latest/ug/how-runtime-monitoring-works-eks.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/guardduty/latest/ug/guardduty_settingup.html"]}},{"id":85,"question_en":"A company plans to create Amazon S3 buckets to store log data. All the S3 buckets will have versioning enabled and will use the S3 Standard storage class. A security engineer needs to implement a solution that protects objects in the S3 buckets from deletion for 90 days. The solution must ensure that no object can be deleted during this time period, even by an administrator or the AWS account root user. Which solution will meet these requirements?","question_zh":"一家公司计划创建 Amazon S3 存储桶来存储日志数据。所有 S3 存储桶都将启用版本控制，并使 用 S3 标准存储类别。 安全工程师需要实施一项解决方案，以保护S3存储桶中的对象在90天内不被删除。该方案必须确保 在此期间任何对象都无法被删除，即使管理员或AWS账户根用户也无法删除。 哪种解决方案能满足这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Enable S3 Object Lock in governance mode. Set a legal hold of 90 days.","B":"Enable S3 Object Lock in governance mode. Set a retention period of 90 days.","C":"Enable S3 Object Lock in compliance mode. Set a retention period of 90 days.","D":"Create an S3 Glacier Vault Lock policy that prevents deletion for 90 days."},"options_zh":{"A":"启用 S3 对象锁定的治理模式，并设置 90 天的法律保留期。","B":"启用 S3 对象锁定的治理模式，并设置保留期为 90 天。","C":"启用 S3 对象锁定的合规模式，并设置保留期为 90 天。","D":"创建一个 S3 Glacier 存储库锁定策略，防止在 90 天内删除。"},"answer":["C"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Storage"],"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選","research":{"verdict":["C"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"both","explanation_en":"S3 Object Lock in Compliance mode with a 90-day retention period is the only option that meets the strict requirement that no one — not even an administrator or the AWS account root user — can delete the objects during the retention window. AWS documentation states explicitly: 'In compliance mode, a protected object version can't be overwritten or deleted by any user, including the root user in your AWS account. When an object is locked in compliance mode, its retention mode can't be changed, and its retention period can't be shortened... The only way to delete an object under the compliance mode before its retention date expires is to delete the associated AWS account.' A fixed 90-day retention period is set via a Retain Until Date on the object (or bucket default), which maps precisely to the requirement. Governance mode, by contrast, can be overridden by any principal granted the s3:BypassGovernanceRetention permission (which an administrator would typically have), so it fails the 'even by an administrator' bar.","explanation_zh":"S3 Object Lock 搭配 Compliance mode 並設定 90 天的 retention period,是唯一符合「即使是管理員或 AWS account root user 也不能刪除物件」這項嚴格要求的方案。AWS 官方文件明確指出:在 compliance mode 下,受保護的 object version 無法被任何使用者覆寫或刪除,包括 AWS 帳戶的 root user;物件一旦以 compliance mode 鎖定,其 retention mode 無法變更,retention period 也無法縮短。在保留期限到期前,唯一能刪除該物件的方式是刪除整個 AWS 帳戶。設定固定的 90 天 retention period(透過物件或 bucket 預設的 Retain Until Date)正好對應題目要求。相對地,governance mode 可以被任何擁有 s3:BypassGovernanceRetention 權限的使用者(管理員通常會有此權限)覆寫,因此無法滿足「即使管理員也不能刪除」的門檻。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"Governance mode can be bypassed by users with the s3:BypassGovernanceRetention permission (including admins), so it fails the 'even by an administrator' requirement. Additionally, a legal hold has no fixed duration — AWS docs state it 'has no expiration date' and remains until explicitly removed, so it cannot be set to a specific '90 days' as the option describes.","why_zh":"Governance mode 可以被具有 s3:BypassGovernanceRetention 權限的使用者(包括管理員)繞過,因此不符合「即使管理員也無法刪除」的要求。此外,legal hold 並沒有固定期限——AWS 文件說明 legal hold『沒有到期日』,會一直存在直到被明確移除,因此無法像選項所述那樣設定成「90 天」。"},{"letter":"B","why_en":"Governance mode retention periods can still be overridden by privileged users with the s3:BypassGovernanceRetention permission, meaning administrators (and by extension anyone granted that permission) could delete the object before the 90 days expire. This does not meet the 'even by an administrator or root user' requirement.","why_zh":"Governance mode 的 retention period 仍然可以被擁有 s3:BypassGovernanceRetention 權限的使用者覆寫,這意味著管理員(或任何被授予該權限的人)仍可在 90 天到期前刪除物件,不符合「即使管理員或 root user 也不能刪除」的要求。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"S3 Glacier Vault Lock applies to S3 Glacier vaults, not to S3 Standard storage class buckets. Since the objects are stored in S3 Standard (not S3 Glacier), a Vault Lock policy is not applicable here.","why_zh":"S3 Glacier Vault Lock 適用於 S3 Glacier 的 vault,而不是 S3 Standard 儲存類別的 bucket。由於題目中的物件是存放在 S3 Standard(而非 S3 Glacier),因此 Vault Lock policy 在此情境下並不適用。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonS3/latest/userguide/object-lock-overview.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonS3/latest/userguide/object-lock.html"]}},{"id":86,"question_en":"A security engineer needs to develop a process to investigate and respond to potential security events on a company’s Amazon EC2 instances. All the EC2 instances are backed by Amazon EBS. The company uses AWS Systems Manager to manage all the EC2 instances and has installed Systems Manager Agent on all the EC2 instances. The process that the security engineer is developing must comply with AWS security best practices and must meet the following requirements: • A compromised EC2 instance’s volatile memory and non-volatile memory must be preserved for forensic purposes. • A compromised EC2 instance’s metadata must be updated with corresponding incident ticket information. • A compromised EC2 instance must remain online during the investigation but must be isolated to prevent the spread of malware. • Any investigative activity during the collection of volatile data must be captured as part of the process. Which combination of steps should the security engineer take to meet these requirements with the LEAST operational overhead? (Select THREE.)","question_zh":"安全工程师需要制定一个流程，用于调查和响应公司Amazon EC2实例上的潜在安全事件。所有EC2 实例均使用Amazon EBS进行支持。该公司使用AWS Systems Manager来管理所有EC2实例，并已在 所有EC2实例上安装了Systems Manager Agent。 安全工程师正在开发的流程必须符合 AWS 安全最佳实践，并满足以下要求： • 为进行取证，受感染的EC2实例的易失性内存和非易失性内存必须予以保留。 • 被入侵的EC2实例的元数据必须更新为相应的事件工单信息。 在调查期间，受感染的EC2实例必须保持在线状态，但需进行隔离以防止恶意软件扩散。 在收集易失性数据期间，任何调查活动都必须作为流程的一部分被记录下来。 安全工程师应采取哪些步骤组合，才能以最少的操作开销满足这些要求？（选择三项。）","options_en":{"A":"Gather any relevant metadata for the compromised EC2 instance. Enable termination protection. Isolate the instance by updating the instance’s security groups to restrict access. Detach the instance from any Auto Scaling groups that the instance is a member of. Deregister the instance from any Elastic Load Balancing resources.","B":"Gather any relevant metadata for the compromised EC2 instance. Enable termination protection. Move the instance to an isolation subnet that denies all source and destination traffic. Associate the instance with the subnet to restrict access. Detach the instance from any Auto Scaling groups that the instance is a member of. Deregister the instance from any Elastic Load Balancing resources.","C":"Use Systems Manager Run Command to invoke scripts that collect volatile data.","D":"Establish a Linux SSH or Windows Remote Desktop Protocol session to the compromised EC2 instance to invoke scripts that collect volatile data.","E":"Create a snapshot of the compromised EC2 instance’s EBS volume for follow-up investigations. Tag the instance with any relevant metadata and incident ticket information.","F":"Create a Systems Manager State Manager association to generate an EBS volume snapshot of the compromised EC2 instance. Tag the instance with any relevant metadata and incident ticket information."},"options_zh":{"A":"收集受感染EC2实例的相关元数据。启用终止保护。通过更新实例的安全组以限制访问，将该 实例隔离。将实例从其所属的任何自动扩展组中分离。从任何弹性负载均衡资源中注销该实 例。","B":"收集受感染EC2实例的相关元数据。启用终止保护。将该实例移至一个拒绝所有源和目标流量 的隔离子网中，并将实例与该子网关联以限制访问。从实例所属的任何自动伸缩组中分离该 实例。将实例从任何弹性负载均衡资源中注销。","C":"使用 Systems Manager 运行命令来调用收集易失性数据的脚本。","D":"建立到受感染EC2实例的Linux SSH或Windows远程桌面协议会话，以调用收集易失性数据的脚 本。","E":"为受感染的EC2实例的EBS卷创建快照，以便后续调查。为该实例添加相关的元数据和事件工 单信息标签。","F":"创建一个 Systems Manager 状态管理器关联，以生成受感染 EC2 实例的 EBS 卷快照。为该实例 添加相关的元数据标签和事件工单信息。"},"answer":["A","C","E"],"multi":true,"vote":{},"tags":["Storage","Compute","Monitoring/Ops"],"difficulty":2,"diff_why":"複選","research":{"verdict":["A","C","E"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"both","explanation_en":"Independently verified against three official AWS sources and the verdict is confirmed as A, C, E. First, isolation: AWS's own GuardDuty remediation guide for a potentially compromised EC2 instance (docs.aws.amazon.com/guardduty/.../compromised-ec2.html) instructs responders to create a dedicated 'Isolation' security group with no 0.0.0.0/0 rules, associate it with the instance, and remove other security groups - i.e., isolate via security groups while the instance keeps running. The AWS-QuarantineEC2Instance Systems Manager Automation runbook implements this exact pattern end-to-end: it gathers instance metadata, verifies/detaches the instance from any Auto Scaling group, creates a snapshot of the root EBS volume, waits for it to complete, and then assigns the isolation security group - all without stopping the instance or touching its subnet/ENI. That matches option A precisely, including the ASG-detach and (per standard containment guidance) ELB-deregistration steps. Option B's 'move to an isolation subnet' is not the AWS-documented mechanism and requires heavier network-interface/subnet changes, so it fails the 'least operational overhead' bar. Second, volatile data collection: AWS Security Incident Response's 'EC2 Triage' capability (docs.aws.amazon.com/security-ir/.../containment-with-ec2-triage-template.html) is explicitly built on Systems Manager Run Command (ssm:SendCommand plus ssm:GetCommandInvocation) so responders can 'collect volatile forensic data from running Amazon EC2 instances... without direct instance access.' The Run Command invocation history itself is the auditable record of investigative activity, satisfying the requirement that activity during volatile-data collection be captured. Option C matches this exactly. Option D (interactive SSH/RDP) both requires direct network access - which conflicts with the isolation requirement - and produces no equivalent centralized, queryable audit trail, so it is inferior to C. Third, non-volatile preservation plus metadata: the AWS-QuarantineEC2Instance runbook itself performs a direct, one-time ec2:CreateSnapshot call at the moment of containment, and standard incident-response guidance tags the instance immediately with case/ticket metadata as an ad hoc action for that specific incident - this is option E. Systems Manager State Manager (docs.aws.amazon.com/systems-manager/.../state-manager-about.html) is documented as a tool for maintaining a recurring/scheduled/persistent configuration state on managed nodes (e.g., periodic patching or compliance scans), not for a single incident-specific snapshot-and-tag action; standing up an association document plus a schedule is strictly more operational overhead than directly calling CreateSnapshot and CreateTags, so option F is a heavier, worse-fit version of E. All three independent checks corroborate the first analyst: the correct combination is A, C, E.","explanation_zh":"已根據三份官方 AWS 文件獨立查證,確認答案為 A、C、E。首先是隔離(isolation):AWS 官方 GuardDuty「可能已遭入侵的 EC2 執行個體」修復指南(docs.aws.amazon.com/guardduty/.../compromised-ec2.html)明確指示應變人員建立一個沒有 0.0.0.0/0 規則的專屬 Isolation 安全群組,將其指派給該實例,並移除其他安全群組 - 也就是透過安全群組隔離,同時讓實例維持運作。AWS-QuarantineEC2Instance 這個 Systems Manager Automation runbook 完整落實了這套流程:先收集實例中繼資料,確認/將實例自 Auto Scaling group 卸離,為根 EBS 磁碟區建立快照並等待其完成,接著才指派隔離安全群組 - 全程不需停止實例,也不動到其子網路/ENI。這正好對應選項 A,亦包含卸離 ASG、以及(依標準圍堵指引)自 ELB 取消註冊等步驟。選項 B 的「移到隔離子網」並非 AWS 文件記載的機制,且需要更繁重的網路介面/子網變更,因此不符合「維運成本最低」的要求。其次是揮發性資料蒐集:AWS Security Incident Response 的「EC2 Triage」能力(docs.aws.amazon.com/security-ir/.../containment-with-ec2-triage-template.html)明確建立在 Systems Manager Run Command(ssm:SendCommand 搭配 ssm:GetCommandInvocation)之上,讓應變人員能「在不直接存取實例的情況下,從運作中的 EC2 實例蒐集揮發性鑑識資料」。Run Command 的呼叫歷程本身即是可稽核的調查活動紀錄,滿足題目要求「蒐集揮發性資料期間的調查活動須被記錄」。選項 C 正對應此做法。選項 D(互動式 SSH/RDP)不僅需要直接的網路存取、與隔離要求相衝突,也無法產生同等集中且可查詢的稽核軌跡,因此劣於 C。第三是非揮發性資料保存與中繼資料:AWS-QuarantineEC2Instance runbook 本身就是在圍堵當下直接呼叫一次性的 ec2:CreateSnapshot,而標準事件應變指引也會針對該特定事件,以臨機的方式立即為實例標記案件/事件單中繼資料 - 這正是選項 E。Systems Manager State Manager(docs.aws.amazon.com/systems-manager/.../state-manager-about.html)文件記載其用途是在受管節點上維持週期性/排程性/持續性的組態狀態(例如定期修補或合規掃描),並非用於單一事件專屬的一次性快照與標籤動作;建立 association 文件並搭配排程,其維運成本必然高於直接呼叫 CreateSnapshot 與 CreateTags,因此選項 F 是 E 的較繁重、較不合適版本。三項獨立查證皆與第一位分析者的結論一致:正確組合為 A、C、E。","distractors":[{"letter":"B","why_en":"AWS's documented isolation mechanism (GuardDuty remediation guide and the AWS-QuarantineEC2Instance runbook) uses a dedicated 'deny-all' security group assigned to the running instance, not a network/subnet move. Relocating the instance to an isolation subnet requires changing its network interface/subnet association - heavier operational overhead - and is not the AWS-documented least-overhead pattern for keeping the instance online while isolated.","why_zh":"AWS 文件記載的隔離機制(GuardDuty 修復指南與 AWS-QuarantineEC2Instance runbook)是為運作中的實例指派一個『全部拒絕』的專屬安全群組,而非搬遷網路/子網。把實例移到隔離子網需要變更其網路介面/子網關聯,維運成本更高,並非 AWS 文件所載、能讓實例維持上線同時隔離、且維運成本最低的做法。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"Establishing an interactive SSH/RDP session requires direct network access to the instance, which conflicts with the isolation requirement, and does not produce the centralized, queryable audit trail (ssm:GetCommandInvocation / Run Command history) that Systems Manager Run Command provides to satisfy the requirement to capture investigative activity.","why_zh":"建立互動式 SSH/RDP 連線需要對實例的直接網路存取,這與隔離要求相衝突,也無法產生 Systems Manager Run Command 所提供、可集中查詢的稽核軌跡(ssm:GetCommandInvocation / Run Command 歷程),因而無法滿足『記錄調查活動』的要求。"},{"letter":"F","why_en":"AWS documents Systems Manager State Manager associations as a mechanism for maintaining recurring or scheduled configuration state on managed nodes, not for a one-off, incident-specific EBS snapshot and unique ticket-tagging action. Standing up an association (document plus schedule) adds setup and ongoing operational overhead compared to directly calling CreateSnapshot and tagging the instance, which is exactly what the AWS-QuarantineEC2Instance runbook itself does.","why_zh":"AWS 文件將 Systems Manager State Manager association 定位為在受管節點上維持週期性或排程性組態狀態的機制,並非用於單一事件專屬的一次性 EBS 快照與獨特事件單標籤動作。建立 association(文件加排程)相較於直接呼叫 CreateSnapshot 並為實例加上標籤(這正是 AWS-QuarantineEC2Instance runbook 本身的做法),會增加額外的設定與持續維運成本。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/systems-manager-automation-runbooks/latest/userguide/aws-quarantineec2instance.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/guardduty/latest/ug/compromised-ec2.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/security-ir/latest/userguide/containment-with-ec2-triage-template.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/systems-manager/latest/userguide/state-manager-about.html"]}},{"id":87,"question_en":"A company must immediately disable compromised IAM users across all AWS accounts and collect all actions performed by the user in the last 7 days. Which solution will meet these requirements?","question_zh":"公司必须立即在所有AWS账户中禁用被入侵的IAM用户，并收集该用户在过去7天内执行的所 有操作。 哪种解决方案能满足这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Disable the IAM user and query CloudTrail logs in Amazon S3 using Athena.","B":"Remove IAM policies and query logs in Security Hub.","C":"Remove permission sets and query logs using CloudWatch Logs Insights.","D":"Disable the user in IAM Identity Center and query the organizational event data store."},"options_zh":{"A":"禁用 IAM 用户，并使用 Athena 查询 Amazon S3 中的 CloudTrail 日志。","B":"在安全中心中删除 IAM 策略和查询日志。","C":"使用 CloudWatch Logs Insights 删除权限集和查询日志。","D":"在 IAM Identity Center 中禁用用户并查询组织事件数据存储。"},"answer":["D"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Security/IAM","Storage","Monitoring/Ops","Analytics"],"difficulty":3,"diff_why":"官方文件判定需斟酌・題庫與社群皆錯","research":{"verdict":["A"],"confidence":"medium","agrees_with":"neither","explanation_en":"CORRECTED from D to A. This question turns on precise AWS terminology, and the question stem is explicit: it says the compromised entities are 'IAM users.' AWS's own IAM Identity Center documentation is emphatic that this is a distinct, non-interchangeable term from an 'IAM Identity Center user': the 'Disable user access' page states, as an Important callout, that 'IAM Identity Center users, groups, and user credentials are different from IAM users, groups, and IAM user credentials. If you are looking for instructions on deactivating users in IAM, see Managing IAM users' in the IAM User Guide. AWS is explicitly telling readers not to reach for IAM Identity Center when the entity in question is an 'IAM user' — which is exactly the mistake option D makes. Disabling a record inside IAM Identity Center does not touch an IAM user's password or access keys at all; it acts on a completely separate identity store, so D fails the 'disable compromised IAM users' requirement on its own terms, regardless of how convenient the 'across all AWS accounts' framing sounds. Option A matches the stated identity type exactly: IAM's own documentation ('To deactivate an access key for an IAM user' in the IAM User Guide) and AWS's official incident-response playbook (aws-samples/aws-customer-playbook-framework, Compromised_IAM_Credentials.md) both describe remediating a compromised IAM user by disabling console password sign-in and deactivating access keys — i.e., literally 'Disable the IAM user.' For the audit half of the requirement, IAM users are account-scoped by definition ('An IAM user is an entity that you create in your AWS account'), so a fleet of compromised IAM users spread across an AWS Organization is exactly what CloudTrail's organization trail feature is built to cover: a single trail, created once from the management or delegated-administrator account by selecting 'Enable for all accounts in my organization,' delivers every member account's CloudTrail logs into one S3 bucket, and AWS documents building an Amazon Athena table over that organization-wide trail data (partitioned by account ID) to run a single SQL query across every account's activity — precisely 'query CloudTrail logs in Amazon S3 using Athena,' filterable to the last 7 days by eventTime. B fails both halves: removing IAM policies does not disable sign-in or invalidate access keys (IAM's docs show that removing permissions 'does not change...or prevent them from accessing the console using an assumed role,' so credentials stay live), and Security Hub aggregates findings, not raw CloudTrail events, so it cannot answer 'all actions performed...in the last 7 days.' C also mismatches the identity type in the question — 'permission sets' are an IAM Identity Center account-assignment construct that IAM users simply don't have — and even within IAM Identity Center's own world, AWS's session-revocation guidance says removing permission set assignments alone only 'prevents the user from assuming any additional IAM roles' without ending an already-active AWS access portal session, so it isn't truly immediate; CloudWatch Logs Insights also has no native cross-account/cross-organization query capability comparable to an organization trail or CloudTrail Lake. D has the same identity-type mismatch as C, and even on IAM Identity Center's own terms it is not fully immediate: AWS's official guidance ('Revoke active IAM role sessions created by permission sets') states that if 'a user has an active AWS access portal session and you disable the user, they can continue to assume new roles until you remove their access' — true lockout needs an SCP deny statement plus explicit session deletion, not just 'disable user.' CloudTrail Lake's organization event data store is also being closed to new customers as of May 31, 2026 per AWS's own availability-change notice, whereas the organization-trail-plus-Athena pattern in A remains the fully current, broadly documented default for querying CloudTrail across every account in an organization. Taken together, A is the only option whose 'disable' action actually acts on the identity type the question names (IAM users) and whose log-collection action is the documented, purpose-built mechanism for querying IAM-user-generated CloudTrail events across an entire AWS Organization.","explanation_zh":"更正為 A(原為 D)。這題的關鍵在於 AWS 精確的專有名詞:題目明確說遭入侵的實體是「IAM users」。AWS 官方 IAM Identity Center 文件明確強調,這與「IAM Identity Center user」是兩個完全不同、不可互換的名詞:『Disable user access』頁面以 Important 提示寫道:『IAM Identity Center users, groups, and user credentials are different from IAM users, groups, and IAM user credentials. If you are looking for instructions on deactivating users in IAM, see Managing IAM users』(於 IAM User Guide)。AWS 等於是明確告訴讀者:當題目中的實體是「IAM user」時,不該去用 IAM Identity Center——而這正是選項 D 犯的錯誤。在 IAM Identity Center 內停用一筆使用者紀錄,完全不會影響某個 IAM user 的密碼或存取金鑰;它作用在完全不同的身分儲存區,因此 D 從根本上就無法滿足「停用遭入侵的 IAM users」這項要求,無論「across all AWS accounts」聽起來多麼契合都一樣。選項 A 則精準對應題目所述的身分類型:IAM 官方文件(IAM User Guide 中『To deactivate an access key for an IAM user』)以及 AWS 官方事件應變手冊(aws-samples/aws-customer-playbook-framework 的 Compromised_IAM_Credentials.md)都描述,要處理遭入侵的 IAM user,做法是停用主控台密碼登入並停用存取金鑰——這正是字面上的「Disable the IAM user」。至於稽核那一半的要求,IAM user 依定義就是以帳戶為範圍的實體(『An IAM user is an entity that you create in your AWS account』),因此一批分散在 AWS Organization 各帳戶中、遭入侵的 IAM users,正好對應 CloudTrail organization trail 這項功能所涵蓋的情境:只要在管理帳戶或委派管理帳戶建立一次 trail 並勾選『Enable for all accounts in my organization』,就能將所有成員帳戶的 CloudTrail 日誌集中送到單一 S3 儲存桶;AWS 也記載了如何針對這個涵蓋全組織的 trail 資料(以帳戶 ID 分區)建立 Amazon Athena 資料表,用單一 SQL 查詢涵蓋所有帳戶的活動——這正是『query CloudTrail logs in Amazon S3 using Athena』,並可用 eventTime 篩選最近 7 天。選項 B 兩項要求都不成立:移除 IAM 政策既不會停用登入,也不會讓存取金鑰失效(IAM 文件指出移除權限『does not change...or prevent them from accessing the console using an assumed role』,憑證仍然有效),而 Security Hub 彙整的是安全發現(findings),並非原始 CloudTrail 事件,無法回答『使用者過去 7 天內執行的所有動作』。選項 C 同樣與題目所述的身分類型不符——「permission sets」是 IAM Identity Center 的帳戶指派機制,IAM user 根本沒有這個概念;即使套用在 IAM Identity Center 的世界裡,AWS 的工作階段撤銷指引也指出,單純移除權限集指派只會『prevents the user from assuming any additional IAM roles』,並不會終止已經存在的 AWS access portal 工作階段,因此並非真正「立即」;CloudWatch Logs Insights 也沒有原生支援可媲美 organization trail 或 CloudTrail Lake 的跨帳戶/跨組織查詢能力。選項 D 與 C 有相同的身分類型錯配問題,而且即使套用在 IAM Identity Center 自身的脈絡下,也並非完全立即生效:AWS 官方指引(『Revoke active IAM role sessions created by permission sets』)明確指出,若『使用者已有作用中的 AWS access portal 工作階段,而您停用該使用者,該使用者在您移除其存取權之前,仍可繼續擔任新角色』——真正的完全鎖定需要 SCP 的 Deny 陳述式加上明確刪除工作階段,而不只是「disable user」。此外,CloudTrail Lake 的 organization event data store 依 AWS 官方的服務異動公告,將於 2026 年 5 月 31 日起停止開放新客戶申請,而選項 A 所用的 organization trail + Athena 模式仍是目前完全通用、文件記載更廣泛的預設做法,可用於查詢整個 AWS Organization 中所有帳戶的 CloudTrail 資料。綜合以上,A 是唯一一個「停用」動作真正作用在題目所指身分類型(IAM users)上、且「收集日誌」動作是官方記載、專為跨整個 AWS Organization 查詢 IAM-user 產生之 CloudTrail 事件而設計的選項。","distractors":[{"letter":"D","why_en":"Disabling 'the user in IAM Identity Center' acts on IAM Identity Center's own separate identity store, not on the 'IAM users' the question names — AWS's disableuser.html page explicitly warns that 'IAM Identity Center users, groups, and user credentials are different from IAM users, groups, and IAM user credentials' and points readers to 'Managing IAM users' in the IAM Guide for that different task. Even taken on its own terms, 'disable user' isn't fully immediate: AWS's official revoke-user-permissions.html guidance says a disabled user with an active AWS access portal session 'can continue to assume new roles until you remove their access' — true lockout needs an SCP deny plus explicit session deletion. CloudTrail Lake's organization event data store is functionally valid for org-wide querying but is being closed to new customers from May 31, 2026, per AWS's own availability-change notice, while the organization-trail-plus-Athena approach in A remains the current, broadly documented default for the identity type actually named in the question.","why_zh":"停用『the user in IAM Identity Center』作用在 IAM Identity Center 自己的身分儲存區,而不是題目所指的『IAM users』——AWS 的 disableuser.html 頁面明確警告『IAM Identity Center users, groups, and user credentials are different from IAM users, groups, and IAM user credentials』,並指示讀者若要處理 IAM 中的停用作業,應參閱 IAM Guide 的『Managing IAM users』。即使只看 IAM Identity Center 自身脈絡,『disable user』也並非完全立即生效:AWS 官方 revoke-user-permissions.html 指出,若停用的使用者已有作用中的 AWS access portal 工作階段,『該使用者在您移除其存取權之前,仍可繼續擔任新角色』——真正鎖定需要 SCP 的 Deny 陳述式加上明確刪除工作階段。CloudTrail Lake 的 organization event data store 在功能上確實能做到跨組織查詢,但依 AWS 官方服務異動公告,將於 2026 年 5 月 31 日起停止開放新客戶申請;相較之下,選項 A 的 organization trail + Athena 做法,對題目實際指名的身分類型(IAM users)而言,才是目前完全通用、文件記載更廣泛的預設做法。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"'Permission sets' are an IAM Identity Center account-assignment construct — an 'IAM user' as named in the question simply doesn't have permission sets, so this option doesn't even address the stated identity type. Even within IAM Identity Center, AWS's own session-revocation guidance says removing permission set assignments alone only 'prevents the user from assuming any additional IAM roles' and does not end an already-active AWS access portal session, so it isn't truly immediate. CloudWatch Logs Insights also has no built-in cross-account, cross-organization query capability equivalent to an organization trail or CloudTrail Lake, so it can't natively satisfy 'across all AWS accounts.'","why_zh":"『permission sets』是 IAM Identity Center 的帳戶指派機制——題目所指的『IAM user』根本沒有 permission sets,所以這個選項連題目所述的身分類型都沒對上。即使放在 IAM Identity Center 的脈絡下,AWS 官方的工作階段撤銷指引也指出,單純移除權限集指派只會『prevents the user from assuming any additional IAM roles』,並不會終止已存在的 AWS access portal 工作階段,因此並非真正「立即」。CloudWatch Logs Insights 也沒有原生支援可媲美 organization trail 或 CloudTrail Lake 的跨帳戶、跨組織查詢能力,無法直接滿足『across all AWS accounts』。"},{"letter":"B","why_en":"Removing IAM policies does not disable an IAM user's ability to sign in or use access keys — IAM's own documentation distinguishes 'disabling the password' from removing permissions, and removing permissions 'does not change their permissions or prevent them from accessing the console using an assumed role,' so long-term credentials stay live. Security Hub is a findings aggregator, not a CloudTrail log store — it does not retain raw event history and cannot answer 'all actions performed by the user in the last 7 days.'","why_zh":"移除 IAM 政策並不會停用某個 IAM user 的登入能力或存取金鑰使用權——IAM 官方文件將『停用密碼』與『移除權限』區分開來,移除權限『does not change their permissions or prevent them from accessing the console using an assumed role』,長期憑證依然有效。Security Hub 是安全發現(findings)彙整服務,並非 CloudTrail 日誌儲存區——它不保留原始事件歷史,無法回答『使用者過去 7 天內執行的所有動作』。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/IAM/latest/UserGuide/id_users.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/IAM/latest/UserGuide/access-keys-admin-managed.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/singlesignon/latest/userguide/disableuser.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/singlesignon/latest/userguide/revoke-user-permissions.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/awscloudtrail/latest/userguide/creating-an-organizational-trail-in-the-console.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/athena/latest/ug/create-cloudtrail-table-org-wide-trail.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/awscloudtrail/latest/userguide/cloudtrail-lake-organizations.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/guardduty/latest/ug/compromised-creds.html","https://github.com/aws-samples/aws-customer-playbook-framework/blob/main/docs/Compromised_IAM_Credentials.md"]}},{"id":88,"question_en":"A company sends Amazon RDS snapshots to two accounts as part of its disaster recovery (DR) plan. The snapshots must be encrypted. However, each account needs to be able to decrypt the snapshots in case of a DR event. Which solution will meet these requirements?","question_zh":"一家公司作为其灾难恢复（DR）计划的一部分，将 Amazon RDS 快照发送到两个账户。这些快照必须经过加密，但每个账户 在发生灾难恢复事件时都必须能够解密这些快照。 哪种解决方案能满足这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Use the default AWS Key Management Service (AWS KMS) key to generate the snapshots. Create an AWS Lambda function that copies the KMS encryption key to the two accounts.","B":"Use an AWS Key Management Service (AWS KMS) customer managed key to generate the snapshots. Create an AWS Lambda function that imports the KMS key in the two accounts.","C":"Use the default AWS Key Management Service (AWS KMS) key to generate the snapshots. Share the KMS key with the two accounts by using an IAM principal that has the proper KMS permissions in each account.","D":"Use an AWS Key Management Service (AWS KMS) customer managed key to generate the snapshots. Share the KMS key with the two accounts by using an IAM principal that has the proper KMS permissions in each account."},"options_zh":{"A":"使用默认的 AWS 密钥管理服务（AWS KMS）密钥生成快照。创建一个 AWS Lambda 函数，将 KMS 加密密钥复制到两 个账户中。","B":"使用 AWS 密钥管理服务（AWS KMS）的客户托管密钥来生成快照。创建一个 AWS Lambda 函数，用于在两个账户中导入 该 KMS 密钥。","C":"使用默认的 AWS 密钥管理服务（AWS KMS）密钥来生成快照。通过在每个账户中使用具有适当 KMS 权限的 IAM 主体， 将 KMS 密钥与两个账户共享。","D":"使用 AWS 密钥管理服务（AWS KMS）的客户托管密钥来生成快照。通过在每个账户中使用具 有适当 KMS 权限的 IAM 主体，将 KMS 密钥与两个账户共享。"},"answer":["D"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Disaster Recovery/HA","Security/IAM","Compute","Database"],"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選","research":{"verdict":["D"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"both","explanation_en":"AWS RDS documentation on \"Sharing encrypted snapshots for Amazon RDS\" explicitly states: \"You can't share a snapshot that has been encrypted using the default KMS key of the AWS account that shared the snapshot.\" This immediately rules out any option built on the default (AWS managed) KMS key, eliminating A and C. The same page documents the official workaround for cross-account encrypted-snapshot DR sharing: (1) create a customer managed KMS key in the source account and, while creating it, grant access to it for the other AWS account(s) — this writes a statement into the key's resource-based key policy; (2) copy the snapshot using that customer managed key and share the copy; (3) in the target account, copy the shared snapshot using a KMS key that belongs to the target account (so each account can independently decrypt/re-encrypt and restore). The AWS KMS documentation \"Allowing users in other accounts to use a KMS key\" confirms the underlying mechanism verbatim: \"Cross-account access requires permission in the key policy of the KMS key and in an IAM policy in the external user's account.\" Option D's phrasing — a customer managed key shared \"by using an IAM principal that has the proper KMS permissions in each account\" — is a compressed but accurate description of this exact two-sided mechanism (key policy grant to the external account + IAM policy delegation to specific principals within it). There is no AWS feature that \"copies\" a KMS key to another account (A) or \"imports\" a KMS key into another account (B) — KMS key import (BYOK) refers to bringing your own external key material into a single KMS key resource; it is unrelated to cross-account sharing and does not replicate or move the key itself. Therefore D is the only option that correctly pairs a customer managed key with the documented cross-account key-policy/IAM-permission model, satisfying the requirement that each account can independently decrypt the snapshot for DR.","explanation_zh":"Amazon RDS 文件「Sharing encrypted snapshots for Amazon RDS」明確指出:「You can't share a snapshot that has been encrypted using the default KMS key of the AWS account that shared the snapshot.」(無法分享以帳戶預設 KMS key 加密的快照)。這直接排除了任何以 default AWS KMS key 為基礎的選項,也就是 A 與 C。同一份文件記載了跨帳戶分享加密快照(DR 情境)的官方解法:(1) 在來源帳戶建立一個 customer managed KMS key,並在建立時就授權給目標帳戶(這會在該 key 的 resource-based key policy 中寫入一條授權陳述);(2) 使用該 customer managed key 複製快照,並分享該副本;(3) 在目標帳戶中,使用屬於目標帳戶自己的 KMS key 再次複製該分享的快照(讓每個帳戶都能各自解密/重新加密並還原)。AWS KMS 文件「Allowing users in other accounts to use a KMS key」逐字確認了底層機制:「Cross-account access requires permission in the key policy of the KMS key and in an IAM policy in the external user's account.」(跨帳戶存取需要 KMS key 的 key policy 授權,同時外部帳戶也需要有 IAM policy 授權)。選項 D 的描述——customer managed key 並「透過在每個帳戶中賦予具備適當 KMS 權限的 IAM principal 來分享」——正是這種雙邊機制(對外部帳戶的 key policy 授權 + 該帳戶內特定 IAM principal 的 IAM policy 委派)的精簡但準確描述。AWS 並沒有所謂「將 KMS key 複製」到另一個帳戶(選項 A)或「將 KMS key 匯入」另一個帳戶(選項 B)的功能——KMS 的 key import(BYOK)指的是將自己的外部金鑰材料匯入單一 KMS key 資源,與跨帳戶分享完全無關,也不會複製或搬移金鑰本身。因此 D 是唯一正確地將 customer managed key 與官方文件記載的跨帳戶 key policy/IAM 權限模型結合的選項,滿足每個帳戶都能各自解密快照以供 DR 使用的需求。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"RDS explicitly disallows sharing snapshots encrypted with the default AWS managed KMS key across accounts (\"You can't share a snapshot that has been encrypted using the default KMS key of the AWS account that shared the snapshot\"). There is also no Lambda-based or any other AWS mechanism to \"copy\" a KMS encryption key to another account — KMS keys are regional, non-exportable resources; only access (via key policy) can be shared, never the key itself.","why_zh":"RDS 文件明確規定,以預設 AWS managed KMS key 加密的快照無法跨帳戶分享(「You can't share a snapshot that has been encrypted using the default KMS key of the AWS account that shared the snapshot」)。此外也沒有任何(包括透過 Lambda)AWS 機制可以將 KMS 加密金鑰「複製」到另一個帳戶——KMS key 是區域性且不可匯出的資源,只能透過 key policy 分享「存取權」,絕不會搬移金鑰本身。"},{"letter":"B","why_en":"Using a customer managed key is directionally correct, but the described mechanism — a Lambda function that \"imports\" the KMS key into the two accounts — mischaracterizes AWS KMS. Key import (BYOK, importing external key material) is used to bring your own key material into a single KMS key resource; it has nothing to do with replicating or sharing a key across accounts, and no such cross-account import mechanism exists in AWS KMS.","why_zh":"使用 customer managed key 的方向正確,但描述的機制——用 Lambda 函式將 KMS key「匯入」兩個帳戶——誤解了 AWS KMS 的運作方式。Key import(自帶金鑰材料,BYOK)是指將外部金鑰材料匯入單一 KMS key 資源,與跨帳戶複製或分享金鑰完全無關,AWS KMS 也不存在這種跨帳戶匯入機制。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"Sharing via an IAM principal with proper KMS permissions in each account correctly describes the cross-account access mechanism, but it is paired here with the default AWS managed KMS key, which RDS explicitly forbids sharing across accounts. The correct key type for this workflow must be a customer managed key, not the default key.","why_zh":"透過在每個帳戶中賦予具備適當 KMS 權限的 IAM principal 來分享,確實正確描述了跨帳戶存取機制,但這裡搭配的是預設 AWS managed KMS key,而 RDS 文件明確規定此類快照無法跨帳戶分享。此工作流程正確的金鑰類型必須是 customer managed key,而非預設金鑰。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonRDS/latest/UserGuide/share-encrypted-snapshot.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/kms/latest/developerguide/key-policy-modifying-external-accounts.html"]}},{"id":89,"question_en":"A company hosts its public website on Amazon EC2 instances behind an Application Load Balancer (ALB). The website is experiencing a global DDoS attack from a specific IoT device brand that uses a unique user agent. A security engineer is creating an AWS WAF web ACL and will associate it with the ALB. Which rule statement will mitigate the current attack and future attacks from these IoT devices without blocking legitimate customers?","question_zh":"一家公司将其公共网站托管在 Amazon EC2 实例上，并置于应用负载均衡器（ALB）之后。该网站 正遭受来自某个特定物联网设备品牌的全球性 DDoS 攻击，该品牌使用了唯一的用户代理标识。安 全工程师正在创建 AWS WAF 网站访问控制列表（web ACL），并计划将其与 ALB 关联。 哪条规则语句可以在不阻止合法客户的情况下，缓解当前及未来来自这些物联网设备的攻击？","options_en":{"A":"Use an IP set match rule statement.","B":"Use a geographic match rule statement.","C":"Use a rate-based rule statement.","D":"Use a string match rule statement on the user agent."},"options_zh":{"A":"使用IP集合匹配规则语句。","B":"使用地理匹配规则语句。","C":"使用基于速率的规则语句。","D":"对用户代理使用字符串匹配规则语句。"},"answer":["D"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Networking/DNS","Security/IAM","Compute"],"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選","research":{"verdict":["D"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"both","explanation_en":"The distinguishing signal in the scenario is a unique User-Agent string sent by one specific IoT device brand, and the requirement is to stop both the current wave and any future traffic from these devices without impacting legitimate customers. AWS WAF's string match rule statement (API name ByteMatchStatement) is purpose-built for this: the AWS documentation states you can 'look for a specific string ... as an exact match for the request's User-agent header,' inspecting the User-Agent header and comparing it against a specified string using Exactly matches, Starts with, Ends with, Contains string, or Contains word conditions. Configuring this rule to match/block on the IoT brand's User-Agent value directly targets the actual attack signature described in the question, works regardless of how many source IPs or countries the botnet uses, and continues to work against future attacks from the same device brand as long as the identifying User-Agent token is present, while leaving normal browser-based customer traffic (which has different User-Agent values) untouched. This exact rule type is walked through in AWS's console tutorial for building a string match condition against the user-agent field. The other three options do not fit this fact pattern as well: (A) An IP set match statement requires enumerating and maintaining a list of IP addresses, but a global DDoS from an IoT botnet involves large numbers of shifting, unpredictable IPs across many networks/ISPs, making an IP allow/deny list impractical to build and keep current, and it ignores the one concrete signal given (the User-Agent) entirely. (B) A geographic match statement blocks/allows traffic only by country of request origin, which is far too coarse: legitimate customers and the compromised/attacking IoT devices can be located in the very same countries, so this control would either fail to stop the attack or collaterally block real customers. (C) A rate-based rule statement counts and throttles requests per aggregation key (by default, source IP address) once they exceed a request-count threshold over an evaluation window; it manages volumetric flooding but does not natively key off the User-Agent value, so a slower/distributed attack from the IoT brand could stay under the rate limit and pass through, while legitimate high-traffic clients sharing an IP (e.g., behind NAT/CGNAT) could be throttled unnecessarily. Because the question's attack signature is specifically the User-Agent string, and only option D directly and durably filters on that signature, D is the single correct answer, confirming the first analyst's verdict.","explanation_zh":"此情境中可辨識的攻擊特徵,是某個 IoT 裝置品牌所發送的獨特 User-Agent 字串,而題目要求同時阻擋目前這波攻擊與未來同品牌裝置的攻擊,且不影響合法客戶。AWS WAF 的 string match rule statement(API 名稱為 ByteMatchStatement)正是為此設計:AWS 官方文件明確指出可以「在請求中尋找特定字串……例如做為請求 User-agent header 的完全比對(exact match)」,也就是檢查 User-Agent header,並以 Exactly matches、Starts with、Ends with、Contains string 或 Contains word 等條件與指定字串比對。將此規則設定為比對/封鎖該 IoT 品牌的 User-Agent 值,能直接針對題目描述的真正攻擊特徵,不論 botnet 使用多少來源 IP 或分佈於哪些國家都能生效,而且只要該識別性 User-Agent token 仍然存在,未來同品牌裝置的攻擊也會持續被擋下,同時完全不影響使用一般瀏覽器 User-Agent 的合法客戶流量。AWS 官方 console 教學中就完整示範了針對 user-agent 欄位建立這種 string match condition 規則的步驟。其餘三個選項都不如此貼合題目情境:(A) IP set match statement 需要列舉並維護一份 IP 位址清單,但全球性 IoT botnet DDoS 涉及跨多個網路/ISP、數量龐大且不斷變動的 IP,使得建立與維護黑白名單不切實際,而且完全沒有利用題目給出的唯一具體特徵(User-Agent)。(B) geographic match statement 僅依請求來源國家封鎖或允許流量,粒度過於粗略:合法客戶與遭入侵/發動攻擊的 IoT 裝置很可能位於相同國家,因此這種控制方式可能無法真正阻止攻擊,或誤傷合法客戶。(C) rate-based rule statement 是依聚合鍵(預設為來源 IP 位址)在評估視窗內對請求數超過門檻的流量進行計數與節流,能處理洪水式流量,但本質上不是依 User-Agent 值來判斷;若同品牌 IoT 裝置以較慢速或分散方式發動攻擊,仍可能低於速率門檻而通過,同時共用同一 IP(例如 NAT/CGNAT 後方)的合法高流量客戶反而可能被不必要地節流。由於題目的攻擊特徵明確是 User-Agent 字串,而四個選項中只有 D 能直接且持久地依此特徵過濾流量,因此 D 是唯一正確答案,與第一位分析者的結論一致。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"IP set match requires enumerating and maintaining a list of IP addresses. A global DDoS from an IoT botnet uses large numbers of shifting, unpredictable IPs across many networks, making this approach impractical to build and maintain, and it ignores the actual distinguishing signal (the unique User-Agent) given in the question.","why_zh":"IP set match 需要列舉並維護一份 IP 位址清單。來自全球 IoT botnet 的 DDoS 攻擊會使用大量、跨網路、不斷變動且難以預測的 IP,導致此作法難以建立與維護,而且完全沒有利用題目所給的真正區別特徵(獨特的 User-Agent)。"},{"letter":"B","why_en":"A geographic match rule blocks or allows traffic by country of origin, which is far too coarse a control. Legitimate customers and the attacking IoT devices could both be located in the same countries, so this would either fail to stop the attack or block legitimate traffic as collateral damage.","why_zh":"geographic match rule 是依請求來源國家封鎖或允許流量,控制粒度過於粗略。合法客戶與發起攻擊的 IoT 裝置可能位於相同國家,因此這種做法可能無法有效阻止攻擊,或誤傷合法流量。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"A rate-based rule statement throttles requests based on volume per aggregation key (by default, source IP), addressing flood-style traffic but not natively using the User-Agent signal. A slower or more distributed attack from the same IoT brand could stay under the rate threshold and pass through, while legitimate high-traffic customers sharing an IP could be throttled unnecessarily.","why_zh":"rate-based rule statement 是依聚合鍵(預設為來源 IP)的請求量進行節流,用於應對洪水式流量,但本質上並非依 User-Agent 特徵判斷。若同品牌 IoT 裝置以較慢或較分散的方式發起攻擊,可能仍低於速率門檻而通過,同時可能不必要地限制共用同一 IP 的合法高流量客戶。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/waf/latest/developerguide/waf-rule-statement-type-string-match.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/waf/latest/developerguide/waf-rule-statement-type-rate-based.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/waf/latest/developerguide/waf-rule-statement-type-geo-match.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/waf/latest/developerguide/waf-rule-statement-type-ip-set-match.html"]}},{"id":90,"question_en":"A company needs a cloud-based, managed desktop solution for its workforce of remote employees. The company wants to ensure that the employees can access the desktops only by using company-provided devices. A security engineer must design a solution that will minimize cost and management overhead. Which solution will meet these requirements?","question_zh":"一家公司需要为远程员工提供基于云的托管桌面解决方案。该公司希望确保员工只能通过公司提供的设备访问桌面。安全工程师 必须设计一种能够最小化成本和管理开销的解决方案。 哪种解决方案能满足这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Deploy a custom virtual desktop infrastructure (VDI) solution with a restriction policy to allow access only from corporate devices.","B":"Deploy a fleet of Amazon EC2 instances. Assign an instance to each employee with certificate-based device authentication that uses Windows Active Directory.","C":"Deploy Amazon WorkSpaces. Set up a trusted device policy with IP blocking on the authentication gateway by using AWS Identity and Access Management (IAM).","D":"Deploy Amazon WorkSpaces. Create client certificates, and deploy them to trusted devices. Enable restricted access at the directory level."},"options_zh":{"A":"部署一个带有访问限制策略的自定义虚拟桌面基础设施（VDI）解决方案，仅允许企业设备访问。","B":"部署一组 Amazon EC2 实例，为每位员工分配一个实例，并使用基于证书的设备认证（结合 Windows Active Directory）进行身 份验证。","C":"部署 Amazon WorkSpaces。使用 AWS 身份和访问管理（IAM）在身份验证网关上设置带有 IP 封锁的可信设备策略。","D":"部署 Amazon WorkSpaces。创建客户端证书，并将其部署到受信任的设备上。在目录级别启用受限访问。"},"answer":["D"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Security/IAM","Compute","Cost Optimization"],"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選","research":{"verdict":["D"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"both","explanation_en":"Amazon WorkSpaces is AWS's fully managed Desktop-as-a-Service (DaaS) offering, which minimizes cost and management overhead compared to a self-built VDI stack or a fleet of individually managed EC2 instances. AWS documents the exact mechanism for restricting WorkSpaces access to company-managed devices under 'Restrict access to trusted devices for WorkSpaces Personal': Step 1 create a root CA and client (device) certificates that chain to it; Step 2 deploy those client certificates to the trusted corporate devices (e.g., via SCCM or MDM); Step 3 'Configure the restriction' by enabling restricted access at the directory level in the WorkSpaces console (Directories > Actions > Update Details), where you import the root certificate so the WorkSpaces client validates it before allowing login or reconnect. This is exactly option D's description. Option C's 'IAM authentication gateway with IP blocking' does not exist as a WorkSpaces trusted-device feature — the actual control is certificate-based and configured at the directory level, not via IAM policies or IP allow-lists. Options A and B require the company to build and operate its own VDI/EC2 and AD authentication infrastructure, which contradicts the requirement to minimize cost and management overhead. Only one option is correct.","explanation_zh":"Amazon WorkSpaces 是 AWS 完全代管的桌面即服務 (DaaS),相較於自行架設的 VDI 架構或需個別管理的 EC2 執行個體機群,能大幅降低成本與管理負擔。AWS 官方文件「Restrict access to trusted devices for WorkSpaces Personal」明確說明限制僅公司管理裝置存取的機制:步驟一建立根憑證 (CA) 與串接至該根憑證的用戶端(裝置)憑證;步驟二將這些用戶端憑證部署到受信任的公司裝置上(例如透過 SCCM 或 MDM);步驟三「Configure the restriction」,在 WorkSpaces 主控台的目錄層級啟用限制存取 (Directories > Actions > Update Details),匯入根憑證,讓 WorkSpaces 用戶端在允許登入或重新連線前先驗證憑證。這正是選項 D 所描述的流程。選項 C 所稱的「以 IAM 為基礎、具 IP 封鎖功能的驗證閘道」並非 WorkSpaces 受信任裝置的實際功能——實際控制機制是以憑證為基礎並在目錄層級設定,而非透過 IAM 政策或 IP 允許清單。選項 A 與 B 都需要公司自行建置並維運 VDI/EC2 與 AD 驗證基礎架構,違背「降低成本與管理負擔」的需求。本題只有一個正確答案。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"A custom, self-built VDI solution (with a restriction policy layered on top) directly contradicts the requirement to minimize cost and management overhead, since the company would need to build, patch, and operate the entire VDI stack itself rather than use a managed AWS service.","why_zh":"自行建置的 VDI 解決方案(再疊加限制政策)違背了「降低成本與管理負擔」的需求,因為公司仍需自行建置、修補並維運整套 VDI 架構,而非使用 AWS 代管服務。"},{"letter":"B","why_en":"Assigning a dedicated EC2 instance per employee with custom certificate-based Active Directory authentication requires the company to build and manage its own remote desktop/authentication layer, AD infrastructure, and instance fleet — high management overhead and not a managed desktop service like WorkSpaces.","why_zh":"為每位員工指派專屬 EC2 執行個體,並自行建置以憑證為基礎的 Active Directory 驗證機制,代表公司必須自行建置並維運遠端桌面/驗證層、AD 基礎架構及執行個體機群,管理負擔高,也不像 WorkSpaces 那樣是代管的桌面服務。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"There is no IAM-based, IP-blocking 'authentication gateway' feature in Amazon WorkSpaces trusted device restriction. The actual documented feature validates client certificates on the device itself and is configured at the directory level (Directories > Update Details), not via IAM policies or an IP allow/deny gateway.","why_zh":"Amazon WorkSpaces 的受信任裝置限制功能中,並不存在以 IAM 為基礎、具 IP 封鎖能力的「authentication gateway」。文件記載的實際功能是在裝置端驗證用戶端憑證,並在目錄層級設定 (Directories > Update Details),而非透過 IAM 政策或 IP 允許/封鎖閘道。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/workspaces/latest/adminguide/trusted-devices.html"]}},{"id":91,"question_en":"A company has a web-based application that runs behind an Application Load Balancer (ALB). The application is experiencing a credential stuffing attack that is producing many failed login attempts. The attack is coming from many IP addresses. The login attempts are using a user agent string of a known mobile device emulator. A security engineer needs to implement a solution to mitigate the credential stuffing attack. The solution must still allow legitimate logins to the application. Which solution will meet these requirements?","question_zh":"一家公司有一个基于Web的应用程序，运行在应用负载均衡器（ALB）之后。该应用程序正遭受凭证填充攻击，导致大量登录 失败尝试。攻击来自多个IP地址，且登录尝试使用了已知的移动设备模拟器的用户代理字符串。安全工程师需要实施一项解决 方案来缓解此次凭证填充攻击，同时仍需允许合法用户正常登录应用程序。 哪种解决方案能满足这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Create an Amazon CloudWatch alarm that reacts to login attempts that contain the specified user agent string. Add an Amazon Simple Notification Service (Amazon SNS) topic to the alarm.","B":"Modify the inbound security group on the ALB to deny traffic from the IP addresses that are involved in the attack.","C":"Create an AWS WAF web ACL for the ALB. Create a custom rule that blocks requests that contain the user agent string of the device emulator.","D":"Create an AWS WAF web ACL for the ALB. Create a custom rule that allows requests from legitimate user agent strings."},"options_zh":{"A":"创建一个 Amazon CloudWatch 警报，用于响应包含指定用户代理字符串的登录尝试。将 Amazon 简单通知服务（Amazon SNS）主题添加到该警报中。","B":"修改ALB的入站安全组，拒绝来自参与攻击的IP地址的流量。","C":"为ALB创建一个AWS WAF网络ACL。创建一条自定义规则，用于阻止包含设备模拟器用户代理字符串的请求。","D":"为ALB创建一个AWS WAF网络ACL，并创建一条自定义规则，允许来自合法用户代理字符串的请求。"},"answer":["C"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Networking/DNS","Security/IAM","Serverless/Integration","Monitoring/Ops"],"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選","research":{"verdict":["C"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"AWS WAF's string match rule statement (ByteMatchStatement) is purpose-built for this scenario: AWS documentation explicitly describes using it to look for 'a specific string ... as an exact match for the request's User-agent header.' Because the attack is uniquely identifiable by a known mobile device emulator's User-Agent string, a custom AWS WAF rule that matches and blocks that exact string isolates the malicious traffic at Layer 7 while leaving every other request (i.e., legitimate logins from real browsers/apps) untouched. The web ACL is attached to the ALB, which is the correct integration point for HTTP-layer inspection in front of an Application Load Balancer. Option A only creates a CloudWatch alarm with an SNS notification - that provides visibility/alerting but takes no blocking action, so failed logins keep hitting the app. Option B modifies the ALB's security group to deny the attacking IPs - but the attack explicitly comes from many IP addresses, so IP-based blocking does not scale and is trivially evaded by rotating IPs; moreover, security groups are stateful allow-lists only (implicit deny) and do not support explicit 'deny' rules, so the action described is not even a valid security group operation - a network ACL would be needed for explicit denies, and even that would not solve the many-IP scaling problem. Option D takes the opposite, allowlist approach - permitting only 'legitimate' user agent strings - which requires enumerating and continuously maintaining every valid browser/device/app user agent used by legitimate users; this is operationally brittle and silently breaks logins whenever a legitimate client's UA string isn't on the list (new browser version, new device, minor variation), which scales far worse than a single targeted blocklist rule. AWS also offers a purpose-built AWS WAF Fraud Control Account Takeover Prevention (ATP) managed rule group specifically for credential stuffing, which would be the more turnkey production recommendation - but ATP is not among the four given options, so it does not change which of A-D is correct. Among the choices actually offered, C is the only one that blocks the identified malicious signature without disrupting legitimate traffic.","explanation_zh":"AWS WAF 的 string match rule statement(ByteMatchStatement)正是為此設計:AWS 官方文件明確說明可用它來尋找「特定字串……作為 request 的 User-agent header 的 exact match」。由於這次攻擊可透過某個已知 mobile device emulator 的 User-Agent 字串被唯一識別出來,建立一個自訂 AWS WAF 規則精準比對並封鎖該字串,就能在第 7 層精確隔離惡意流量,同時完全不影響其他請求(也就是使用真實瀏覽器或 App 的合法登入)。這個 web ACL 附加到 ALB,是在 Application Load Balancer 前面做 HTTP 層檢查的正確整合點。選項 A 只是建立 CloudWatch alarm 搭配 SNS 通知 - 這只提供可視性與警示,並沒有採取任何封鎖動作,失敗的登入嘗試仍會持續打到應用程式。選項 B 修改 ALB 的 security group 來拒絕攻擊來源 IP - 但題目明確說攻擊來自許多 IP 位址,以 IP 為基礎的封鎖無法擴展,且攻擊者只要輪換 IP 就能輕易規避;更重要的是,security group 本質上只是 stateful 的 allow-list(隱含 deny),並不支援明確的「deny」規則,所以題目描述的操作在技術上根本不成立 - 若要明確拒絕流量需要用 network ACL,而且即便如此也無法解決多 IP 造成的擴展性問題。選項 D 採取相反的 allowlist 做法 - 只允許「合法」的 user agent 字串通過 - 這需要列舉並持續維護所有合法使用者可能用到的每一種瀏覽器/裝置/App 的 user agent,操作上非常脆弱,只要有合法使用者的 UA 字串未列在清單裡(新版瀏覽器、新裝置、些微差異)就會悄悄擋掉正常登入,擴展性遠不如針對性的單一封鎖規則。AWS 也提供專門針對 credential stuffing 設計的 AWS WAF Fraud Control Account Takeover Prevention(ATP)managed rule group,是更「開箱即用」的正式建議做法 - 但 ATP 並不在這四個選項之中,因此不影響 A-D 之間何者正確的判斷。在題目實際給出的選項中,只有 C 能夠封鎖已識別的惡意特徵,同時不影響合法流量。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"A CloudWatch alarm with an SNS topic only generates a notification when the specified condition occurs - it takes no action to block or mitigate the failed login attempts, so the credential stuffing attack continues unaffected.","why_zh":"CloudWatch alarm 搭配 SNS topic 只會在符合條件時發出通知,並不會採取任何封鎖或緩解動作,因此 credential stuffing 攻擊仍會持續不受影響。"},{"letter":"B","why_en":"The attack originates from many distinct IP addresses, so blocking specific IPs via the security group does not scale and is easily evaded by rotating to new IPs. Additionally, security groups only support allow rules (stateful, implicit deny) - they cannot be configured with explicit deny rules, so this action isn't even technically valid; a network ACL would be needed for explicit denies, and even then it wouldn't address the many-IP scaling problem.","why_zh":"攻擊來自許多不同的 IP 位址,透過 security group 封鎖特定 IP 無法擴展,攻擊者輪換新 IP 即可輕易規避。此外,security group 只支援 allow 規則(stateful、隱含 deny),並不能設定明確的 deny 規則,所以這個操作在技術上根本不成立;若要明確拒絕流量需要用 network ACL,但即便如此也無法解決多 IP 造成的擴展性問題。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"An allowlist of 'legitimate' user agent strings is operationally fragile - it requires continuously enumerating every valid browser/device/app user agent across all legitimate users, and silently breaks logins for any client whose UA string isn't on the list (new browser versions, new devices, minor variations), which is a worse outcome than targeting the known-bad signature directly.","why_zh":"以「合法」user agent 字串建立 allowlist 在維運上非常脆弱 - 需要持續列舉所有合法使用者可能用到的每一種瀏覽器/裝置/App 的 user agent,且只要有客戶端的 UA 字串不在清單上(新版瀏覽器、新裝置、些微差異)就會悄悄擋掉其登入,這比直接針對已知惡意特徵封鎖的做法更糟。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/waf/latest/developerguide/waf-rule-statement-type-string-match.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/waf/latest/developerguide/waf-rate-based-example-limit-login-page-keys.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/waf/latest/developerguide/waf-atp.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/waf/latest/developerguide/aws-managed-rule-groups-atp.html"]}},{"id":92,"question_en":"A security engineer is asked to update an AWS CloudTrail log file prefix for an existing trail. When attempting to save the change in the CloudTrail console, the security engineer receives the following error message: “There is a problem with the bucket policy.” What will enable the security engineer to save the change?","question_zh":"安全工程师被要求更新现有追踪的 AWS CloudTrail 日志文件前缀。当尝试在 CloudTrail 控制台中保存更改时，该安全工程 师收到以下错误消息：“存储桶策略存在问题。” 什么能让安全工程师保存更改？","options_en":{"A":"Create a new trail with the updated log file prefix, and then delete the original trail.","B":"Update the existing bucket policy in the Amazon S3 console to allow the security engineer’s principal to perform PutBucketPolicy, and then update the log file prefix in the CloudTrail console.","C":"Update the existing bucket policy in the Amazon S3 console with the new log file prefix, and then update the log file prefix in the CloudTrail console.","D":"Update the existing bucket policy in the Amazon S3 console to allow the security engineer’s principal to perform GetBucketPolicy, and then update the log file prefix in the CloudTrail console."},"options_zh":{"A":"使用更新后的日志文件前缀创建一个新的跟踪文件，然后删除原始的跟踪文件。","B":"在 Amazon S3 控制台中更新现有的存储桶策略，允许安全工程师的主体执行 PutBucketPolicy 操作，然后在 CloudTrail 控 制台中更新日志文件前缀。","C":"在 Amazon S3 控制台中使用新的日志文件前缀更新现有的存储桶策略，然后在 CloudTrail 控制台中更新日志文件前 缀。","D":"在 Amazon S3 控制台中更新现有的存储桶策略，允许安全工程师的主体执行 GetBucketPolicy 操作，然后在 CloudTrail 控 制台中更新日志文件前缀。"},"answer":["C"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Storage","Monitoring/Ops"],"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選","research":{"verdict":["C"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"both","explanation_en":"AWS CloudTrail's official documentation on the S3 bucket policy for CloudTrail includes a troubleshooting subsection titled 'Changing a prefix for an existing bucket' that describes this exact scenario verbatim: 'If you try to add, modify, or remove a log file prefix for an S3 bucket that receives logs from a trail, you might see the error: There is a problem with the bucket policy... To resolve this issue, use the Amazon S3 console to update the prefix in the bucket policy, and then use the CloudTrail console to specify the same prefix for the bucket in the trail.' The documented procedure is: (1) in the S3 console, edit the bucket policy's s3:PutObject statement so the Resource ARN reflects the new prefix (e.g., arn:aws:s3:::bucket-name/prefix/AWSLogs/accountID/*) and save it; then (2) in the CloudTrail console, update the trail's Log file prefix setting to match that same new prefix and save. CloudTrail validates that the prefix configured on the trail is consistent with what the bucket policy authorizes for s3:PutObject before it will accept the change - a stale prefix in the policy causes the save to fail with exactly the quoted error. This is precisely option C's sequence: update the bucket policy with the new prefix first, then update CloudTrail's log file prefix to match.","explanation_zh":"AWS CloudTrail 官方文件中關於 S3 bucket policy for CloudTrail 的章節,有一個疑難排解子章節「Changing a prefix for an existing bucket」逐字描述了這個情境:「若你嘗試新增、修改或移除某個正在接收 trail 日誌的 S3 bucket 的 log file prefix,可能會看到錯誤訊息:There is a problem with the bucket policy...若要解決此問題,請使用 Amazon S3 主控台更新 bucket policy 中的 prefix,然後使用 CloudTrail 主控台為該 bucket 在 trail 中指定相同的 prefix。」文件記載的具體步驟是:(1) 在 S3 主控台編輯 bucket policy 中 s3:PutObject 陳述式的 Resource ARN,使其反映新的 prefix(例如 arn:aws:s3:::bucket-name/prefix/AWSLogs/accountID/*)並儲存;接著 (2) 在 CloudTrail 主控台將該 trail 的 Log file prefix 設定更新為與 bucket policy 相同的新 prefix,再儲存。CloudTrail 在接受變更前,會驗證 trail 上設定的 prefix 是否與 bucket policy 中 s3:PutObject 所授權的 prefix 一致——若 policy 中仍是舊的 prefix,儲存就會出現題目所述的錯誤。這正是選項 C 所描述的順序:先更新 bucket policy 為新 prefix,再更新 CloudTrail 的 log file prefix 使其一致。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"Creating a new trail and deleting the original is unnecessary, destructive, and not the documented remedy - it discards the trail's history, its ARN, and any dependent configuration (e.g., CloudWatch Logs integration, aws:SourceArn references) for no benefit. AWS's own troubleshooting guide fixes the mismatch in place rather than recreating the trail.","why_zh":"建立新 trail 並刪除原本的 trail 既不必要也具破壞性,並非官方文件記載的解決方法——這會使 trail 的歷史紀錄、ARN 以及任何相依設定(例如 CloudWatch Logs 整合、aws:SourceArn 參照)全部遺失,卻沒有帶來任何好處。AWS 官方疑難排解指南是直接修正 prefix 不一致的問題,而非重建 trail。"},{"letter":"B","why_en":"The error is a validation failure caused by a prefix mismatch between the bucket policy's s3:PutObject Resource ARN and the prefix being configured in CloudTrail - it is not caused by the engineer lacking the s3:PutBucketPolicy permission needed to edit the policy in the first place. Granting PutBucketPolicy would only affect whether the engineer's IAM principal can call that S3 API; it does nothing to correct the prefix text itself, so the CloudTrail save would still fail afterward.","why_zh":"此錯誤是因為 bucket policy 中 s3:PutObject 的 Resource ARN 與 CloudTrail 欲設定的 prefix 不一致所導致的驗證失敗,並非因為工程師缺少編輯 policy 所需的 s3:PutBucketPolicy 權限。授予 PutBucketPolicy 權限只會影響工程師的 IAM principal 是否能呼叫該 S3 API,並不會修正 prefix 文字本身,因此即使授權後,CloudTrail 端的儲存仍會失敗。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"GetBucketPolicy is a read-only permission for viewing a bucket policy's contents; it has no effect on writing/updating the policy and no bearing on the write-time prefix validation error CloudTrail returns. It does not address the root cause (a stale prefix in the policy's Resource ARN) at all.","why_zh":"GetBucketPolicy 只是用於檢視 bucket policy 內容的唯讀權限,對於寫入/更新 policy 沒有作用,也與 CloudTrail 在儲存時進行的 prefix 驗證錯誤毫無關係。它完全沒有解決根本原因(policy 中 Resource ARN 的 prefix 已過時)。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/awscloudtrail/latest/userguide/create-s3-bucket-policy-for-cloudtrail.html#cloudtrail-add-change-or-remove-a-bucket-prefix"]}},{"id":93,"question_en":"A company runs an application on a fleet of Amazon EC2 instances. The application is accessible to users around the world. The company associates an AWS WAF web ACL with an Application Load Balancer (ALB) that routes traffic to the EC2 instances. A security engineer is investigating a sudden increase in traffic to the application. The security engineer discovers a significant amount of potentially malicious requests coming from hundreds of IP addresses in two countries. The security engineer wants to quickly limit the potentially malicious requests but does not want to prevent legitimate users from accessing the application. Which solution will meet these requirements?","question_zh":"一家公司在一组 Amazon EC2 实例上运行应用程序，该应用程序面向全球用户开放。公司为一个应用负载均衡器（ALB） 关联了 AWS WAF 网站访问控制列表（web ACL），由该负载均衡器将流量路由到 EC2 实例。 安全工程师正在调查应用程序流量突然增加的情况。该工程师发现，来自两个国家的数百个IP地址 发来了大量可能具有恶意的请求。安全工程师希望快速限制这些潜在的恶意请求，但又不想阻止合 法用户访问应用程序。 哪种解决方案能满足这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Use AWS WAF to implement a rate-based rule for all incoming requests.","B":"Use AWS WAF to implement a geographical match rule to block all incoming traffic from the two countries.","C":"Edit the ALB security group to include a geographical match rule to block all incoming traffic from the two countries.","D":"Add deny rules to the ALB security group that prohibit incoming requests from the IP addresses."},"options_zh":{"A":"使用 AWS WAF 为所有传入请求实施基于速率的规则。","B":"使用 AWS WAF 实施地理位置匹配规则，阻止来自这两个国家的所有传入流量。","C":"编辑ALB安全组，添加地理位置匹配规则，以阻止来自这两个国家的所有传入流量。","D":"向ALB安全组添加拒绝规则，禁止来自这些IP地址的传入请求。"},"answer":["A"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Networking/DNS","Security/IAM","Compute"],"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選","research":{"verdict":["A"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"The requirement has two parts: (1) quickly limit the malicious requests, and (2) do not block legitimate users. AWS WAF rate-based rules count incoming requests per aggregation key (by default, source IP address) over a rolling evaluation window (as short as 1 minute, commonly 5 minutes) and only rate-limit (e.g., block) the specific IPs whose request rate exceeds the configured threshold. This targets abusive behavior directly, regardless of the requester's country, so legitimate users everywhere -- including any legitimate users located in the same two countries as the attackers -- continue to be served normally as long as their request rate stays under the threshold. A geographic match rule (B) would block ALL traffic from the two named countries, including any legitimate customers located there, which directly violates the stated requirement not to prevent legitimate users from accessing the application. Security groups (C and D) are stateful, allow-only virtual firewalls: AWS VPC documentation explicitly states 'You can specify allow rules, but not deny rules,' and security groups have no geographic matching capability at all -- they only evaluate protocol, port, and source/destination IP/CIDR or security group references. Therefore C and D are not technically achievable as described. The correct and only defensible answer is A.","explanation_zh":"此需求包含兩個要件：(1) 快速限制惡意請求,(2) 不能封鎖合法使用者。AWS WAF 的 rate-based rule 會依聚合鍵值(預設為來源 IP 位址)在滾動評估視窗內(短則 1 分鐘,常見為 5 分鐘)計算請求數量,只針對超過設定門檻的特定 IP 進行限速或封鎖。這種做法是針對「異常行為」本身,而不是針對「來源國家」,因此無論這些惡意 IP 來自哪個國家,只要某個使用者的請求頻率未超過門檻,該使用者(即使身處那兩個國家)仍能正常存取應用程式,完全符合「不封鎖合法使用者」的要求。選項 B 的 geographic match rule 會封鎖來自那兩個國家的「所有」流量,包含當地合法客戶,直接違反題目明確提出的限制條件。至於選項 C 與 D,security group 是 stateful、僅支援「允許 (allow)」規則的虛擬防火牆:AWS VPC 官方文件明確指出「You can specify allow rules, but not deny rules」,而且 security group 完全沒有地理位置比對能力,只能依協定、埠號、以及來源/目的 IP 或 CIDR(或安全群組參照)進行比對。因此 C、D 在技術上根本無法實作題目所描述的規則。正確且唯一合理的答案是 A。","distractors":[{"letter":"B","why_en":"Geographic match rules block or allow traffic strictly by the country of origin derived from the source IP. This would indiscriminately block every request from the two countries, including legitimate users located there, directly violating the requirement not to prevent legitimate users from accessing the application.","why_zh":"Geographic match rule 是依來源 IP 判斷所屬國家後整批允許或封鎖流量。這會不分青紅皂白地封鎖那兩個國家的所有請求,包含當地的合法使用者,直接違反題目「不能阻擋合法使用者」的要求。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"Security groups have no geographic matching capability whatsoever -- they can only filter by protocol, port, and source/destination IP address, CIDR range, or referenced security group. This option describes a feature that does not exist for security groups.","why_zh":"Security group 完全沒有地理位置比對功能,只能依協定、埠號、以及來源/目的 IP、CIDR 範圍或參照的 security group 來過濾流量。此選項描述的是 security group 並不具備的功能。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"Security groups only support allow rules; there is no way to add explicit deny rules to a security group to block specific IP addresses. Blocking hundreds of individual IPs this way is also operationally impractical even if it were possible.","why_zh":"Security group 只支援允許 (allow) 規則,無法針對特定 IP 位址新增明確的拒絕 (deny) 規則。即便技術上可行,要逐一封鎖數百個 IP 也在維運上不切實際。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/waf/latest/developerguide/waf-rule-statement-type-rate-based.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/waf/latest/developerguide/waf-rule-statement-type-geo-match.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/vpc/latest/userguide/security-group-rules.html"]}},{"id":94,"question_en":"A company begins to use AWS WAF after experiencing an increase in traffic to the company ' s public web applications. A security engineer needs to determine if the increase in traffic is because of application-layer attacks. The security engineer needs a solution to analyze AWS WAF traffic. Which solution will meet this requirement?","question_zh":"一家公司在其公共网络应用流量增加后开始使用 AWS WAF。安全工程师需要确定流量增长是否由应用层攻击引起，并需 要一种解决方案来分析 AWS WAF 的流量。 哪种解决方案能满足这一要求？","options_en":{"A":"Configure AWS WAF to send logs to a trail in AWS CloudTrail. Create an Amazon Data Firehose delivery stream to send the logs to Amazon OpenSearch Service. Use OpenSearch Dashboards and an Amazon Athena connector to query the logs.","B":"Configure AWS WAF to send logs to an Amazon S3 bucket. Configure an OpenSearch table with a partition projection of the S3 bucket. Use OpenSearch to query the data in the S3 bucket.","C":"Configure AWS WAF to send logs to an Amazon S3 bucket. Configure an Amazon Athena table with a partition projection of the S3 bucket. Use Athena to query the data in the S3 bucket.","D":"Configure AWS WAF to send logs to a trail in AWS CloudTrail. Create an Amazon Data Firehose delivery stream to send the logs to an Amazon S3 bucket. Use Amazon Athena to query the data in the S3 bucket."},"options_zh":{"A":"配置 AWS WAF 将日志发送到 AWS CloudTrail 中的追踪。创建 Amazon Data Firehose 传输流，将日志发送至 Amazon OpenSearch Service。使用 OpenSearch Dashboards 和 Amazon Athena 连接器查询日志。","B":"配置 AWS WAF 将日志发送到 Amazon S3 存储桶。在 OpenSearch 中创建一个包含 S3 存储桶分区投影的表，并使用 OpenSearch 查询 S3 存储桶中的数据。","C":"配置 AWS WAF 将日志发送到 Amazon S3 存储桶。在 S3 存储桶上配置一个带有分区投影的 Amazon Athena 表，并使用 Athena 查询存储桶中的数据。","D":"配置 AWS WAF 将日志发送到 AWS CloudTrail 中的追踪。创建 Amazon Data Firehose 传输流，将日志发送至 Amazon S3 存储桶，并使用 Amazon Athena 查询 S3 存储桶中的数据。"},"answer":["C"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Security/IAM","Storage","Monitoring/Ops","Analytics"],"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選","research":{"verdict":["C"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"AWS WAF web ACL traffic logs can only be sent to one of three destinations: Amazon CloudWatch Logs, Amazon S3, or Amazon Kinesis Data Firehose (Amazon Data Firehose). There is no AWS CloudTrail path for WAF traffic logs, so any option routing WAF logs 'to a trail in AWS CloudTrail' is factually wrong and describes a configuration that AWS WAF does not support. That eliminates options A and D immediately. Between the remaining S3-based options, AWS Athena has official, dedicated documentation ('Create a table for AWS WAF S3 logs in Athena using partition projection') describing exactly this pattern: send WAF logs to S3, create an Athena table over the bucket using partition projection (a table property that lets Athena compute Hive-style partition locations from the S3 key format instead of relying on Glue Data Catalog partition metadata or manual ALTER TABLE ADD PARTITION calls), and query with standard SQL. Partition projection is an Athena/Glue table-definition feature, not a capability of Amazon OpenSearch Service, so option B's premise of an 'OpenSearch table with partition projection' does not correspond to any real AWS feature. That leaves option C as the only solution that uses documented, real AWS WAF logging destinations and a documented Athena querying pattern to analyze traffic for application-layer attack patterns.","explanation_zh":"AWS WAF 的 web ACL 流量日誌只能傳送到三種目的地之一:Amazon CloudWatch Logs、Amazon S3,或 Amazon Kinesis Data Firehose(Amazon Data Firehose)。並不存在將 WAF 流量日誌傳送到 AWS CloudTrail 追蹤(trail)的路徑,因此任何提到「將日誌傳送到 CloudTrail 中的追蹤」的選項,描述的都是 AWS WAF 不支援的設定,這直接排除了選項 A 與 D。在剩下以 S3 為基礎的兩個選項中,AWS Athena 官方文件中有專門的頁面「Create a table for AWS WAF S3 logs in Athena using partition projection」,說明的正是這個模式:將 WAF 日誌傳送到 S3,再用 partition projection 這個資料表屬性,讓 Athena 直接根據 S3 物件鍵格式計算出 Hive 風格的分區位置,而不需依賴 Glue Data Catalog 的分區中繼資料或手動執行 ALTER TABLE ADD PARTITION,最後用標準 SQL 查詢。Partition projection 是 Athena/Glue 資料表定義層級的功能,並非 Amazon OpenSearch Service 的能力,因此選項 B 所描述的「具備 partition projection 的 OpenSearch table」並不對應任何真實存在的 AWS 功能。因此,選項 C 是唯一同時使用真實且有文件記載的 AWS WAF 日誌目的地,以及有文件記載的 Athena 查詢模式,來分析流量是否來自應用層攻擊的解決方案。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"AWS WAF cannot send traffic logs to an AWS CloudTrail trail; the only supported WAF logging destinations are Amazon S3, CloudWatch Logs, and Kinesis Data Firehose. This option describes a non-existent logging path, and even if the Firehose-to-OpenSearch part were valid on its own, the CloudTrail source step makes the whole solution unworkable.","why_zh":"AWS WAF 無法將流量日誌傳送到 AWS CloudTrail 的追蹤;WAF 支援的日誌目的地只有 Amazon S3、CloudWatch Logs 與 Kinesis Data Firehose。此選項描述了一條不存在的日誌路徑,即便後段「Firehose 傳送到 OpenSearch」本身可行,前段以 CloudTrail 作為來源就使整個方案無法成立。"},{"letter":"B","why_en":"\"Partition projection\" is an Amazon Athena (Glue Data Catalog) table property; Amazon OpenSearch Service has no equivalent feature and cannot directly query data sitting in an S3 bucket using this mechanism. The described setup does not match any real OpenSearch capability.","why_zh":"「Partition projection」是 Amazon Athena(Glue Data Catalog)的資料表屬性;Amazon OpenSearch Service 並沒有對應的功能,也無法透過這種機制直接查詢存放在 S3 儲存桶中的資料。此選項描述的設定不對應任何真實的 OpenSearch 能力。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"Like option A, this relies on AWS WAF sending logs to a CloudTrail trail, which is not a supported AWS WAF logging destination. Even though the rest of the pipeline (Firehose to S3, then Athena) is technically sound, the CloudTrail step breaks the solution at its source.","why_zh":"與選項 A 相同,此選項依賴 AWS WAF 將日誌傳送到 CloudTrail 的追蹤,而這並非 AWS WAF 支援的日誌目的地。儘管後續流程(Firehose 傳送到 S3,再用 Athena 查詢)在技術上是合理的,但一開始的 CloudTrail 步驟就讓整個方案無法成立。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/waf/latest/developerguide/logging-destinations.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/athena/latest/ug/create-waf-table-partition-projection.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/athena/latest/ug/partition-projection.html"]}},{"id":95,"question_en":"A company runs an application outside of AWS. The external application authenticates to AWS as an IAM user. A security engineer needs to migrate the external application to use an IAM role. The company’s human users already use IAM roles with AWS IAM Identity Center. Which solution will give the external application the ability to use an IAM role?","question_zh":"一家公司运行的应用程序位于 AWS 之外。该外部应用程序以 IAM 用户身份对 AWS 进行身份验证。安全工程师需要将该外 部应用程序迁移为使用 IAM 角色。该公司的人工用户已通过 AWS IAM 身份中心使用 IAM 角色。 哪种解决方案能让外部应用程序具备使用 IAM 角色的能力？","options_en":{"A":"Set up the external application as a managed application in IAM Identity Center. Create a new account assignment to generate an IAM role for the external application to use.","B":"Create an AWS Verified Access instance. Set up a trust provider for the external application. Create a Verified Access policy to allow the external application to assume an IAM role.","C":"Use IAM Roles Anywhere. Create a trust anchor and profile on AWS. Set up the credential helper tool in the external application. Configure an IAM role to trust IAM Roles Anywhere.","D":"Enable federation with IAM. Configure SAML 2.0 federation by adding a relying party trust between the external application and AWS. Set up an IAM role for the external application to assume."},"options_zh":{"A":"在 IAM Identity Center 中将外部应用程序设置为托管应用程序。创建新的账户分配，以生成供外部应用程序使用的 IAM 角色。","B":"创建一个 AWS Verified Access 实例，为外部应用程序设置信任提供方，并创建 Verified Access 策略，以允许该外 部应用程序担任 IAM 角色。","C":"使用 IAM 角色任意功能。在 AWS 上创建信任锚点和配置文件，在外部应用程序中设置凭证辅助工具，并配置 IAM 角色以信任 IAM 角色任意功能。","D":"启用与 IAM 的联合身份验证。通过在外部应用程序和 AWS 之间添加信任关系来配置 SAML 2.0 联合身份验证， 并为外部应用程序设置一个可承担的 IAM 角色。"},"answer":["C"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Migration","Security/IAM"],"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選","research":{"verdict":["C"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"both","explanation_en":"AWS IAM Roles Anywhere is purpose-built for exactly this scenario: it lets workloads such as servers, containers, and applications running outside of AWS obtain temporary security credentials from IAM without storing long-term IAM user access keys. The workflow is to create a trust anchor (referencing AWS Private CA or an external CA), create a profile that specifies which IAM role(s) can be assumed, install the IAM Roles Anywhere credential helper tool in the external application, and configure the IAM role's trust policy to trust the IAM Roles Anywhere service. The application then authenticates using an X.509 certificate issued by the trusted CA and receives temporary IAM role credentials in exchange, eliminating the long-term IAM user credentials entirely. This matches option C precisely. Option A is incorrect because IAM Identity Center 'managed applications' and account assignments are a mechanism for granting human users and groups (via permission sets) federated access to AWS accounts or pre-integrated SaaS applications; it is not a mechanism for issuing an assumable IAM role to an arbitrary external non-human application authenticating with a certificate. Option B is incorrect because AWS Verified Access is a Zero Trust service for granting access to internal corporate web applications based on identity and device posture; it does not issue IAM role credentials to an external application. Option D is incorrect because SAML 2.0 federation is designed for browser-based (or SDK-based) human user or workforce identity federation via an external IdP with assertions, not for a standalone external application replacing an IAM user's static credentials; it also requires an existing SAML IdP relationship that isn't part of the given setup (which already uses IAM Identity Center, not SAML federation, for humans).","explanation_zh":"AWS IAM Roles Anywhere 正是為此情境所設計:它讓在 AWS 之外執行的伺服器、容器和應用程式等工作負載,能夠從 IAM 取得臨時安全憑證,而不需要儲存長期的 IAM 使用者存取金鑰。其運作方式是建立一個 trust anchor(參照 AWS Private CA 或外部 CA)、建立一個指定可扮演哪些 IAM role 的 profile、在外部應用程式中安裝 IAM Roles Anywhere 的 credential helper 工具,並設定該 IAM role 的信任政策以信任 IAM Roles Anywhere 服務。應用程式接著使用受信任 CA 所發出的 X.509 憑證進行驗證,並換取臨時的 IAM role 憑證,完全免除長期 IAM 使用者憑證。這正好對應選項 C。選項 A 錯誤,因為 IAM Identity Center 的「managed application」與帳戶指派機制,是用來透過權限集(permission set)授予人類使用者與群組對 AWS 帳戶或預先整合 SaaS 應用程式的聯合存取權,並非用來讓以憑證驗證的任意外部非人類應用程式取得可扮演的 IAM role。選項 B 錯誤,因為 AWS Verified Access 是一項 Zero Trust 服務,依據身分與裝置狀態授予對內部企業網頁應用程式的存取權,並不會發放 IAM role 憑證給外部應用程式。選項 D 錯誤,因為 SAML 2.0 聯合驗證是設計用於透過外部 IdP 以斷言(assertion)進行以瀏覽器(或 SDK)為基礎的人類使用者或員工身分聯合驗證,而非用來取代獨立外部應用程式原有的 IAM 使用者靜態憑證;此外題目描述人類使用者已透過 IAM Identity Center(而非 SAML 聯合驗證)使用 IAM role,與此選項的前提也不吻合。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"IAM Identity Center managed applications and account assignments grant human users and groups federated access via permission sets to AWS accounts or pre-integrated SaaS apps. There is no mechanism here for a non-human external application authenticating with certificates to obtain an assumable IAM role this way.","why_zh":"IAM Identity Center 的 managed application 與帳戶指派機制,是透過權限集授予人類使用者與群組對 AWS 帳戶或預先整合 SaaS 應用程式的聯合存取權,並沒有讓以憑證驗證的非人類外部應用程式藉此取得可扮演 IAM role 的機制。"},{"letter":"B","why_en":"AWS Verified Access provides Zero Trust access to internal corporate web applications based on user identity and device posture signals; it does not issue temporary IAM role credentials to an external application.","why_zh":"AWS Verified Access 是根據使用者身分與裝置狀態訊號,提供對內部企業網頁應用程式的 Zero Trust 存取,並不會發放臨時 IAM role 憑證給外部應用程式。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"SAML 2.0 federation is designed for human/workforce identity federation with an external IdP via browser-based or SDK-based assertions, not for migrating a standalone external application off static IAM user credentials; the company's humans already use IAM Identity Center, not SAML federation, making this option inconsistent with the setup.","why_zh":"SAML 2.0 聯合驗證是設計用於透過外部 IdP 以瀏覽器或 SDK 為基礎的斷言,進行人類/員工身分聯合驗證,而非用來將獨立的外部應用程式從靜態 IAM 使用者憑證遷移出來;而且題目中人類使用者已使用 IAM Identity Center 而非 SAML 聯合驗證,與此選項的情境不一致。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/rolesanywhere/latest/userguide/introduction.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/rolesanywhere/latest/userguide/getting-started.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/rolesanywhere/latest/userguide/credential-helper.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/singlesignon/latest/userguide/account-instances-identity-center.html"]}},{"id":96,"question_en":"A company recently experienced a malicious attack on its cloud-based environment. The company successfully contained and eradicated the attack. A security engineer is performing incident response work. The security engineer needs to recover an Amazon RDS database cluster to the last known good version. The database cluster is configured to generate automated backups with a retention period of 14 days. The initial attack occurred 5 days ago at exactly 3:15 PM. Which solution will meet this requirement?","question_zh":"一家公司最近遭遇了针对其基于云环境的恶意攻击。该公司已成功遏制并清除了此次攻击。目前，安全工程师正在执行 事件响应工作，需要将Amazon RDS数据库集群恢复到最后一次已知的正常版本。该数据库集群配置为自动生成备份，保 留周期为14天。最初的攻击发生在5天前下午3:15。 哪种解决方案能满足这一要求？","options_en":{"A":"Identify the Regional cluster ARN for the database. Use the ARN to restore the Regional cluster by using the restore to point in time feature. Set a target time 5 days ago at 3:14 PM.","B":"Identify the Regional cluster ARN for the database. List snapshots that have been taken of the cluster. Restore the database by using the snapshot that has a creation time that is closest to 5 days ago at 3:14 PM.","C":"List all snapshots that have been taken of all the company ' s RDS databases. Identify the snapshot that was taken closest to 5 days ago at 3:14 PM and restore it.","D":"Identify the Regional cluster ARN for the database. Use the ARN to restore the Regional cluster by using the restore to point in time feature. Set a target time 14 days ago."},"options_zh":{"A":"确定数据库的区域集群ARN。使用该ARN通过“按时间点恢复”功能来恢复区域集群，并将目标时间设置为5 天前下午3:14。","B":"确定数据库的区域集群ARN。列出已对该集群创建的快照。使用创建时间最接近5天前下午3:14的那个快照来恢复 数据库。","C":"列出公司所有RDS数据库所创建的所有快照。找出距离5天前下午3:14最近的快照并将其恢复。","D":"确定数据库的区域集群ARN。使用该ARN通过“按时间点恢复”功能来恢复区域集群，并将目标时间设置为14天前。"},"answer":["A"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Database"],"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選","research":{"verdict":["A"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"Amazon Aurora automated backups are continuous and incremental: Aurora uploads transaction log records to Amazon S3 continuously, so restore-db-cluster-to-point-in-time (RestoreDBClusterToPointInTime) can target any exact second within the backup retention period, not just the moment of a discrete daily snapshot. Given the attack occurred exactly 5 days ago at 3:15 PM, identifying the Regional cluster ARN (the per-Region DB cluster ARN, as opposed to a global-cluster ARN which omits the Region) and issuing a point-in-time restore to 3:14 PM (one minute before compromise) recovers the cluster to the precise last-known-good state with minimal legitimate data loss. Option B is wrong because restoring from the 'closest snapshot' is limited to the granularity of the daily automated snapshot schedule, which is far coarser than PITR's log-replay precision and could land well before or after the ideal target. Option C incorrectly broadens scope to all of the company's RDS databases instead of the one identified compromised cluster, and still relies on imprecise snapshot timing. Option D needlessly restores all the way to 14 days ago (the full retention boundary), discarding up to 9 extra days of valid, uncompromised data when a precise 5-day target is achievable via PITR.","explanation_zh":"Amazon Aurora 的自動備份是連續且累加式的：Aurora 會持續將交易紀錄檔（transaction log）上傳至 Amazon S3，因此 restore-db-cluster-to-point-in-time（RestoreDBClusterToPointInTime）可以將還原目標精確定位到備份保留期間內任何一秒，而不只是每日離散 snapshot 建立的那個時間點。由於攻擊發生在恰好 5 天前的 3:15 PM，先識別該 Regional cluster ARN（區域性、含 Region 的 DB cluster ARN，區別於不含 Region 的 global-cluster ARN），再使用 restore to point in time 將目標時間設為 3:14 PM（攻擊發生前一分鐘），即可精確還原到最後已知的良好狀態，並將合法資料的損失降到最低。選項 B 錯誤，因為還原至「最接近」的 snapshot,精確度僅受限於每日自動 snapshot 的排程頻率,遠不如 PITR 透過交易紀錄檔重播所能達到的精確度,還原時間點可能明顯偏離理想目標。選項 C 錯誤地將範圍擴大到公司所有 RDS 資料庫,而非僅針對已識別的受害 cluster,且仍依賴不精確的 snapshot 時間。選項 D 會不必要地回溯到 14 天前（保留期上限）,在明明可用 PITR 精確還原到 5 天前的情況下,白白捨棄了最多 9 天額外的有效、未受攻擊影響的資料。","distractors":[{"letter":"B","why_en":"Restoring from the closest available snapshot only achieves the granularity of the automated snapshot schedule (typically once daily), which is far less precise than point-in-time recovery's ability to target an exact second using continuous transaction log replay.","why_zh":"還原至最接近的 snapshot,其精確度僅受限於自動 snapshot 排程的頻率（通常為每日一次）,遠不如 point-in-time recovery 透過連續交易紀錄檔重播精確定位到某一秒的能力。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"Listing and searching snapshots across all of the company's RDS databases is unnecessary and inefficient scope creep when the incident response task is specifically about recovering one identified, compromised cluster, and it still suffers from B's imprecise snapshot-timing limitation.","why_zh":"當事件應變任務明確是要復原某一個已識別、受攻擊的 cluster 時,列出並搜尋公司所有 RDS 資料庫的 snapshot 是不必要且沒有效率的範圍擴張,而且仍有選項 B 所述 snapshot 時間不精確的限制。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"Setting the target time to 14 days ago (the full retention boundary) restores far earlier than necessary, discarding legitimate data created between 14 days ago and just before the attack 5 days ago, when a precise 5-day-ago target is achievable and preferred.","why_zh":"將目標時間設為 14 天前（保留期上限）,還原的時間點遠比實際需要更早,會捨棄從 14 天前到 5 天前攻擊發生前這段期間所產生的合法資料,而實際上可以且應該精確設定在 5 天前的時間點。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonRDS/latest/AuroraUserGuide/aurora-pitr.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonRDS/latest/AuroraUserGuide/Aurora.Managing.Backups.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonRDS/latest/AuroraUserGuide/USER_Tagging.ARN.Constructing.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonRDS/latest/UserGuide/USER_PIT.html"]}},{"id":97,"question_en":"A company has installed a third-party application that is distributed on several Amazon EC2 instances and on- premises servers. Occasionally, the company ' s IT team needs to use SSH to connect to each machine to perform software maintenance tasks. Outside these time slots, the machines must be completely isolated from the rest of the network. The company does not want to maintain any SSH keys. Additionally, the company wants to pay only for machine hours when there is an SSH connection. Which solution will meet these requirements?","question_zh":"一家公司安装了一个第三方应用程序，该程序部署在多个Amazon EC2实例和本地服务器上。公司的IT团队偶尔需要通过SSH 连接到每台机器以执行软件维护任务。在非维护时段，这些机器必须与网络其余部分完全隔离。公司不希望维护任何SSH密钥， 同时希望仅在建立SSH连接时为机器运行时间付费。 哪种解决方案能满足这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Create a bastion host with port forwarding to connect to the machines.","B":"Set up AWS Systems Manager Session Manager to allow temporary connections.","C":"Use AWS CloudShell to create serverless connections.","D":"Set up an interface VPC endpoint for each machine for private connection."},"options_zh":{"A":"创建一个堡垒机，并通过端口转发连接到目标机器。","B":"配置 AWS Systems Manager Session Manager 以允许临时连接。","C":"使用 AWS CloudShell 创建无服务器连接。","D":"为每台机器设置一个接口VPC端点，以实现私有连接。"},"answer":["B"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Compute","Monitoring/Ops"],"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選","research":{"verdict":["B"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"both","explanation_en":"AWS Systems Manager Session Manager documentation states verbatim: 'You can manage your Amazon EC2 instances, edge devices, on-premises servers, and virtual machines (VMs)... Session Manager provides secure node management without the need to open inbound ports, maintain bastion hosts, or manage SSH keys.' It explicitly supports both Amazon EC2 instances and non-EC2 nodes (on-premises servers and VMs) in hybrid and multicloud environments via the SSM Agent and hybrid activations (Activation Code/ID), matching the scenario's mixed EC2 + on-premises fleet. Access is controlled entirely through IAM policies rather than SSH key pairs, satisfying 'the company does not want to maintain any SSH keys.' Because no inbound ports need to be open, the machines stay isolated from SSH access outside of active, IAM-authorized sessions. On the 'pay only for machine hours when there is an SSH connection' requirement: the AWS Systems Manager pricing page confirms Session Manager access to EC2 instances carries no additional charge beyond the instance itself, and for on-premises servers it uses the 'Advanced' on-premises instance tier, billed per activated managed-instance-hour, explicitly stating 'charges are not incurred for the hours where an advanced on-premises instance is de-registered, shut down, or terminated for the entire hour.' This means on-premises machines can be registered (activated) as SSM managed instances only during maintenance windows and de-registered afterward, so SSM charges track the actual connection window - directly satisfying this requirement in a way no other option does. Option A fails because a bastion host is a persistent, separately-billed instance that still requires SSH key management and bills by instance-hour regardless of SSH activity. Option C (CloudShell) is a browser shell for managing AWS resources via CLI and per AWS's own CloudShell FAQ cannot access resources inside a private VPC, let alone on-premises servers. Option D (interface VPC endpoints) provides private connectivity to AWS service APIs via PrivateLink and has no role in brokering SSH-like access to instances, and does not apply to on-premises servers at all.","explanation_zh":"AWS Systems Manager Session Manager 官方文件明確指出:「You can manage your Amazon EC2 instances, edge devices, on-premises servers, and virtual machines (VMs)... Session Manager provides secure node management without the need to open inbound ports, maintain bastion hosts, or manage SSH keys.」它明確支援 Amazon EC2 執行個體以及混合與多雲環境中的 non-EC2 節點(透過 SSM Agent 與 hybrid activation,包括 Activation Code/ID 註冊 on-premises 伺服器與 VM),正好對應題目中 EC2 加上地端伺服器混合的情境。存取權完全透過 IAM policy 控管,而非 SSH 金鑰對,符合「公司不想維護任何 SSH 金鑰」的要求。由於不需要開放任何 inbound port,機器在沒有經過 IAM 授權的連線階段時,可維持與 SSH 存取隔離。關於「只在有 SSH 連線的機器時數付費」這項需求:AWS Systems Manager 定價頁面確認,透過 Session Manager 存取 EC2 執行個體不會產生額外費用(僅有執行個體本身的費用);而地端伺服器則採用 Advanced 現場部署執行個體方案,依「已啟用為受管執行個體的時數」計費,並明確說明「針對已取消註冊、關閉或終止達完整時數的進階內部部署執行個體,不會產生任何費用」。這意味著地端機器可以只在維護時段內註冊(啟用)為 SSM 受管執行個體,結束後立即取消註冊,使 SSM 費用完全對應實際連線時段 - 這正是其他選項都無法滿足的需求。選項 A 錯誤,因為 bastion host 是一台持續運行、需獨立計費的執行個體,無論是否有 SSH 活動都依執行個體時數計費,且仍需管理 SSH 金鑰。選項 C(CloudShell)是透過瀏覽器管理 AWS 資源的 CLI shell,依 AWS 官方 CloudShell FAQ 所述,CloudShell 無法存取私有 VPC 內的資源,更不用說地端伺服器。選項 D(interface VPC endpoint)透過 PrivateLink 提供對 AWS 服務 API 的私有連線,與建立類 SSH 存取管道毫無關係,且完全不適用於地端伺服器。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"A bastion host is a dedicated, persistently running (and billed) EC2 instance that still requires SSH key pairs to be created, distributed, and rotated, and it bills by instance-hour regardless of whether an SSH session is actually active, contradicting both the 'no SSH keys' and 'pay only when connected' requirements.","why_zh":"Bastion host 是一台專用且持續運行(並持續計費)的 EC2 執行個體,仍需要建立、分發並輪替 SSH 金鑰對,且無論是否有實際 SSH 連線都依執行個體時數計費,直接違反「不維護 SSH 金鑰」與「只在連線時付費」兩項需求。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"AWS CloudShell is a browser-based shell pre-loaded with the AWS CLI for managing AWS resources. AWS's own CloudShell FAQ states it cannot access resources inside a private VPC in this release, so it cannot reach EC2 instances or on-premises servers via SSH at all.","why_zh":"AWS CloudShell 是預載 AWS CLI 的瀏覽器式 shell,用於管理 AWS 資源。AWS 官方 CloudShell FAQ 指出,此版本的 CloudShell 無法存取私有 VPC 內的資源,因此完全無法透過 SSH 連線到 EC2 執行個體或地端伺服器。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"Interface VPC endpoints (AWS PrivateLink) provide private network access to AWS service APIs from within a VPC; they don't broker interactive shell/SSH access to instances and have no applicability to on-premises servers outside AWS.","why_zh":"Interface VPC endpoint(AWS PrivateLink)提供從 VPC 內部私有存取 AWS 服務 API 的方式,並不能作為互動式 shell 或 SSH 存取執行個體的仲介,也完全不適用於 AWS 之外的地端伺服器。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/systems-manager/latest/userguide/session-manager.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/systems-manager/latest/userguide/systems-manager-hybrid-multicloud.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/systems-manager/latest/userguide/hybrid-activation-managed-nodes.html","https://aws.amazon.com/systems-manager/pricing/"]}},{"id":98,"question_en":"A company’s data scientists use Amazon SageMaker with datasets stored in Amazon S3. Data older than 45 days must be removed according to policy. Which action should enforce this policy?","question_zh":"公司的数据科学家使用 Amazon SageMaker，并将数据集存储在 Amazon S3 中。根据政策，超过 45 天的数据必须被删除。 应采取什么措施来执行此政策？","options_en":{"A":"Configure an S3 Lifecycle rule to delete objects after 45 days.","B":"Create a Lambda function triggered on object upload to delete old data.","C":"Create a scheduled Lambda function to delete old objects monthly.","D":"Configure S3 Intelligent-Tiering."},"options_zh":{"A":"配置一个S3生命周期规则，使对象在45天后被删除。","B":"创建一个在对象上传时触发的 Lambda 函数，用于删除旧数据。","C":"创建一个定时的 Lambda 函数，每月删除旧对象。","D":"配置 S3 智能分层。"},"answer":["A"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Storage","Compute"],"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選","research":{"verdict":["A"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"both","explanation_en":"AWS S3 Lifecycle configuration natively supports age-based object deletion through the Expiration action's <Days> element. AWS documentation states that the value you specify 'is the number of days since object creation when the action will occur,' and Amazon S3 calculates the exact deletion date by adding that number of days to the object's creation (last modified) time, rounding up to the next midnight UTC. This means a Lifecycle rule can be configured to expire (permanently delete, in a non-versioned bucket) objects exactly 45 days after creation, with no custom code, no compute resources, and no scheduling logic to maintain. This is precisely the mechanism AWS designed for enforcing time-based data retention/removal policies on S3 data, making it the correct and most operationally sound choice for the data scientists' SageMaker datasets. Option B is incorrect because triggering a Lambda function on every object upload only fires once per object and provides no ongoing mechanism to detect when that specific object later crosses the 45-day threshold; it would require additional scheduling logic to actually check ages later, which defeats the trigger design. Option C is incorrect because a scheduled monthly Lambda function reinvents Lifecycle expiration with custom code that must handle pagination, retries, IAM permissions, and error handling, and a monthly cadence also risks retaining objects well beyond 45 days between runs, missing the policy's precision. Option D is incorrect because S3 Intelligent-Tiering only automatically moves objects between access tiers (e.g., Frequent Access, Infrequent Access, Archive) to optimize storage cost based on access patterns; it never deletes objects, so it cannot enforce any deletion policy at all.","explanation_zh":"AWS S3 Lifecycle configuration 透過 Expiration action 的 <Days> 元素,原生支援以物件年齡為基礎的自動刪除。AWS 文件指出,你指定的數值「是自物件建立起算,執行該動作前的天數」,Amazon S3 會將該天數加到物件的建立(最後修改)時間上,並向上取整到下一個 UTC 午夜,以此計算出精確的刪除日期。這意味著只需設定一條 Lifecycle 規則,即可在物件建立後恰好 45 天將其到期(在未啟用版本控制的儲存桶中即為永久刪除),完全不需要自訂程式碼、運算資源,也不需要維護排程邏輯。這正是 AWS 為強制執行以時間為基礎的資料保留/刪除政策所設計的機制,對於資料科學家在 SageMaker 使用的資料集而言,是正確且最符合維運效益的選擇。選項 B 錯誤,因為在物件上傳時觸發的 Lambda 函式只會針對該次上傳執行一次,無法持續偵測該物件日後何時跨過 45 天門檻;若要真正檢查物件年齡,仍需額外的排程邏輯,這與「上傳觸發」的設計相違背。選項 C 錯誤,因為每月排程執行的 Lambda 函式等同於用自訂程式碼重新實作 Lifecycle 到期機制,必須自行處理分頁、重試、IAM 權限與錯誤處理,而且每月執行一次的頻率也可能導致物件在兩次執行之間被保留超過 45 天,無法精確符合政策要求。選項 D 錯誤,因為 S3 Intelligent-Tiering 只會根據存取模式自動將物件在不同存取層級(例如 Frequent Access、Infrequent Access、Archive)之間搬移,以節省儲存成本,它從不刪除物件,因此完全無法強制執行任何刪除政策。","distractors":[{"letter":"B","why_en":"An upload-triggered Lambda function only runs once at the moment of upload and has no built-in way to later detect that the object has aged past 45 days; it would need separate scheduling logic to check ages, which the trigger itself does not provide.","why_zh":"上傳觸發的 Lambda 函式只會在上傳當下執行一次,並沒有內建機制可以在日後偵測物件已超過 45 天;若要檢查物件年齡,仍需要額外的排程邏輯,而觸發本身並不具備此功能。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"A monthly scheduled Lambda function duplicates native Lifecycle expiration with custom code requiring pagination, retries, IAM permissions, and error handling, and its monthly cadence risks objects being retained well past the 45-day mark between executions.","why_zh":"每月排程的 Lambda 函式等同於用自訂程式碼重新實作原生的 Lifecycle 到期功能,需要處理分頁、重試、IAM 權限與錯誤處理,而且每月一次的執行頻率也可能導致物件在兩次執行之間被保留超過 45 天。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"S3 Intelligent-Tiering only automatically moves objects between storage access tiers to optimize cost based on access patterns; it never deletes objects and therefore cannot enforce a data removal policy.","why_zh":"S3 Intelligent-Tiering 只會根據存取模式自動將物件搬移到不同的儲存存取層級以節省成本,它從不刪除物件,因此無法強制執行資料刪除政策。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonS3/latest/userguide/intro-lifecycle-rules.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonS3/latest/userguide/object-lifecycle-mgmt.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonS3/latest/userguide/lifecycle-configuration-examples.html"]}},{"id":99,"question_en":"A company needs centralized log monitoring with automatic detection across hundreds of AWS accounts. Which solution meets these requirements with the LEAST operational effort?","question_zh":"一家公司需要对数百个AWS账户进行集中式日志监控，并实现自动检测。 哪种解决方案在满足这些要求的同时，所需的操作工作量最少？","options_en":{"A":"Designate a GuardDuty administrator account and enable protections.","B":"Centralize CloudWatch logs and use Inspector.","C":"Centralize CloudTrail logs and query with Athena.","D":"Stream logs to Kinesis and process with Lambda."},"options_zh":{"A":"指定一个 GuardDuty 管理员账户并启用保护功能。","B":"集中管理 CloudWatch 日志并使用 Inspector。","C":"集中管理 CloudTrail 日志并使用 Athena 进行查询。","D":"将日志流式传输到 Kinesis 并使用 Lambda 进行处理。"},"answer":["A"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Security/IAM","Compute","Serverless/Integration","Monitoring/Ops","Analytics"],"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選","research":{"verdict":["A"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"AWS documentation confirms GuardDuty is purpose-built for exactly this scenario. Through AWS Organizations, the management account designates a single delegated GuardDuty administrator account, which can then enable and centrally manage GuardDuty for all member accounts in the organization — up to 50,000 member accounts — including setting an 'auto-enable' preference so GuardDuty turns on automatically for existing and future accounts with no per-account setup. Once enabled in an account, GuardDuty 'automatically starts ingesting the foundational data sources' (CloudTrail management events, VPC Flow Logs, DNS logs) and generates findings natively — 'You don't need to enable anything else for GuardDuty to start analyzing and processing these data sources.' This is native, centralized, automatic threat detection at organization scale with essentially zero custom infrastructure, which is the least operational effort of the four options. Option B is wrong because Amazon Inspector performs vulnerability/CVE scanning of EC2, ECR images, and Lambda code — it does not analyze logs for threat activity, and simply centralizing CloudWatch Logs provides no built-in detection logic. Option C only centralizes CloudTrail logs into one location for ad hoc querying via Athena; there is no automatic detection, so engineers must write and continuously maintain their own detection queries. Option D requires building an entire custom log ingestion, parsing, and detection pipeline with Kinesis and Lambda across hundreds of accounts, making it the most operationally intensive option of all.","explanation_zh":"AWS 文件證實 GuardDuty 正是為此情境設計。透過 AWS Organizations,管理帳戶可指定單一委派 GuardDuty 管理帳戶(delegated administrator account),該帳戶即可集中啟用並管理組織內所有成員帳戶的 GuardDuty,最多可支援 50,000 個成員帳戶,並可設定「自動啟用」偏好設定,讓 GuardDuty 對現有及未來新增的帳戶自動啟用,完全不需逐個帳戶手動設定。帳戶一旦啟用 GuardDuty,便會「自動開始擷取基礎資料來源」(CloudTrail 管理事件、VPC Flow Logs、DNS 記錄)並原生產生偵測結果——文件明確指出「不需要再啟用任何其他項目,GuardDuty 就會開始分析並處理這些資料來源」。這代表在組織規模下,以幾乎零自訂基礎架構即可達成原生、集中且自動的威脅偵測,是四個選項中維運負擔最低的方案。選項 B 錯誤,因為 Amazon Inspector 是針對 EC2、ECR 映像及 Lambda 程式碼進行弱點/CVE 掃描,並不會分析日誌中的威脅活動,單純集中 CloudWatch Logs 也沒有內建偵測邏輯。選項 C 只是將 CloudTrail 日誌集中到單一位置供 Athena 臨時查詢,沒有自動偵測能力,工程師仍須自行撰寫並持續維護偵測查詢。選項 D 需要針對數百個帳戶,用 Kinesis 與 Lambda 從零建置完整的日誌擷取、解析與偵測管線,是四個選項中維運工作量最大的方案。","distractors":[{"letter":"B","why_en":"Amazon Inspector performs automated vulnerability and CVE scanning for EC2, ECR container images, and Lambda functions. It does not analyze logs for threat activity, and centralizing CloudWatch Logs alone provides no native cross-account detection logic, so it doesn't meet the stated requirement.","why_zh":"Amazon Inspector 是針對 EC2、ECR 容器映像及 Lambda 函式進行自動化弱點與 CVE 掃描,並不會分析日誌中的威脅活動,單純集中 CloudWatch Logs 也沒有原生的跨帳戶偵測邏輯,無法滿足題目需求。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"Centralizing CloudTrail logs into a single account and querying with Athena provides visibility and searchability, but it is not automatic detection — engineers must design, write, and continuously maintain the detection queries themselves, which increases operational effort significantly.","why_zh":"將 CloudTrail 日誌集中到單一帳戶並用 Athena 查詢,只提供可視性與可查詢性,並非自動偵測,工程師仍須自行設計、撰寫並持續維護偵測查詢,維運負擔明顯較高。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"Streaming logs to Kinesis and processing with Lambda requires building an entire custom log ingestion, parsing, and threat-detection pipeline from scratch across hundreds of accounts, making it the most operationally intensive option among the four.","why_zh":"將日誌串流至 Kinesis 並用 Lambda 處理,需要針對數百個帳戶從零建置完整的日誌擷取、解析與威脅偵測管線,是四個選項中維運工作量最大的方案。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/guardduty/latest/ug/what-is-guardduty.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/guardduty/latest/ug/guardduty_organizations.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/guardduty/latest/ug/guardduty_data-sources.html"]}},{"id":100,"question_en":"A security engineer for a company needs to design an incident response plan that addresses compromised IAM user account credentials. The company uses an organization in AWS Organizations and AWS IAM Identity Center to manage user access. The company uses a delegated administrator account to implement AWS Security Hub. The delegated administrator account contains an organizational trail in AWS CloudTrail that logs all events to an Amazon S3 bucket. The company has also configured an organizational event data store that captures all events from the trail. The incident response plan must provide steps that the security engineer can take to immediately disable any compromised IAM user when the security engineer receives a notification of a security incident. The plan must prevent the IAM user from being used in any AWS account. The plan must also collect all AWS actions that the compromised IAM user performed across all accounts in the previous 7 days. Which solution will meet these requirements?","question_zh":"一家公司的安全工程师需要设计一个事件响应计划，以应对IAM用户账户凭证被泄露的情况。该公司使用AWS Organizations中的组织 架构以及AWS IAM Identity Center来管理用户访问权限。公司通过委派管理员账户来实施AWS Security Hub。该委派管理员账户在 AWS CloudTrail中包含一个组织级追踪功能，用于将所有事件日志记录到Amazon S3存储桶中。此外，公司还配置了组织级事件数据存 储，用于捕获来自该追踪的所有事件。 事件响应计划必须包含安全工程师在收到安全事件通知后，可立即采取的步骤，以禁用任何已遭入侵的IAM用户。该计划必须防止该 IAM用户在任何AWS账户中被使用，并且还需收集该受感染的IAM用户在过去7天内在所有账户中执行的所有AWS操作记录。 哪种解决方案能满足这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Disable the compromised IAM user in the organization management account. Use Amazon Athena to query the organizational CloudTrail logs in the S3 bucket for actions that the IAM user performed in the previous 7 days.","B":"Remove all IAM policies that are attached to the IAM user in the organization management account. Use AWS Security Hub to query the CloudTrail logs for actions that the IAM user performed in the previous 7 days.","C":"Remove any permission sets that are assigned to the IAM user in IAM Identity Center. Use Amazon CloudWatch Logs Insights to query the CloudTrail logs in the S3 bucket for actions that the IAM user performed in the previous 7 days.","D":"Disable the IAM user’s access in IAM Identity Center. Use AWS CloudTrail to query the organizational event data store for actions that the IAM user performed in the previous 7 days."},"options_zh":{"A":"在组织管理账户中禁用受感染的IAM用户。使用Amazon Athena查询S3存储桶中的组织CloudTrail日志，以查找该 IAM用户在过去7天内执行的操作。","B":"删除组织管理账户中与该IAM用户关联的所有IAM策略。使用AWS Security Hub查询CloudTrail日志，以获取该 IAM用户在过去7天内执行的操作。","C":"删除在 IAM 身份中心中分配给该 IAM 用户的任何权限集。使用 Amazon CloudWatch Logs Insights 查询 S3 存储桶中 的 CloudTrail 日志，以查找该 IAM 用户在过去 7 天内执行的操作。","D":"在 IAM Identity Center 中禁用该 IAM 用户的访问权限。使用 AWS CloudTrail 查询组织事件数据存储，以获 取该 IAM 用户在过去 7 天内执行的操作。"},"answer":["D"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Organizations/Governance","Security/IAM","Storage","Monitoring/Ops","Analytics"],"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選","research":{"verdict":["D"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"CORRECTED to D. The first analyst's case for A leans entirely on the literal AWS-resource-type meaning of 'IAM user,' but that literal reading actually breaks option A in two independent ways rather than helping it, and the question's own scenario framing points the other way. First, AWS IAM documentation is explicit that an IAM user 'is an entity that you create in your AWS account' — IAM users and their credentials are strictly per-account resources. There is no single console or API action that disables 'an IAM user' and has that action apply 'across all AWS accounts' in an Organization, because the same person would need a separately-created IAM user in every account. Second, and this is the sharper problem with A specifically in Q100: option A only disables the user 'in the organization management account' — one named account — while the scenario never states the compromised user lives there. If the user's IAM identity actually exists in a member account (the far more common real-world case, and consistent with the company centralizing access through IAM Identity Center rather than scattering standalone IAM users), disabling a user 'in the organization management account' does nothing at all to that compromised identity. So A fails the 'prevent the user from being used in any AWS account' requirement on two counts: per-account IAM scoping, and a location mismatch that the option itself introduces. Third, re-reading the scenario's own setup is decisive here: the company explicitly 'uses AWS IAM Identity Center to manage user access.' That establishes IAM Identity Center as this company's access-management system of record. In that architecture, 'IAM user' in the question stem is being used the way these exam scenarios routinely use it — colloquially, to mean 'the compromised user identity' — not as a claim that a standalone AWS::IAM::User resource is the credential being described. Reading option D under that lens ('Disable the IAM user's access in IAM Identity Center') is exactly what the security engineer would do to the identity the company actually manages. AWS's IAM Identity Center documentation confirms the mechanism: disabling (or deleting) a user 'will immediately be prevented from signing in to the AWS access portal and will not be able to create new sign in sessions,' which is a single action that removes that person's ability to obtain new access to every assigned AWS account and application, not just one account — directly satisfying 'prevent the IAM user from being used in any AWS account' as a single step. Compare this to Q87, where the scenario never mentioned Identity Center as the access path for the compromised entity, leaving more ambiguity; Q100 removes that ambiguity by naming IAM Identity Center as the access-management system up front, which if anything makes the case for D stronger here than in Q87, not weaker. For the audit requirement, AWS CloudTrail Lake's organization event data store is the purpose-built, documented resource that aggregates events from every account in the Organization, queryable with a single SQL statement scoped by eventTime to the trailing 7 days and filtered on the user identity — exactly matching 'collect all AWS actions... across all accounts in the previous 7 days' in one query, and option D correctly names 'AWS CloudTrail' (the service that hosts CloudTrail Lake) as the tool used to run that query. Options A (Athena over S3, plus the management-account-only disable) and C (permission-set removal, which per AWS's own guidance does not immediately terminate an already-active access portal session, plus CloudWatch Logs Insights which is not the native cross-account CloudTrail Lake query surface) and B (Security Hub is a findings aggregator, not a log store, and cannot answer 'all actions in the last 7 days') all fall short of one or both requirements. D is the only option whose disable action is genuinely single-step and cross-account by design, and whose query mechanism is the AWS-documented cross-account audit tool. The dump/community answer of D is confirmed.","explanation_zh":"更正為 D。第一位分析師支持 A 的論點,完全建立在把「IAM user」視為 AWS 資源類型的字面定義上,但這種字面解讀其實從兩個獨立角度都會讓 A 站不住腳,而題目本身的情境設定也指向相反方向。首先,AWS IAM 文件明確指出,IAM user「是您在 AWS 帳戶中建立的實體」——IAM user 與其憑證完全是以帳戶為單位的資源。沒有任何單一主控台或 API 動作能停用某個「IAM user」並使其效果「涵蓋 Organization 中所有 AWS 帳戶」,因為同一個人若要跨帳戶存取,必須在每個帳戶各自建立獨立的 IAM user。其次,這是 A 在 Q100 中更明顯的問題:選項 A 只在「organization management account」(單一指定帳戶)中停用該使用者,但題目從未說明遭入侵的使用者身分就位於該帳戶。若該 IAM 身分實際上存在於某個成員帳戶中(這在現實中更常見,也與公司透過 IAM Identity Center 集中管理存取、而非分散建立獨立 IAM user 的情境相符),那麼在「organization management account」中停用使用者,對該遭入侵身分完全沒有作用。因此 A 在「防止該使用者在任何 AWS 帳戶中被使用」這項需求上,同時犯了兩個錯:IAM 以帳戶為範圍的本質限制,以及選項本身引入的帳戶不符問題。第三,重新檢視題目本身的情境設定具有決定性:公司明確「使用 AWS IAM Identity Center 來管理使用者存取權」。這確立了 IAM Identity Center 是這家公司實際使用的存取管理系統。在這樣的架構下,題目中的「IAM user」正是這類考題常見的用法——泛指「遭入侵的使用者身分」,而非主張所描述的憑證是一個獨立的 AWS::IAM::User 資源。以此角度閱讀選項 D(「在 IAM Identity Center 中停用該 IAM user 的存取權」),正是安全工程師針對公司實際管理的身分所應採取的動作。AWS 的 IAM Identity Center 文件確認了此機制:停用(或刪除)使用者「將立即被阻止登入 AWS access portal,且無法建立新的登入工作階段」——這是單一動作,即可移除該人員取得所有已指派 AWS 帳戶與應用程式新存取權的能力,而非僅限單一帳戶,直接滿足「防止該 IAM user 在任何 AWS 帳戶中被使用」這項單步驟需求。與 Q87 相比,Q87 的情境從未提及 Identity Center 是遭入侵實體的存取途徑,留下更多模糊空間;而 Q100 一開始就明確指出 IAM Identity Center 是存取管理系統,消除了這種模糊性,這使得 D 在本題中的論證比 Q87 更強而非更弱。至於稽核需求,AWS CloudTrail Lake 的 organization event data store 是專為此設計、有文件記載的資源,會彙整 Organization 中所有帳戶的事件,可用單一 SQL 陳述式以 eventTime 限制在過去 7 天內,並依使用者身分篩選——恰好符合「收集過去 7 天內、跨所有帳戶的所有 AWS 動作」這項需求,且選項 D 正確地將「AWS CloudTrail」(承載 CloudTrail Lake 的服務)列為執行該查詢的工具。選項 A(以 Athena 查詢 S3,且僅在管理帳戶停用)、選項 C(移除權限集,但依 AWS 官方指引,這並不會立即終止已存在的 access portal 工作階段,且 CloudWatch Logs Insights 並非原生的跨帳戶 CloudTrail Lake 查詢介面)、以及選項 B(Security Hub 是發現彙整服務,並非日誌儲存,無法回答「過去 7 天內的所有動作」)都未能同時滿足兩項需求。D 是唯一一個停用動作真正屬於單步驟且天生跨帳戶、查詢機制也是 AWS 官方記載之跨帳戶稽核工具的選項。因此確認 dump/社群答案 D 為正確答案。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"Doubly flawed: (1) IAM users are per-account resources ('an entity that you create in your AWS account'), so there is no single action that disables an IAM user 'across all AWS accounts' — each account has its own separate IAM user store; and (2) the option only disables the user 'in the organization management account,' but the scenario never states the compromised user resides there, so if the identity is in a member account this action does not touch it at all. Athena querying S3 also depends on logs already being centralized via the organization trail, which happens to be true here, but that alone doesn't fix the disable-step's scope problem.","why_zh":"有兩個缺陷:(1) IAM user 是以帳戶為範圍的資源(「您在 AWS 帳戶中建立的實體」),因此沒有單一動作能讓 IAM user 的停用『涵蓋所有 AWS 帳戶』——每個帳戶都有各自獨立的 IAM user 儲存;(2) 該選項僅在『organization management account』中停用使用者,但題目從未說明遭入侵的使用者就位於該帳戶,若身分實際位於成員帳戶,此動作完全不會影響到它。以 Athena 查詢 S3 雖然仰賴日誌已透過 organization trail 集中(此題確實如此),但這並不能解決停用步驟本身的範圍問題。"},{"letter":"B","why_en":"Security Hub is a findings aggregator across security services, not a log storage or query engine — it does not retain raw CloudTrail events and cannot answer 'all actions performed by the user in the previous 7 days.' Removing IAM policies also does not disable a user or terminate active sessions/credentials; the user's access key or console session can remain usable via any remaining implicit, resource-based, or cached permissions until credentials are explicitly deactivated.","why_zh":"Security Hub 是跨安全服務的發現彙整工具,並非日誌儲存或查詢引擎——它不會保留原始 CloudTrail 事件,無法回答『使用者過去 7 天內執行的所有動作』。移除 IAM 政策也不會停用使用者或終止已存在的工作階段/憑證;在明確停用憑證之前,該使用者的存取金鑰或主控台工作階段仍可能透過任何殘留的隱含、資源型或快取權限繼續被使用。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"Per AWS's own IAM Identity Center guidance, removing permission set assignments alone does not immediately cut off an active session — if a user already has an active AWS access portal session, they can continue operating with previously assumed roles until access is more thoroughly revoked, so this is a slower/incomplete disable path compared to directly disabling the user. CloudWatch Logs Insights is also not the native, purpose-built cross-account query surface for organization-wide CloudTrail data — that role belongs to CloudTrail Lake's organization event data store, which option D correctly uses.","why_zh":"根據 AWS 官方 IAM Identity Center 指引,單純移除權限集指派並不會立即中斷已存在的工作階段——若使用者已有作用中的 AWS access portal 工作階段,在存取權被更徹底撤銷之前,該使用者仍可繼續使用先前已擔任的角色,因此相較於直接停用使用者,這是較慢且不完整的停用途徑。CloudWatch Logs Insights 也並非原生、專為跨帳戶、跨組織 CloudTrail 資料查詢所設計的介面;這個角色屬於 CloudTrail Lake 的 organization event data store,而選項 D 正確地使用了它。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/singlesignon/latest/userguide/disableuser.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/singlesignon/latest/userguide/deleteusers.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/singlesignon/latest/userguide/revoke-user-permissions.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/IAM/latest/UserGuide/id_users.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/awscloudtrail/latest/userguide/cloudtrail-lake-organizations.html"]}},{"id":101,"question_en":"A company operates an Amazon EC2 instance that is registered as a target of a Network Load Balancer (NLB). The NLB is associated with a security group. The security group allows inbound TCP traffic on port 22 from 10.0.0.0/23. The company maps the NLB to two subnets that share the same network ACL and route table. The route table has a route for 0.0.0.0/0 to an internet gateway. The network ACL has one inbound rule that has a priority of 20 and that allows TCP traffic on port 22 from 10.0.0.0/16. A security engineer receives an alert that there is an unauthorized SSH session on the EC2 instance. The unauthorized session originates from 10.0.1.5. The company ' s incident response procedure requires unauthorized SSH sessions to beimmediately interrupted. The instance must remain running, and its memory must remain intact. Which solution will meet these requirements?","question_zh":"一家公司运行着一个注册为网络负载均衡器（NLB）目标的 Amazon EC2 实例。该 NLB 与一个安 全组相关联，该安全组允许来自 10.0.0.0/23 网段的入站 TCP 流量，端口为 22。 该公司将NLB映射到两个共享同一网络ACL和路由表的子网。该路由表包含一条指向互联网网关的0. 0.0.0/0路由。网络ACL具有一条入站规则，优先级为20，允许来自10.0.0.0/16的TCP 22端口流量。 安全工程师收到警报，称EC2实例上存在未经授权的SSH会话，该会话来自IP地址10.0.1.5。公司事 件响应流程要求立即中断此类未经授权的SSH会话。实例必须保持运行状态，且其内存内容不得被 破坏。 哪种解决方案能满足这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Restart the EC2 instance from either the AWS Management Console or the AWS CLI.","B":"Add a new inbound rule that has a priority of 10 to the network ACL to deny TCP traffic on port 22 from 10.0.1.5.","C":"Remove the security group rule that allows inbound TCP traffic on port 22 from 10.0.0.0/16.","D":"Update the route table to remove the route to the internet gateway."},"options_zh":{"A":"通过 AWS 管理控制台或 AWS CLI 重启 EC2 实例。","B":"向网络ACL添加一条优先级为10的新入站规则，以拒绝来自10.0.1.5的端口22上的TCP流量。","C":"删除允许从 10.0.0.0/16 进入的端口 22 上 TCP 流量的安全组规则。","D":"更新路由表，移除通往互联网网关的路由。"},"answer":["B"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Networking/DNS","Compute"],"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選","research":{"verdict":["B"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"AWS's own documentation resolves this decisively. The EC2 'security group connection tracking' guide states explicitly: 'When you change a security group rule, its tracked connections are not immediately interrupted. The security group continues to allow packets until existing connections time out. To ensure that traffic is immediately interrupted... you can use a network ACL for your subnet. Network ACLs are stateless and therefore do not automatically allow response traffic. Adding a network ACL that blocks traffic in either direction breaks existing connections.' This is the exact scenario in the question: an already-established SSH TCP session must be interrupted immediately. Network ACLs are stateless and are evaluated per packet, in both directions, for every packet that crosses the subnet boundary, including packets belonging to an already-open connection (NACLs save no state about prior packets, so there is no 'established connection' exception the way there is for security groups). Rules are evaluated in ascending rule-number order and the first match wins. Adding an inbound deny rule with priority 10 for source 10.0.1.5 on port 22 is evaluated before the existing priority-20 allow rule, so the very next packet from that attacker IP (in either direction, since return traffic is likewise not automatically permitted) is dropped, tearing down the session immediately. The instance itself is never touched, so it keeps running with memory intact, exactly as required. Option C fails for two independent reasons: (1) the security group in the scenario allows inbound TCP 22 from 10.0.0.0/23, not the 10.0.0.0/16 range this option describes, so no matching rule even exists to remove; (2) more fundamentally, AWS documentation confirms security groups use stateful connection tracking, so even a matching rule change would not immediately interrupt the already-tracked SSH session -- it would continue to be allowed until the tracked connection times out, directly violating the 'immediately interrupted' requirement. Option A (restart) would interrupt the session but explicitly violates the requirement that the instance remain running with memory intact. Option D (removing the internet gateway route) is overly broad, would sever all inbound and outbound internet connectivity for both subnets sharing that route table, and -- since route table changes affect routing rather than an established flow's packet filtering state -- offers no documented guarantee of immediately tearing down an existing connection either. Only B uses the one mechanism AWS explicitly recommends for immediately breaking an existing connection without touching the instance.","explanation_zh":"AWS 官方文件直接解答了這個問題。EC2「security group connection tracking」文件明確指出:「當你變更 security group 規則時,其已追蹤的連線不會立即被中斷。security group 會持續允許封包通過,直到既有連線逾時為止。若要確保流量立即被中斷...可以在子網使用 network ACL。network ACL 是無狀態的,因此不會自動允許回應流量。新增一條在任一方向阻擋流量的 network ACL,會中斷既有連線。」這正是題目描述的情境:必須立即中斷一個已經建立的 SSH TCP session。network ACL 是無狀態的,對於跨越子網邊界的每一個封包,無論方向,都會逐一評估,包含屬於已經開啟連線的封包(因為 NACL 不會保留先前封包的狀態,所以不像 security group 那樣有「已建立連線」的例外)。規則會依規則編號由小到大依序評估,第一個符合的規則即生效。新增一條 priority 為 10、針對來源 10.0.1.5 port 22 的 inbound deny 規則,會在既有 priority 20 的 allow 規則之前被評估,因此該攻擊者 IP 的下一個封包(無論方向,因為回應流量同樣不會被自動允許)就會被丟棄,立即中斷該 session。此過程完全不需要動到 EC2 instance 本身,因此 instance 持續運行、記憶體維持完整,完全符合要求。選項 C 有兩個獨立的錯誤原因:(1) 題目中的 security group 允許的來源是 10.0.0.0/23,並非此選項所描述的 10.0.0.0/16,因此根本沒有對應的規則可以移除;(2) 更根本的問題是,AWS 文件證實 security group 使用 stateful 的連線追蹤機制,因此即使規則範圍相符,變更規則也不會立即中斷已被追蹤的 SSH session,該連線會持續被允許直到追蹤逾時,直接違反「立即中斷」的要求。選項 A(重新啟動)雖能中斷 session,但明確違反了「instance 必須持續運行且記憶體維持完整」的要求。選項 D(移除 internet gateway 路由)範圍過大,會切斷共用該路由表的兩個子網對外的所有連入與連出流量,而且路由表的變更影響的是路由本身,而非既有流量的封包過濾狀態,同樣沒有文件保證能立即中斷既有連線。只有 B 使用了 AWS 官方明確建議、可在不動到 instance 的情況下立即中斷既有連線的機制。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"Restarting the EC2 instance would interrupt the SSH session, but it directly violates the explicit requirement that the instance must remain running and its memory must remain intact for forensic/incident-response purposes.","why_zh":"重新啟動 EC2 instance 雖然能中斷 SSH session,但直接違反了「instance 必須持續運行、記憶體必須維持完整」以供事件回應與取證使用的明確要求。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"The security group in the scenario allows traffic from 10.0.0.0/23, not 10.0.0.0/16 as this option describes, so there is no matching rule to remove. Even if the CIDR matched, AWS documentation confirms security groups use stateful connection tracking: changing or removing a rule does not immediately interrupt already-tracked connections, which continue to be allowed until they time out -- failing the 'immediately interrupted' requirement, and it would also broadly affect all hosts in that CIDR rather than surgically targeting only the attacker.","why_zh":"題目中的 security group 允許的來源是 10.0.0.0/23,並非此選項所描述的 10.0.0.0/16,因此沒有對應規則可移除。即使 CIDR 相符,AWS 文件證實 security group 使用 stateful 連線追蹤機制:變更或移除規則不會立即中斷已被追蹤的連線,該連線會持續被允許直到逾時為止,無法滿足「立即中斷」的要求,而且這樣做也會廣泛影響該 CIDR 範圍內的所有主機,而非精準針對攻擊者。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"Removing the internet gateway route would cut off all inbound and outbound internet connectivity for both subnets sharing that route table, an overly broad and disruptive action, and there is no documented guarantee that a route table change immediately drops packets of an already-established connection the way a stateless network ACL deny rule does.","why_zh":"移除 internet gateway 的路由會切斷共用該路由表的兩個子網對外的所有連入與連出流量,影響範圍過大且具破壞性,而且並沒有文件保證路由表的變更能像無狀態的 network ACL deny 規則一樣,立即丟棄已建立連線的封包。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AWSEC2/latest/UserGuide/security-group-connection-tracking.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/vpc/latest/userguide/vpc-network-acls.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/vpc/latest/userguide/infrastructure-security.html"]}},{"id":102,"question_en":"A security engineer receives a notice about suspicious activity from a Linux-based Amazon EC2 instance that uses Amazon Elastic Block Store (Amazon EBS)-based storage. The instance is making connections to known malicious addresses. The instance is in a development account within a VPC that is in the us-east-1 Region. The VPC contains an internet gateway and has a subnet in us-east-1a and us-east-1b. Each subnet is associated with a route table that uses the internet gateway as a default route. Each subnet also uses the default network ACL. The suspicious EC2 instance runs within the us-east-1b subnet. During an initial investigation, a security engineer discovers that the suspicious instance is the only instance that runs in the subnet. Which response will immediately mitigate the attack and help investigate the root cause?","question_zh":"安全工程师收到一条关于Linux系统Amazon EC2实例的可疑活动通知，该实例使用基于Amazon弹 性块存储（Amazon EBS）的存储，并正在连接已知的恶意地址。 该实例位于美国东部（us-east-1）区域内的一个VPC中的开发账户中。该VPC包含一个互联网网关， 并在us-east-1a和us-east-1b两个可用区中各有一个子网。每个子网都关联了一个使用互联网网关作 为默认路由的路由表，同时每个子网也使用默认的网络ACL。可疑的EC2实例运行在us-east-1b子 网内。在初步调查过程中，安全工程师发现该可疑实例是该子网中唯一运行的实例。 哪种响应能立即缓解攻击并有助于调查根本原因？","options_en":{"A":"Log in to the suspicious instance and use the netstat command to identify remote connections. Use the IP addresses from these remote connections to create deny rules in the security group of the instance. Install diagnostic tools on the instance for investigation. Update the outbound network ACL for the subnet in us-east-1b to explicitly deny all connections as the first rule during the investigation of the instance.","B":"Update the outbound network ACL for the subnet in us-east-1b to explicitly deny all connections as the first rule. Replace the security group with a new security group that allows connections only from a diagnostics security group. Update the outbound network ACL for the us-east-1b subnet to remove the deny all rule. Launch a new EC2 instance that has diagnostic tools. Assign the new security group to the new EC2 instance. Use the new EC2 instance to investigate the suspicious instance.","C":"Ensure that the Amazon Elastic Block Store (Amazon EBS) volumes that are attached to the suspicious EC2 instance will not delete upon termination. Terminate the instance. Launch a new EC2 instance in us-east-1a that has diagnostic tools. Mount the EBS volumes from the terminated instance for investigation.","D":"Create an AWS WAF web ACL that denies traffic to and from the suspicious instance. Attach the AWS WAF web ACL to the instance to mitigate the attack. Log in to the instance and install diagnostic tools to investigate the instance."},"options_zh":{"A":"登录可疑实例，使用 netstat 命令识别远程连接。根据这些远程连接的 IP 地址，在实例的安 全组中创建拒绝规则。在实例上安装诊断工具以进行调查。在调查期间，将 us-east-1b 子 网的出站网络 ACL 更新为第一条规则，明确拒绝所有连接。","B":"将 us-east-1b 区域子网的出站网络 ACL 更新为第一条规则明确拒绝所有连接。用一个新的安 全组替换原有安全组，该新安全组仅允许来自诊断安全组的连接。将 us-east-1b 子网的出站 网络 ACL 更新，移除拒绝所有连接的规则。启动一台配备诊断工具的新 EC2 实例，并将新 安全组分配给该实例。使用这台新的 EC2 实例来调查可疑实例。","C":"确保与可疑EC2实例关联的Amazon弹性块存储（Amazon EBS）卷在实例终止时不会被删除。 终止该实例，然后在us-east-1a区域启动一个配备诊断工具的新EC2实例，并将已终止实例 的EBS卷挂载到新实例上进行调查。","D":"创建一个 AWS WAF 网络 ACL，拒绝与可疑实例之间的流量。将该 AWS WAF 网络 ACL 附 加到实例上以缓解攻击。登录实例并安装诊断工具以调查该实例。"},"answer":["C"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Security/IAM","Storage","Compute"],"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選","research":{"verdict":["B"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"community","explanation_en":"The correct answer is B, not C. Two independent AWS facts break option C and validate B. First, Amazon EBS volumes are strictly tied to their Availability Zone: AWS documentation states 'You can attach volumes to instances that are in the same Availability Zone only,' and the same AZ constraint applies to restoring/attaching volumes for investigation. The compromised instance runs in us-east-1b, so its EBS volumes cannot be attached to a new instance launched in us-east-1a as option C proposes — this makes C technically impossible, not merely a worse choice. Second, AWS's own GuardDuty guidance for remediating a compromised EC2 instance explicitly warns that changing an instance's security group does NOT stop already-established connections: 'The existing tracked connections won't be terminated as a result of changing security groups - only future traffic will be effectively blocked by the new security group,' and it points to enforcing NACLs to cut off suspicious existing connections. NACLs are stateless, so a deny-all outbound rule takes effect immediately against all traffic, including already-tracked malicious connections — which is exactly what is needed to IMMEDIATELY mitigate an actively-beaconing instance. Option B's sequence matches this: (1) set the outbound NACL to deny-all as the first rule, instantly severing all traffic including the malicious C2 connections; (2) replace the instance's security group with one that allows inbound only from a diagnostics security group, establishing a controlled channel; (3) remove the temporary deny-all NACL rule now that the security group enforces isolation, restoring normal subnet-level routing while the instance itself stays locked down; (4) launch a new, trusted EC2 instance with diagnostic tooling, assign it the diagnostics security group, and use it to investigate the suspicious instance over the now-controlled channel — never logging into or trusting the compromised host directly. This is consistent with the same isolate-while-running philosophy AWS documents in its EC2 quarantine automation (isolation security group, no need to stop or terminate the instance) referenced in the earlier Q86 of this exam: Q86 establishes the general, least-overhead containment pattern (isolate via security group, use SSM Run Command for volatile forensics) for a general incident-response setup, while Q102 asks for an active, ongoing malicious connection that must be cut immediately — and even in that more urgent scenario, AWS's documented answer is still isolate first (NACL to kill existing connections, then SG to control future access), not jump straight to termination. Termination is AWS's documented last resort, used only 'if you are unable to identify and stop unauthorized activity' through isolation — it is not the first move, and here it is additionally disqualified by the cross-AZ EBS attachment restriction. Option A fails because security group changes alone do not stop already-established connections (per the GuardDuty doc), and it has the engineer log into and install tools directly on the still-compromised, untrusted host, which is poor forensic hygiene and delays isolation until after manual investigation. Option D is invalid because AWS WAF web ACLs can only be associated with CloudFront distributions, Application Load Balancers, API Gateway REST APIs, AppSync GraphQL APIs, App Runner services, or Verified Access instances — never directly with an EC2 instance.","explanation_zh":"正確答案是 B,不是 C。有兩項獨立的 AWS 事實直接推翻了選項 C,並驗證了 B 的正確性。第一,Amazon EBS 磁碟區與其可用區(Availability Zone)是嚴格綁定的:AWS 文件明確指出「磁碟區只能附加到位於相同可用區的執行個體」,而還原/掛載磁碟區以進行調查時同樣受此限制。受駭執行個體運行在 us-east-1b,因此其 EBS 磁碟區根本無法附加到選項 C 所提議、新啟動於 us-east-1a 的執行個體上 — 這使得 C 在技術上根本不可行,而不只是較差的選擇。第二,AWS 官方針對受駭 EC2 執行個體的補救指引明確警告,僅變更安全群組並不會終止已建立的連線:「變更安全群組不會終止現有已追蹤的連線 — 只有未來的流量才會被新的安全群組有效阻擋」,並指引應搭配強制執行 NACL 規則以切斷可疑的既有連線。NACL 是無狀態的,因此設定 outbound 全部拒絕的規則會立即對所有流量生效,包含已經建立追蹤的惡意連線 — 這正是要「立即」緩解一個持續對外連線的執行個體所需要的做法。選項 B 的步驟正好對應:(1) 將 outbound NACL 設為 deny-all 作為第一條規則,立即切斷所有流量,包括惡意的 C2 連線;(2) 將執行個體的安全群組替換為僅允許來自診斷安全群組連線的新安全群組,建立一個受控的存取通道;(3) 在安全群組已能強制隔離的前提下,移除暫時的 deny-all NACL 規則,恢復子網路層級的正常路由,同時執行個體本身仍受到嚴密管控;(4) 啟動一台新的、受信任且已安裝診斷工具的 EC2 執行個體,賦予其診斷安全群組,透過這個已受控的通道去調查可疑執行個體 — 全程不登入或信任受駭主機本身。這與 AWS 在 EC2 隔離自動化文件中所記載的「維持上線、以隔離取代終止」的原則一致(即本次考試較早的 Q86 所參照的隔離安全群組做法,不需要停止或終止執行個體):Q86 描述的是一般事件應變架構下、維運成本最低的隔離模式(以安全群組隔離,搭配 SSM Run Command 取得揮發性鑑識資料),而 Q102 描述的是一個必須立即切斷的、持續進行中的惡意連線 — 即便情況更為緊急,AWS 文件所給出的做法仍是先隔離(先用 NACL 切斷既有連線,再用安全群組控管未來存取),而不是直接跳到終止執行個體。終止是 AWS 文件中明確的最後手段,僅在「無法識別並停止未授權活動」時才建議使用 — 它並非第一步驟,而在本題中,C 還額外受到跨可用區 EBS 掛載限制而根本不可行。選項 A 之所以錯誤,是因為僅變更安全群組並不會終止已建立的連線(依 GuardDuty 文件所述),而且該選項要求工程師登入並直接在仍受駭、不可信的主機上安裝工具,這是不良的鑑識做法,而且會把隔離動作延後到人工調查之後才進行。選項 D 不成立,因為 AWS WAF 的 web ACL 只能關聯到 CloudFront distribution、Application Load Balancer、API Gateway REST API、AppSync GraphQL API、App Runner 服務或 Verified Access instance — 完全無法直接附加到 EC2 執行個體上。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"Security group changes do not terminate already-established/tracked connections per AWS's own GuardDuty remediation guidance — only future traffic is blocked — so this option fails to immediately stop an already-active malicious connection. It also has the engineer log into and install diagnostic tools directly on the still-untrusted, potentially compromised host before isolating it, which is poor forensic practice and delays containment.","why_zh":"依照 AWS 自己的 GuardDuty 補救指引,變更安全群組並不會終止已建立/已追蹤的連線,只會阻擋未來的流量,因此此選項無法立即阻止已在進行中的惡意連線。此外,它讓工程師在尚未隔離之前,直接登入並在仍不可信、可能受駭的主機上安裝診斷工具,這是不良的鑑識做法,也會拖延圍堵時機。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"Amazon EBS volumes can only be attached to EC2 instances within the same Availability Zone. The compromised instance is in us-east-1b, so its EBS volumes cannot be mounted onto a new instance launched in us-east-1a as this option proposes — the investigation step is technically impossible, not merely riskier than isolating. Terminating first also destroys all volatile evidence (running processes, network connections, memory state), leaving only static disk data for investigation.","why_zh":"Amazon EBS 磁碟區只能附加到位於相同可用區的 EC2 執行個體。受駭執行個體位於 us-east-1b,因此其 EBS 磁碟區無法如此選項所提議掛載到新啟動於 us-east-1a 的執行個體上 — 這個調查步驟在技術上根本不可行,而不僅是比隔離風險更高。此外,先終止執行個體會摧毀所有揮發性證據(執行中的程序、網路連線、記憶體狀態),只留下靜態磁碟資料可供調查。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"AWS WAF web ACLs can only be associated with CloudFront distributions, Application Load Balancers, API Gateway REST APIs, AppSync GraphQL APIs, App Runner services, or Verified Access instances — there is no mechanism to attach a WAF web ACL directly to an EC2 instance, making this option technically impossible.","why_zh":"AWS WAF 的 web ACL 只能關聯到 CloudFront distribution、Application Load Balancer、API Gateway REST API、AppSync GraphQL API、App Runner 服務或 Verified Access instance,並沒有任何機制可以將 WAF web ACL 直接附加到 EC2 執行個體上,因此此選項在技術上根本不可行。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/guardduty/latest/ug/compromised-ec2.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/ebs/latest/userguide/ebs-attaching-volume.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/ebs/latest/userguide/ebs-restoring-volume.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/waf/latest/developerguide/web-acl-associating.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/systems-manager-automation-runbooks/latest/userguide/aws-quarantineec2instance.html"]}},{"id":103,"question_en":"A company is running its application on AWS. The company has a multi-environment setup, and each environment is isolated in a separate AWS account. The company has an organization in AWS Organizations to manage the accounts. There is a single dedicated security account for the organization. The company must create an inventory of all sensitive data that is stored in Amazon S3 buckets across the organization ' s accounts. The findings must be visible from a single location.Which solution will meet these requirements?","question_zh":"一家公司正在 AWS 上运行其应用程序。该公司采用多环境架构，每个环境都隔离在独立的 AWS 账户中，并通过 AWS Organizations 中的一个组织来管理这些账户。该组织还拥有一个专用的安全账户。公司需要创建一份清单，列出所有存储在组 织各账户 Amazon S3 存储桶中的敏感数据，且所有发现结果必须能够在一个统一位置查看。 哪种解决方案能满足这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Set the security account as the delegated administrator for Amazon Macie and AWS Security Hub. Enable and configure Macie to publish sensitive data findings to Security Hub.","B":"Set the security account as the delegated administrator for AWS Security Hub. In each account, configure Amazon Inspector to scan the S3 buckets for sensitive data. Publish sensitive data findings to Security Hub.","C":"In each account, configure Amazon Inspector to scan the S3 buckets for sensitive data. Enable Amazon Inspector integration with AWS Trusted Advisor. Publish sensitive data findings to Trusted Advisor.","D":"In each account, enable and configure Amazon Macie to detect sensitive data. Enable Macie integration with AWS Trusted Advisor. Publish sensitive data findings to Trusted Advisor."},"options_zh":{"A":"将安全账户设置为 Amazon Macie 和 AWS Security Hub 的委派管理员。启用并配置 Macie，使其将敏感数据发现结果 发布到 Security Hub。","B":"将安全账户设置为 AWS Security Hub 的委派管理员。在每个账户中，配置 Amazon Inspector 扫描 S3 存储桶中的敏感数据， 并将敏感数据发现结果发布到 Security Hub。","C":"在每个账户中，配置 Amazon Inspector 以扫描 S3 存储桶中的敏感数据。启用 Amazon Inspector 与 AWS Trusted Advisor 的 集成，并将敏感数据发现结果发布到 Trusted Advisor。","D":"在每个账户中，启用并配置 Amazon Macie 以检测敏感数据。启用 Macie 与 AWS Trusted Advisor 的集成，并将敏感数据发 现结果发布到 Trusted Advisor。"},"answer":["A"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Organizations/Governance","Security/IAM","Storage"],"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選","research":{"verdict":["A"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"Amazon Macie natively supports AWS Organizations delegated administration: the management account can designate a member account (here, the dedicated security account) as the Macie administrator, which then automatically enables Macie for and centrally manages sensitive data discovery across every member account in the organization. Macie also has a built-in integration with AWS Security Hub, and once configured, it publishes both policy findings and sensitive data findings to Security Hub in the standard AWS Security Finding Format (ASFF). Making the security account the delegated administrator for both Macie and Security Hub, and enabling Macie to publish sensitive data findings to Security Hub, gives a single, centralized location (Security Hub in the security account) showing an aggregated inventory of sensitive data findings from every S3 bucket across all accounts. This exactly matches option A. Option B fails because Amazon Inspector does not scan S3 buckets for sensitive data at all -- its documented scan types are limited to Amazon EC2 (vulnerabilities/network exposure), Amazon ECR (container image vulnerabilities), AWS Lambda (code scanning), and Code Security (application code/IaC); there is no S3 sensitive-data discovery capability to publish to Security Hub. Option C fails for the same reason (Inspector has no S3 scanning capability) and additionally proposes routing findings to AWS Trusted Advisor, which has no documented mechanism for ingesting security findings from other services. Option D correctly uses Macie for sensitive data detection but incorrectly routes findings to Trusted Advisor instead of Security Hub; Trusted Advisor provides its own independent checks and recommendations and has no integration that accepts Macie findings, so this would not create a single centralized inventory view.","explanation_zh":"Amazon Macie 原生支援 AWS Organizations 的委派管理員機制:管理帳戶可以指定一個成員帳戶(此處為專用的安全帳戶)作為 Macie 的管理員帳戶,該帳戶便能自動為組織內所有成員帳戶啟用 Macie,並集中管理跨帳戶的敏感資料探索作業。Macie 同時內建與 AWS Security Hub 的整合功能,設定完成後,Macie 會以標準的 AWS Security Finding Format(ASFF)將 policy findings 與 sensitive data findings 一併發布到 Security Hub。將安全帳戶設定為 Macie 與 Security Hub 的委派管理員,並啟用 Macie 將 sensitive data findings 發布至 Security Hub,即可在單一集中位置(安全帳戶中的 Security Hub)看到跨所有帳戶、所有 S3 儲存桶彙整而成的敏感資料清單,完全符合選項 A 的做法。選項 B 錯誤,因為 Amazon Inspector 完全不具備掃描 S3 儲存桶敏感資料的能力 -- 其官方文件列出的掃描類型僅限於 Amazon EC2(漏洞/網路暴露)、Amazon ECR(容器映像漏洞)、AWS Lambda(程式碼掃描)以及 Code Security(應用程式碼/IaC),並無任何 S3 敏感資料探索功能可發布至 Security Hub。選項 C 同樣因 Inspector 缺乏 S3 掃描能力而錯誤,且額外提出將 findings 匯入 AWS Trusted Advisor,但 Trusted Advisor 並無任何記載的機制可接收其他服務的安全性 findings。選項 D 雖然正確使用 Macie 進行敏感資料偵測,但錯誤地將 findings 導向 Trusted Advisor 而非 Security Hub;Trusted Advisor 提供的是自身獨立的檢查與建議,並沒有可接收 Macie findings 的整合功能,因此無法建立單一集中的清單檢視。","distractors":[{"letter":"B","why_en":"Amazon Inspector's documented scan targets are EC2, ECR, Lambda, and Code Security -- it has no capability to scan S3 buckets for sensitive data, so there is nothing for it to publish to Security Hub in this scenario.","why_zh":"Amazon Inspector 官方文件記載的掃描對象僅有 EC2、ECR、Lambda 與 Code Security -- 它並不具備掃描 S3 儲存桶敏感資料的功能,因此在此情境下也沒有任何相關 findings 可發布至 Security Hub。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"This compounds the same flaw as B (Inspector cannot scan S3 for sensitive data) and additionally relies on a nonexistent integration between security scanning services and AWS Trusted Advisor.","why_zh":"此選項延續了與 B 相同的錯誤(Inspector 無法掃描 S3 敏感資料),並額外依賴一個並不存在的、安全掃描服務與 AWS Trusted Advisor 之間的整合機制。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"Macie is the correct tool for sensitive data detection, but Trusted Advisor has no documented integration for ingesting Macie findings, so this would not provide a single centralized inventory view; Security Hub is the correct central destination, not Trusted Advisor.","why_zh":"Macie 確實是偵測敏感資料的正確工具,但 Trusted Advisor 並沒有任何記載的整合機制可接收 Macie 的 findings,因此無法提供單一集中的清單檢視;正確的集中彙整目的地應為 Security Hub,而非 Trusted Advisor。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/macie/latest/user/accounts-mgmt-ao.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/macie/latest/user/accounts-mgmt-ao-administer.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/macie/latest/user/securityhub-integration.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/inspector/latest/user/scanning-resources.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/inspector/latest/user/supported.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/organizations/latest/userguide/services-that-can-integrate-macie.html"]}},{"id":104,"question_en":"An IAM user receives an Access Denied message when the user attempts to access objects in an Amazon S3 bucket. The user and the S3 bucket are in the same AWS account. The S3 bucket is configured to use server- side encryption with AWS KMS keys (SSE-KMS) to encrypt all of its objects at rest by using a customer managed key from the same AWS account. The S3 bucket has no bucket policy defined. The IAM user has been granted permissions through an IAM policy that allows thekms:Decryptpermission to the customer managed key. The IAM policy also allows thes3:List* ands3:Get* permissions for the S3 bucket and its objects. Which of the following is a possible reason that the IAM user cannot access the objects in the S3 bucket?","question_zh":"当IAM用户尝试访问Amazon S3存储桶中的对象时，会收到“访问被拒绝”的消息。该用户与S3存 储桶位于同一个AWS账户中。该S3存储桶已配置为使用AWS KMS密钥（SSE-KMS）进行服务器端 加密，以通过同一AWS账户中的客户管理密钥对所有静态数据进行加密。该S3存储桶未定义任何存 储桶策略。该IAM用户已通过IAM策略获得权限，允许其对客户管理的密钥执行kms:Decrypt操作。 此外，该IAM策略还授予了用户对S3存储桶及其对象的s3:List*和s3:Get*权限。 以下哪一项可能是导致 IAM 用户无法访问 S3 存储桶中对象的原因？","options_en":{"A":"The IAM policy needs to allow thekms:DescribeKeypermission.","C":"An S3 bucket policy needs to be added to allow the IAM user to access the objects.","D":"The KMS key policy has been edited to remove the ability for the AWS account to have full access to the key.","B":"The S3 bucket has been changed to use the AWS managed key to encrypt objects at rest."},"options_zh":{"A":"IAM 策略需要允许 kms:DescribeKey 权限。","B":"S3 存储桶已更改为使用 AWS 管理的密钥对静态数据进行加密。","C":"需要添加一个S3存储桶策略，以允许IAM用户访问对象。","D":"已编辑KMS密钥策略，移除了AWS账户对密钥的完全访问权限。"},"answer":["D"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Security/IAM","Storage"],"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選","research":{"verdict":["D"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"Verified against AWS documentation. Every KMS key's default key policy begins with an 'Enable IAM User Permissions' statement that grants the account root principal kms:* and, per AWS's own wording, 'allows the account to use IAM policies... to delegate the permissions.' AWS KMS docs state explicitly: 'Without this permission, IAM policies that allow access to the key are ineffective, although IAM policies that deny access to the key are still effective.' In this scenario the IAM user already has kms:Decrypt plus s3:List*/s3:Get*, and the Amazon S3 SSE-KMS documentation confirms that for a customer managed key, kms:GenerateDataKey (upload) and kms:Decrypt (download) are the only permissions required -- and that this permission is checked against the key policy. If someone edited the key policy to remove the 'Enable IAM User Permissions' statement (i.e. removed the account's own full/root access to the key), the account can no longer use IAM policies to grant kms:Decrypt at all, so the otherwise-correct IAM policy becomes ineffective and Access Denied results. That is exactly option D. Option A is ruled out: I checked both the general SSE-KMS permissions page and the S3 403-troubleshooting page, and both list only kms:GenerateDataKey and kms:Decrypt as required for GetObject/PutObject -- there is no documented requirement for kms:DescribeKey to download or view an SSE-KMS object, whether via the API/CLI or the S3 console (DescribeKey is a separate requirement for viewing key details in the KMS console itself, not for S3 object access). Option B contradicts the question's explicit premise that the bucket uses a customer managed key. Option C is unnecessary because IAM identity-based policies alone are sufficient for same-account S3 access; no bucket policy is required. There is exactly one correct answer.","explanation_zh":"已對照 AWS 官方文件驗證。每個 KMS 金鑰的預設金鑰政策一開始都有一個「Enable IAM User Permissions」陳述,授予該帳戶 root 主體 kms:* 權限,並依 AWS 文件所述「允許該帳戶使用 IAM policy 來委派這些權限」。AWS KMS 文件明確指出:「若移除此權限,允許存取金鑰的 IAM policy 將失效,但拒絕存取的 IAM policy 仍然有效」。在此情境中,該 IAM 使用者已經擁有 kms:Decrypt 以及 s3:List*/s3:Get*,而 Amazon S3 的 SSE-KMS 文件也確認:對於 customer managed key,下載物件只需要 kms:Decrypt(上傳則需要 kms:GenerateDataKey),且這項權限會對照 key policy 進行檢查。若有人編輯 key policy 移除了「Enable IAM User Permissions」陳述(也就是移除了該帳戶本身對金鑰的完整/root 存取權),該帳戶就無法再透過 IAM policy 授予 kms:Decrypt,原本正確的 IAM policy 因此失效,導致 Access Denied。這正是選項 D 所描述的情況。選項 A 可排除:我查閱了 SSE-KMS 權限說明頁面與 S3 403 疑難排解頁面,兩者都只列出 kms:GenerateDataKey 與 kms:Decrypt 為 GetObject/PutObject 所需權限,並無任何文件指出下載或檢視 SSE-KMS 物件需要 kms:DescribeKey,無論是透過 API/CLI 或 S3 主控台皆然(DescribeKey 是在 KMS 主控台檢視金鑰詳細資訊時的另一項需求,與 S3 物件存取無關)。選項 B 與題目明確敘述「該儲存桶使用 customer managed key」的前提矛盾。選項 C 並非必要,因為同一帳戶內單靠 IAM 身分政策即足以授予 S3 存取權,不需要額外的 bucket policy。本題僅有一個正確答案。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"Confirmed via both the SSE-KMS permissions documentation and the S3 403-error troubleshooting guide: only kms:GenerateDataKey (upload) and kms:Decrypt (download) are required for a customer managed key. kms:DescribeKey is never listed as a requirement for S3 GetObject, via API, CLI, or the console, so this cannot explain the Access Denied.","why_zh":"已透過 SSE-KMS 權限文件與 S3 403 錯誤疑難排解指南確認:customer managed key 僅需要 kms:GenerateDataKey(上傳)與 kms:Decrypt(下載)。無論透過 API、CLI 或主控台,文件從未將 kms:DescribeKey 列為 S3 GetObject 的必要權限,因此不能解釋此處的 Access Denied。"},{"letter":"B","why_en":"This directly contradicts the question's stated setup that the bucket 'is configured to use SSE-KMS... by using a customer managed key,' so assuming it silently switched to the AWS managed key is inconsistent with the given facts.","why_zh":"此選項與題目明確敘述的「該儲存桶使用 customer managed key 進行 SSE-KMS 加密」直接矛盾,假設它悄悄切換為 AWS managed key 與題目給定事實不一致。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"Since the user and bucket are in the same AWS account, IAM identity-based policies alone are sufficient to grant S3 access; a bucket policy is not required for same-account access when suitable IAM permissions already exist.","why_zh":"由於使用者與儲存桶在同一個 AWS 帳戶內,單靠 IAM 身分政策即足以授予 S3 存取權;在已有適當 IAM 權限的情況下,同帳戶存取並不需要額外的 bucket policy。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/kms/latest/developerguide/key-policy-default.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonS3/latest/userguide/UsingKMSEncryption.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonS3/latest/userguide/troubleshoot-403-errors.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/kms/latest/developerguide/policy-evaluation.html","https://repost.aws/knowledge-center/s3-bucket-access-default-encryption","https://repost.aws/knowledge-center/decrypt-kms-encrypted-objects-s3"]}},{"id":105,"question_en":"A company needs to develop a code-signing application that will use a certificate authority (CA) to sign a code-signing certificate. The solution must use an AWS KMS asymmetric key. The solution needs to collect and store immutable evidence about the creation, origin, and use of the KMS key for compliance purposes. This information must be made available to internal auditors. Which solution meets these requirements?","question_zh":"一家公司需要开发一个代码签名应用程序，该程序将使用证书颁发机构（CA）来签署代码签名证书。解决方案必须使用 AWS KMS 的非对称密钥，并需收集和存储有关 KMS 密钥创建、来源和使用的不可篡改的证据，以满足合规要求。这些信 息必须可供内部审计人员访问。 哪种解决方案符合这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Create an Amazon S3 bucket with S3 Object Lock enabled. Create an AWS CloudTrail trail with an event selector and log file validation enabled for all kms.amazonaws.com CreateKey events. Configure the event selector to send the CreateKey events to the S3 bucket. Create the KMS key. Update the event selector to filter for API calls that reference the KMS key ARN. Provide the auditors with access to the S3 bucket.","B":"Implement logging for application operations that reference the KMS key. Ensure that the logs contain all associated metadata. Store the logs in an Amazon CloudWatch Logs log group. Configure an automated export of the log group. Send the export to the auditors.","C":"Create an Amazon DynamoDB table that the auditors can access. Create an AWS Lambda function that an Amazon EventBridge rule invokes. Configure the EventBridge rule to monitor KMS API calls. Configure the EventBridge rule to filter for all API calls that reference the KMS key ARN. Configure the Lambda function to store the contents of the API calls in the DynamoDB table.","D":"Set up Amazon CloudWatch Logs Insights with a custom metric to track KMS key usage. Visualize the metrics by using a CloudWatch dashboard with real-time monitoring. Configure CloudWatch alarms. Use a subscription filter to replicate the data to a separate account for the auditors to review."},"options_zh":{"A":"创建一个启用S3对象锁定功能的Amazon S3存储桶。创建一个AWS CloudTrail追踪，为所有kms.amazonaws.com CreateKey事件启用事件选择器和日志文件验证功能。配置事件选择器，将CreateKey事件发送到该S3存储桶。创建 KMS密钥。更新事件选择器，以筛选引用该KMS密钥ARN的API调用。向审计人员授予访问该S3存储桶的权限。","B":"为引用KMS密钥的应用程序操作实现日志记录。确保日志包含所有相关的元数据。将日志存储在Amazon CloudWatch Logs的日志组中。配置日志组的自动导出，并将导出内容发送给审计人员。","C":"创建一个审计员可访问的 Amazon DynamoDB 表。创建一个由 Amazon EventBridge 规则触发的 AWS Lambda 函数。配 置 EventBridge 规则以监控 KMS API 调用，并设置该规则筛选所有引用 KMS 密钥 ARN 的 API 调用。配置 Lambda 函数将这些 API 调用的内容存储到 DynamoDB 表中。","D":"使用自定义指标设置 Amazon CloudWatch Logs Insights 以跟踪 KMS 密钥使用情况。通过 CloudWatch 控制面板可视化 这些指标，并实现实时监控。配置 CloudWatch 警报。使用订阅过滤器将数据复制到另一个账户，供审计人员审查。"},"answer":["A"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Security/IAM","Storage","Compute","Database","Serverless/Integration","Monitoring/Ops"],"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選","research":{"verdict":["A"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"Verified against AWS documentation on CloudTrail log file validation, S3 Object Lock, and KMS/CloudTrail integration. The requirement is 'immutable evidence' of a KMS key's creation, origin, and use for compliance auditing -- this requires both (1) prevention of tampering/deletion and (2) cryptographic proof that no tampering occurred. S3 Object Lock delivers (1): AWS documentation states it 'can help prevent Amazon S3 objects from being deleted or overwritten for a fixed amount of time or indefinitely' using a write-once-read-many (WORM) model, and it has been independently assessed by Cohasset Associates for SEC 17a-4, CFTC, and FINRA regulatory use -- squarely a 'compliance' storage mechanism. CloudTrail log file integrity validation delivers (2): it uses SHA-256 hashing for each log file and SHA-256-with-RSA digital signing of hourly digest files (each referencing the signature of the prior digest, forming a chain), making it 'computationally infeasible to modify, delete, or forge CloudTrail log files without detection.' Combining both is exactly how AWS defines tamper-evident, durable audit evidence. On sequencing: this is not overcomplicated, it is necessary. The KMS/CloudTrail integration documentation confirms AWS KMS adds the affected key's ARN into the responseElements field of the log entry for key-management operations 'even when the API operation doesn't return the key ARN' -- meaning the CreateKey event itself is how you learn the new key's ARN. Since the key does not exist before CreateKey runs, you cannot pre-filter an event selector by that key's ARN; you must first capture CreateKey broadly (by eventSource kms.amazonaws.com, a management event), let the key be created, extract its ARN from the resulting log entry, and only then narrow the event selector to that specific ARN to continuously capture all subsequent 'use' (Sign/Verify, GetPublicKey, PutKeyPolicy, etc.) events tied to that exact key. That two-step sequence is required to capture both origin (the CreateKey event) and ongoing use (post-creation events scoped to the key's ARN) with a single trail. Option A is the only option that pairs a genuine WORM control with a cryptographically verifiable, tamper-evident log stream, and gives auditors direct, least-privilege read access to that evidence store. Option B (CloudWatch Logs, manually exported) has no WORM guarantee and no cryptographic integrity chain -- entries and exports can be altered or the manual export step skipped/tampered with, and CloudWatch Logs retention/mutation controls don't provide compliance-grade immutability. Option C (DynamoDB via EventBridge/Lambda) stores plain, mutable rows; DynamoDB items can be updated or deleted by any principal with write permission, and there's no cryptographic chain proving the data wasn't altered after being written. Option D (CloudWatch Logs Insights, metrics, dashboards, alarms, cross-account subscription filter) is built for monitoring and alerting, not immutable evidentiary retention -- none of its components enforce WORM or provide tamper-evidence, and it doesn't address the 'origin' (key creation) requirement at all. There is exactly one correct answer.","explanation_zh":"已對照 AWS 官方文件(CloudTrail log file validation、S3 Object Lock、KMS 與 CloudTrail 整合)進行驗證。題目要求針對 KMS 金鑰的建立、來源與使用保存「不可變(immutable)」的合規證據 -- 這需要同時具備(1)防止竄改/刪除的機制,以及(2)可加密驗證未遭竄改的證明。S3 Object Lock 提供(1):AWS 文件指出它「可協助防止 Amazon S3 物件在固定時間內或無限期地被刪除或覆寫」,採用 write-once-read-many(WORM)模型,且已由 Cohasset Associates 針對 SEC 17a-4、CFTC 與 FINRA 法規用途進行獨立評估 -- 正是典型的「合規」儲存機制。CloudTrail log file integrity validation 提供(2):它針對每個 log file 使用 SHA-256 雜湊,並對每小時產生的 digest file 使用 SHA-256 with RSA 數位簽署(每個 digest 皆包含前一個 digest 的簽章,形成鏈狀結構),使得「在不被偵測到的情況下修改、刪除或偽造 CloudTrail log file 在運算上是不可行的」。將兩者結合,正是 AWS 定義「防竄改、持久的稽核證據」的標準做法。關於流程順序:這並非過度複雜,而是必要的。KMS 與 CloudTrail 整合文件確認,AWS KMS 會將受影響金鑰的 ARN 加入金鑰管理操作的 log 項目的 responseElements 欄位,「即使該 API 操作本身不會回傳金鑰 ARN」-- 也就是說,CreateKey 事件本身正是你得知新金鑰 ARN 的方式。由於金鑰在 CreateKey 執行前尚不存在,你無法事先以該金鑰的 ARN 篩選 event selector;必須先廣泛擷取 CreateKey(以 eventSource kms.amazonaws.com 這類 management event 為條件),待金鑰建立後,從產生的 log 項目取得其 ARN,再將 event selector 縮小為該特定 ARN,以持續擷取後續所有與該金鑰相關的「使用」事件(如 Sign/Verify、GetPublicKey、PutKeyPolicy 等)。這個兩階段流程正是在單一 trail 中同時擷取「來源」(CreateKey 事件)與「持續使用」(建立後依 ARN 篩選的事件)所必需的。選項 A 是唯一同時具備真正 WORM 控制與可加密驗證、防竄改的 log 串流,並讓稽核人員以最小權限直接讀取該證據儲存區的選項。選項 B(CloudWatch Logs、手動匯出)沒有 WORM 保證,也沒有加密完整性鏈 -- 項目與匯出結果都可能被更改,或手動匯出步驟可能被跳過或竄改,CloudWatch Logs 的保留/變更控制並不具備合規等級的不可變性。選項 C(透過 EventBridge/Lambda 寫入 DynamoDB)儲存的是一般、可變的資料列;任何具有寫入權限的主體都能更新或刪除 DynamoDB 項目,且沒有加密鏈可證明資料寫入後未被竄改。選項 D(CloudWatch Logs Insights、自訂指標、儀表板、警示、跨帳戶訂閱過濾器)是為監控與警示而設計,而非不可變證據保存 -- 其任何元件皆未強制執行 WORM 或提供防竄改證明,且完全未處理「來源」(金鑰建立)這項需求。本題僅有一個正確答案。","distractors":[{"letter":"B","why_en":"CloudWatch Logs has no WORM guarantee and no cryptographic integrity-validation chain analogous to CloudTrail digest files. A manually exported log is also not tamper-evident -- the export step itself, and the exported copy, can be altered without detection, so this does not meet an 'immutable evidence' bar.","why_zh":"CloudWatch Logs 不具備 WORM 保證,也沒有類似 CloudTrail digest file 的加密完整性驗證鏈。手動匯出的日誌同樣不具防竄改性 -- 匯出步驟本身以及匯出後的副本都可能在未被偵測的情況下遭到更改,因此無法達到「不可變證據」的標準。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"DynamoDB items written via a Lambda function are ordinary mutable database records; any principal with dynamodb:UpdateItem/DeleteItem permission can alter or remove them, and there is no built-in cryptographic proof (comparable to CloudTrail's SHA-256 digest signing) that the stored call data hasn't been changed since it was written.","why_zh":"透過 Lambda 函式寫入的 DynamoDB 項目屬於一般可變的資料庫記錄;任何具有 dynamodb:UpdateItem/DeleteItem 權限的主體都能修改或刪除這些記錄,且並無類似 CloudTrail SHA-256 digest 簽署的內建加密證明,無法保證儲存的呼叫資料自寫入後未遭更改。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"This entire stack (Logs Insights, custom metrics, dashboards, alarms, cross-account subscription filter) is designed for real-time monitoring and alerting, not evidentiary retention. None of these components enforce write-once storage or provide cryptographic tamper-evidence, and the design never addresses capturing the key's creation/origin at all.","why_zh":"整套架構(Logs Insights、自訂指標、儀表板、警示、跨帳戶訂閱過濾器)是為即時監控與警示而設計,並非用於證據保存。這些元件都未強制執行一次寫入(write-once)的儲存方式,也未提供加密防竄改證明,且此設計完全未處理擷取金鑰建立/來源資訊的需求。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonS3/latest/userguide/object-lock.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/awscloudtrail/latest/userguide/cloudtrail-log-file-validation-intro.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/awscloudtrail/latest/userguide/cloudtrail-log-file-validation-enabling.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/kms/latest/developerguide/logging-using-cloudtrail.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/awscloudtrail/latest/userguide/logging-management-events-with-cloudtrail.html"]}},{"id":106,"question_en":"A security engineer discovers that a company ' s user passwords have no required minimum length. The company is using the following two identity providers (IdPs): • AWS Identity and Access Management (IAM) federated with on-premises Active Directory • Amazon Cognito user pools that contain the user database for an AWS Cloud application that the company developed Which combination of actions should the security engineer take to implement a required minimum length for the passwords? (Select TWO.)","question_zh":"一名安全工程师发现，该公司用户的密码没有设置最低长度要求。该公司正在使用以下两个身 份提供商（IdP）： • AWS 身份和访问管理（IAM）与本地 Active Directory 实现联合 • 亚马逊 Cognito 用户池，包含该公司开发的 AWS 云应用程序的用户数据库 安全工程师应采取哪些操作组合来实施密码所需的最小长度？（选择两项。）","options_en":{"A":"Update the password length policy in the IAM configuration.","B":"Update the password length policy in the Cognito configuration.","C":"Update the password length policy in the on-premises Active Directory configuration.","D":"Create an SCP in AWS Organizations. Configure the SCP to enforce a minimum password length for IAM and Cognito.","E":"Create an IAM policy that includes a condition for minimum password length. Enforce the policy for IAM and Cognito."},"options_zh":{"A":"在 IAM 配置中更新密码长度策略。","B":"在 Cognito 配置中更新密码长度策略。","C":"更新本地 Active Directory 配置中的密码长度策略。","D":"在 AWS Organizations 中创建一个服务控制策略（SCP），并配置该策略以强制 IAM 和 Cognito 使用最小密码长度。","E":"创建一个包含最小密码长度条件的 IAM 策略，并对 IAM 和 Cognito 强制执行该策略。"},"answer":["B","C"],"multi":true,"vote":{},"tags":["Organizations/Governance","Security/IAM","Database"],"difficulty":2,"diff_why":"複選","research":{"verdict":["B","C"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"both","explanation_en":"There are two separate identity sources here, and each one enforces its own password rules independently of IAM. First, the on-premises Active Directory is federated into AWS (via AD Connector/SAML). AD-federated users never have an IAM user password at all — they authenticate against AD and receive temporary AWS credentials through STS. Because of this, the IAM account password policy (IAM > Account settings) has no effect on them: AWS documentation is explicit that this policy is a 'password policy for IAM users' and governs only native IAM user console passwords, not identities coming from an external IdP. The only place that can raise the minimum password length for these users is the AD password policy itself (Option C). Second, the mobile/web app uses an Amazon Cognito user pool for its own local users. Cognito user pools have their own independently configurable password policy (minimum length, character requirements, temporary password validity, etc.) set per pool, which is documented as the mechanism to enforce complexity for local Cognito users (Option B). Note that even Cognito explicitly states federated users don't use the user pool password at all — reinforcing that each IdP's own password store must be configured directly. Together, B and C cover both identity sources; there is no cross-cutting IAM policy, condition key, or SCP that can enforce password length on AD or Cognito credentials.","explanation_zh":"這裡有兩個各自獨立的身分來源,各自用自己的規則管理密碼,而不是透過 IAM 統一控管。首先,地端 Active Directory 是透過聯合驗證 (federation,例如 AD Connector/SAML) 接入 AWS 的,這些使用者根本沒有 IAM 使用者密碼——他們是向 AD 驗證身分後,透過 STS 取得臨時憑證。因此 IAM 帳戶密碼政策 (IAM > Account settings) 對他們完全沒有作用;AWS 文件明確指出該政策是「IAM 使用者的密碼政策」,只管理原生 IAM 使用者的主控台密碼,不涉及外部 IdP 的身分。唯一能提高這些使用者最短密碼長度的地方,就是 AD 本身的密碼原則 (選項 C)。第二,App 使用 Amazon Cognito 使用者集區管理自己的本地使用者,而 Cognito 使用者集區有自己獨立可設定的密碼原則 (最短長度、字元要求、臨時密碼有效期等),每個集區各自設定,這正是強制本地 Cognito 使用者密碼複雜度的官方作法 (選項 B)。值得一提的是,Cognito 文件也明確說明聯合使用者根本不使用使用者集區密碼——再次證實必須直接到各個 IdP 自己的密碼儲存區去設定。B 和 C 合起來涵蓋了這兩個身分來源;並不存在能同時管控 AD 與 Cognito 密碼長度的跨服務 IAM 政策、條件鍵或 SCP。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"The IAM account password policy only governs native IAM user console passwords. AD-federated users authenticate through the external IdP and never have an IAM password to begin with, so changing this setting has zero effect on them.","why_zh":"IAM 帳戶密碼政策只管理原生 IAM 使用者的主控台密碼。AD 聯合驗證的使用者是透過外部 IdP 驗證,本來就沒有 IAM 密碼,所以修改這項設定對他們完全沒有影響。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"Service control policies (SCPs) manage which AWS API actions principals in an account/OU can call — they have no mechanism to define or enforce password complexity/length for Cognito user pool users or AD accounts. No such SCP capability exists.","why_zh":"服務控制政策 (SCP) 管理的是帳戶/OU 內主體可以呼叫哪些 AWS API 動作,並沒有機制可以定義或強制 Cognito 使用者集區使用者或 AD 帳戶的密碼複雜度/長度。並不存在這種 SCP 功能。"},{"letter":"E","why_en":"IAM policies with condition keys constrain API call context (e.g., MFA present, source IP) for actions the principal is permitted to perform — there is no IAM condition key that validates or enforces a minimum password length, and IAM policies have no jurisdiction over Cognito user pool password rules or AD credentials at all.","why_zh":"帶有條件鍵的 IAM 政策是用來限制主體執行動作時的 API 呼叫情境 (例如是否有 MFA、來源 IP 等),並沒有任何 IAM 條件鍵可以驗證或強制最短密碼長度,而且 IAM 政策本來就管不到 Cognito 使用者集區的密碼規則或 AD 的憑證。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/IAM/latest/UserGuide/id_credentials_passwords_account-policy.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/cognito/latest/developerguide/managing-users-passwords.html"]}},{"id":107,"question_en":"A company uses SAML federation to grant users access to AWS accounts. A company workload that is in an isolated AWS account runs on immutable infrastructure with no human access to Amazon EC2. The company requires a specialized user known as a break-glass user to have access to the workload AWS account and instances in the case of SAML errors. A recent audit discovered that the company did not create the break- glass user for the AWS account that contains the workload. The company must create the break-glass user. The company must log any activities of the break-glass user and send the logs to a security team. Which combination of solutions will meet these requirements? (Select TWO.)","question_zh":"一家公司使用SAML联合身份验证来授予用户访问AWS账户的权限。该公司位于隔离的AWS账户中 的工作负载运行在不可变的基础设施上，且无任何人员可访问Amazon EC2。公司 需要一个称为“破窗用户”的专用用户，在发生SAML错误时，才能访问工作负载的AWS账户和实例。最近的一次审 计发现，该公司未为包含该工作负载的AWS账户创建破窗用户。 公司必须创建“破窗”用户。公司必须记录“破窗”用户的任何操作活动，并将日志发送给安全团队。 哪种解决方案的组合可以满足这些要求？（选择两项。）","options_en":{"A":"Create a local individual break-glass IAM user for the security team. Create a trail in AWS CloudTrail that has Amazon CloudWatch Logs turned on. Use Amazon EventBridge to monitor local user activities.","B":"Create a break-glass EC2 key pair for the AWS account. Provide the key pair to the security team. Use AWS CloudTrail to monitor key pair activity. Send notifications to the security team by using Amazon SNS.","C":"Create a break-glass IAM role for the account. Allow security team members to perform the AssumeRoleWithSAML operation. Create an AWS CloudTrail trail that has Amazon CloudWatch Logs turned on. Use Amazon EventBridge to monitor security team activities.","D":"Create a local individual break-glass IAM user on the operating system level of each workload instance. Configure unrestricted security groups on the instances to grant access to the break-glass IAM users.","E":"Configure AWS Systems Manager Session Manager for Amazon EC2. Configure an AWS CloudTrail filter based on Session Manager. Send the results to an Amazon SNS topic."},"options_zh":{"A":"为安全团队创建一个本地的独立应急IAM用户。在AWS CloudTrail中创建一个启用Amazon CloudWatch Logs的日志 追踪。使用Amazon EventBridge监控本地用户的活动。","B":"为AWS账户创建一个紧急访问用的EC2密钥对，将该密钥对提供给安全团队。使用AWS CloudTrail监控密钥对的活 动，并通过Amazon SNS向安全团队发送通知。","C":"为该账户创建一个破窗IAM角色，允许安全团队成员执行AssumeRoleWithSAML操作。创建一个启用Amazon CloudWatch日志的AWS CloudTrail追踪，并使用Amazon EventBridge监控安全团队的操作活动。","D":"在每个工作负载实例的操作系统级别创建本地的独立“破玻璃”IAM用户，并为这些实例配置无限制的安全组，以授 予“破玻璃”IAM用户访问权限。","E":"为 Amazon EC2 配置 AWS Systems Manager Session Manager。基于 Session Manager 配置 AWS CloudTrail 过滤器， 并将结果发送到 Amazon SNS 主题。"},"answer":["A","E"],"multi":true,"vote":{},"tags":["Security/IAM","Compute","Serverless/Integration","Monitoring/Ops"],"difficulty":2,"diff_why":"複選","research":{"verdict":["A","E"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"both","explanation_en":"A break-glass user exists precisely to provide access when the normal authentication path (here, SAML federation) has failed, so the account-level break-glass mechanism must not itself depend on the SAML IdP being available. AWS's own emergency-access guidance is explicit on this point: if you want a configuration that does not depend on the external identity provider, you set up 'AWS break-glass access' as an alternative to SAML-based federation, and break-glass procedures are defined to cover scenarios including 'the failure of the organization's identity provider.' That means the question's 'SAML errors' scenario is the general case of IdP/federation failure, not some narrower issue isolated to one account -- so a break-glass path that still round-trips through SAML does not solve the stated problem for any account. Option A creates a standalone local IAM user (independent of the external IdP) for the security team, with an AWS CloudTrail trail delivering to CloudWatch Logs and Amazon EventBridge monitoring its activity -- this satisfies account-level emergency access that keeps working even during a full SAML outage, plus the required logging and notification to the security team. Option C's AssumeRoleWithSAML still requires the SAML IdP to authenticate the security team member before the role can be assumed; even if one argues the security team has 'their own' SAML session, they are still going through the same SAML trust relationship and IdP infrastructure that is stated to be in error, so C is self-defeating for the account-access requirement. For instance-level access on immutable infrastructure with no routine human access to EC2, AWS Systems Manager Session Manager provides secure, keyless, auditable shell access without opening inbound ports or requiring SSH key pairs, and session activity/API calls are natively recorded in AWS CloudTrail, which can be filtered and routed to Amazon SNS to notify the security team (option E). Together, A covers account-level break-glass access and E covers instance-level access, meeting both layers the question asks for with proper logging in each. Option B relies on an EC2 key pair handed to the security team, which contradicts the immutable/no-human-access design and provides weaker auditability than Session Manager. Option D creates OS-level local users on each instance and opens unrestricted security groups, a severe anti-pattern that exposes instances to the entire internet and is incompatible with an immutable, no-direct-access architecture. There are exactly two correct options: A and E.","explanation_zh":"break-glass 使用者存在的目的，正是為了在正常驗證途徑（此處為 SAML 聯合驗證）失效時仍能提供存取能力，因此帳戶層級的 break-glass 機制本身不應依賴 SAML IdP 正常運作。AWS 官方的緊急存取指引明確指出：若希望配置不依賴外部身分提供者，應設定「AWS break-glass access」作為 SAML 聯合驗證的替代方案，且 break-glass 程序的設計情境本身就包含「組織的身分提供者發生故障」。這表示題目中「SAML 錯誤」的情境是指聯合驗證/IdP 層級的普遍性故障，而非侵限於某單一帳戶的狹隘問題——因此任何仍需繞經 SAML 的 break-glass 途徑，都無法解決題目所描述的問題。選項 A 建立一個獨立的本機 IAM 使用者（不依賴外部身分提供者）供安全團隊使用，並透過啟用 Amazon CloudWatch Logs 的 AWS CloudTrail 追蹤搭配 Amazon EventBridge 監控活動，即使在 SAML 完全中斷期間仍可運作，同時滿足所需的記錄與安全團隊通知需求。選項 C 的 AssumeRoleWithSAML 仍需要 SAML IdP 先驗證安全團隊成員身分才能扮演角色；即便安全團隊有「自己的」SAML 工作階段，仍是透過同一套發生錯誤的 SAML 信任關係與 IdP 基礎設施，因此就帳戶層級存取需求而言，C 是自我矛盾的設計。至於在不允許人員直接存取 EC2 的不可變基礎設施上進行執行個體層級存取，AWS Systems Manager 的 Session Manager 提供安全、免金鑰、可稽核的 Shell 存取方式，不需開放連入連接埠或使用 SSH 金鑰對，且其工作階段活動與 API 呼叫會原生記錄於 AWS CloudTrail，可篩選後透過 Amazon SNS 通知安全團隊（選項 E）。A 負責帳戶層級的 break-glass 存取，E 負責執行個體層級存取，兩者合併涵蓋題目要求的兩個層面，並各自具備妥善記錄。選項 B 依賴交付給安全團隊的 EC2 金鑰對，與「不可變、無人員存取」的設計相矛盾，且稽核能力遜於 Session Manager。選項 D 在每個執行個體的作業系統層級建立本機使用者，並開放無限制的安全群組，是嚴重的安全反模式，會將執行個體暴露於整個網際網路，與不可變且禁止直接存取的架構原則不符。正確答案恰好為兩個：A 與 E。","distractors":[{"letter":"B","why_en":"An EC2 key pair handed directly to the security team contradicts the immutable infrastructure design with no human access to instances, and key-pair SSH access is far less auditable than Session Manager's native CloudTrail-recorded sessions; it does not address the account-level SAML-failure access requirement at all.","why_zh":"直接交付給安全團隊的 EC2 金鑰對違背了不可變基礎設施且不允許人員存取執行個體的設計，且以金鑰對進行 SSH 存取的可稽核性遠不如 Session Manager 原生透過 CloudTrail 記錄的工作階段；此選項也完全未處理帳戶層級 SAML 失效時的存取需求。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"Allowing the security team to perform AssumeRoleWithSAML still routes through the same SAML identity provider and trust relationship that AWS's break-glass guidance identifies as the very thing that can fail; a solution meant to survive 'SAML errors' cannot itself require SAML authentication to succeed, making this option self-defeating.","why_zh":"讓安全團隊執行 AssumeRoleWithSAML，仍會經過與 AWS break-glass 指引中所指出可能故障的同一套 SAML 身分提供者與信任關係；一個本應在「SAML 發生錯誤」時仍可運作的解法，不能反過來要求 SAML 驗證成功，因此此選項自相矛盾。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"Creating OS-level local users on each instance plus unrestricted security groups is a severe security anti-pattern that exposes instances to the entire internet, and is fundamentally inconsistent with an immutable, no-direct-human-access infrastructure design.","why_zh":"在每個執行個體上建立作業系統層級的本機使用者，並搭配無限制的安全群組，是嚴重的安全反模式，會將執行個體暴露於整個網際網路，且從根本上與不可變、禁止人員直接存取的基礎設施設計原則不符。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/singlesignon/latest/userguide/emergency-access.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/wellarchitected/latest/devops-guidance/ag.sad.5-implement-break-glass-procedures.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/singlesignon/latest/userguide/emergency-access-implementation.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/systems-manager/latest/userguide/session-manager-auditing.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/systems-manager/latest/userguide/session-manager-logging-cloudwatch-logs.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/systems-manager/latest/userguide/session-manager.html"]}},{"id":108,"question_en":"A security engineer needs to protect a public web application that runs in a VPC. The VPC hosts the origin for an Amazon CloudFront distribution. The application has experienced multiple layer 7 DDoS attacks. An AWS WAF web ACL is associated with the CloudFront distribution. The web ACL contains one AWS managed rule to protect against known IP addresses that have bad reputations. The security engineer must configure an automated solution that detects and mitigates layer 7 DDoS attacks in real time with no manual effort. Which solution will meet these requirements?","question_zh":"安全工程师需要保护一个运行在VPC中的公共Web应用程序。该VPC托管了Amazon CloudFront分发的源站。该应用曾遭受 多次第七层DDoS攻击。已将AWS WAF网络ACL与CloudFront分发关联，该网络ACL包含一条AWS托管规则，用于防护具 有不良声誉的已知IP地址。 安全工程师必须配置一种自动化解决方案，以实时检测并缓解第七层DDoS攻击，且无需人工干预。 哪种解决方案能满足这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Enable AWS Shield Advanced on the CloudFront distribution. Configure alerts in Amazon CloudWatch for DDoS indicators.","B":"Enable AWS Shield Advanced and configure proactive engagement with the AWS DDoS Response Team (DRT).","C":"Deploy AWS Network Firewall in the VPC. Create security policies that detect DDoS indicators. Create an AWS Lambda function to automatically update the web ACL rules during an attack.","D":"Add a rate-based rule to the web ACL. Enable AWS Shield Advanced. Enable automatic application layer DDoS mitigation on the CloudFront distribution."},"options_zh":{"A":"在 CloudFront 分发中启用 AWS Shield Advanced，并在 Amazon CloudWatch 中为 DDoS 指标配置告警。","B":"启用 AWS Shield Advanced 并配置与 AWS DDoS 响应团队（DRT）的主动协作。","C":"在VPC中部署AWS网络防火墙，创建用于检测DDoS迹象的安全策略，并创建一个AWS Lambda函数，在攻击发生时自动更新Web ACL规则。","D":"向网络ACL添加基于速率的规则。启用AWS Shield Advanced。在CloudFront分发中启用自动 应用层DDoS缓解。"},"answer":["D"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Networking/DNS","Security/IAM","Compute","Monitoring/Ops"],"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選","research":{"verdict":["D"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"Verified against the AWS WAF/Shield Advanced documentation. The feature 'Shield Advanced automatic application layer DDoS mitigation' is described precisely: when you enable it on a resource (here, the CloudFront distribution) that is associated with a web ACL, Shield Advanced automatically adds a dedicated rule group (name starts with ShieldMitigationRuleGroup) to that web ACL. This rule group always contains a rate-based rule, ShieldKnownOffenderIPRateBasedRule, which immediately rate-limits traffic from known DDoS sources as a front-line defense. During an actual attack, Shield Advanced also analyzes traffic to identify an attack signature, validates it against historical traffic so it won't affect legitimate requests, and then automatically deploys custom AWS WAF rules into that same rule group to Block (or Count) the malicious traffic -- all without any human writing or updating WAF rules. The docs also explicitly recommend, as an optional but recommended step, adding a rate-based rule to the web ACL for baseline per-IP protection even before Shield Advanced's automatic rules kick in. This maps exactly to option D: add a rate-based rule to the web ACL, enable Shield Advanced (a prerequisite -- automatic application layer mitigation is a Shield Advanced-only feature, not available under Shield Standard), and enable automatic application layer DDoS mitigation on the CloudFront distribution. This delivers real-time, automated detection and mitigation with zero manual effort, exactly as required. There is exactly one correct answer.","explanation_zh":"已對照 AWS WAF / Shield Advanced 官方文件驗證。「Shield Advanced automatic application layer DDoS mitigation」這項功能的行為描述得非常明確:當你在已關聯 web ACL 的資源(此處為 CloudFront distribution)上啟用此功能後,Shield Advanced 會自動在該 web ACL 中新增一個專屬 rule group(名稱以 ShieldMitigationRuleGroup 開頭)。這個 rule group 永遠包含一條 rate-based rule,名為 ShieldKnownOffenderIPRateBasedRule,會立即針對已知的 DDoS 來源進行流量速率限制,作為第一線防禦。在實際攻擊發生時,Shield Advanced 還會分析流量以找出攻擊特徵,並先對照歷史流量驗證該特徵不會影響正常請求,然後自動在同一個 rule group 中部署自訂的 AWS WAF 規則,以 Block(或 Count)惡意流量——整個過程完全不需要人工撰寫或更新 WAF 規則。文件也明確建議(選用但建議的步驟)在 web ACL 中加入 rate-based rule,以在 Shield Advanced 的自動規則生效之前提供基本的單一 IP 防護。這正好對應選項 D:在 web ACL 加入 rate-based rule、啟用 Shield Advanced(這是前提條件——automatic application layer DDoS mitigation 是 Shield Advanced 專屬功能,Shield Standard 不提供),並在 CloudFront distribution 上啟用 automatic application layer DDoS mitigation。這樣就能達到即時、自動化的偵測與緩解,完全不需人工介入,正好符合題目要求。本題僅有一個正確答案。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"Enabling Shield Advanced and configuring CloudWatch alerts only gives visibility and notification of DDoS indicators (metrics/alarms). It does not perform any mitigation -- a human still has to see the alert and take action (e.g., write or update a WAF rule). This fails the 'automated detection and mitigation' requirement and requires manual effort.","why_zh":"啟用 Shield Advanced 並設定 CloudWatch 警示,只能提供 DDoS 指標的可見性與通知(metrics/alarms),並不會執行任何緩解動作——仍需要有人看到警示後才能採取行動(例如撰寫或更新 WAF 規則)。這無法滿足「自動化偵測與緩解」的要求,仍需人工介入。"},{"letter":"B","why_en":"Shield Advanced with proactive engagement means AWS's Shield Response Team (SRT) will proactively reach out and assist during an attack, but this is a human-in-the-loop, support-based engagement -- not an automated, real-time technical mitigation mechanism. It does not by itself deploy WAF rules automatically.","why_zh":"Shield Advanced 搭配 proactive engagement,代表 AWS 的 Shield Response Team (SRT) 會在攻擊發生時主動聯繫並協助客戶,但這是需要人工介入的支援性服務,並非自動化、即時的技術緩解機制。它本身並不會自動部署 WAF 規則。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"AWS Network Firewall operates within the VPC at the network/transport layer (L3/L4) on VPC traffic, and CloudFront sits in front of the VPC as a global edge service -- Network Firewall cannot inspect or protect CloudFront's layer 7 (HTTP/HTTPS) traffic. Building a custom Lambda-based detection-and-WAF-update pipeline also reinvents, with far more operational complexity and latency, functionality that Shield Advanced's automatic application layer DDoS mitigation already provides natively and faster.","why_zh":"AWS Network Firewall 運作於 VPC 內部的網路/傳輸層(L3/L4),用於檢查 VPC 流量,而 CloudFront 是位於 VPC 之前的全球邊緣服務——Network Firewall 無法檢查或保護 CloudFront 的第 7 層(HTTP/HTTPS)流量。此外,自行建置以 Lambda 為基礎的偵測並更新 web ACL 的機制,等同於重新發明 Shield Advanced automatic application layer DDoS mitigation 原生就已提供、且反應更快的功能,同時大幅增加維運複雜度與延遲。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/waf/latest/developerguide/ddos-automatic-app-layer-response-config.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/waf/latest/developerguide/ddos-automatic-app-layer-response-behavior.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/waf/latest/developerguide/ddos-automatic-app-layer-response-rg.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/waf/latest/developerguide/ddos-app-layer-protections.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/waf/latest/developerguide/manage-protection.html"]}},{"id":109,"question_en":"A company is running a new workload across accounts in an organization in AWS Organizations. All running resources must have a tag of CostCenter, and the tag must have one of three approved values. The company must enforce this policy and must prevent any changes of the CostCenter tag to a non-approved value. Which solution will meet these requirements?","question_zh":"一家公司正在 AWS Organizations 中的多个账户间运行新的工作负载。所有运行中的资源都必须包含 名为 CostCenter 的标签，且该标签的值必须为三个批准值之一。公司必须强制执行此策略，并防止将 CostCenter 标签更改为未批准的值。 哪种解决方案能满足这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Use AWS Config custom policy rule and an SCP to deny non-approved aws:RequestTag/CostCenter values.","B":"Use CloudTrail + EventBridge + Lambda to block creation.","C":"Enable tag policies, define allowed values, enforce noncompliant operations, and use an SCP to deny creation when aws:RequestTag/CostCenter is null.","D":"Enable tag policies and use EventBridge + Lambda to block changes."},"options_zh":{"A":"使用 AWS Config 自定义策略规则和 SCP 来拒绝未经批准的 aws:RequestTag/CostCenter 值。","B":"使用 CloudTrail + EventBridge + Lambda 来阻止创建。","C":"启用标签策略，定义允许的值，强制执行不合规操作，并使用 SCP 在 aws:RequestTag/CostCenter 为空时拒绝创建。","D":"启用标签策略，并使用 EventBridge 和 Lambda 来阻止更改。"},"answer":["C"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Organizations/Governance","Compute","Serverless/Integration","Monitoring/Ops"],"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選","research":{"verdict":["C"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"both","explanation_en":"Verified directly against the AWS Organizations tag policies documentation. Enabling a tag policy with 'Basic compliance rules' and the 'Prevent noncompliant operations for this tag' setting (the enforced_for field in JSON) genuinely blocks -- not just reports on -- resource creation and tagging API calls that supply a CostCenter value outside the allowed list; this is a true request-time preventive control, confirmed by the enforcement doc's own wording: 'you can prevent resource creation with tag values that do not meet the requirements specified in your tag policy... blocks Amazon EC2 create operations if the supplied CostCenter tag key does not have a tag value of...'. However, the same page explicitly flags a gap: 'Basic compliance rules do not enforce tag compliance on resources that are created without tags... You cannot use this capability to ensure that required or mandatory tag keys are configured at resource creation,' and it directs readers to close that gap with 'Use SCPs to prevent IAM users and roles in target accounts from creating certain resource types if the request doesn't include the specified tags.' The tag-policies best-practices page repeats this as an explicit recommendation: 'Consider creating an SCP to set guardrails around resource creation requests... Resources that have never had tags attached to them don't show as noncompliant in reports... you can use a service control policy (SCP) to set guardrails around resource creation requests.' So the tag-policy-plus-null-check-SCP pairing in option C is AWS's own documented combined pattern, and together the two halves are complete: the tag policy enforcement mode blocks wrong/non-approved CostCenter values, and the SCP with a Null condition on aws:RequestTag/CostCenter denies creation when the tag is absent altogether -- covering both the 'must have one of three approved values' and 'prevent changes to non-approved values' requirements for every resource across the org. Option A fails because AWS Config rules (including custom policy rules built on Config) are a detective/reporting control -- they evaluate resource configuration after the fact and record compliance status, they do not block the underlying API call, so pairing it with an SCP still only covers the wrong-value case and does nothing preventive for missing tags beyond what the SCP itself does; it also doesn't use the org-wide tag policy mechanism AWS designed for this exact requirement. Option B (CloudTrail + EventBridge + Lambda to 'block creation') is inherently reactive: CloudTrail events and EventBridge rules fire after an API call has already been logged, so by the time a Lambda function could act, the resource has already been created with the noncompliant tag -- this is remediation, not prevention. Option D has the same reactive flaw (EventBridge/Lambda run after the tagging event has occurred) and also doesn't invoke tag policy's actual preventive enforcement mode, so it can't genuinely 'block' changes in real time. There is exactly one correct answer: C.","explanation_zh":"已直接對照 AWS Organizations tag policies 官方文件驗證。啟用 tag policy 的「Basic compliance rules」並勾選「Prevent noncompliant operations for this tag」(JSON 中的 enforced_for 欄位),確實會真正封鎖(而不只是回報)帶有不在允許清單內 CostCenter 值的資源建立與標籤 API 呼叫;這是貨真價實的請求時預防性控制,文件原文寫道:「you can prevent resource creation with tag values that do not meet the requirements specified in your tag policy... blocks Amazon EC2 create operations if the supplied CostCenter tag key does not have a tag value of...」。不過同一頁文件也明確指出其缺口:「Basic compliance rules do not enforce tag compliance on resources that are created without tags... You cannot use this capability to ensure that required or mandatory tag keys are configured at resource creation」,並建議以「Use SCPs to prevent IAM users and roles in target accounts from creating certain resource types if the request doesn't include the specified tags」來補上這個缺口。tag policies 最佳實務頁面也重複了這項明確建議:「Consider creating an SCP to set guardrails around resource creation requests... Resources that have never had tags attached to them don't show as noncompliant in reports... you can use a service control policy (SCP) to set guardrails around resource creation requests」。因此選項 C 中「tag policy 強制模式 + null 檢查 SCP」的搭配,正是 AWS 官方文件記載的建議組合,而且兩者合併後涵蓋完整需求:tag policy 的強制模式封鎖錯誤/未核准的 CostCenter 值,而針對 aws:RequestTag/CostCenter 使用 Null 條件的 SCP 則在標籤完全缺失時拒絕建立——同時滿足「必須具備三個核准值之一」與「防止變更為非核准值」這兩項需求,適用於組織內所有資源。選項 A 錯誤,因為 AWS Config 規則(包括建立在 Config 之上的自訂政策規則)屬於偵測性/回報性控制——它們是在資源設定完成後才進行評估並記錄合規狀態,並不會封鎖底層的 API 呼叫,因此即使搭配 SCP,也只能處理錯誤值的情境,對於缺少標籤的情況並沒有比 SCP 本身多提供任何預防效果;此外它也沒有使用 AWS 專為此需求設計的組織層級 tag policy 機制。選項 B(CloudTrail + EventBridge + Lambda 來「封鎖建立」)本質上是被動反應式的:CloudTrail 事件與 EventBridge 規則是在 API 呼叫已被記錄之後才觸發,等到 Lambda 函式能採取行動時,資源早已用不合規的標籤建立完成——這是事後補救,而非事前預防。選項 D 有相同的被動反應缺陷(EventBridge/Lambda 是在標籤事件發生之後才執行),而且也沒有啟用 tag policy 真正的預防性強制模式,因此無法真正即時「封鎖」變更。本題確實只有一個正確答案:C。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"AWS Config (including custom policy rules) is a detective/reporting mechanism: it evaluates resources after they exist and reports compliance status, it does not block the API call at request time. Pairing it with an SCP still leaves no preventive coverage beyond what the SCP alone provides, and it bypasses the org-wide tag policy feature AWS built specifically to enforce approved tag values.","why_zh":"AWS Config(包括自訂政策規則)屬於偵測性/回報性機制:它是在資源已經存在之後才進行評估並回報合規狀態,並不會在請求時封鎖 API 呼叫。搭配 SCP 之後,其預防效果並不會超出 SCP 本身所能提供的範圍,而且也繞過了 AWS 專為強制核准標籤值而設計的組織層級 tag policy 功能。"},{"letter":"B","why_en":"CloudTrail logs and EventBridge rules fire only after an API call has already been recorded, meaning any resource has already been created with the noncompliant tag before a Lambda function could react. This is a reactive remediation pattern, not a preventive control, and does not meet a 'prevent' requirement.","why_zh":"CloudTrail 日誌與 EventBridge 規則只會在 API 呼叫已被記錄之後才觸發,也就是說在 Lambda 函式能做出反應之前,資源早已帶著不合規標籤被建立完成。這屬於事後補救的被動模式,並非預防性控制,無法滿足「prevent」的需求。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"Even with tag policies enabled, using EventBridge and Lambda to 'block changes' is still reactive -- the event fires after the tagging operation has already occurred, so the change cannot genuinely be blocked in real time. This approach also doesn't leverage tag policy's actual enforcement (blocking) mode.","why_zh":"即使啟用了 tag policies,使用 EventBridge 與 Lambda 來「封鎖變更」仍然是被動反應式的——事件是在標籤操作已經發生之後才觸發,因此無法真正即時封鎖該項變更。此做法也沒有運用 tag policy 真正的強制(封鎖)模式。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/organizations/latest/userguide/orgs_manage_policies_tag-policies-enforcement.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/organizations/latest/userguide/orgs_manage_policies_tag-policies-best-practices.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/organizations/latest/userguide/orgs_manage_policies_supported-resources-enforcement.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/organizations/latest/userguide/orgs_manage_policies_tag-policies-getting-started.html"]}},{"id":110,"question_en":"A company has an organization in AWS Organizations. The company uses AWS IAM Identity Center and an external identity provider to manage access. The company needs a solution that maintains access to AWS if the identity provider has an outage. The solution must be able to attribute any emergency access to an individual administrator. Which solution will meet these requirements?","question_zh":"一家公司使用 AWS Organizations 进行组织管理，并通过 AWS IAM Identity Center 和外部身份提供商来管理访问权限。该公 司需要一种解决方案，以确保在身份提供商发生中断时仍能维持对 AWS 的访问。该解决方案必须能够将任何紧急访问行为 追溯到特定的管理员个人。 哪种解决方案能满足这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Create IAM users for emergency administrators. Set strong passwords and MFA for the IAM users. Assign permissions that grant the IAM users cross-account access to accounts within the organization to perform emergency change actions.","B":"Create emergency users within the identity provider. Enable System for Cross-domain Identity Management provisioning to help ensure mapping between IAM Identity Center and the identity provider. Assign permission sets in IAM Identity Center to the emergency users to give the users cross- account access to perform emergency change actions.","C":"Configure a secondary identity provider in IAM Identity Center. Create emergency users in the secondary identity provider that have permissions to perform cross-account emergency change actions. Change the IAM Identity Center external identity provider to the secondary identity provider.","D":"Create access keys for the management account’s root user. Store the access keys in a shared secret vault for use by any emergency administrator. Use the access keys to perform emergency change actions across the organization."},"options_zh":{"A":"为应急管理员创建 IAM 用户。为这些 IAM 用户设置强密码并启用多因素认证（MFA）。分配权限，使 IAM 用户能够 跨账户访问组织内的其他账户，以执行紧急变更操作。","B":"在身份提供商中创建紧急用户。启用跨域身份管理（SCIM）配置，以帮助确保 IAM Identity Center 与身份提供商之间的映射关系。将 IAM Identity Center 中的权限集分配给这些紧急用户， 使其能够跨账户访问并执行紧急变更操作。","C":"在 IAM Identity Center 中配置一个备用身份提供商。在该备用身份提供商中创建具有执行跨账 户紧急变更操作权限的紧急用户。将 IAM Identity Center 的外部身份提供商更改为该备用身 份提供商。","D":"为管理账户的根用户创建访问密钥，并将这些密钥存储在共享的密钥保险库中，供任何应 急管理员使用。利用这些访问密钥在组织范围内执行紧急变更操作。"},"answer":["A"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Organizations/Governance","Security/IAM"],"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選","research":{"verdict":["A"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"AWS's own IAM Identity Center emergency-access documentation states that the IdP-federation-based break-glass configuration (using your external IdP to sign in directly to accounts, or by extension SCIM-provisioned emergency users) 'works when IAM Identity Center is unavailable, but the IAM data plane and your external identity provider (IdP) are available,' and explicitly says: 'If you prefer to not depend on the external IdP, consider setting up AWS break-glass access' using native IAM users. AWS's IAM documentation reinforces this: creating an IAM user is 'one of the recommended reasons to create an IAM user so that you can access your AWS account if your identity provider isn't accessible.' Option A creates individual, named IAM users (with strong passwords and MFA, and cross-account role permissions) entirely outside the IAM Identity Center/external IdP chain, so they remain usable during an IdP outage, and each administrator's actions are attributable via CloudTrail through their own distinct IAM user identity. Option B still depends on SCIM provisioning and sign-in through the very external IdP that is down, so it fails during the exact scenario described. Option C is impractical and still IdP-dependent: IAM Identity Center supports only one active external identity source at a time, switching it is a slow manual operation, and if admins normally authenticate via the down IdP they may be unable to reach the console to make the change in the first place. Option D violates AWS's explicit best practice of never creating access keys for the root user, and a credential shared by multiple emergency administrators in a vault cannot attribute actions to an individual, since CloudTrail would log the same principal for everyone who uses it. Therefore A is the only solution that is both resilient to an external IdP outage and provides individual attribution.","explanation_zh":"AWS 官方 IAM Identity Center 緊急存取文件指出,依賴外部 IdP 聯合驗證的緊急存取設定(直接透過外部 IdP 登入帳戶,或以此延伸的 SCIM 佈建緊急使用者)「僅在 IAM Identity Center 無法使用,但 IAM 資料層與您的外部身分提供者(IdP)仍可使用時才有效」,並明確建議「若不想依賴外部 IdP,可考慮設定 AWS break-glass access」,即使用原生 IAM 使用者。AWS IAM 文件也強調,建立 IAM 使用者是「當您的身分提供者無法存取時,用以存取 AWS 帳戶的建議情境之一」。選項 A 建立個別、具名的 IAM 使用者(具備強密碼與 MFA,並搭配跨帳戶角色權限),完全獨立於 IAM Identity Center/外部 IdP 的聯合驗證鏈之外,因此在 IdP 中斷期間仍可使用,且每位管理員都有各自獨立的 IAM 使用者身分,可透過 CloudTrail 個別歸責。選項 B 仍依賴 SCIM 佈建以及透過那個正在中斷的外部 IdP 進行登入,因此在題目描述的情境下正好會失效。選項 C 不切實際且仍依賴 IdP:IAM Identity Center 一次只能有一個作用中的外部身分來源,切換身分來源是緩慢的手動操作,若管理員平常就是透過已中斷的 IdP 登入,可能連主控台都無法存取以進行此變更。選項 D 違反 AWS 明確的最佳實務,即絕不應為 root 使用者建立存取金鑰,而且存放在密碼庫中、由多位緊急管理員共用的憑證無法將操作歸責到個別管理員,因為 CloudTrail 會將所有使用者的操作記錄為同一個 principal。因此,選項 A 是唯一能在外部 IdP 中斷時仍具韌性,且能個別歸責的解決方案。","distractors":[{"letter":"B","why_en":"Emergency users provisioned via SCIM and authenticated through IAM Identity Center's federation with the external IdP still fundamentally depend on that same IdP being reachable, so this approach fails during exactly the outage scenario the question describes.","why_zh":"透過 SCIM 佈建、並透過 IAM Identity Center 與外部 IdP 聯合驗證的緊急使用者,本質上仍依賴該同一個 IdP 可被存取,因此在題目描述的中斷情境下正好會失效。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"IAM Identity Center supports only one active external identity source at a time, and switching to a secondary IdP during an active outage is a slow, disruptive manual change rather than a standing emergency mechanism, and admins who normally sign in via the down IdP may be unable to reach the console to perform the switch.","why_zh":"IAM Identity Center 一次只能有一個作用中的外部身分來源,在中斷期間切換到次要 IdP 是緩慢且具破壞性的手動變更,並非現成的緊急機制,而且平常透過已中斷 IdP 登入的管理員可能無法存取主控台來執行此切換。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"Creating root user access keys directly contradicts AWS's explicit best practice of never generating root access keys, and a credential shared among multiple emergency administrators provides no individual attribution in CloudTrail logs.","why_zh":"建立 root 使用者存取金鑰直接違反 AWS 明確的最佳實務(絕不應產生 root 存取金鑰),且由多位緊急管理員共用同一組憑證,在 CloudTrail 記錄中無法做到個別歸責。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/singlesignon/latest/userguide/emergency-access.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/IAM/latest/UserGuide/getting-started-emergency-iam-user.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/wellarchitected/latest/devops-guidance/ag.sad.5-implement-break-glass-procedures.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/singlesignon/latest/userguide/emergency-access-planning.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/IAM/latest/UserGuide/root-user-best-practices.html"]}},{"id":111,"question_en":"A company runs an application on a fleet of Amazon EC2 instances. The application is accessible to users around the world. The company associates an AWS WAF web ACL with an Application Load Balancer (ALB) that routes traffic to the EC2 instances. A security engineer is investigating a sudden increase in traffic to the application. The security engineer discovers a significant amount of potentially malicious requests coming from hundreds of IP addresses in two countries. The security engineer wants to quickly limit the potentially malicious requests. The security engineer does not want to prevent legitimate users from accessing the application. Which solution will meet these requirements?","question_zh":"一家公司在一组 Amazon EC2 实例上运行应用程序，该应用程序面向全球用户开放。公司为一个 应用负载均衡器（ALB）关联了 AWS WAF 网站访问控制列表（web ACL），由该负载均衡器将 流量路由到 EC2 实例。 安全工程师正在调查应用程序流量的突然增加。该工程师发现，来自两个国家数百个IP地址的大量 请求可能具有恶意性质。安全工程师希望快速限制这些潜在的恶意请求，但又不希望阻止合法用户 访问应用程序。 哪种解决方案能满足这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Use AWS WAF to implement a rate-based rule for all incoming requests.","B":"Use AWS WAF to implement a geographical match rule to block all incoming traffic from the two countries.","C":"Edit the ALB security group to include a geographical match rule to block all incoming traffic from the two countries.","D":"Add deny rules to the ALB security group that prohibit incoming requests from the IP addresses."},"options_zh":{"A":"使用 AWS WAF 为所有传入请求实施基于速率的规则。","B":"使用 AWS WAF 实施地理位置匹配规则，阻止来自这两个国家的所有传入流量。","C":"编辑ALB安全组，添加地理位置匹配规则，以阻止来自这两个国家的所有传入流量。","D":"向ALB安全组添加拒绝规则，禁止来自这些IP地址的传入请求。"},"answer":["A"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Networking/DNS","Security/IAM","Compute"],"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選","research":{"verdict":["A"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"The requirement has two parts: (1) quickly limit the malicious requests, and (2) do not block legitimate users. AWS WAF rate-based rules count incoming requests per aggregation key (by default, source IP address) over a rolling evaluation window and only rate-limit (e.g., block) the specific IPs whose request rate exceeds the configured threshold. This targets the abusive behavior directly, regardless of the requester's country, so legitimate users everywhere -- including any legitimate users located in the same two countries as the attackers -- continue to be served normally as long as their request rate stays under the threshold. A geographic match rule (B) would block ALL traffic from the two named countries, including any legitimate customers located there, which directly violates the requirement not to prevent legitimate users from accessing the application. Security groups (C and D) are stateful, allow-only virtual firewalls: AWS VPC documentation explicitly states 'You can specify allow rules, but not deny rules,' and security groups have no geographic matching capability at all -- they only evaluate protocol, port, and source/destination IP/CIDR or security group references. Therefore C and D are not technically achievable as described. The correct and only defensible answer is A. This question is a near-duplicate of Q93 in the same exam (identical scenario and options, with only a cosmetic sentence-split rephrasing of the requirement); re-verifying against current AWS WAF rate-based-rule and VPC security-group documentation confirms the same conclusion applies with no change.","explanation_zh":"此需求包含兩個要件：(1) 快速限制惡意請求，(2) 不能封鎖合法使用者。AWS WAF 的 rate-based rule 會依聚合鍵值（預設為來源 IP 位址）在滾動評估視窗內計算請求數量，只針對超過設定門檻的特定 IP 進行限速或封鎖。這種做法是針對「異常行為」本身，而不是針對「來源國家」，因此無論這些惡意 IP 來自哪個國家，只要某個使用者的請求頻率未超過門檻，該使用者（即使身處那兩個國家）仍能正常存取應用程式，完全符合「不封鎖合法使用者」的要求。選項 B 的 geographic match rule 會封鎖來自那兩個國家的「所有」流量，包含當地合法客戶，直接違反題目明確提出的限制條件。至於選項 C 與 D，security group 是 stateful、僅支援「允許（allow）」規則的虛擬防火牆：AWS VPC 官方文件明確指出「You can specify allow rules, but not deny rules」，而且 security group 完全沒有地理位置比對能力，只能依協定、埠號、以及來源/目的 IP 或 CIDR（或安全群組參照）進行比對。因此 C、D 在技術上根本無法實作題目所描述的規則。正確且唯一合理的答案是 A。此題與同份考卷的第 93 題幾乎完全相同（情境與選項一致，需求說明僅將一句話拆成兩句、無實質語義差異）；重新比對現行 AWS WAF rate-based rule 與 VPC security group 官方文件後，結論不變。","distractors":[{"letter":"B","why_en":"Geographic match rules block or allow traffic strictly by the country of origin derived from the source IP. This would indiscriminately block every request from the two countries, including legitimate users located there, directly violating the requirement not to prevent legitimate users from accessing the application.","why_zh":"Geographic match rule 是依來源 IP 判斷所屬國家後整批允許或封鎖流量。這會不分青紅皂白地封鎖那兩個國家的所有請求，包含當地的合法使用者，直接違反題目「不能阻擋合法使用者」的要求。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"Security groups have no geographic matching capability whatsoever -- they can only filter by protocol, port, and source/destination IP address, CIDR range, or referenced security group. This option describes a feature that does not exist for security groups.","why_zh":"Security group 完全沒有地理位置比對功能，只能依協定、埠號、以及來源/目的 IP、CIDR 範圍或參照的 security group 來過濾流量。此選項描述的是 security group 並不具備的功能。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"Security groups only support allow rules; there is no way to add explicit deny rules to a security group to block specific IP addresses. Blocking hundreds of individual IPs this way is also operationally impractical even if it were possible.","why_zh":"Security group 只支援允許（allow）規則，無法針對特定 IP 位址新增明確的拒絕（deny）規則。即便技術上可行，要逐一封鎖數百個 IP 也在維運上不切實際。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/waf/latest/developerguide/waf-rule-statement-type-rate-based.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/waf/latest/developerguide/waf-rule-statement-type-geo-match.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/vpc/latest/userguide/security-group-rules.html"]}},{"id":112,"question_en":"A company runs a global ecommerce website that is hosted on AWS. The company uses Amazon CloudFront to serve content to its user base. The company wants to block inbound traffic from a specific set of countries to comply with recent data regulation policies. Which solution will meet these requirements MOST cost-effectively?","question_zh":"一家公司运营着一个托管在 AWS 上的全球电子商务网站，并使用 Amazon CloudFront 向用户分发内 容。该公司希望根据最新的数据监管政策，阻止来自特定国家的入站流量。 哪种解决方案能以最具成本效益的方式满足这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Create an AWS WAF web ACL with an IP match condition to deny the countries ' IP ranges. Associate the web ACL with the CloudFront distribution.","B":"Create an AWS WAF web ACL with a geo match condition to deny the specific countries. Associate the web ACL with the CloudFront distribution.","C":"Use the geo restriction feature in CloudFront to deny the specific countries.","D":"Use geolocation headers in CloudFront to deny the specific countries."},"options_zh":{"A":"创建一个 AWS WAF 网站访问控制列表（web ACL），并添加 IP 匹配条件以拒绝指定国家的 IP 地址范围，然后将该 web ACL 与 CloudFront 分发关联。","B":"创建一个带有地理位置匹配条件的 AWS WAF 网站访问控制列表（web ACL），以拒绝特定 国家的访问请求，并将该 web ACL 与 CloudFront 分发配置关联。","C":"使用 CloudFront 的地理限制功能来拒绝特定国家的访问。","D":"使用 CloudFront 的地理位置标头来拒绝特定国家。"},"answer":["C"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Networking/DNS","Security/IAM","Cost Optimization"],"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選","research":{"verdict":["C"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"both","explanation_en":"Verified against AWS documentation. CloudFront's geographic restrictions (geo blocking) feature, documented at 'Restrict the geographic distribution of your content,' lets you configure an allowlist or denylist of countries directly on the distribution; when a request comes from a blocked country, the edge location itself returns HTTP 403 without forwarding the request further. This is a native distribution setting (found under the Geographic Restrictions section of a CloudFront distribution's configuration) and is billed as part of standard CloudFront usage -- there is no separate line item, subscription, or per-request charge for turning it on. I confirmed this by checking the CloudFront FAQ page: features that do carry additional charges (Lambda@Edge invocations, embedded POPs, HTTP/3 in some contexts, CloudFront Security Bundles, standard access log delivery in certain configurations) are each explicitly called out with a dedicated 'does this require extra charges' FAQ entry, while the geographic-restriction FAQ ('Can I choose to have content served only to, or withheld from, specific countries?') has no such caveat, meaning it's covered by ordinary data-transfer/request pricing. By contrast, both WAF-based options (A and B) require creating a web ACL and associating it with the CloudFront distribution, which AWS WAF's own pricing page confirms is billed per web ACL created (a flat monthly fee), per rule added to that web ACL (a flat monthly fee per rule), and per million web requests inspected -- these charges apply in addition to CloudFront's normal pricing regardless of whether the WAF rule uses a geo-match statement (B) or an IP-set/IP-match statement listing each country's CIDR ranges (A). So while A and B can both technically achieve the blocking, they are strictly more expensive than the built-in CloudFront feature for the same outcome. Option D is not a valid blocking mechanism at all: CloudFront can add a viewer-country header (CloudFront-Viewer-Country) to requests forwarded to the origin, but this only informs the origin application of the viewer's country -- CloudFront itself does not deny or block the request based on that header, so the origin would have to implement its own logic, which doesn't satisfy 'block inbound traffic' at the edge and is not what the option even describes as a real feature. There is exactly one correct answer: C.","explanation_zh":"已對照 AWS 官方文件驗證。CloudFront 的 geographic restrictions(地理限制,俗稱 geo blocking)功能記載於「Restrict the geographic distribution of your content」文件中,可直接在 distribution 上設定 allowlist 或 denylist 國家清單;當請求來自被封鎖的國家時,邊緣節點本身就會回傳 HTTP 403,不會再將請求轉發下去。這是 CloudFront distribution 設定中原生內建的選項(位於 distribution 設定的 Geographic Restrictions 區塊),且屬於標準 CloudFront 用量計費的一部分——啟用它不會產生額外的項目、訂閱費或每請求收費。我透過查閱 CloudFront FAQ 頁面確認這一點:真正會產生額外費用的功能(如 Lambda@Edge 呼叫次數、embedded POP、某些情境下的 HTTP/3、CloudFront Security Bundles、特定設定下的標準存取日誌交付)都各自有專屬的「是否需要額外收費」FAQ 條目說明,而地理限制的 FAQ(「我可以選擇只在指定國家/地區中提供或不提供內容嗎?」)並沒有這類額外收費的說明,代表它已包含在一般的資料傳輸/請求計費中。相對地,兩個基於 WAF 的選項(A 與 B)都需要建立一個 web ACL 並將其關聯至 CloudFront distribution,而 AWS WAF 官方定價頁面明確指出計費是依「每個建立的 web ACL」(固定月費)、「該 web ACL 中新增的每個規則」(每規則固定月費)以及「檢查的每百萬個 Web 請求數」來收費——無論該 WAF 規則使用的是 geo match 陳述式(選項 B)還是列出各國 CIDR 範圍的 IP set/IP match 陳述式(選項 A),這些費用都是在 CloudFront 原本的計費之外額外產生的。因此,雖然 A 與 B 在技術上都能達成封鎖效果,但相較於 CloudFront 內建功能,兩者在達成相同結果時的成本都更高。選項 D 則根本不是有效的封鎖機制:CloudFront 可以在轉發給來源伺服器的請求中加入 viewer-country 標頭(CloudFront-Viewer-Country),但這只是讓來源應用程式得知使用者所在國家——CloudFront 本身並不會依據這個標頭拒絕或封鎖請求,來源伺服器必須自行實作邏輯才能達到封鎖效果,這無法滿足在邊緣「封鎖傳入流量」的要求,而且該選項描述的也並非 CloudFront 真實存在的封鎖功能。本題僅有一個正確答案:C。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"Technically achieves the blocking goal via an IP-match statement listing each target country's CIDR ranges, but requires creating and associating a web ACL with CloudFront. AWS WAF's pricing page confirms this incurs a flat monthly charge per web ACL, a flat monthly charge per rule, and a per-million-request inspection fee -- all on top of normal CloudFront charges, making it more expensive than CloudFront's native geo restriction for the same outcome. It's also more brittle to maintain since IP ranges per country change over time, unlike WAF's built-in geo match database.","why_zh":"雖然透過列出各目標國家 CIDR 範圍的 IP match 陳述式在技術上可以達成封鎖目的,但需要建立 web ACL 並將其關聯至 CloudFront。AWS WAF 定價頁面證實這會產生每個 web ACL 的固定月費、每個規則的固定月費,以及依檢查請求數計費的費用——這些都是在一般 CloudFront 費用之外額外產生的,使其比 CloudFront 內建的地理限制功能更昂貴。此外,各國 IP 範圍會隨時間變動,維護成本也高於 WAF 內建的 geo match 資料庫。"},{"letter":"B","why_en":"Also technically achieves the blocking goal using AWS WAF's geo match rule statement (which matches country of origin directly, without needing to maintain IP ranges), and is a cleaner WAF-based approach than option A. However it still requires creating a web ACL and associating it with CloudFront, which per AWS WAF's pricing page incurs a per-web-ACL monthly charge, a per-rule monthly charge, and per-million-request charges on top of standard CloudFront pricing -- making it more expensive than the free, built-in CloudFront geo restriction feature for this same use case.","why_zh":"使用 AWS WAF 的 geo match 規則陳述式(直接比對請求的來源國家,不需維護 IP 範圍)在技術上同樣能達成封鎖目的,且比選項 A 更為簡潔的 WAF 作法。但仍需要建立 web ACL 並將其關聯至 CloudFront,依 AWS WAF 定價頁面所述,這會產生每個 web ACL 的月費、每個規則的月費,以及依請求數計費的費用,皆為標準 CloudFront 費用之外的額外支出——相較於免費且內建的 CloudFront 地理限制功能,在此情境下成本較高。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"Not a real blocking mechanism. CloudFront can add a CloudFront-Viewer-Country header to requests it forwards to the origin, but this only passes country information along for the origin to act on -- CloudFront itself does not deny or block the request at the edge based on this header. Implementing actual blocking would require custom origin-side logic, which fails to meet the requirement of blocking inbound traffic and is not what this option describes as an actual CloudFront feature.","why_zh":"這並非真實存在的封鎖機制。CloudFront 可以在轉發給來源伺服器的請求中加入 CloudFront-Viewer-Country 標頭,但這只是把國家資訊傳遞給來源伺服器處理——CloudFront 本身並不會依此標頭在邊緣端拒絕或封鎖請求。若要真正實現封鎖,還需要來源端自行實作邏輯,這無法滿足「封鎖傳入流量」的需求,且該選項所描述的也不是 CloudFront 實際具備的功能。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonCloudFront/latest/DeveloperGuide/georestrictions.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonCloudFront/latest/DeveloperGuide/DownloadDistValuesEnableGeoRestriction.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/waf/latest/developerguide/waf-rule-statement-type-geo-match.html","https://aws.amazon.com/waf/pricing/","https://aws.amazon.com/cloudfront/faqs/"]}},{"id":113,"question_en":"A security engineer wants to evaluate configuration changes to a specific AWS resource to ensure that the resource meets compliance standards. However, the security engineer is concerned about a situation in which several configuration changes are made to the resource in quick succession. The security engineer wants to record only the latest configuration of that resource to indicate the cumulative impact of the set of changes. Which solution will meet this requirement in the MOST operationally efficient way?","question_zh":"安全工程师希望评估对特定 AWS 资源的配置更改，以确保该资源符合合规标准。然而，该工程师担心在短时间内对该资源进 行多次连续配置更改的情况。因此，工程师希望仅记录该资源的最新配置，以反映一系列更改的累积影响。 哪种解决方案能以最高效的操作方式满足这一需求？","options_en":{"A":"Use AWS CloudTrail to detect the configuration changes by filtering API calls to monitor the changes. Use the most recent API call to indicate the cumulative impact of multiple calls.","B":"Use AWS Config to detect the configuration changes and to record the latest configuration in case of multiple configuration changes.","C":"Use Amazon CloudWatch to detect the configuration changes by filtering API calls to monitor the changes. Use the most recent API call to indicate the cumulative impact of multiple calls.","D":"Use AWS Cloud Map to detect the configuration changes. Generate a report of configuration changes from AWS Cloud Map to track the latest state by using a sliding time window."},"options_zh":{"A":"使用 AWS CloudTrail 通过筛选 API 调用来检测配置变更，以监控变化情况。使用最近一次的 API 调用表示多次调用的 累积影响。","B":"使用 AWS Config 检测配置变更，并在发生多次配置变更时记录最新的配置。","C":"使用 Amazon CloudWatch 通过筛选 API 调用来检测配置变更，以监控这些变化。使用最近一次的 API 调用来表示 多次调用的累积影响。","D":"使用 AWS Cloud Map 检测配置变更，并通过滑动时间窗口生成配置变更报告，以跟踪最新状态。"},"answer":["B"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Organizations/Governance","Monitoring/Ops"],"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選","research":{"verdict":["B"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"both","explanation_en":"Confirmed against the official AWS Config FAQ. The FAQ directly addresses this exact scenario under 'Does AWS Config record every state that a resource has been in?': 'AWS Config detects change to a resource's configuration and records the configuration state that resulted from that change. In cases where several configuration changes are made to a resource in quick succession, AWS Config will record only the latest configuration of that resource that represents the cumulative impact of the set of changes. In these situations, AWS Config will list only the latest change in the relatedEvents field of the Configuration Item.' This is a native behavior of AWS Config's configuration recorder and configuration item model, not something that needs to be engineered -- AWS Config discovers resources, generates a configuration item whenever a change is detected, and de-duplicates rapid-fire changes into a single consolidated configuration item automatically. That makes option B the most operationally efficient solution with no custom logic required. Option A (CloudTrail) only logs discrete API call events; there is no native concept of a consolidated 'latest cumulative' resource state, so identifying the right call would require custom filtering and correlation logic. Option C (CloudWatch) is built for metrics, logs, and alarms, not configuration state tracking, and suffers the same problem as CloudTrail if used to filter API calls. Option D (AWS Cloud Map) is a service discovery tool for registering and locating application resources by custom names; it has no capability to detect or record AWS resource configuration changes at all, making it irrelevant to this scenario. There is exactly one correct answer.","explanation_zh":"已對照 AWS Config 官方 FAQ 驗證。該 FAQ 針對這個確切情境直接說明:「Does AWS Config record every state that a resource has been in?」的回答是:「AWS Config 偵測資源組態的變更,並記錄該次變更所產生的組態狀態。若短時間內對某資源進行了多次連續的組態變更,AWS Config 只會記錄該資源反映這整組變更累積影響的最新組態。在這種情況下,AWS Config 只會在 Configuration Item 的 relatedEvents 欄位中列出最新的那次變更。」這是 AWS Config 的 configuration recorder 與 configuration item 模型的原生行為,不需要額外開發:AWS Config 會探索資源,每當偵測到變更就產生一個 configuration item,並自動將短時間內快速發生的多次變更去重、整合成單一組態項目。因此選項 B 是不需要任何自訂邏輯即可達成需求、維運效率最高的解法。選項 A 的 CloudTrail 只會記錄離散的 API 呼叫事件,並沒有內建「整合後最新累積狀態」的概念,要判斷正確的那次呼叫需要自行建立過濾與關聯邏輯。選項 C 的 CloudWatch 是為指標、日誌與警示設計的,並非用於追蹤組態狀態,若用來過濾 API 呼叫也會遇到與 CloudTrail 相同的問題。選項 D 的 AWS Cloud Map 是用於以自訂名稱註冊與尋找應用程式資源的服務探索工具,完全沒有偵測或記錄 AWS 資源組態變更的能力,與此情境完全無關。本題僅有一個正確答案。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"CloudTrail logs API calls as discrete events with no native concept of a resource's consolidated configuration state. Determining 'the most recent call reflecting cumulative impact' would require custom event filtering and correlation logic, which AWS Config provides natively and CloudTrail does not.","why_zh":"CloudTrail 只會將 API 呼叫記錄為個別離散事件,並沒有內建「資源整合組態狀態」的概念。要判斷「反映累積影響的最新呼叫」需要自行建立事件過濾與關聯邏輯,而這正是 AWS Config 原生就能提供、CloudTrail 卻沒有的能力。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"Amazon CloudWatch is designed for metrics, logs, and alarms, not for tracking AWS resource configuration state. Like CloudTrail, filtering API calls in CloudWatch to infer the latest cumulative configuration requires custom logic, making it an inefficient, non-purpose-built solution.","why_zh":"Amazon CloudWatch 主要用於指標、日誌與警示,並非用來追蹤 AWS 資源的組態狀態。與 CloudTrail 相同,在 CloudWatch 中過濾 API 呼叫以推斷最新的累積組態需要自訂邏輯,並非針對此需求設計的高效解法。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"AWS Cloud Map is a service discovery service used to register and locate application components (such as microservices) by custom names; it has no feature for detecting or reporting AWS resource configuration changes, making it entirely inapplicable to this scenario.","why_zh":"AWS Cloud Map 是一項服務探索服務,用於以自訂名稱註冊與尋找應用程式元件(例如微服務),完全沒有偵測或回報 AWS 資源組態變更的功能,因此完全不適用於此情境。"}],"sources":["https://aws.amazon.com/config/faqs/","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/config/latest/developerguide/config-concepts.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/config/latest/developerguide/how-does-config-work.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/config/latest/developerguide/faq.html"]}},{"id":114,"question_en":"A security engineer has designed a VPC to segment private traffic from public traffic. The VPC includes two Availability Zones. The security engineer has provisioned each Availability Zone with one private subnet and one public subnet. The security engineer has created three route tables for use with the environment. One route table is for the public subnets, and two route tables are for the private subnets (one route table for the private subnet in each Availability Zone). The security engineer discovers that all four subnets are attempting to route traffic out through the internet gateway that is attached to the VPC. Which combination of steps should the security engineer take to remediate this scenario? (Select TWO.)","question_zh":"安全工程师设计了一个VPC，用于将私有流量与公共流量进行隔离。该VPC包含两个可用区，每个 可用区均配置了一个私有子网和一个公共子网。安全工程师为该环境创建了三个路由表：一个用于 公共子网，另外两个分别用于私有子网（每个可用区的私有子网对应一个路由表）。 安全工程师发现，所有四个子网都在尝试通过连接到VPC的互联网网关路由流量。 安全工程师应采取哪些步骤组合来解决此情况？（选择两项。）","options_en":{"A":"Verify that a NAT gateway has been provisioned in the public subnet in each Availability Zone.","B":"Verify that a NAT gateway has been provisioned in the private subnet in each Availability Zone.","C":"Modify the route tables that are associated with each of the public subnets. Create a new route for local destinations to the VPC CIDR range.","D":"Modify the route tables that are associated with each of the private subnets. Create a new route for the destination 0.0.0.0/0. Specify the NAT gateway in the public subnet of the same Availability Zone as the target of the route.","E":"Modify the route tables that are associated with each of the private subnets. Create a new route for the destination 0.0.0.0/0. Specify the internet gateway as the target of the route."},"options_zh":{"A":"验证每个可用区的公共子网中是否已配置了NAT网关。","B":"验证每个可用区的私有子网中是否已配置了NAT网关。","C":"修改与每个公共子网关联的路由表，为VPC CIDR范围内的本地目标创建新的路由。","D":"修改与每个私有子网关联的路由表。为目的地 0.0.0.0/0 创建一条新路由，并将同一可用区中公 共子网的 NAT 网关指定为该路由的目标。","E":"修改与每个私有子网关联的路由表。为目的地 0.0.0.0/0 创建一条新路由，并将互联网网关指定 为该路由的目标。"},"answer":["A","D"],"multi":true,"vote":{},"tags":["Networking/DNS"],"difficulty":2,"diff_why":"複選","research":{"verdict":["A","D"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"both","explanation_en":"Verified against AWS documentation. This scenario matches AWS's own reference architecture 'Example: VPC with servers in private subnets and NAT': the public subnet route table has local routes plus a 0.0.0.0/0 route to the internet gateway, while each private subnet's route table has local routes plus a 0.0.0.0/0 route to the NAT gateway (not the IGW). AWS's NAT gateway documentation and CLI walkthrough both state the NAT gateway is created in a public subnet, using an Elastic IP, and traffic from the private subnet is then routed to it -- 'Allocate an Elastic IP, create a NAT Gateway in a public subnet, and add a route to allow private subnet instances to access the internet.' Since all four subnets here are routing straight to the IGW, the private subnets are clearly missing (or never had) the NAT-gateway route, and it must be confirmed a NAT gateway actually exists in the public subnet of each AZ before that route can be added -- one NAT gateway per AZ preserves the two-AZ resiliency design. That is exactly A (verify NAT gateway is provisioned in the public subnet per AZ) plus D (add 0.0.0.0/0 in each private route table targeting the same-AZ NAT gateway). B inverts the required placement: a NAT gateway is never placed inside a private subnet, since it needs its own route to the IGW and a public IP to perform translation -- a NAT gateway in a private subnet couldn't reach the internet itself. C is a no-op: local routes for the VPC CIDR are automatically created and cannot be removed or need re-adding, so this does not address the described problem and doesn't touch the private subnets' internet routing at all. E preserves exactly the broken behavior described in the question (private subnets routing directly to the IGW) rather than fixing it -- sending private instances straight to the IGW would require them to have public IPs and defeats the purpose of a private subnet. There are exactly two correct letters.","explanation_zh":"已對照 AWS 官方文件驗證。此情境完全對應 AWS 官方參考架構「Example: VPC with servers in private subnets and NAT」:公共子網的路由表包含 local 路由,再加上一條指向 internet gateway 的 0.0.0.0/0 路由;而每個私有子網的路由表則包含 local 路由,再加上一條指向 NAT gateway(而非 IGW)的 0.0.0.0/0 路由。AWS 的 NAT gateway 文件與 CLI 教學都明確指出,NAT gateway 是建立在公共子網中,並使用 Elastic IP,私有子網的流量再路由到該 NAT gateway——「配置 Elastic IP、在公共子網中建立 NAT Gateway,然後新增路由讓私有子網的執行個體能存取網際網路」。由於題目中所有四個子網目前都直接路由到 IGW,顯然私有子網缺少(或從未配置)指向 NAT gateway 的路由,而在新增該路由之前,必須先確認每個可用區的公共子網中確實已配置 NAT gateway——每個可用區各一個 NAT gateway,才能維持雙可用區的高可用性設計。這正是選項 A(確認每個可用區的公共子網中已配置 NAT gateway)加上選項 D(在每個私有子網路由表中新增 0.0.0.0/0 路由,目標指向同一可用區公共子網中的 NAT gateway)。選項 B 把配置位置弄反了:NAT gateway 絕不會放在私有子網中,因為它自身需要一條指向 IGW 的路由以及公有 IP 才能執行位址轉換——若 NAT gateway 放在私有子網,它自己就無法連上網際網路。選項 C 是無效操作:VPC CIDR 的 local 路由是自動建立的,不會被移除也不需要重新新增,因此完全無法解決題目描述的問題,也完全沒有處理私有子網的網際網路路由。選項 E 恰好維持題目中描述的錯誤行為(私有子網直接路由到 IGW),而非修正它——讓私有子網的執行個體直接透過 IGW 對外,需要它們具備公有 IP,這違背了私有子網的設計目的。本題恰好有兩個正確選項。","distractors":[{"letter":"B","why_en":"Inverts the required placement. A NAT gateway must sit in a public subnet (with its own route to the internet gateway and an Elastic IP) so it can reach the internet on behalf of private-subnet resources. A NAT gateway placed in a private subnet would have no path to the internet itself and could not perform address translation for anything.","why_zh":"把配置位置弄反了。NAT gateway 必須位於公共子網中(擁有自己指向 internet gateway 的路由以及 Elastic IP),才能代表私有子網的資源對外連線。若將 NAT gateway 放在私有子網,它自身就沒有通往網際網路的路徑,也就無法為任何資源執行位址轉換。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"The local route for the VPC CIDR range is created automatically for every route table and cannot be deleted; it is not the cause of traffic incorrectly routing to the internet gateway, and re-adding it does nothing to fix the private subnets' internet-bound routing.","why_zh":"VPC CIDR 範圍的 local 路由對每個路由表都是自動建立的,無法被刪除;它並非流量錯誤路由到 internet gateway 的原因,重新新增這條路由也無法修正私有子網對外流量的路由問題。"},{"letter":"E","why_en":"This reproduces the exact broken behavior described in the question (private subnets sending traffic straight to the internet gateway) instead of fixing it. Routing private subnet traffic to the IGW would also require the private instances to have public IPs, undermining the entire purpose of separating private from public subnets.","why_zh":"此選項會重現題目所描述的錯誤行為(私有子網把流量直接送往 internet gateway),而非修正它。若將私有子網流量路由到 IGW,還需要這些私有執行個體具備公有 IP,這將完全違背區隔私有子網與公共子網的初始設計目的。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/vpc/latest/userguide/vpc-example-private-subnets-nat.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/vpc/latest/userguide/route-table-options.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/vpc/latest/userguide/nat-gateway-working-with.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/vpc/latest/userguide/getting-started-with-amazon-vpc-using-the-aws-cli.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/vpc/latest/userguide/vpc-nat.html"]}},{"id":115,"question_en":"A company uses AWS Organizations to manage its AWS accounts in a single organization. The company applies the FullAWSAccess SCP to every OU. However, now the company must explicitly deny specific services. The company needs a solution that restricts any users in the organization from using the explicitly denied services. Additionally, the solution must enforce all Amazon S3 buckets across the organization to have a minimum TLS version of 1.2. The company requires a central solution that applies to all existing accounts and any new accounts that the company creates in the future. Which solution will meet these requirements?","question_zh":"一家公司使用 AWS Organizations 在一个组织中管理其 AWS 账户。该公司将 FullAWSAccess SCP 应用于每个 OU。但现在，公司必须明确拒绝某些特定服务。公司需要一种解决方案，以限制组织 内任何用户使用被明确拒绝的服务。 此外，该解决方案必须强制要求组织内所有 Amazon S3 存储桶使用至少 TLS 1.2 版本。公司需要一 个集中式解决方案，适用于当前所有现有账户以及未来创建的任何新账户。 哪种解决方案能满足这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Create an SCP that denies a list of services that are restricted in the organization. Create an RCP to deny s3:* where the TLS version is less than 1.2. Attach both policies to the root of the organization.","B":"Create an SCP that denies a list of services that are restricted in the organization. Create an RCP to deny s3:* where the TLS version is less than 1.2. Attach the SCP to the root OU. Attach the RCP to each account within the organization.","C":"Create an SCP deny statement to disallow s3:* where the TLS version is less than 1.2. Create an RCP that denies a list of services that are restricted in the organization. Attach both policies to the root OU.","D":"Create an SCP that denies a list of services that are restricted in the organization. Create a declarative policy to deny s3:* where the TLS version is less than 1.2. Attach both policies to the root of the organization."},"options_zh":{"A":"创建一个SCP，拒绝组织中受限的服务列表。创建一个RCP，拒绝TLS版本低于1.2的s3:*操作。 将这两项策略附加到组织的根目录。","B":"创建一个SCP，拒绝组织中受限的服务列表。创建一个RCP，拒绝TLS版本低于1.2的s3:*操作。 将SCP附加到根OU，将RCP附加到组织内的每个账户。","C":"创建一条 SCP 拒绝语句，禁止 TLS 版本低于 1.2 的 s3:* 操作。创建一条 RCP，拒绝组织中受 限的一系列服务。将这两项策略附加到根 OU 上。","D":"创建一个 SCP，拒绝组织中受限的服务列表。创建一项声明式策略，拒绝 TLS 版本低于 1. 2 的 s3:* 操作。将这两项策略附加到组织的根节点。"},"answer":["A"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Organizations/Governance","Storage"],"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選","research":{"verdict":["A"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"Confirmed against current AWS Organizations and Amazon S3 documentation. Two distinct problems require two distinct policy types. First, denying specific services for IAM principals across the org is exactly what service control policies (SCPs) do: an SCP is a JSON policy attached to the org root, an OU, or an account that sets the maximum permissions for IAM principals in member accounts, and it is evaluated alongside the existing FullAWSAccess SCP. Second, enforcing a minimum TLS version on S3 access org-wide is a resource-centric guardrail -- this is what resource control policies (RCPs) are for. AWS's own RCP documentation states RCPs 'offer central control over the maximum available permissions for resources in your organization,' Amazon S3 is on the documented list of services that support RCPs, and the S3 'Enforcing encryption in transit' documentation explicitly lists RCPs (alongside bucket policies, SCPs, and VPC endpoint policies) as a supported mechanism to require a specific TLS version. The exact condition key is s3:TlsVersion, used with a NumericLessThan condition (e.g. {\"NumericLessThan\": {\"s3:TlsVersion\": \"1.2\"}}) in a Deny statement -- this is the same condition key AWS uses in its bucket-policy TLS examples, and it is valid inside an RCP because RCP syntax mirrors resource-based policy syntax and supports the Condition element. Both SCPs and RCPs, when attached to the organization root, are inherited down through every OU and every account -- both existing and any created in the future -- which is exactly the 'central, all existing and future accounts' requirement in the question. That matches option A precisely: SCP denying the restricted services list + RCP denying s3:* when s3:TlsVersion < 1.2, both attached at the org root. There is exactly one correct answer.","explanation_zh":"已對照最新的 AWS Organizations 與 Amazon S3 官方文件驗證。題目其實包含兩個不同性質的需求,需要兩種不同的政策類型分別處理。第一,要在整個組織內對 IAM 主體明確拒絕存取特定服務,這正是 service control policy (SCP) 的用途:SCP 是附加於 org root、OU 或帳戶的 JSON 政策,用來設定成員帳戶內 IAM 主體的權限上限,並與既有的 FullAWSAccess SCP 一併評估。第二,要在組織層級對 S3 存取強制最低 TLS 版本,這屬於以「資源」為中心的防護機制——這正是 resource control policy (RCP) 的設計目的。AWS 官方 RCP 文件明確指出 RCP「可針對組織內資源的最大可用權限提供中央控管」,而 Amazon S3 正列在支援 RCP 的服務清單中;S3 的「Enforcing encryption in transit」文件也明確將 RCP(與 bucket policy、SCP、VPC endpoint policy 並列)列為可用來強制特定 TLS 版本的機制之一。確切的條件鍵是 s3:TlsVersion,搭配 NumericLessThan 條件使用(例如 {\"NumericLessThan\": {\"s3:TlsVersion\": \"1.2\"}})寫在 Deny 陳述句中——這與 AWS 在 bucket policy TLS 範例中使用的條件鍵完全相同,而且因為 RCP 語法沿用 resource-based policy 語法並支援 Condition 元素,所以同樣適用於 RCP。無論是 SCP 還是 RCP,只要附加在組織 root,就會自動繼承套用到底下所有 OU 與所有帳戶——包括現有與未來新建立的帳戶——這正好符合題目要求的「集中管理、涵蓋現有及未來所有帳戶」。這與選項 A 完全吻合:SCP 拒絕受限服務清單 + RCP 在 s3:TlsVersion < 1.2 時拒絕 s3:*,兩者皆附加於 org root。本題僅有一個正確答案。","distractors":[{"letter":"B","why_en":"The SCP and RCP content is correct, but attaching the RCP to each account individually breaks the 'central' and 'future accounts' requirements: any account created after the fact would not automatically have the RCP applied, requiring manual per-account maintenance. AWS documentation confirms RCPs (like SCPs) support attachment at root, OU, or account level specifically so that root-level attachment can achieve org-wide, self-propagating coverage -- which this option abandons for RCP.","why_zh":"SCP 與 RCP 的內容本身正確,但將 RCP 逐一附加到每個帳戶會破壞題目要求的「集中管理」與「涵蓋未來帳戶」條件:之後新建立的帳戶不會自動套用該 RCP,必須手動逐一維護。AWS 文件確認 RCP(如同 SCP)支援附加於 root、OU 或帳戶層級,目的正是讓附加在 root 層級時能自動涵蓋整個組織且對新帳戶自動生效——此選項卻放棄了 RCP 的這項優勢。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"This swaps the two policy types to the wrong job. SCPs restrict actions available to IAM principals (identities) and are not the resource-centric guardrail mechanism documented for S3; RCPs are documented specifically as setting the maximum permissions available to resources (like S3 buckets) and appear in AWS's own S3 encryption-in-transit documentation as the org-wide mechanism for TLS enforcement, not as a general service-denial tool. Using an RCP to deny broad services and an SCP to enforce S3 TLS reverses their documented purposes.","why_zh":"此選項把兩種政策類型的職責對調錯了。SCP 是限制 IAM 主體(身分)可用的動作,並非 AWS 文件中針對 S3 所描述的「以資源為中心」防護機制;RCP 則明確被文件定義為設定資源(例如 S3 儲存桶)可用權限的上限,且在 AWS 官方 S3 傳輸加密文件中被列為組織層級強制 TLS 的機制,而非泛用的服務拒絡工具。用 RCP 去拒絕大範圍服務、用 SCP 去強制 S3 TLS,正好顛倒了兩者文件記載的用途。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"Declarative policies are a separate AWS Organizations policy type designed to centrally set and enforce baseline configuration defaults for specific integrated services (for example EC2 instance metadata defaults, VPC Block Public Access, or S3 account-level public access block settings) at the service control-plane level. They are not an IAM-style Deny/Allow access-control mechanism with Condition-based evaluation against request context like s3:TlsVersion, and they are not documented as a way to deny access to arbitrary AWS services or to enforce a minimum TLS version condition on S3 API calls. That makes D unable to satisfy either requirement in the question.","why_zh":"Declarative policy 是另一種獨立的 AWS Organizations 政策類型,設計目的是在服務控制層級,集中設定並強制套用特定已整合服務的基準組態預設值(例如 EC2 instance metadata 預設值、VPC Block Public Access,或 S3 帳戶層級的公開存取封鎖設定)。它並不是像 IAM 那樣具備 Deny/Allow 與 Condition 判斷(例如根據 s3:TlsVersion 這類請求內容評估)的存取控制機制,文件中也沒有記載可用它來拒絕任意 AWS 服務或對 S3 API 呼叫強制最低 TLS 版本。因此選項 D 無法滿足題目中任一項需求。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/organizations/latest/userguide/orgs_manage_policies_rcps.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/organizations/latest/userguide/orgs_manage_policies_rcps_syntax.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/organizations/latest/userguide/orgs_manage_policies_rcps_examples.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonS3/latest/userguide/UsingEncryptionInTransit.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonS3/latest/userguide/amazon-s3-policy-keys.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/organizations/latest/userguide/orgs_manage_policies_declarative_policies.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/organizations/latest/userguide/orgs_manage_policies_scps.html"]}},{"id":116,"question_en":"A company must capture AWS CloudTrail data events and must retain the logs for 7 years. The logs must be immutable and must be available to be searched by complex queries. The company also needs to visualize the data from the logs. Which solution will meet these requirements MOST cost-effectively?","question_zh":"公司必须捕获 AWS CloudTrail 的数据事件，并保留日志 7 年。日志必须不可篡改，并支持通过复 杂查询进行搜索。此外，公司还需要对日志中的数据进行可视化展示。 哪种解决方案能以最具成本效益的方式满足这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Create a CloudTrail Lake data store. Implement CloudTrail Lake dashboards to visualize and query the results.","B":"Use the CloudTrail Event History feature in the AWS Management Console. Visualize and query the results in the console.","C":"Send the CloudTrail logs to an Amazon S3 bucket. Provision a persistent Amazon EMR cluster that has access to the S3 bucket. Enable S3 Object Lock on the S3 bucket. Use Apache Spark to perform queries. Use Amazon QuickSight for visualizations.","D":"Send the CloudTrail logs to a log group in Amazon CloudWatch Logs. Set the CloudWatch Logs stream to send the data to an Amazon OpenSearch Service domain. Enable cold storage for the OpenSearch Service domain. Use OpenSearch Dashboards for visualizations and queries."},"options_zh":{"A":"创建 CloudTrail Lake 数据存储，并实现 CloudTrail Lake 仪表板以可视化和查询结果。","B":"使用 AWS 管理控制台中的 CloudTrail 事件历史功能，在控制台中查看和查询结果。","C":"将 CloudTrail 日志发送到 Amazon S3 存储桶。配置一个可持久运行且能访问该 S3 存储桶的 Amazon EMR 集群。在 S3 存储桶上启用 S3 对象锁定功能。使用 Apache Spark 执行查询， 并使用 Amazon QuickSight 进行可视化。","D":"将 CloudTrail 日志发送到 Amazon CloudWatch Logs 中的日志组。将 CloudWatch Logs 流配置为将数据发送至 Amazon OpenSearch Service 域。为 OpenSearch Service 域启用 冷存储。使用 OpenSearch Dashboards 进行可视化和查询。"},"answer":["A"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Storage","Cost Optimization","Monitoring/Ops","Analytics"],"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選","research":{"verdict":["A"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"CloudTrail Lake's 'Seven-year retention pricing' option (BillingMode=FIXED_RETENTION_PRICING) has a default retention period of 2,557 days AND a maximum retention period of 2,557 days -- both figures are identical and equal exactly 7 years, confirmed against current AWS documentation. This means the 7-year requirement sits exactly at the maximum supported by this pricing tier, not beyond it, and retention storage is included in ingestion pricing at no extra charge (no separate archival tier or lifecycle policy needed). AWS documentation explicitly defines an event data store as 'an immutable collection of events' -- this is the service's own terminology, not merely 'hard to delete,' satisfying the tamper-resistance requirement directly. CloudTrail Lake also supports data events (via advanced event selectors, alongside management and network activity events), a native SQL query engine for complex queries, and both managed and custom dashboards for visualization -- all within one integrated, serverless service requiring no infrastructure to provision or operate. This makes option A the most cost-effective choice. Option C requires a persistent (always-on) EMR cluster, which incurs continuous compute cost regardless of query frequency, plus manual engineering of S3 Object Lock for immutability and Spark job maintenance. Option D requires a continuously running OpenSearch Service domain (even with UltraWarm/cold storage tiers) plus CloudWatch Logs ingestion and indexing costs, which is also more expensive and operationally heavier than a fully managed CloudTrail Lake data store. Option B (CloudTrail Event History) is disqualified outright: it retains only 90 days of management events by default and provides no complex querying or dashboard capability. Exactly one option (A) satisfies all stated requirements at the lowest operational and cost overhead.","explanation_zh":"CloudTrail Lake 的「Seven-year retention pricing」選項(BillingMode=FIXED_RETENTION_PRICING)預設保留期限與最大保留期限皆為 2,557 天,兩者數值相同,且恰好等於 7 年,此數字已對照目前 AWS 官方文件核實。也就是說,7 年的需求正好落在此定價層級所支援的最大值上,而非超出上限,且保留費用已包含在資料擷取(ingestion)費用中,無需額外的歸檔層或生命週期政策。AWS 官方文件明確將 event data store 定義為「不可變(immutable)的事件集合」,這是服務本身使用的正式用語,而非僅止於「難以刪除」,直接滿足防竄改(tamper-resistant)的要求。CloudTrail Lake 也支援透過進階事件選取器(advanced event selectors)擷取 data events(以及 management 與 network activity events)、內建 SQL 查詢引擎可執行複雜查詢,並提供 managed 與 custom dashboards 進行視覺化——這些功能全部整合在同一個受管、無伺服器的服務中,不需要佈建或維運任何基礎設施。這使選項 A 成為成本最有效的方案。選項 C 需要一個持續運作(persistent)的 EMR 叢集,無論查詢頻率高低都會持續產生運算費用,還需手動設定 S3 Object Lock 以達成不可變性,並維護 Spark 作業。選項 D 需要持續運行的 OpenSearch Service 網域(即使使用 UltraWarm/cold storage 層級),再加上 CloudWatch Logs 的擷取與索引費用,同樣比完全受管的 CloudTrail Lake 更昂貴且維運負擔更重。選項 B(CloudTrail Event History)直接被排除:預設僅保留 90 天的管理事件,且不具備複雜查詢或儀表板能力。只有選項 A 能以最低的維運與成本負擔同時滿足題目所有需求。","distractors":[{"letter":"B","why_en":"CloudTrail Event History in the console only retains 90 days of management events by default and provides no long-term retention, no complex SQL querying, and no dashboard visualization capability, making it wholly unsuitable for a 7-year retention requirement.","why_zh":"主控台中的 CloudTrail Event History 預設僅保留 90 天的管理事件,不具備長期保留、複雜 SQL 查詢或儀表板視覺化功能,完全無法滿足 7 年保留需求。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"Sending logs to S3 with Object Lock does achieve immutability and long retention, but requiring a persistent (always-on) EMR cluster to run Spark queries incurs continuous compute charges regardless of query frequency, plus the operational overhead of managing the cluster and separately wiring up QuickSight, making it far less cost-effective than the fully managed CloudTrail Lake option.","why_zh":"將記錄傳送到具備 Object Lock 的 S3 確實能達成不可變性與長期保留,但需要維持一個持續運作(persistent)的 EMR 叢集來執行 Spark 查詢,無論查詢頻率高低都會持續產生運算費用,還要額外維運叢集並自行整合 QuickSight,遠比完全受管的 CloudTrail Lake 方案昂貴。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"Routing CloudTrail logs through CloudWatch Logs into an OpenSearch Service domain adds ingestion and indexing costs, and requires a continuously running OpenSearch domain (even with cold/UltraWarm storage) to be provisioned and maintained, which is more expensive and operationally complex than a native CloudTrail Lake data store.","why_zh":"將 CloudTrail 記錄透過 CloudWatch Logs 導入 OpenSearch Service 網域會增加擷取與索引成本,且即使啟用 cold/UltraWarm storage,仍需持續佈建與維護 OpenSearch 網域,這比原生的 CloudTrail Lake data store 更昂貴且維運更複雜。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/awscloudtrail/latest/userguide/cloudtrail-lake-manage-costs.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/awscloudtrail/latest/userguide/cloudtrail-lake-concepts.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/awscloudtrail/latest/userguide/lake-dashboard.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/awscloudtrail/latest/userguide/query-event-data-store-cloudtrail.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/awscloudtrail/latest/userguide/cloudtrail-lake-service-availability-change.html"]}},{"id":117,"question_en":"A company needs to scan all AWS Lambda functions for code vulnerabilities.","question_zh":"公司需要扫描所有 AWS Lambda 函数以查找代码漏洞。","options_en":{"A":"Use Amazon Macie.","B":"Enable Amazon Inspector Lambda scanning.","C":"Use GuardDuty and Security Hub.","D":"Use GuardDuty Lambda Protection."},"options_zh":{"A":"使用 Amazon Macie。","B":"启用 Amazon Inspector 的 Lambda 扫描功能。","C":"使用 GuardDuty 和 Security Hub。","D":"使用 GuardDuty Lambda 保护。"},"answer":["B"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Security/IAM","Compute"],"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選","research":{"verdict":["B"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"Verified against AWS documentation. Amazon Inspector offers two Lambda scan types: Lambda standard scanning (the default, which scans application dependencies for package vulnerabilities) and Lambda code scanning, which the docs describe explicitly as scanning 'custom application code in your Lambda functions and layers for code vulnerabilities' using automated reasoning and machine learning. That is a direct match for the requirement to scan Lambda function code for vulnerabilities - it inspects the actual function code the developer wrote, not just its third-party dependencies. Option A (Macie) is wrong: Macie discovers and classifies sensitive data (like PII) primarily in Amazon S3, and has no capability to scan Lambda code for vulnerabilities. Option C (GuardDuty and Security Hub) is wrong: GuardDuty is a threat-detection service that analyzes logs (CloudTrail, VPC Flow Logs, DNS logs) for malicious activity, and Security Hub aggregates and normalizes findings from services like GuardDuty and Inspector - neither one performs static code vulnerability scanning itself. Option D (GuardDuty Lambda Protection) is wrong: per the GuardDuty documentation, Lambda Protection 'monitors Lambda network activity logs to identify potential security threats when Lambda functions are invoked' - it is a runtime network-activity threat detector, not a code scanner, and it detects threats like a function communicating with a known-malicious IP, not vulnerable code patterns. There is exactly one correct answer, B.","explanation_zh":"已對照 AWS 官方文件驗證。Amazon Inspector 提供兩種 Lambda 掃描類型:Lambda standard scanning(預設類型,掃描應用程式相依套件以找出 package vulnerabilities)以及 Lambda code scanning,文件明確指出此類型會「掃描 Lambda 函式與 layer 中的自訂應用程式程式碼,找出 code vulnerabilities」,採用自動推理與機器學習技術。這正好對應題目「掃描 Lambda 函式程式碼中的漏洞」的需求 - 它檢查的是開發者實際撰寫的函式程式碼,而不只是第三方相依套件。選項 A(Macie)錯誤:Macie 主要用於在 Amazon S3 中探索與分類敏感資料(例如 PII),並不具備掃描 Lambda 程式碼漏洞的能力。選項 C(GuardDuty 和 Security Hub)錯誤:GuardDuty 是威脅偵測服務,分析 CloudTrail、VPC Flow Logs、DNS logs 等紀錄以偵測惡意活動;Security Hub 則是彙整與正規化來自 GuardDuty、Inspector 等服務的發現結果 - 兩者本身都不執行靜態程式碼漏洞掃描。選項 D(GuardDuty Lambda Protection)錯誤:依 GuardDuty 文件所述,Lambda Protection「監控 Lambda 網路活動紀錄,在 Lambda 函式被呼叫時識別潛在安全威脅」- 這是執行階段的網路活動威脅偵測功能,並非程式碼掃描工具,它偵測的是例如函式與已知惡意 IP 通訊等威脅,而非有漏洞的程式碼模式。本題僅有一個正確答案,即 B。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"Amazon Macie discovers and classifies sensitive data (such as PII) primarily stored in Amazon S3. It has no code analysis or vulnerability scanning capability and cannot inspect Lambda function code.","why_zh":"Amazon Macie 用於探索與分類主要儲存在 Amazon S3 中的敏感資料(例如 PII)。它沒有程式碼分析或漏洞掃描能力,無法檢查 Lambda 函式程式碼。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"GuardDuty analyzes logs (CloudTrail, VPC Flow Logs, DNS logs) to detect malicious activity, and Security Hub aggregates/normalizes findings from multiple security services. Neither performs static analysis of Lambda function source code.","why_zh":"GuardDuty 分析 CloudTrail、VPC Flow Logs、DNS logs 等紀錄以偵測惡意活動,Security Hub 則彙整並正規化多個安全服務的發現結果。兩者都不對 Lambda 函式原始程式碼進行靜態分析。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"Per AWS documentation, GuardDuty Lambda Protection monitors Lambda network activity logs to identify potential security threats when functions are invoked (runtime network threat detection) - it does not scan the function's code for vulnerabilities.","why_zh":"根據 AWS 文件,GuardDuty Lambda Protection 監控 Lambda 的網路活動紀錄,在函式被呼叫時識別潛在安全威脅(屬於執行階段的網路威脅偵測)- 它並不會掃描函式程式碼中的漏洞。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/inspector/latest/user/scanning-lambda.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/inspector/latest/user/scanning_resources_lambda_code.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/guardduty/latest/ug/lambda-protection.html"]}},{"id":118,"question_en":"A company has an encrypted Amazon Aurora DB cluster in the us-east-1 Region that uses an AWS KMS customer managed key. The company must copy a DB snapshot to the us-west-1 Region but cannot access the encryption key across Regions. What should the company do to properly encrypt the snapshot in us-west-1?","question_zh":"一家公司在 us-east-1 区域中有一个使用 AWS KMS 客户管理密钥加密的 Amazon Aurora 数据库集群。该公司需要将数据库 快照复制到 us-west-1 区域，但无法跨区域访问该加密密钥。 公司应采取什么措施才能正确加密位于 us-west-1 区域的快照？","options_en":{"A":"Store the customer managed key in AWS Secrets Manager in us-west-1.","B":"Create a new customer managed key in us-west-1 and use it to encrypt the snapshot.","C":"Create an IAM policy to allow access to the key in us-east-1 from us-west-1.","D":"Create an IAM policy that allows RDS in us-west-1 to access the key in us-east-1."},"options_zh":{"A":"将客户管理的密钥存储在 us-west-1 区域的 AWS Secrets Manager 中。","B":"在 us-west-1 区域创建一个新的客户管理密钥，并使用该密钥加密快照。","C":"创建一个 IAM 策略，允许从 us-west-1 访问位于 us-east-1 的密钥。","D":"创建一个 IAM 策略，允许位于 us-west-1 的 RDS 访问位于 us-east-1 的密钥。"},"answer":["B"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Security/IAM","Database"],"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選","research":{"verdict":["B"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"Verified against the Amazon Aurora User Guide's cross-region encrypted snapshot copy documentation. The docs are explicit: when using --kms-key-id (CLI) or KmsKeyId (API) to copy a DB cluster snapshot, 'You must use this option if the DB cluster snapshot is encrypted and you are copying the snapshot to another AWS Region. In that case, you must specify a KMS key for the destination AWS Region.' AWS KMS keys are strictly regional resources -- a KMS key created in us-east-1 physically does not exist in us-west-1 and cannot be referenced by any RDS/Aurora API call made against us-west-1. There is no IAM policy, resource policy, or grant that makes a KMS key in one Region directly usable to encrypt a resource in another Region (this is different from cross-account access, which IAM/key-policy grants can bridge). Therefore the only way to properly encrypt the snapshot copy in us-west-1 is to create a new customer managed key in us-west-1 (or use an existing one, or a multi-Region key configured for that Region) and pass its key ID as the destination-Region KMS key for the copy operation. That is exactly option B. There is exactly one correct answer.","explanation_zh":"已對照 Amazon Aurora 使用者指南中關於跨區域複製加密快照的文件進行驗證。文件明確指出:在使用 --kms-key-id(CLI)或 KmsKeyId(API)複製 DB 叢集快照時,「如果該 DB 叢集快照已加密,且您要將快照複製到另一個 AWS 區域,則必須使用此選項。在此情況下,您必須指定目的地 AWS 區域的 KMS 金鑰。」AWS KMS 金鑰是嚴格屬於區域性的資源——在 us-east-1 建立的 KMS 金鑰實際上並不存在於 us-west-1,任何對 us-west-1 發出的 RDS/Aurora API 呼叫都無法參照它。沒有任何 IAM 政策、資源政策或 grant 能讓某個區域的 KMS 金鑰直接被另一個區域用來加密資源(這與跨帳戶存取不同,跨帳戶情境下 IAM/金鑰政策確實可以搭橋)。因此,要在 us-west-1 正確加密該快照複本,唯一方法就是在 us-west-1 建立一個新的 customer managed key(或使用該區域既有的金鑰、或設定給該區域的 multi-Region key),並在複製作業中將其金鑰 ID 指定為目的地區域的 KMS 金鑰。這正是選項 B。本題僅有一個正確答案。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"AWS Secrets Manager stores secrets such as passwords and API keys; it is not a mechanism for making a KMS key usable across Regions, and RDS/Aurora snapshot copy operations do not read encryption keys from Secrets Manager. The regional isolation of the KMS key itself is unaffected by where you store a reference to it.","why_zh":"AWS Secrets Manager 用於儲存密碼、API 金鑰等機密資訊,並不是讓 KMS 金鑰能跨區域使用的機制,RDS/Aurora 快照複製作業也不會從 Secrets Manager 讀取加密金鑰。KMS 金鑰本身的區域隔離性不會因為你把它的參照存放在哪裡而改變。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"IAM policies can grant cross-account access to a KMS key (via the key policy plus IAM permissions), but they cannot make a Region-bound KMS key physically accessible from a different Region. The cross-region snapshot copy documentation requires specifying a destination-Region key, not an IAM policy granting cross-region access.","why_zh":"IAM 政策可以透過金鑰政策加上 IAM 權限授予跨帳戶的 KMS 金鑰存取權,但無法讓一個綁定於特定區域的 KMS 金鑰在物理上被另一個區域存取。跨區域快照複製文件要求的是指定目的地區域的金鑰,而不是建立允許跨區域存取的 IAM 政策。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"Similarly, granting RDS in us-west-1 IAM permission to call KMS actions does not overcome the fact that the target key physically resides only in us-east-1. RDS in the destination Region must be given a key ID that exists in that same Region; no IAM policy changes this requirement.","why_zh":"同樣地,授予位於 us-west-1 的 RDS 呼叫 KMS 動作的 IAM 權限,也無法克服目標金鑰實際上只存在於 us-east-1 這一事實。目的地區域的 RDS 必須被指定一個存在於同一區域的金鑰 ID,任何 IAM 政策都無法改變這項要求。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonRDS/latest/AuroraUserGuide/USER_CopyDBClusterSnapshot.Encrypted.CrossRegion.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonRDS/latest/UserGuide/USER_CopySnapshot.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonRDS/latest/AuroraUserGuide/aurora-copy-snapshot.html"]}},{"id":119,"question_en":"A company has multiple accounts in the AWS Cloud. Users in the developer account need to have access to specific resources in the production account. What is the MOST secure way to provide this access?","question_zh":"一家公司在 AWS 云中拥有多个账户。开发账户中的用户需要访问生产账户中的特定资源。 提供这种访问的最安全方式是什么？","options_en":{"A":"Create one IAM user in the production account. Grant the appropriate permissions to the resources that are needed. Share the password only with the users that need access.","B":"Create cross-account access with an IAM role in the developer account. Grant the appropriate permissions to this role. Allow users in the developer account to assume this role to access the production resources.","C":"Create cross-account access with an IAM user account in the production account. Grant the appropriate permissions to this user account. Allow users in the developer account to use this user account to access the production resources.","D":"Create cross-account access with an IAM role in the production account. Grant the appropriate permissions to this role. Allow users in the developer account to assume this role to access the production resources."},"options_zh":{"A":"在生产账户中创建一个 IAM 用户，为其授予所需资源的相应权限。仅与需要访问权限的用户共享密码。","B":"在开发账户中创建一个 IAM 角色以实现跨账户访问。为该角色授予适当的权限，并允 许开发账户中的用户担任此角色，从而访问生产环境资源。","C":"在生产账户中创建一个IAM用户账户，用于跨账户访问。为该用户账户授予适当的权限，并允 许开发账户中的用户通过此账户访问生产资源。","D":"在生产账户中创建一个 IAM 角色以实现跨账户访问。为该角色授予适当的权限，并允 许开发账户中的用户承担此角色，从而访问生产资源。"},"answer":["D"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Organizations/Governance","Security/IAM"],"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選","research":{"verdict":["D"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"The AWS IAM tutorial 'Delegate access across AWS accounts using IAM roles' describes exactly this pattern: the resource-owning account (here, production) is the 'Destination' account, and the account whose users need access (here, developer) is the 'Originating' account. Step 1 of the tutorial is explicitly titled 'Create a role in the Destination Account' — you create an IAM role in the account that owns the resources, define the Originating account as a trusted entity in the role's trust policy, and attach a permissions policy scoped to the specific resources. Developer-account users (or a role/group they belong to) are then granted sts:AssumeRole permission to switch into that role and obtain temporary credentials scoped to only what the role allows. This is most secure because: (1) permissions are defined once, at the resource, in the account that owns it, so there is a single source of truth; (2) access is via temporary STS credentials, not long-term shared secrets; (3) access can be scoped narrowly and revoked centrally by deleting/modifying the trust policy or role's permissions in production. Option B has it backwards — an IAM role's permissions policy grants access to resources within its own account. A role sitting in the developer account cannot itself grant access to S3 buckets or other resources that live in production; it would need to assume yet another role in production anyway, making it a redundant middle step, not a simplification.","explanation_zh":"AWS IAM 教學文件《Delegate access across AWS accounts using IAM roles》正是描述這個情境：擁有資源的帳戶(此處為 production)稱為 'Destination' 帳戶，需要存取權的使用者所在帳戶(此處為 developer)稱為 'Originating' 帳戶。教學的第一步標題就是「Create a role in the Destination Account」— 也就是在擁有資源的帳戶(production)中建立 IAM role，在該 role 的信任政策(trust policy)中將 Originating 帳戶(developer)設為受信任實體(trusted entity)，並附加一個僅限於特定資源的權限政策。接著授予 developer 帳戶中的使用者(或其所屬的 role/group) sts:AssumeRole 權限，讓他們可以切換到該 role 並取得僅限於該 role 授權範圍的暫時憑證。這是最安全的做法，因為：(1) 權限定義只存在一處，且是在擁有資源的帳戶中定義，形成單一事實來源；(2) 存取是透過 STS 暫時憑證，而非長期共用密鑰；(3) 可以在 production 端集中限縮存取範圍或撤銷(修改/刪除信任政策或權限)。選項 B 方向恰好相反 — IAM role 的權限政策只能授予其自身所在帳戶內的資源存取權。若 role 建立在 developer 帳戶，它本身無法授予對 production 資源(例如 S3 bucket)的存取權，還是得再去 assume production 帳戶中的另一個 role，等於多繞了一圈，並非簡化。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"A single shared IAM user with a shared password in the production account violates least-privilege and non-repudiation: multiple developers using one identity means no individual accountability, and a long-term shared password is a static credential that is hard to rotate and easy to leak.","why_zh":"在 production 帳戶中建立單一 IAM user 並共用密碼，違反最小權限與可歸責性原則：多名開發者共用同一個身分，無法做到個別問責，且長期共用密碼屬於靜態憑證，難以輪替、容易外洩。"},{"letter":"B","why_en":"Placing the cross-account role in the developer (originating) account is backwards. An IAM role's attached permissions policy only grants access to resources within its own account; a role in the developer account cannot directly authorize access to production resources, so this design does not achieve the goal as described.","why_zh":"將跨帳戶 role 建立在 developer(來源)帳戶方向錯誤。IAM role 所附加的權限政策只能授予其自身帳戶內資源的存取權；建立在 developer 帳戶的 role 無法直接授權存取 production 的資源，因此這個設計無法達成題目要求的目標。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"A shared 'cross-account IAM user' in production used by multiple developer-account users is essentially the same anti-pattern as A: a shared long-term credential with no individual identity, no temporary credentials, and no clean revocation path — the opposite of AWS security best practices.","why_zh":"在 production 建立一個由多名 developer 帳戶使用者共用的「跨帳戶 IAM user」，本質上與選項 A 相同的反模式：共用長期憑證、沒有個別身分、沒有暫時憑證，也無法乾淨地撤銷存取權，違反 AWS 安全最佳實務。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/IAM/latest/UserGuide/tutorial_cross-account-with-roles.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/IAM/latest/UserGuide/id_roles_common-scenarios_aws-accounts.html"]}},{"id":120,"question_en":"A company runs a web application on a fleet of Amazon EC2 instances that are in an Auto Scaling group. The EC2 instances are in the same VPC subnet as other workloads. A security engineer deploys Amazon GuardDuty and integrates it with AWS Security Hub. The security engineer needs to implement anautomated solutionto detect and respond to anomalous traffic patterns. The solution must follow AWS best practices forinitial incident responseand mustminimize disruptionto the web application. Which solution will meet these requirements?","question_zh":"一家公司在由自动扩展组管理的一组 Amazon EC2 实例上运行 Web 应用程序。这些 EC2 实例与其他 工作负载位于同一个 VPC 子网中。 安全工程师部署了Amazon GuardDuty，并将其与AWS Security Hub集成。该工程师需要实施一个自 动化解决方案，以检测和响应异常流量模式。该方案必须遵循AWS关于初始事件响应的最佳实践， 并尽量减少对Web应用程序的干扰。 哪种解决方案能满足这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Disable the instance profile access keys by using AWS Lambda.","B":"Remove the affected instance from the Auto Scaling group and isolate it with a restricted security group by using AWS Lambda.","C":"Update the network ACL to block the detected traffic source.","D":"Send GuardDuty findings to Amazon SNS for email notification."},"options_zh":{"A":"使用 AWS Lambda 禁用实例配置文件的访问密钥。","B":"使用 AWS Lambda 将受影响的实例从自动扩展组中移除，并通过受限的安全组将其隔离。","C":"更新网络ACL以阻止检测到的流量来源。","D":"将 GuardDuty 的发现结果发送到 Amazon SNS 以进行电子邮件通知。"},"answer":["B"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Security/IAM","Compute","Serverless/Integration"],"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選","research":{"verdict":["B"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"AWS's documented remediation pattern for a potentially compromised EC2 instance (GuardDuty User Guide, 'Remediating a potentially compromised Amazon EC2 instance') is a two-step response: first identify/investigate, then isolate the instance by creating a dedicated Isolation security group with no inbound or outbound rule allowing 0.0.0.0/0 traffic, and associating it with the instance in place of its other security groups. AWS explicitly favors isolation over immediate termination as the initial step so the instance and its evidence are preserved for investigation, rather than destroyed. Because this instance is a member of an Auto Scaling group, isolating it in place would leave a now-unhealthy/quarantined instance still counted toward the group's desired capacity (or continuing to serve traffic if health checks don't catch it), so best practice is to first remove/detach the instance from the ASG. This lets the ASG's health check mechanism immediately launch a replacement healthy instance, preserving the web application's capacity and availability, then apply the restricted security group to the removed instance for isolation and forensic investigation. Both actions (detach from ASG + apply isolation security group) can be fully automated by a Lambda function triggered from the GuardDuty finding (via Security Hub/EventBridge), satisfying the 'automated solution' requirement while following the documented incident-response pattern and minimizing disruption to the running application. Option A only revokes the instance's ability to call AWS APIs via its instance profile; it does nothing to block the anomalous network traffic itself, which is what GuardDuty flagged. Option C modifies a network ACL, which applies at the subnet level, collaterally affecting every other unrelated workload sharing that same VPC subnet -- the opposite of minimizing disruption. Option D only forwards findings to a human via email; it is a notification mechanism, not an automated detection-to-response action.","explanation_zh":"根據 AWS GuardDuty 使用者指南「Remediating a potentially compromised Amazon EC2 instance」所記載的補救模式，處理疑似受感染的 EC2 執行個體分為兩個步驟：先識別與調查，再進行隔離—建立一個專用的 Isolation security group（不允許任何 0.0.0.0/0 的進出流量），並將其取代該執行個體原有的所有 security group。AWS 明確建議將「隔離」而非直接「終止」作為初始應變步驟，以保留執行個體與其證據供後續調查，而非直接銷毀。由於該執行個體是 Auto Scaling group 的成員，若原地隔離，會使一個已被隔離、不健康的執行個體仍計入該群組的期望容量（或若健康檢查未及時偵測，可能仍持續服務流量），因此最佳實務是先將該執行個體從 ASG 中移除/detach。這樣可讓 ASG 的健康檢查機制立即啟動一個新的健康執行個體來取代，維持 web 應用程式的容量與可用性，然後再對已移出的執行個體套用隔離用的 security group 以進行隔離與取證調查。這兩個動作（從 ASG 移除 + 套用隔離用 security group）都可以透過由 GuardDuty 發現項目（經 Security Hub/EventBridge）觸發的 AWS Lambda 函式完全自動化，符合題目「automated solution」的要求，同時遵循文件記載的事件應變模式，並將對正在運行中應用程式的干擾降到最低。選項 A 只是撤銷該執行個體透過 instance profile 呼叫 AWS API 的能力，完全無法阻擋 GuardDuty 偵測到的異常網路流量本身。選項 C 修改的 network ACL 是套用在整個 subnet 層級，會連帶影響同一 VPC subnet 中所有其他不相關的工作負載，與「將干擾降到最低」的要求恰恰相反。選項 D 只是將發現項目透過電子郵件轉發給人員，屬於通知機制，並非自動化的偵測到應變動作。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"Disabling the instance profile's access keys only removes the instance's ability to call AWS APIs. It does nothing to stop or contain the anomalous network traffic (e.g., outbound C2 traffic, port scanning) at the network layer, which is the actual threat GuardDuty flagged and the thing the incident response needs to address.","why_zh":"停用 instance profile 的 access key 只會移除該執行個體呼叫 AWS API 的能力，對於在網路層面的異常流量（例如對外的 C2 連線、port scanning）完全沒有阻擋效果，而這才是 GuardDuty 偵測到的實際威脅，也是事件應變真正需要處理的問題。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"Network ACLs are stateless rules that apply at the entire subnet level, not to a single instance. Blocking a traffic source this way would affect every other workload sharing that same VPC subnet, directly violating the requirement to minimize disruption -- it disrupts unrelated workloads instead of just isolating the compromised one.","why_zh":"Network ACL 是無狀態規則，套用範圍是整個 subnet，而非單一執行個體。以此方式封鎖流量來源會影響同一個 VPC subnet 中所有其他的工作負載，直接違反「將干擾降到最低」的要求—反而干擾了不相關的工作負載，而不是只隔離受感染的那一台。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"Sending findings to SNS for email notification only alerts a human; it provides no automated detection-to-response action at all, failing the question's explicit 'automated solution' requirement and AWS's guidance to isolate the instance as an initial automated step.","why_zh":"將發現項目傳送到 SNS 進行電子郵件通知，只是通知人員，完全沒有任何自動化的偵測到應變動作，無法滿足題目明確要求的「automated solution」，也不符合 AWS 建議將隔離執行個體作為初始自動化步驟的指引。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/guardduty/latest/ug/compromised-ec2.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/systems-manager-automation-runbooks/latest/userguide/aws-quarantineec2instance.html"]}},{"id":121,"question_en":"A company is using AWS WAF to protect a customized public API service that is based on Amazon EC2 instances. The API uses an Application Load Balancer. The AWS WAF web ACL is configured with an AWS Managed Rules rule group. After a software upgrade to the API and the client application, some types of requests are no longer working and are causing application stability issues. A security engineer discovers that AWS WAF logging is not turned on for the web ACL. The security engineer needs to immediately return the application to service, resolve the issue, and ensure that logging is not turned off in the future. The security engineer turns on logging for the web ACL and specifies Amazon CloudWatch Logs as the destination. Which additional set of steps should the security engineer take to meet the requirements?","question_zh":"一家公司正在使用 AWS WAF 来保护基于 Amazon EC2 实例的自定义公共 API 服务，该 API 使用了 应用负载均衡器。AWS WAF 的网络 ACL 配置了 AWS 管理规则规则组。在对 API 和客户端应用程 序进行软件升级后，某些类型的请求无法正常工作，并导致了应用稳定性问题。安全工程师发现，该 网络 ACL 的 AWS WAF 日志记录功能未启用。 安全工程师需要立即恢复应用程序服务，解决该问题，并确保今后不再关闭日志记录功能。安全工程 师已为网络ACL开启日志记录，并将Amazon CloudWatch Logs指定为日志目标。 安全工程师还应采取哪些额外步骤来满足要求？","options_en":{"A":"Edit the rules in the web ACL to include rules with Count actions. Review the logs to determine which rule is blocking the request. Modify the IAM policy of all AWS WAF administrators so that they cannot remove the logging configuration for any AWS WAF web ACLs.","B":"Edit the rules in the web ACL to include rules with Count actions. Review the logs to determine which rule is blocking the request. Modify the AWS WAF resource policy so that AWS WAF administrators cannot remove the logging configuration for any AWS WAF web ACLs.","C":"Edit the rules in the web ACL to include rules with Count and Challenge actions. Review the logs to determine which rule is blocking the request. Modify the AWS WAF resource policy so that AWS WAF administrators cannot remove the logging configuration for any AWS WAF web ACLs.","D":"Edit the rules in the web ACL to include rules with Count and Challenge actions. Review the logs to determine which rule is blocking the request. Modify the IAM policy of all AWS WAF administrators so that they cannot remove the logging configuration for any AWS WAF web ACLs."},"options_zh":{"A":"编辑网络ACL中的规则，添加包含计数操作的规则。查看日志以确定是哪条规则阻止了请求。 修改所有AWS WAF管理员的IAM策略，使其无法删除任何AWS WAF网络ACL的日志配置。","B":"编辑网络ACL中的规则，添加包含计数操作的规则。查看日志以确定是哪条规则阻止了请求。 修改AWS WAF资源策略，使AWS WAF管理员无法删除任何AWS WAF网络ACL的日志配置。","C":"编辑网络ACL中的规则，添加包含计数和挑战操作的规则。查看日志以确定是哪条规则阻止了请求。修改AWS WAF资源策略，使AWS WAF管理员无法删除任何AWS WAF网络ACL的日志配置。","D":"编辑网络ACL中的规则，添加包含计数和挑战操作的规则。查看日志以确定是哪条规则阻止了请求。修改所有AWS WAF管理员的IAM策略，使其无法删除任何AWS WAF网络ACL的日志配置。"},"answer":["A"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Networking/DNS","Security/IAM","Compute","Monitoring/Ops"],"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選","research":{"verdict":["A"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"Restoring service immediately while diagnosing which rule is at fault is the documented AWS WAF troubleshooting pattern: switch the suspect rule(s) to Count action so AWS WAF stops blocking (service resumes) while still evaluating and logging matches, letting the engineer identify the offending rule from the CloudWatch Logs output. Challenge (and CAPTCHA) actions are a separate mechanism that issues a silent browser interstitial or puzzle to distinguish humans from bots, requiring client-side JavaScript/iOS/Android SDK integration or a GET text/html browser request; a programmatic API client generally cannot satisfy a Challenge, so adding Challenge actions would not restore service and is irrelevant to this troubleshooting goal, ruling out C and D. For preventing logging from being disabled going forward, AWS WAF's own IAM integration documentation states plainly: AWS WAF supports resource-based policies, and 'AWS WAF uses resource based policies to support the sharing of rule groups across accounts' via the PutPermissionPolicy API -- and explicitly adds 'This functionality isn't available through other means, such as the console or CloudFormation.' In other words, the one and only resource-based policy construct AWS WAF has is scoped to cross-account rule group sharing; it cannot be used to restrict who can call wafv2:PutLoggingConfiguration or wafv2:DeleteLoggingConfiguration. Restricting those actions must therefore be done through an IAM identity-based policy applied to the WAF administrators (e.g., a Deny on wafv2:DeleteLoggingConfiguration), which is exactly what option A describes. Options B and D invoke an 'AWS WAF resource policy' for this purpose that does not exist for logging configuration, so they are eliminated alongside C.","explanation_zh":"在診斷是哪個規則造成問題的同時立即恢復服務,這是 AWS WAF 官方記載的疑難排解模式:將可疑規則的動作改為 Count,讓 AWS WAF 停止封鎖(服務隨即恢復),但仍持續評估並記錄符合的請求,工程師便能從 CloudWatch Logs 的輸出中找出造成問題的規則。Challenge(以及 CAPTCHA)動作是另一套機制,用於發出無聲的瀏覽器插頁式驗證或拼圖,以區分真人與機器人,需要用戶端整合 JavaScript/iOS/Android SDK,或是透過 GET text/html 的瀏覽器請求;一般的程式化 API 用戶端通常無法完成 Challenge 驗證,因此加入 Challenge 動作無法恢復服務,也與此處的疑難排解目標無關,故排除 C 與 D。至於要防止日後再次關閉日誌記錄,AWS WAF 官方 IAM 整合文件明確指出:AWS WAF 支援資源型政策,而「AWS WAF 使用資源型政策來支援跨帳戶共用 rule group」,做法是透過 PutPermissionPolicy API;文件更明確補充「此功能無法透過其他方式使用,例如主控台或 CloudFormation」。換言之,AWS WAF 唯一擁有的資源型政策機制,其適用範圍僅限於跨帳戶 rule group 共用,無法用來限制誰可以呼叫 wafv2:PutLoggingConfiguration 或 wafv2:DeleteLoggingConfiguration。因此,若要限制這些操作,必須透過套用於 WAF 管理員的 IAM 身分型政策(例如對 wafv2:DeleteLoggingConfiguration 設定 Deny)來達成,這正是選項 A 所描述的做法。選項 B 與 D 所稱用於此目的的「AWS WAF resource policy」並不存在於日誌記錄設定的情境中,因此連同選項 C 一併排除。","distractors":[{"letter":"B","why_en":"AWS WAF's resource-based policy capability is limited to PutPermissionPolicy for cross-account rule group sharing; AWS documentation explicitly states 'this functionality isn't available through other means,' so there is no resource policy that can restrict logging configuration changes. This option references a non-existent use of that construct.","why_zh":"AWS WAF 的資源型政策能力僅限於透過 PutPermissionPolicy 進行跨帳戶 rule group 共用;AWS 文件明確指出「此功能無法透過其他方式使用」,因此並不存在可用來限制日誌記錄設定變更的資源型政策。此選項所指的用法並不存在。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"Challenge requires client-side support (JavaScript, iOS/Android SDK, or a browser GET request) to solve the silent challenge; a machine API client cannot complete it, so adding Challenge actions would further break the API rather than restore service, and it also relies on the same non-existent 'AWS WAF resource policy' for logging.","why_zh":"Challenge 動作需要用戶端支援(JavaScript、iOS/Android SDK,或瀏覽器的 GET 請求)才能完成無聲驗證;機器化的 API 用戶端無法完成此驗證,因此加入 Challenge 動作只會讓 API 進一步中斷,而非恢復服務,且此選項同樣仰賴並不存在的「AWS WAF resource policy」來限制日誌記錄。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"Combines the same flawed Challenge-action addition as option C with the correct IAM policy mechanism, but the Challenge portion makes it unsuitable for restoring a programmatic API's service, so it is still incorrect.","why_zh":"此選項結合了選項 C 中錯誤的 Challenge 動作添加,以及正確的 IAM 政策機制,但 Challenge 的部分使其不適合用於恢復程式化 API 的服務,因此整體仍不正確。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/waf/latest/developerguide/security_iam_service-with-iam.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/waf/latest/developerguide/waf-rule-action.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/waf/latest/developerguide/web-acl-rule-group-override-options.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/waf/latest/developerguide/waf-captcha-and-challenge.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/waf/latest/developerguide/waf-captcha-and-challenge-how-it-works.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/waf/latest/developerguide/logging-cw-logs.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/waf/latest/APIReference/API_PutPermissionPolicy.html"]}},{"id":122,"question_en":"A company wants to improve the remediation of specific security incidents. Currently, a security engineer performs network isolation manually if traffic from Amazon EC2 instances to known command and control servers is detected. The manual network isolation process is error prone. The security engineer must automate the process. The security engineer enables Amazon GuardDuty. The security engineer configures instances to be managed by AWS Systems Manager. The security engineer prepares a Systems Manager Automation document to change security groups on selected instances. Which solution will meet these requirements?","question_zh":"一家公司希望改进特定安全事件的响应处理。目前，当检测到Amazon EC2实例向已知的命令与控制服务器发送流量时，安 全工程师会手动执行网络隔离操作。这种手动隔离流程容易出错，因此安全工程师需要将该过程自动化。 安全工程师启用了 Amazon GuardDuty。安全工程师将实例配置为由 AWS Systems Manager 管理。安全工程师准备了一份 Systems Manager 自动化文档，用于更改选定实例的安全组。 哪种解决方案能满足这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Create a permanent Amazon Detective investigation. Select all resources to monitor. Configure Detective to invoke the Systems Manager document if known command and control traffic is detected.","B":"Set up AWS Config. Use the managed rule ec2-prefix-list-tagged to detect traffic to network prefixes tagged for command and control activity. Configure automatic remediation and select the Automation document.","C":"Enable Systems Manager OpsCenter. Create an Amazon EventBridge rule to transform GuardDuty alerts of command and control traffic for OpsCenter. Use the Automation document for remediation.","D":"Configure AWS Security Hub CSPM. Use NIST SP 800-53 scans to report compromised instances based on NIST alerts. Create an automation rule to invoke the Automation document."},"options_zh":{"A":"创建一个永久的 Amazon Detective 调查。选择所有要监控的资源。配置 Detective 在检测到已知的命令与控制流量时， 调用 Systems Manager 文档。","B":"配置 AWS Config。使用托管规则 ec2-prefix-list-tagged 来检测流向已标记为命令与控制活动的网络前缀的流量。配置 自动修复并选择自动化文档。","C":"启用 Systems Manager OpsCenter。创建一个 Amazon EventBridge 规则，将 GuardDuty 检测到的命令与控制流量告警 转换为 OpsCenter 可处理的格式，并使用自动化文档进行修复操作。","D":"配置 AWS Security Hub 的云安全态势管理（CSPM）。使用 NIST SP 800-53 扫描，根据 NIST 告警报告受感染的 实例。创建自动化规则以调用自动化文档。"},"answer":["C"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Organizations/Governance","Security/IAM","Compute","Serverless/Integration","Monitoring/Ops"],"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選","research":{"verdict":["C"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"GuardDuty raises Backdoor:EC2/C&CActivity findings when an EC2 instance communicates with a known command-and-control IP; GuardDuty findings are published as EventBridge events. AWS documentation for Systems Manager OpsCenter explicitly describes this exact chain: you configure an EventBridge rule (or use the pre-configured default rules from OpsCenter's Integrated Setup) to automatically create an OpsItem when a matching event (such as a GuardDuty finding) occurs. Each OpsItem then has a Runbooks section from which you can execute a Systems Manager Automation runbook to remediate the associated resource, and if EventBridge is the trigger that created the OpsItem, EventBridge also associates a runbook with that OpsItem so remediation can run automatically. This matches option C perfectly: GuardDuty detects C2 traffic -> EventBridge rule creates an OpsItem in OpsCenter -> the prepared Automation document runs to change the security group and isolate the instance. Option A fails because Amazon Detective is a post-incident investigation and visualization service with no documented capability to invoke an Automation document; it only helps analysts explore a finding's context after the fact. Option B fails because the AWS Config managed rule ec2-prefix-list-tagged only checks whether EC2 managed prefix lists carry required tags for governance purposes -- it has nothing to do with detecting live communication with C2 servers. Option D fails because Security Hub CSPM automation rules, per AWS documentation, only modify ASFF finding fields (severity, workflow status, notes) or feed ticketing integrations when criteria match; they do not invoke Systems Manager Automation runbooks directly. NIST SP 800-53 standard checks in Security Hub also evaluate configuration compliance, not live C2 network behavior, so D cannot serve as the detection-to-remediation mechanism this scenario requires.","explanation_zh":"GuardDuty 在偵測到 EC2 執行個體與已知 command-and-control IP 通訊時,會產生 Backdoor:EC2/C&CActivity 系列 finding,而 GuardDuty finding 會以 EventBridge 事件的形式發佈。Systems Manager OpsCenter 的官方文件明確描述了這條鏈路:你可以設定 EventBridge 規則(或使用 OpsCenter Integrated Setup 內建的預設規則),讓符合條件的事件(例如 GuardDuty finding)自動建立 OpsItem。每個 OpsItem 都有 Runbooks 區段,可以在其中執行 Systems Manager Automation runbook 來補救相關資源;而且若 OpsItem 是由 EventBridge 觸發建立的,EventBridge 還會將 runbook 與該 OpsItem 關聯,讓補救動作可以自動執行。這正好對應選項 C 的流程:GuardDuty 偵測到 C2 流量 -> EventBridge 規則在 OpsCenter 建立 OpsItem -> 已備妥的 Automation document 執行、變更安全群組以隔離該執行個體。選項 A 不成立,因為 Amazon Detective 是事後調查與視覺化服務,文件中並無說明它能觸發 Automation document,它只協助分析師在事後探索 finding 的上下文。選項 B 不成立,因為 AWS Config 受管規則 ec2-prefix-list-tagged 只檢查 EC2 managed prefix list 是否具備治理所需的標籤,與偵測即時 C2 通訊完全無關。選項 D 不成立,因為根據文件,Security Hub CSPM 的 automation rule 在條件符合時只會修改 ASFF finding 的欄位(如嚴重性、工作流程狀態、備註)或推送至票務整合系統,並不會直接呼叫 Systems Manager Automation runbook;而 Security Hub 中的 NIST SP 800-53 標準檢查同樣是評估組態合規性,而非即時 C2 網路行為,因此無法作為本情境所需的偵測到補救的機制。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"Amazon Detective is an investigative and visualization service used to analyze findings and their context after they occur; AWS documentation gives it no mechanism to automatically invoke a Systems Manager Automation document in response to a detection.","why_zh":"Amazon Detective 是事後用於分析 finding 與其相關上下文的調查與視覺化服務,文件中並未賦予它在偵測後自動呼叫 Systems Manager Automation document 的機制。"},{"letter":"B","why_en":"The AWS Config managed rule ec2-prefix-list-tagged only evaluates whether EC2 managed prefix lists carry required tags for governance/compliance purposes; it does not inspect live network traffic or detect communication with C2 servers, so it cannot serve as the detection trigger in this scenario.","why_zh":"AWS Config 受管規則 ec2-prefix-list-tagged 僅用於評估 EC2 managed prefix list 是否具備治理或合規所需的標籤,並不會檢視即時網路流量或偵測與 C2 伺服器的通訊,因此無法作為此情境的偵測觸發來源。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"Per AWS documentation, Security Hub CSPM automation rules only update ASFF finding fields (such as severity, workflow status, or notes) or route findings to ticketing integrations when criteria match -- they do not directly invoke Systems Manager Automation runbooks. NIST SP 800-53 standard scans in Security Hub also assess configuration compliance rather than live C2 network traffic, so this option cannot detect or remediate the described threat.","why_zh":"根據文件,Security Hub CSPM 的 automation rule 在條件符合時只會更新 ASFF finding 的欄位(如嚴重性、工作流程狀態或備註)或將 finding 推送至票務整合系統,並不會直接呼叫 Systems Manager Automation runbook。Security Hub 中的 NIST SP 800-53 標準掃描同樣是評估組態合規性,而非即時的 C2 網路流量,因此此選項無法偵測或補救題目所描述的威脅。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/guardduty/latest/ug/guardduty_finding-types-active.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/guardduty/latest/ug/guardduty_findings_eventbridge.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/systems-manager/latest/userguide/OpsCenter-create-OpsItems.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/systems-manager/latest/userguide/OpsCenter-remediating.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/config/latest/developerguide/ec2-prefix-list-tagged.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/securityhub/latest/userguide/automation-rules.html"]}},{"id":123,"question_en":"A company uses AWS Organizations to manage an organization that consists of three workload OUs:Production, Development, and Testing. The company uses AWS CloudFormation templates to define and deploy workload infrastructure in AWS accounts that are associated with the OUs. Different SCPs are attached to each workload OU. The company successfully deployed a CloudFormation stack update to workloads in the Development OU and the Testing OU. When the company uses the same CloudFormation template to deploy the stack update in an account in the Production OU, the update fails. The error message reports insufficient IAM permissions. What is the FIRST step that a security engineer should take to troubleshoot this issue?","question_zh":"一家公司使用 AWS Organizations 来管理一个包含三个工作负载组织单元（OU）的架构：生产、开发和测试。该公司使 用 AWS CloudFormation 模板在与这些 OU 关联的 AWS 账户中定义并部署工作负载基础设施。每个工作负载 OU 都附加 了不同的服务控制策略（SCP）。 该公司成功将 CloudFormation 堆栈更新部署到了开发 OU 和测试 OU 中的工作负载。但当公司使用相同的 CloudFormation 模 板在生产 OU 的某个账户中部署该堆栈更新时，更新失败，错误消息显示 IAM 权限不足。 安全工程师在排查此问题时，应采取的第一步是什么？","options_en":{"A":"Review the AWS CloudTrail logs in the account in the Production OU. Search for any failed API calls from CloudFormation during the deployment attempt.","B":"Remove all the SCPs that are attached to the Production OU. Rerun the CloudFormation stack update to determine if the SCPs were preventing the CloudFormation API calls.","C":"Confirm that the role used by CloudFormation has sufficient permissions to create, update, and delete the resources that are referenced in the CloudFormation template.","D":"Make all the SCPs that are attached to the Production OU the same as the SCPs that are attached to the Testing OU."},"options_zh":{"A":"检查生产OU中该账户的AWS CloudTrail日志，搜索部署尝试期间CloudFormation发出的任何失败API调用。","B":"移除所有附加到生产OU的SCP。重新运行CloudFormation堆栈更新，以确定这些SCP是否阻止了CloudFormation API调用。","C":"确认 CloudFormation 所使用的角色具有足够的权限，以创建、更新和删除 CloudFormation 模板中引用的资源。","D":"将所有附加到生产OU的SCP设置为与附加到测试OU的SCP相同。"},"answer":["A"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Organizations/Governance","Security/IAM","Monitoring/Ops"],"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選","research":{"verdict":["A"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"both","explanation_en":"The FIRST step in any access-denied troubleshooting workflow is to gather evidence before changing anything, and AWS CloudTrail is the authoritative source for that evidence. AWS's IAM troubleshooting documentation ('Troubleshoot access denied error messages') confirms that access-denied error messages recorded for a request follow a predictable format that identifies the policy type responsible for the denial: an explicit SCP deny appears as 'with an explicit deny in a service control policy' (optionally with the policy ARN), an implicit SCP denial appears as 'because no service control policy allows the action', and a plain identity-based policy denial is reported without any SCP-specific phrase. These error messages are exactly what gets captured in CloudTrail's event records for the failed API calls. Since the same CloudFormation template already succeeded in the Development and Testing OUs, and the only stated difference is the SCPs attached per OU, reviewing the CloudTrail records of the failed CloudFormation/underlying-service API calls in the Production account will reveal the exact action, the resource, and critically whether the deny originated from an SCP, a permissions boundary, or the execution role's own identity-based policy. This diagnostic step is safe, non-destructive, and directly informs whether the fix belongs in the IAM role (option C) or the SCP, without guessing. Option B (stripping all Production SCPs) is a destructive, high-risk action on a production environment and is a 'fix-by-trial' approach rather than diagnosis. Option D (copying Testing's SCPs onto Production) assumes SCPs are the cause before confirming it, and undermines the intentionally stricter guardrails on Production. Option C is a reasonable remediation candidate but presumes the cause is the execution role rather than the SCP layer, which the CloudTrail evidence should establish first. AWS's own CloudFormation troubleshooting guide ('Insufficient IAM permissions') simply says to review IAM policy/permissions generically, but it doesn't address the cross-OU SCP variable in this scenario -- CloudTrail is what actually distinguishes the layer at fault.","explanation_zh":"任何「拒絕存取」的故障排查,第一步都應該是先收集證據,而不是直接動手改動任何設定,AWS CloudTrail 正是取得這項證據的權威來源。AWS 官方 IAM 疑難排解文件(Troubleshoot access denied error messages)指出,存取被拒的錯誤訊息會依循固定格式,標明造成拒絕的 policy 類型:SCP 的明確拒絕會顯示「with an explicit deny in a service control policy」(有時附上 policy ARN);SCP 的隱含拒絕會顯示「because no service control policy allows the action」;而單純的 identity-based policy 拒絕則不會出現任何 SCP 專屬字樣。這些錯誤訊息正是 CloudTrail 針對失敗 API 呼叫所記錄的內容。由於同一份 CloudFormation 範本已經在 Development 和 Testing OU 成功部署過,唯一明確提到的差異就是各 OU 掛的 SCP 不同,因此檢視 Production 帳戶中失敗的 CloudFormation(及其呼叫的底層服務)API 呼叫的 CloudTrail 紀錄,可以得知確切的 action、resource,以及最關鍵的一點:這次拒絕究竟來自 SCP、permission boundary,還是執行角色本身的 identity-based policy。這個診斷步驟安全且不具破壞性,能直接指引後續應該修正 IAM role(選項 C)還是 SCP,而不必憑猜測行事。選項 B(移除 Production 所有 SCP)是對正式環境做出破壞性、高風險的動作,屬於「先改再看」而非診斷。選項 D(把 Testing 的 SCP 直接套用到 Production)在尚未確認 SCP 就是根因之前就先假定答案,而且會削弱 Production 原本刻意設置的更嚴格防護。選項 C 雖然是合理的補救候選方案,但它預設問題出在執行角色而非 SCP 層,應該先靠 CloudTrail 證據來確立這一點。AWS 官方的 CloudFormation 疑難排解文件(Insufficient IAM permissions)只是泛泛建議檢查 IAM policy/permissions,並未針對本情境中「各 OU 的 SCP 不同」這個關鍵變數提出對應做法——真正能區分問題出在哪一層的,是 CloudTrail。","distractors":[{"letter":"B","why_en":"Removing all SCPs from the Production OU as a diagnostic test is destructive: it strips away all organizational guardrails from a production environment purely to test a hypothesis, and is not a 'first step' -- evidence should be gathered before taking any remediation or disruptive action.","why_zh":"為了測試假設而移除 Production OU 的所有 SCP,等同於暫時拿掉正式環境的所有組織層防護,這是破壞性的動作,也不該是「第一步」——應該先收集證據,再決定是否需要進行任何補救或具破壞性的操作。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"Confirming the CloudFormation execution role's permissions is a reasonable subsequent step, but it presumes the root cause is the IAM role rather than the SCP layer. Given that SCPs are explicitly stated to differ per OU and Dev/Test already succeeded with the same template, checking CloudTrail first is the more appropriate diagnostic starting point to determine which layer (role vs. SCP) actually caused the denial.","why_zh":"確認 CloudFormation 執行角色的權限是合理的後續步驟,但這預設了根因出在 IAM role 而非 SCP 層。由於題目明確指出各 OU 的 SCP 不同,且 Dev/Test 用同一份範本已經成功,先查看 CloudTrail 才是更恰當的診斷起點,能確定究竟是角色權限還是 SCP 造成了這次拒絕。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"Making Production's SCPs identical to Testing's defeats the purpose of having stricter, environment-specific guardrails on Production, and is a remediation action taken without first confirming that SCPs are even the actual cause of the failure.","why_zh":"把 Production 的 SCP 改成跟 Testing 一樣,會破壞針對 Production 特別設置的更嚴格防護的初衷,而且這是在尚未確認 SCP 真的是造成失敗的原因之前,就先採取的補救行動。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/IAM/latest/UserGuide/troubleshoot_access-denied.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AWSCloudFormation/latest/UserGuide/troubleshooting.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/organizations/latest/userguide/orgs_manage_policies_scps.html"]}},{"id":124,"question_en":"A company ' s security team wants to receive near-real-time email notifications about AWS abuse reports related to DoS attacks. An Amazon SNS topic already exists and is subscribed to by the security team. What should the security engineer do next?","question_zh":"一家公司的安全团队希望接收与DoS攻击相关的AWS滥用报告的近实时电子邮件通知。目前已有Amazon SNS主题，并且安 全团队已订阅该主题。 安全工程师接下来应该做什么？","options_en":{"A":"Poll Trusted Advisor for abuse notifications by using a Lambda function.","B":"Create an Amazon EventBridge rule that matches AWS Health events for AWS_ABUSE_DOS_REPORT and publishes to SNS.","C":"Poll the AWS Support API for abuse cases by using a Lambda function.","D":"Detect abuse reports by using CloudTrail logs and CloudWatch alarms."},"options_zh":{"A":"使用 Lambda 函数向可信顾问轮询滥用通知。","B":"创建一个 Amazon EventBridge 规则，用于匹配 AWS Health 中的 AWS_ABUSE_DOS_ REPORT 事件，并将其发布到 SNS。","C":"使用 Lambda 函数轮询 AWS 支持 API 以检测滥用情况。","D":"使用 CloudTrail 日志和 CloudWatch 警报来检测滥用报告。"},"answer":["B"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Compute","Serverless/Integration","Monitoring/Ops"],"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選","research":{"verdict":["B"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"AWS delivers abuse notifications, including DoS-related abuse reports, as AWS Health events. AWS's own EventBridge documentation gives the exact condition-key example events:detail.eventTypeCode = \"AWS_ABUSE_DOS_REPORT\" together with events:detail.service = \"ABUSE\", confirming this is a real, documented AWS Health event type code (verified directly against the current EventBridge IAM condition-keys page). The AWS Health EventBridge integration guide also explicitly calls out \"AWS Health Abuse events\" as a security use case for EventBridge rules. AWS Health events (source aws.health) are natively integrated with Amazon EventBridge, so a rule can match on this eventTypeCode and route the event directly to an existing SNS topic, giving a push-based, near-real-time notification with no polling delay. Option A and C are wrong because polling Trusted Advisor or the AWS Support API via a scheduled Lambda function introduces latency and re-implements, with extra operational overhead, a push mechanism AWS Health plus EventBridge already provides natively -- it is not genuinely near-real-time and is not the AWS-recommended pattern. Option D is wrong because CloudTrail logs and CloudWatch alarms observe API activity and metrics generated within your own account; they cannot detect AWS's own determination, made by AWS's abuse team, that your account is a source of outbound DoS/abuse traffic -- that determination only reaches you as an AWS Health abuse event. Therefore creating an EventBridge rule matching the AWS Health abuse event and publishing to the existing SNS topic is the correct, minimal next step.","explanation_zh":"AWS 會將濫用通知(包含與 DoS 攻擊相關的濫用報告)以 AWS Health event 的形式傳遞。AWS 官方 EventBridge 文件中給出的條件鍵範例明確使用了 events:detail.eventTypeCode = \"AWS_ABUSE_DOS_REPORT\" 以及 events:detail.service = \"ABUSE\",經直接比對現行 EventBridge IAM 條件鍵文件頁面後,證實這是一個真實且有文件記載的 AWS Health event type code。AWS Health 的 EventBridge 整合文件中也明確將「AWS Health Abuse events」列為 EventBridge 規則的安全性使用案例之一。AWS Health events(來源為 aws.health)與 Amazon EventBridge 有原生整合,因此可以建立一條規則比對此 eventTypeCode,並直接將事件路由到既有的 SNS 主題,達成推送式、近乎即時的通知,不會有輪詢造成的延遲。選項 A 與 C 錯誤,因為透過排程的 Lambda function 輪詢 Trusted Advisor 或 AWS Support API 會引入延遲,且是在重新發明一套 AWS Health 加 EventBridge 已經原生提供的推送機制,額外增加維運負擔——這並非真正的近乎即時,也不是 AWS 建議的做法。選項 D 錯誤,因為 CloudTrail 日誌與 CloudWatch 警示只能觀察您自己帳戶內產生的 API 活動與指標,無法偵測到 AWS 濫用團隊自行判定「您的帳戶是對外 DoS/濫用流量來源」這件事——這項判定只會透過 AWS Health 的濫用事件通知您。因此,建立比對 AWS Health 濫用事件的 EventBridge 規則並發佈到既有 SNS 主題,才是正確且最精簡的下一步。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"Polling Trusted Advisor with a scheduled Lambda function introduces inherent delay based on the polling interval and duplicates a notification mechanism that AWS Health plus EventBridge already delivers natively and faster; Trusted Advisor is also not the documented source for AWS abuse team determinations.","why_zh":"使用排程的 Lambda function 輪詢 Trusted Advisor,會依輪詢間隔產生固有延遲,且重複建置了一套 AWS Health 加 EventBridge 早已原生提供、速度更快的通知機制;Trusted Advisor 也並非 AWS 濫用團隊判定結果的文件記載來源。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"Polling the AWS Support API for abuse cases via Lambda also suffers from polling latency and unnecessary complexity compared to the native, push-based AWS Health-to-EventBridge-to-SNS integration that AWS documents for this exact scenario.","why_zh":"透過 Lambda 輪詢 AWS Support API 取得濫用案例,同樣存在輪詢延遲與不必要的複雜度,相較於 AWS 文件針對此情境所描述的原生推送式 AWS Health 到 EventBridge 到 SNS 整合方案,效率較差。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"CloudTrail and CloudWatch reflect activity and metrics visible within your own account; they cannot surface AWS's external determination (made by AWS's own abuse-response team) that your account is a source of DoS/abuse traffic, since that finding is never recorded as an API call or metric in your account.","why_zh":"CloudTrail 與 CloudWatch 反映的是您帳戶內部可見的活動與指標;它們無法呈現 AWS 外部(由 AWS 自身濫用回應團隊)所做出的「您的帳戶是 DoS/濫用流量來源」判定,因為這項結論從未以 API 呼叫或指標的形式記錄在您的帳戶中。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/eventbridge/latest/userguide/eb-use-conditions.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/health/latest/ug/creating-event-bridge-events-rule-for-aws-health.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/health/latest/ug/aws-health-concepts-and-terms.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/health/latest/ug/about-public-events.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/health/latest/ug/aws-health-events-eventbridge-schema.html"]}},{"id":125,"question_en":"A company wants to implement a content delivery network (CDN) for an upcoming product launch. The origin for distribution is a web server outside the AWS Cloud. The origin requires an authorization header from each request. Which solution will meet these requirements?","question_zh":"一家公司希望为即将推出的产品发布实施内容分发网络（CDN）。分发的源服务器位于AWS云外部，该源服务器要求 每个请求都包含授权头信息。 哪种解决方案能满足这些要求？","options_en":{"B":"Create an Amazon CloudFront distribution. Configure CloudFront to use an origin access control (OAC). Specify the web server as the origin. Include the required authorization header in the OAC request. Configure the web server to respond to requests from authorized users by using a signed URL.","C":"Create an Amazon CloudFront distribution. Configure CloudFront to forward a custom header to the origin. Specify trusted key groups for the distribution. Configure the web server to respond to requests from authorized users by using a signed URL.","D":"Use AWS Global Accelerator to create an origin access control (OAC). Specify the web server as the origin. Include a custom header in the request. Configure the web server to respond to requests from authorized users by using a signed cookie in the response header.","A":"Use AWS Global Accelerator to create a custom routing accelerator. Configure the accelerator to use TCP. Specify the web server’s IP address. Include the required authorization header in the request. Configure the web server to respond to requests from authorized users by using a signed cookie in the response header."},"options_zh":{"A":"使用 AWS 全球加速器创建自定义路由加速器。将加速器配置为使用 TCP 协议，并指定 Web 服务器的 IP 地址。在 请求中包含所需的授权头信息。配置 Web 服务器通过响应头中的签名 Cookie 来响应授权用户发出的请求。","B":"创建一个 Amazon CloudFront 分发。配置 CloudFront 使用源访问控制（OAC），将 Web 服务器指定为源。在 OAC 请求中包含所需的授权头信息，并配置 Web 服务器通过使用签名 URL 来响应授权用户的请求。","C":"创建一个 Amazon CloudFront 分发。配置 CloudFront 将自定义标头转发至源站。为该分发指定受信任的密钥组。配 置 Web 服务器，使其通过使用签名 URL 来响应授权用户的请求。","D":"使用 AWS 全球加速器创建源访问控制（OAC），将 Web 服务器指定为源。在请求中包含自定义标头，并配置 Web 服务器通过响应头中的签名 Cookie 来响应授权用户发出的请求。"},"answer":["C"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Networking/DNS"],"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選","research":{"verdict":["C"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"The origin is an HTTP web server outside AWS (a custom origin), and it requires an authorization header on every request. CloudFront's documented mechanism for this exact scenario is to configure the distribution to add a custom header (e.g., a shared secret or an Authorization value) to every origin request, and configure the origin to reject requests that don't include it. This is described in the CloudFront Developer Guide under 'Restrict access to files on custom origins,' which explicitly states you can 'set up custom headers to restrict access' for a custom origin, alongside Viewer Protocol Policy and Origin Protocol Policy to keep the header encrypted in transit. Separately, to control which end users can retrieve content through CloudFront (viewer-facing authorization), you use signed URLs or signed cookies together with trusted key groups, which is exactly what option C describes: custom header forwarded to the origin (satisfies the origin's authorization requirement) plus trusted key groups and signed URLs (satisfies user-level access control). This combination is fully supported for any custom HTTP(S) origin, including one hosted outside AWS.\n\nOption B is incorrect because origin access control (OAC) is designed specifically for AWS-native origin types that support SigV4 request signing: Amazon S3 buckets, Lambda function URLs, AWS Elemental MediaStore, and AWS Elemental MediaPackage v2. AWS documentation ('Restrict access to files,' 'Restrict access to an Amazon S3 origin,' 'Restrict access to an AWS Lambda function URL origin') never lists a generic external HTTP server as a supported OAC origin type, and OAC has no concept of 'include an auth header in the OAC request' — that phrasing does not correspond to any real OAC configuration. A third-party web server cannot validate AWS SigV4 signatures, so OAC cannot be used to authenticate to it at all.\n\nOptions A and D are incorrect because AWS Global Accelerator is a network-layer (TCP/UDP) traffic manager, not a content delivery network with HTTP-layer features. It has no origin access control feature, no custom header injection capability, and no signed cookie/URL mechanism — none of these CloudFront-specific concepts exist in Global Accelerator at all, making both options fabricated.","explanation_zh":"此題的 origin 是 AWS 外部的一台 HTTP 網頁伺服器（即 custom origin），而且該伺服器要求每個請求都要帶有 authorization header。CloudFront 官方文件針對這種情境的作法,是設定 distribution 在轉發到 origin 的請求中加入自訂 header（例如共用密鑰或 Authorization 值），並讓 origin 端只接受帶有該 header 的請求。這正是 CloudFront Developer Guide 中「Restrict access to files on custom origins」章節所描述的方法,文件明確指出可以透過設定自訂 headers 來限制對 custom origin 的存取,並搭配 Viewer Protocol Policy 與 Origin Protocol Policy 確保 header 在傳輸過程中是加密的。另外,若要控制哪些終端使用者可以透過 CloudFront 取得內容(即 viewer 端授權),則使用 signed URL 或 signed cookie 搭配 trusted key groups。選項 C 正好結合了這兩者:轉發自訂 header 給 origin(滿足 origin 的授權要求)加上 trusted key groups 與 signed URL(滿足使用者層級的存取控制)。這個組合完全適用於任何 custom HTTP(S) origin,包括架設在 AWS 之外的伺服器。\n\n選項 B 錯誤,因為 origin access control(OAC)是專為支援 SigV4 請求簽章的 AWS 原生 origin 類型設計的,包括 Amazon S3 bucket、Lambda function URL、AWS Elemental MediaStore 以及 AWS Elemental MediaPackage v2。AWS 官方文件(如「Restrict access to files」、「Restrict access to an Amazon S3 origin」、「Restrict access to an AWS Lambda function URL origin」)從未將一般的外部 HTTP 伺服器列為 OAC 支援的 origin 類型,而且 OAC 也沒有「在 OAC request 中加入 auth header」這種設定,這種說法並不對應任何實際存在的 OAC 功能。第三方網頁伺服器根本無法驗證 AWS SigV4 簽章,所以 OAC 完全無法用來對其進行身份驗證。\n\n選項 A 與 D 錯誤,因為 AWS Global Accelerator 是網路層(TCP/UDP)的流量管理服務,並非具備 HTTP 層功能的內容傳遞網路(CDN)。它沒有 origin access control 功能,沒有自訂 header 注入能力,也沒有 signed cookie 或 signed URL 機制——這些 CloudFront 專屬的概念在 Global Accelerator 中根本不存在,因此這兩個選項都是憑空捏造的。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"Global Accelerator custom routing accelerators operate at the TCP/UDP layer and have no concept of HTTP headers, signed cookies, or authorization headers. This option fabricates CloudFront-style features onto a service that doesn't support them.","why_zh":"Global Accelerator 的 custom routing accelerator 運作在 TCP/UDP 層,並沒有 HTTP header、signed cookie 或 authorization header 的概念。此選項把 CloudFront 才有的功能硬套在不支援這些功能的服務上。"},{"letter":"B","why_en":"OAC only supports AWS-native origins (S3, Lambda function URLs, MediaStore, MediaPackage v2) that can validate SigV4 signatures. A third-party external web server cannot use OAC, and 'include auth header in the OAC request' is not a real configuration option.","why_zh":"OAC 僅支援能夠驗證 SigV4 簽章的 AWS 原生 origin(S3、Lambda function URL、MediaStore、MediaPackage v2)。第三方外部網頁伺服器無法使用 OAC,而「在 OAC request 中加入 auth header」也不是真實存在的設定選項。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"Global Accelerator has no 'origin access control' feature at all — this is a CloudFront/S3 concept. This option conflates two unrelated AWS services and their features.","why_zh":"Global Accelerator 完全沒有「origin access control」這項功能,這是 CloudFront/S3 的概念。此選項混淆了兩個不相關的 AWS 服務及其功能。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonCloudFront/latest/DeveloperGuide/private-content-overview.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonCloudFront/latest/DeveloperGuide/add-origin-custom-headers.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonCloudFront/latest/DeveloperGuide/private-content-restricting-access-to-origin.html"]}},{"id":126,"question_en":"A company needs to follow security best practices to deploy resources from an AWS CloudFormation template. The CloudFormation template must be able to configure sensitive database credentials. The company already uses AWS Key Management Service (AWS KMS) and AWS Secrets Manager. Which solution will meet the requirements?","question_zh":"公司需要遵循安全最佳实践，从 AWS CloudFormation 模板中部署资源。该 CloudFormation 模 板必须能够配置敏感的数据库凭据。该公司已使用 AWS 密钥管理服务（AWS KMS）和 AWS Secrets Manager。 哪种方案能满足要求？","options_en":{"A":"Use a dynamic reference in the CloudFormation template to reference the database credentials in Secrets Manager.","B":"Use a parameter in the CloudFormation template to reference the database credentials. Encrypt the CloudFormation template by using AWS KMS.","C":"Use a SecureString parameter in the CloudFormation template to reference the database credentials in Secrets Manager.","D":"Use a SecureString parameter in the CloudFormation template to reference an encrypted value in AWS KMS."},"options_zh":{"A":"在 CloudFormation 模板中使用动态引用，以引用 Secrets Manager 中的数据库凭据。","B":"在 CloudFormation 模板中使用参数来引用数据库凭据，并通过 AWS KMS 对 CloudFormation 模板进行加密。","C":"在 CloudFormation 模板中使用 SecureString 参数来引用 Secrets Manager 中的数据库凭据。","D":"在 CloudFormation 模板中使用 SecureString 参数来引用 AWS KMS 中的加密值。"},"answer":["A"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Security/IAM","Database","Monitoring/Ops"],"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選","research":{"verdict":["A"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"Verified against AWS documentation. The CloudFormation best-practices guide explicitly states: 'For sensitive information such as passwords, API keys, and other secrets, use AWS Systems Manager Parameter Store or AWS Secrets Manager instead of embedding them directly in your templates. Use dynamic references in your templates to securely retrieve these values during stack operations.' A dynamic reference such as {{resolve:secretsmanager:secret-id:SecretString:json-key:version-stage:version-id}} lets CloudFormation fetch the current database credential value from Secrets Manager at stack create/update time, so the plaintext secret never appears in the template body, in CloudFormation API call parameters logged to CloudTrail, or in the console/CLI output -- this is exactly option A. I independently checked the CloudFormation-supplied parameter types documentation and confirmed there is no SecureString template parameter type in CloudFormation, in any context: the 'Unsupported Systems Manager parameter types' section states plainly, 'CloudFormation doesn't support defining template parameters as SecureString Systems Manager parameter types. However, you can specify secure strings as parameter values for certain resources' via dynamic references -- meaning SecureString is only reachable as a value fetched by a dynamic reference, never as a declared parameter Type. This rules out both C ('SecureString parameter... referencing Secrets Manager') and D ('SecureString parameter... referencing KMS'), since no such parameter type exists for either Secrets Manager or a raw KMS-encrypted value; these options describe a construct CloudFormation does not have. Option B is also wrong: a Parameter of type String (even with NoEcho) still requires the plaintext credential to be supplied as a stack parameter value and does not integrate with Secrets Manager at all; encrypting the template file with KMS only protects the template artifact at rest, not the runtime parameter value passed through the CreateStack/UpdateStack API, and is not how AWS documents securing sensitive template values. There is exactly one correct answer.","explanation_zh":"已對照 AWS 官方文件驗證。CloudFormation 最佳實務指南明確指出:「對於密碼、API 金鑰等敏感資訊,應使用 AWS Systems Manager Parameter Store 或 AWS Secrets Manager,而不要直接寫入範本中。在範本中使用 dynamic references,以便在堆疊操作期間安全地取得這些值。」像 {{resolve:secretsmanager:secret-id:SecretString:json-key:version-stage:version-id}} 這樣的 dynamic reference,可讓 CloudFormation 在建立/更新堆疊時直接從 Secrets Manager 擷取目前的資料庫憑證值,因此明文憑證不會出現在範本內容、CloudTrail 記錄的 CloudFormation API 呼叫參數,或主控台/CLI 輸出中——這正是選項 A 所描述的方式。我另外查閱了 CloudFormation 提供的參數類型文件,確認在任何情境下 CloudFormation 都沒有 SecureString 範本參數類型:文件中「Unsupported Systems Manager parameter types」一節明確指出:「CloudFormation 不支援將範本參數定義為 SecureString 類型的 Systems Manager 參數。不過,您可以透過某些資源將 secure string 指定為參數值」,也就是說 SecureString 只能透過 dynamic reference 取得的「值」出現,絕不會是宣告的參數 Type。因此選項 C(「SecureString 參數…參照 Secrets Manager」)與選項 D(「SecureString 參數…參照 KMS」)皆可排除,因為無論是 Secrets Manager 還是原始 KMS 加密值,都不存在這種參數類型;這兩個選項描述的是 CloudFormation 根本沒有的機制。選項 B 同樣錯誤:即使設定 NoEcho,String 類型的 Parameter 仍需要在堆疊參數值中提供明文憑證,且完全未與 Secrets Manager 整合;將範本檔案以 KMS 加密只能保護靜態存放的範本檔案本身,無法保護透過 CreateStack/UpdateStack API 傳遞的執行期參數值,這也不是 AWS 文件中保護範本敏感值所建議的方式。本題僅有一個正確答案。","distractors":[{"letter":"B","why_en":"Encrypting the template file with KMS only protects the artifact at rest; the plaintext credential must still be supplied as a runtime String parameter value through the CloudFormation API, which is not protected by template-file encryption and does not leverage Secrets Manager at all.","why_zh":"以 KMS 加密範本檔案僅能保護靜態存放的檔案本身;明文憑證仍須以執行期的 String 參數值透過 CloudFormation API 傳入,範本檔案加密無法保護此傳遞過程,且完全未運用 Secrets Manager。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"CloudFormation documentation explicitly states it does not support defining template parameters as SecureString Systems Manager parameter types, and there is no SecureString parameter type that references Secrets Manager -- this construct does not exist.","why_zh":"CloudFormation 文件明確指出不支援將範本參數定義為 SecureString 類型的 Systems Manager 參數,也沒有可參照 Secrets Manager 的 SecureString 參數類型——這種機制並不存在。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"Same underlying issue as C: SecureString is not a supported CloudFormation template parameter type in any context, including one referencing a raw KMS-encrypted value; secure strings can only be pulled in as resolved values via dynamic references, not declared as a parameter Type.","why_zh":"與選項 C 的問題相同:SecureString 在任何情境下都不是 CloudFormation 支援的範本參數類型,包括參照原始 KMS 加密值的情況;secure string 只能透過 dynamic reference 以「已解析的值」方式取得,不能宣告為參數的 Type。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AWSCloudFormation/latest/UserGuide/best-practices.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AWSCloudFormation/latest/UserGuide/cloudformation-supplied-parameter-types.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AWSCloudFormation/latest/UserGuide/dynamic-references-secretsmanager.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AWSCloudFormation/latest/UserGuide/dynamic-references.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/secretsmanager/latest/userguide/cfn-example_reference-secret.html"]}},{"id":127,"question_en":"A company needs to implement data lifecycle management for Amazon RDS snapshots. The company will use AWS Backup to manage the snapshots. The company must retain RDS automated snapshots for 5 years and will use Amazon S3 for long-term archival storage. Which solution will meet these requirements?","question_zh":"公司需要为 Amazon RDS 快照实施数据生命周期管理。公司将使用 AWS Backup 来管理这些快照， 必须保留 RDS 自动快照 5 年，并使用 Amazon S3 进行长期归档存储。 哪种解决方案能满足这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Use AWS Backup to apply a 5-year retention tag to the RDS snapshots.","B":"Enable versioning on the S3 bucket that AWS Backup uses for the RDS snapshots. Configure a 5-year retention period.","C":"Create an S3 Lifecycle policy. Include a 5-year retention period for the S3 bucket that AWS Backup uses for the RDS snapshots.","D":"Create a backup plan in AWS Backup. Configure a 5-year retention period."},"options_zh":{"A":"使用 AWS Backup 为 RDS 快照应用 5 年保留标签。","B":"在 AWS Backup 用于 RDS 快照的 S3 存储桶上启用版本控制，并配置 5 年的保留期。","C":"创建一个 S3 生命周期策略，为 AWS Backup 用于 RDS 快照的 S3 存储桶设置 5 年的保留期。","D":"在 AWS Backup 中创建备份计划，并配置 5 年的保留周期。"},"answer":["D"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Storage","Database"],"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選","research":{"verdict":["D"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"AWS Backup stores recovery points in backup vaults. AWS documentation consistently defines a backup vault as 'a secure AWS Backup container that stores immutable backups separately from source instances with encryption and resource-based access policies' -- it is an AWS-managed abstraction, not a customer-visible S3 bucket that you can attach S3 Lifecycle rules to or enable S3 versioning on. Retention is instead governed natively by the backup plan's lifecycle settings: AWS Backup's 'about backup plans' documentation states that 'AWS Backup also seamlessly manages your backup plan's lifecycle based on your retention settings.' When you create a backup plan (or edit a backup rule) you specify a retention period (e.g. 5 years / ~1825-2000 days, or use Backup Vault Lock to make it immutable), and AWS Backup automatically expires and deletes the recovery point once that period elapses; it can also transition eligible backups to cold storage for long-term, cost-effective archival, satisfying the 'S3 for long-term archival' requirement without any customer-managed S3 object handling. For RDS/Aurora specifically, AWS Backup documentation notes that only one recovery point exists per resource at a time, and changing the retention period updates that existing recovery point's expiration rather than creating a new one -- again confirming retention is a plan/lifecycle-level property, not an S3-object-level property. This makes option D, creating a backup plan with a 5-year retention period, the correct and only valid mechanism. Option A is wrong because AWS Backup does not use resource tags to define retention duration; tags are used only for resource selection/assignment into a backup plan, never for expressing how long a recovery point should be kept. Options B and C are both wrong for the same underlying reason: they assume RDS snapshots managed by AWS Backup live as ordinary, customer-manageable objects in an S3 bucket, but AWS Backup abstracts all recovery points behind backup vaults, so S3 bucket-level versioning (B) and S3 Lifecycle policies (C) simply do not apply to them. There is exactly one correct answer.","explanation_zh":"AWS Backup 會將復原點(recovery point)儲存在 backup vault 中。AWS 官方文件一致將 backup vault 定義為「一個安全的 AWS Backup 容器,以加密方式與資源型存取政策,將備份與來源執行個體分開儲存並保持不可變(immutable)」——這是由 AWS 管理的抽象層,並不是客戶可見、可以直接套用 S3 Lifecycle 規則或啟用 S3 版本控制的 S3 bucket。保留期則是透過 backup plan 內的 lifecycle 設定原生控管:AWS Backup 的 backup plan 說明文件指出「AWS Backup 也會依據你的保留設定,無縫地管理 backup plan 的 lifecycle」。當你建立 backup plan(或編輯 backup rule)時,你會指定一個保留期(例如 5 年,約 1825-2000 天,亦可搭配 Backup Vault Lock 使其不可變更),AWS Backup 會在期限到達時自動使該復原點到期並刪除;它也能將符合條件的備份轉移到 cold storage,以具成本效益的方式做長期封存,這樣就能滿足「使用 S3 做長期封存」的需求,而完全不需要客戶自行管理 S3 物件。特別針對 RDS/Aurora,AWS Backup 文件說明每個資源同一時間只會有一個復原點,變更保留期時只會更新該既有復原點的到期時間,而不會建立新的復原點——這再次證明保留期是 plan/lifecycle 層級的屬性,而非 S3 物件層級的屬性。因此選項 D,建立一個設定 5 年保留期的 backup plan,是唯一正確且有效的機制。選項 A 錯誤,因為 AWS Backup 並非透過資源標籤(tag)來定義保留期限;標籤僅用於將資源選取/指派進 backup plan,從未用於表達復原點應保留多久。選項 B 與 C 皆錯誤,原因相同:它們誤以為由 AWS Backup 管理的 RDS 快照,是以一般客戶可管理的物件形式存放在 S3 bucket 中,但 AWS Backup 將所有復原點抽象化並封裝在 backup vault 之後,因此 S3 bucket 層級的版本控制(B)與 S3 Lifecycle 政策(C)根本無法套用於這些復原點。本題僅有一個正確答案。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"AWS Backup does not use resource tags to define retention duration. Tags are used only for resource assignment/selection into backup plans; retention is governed exclusively by the lifecycle/retention period settings configured within the backup plan or backup rule itself.","why_zh":"AWS Backup 並不會透過資源標籤來定義保留期限。標籤僅用於將資源指派/選取進 backup plan;保留期完全是由 backup plan 或 backup rule 內配置的 lifecycle/retention period 設定所控制。"},{"letter":"B","why_en":"AWS Backup recovery points are stored in AWS-managed backup vaults -- immutable, encrypted containers -- not in a customer-visible or customer-manageable S3 bucket. There is no S3 bucket exposed to the customer on which to enable versioning to manage RDS snapshot retention through AWS Backup.","why_zh":"AWS Backup 的復原點是儲存在 AWS 管理的 backup vault(不可變、加密的容器)中,而不是儲存在客戶可見或可管理的 S3 bucket 裡。並沒有任何暴露給客戶的 S3 bucket 可以讓你啟用版本控制,來透過 AWS Backup 管理 RDS 快照的保留。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"Since AWS Backup abstracts storage into backup vaults rather than a directly manageable S3 bucket, S3 Lifecycle policies cannot be applied to control the retention of RDS recovery points managed by AWS Backup; retention must instead be set through the backup plan's own lifecycle configuration.","why_zh":"由於 AWS Backup 將儲存抽象化為 backup vault,而非可直接管理的 S3 bucket,因此無法套用 S3 Lifecycle 政策來控制由 AWS Backup 管理的 RDS 復原點的保留期;保留期必須透過 backup plan 本身的 lifecycle 設定來配置。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/aws-backup/latest/devguide/about-backup-plans.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/aws-backup/latest/devguide/whatisbackup.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/aws-backup/latest/devguide/vaults.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/aws-backup/latest/devguide/creating-a-backup-plan.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/aws-backup/latest/devguide/point-in-time-recovery-retention-period.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/aws-backup/latest/devguide/deleting-backups.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/aws-backup/latest/devguide/tags-on-backups.html"]}},{"id":128,"question_en":"A company runs a web application on a fleet of Amazon EC2 instances that are in an Auto Scaling group. The EC2 instances are in the same VPC subnet as other workloads. A security engineer deploys an Amazon GuardDuty detector in the same AWS Region as the EC2 instances and integrates GuardDuty with AWS Security Hub. The security engineer needs to implement an automated solution to detect and appropriately respond to anomalous traffic patterns for the web application. The solution must comply with AWS best practices forinitial response to security incidentsand mustminimize disruptionto the web application. Which solution will meet these requirements?","question_zh":"一家公司在由自动扩展组管理的一组 Amazon EC2 实例上运行 Web 应用程序。这些 EC2 实例与其他 工作负载位于同一个 VPC 子网中。 安全工程师在与EC2实例相同的AWS区域中部署了Amazon GuardDuty检测器，并将GuardDuty与 AWS Security Hub集成。 安全工程师需要实施一种自动化解决方案，以检测并妥善响应Web应用中的异常流量模式。该 方案必须符合AWS在安全事件初始响应方面的最佳实践，并尽可能减少对Web应用的干扰。 哪种解决方案能满足这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Disable the EC2 instance profile credentials by using AWS Lambda.","B":"Create an Amazon EventBridge rule that invokes an AWS Lambda function when GuardDuty detects anomalous traffic. Configure the function to remove the affected instance from the Auto Scaling group and attach a restricted security group.","C":"Update the subnet network ACL to block traffic from the detected source IP addresses.","D":"Send GuardDuty findings to Amazon SNS for email notification."},"options_zh":{"A":"使用 AWS Lambda 禁用 EC2 实例配置文件凭据。","B":"创建一个 Amazon EventBridge 规则，当 GuardDuty 检测到异常流量时调用 AWS Lambda 函数。 配置该函数以将受影响的实例从自动扩展组中移除，并附加一个受限的安全组。","C":"更新子网网络ACL，以阻止来自检测到的源IP地址的流量。","D":"将 GuardDuty 的发现结果发送到 Amazon SNS 以进行电子邮件通知。"},"answer":["B"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Security/IAM","Compute","Serverless/Integration"],"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選","research":{"verdict":["B"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"both","explanation_en":"This question is a near-duplicate of Q120, with only cosmetic wording differences that do not change the analysis: it adds that the GuardDuty detector is deployed 'in the same AWS Region as the EC2 instances' (a technical prerequisite for GuardDuty to see the traffic, not a distinguishing detail), it renames 'network ACL' to 'subnet network ACL' in option C (same scope, still subnet-wide), and critically, option B now spells out the exact automation mechanism -- an Amazon EventBridge rule that invokes an AWS Lambda function when GuardDuty detects anomalous traffic, with the function removing the instance from the Auto Scaling group and attaching a restricted security group. This is precisely the architecture AWS documents for automated, event-driven incident response: GuardDuty findings are published to EventBridge, which triggers a Lambda function to remediate. AWS's GuardDuty user guide, 'Remediating a potentially compromised Amazon EC2 instance,' directs engineers to create a dedicated isolation security group with no 0.0.0.0/0 inbound/outbound rules and associate it with the compromised instance, rather than terminating it, in order to preserve forensic evidence. Because the instance is managed by an Auto Scaling group, it must first be removed from the group so the ASG's health check automatically replaces it with a new healthy instance, preserving application capacity and minimizing disruption -- this is the same behavior implemented by the AWS-QuarantineEC2Instance SSM Automation runbook. Option A only disables the instance's IAM credentials and does nothing to block the anomalous network traffic itself. Option C modifies a network ACL at the subnet level, collaterally affecting every other unrelated workload sharing that subnet. Option D only sends a notification for a human to act on, providing no automated response at all. The answer is unambiguously B, matching Q120's resolution.","explanation_zh":"此題與 Q120 幾乎完全相同,僅有幾處純文字上的差異,不影響分析結果:題目多說明 GuardDuty detector 部署在與 EC2 執行個體「相同的 AWS 區域」(這只是 GuardDuty 能偵測到流量的技術前提,並非用來區分選項的關鍵細節);選項 C 將「network ACL」改稱為「subnet network ACL」,範圍其實相同,依然是整個 subnet 層級;而關鍵是選項 B 明確寫出了自動化的具體機制——建立一個 Amazon EventBridge 規則,在 GuardDuty 偵測到異常流量時觸發 AWS Lambda 函式,並由該函式將受影響的執行個體從 Auto Scaling group 中移除、附加受限的 security group。這正是 AWS 官方文件所描述的事件驅動自動化事件回應架構:GuardDuty 的發現項目會發布到 EventBridge,再由其觸發 Lambda 函式進行修復。AWS GuardDuty 使用者指南中「Remediating a potentially compromised Amazon EC2 instance」建議建立一個不允許 0.0.0.0/0 進出流量的專用隔離 security group 並套用到受感染的執行個體上,而不是直接終止它,以保留取證證據。由於該執行個體由 Auto Scaling group 管理,必須先將其從群組中移除,讓 ASG 的健康檢查機制自動以一個新的健康執行個體取代,藉此維持應用程式容量並將干擾降到最低——這與 AWS-QuarantineEC2Instance SSM Automation runbook 的處理方式一致。選項 A 僅停用該執行個體的 IAM 憑證,完全無法阻擋異常的網路流量本身。選項 C 修改的是 subnet 層級的 network ACL,會連帶影響同一 subnet 中其他不相關的工作負載。選項 D 只發送通知讓人員處理,完全沒有自動化的應變動作。答案明確為 B,與 Q120 的結論一致。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"Disabling the EC2 instance profile credentials only removes the instance's ability to call AWS APIs; it does nothing to stop or contain the anomalous network traffic (e.g., outbound C2 traffic) at the network layer, which is the actual threat GuardDuty flagged.","why_zh":"停用 EC2 instance profile 的憑證只會移除該執行個體呼叫 AWS API 的能力,對於網路層面的異常流量(例如對外的 C2 連線)完全沒有阻擋效果,而這才是 GuardDuty 偵測到的實際威脅。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"Network ACLs apply at the subnet level, so blocking traffic from the detected source IP addresses this way would affect every other workload sharing that same VPC subnet, violating the requirement to minimize disruption beyond the compromised instance.","why_zh":"Network ACL 是套用在整個 subnet 層級,以此方式封鎖來自偵測到的來源 IP 位址的流量,會影響同一個 VPC subnet 中所有其他的工作負載,違反了將影響範圍侵限縮在受感染執行個體之外、降低干擾的要求。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"Sending findings to SNS only notifies a human; it provides no automated detection-to-response action, failing the question's explicit requirement for an automated solution.","why_zh":"將發現項目傳送到 SNS 只是通知人員,並未提供任何自動化的偵測到應變動作,無法滿足題目明確要求的自動化解決方案。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/guardduty/latest/ug/compromised-ec2.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/systems-manager-automation-runbooks/latest/userguide/aws-quarantineec2instance.html"]}},{"id":129,"question_en":"A company uses an organization in AWS Organizations to manage multiple AWS accounts. A security engineer creates a WAF policy in AWS Firewall Manager in the us-east-1 Region. The security engineer sets the policy scope to apply to resources that are tagged withWAF-protected:truein one of the member accounts in the organization. The security engineer sets up a configuration to automatically remediate any noncompliant resources. In a member account, the security engineer attempts to protect an Amazon API Gateway REST API in the us- east-1 Region by using a web ACL. However, after several minutes, the REST API is still not associated with the web ACL. What is the likely cause of this issue?","question_zh":"一家公司使用 AWS Organizations 中的组织来管理多个 AWS 账户。安全工程师在 us-east-1 区域的 AWS Firewall Manager 中创建了一个 WAF 策略，并将策略范围设置为应用于组织内某个成员账户中 标签为 WAF-protected:true 的资源。安全工程师还配置了自动修复任何不符合要求资源的设置。 在成员账户中，安全工程师尝试通过使用网络ACL来保护位于us-east-1区域的Amazon API Gateway REST API。然而，几分 钟后，该REST API仍未与网络ACL关联。 这个问题的可能原因是什么？","options_en":{"A":"Web ACLs cannot be applied to REST APIs.","B":"The REST API is missing a tag that includes theWAF-protectedkey and a value oftrue.","C":"The web ACL is already associated with another REST API.","D":"The web ACL is already associated with an Amazon CloudFront distribution."},"options_zh":{"A":"Web ACL 无法应用于 REST API。","B":"REST API 缺少一个包含 WAF 保护密钥且值为 true 的标签。","C":"该网络ACL已与另一个REST API关联。","D":"该网络ACL已与Amazon CloudFront分发关联。"},"answer":["B"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Networking/DNS","Organizations/Governance","Security/IAM","Serverless/Integration"],"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選","research":{"verdict":["B"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"A Firewall Manager AWS WAF policy applies only to resources that fall within the policy scope. Here the scope was set to 'resources tagged WAF-protected:true', which corresponds to the 'Only resources that have any of the tags that you specify' scope option. Firewall Manager continuously evaluates in-scope resources and, with automatic remediation enabled, associates its managed web ACL with them. An API Gateway REST API that is missing the WAF-protected=true tag is out of scope, so Firewall Manager never treats it as noncompliant and never auto-associates the web ACL. Resource tags only match when both the key and value are identical, so the missing tag is the likely cause.","explanation_zh":"Firewall Manager 的 AWS WAF 政策只會套用到落在政策範圍（scope）內的資源。本題的範圍設定為『帶有 WAF-protected:true 標籤的資源』，對應到 scope 選項中的『Only resources that have any of the tags that you specify』。Firewall Manager 會持續評估範圍內的資源，並在啟用自動修復（automatic remediation）時，把它管理的 web ACL 關聯到這些資源。若該 API Gateway REST API 缺少 WAF-protected=true 標籤，就落在範圍之外，Firewall Manager 不會把它視為不合規，也就不會自動關聯 web ACL。資源標籤必須 key 與 value 完全相符才算命中，因此缺少該標籤是最可能的原因。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"False. AWS WAF web ACLs can be associated with API Gateway REST API stages; AWS documents this directly ('Associate an AWS WAF web ACL with an API stage') and the AssociateWebACL API lists API Gateway as a supported resource.","why_zh":"錯誤。AWS WAF web ACL 可以關聯到 API Gateway REST API 的 stage；AWS 文件直接記載（『Associate an AWS WAF web ACL with an API stage』），且 AssociateWebACL API 也列出 API Gateway 為支援的資源。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"Wrong. A Regional web ACL (which a Firewall Manager WAF policy manages) can be associated with multiple regional resources simultaneously, so an existing association with another REST API would not block this one.","why_zh":"錯誤。Regional web ACL（Firewall Manager WAF 政策所管理者）可同時關聯多個 regional 資源，因此已關聯到另一個 REST API 不會阻擋此次關聯。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"Wrong. CloudFront distributions require a Global (CLOUDFRONT) scope web ACL, whereas API Gateway in us-east-1 uses a Regional web ACL; these are separate objects/policies. A CloudFront association does not prevent associating a Regional web ACL with a REST API.","why_zh":"錯誤。CloudFront distribution 需使用 Global（CLOUDFRONT）範圍的 web ACL，而 us-east-1 的 API Gateway 使用 Regional web ACL；兩者是不同的物件/政策。與 CloudFront 的關聯並不會阻擋將 Regional web ACL 關聯到 REST API。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/waf/latest/developerguide/policy-scope.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/waf/latest/developerguide/working-with-policies.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/apigateway/latest/developerguide/apigateway-control-access-aws-waf.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/waf/latest/developerguide/web-acl-associating.html"]}},{"id":130,"question_en":"A company uses AWS Config rules to identify Amazon S3 buckets that are not compliant with the company’s data protection policy. The S3 buckets are hosted in several AWS Regions and several AWS accounts. The accounts are in an organization in AWS Organizations. The company needs a solution to remediate the organization ' s existing noncompliant S3 buckets and any noncompliant S3 buckets that are created in the future. Which solution will meet these requirements?","question_zh":"一家公司使用 AWS Config 规则来识别不符合其数据保护策略的 Amazon S3 存储桶。这些 S3 存储桶分布在多个 AWS 区域和 多个 AWS 账户中，而这些账户属于 AWS Organizations 中的一个组织。该公司需要一种解决方案，以修复当前组织内所有 不符合要求的 S3 存储桶，并确保未来创建的任何不符合要求的 S3 存储桶也能得到及时处理。 哪种解决方案能满足这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Deploy an AWS Config aggregator with organization-wide resource data aggregation. Create an AWS Lambda function that responds to AWS Config findings of noncompliant S3 buckets by deleting or reconfiguring the S3 buckets.","B":"Deploy an AWS Config aggregator with organization-wide resource data aggregation. Create an SCP that contains a Deny statement that prevents the creation of new noncompliant S3 buckets. Apply the SCP to all OUs in the organization.","C":"Deploy an AWS Config aggregator that scopes only the accounts and Regions that the company currently uses. Create an AWS Lambda function that responds to AWS Config findings of noncompliant S3 buckets by deleting or reconfiguring the S3 buckets.","D":"Deploy an AWS Config aggregator that scopes only the accounts and Regions that the company currently uses. Create an SCP that contains a Deny statement that prevents the creation of new noncompliant S3 buckets. Apply the SCP to all OUs in the organization."},"options_zh":{"A":"部署一个支持跨组织资源数据聚合的 AWS Config 聚合器。创建一个 AWS Lambda 函数，用于响应 AWS Config 发现 的不符合合规要求的 S3 存储桶，并删除或重新配置这些 S3 存储桶。","B":"部署一个 AWS Config 聚合器，以实现跨整个组织的资源数据聚合。创建一个包含拒绝语句的服务控制策略（SCP），以防止 创建新的不符合合规要求的 S3 存储桶，并将该 SCP 应用于组织中的所有组织单元（OU）。","C":"部署一个 AWS Config 聚合器，仅涵盖公司当前使用的账户和区域。创建一个 AWS Lambda 函数，用于响应 AWS Config 发现的不符合合规要求的 S3 存储桶，并删除或重新配置这些 S3 存储桶。","D":"部署一个 AWS Config 聚合器，仅涵盖公司当前使用的账户和区域。创建一个包含拒绝语句的 SCP，以防止创建新的 不符合合规要求的 S3 存储桶，并将该 SCP 应用于组织中的所有 OU。"},"answer":["A"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Organizations/Governance","Storage","Compute"],"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選","research":{"verdict":["A"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"The requirement has two parts: remediate EXISTING noncompliant S3 buckets AND handle FUTURE noncompliant buckets, across many accounts/Regions in an AWS Organization. Only the Lambda-based options (A and C) can remediate existing resources, because they respond to AWS Config compliance findings and delete or reconfigure the offending buckets; an SCP Deny statement (B and D) is purely preventive and cannot touch buckets that already exist, so B and D fail the 'remediate existing' requirement outright. Between A and C, the deciding qualifier is 'the organization's ... buckets and any created in the future.' An organization-wide AWS Config aggregator automatically covers all current AND newly added accounts in the organization, whereas C's aggregator scoped to 'only the accounts and Regions the company currently uses' would silently miss accounts/Regions added later, breaking the future coverage. Note the aggregator is a read-only view and cannot itself mutate resources, but in A the remediation is performed by the Lambda (via cross-account permissions) using the org-wide aggregated compliance data as its signal. Therefore A is correct.","explanation_zh":"需求分兩部分：修復現有不合規的 S3 buckets，並處理未來新建的不合規 buckets，且橫跨 AWS Organizations 內多個帳號與多個 Region。只有以 Lambda 為基礎的選項（A 與 C）能修復現有資源，因為它們回應 AWS Config 的合規性發現並刪除或重新設定違規 bucket；而 SCP 的 Deny 陳述（B 與 D）純屬預防性質，無法動到已存在的 bucket，因此 B、D 直接無法滿足『修復現有』的要求。A 與 C 之間的決勝點在於題目說『組織的 buckets 以及未來建立的』。organization-wide 的 AWS Config aggregator 會自動涵蓋組織內所有現有與新加入的帳號，而 C 的 aggregator 只涵蓋『目前使用的帳號與 Region』，日後新增的帳號/Region 會被漏掉，無法保證未來覆蓋。須注意 aggregator 本身是唯讀檢視、無法自行變更資源，但在 A 中實際的修復是由 Lambda（透過跨帳號權限）根據組織彙總的合規資料執行。故 A 正確。","distractors":[{"letter":"B","why_en":"An SCP Deny statement is preventive only; it blocks future noncompliant bucket creation but cannot remediate the existing noncompliant buckets, so it fails half the requirement. SCPs also cannot reliably evaluate all data-protection compliance conditions at PutBucket time.","why_zh":"SCP 的 Deny 只是預防性，能阻擋未來建立不合規 bucket，卻無法修復現有的不合規 bucket，未滿足一半需求；且 SCP 在 PutBucket 當下也難以可靠評估所有資料保護合規條件。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"The remediation Lambda is fine, but scoping the aggregator to only currently-used accounts and Regions means newly added accounts/Regions in the organization are not covered, so future noncompliant buckets in new accounts would be missed.","why_zh":"修復用的 Lambda 沒問題，但 aggregator 僅限目前使用的帳號與 Region，組織日後新增的帳號/Region 不會被涵蓋，導致新帳號中未來的不合規 bucket 被漏掉。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"Combines both flaws: the SCP Deny is preventive-only and cannot fix existing buckets, and the narrowly scoped aggregator misses future accounts/Regions. It fails the 'remediate existing' requirement.","why_zh":"同時具備兩個缺陷：SCP Deny 僅預防、無法修復現有 bucket，且範圍受限的 aggregator 漏掉未來的帳號/Region，未滿足『修復現有』的需求。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/config/latest/developerguide/aggregate-data.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/config/latest/developerguide/setup-aggregator-console.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/config/latest/developerguide/remediation.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/organizations/latest/userguide/orgs_manage_policies_scps.html"]}},{"id":131,"question_en":"A company is undergoing a security audit. The company issues IAM user credentials for an auditor. Because of third-party integration requirements, the auditor is unable to assume an IAM role. The auditor attempts to log in to AWS for the first time to reset the account password and to configure multi-factor authentication (MFA). However, the auditor receives an “Access Denied” error during the attempt to reset the password. The auditor’s account has the following IAM permissions: securityhub:Get* securityhub:List* securityhub:BatchGet* securityhub:Describe* iam:ChangePassword on arn:aws:iam::*:user/${aws:username} Which action will resolve this error?","question_zh":"一家公司正在接受安全审计。该公司为审计人员发放了IAM用户凭证。由于第三方集成的要求，审计人员无法承担IAM角色。审计 人员首次尝试登录AWS以重置账户密码并配置多因素认证（MFA），但在重置密码时收到了“访问被拒绝”的错误提示。 审计员账户具有以下 IAM 权限： securityhub:Get* securityhub：列出* securityhub：BatchGet* securityhub：Describe* iam:ChangePassword aws:iam::*:user/${aws:username} 哪个操作可以解决此错误？","options_en":{"A":"The auditor needs to configure MFA before resetting the password.","B":"The auditor must create a more complex password that requires additional characters or symbols.","C":"Add iam:GetAccountPasswordPolicy with Resource: \" * \" to the auditor’s user account policy.","D":"Add iam:ChangePassword with Resource: \" * \" to the auditor’s user account policy."},"options_zh":{"A":"审计员在重置密码前需要先配置多因素认证。","B":"审计员必须创建一个更复杂的密码，需要包含额外的字符或符号。","C":"将 iam:GetAccountPasswordPolicy 权限（资源为“*”）添加到审计员的用户账户策略中。","D":"将“ChangePassword”权限及其资源设置为“*”，添加到审计员的用户账户策略中。"},"answer":["C"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Security/IAM"],"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選","research":{"verdict":["C"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"The auditor already has iam:ChangePassword scoped to arn:aws:iam::*:user/${aws:username}, which is exactly what AWS's recommended self-service password policy grants. The missing piece is iam:GetAccountPasswordPolicy with Resource \"*\". AWS documentation for 'Permit IAM users to change their own passwords' states that the recommended policy pairs iam:ChangePassword with iam:GetAccountPasswordPolicy, and explicitly says: 'this permission is required so that the user can view the account password policy on the Change password page. The user must be allowed to read the current password policy to ensure that the changed password meets the requirements of the policy.' Without iam:GetAccountPasswordPolicy, the Change password page cannot load the account password requirements and the user hits Access Denied when resetting the password on first sign-in. Adding iam:GetAccountPasswordPolicy with Resource \"*\" (option C) resolves the error.","explanation_zh":"此稽核員的權限已包含 iam:ChangePassword 且範圍限定於 arn:aws:iam::*:user/${aws:username}，這正是 AWS 建議的自助改密碼原則所授予的內容。真正缺少的是帶有 Resource \"*\" 的 iam:GetAccountPasswordPolicy。AWS 官方文件「Permit IAM users to change their own passwords」中建議的原則會將 iam:ChangePassword 與 iam:GetAccountPasswordPolicy 成對授予，並明確指出：此權限是必要的，讓使用者能在『變更密碼』頁面檢視帳戶密碼原則；使用者必須被允許讀取目前的密碼原則，以確保變更後的密碼符合原則要求。缺少 iam:GetAccountPasswordPolicy 時，變更密碼頁面無法載入帳戶密碼要求，導致使用者首次登入重設密碼時出現 Access Denied。加入帶有 Resource \"*\" 的 iam:GetAccountPasswordPolicy（選項 C）即可解決此錯誤。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"MFA is not a prerequisite for resetting a password. The user is not required to configure MFA before setting a password; the flow is blocked by a missing IAM permission (GetAccountPasswordPolicy), not by MFA ordering.","why_zh":"MFA 並非重設密碼的前置條件。使用者不需要先設定 MFA 才能設定密碼；此流程是被缺少的 IAM 權限（GetAccountPasswordPolicy）擋住，而非 MFA 的先後順序。"},{"letter":"B","why_en":"A weak/complex password would produce a validation message about password requirements, not an 'Access Denied' authorization error. The Access Denied is an IAM permissions failure, not a password-strength failure.","why_zh":"密碼過弱或需要更複雜的字元會出現密碼要求的驗證訊息，而非『Access Denied』授權錯誤。Access Denied 是 IAM 權限失敗，而非密碼強度問題。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"The auditor already has iam:ChangePassword. Broadening its resource to \"*\" changes nothing about the failure, and because the auditor cannot assume roles, scope-widening to other users is unnecessary and against least privilege; the ChangePassword statement is already correct per the AWS reference policy.","why_zh":"稽核員已擁有 iam:ChangePassword。將其資源放寬為 \"*\" 對此失敗毫無幫助；且因稽核員無法擔任角色，將範圍擴大到其他使用者既不必要也違反最小權限。ChangePassword 陳述式已與 AWS 參考原則一致。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/IAM/latest/UserGuide/id_credentials_passwords_enable-user-change.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/IAM/latest/UserGuide/id_credentials_passwords_user-change-own.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/IAM/latest/UserGuide/security-iam-awsmanpol.html"]}},{"id":132,"question_en":"A company is planning to migrate its applications to AWS in a single AWS Region. The company’s applications will use a combination of Amazon EC2 instances, Elastic Load Balancing (ELB) load balancers, and Amazon S3 buckets. The company wants to complete the migration as quickly as possible. All the applications must meet the following requirements: • Data must be encrypted at rest. • Data must be encrypted in transit. • Endpoints must be monitored for anomalous network traffic. Which combination of steps should a security engineer take to meet these requirements with the LEAST effort? (Select THREE.)","question_zh":"一家公司计划将其应用程序迁移到AWS的单个区域。该公司的应用程序将使用Amazon EC2实例、弹性负载均衡（ELB）负载 均衡器以及Amazon S3存储桶的组合。公司希望尽快完成迁移，所有应用程序必须满足以下要求： • 数据在静态存储时必须进行加密。 数据在传输过程中必须加密。 必须对端点进行监控，以检测异常的网络流量。 安全工程师应采取哪些步骤组合，才能以最少的努力满足这些要求？（选择三项。）","options_en":{"A":"Install the Amazon Inspector agent on EC2 instances by using AWS Systems Manager Automation.","B":"Enable Amazon GuardDuty in all AWS accounts.","C":"Create VPC endpoints for Amazon EC2 and Amazon S3. Update VPC route tables to use only the secure VPC endpoints.","D":"Configure AWS Certificate Manager (ACM). Configure the load balancers to use certificates from ACM.","E":"Use AWS Key Management Service (AWS KMS) for key management. Create an S3 bucket policy to deny any PutObject command with a condition for x-amz-meta-side-encryption.","F":"Use AWS Key Management Service (AWS KMS) for key management. Create an S3 bucket policy to deny any PutObject command with a condition for x-amz-server-side-encryption."},"options_zh":{"A":"使用 AWS Systems Manager Automation 在 EC2 实例上安装 Amazon Inspector 代理。","B":"在所有 AWS 账户中启用 Amazon GuardDuty。","C":"为 Amazon EC2 和 Amazon S3 创建 VPC 终端节点，并更新 VPC 路由表，使其仅使用安全的 VPC 终端节点。","D":"配置 AWS 证书管理器（ACM），并将负载均衡器配置为使用来自 ACM 的证书。","E":"使用 AWS 密钥管理服务（AWS KMS）进行密钥管理。创建一个 S3 存储桶策略，拒绝任何带有 x-amz-meta-side- encryption 条件的 PutObject 操作。","F":"使用 AWS 密钥管理服务（AWS KMS）进行密钥管理。创建一个 S3 存储桶策略，拒绝任何带有 x-amz-server-side- encryption 条件的 PutObject 操作。"},"answer":["B","D","F"],"multi":true,"vote":{},"tags":["Migration","Security/IAM","Storage","Compute","Monitoring/Ops"],"difficulty":2,"diff_why":"複選","research":{"verdict":["B","D","F"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"Three requirements map to three least-effort managed services. Encryption in transit: ACM issues/manages free public TLS certificates, and attaching them to an ELB HTTPS/TLS listener terminates TLS with no cert-rotation effort (D). Encryption at rest for S3: use KMS for key management and enforce it with a bucket policy that denies any s3:PutObject unless the request carries the server-side-encryption header. The valid S3 condition key is s3:x-amz-server-side-encryption (F). Option E is a trap: x-amz-meta-side-encryption is not a real encryption condition key (x-amz-meta-* is the user-metadata prefix), so that policy would not enforce encryption. Endpoint/network anomaly monitoring: GuardDuty, once enabled, automatically ingests VPC Flow Logs, Route 53 DNS query logs, and CloudTrail management events to detect anomalous and malicious network traffic with no agents to install and nothing else to configure (B) - the lowest-effort choice.","explanation_zh":"三項需求對應三個最省力的受控服務。傳輸中加密：ACM 免費簽發並自動管理公有 TLS 憑證，掛到 ELB 的 HTTPS/TLS 監聽器即完成 TLS 終止且免手動輪替（D）。S3 靜態加密：以 KMS 做金鑰管理，並用 bucket policy 拒絕未帶伺服器端加密標頭的 s3:PutObject 來強制加密；正確的條件鍵是 s3:x-amz-server-side-encryption（F）。選項 E 是陷阱：x-amz-meta-side-encryption 並非真實的加密條件鍵（x-amz-meta-* 是使用者中繼資料前綴），該政策無法強制加密。端點/網路異常監控：GuardDuty 一經啟用即自動分析 VPC Flow Logs、Route 53 DNS 查詢日誌與 CloudTrail 管理事件以偵測異常與惡意網路流量，無需安裝代理、無需額外設定（B），為最省力選項。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"Amazon Inspector performs vulnerability/CVE and network-reachability assessment, not continuous monitoring for anomalous network traffic; installing agents via SSM is also more effort than agentless GuardDuty.","why_zh":"Amazon Inspector 做的是弱點/CVE 與網路可達性評估，並非對異常網路流量的持續監控；且透過 SSM 安裝代理比免代理的 GuardDuty 更費工。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"VPC endpoints keep traffic on the AWS backbone but do not monitor for anomalous network traffic, and forcing route tables to use only these endpoints adds effort while satisfying none of the three stated requirements directly.","why_zh":"VPC 端點讓流量走 AWS 骨幹，但不會監控異常網路流量；強制路由表只用這些端點反而增加工作量，且無法直接滿足題目三項需求中的任一項。"},{"letter":"E","why_en":"Uses the condition key x-amz-meta-side-encryption, which is not a valid S3 encryption condition key (x-amz-meta-* is the user-metadata prefix), so the bucket policy would fail to enforce encryption at rest.","why_zh":"使用了 x-amz-meta-side-encryption 這個條件鍵，但它並非有效的 S3 加密條件鍵（x-amz-meta-* 是使用者中繼資料前綴），因此該 bucket policy 無法真正強制靜態加密。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonS3/latest/userguide/UsingKMSEncryption.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonS3/latest/userguide/amazon-s3-policy-keys.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/guardduty/latest/ug/guardduty_data-sources.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/elasticloadbalancing/latest/userguide/data-protection.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/acm/latest/userguide/acm-overview.html"]}},{"id":133,"question_en":"A security engineer uses Amazon Macie to scan a company ' s Amazon S3 buckets for sensitive data. The company has many S3 buckets and many objects stored in the S3 buckets. The security engineer must identify S3 buckets that contain sensitive data and must perform additional scanning on those S3 buckets. Which solution will meet these requirements with the LEAST administrative overhead?","question_zh":"安全工程师使用 Amazon Macie 扫描公司 Amazon S3 存储桶中的敏感数据。该公司拥有大量 S3 存储桶，以及存储在这些存储桶中的众 多对象。安全工程师需要识别包含敏感数据的 S3 存储桶，并对这些存储桶执行进一步扫描。 哪种解决方案能在最少的管理开销下满足这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Configure S3 Cross-Region Replication (CRR) on the S3 buckets to replicate the objects to a second AWS Region. Configure Macie in the second Region to scan the replicated objects daily.","B":"Create an AWS Lambda function as an S3 event destination for the S3 buckets. Configure the Lambda function to start a Macie scan of an object when the object is uploaded to an S3 bucket.","C":"Configure Macie automated discovery to continuously sample data from the S3 buckets. Perform full scans of the S3 buckets where Macie discovers sensitive data.","D":"Configure Macie scans to run on the S3 buckets. Aggregate the results of the scans in an Amazon DynamoDB table. Use the DynamoDB table for queries."},"options_zh":{"A":"在S3存储桶上配置S3跨区域复制（CRR），将对象复制到第二个AWS区域。在第二个区域中配置Macie，每天扫描复制的对 象。","B":"创建一个 AWS Lambda 函数作为 S3 存储桶的事件目标。配置该 Lambda 函数，以便在对象上传到 S3 存储桶时启动 Macie 对该 对象的扫描。","C":"配置 Macie 自动发现功能，持续从 S3 存储桶中采样数据，并对 Macie 发现敏感数据的 S3 存储桶执行完整扫描。","D":"配置 Macie 扫描以在 S3 存储桶上运行，将扫描结果汇总到 Amazon DynamoDB 表中，并使用该 DynamoDB 表进行查询。"},"answer":["C"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Security/IAM","Storage","Compute","Database"],"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選","research":{"verdict":["C"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"Amazon Macie offers two discovery methods. Automated sensitive data discovery evaluates the S3 bucket inventory on a daily basis and uses sampling techniques to select and analyze representative objects, giving broad, low-effort visibility into which buckets likely contain sensitive data. Sensitive data discovery jobs then provide deeper, targeted (full) analysis of the specific buckets you select. Option C chains these two native features exactly as AWS intends: enable automated discovery (a single toggle, continuous sampling) to surface buckets with sensitive data, then run full discovery-job scans on only those buckets. This is the least-administrative-overhead approach because it requires no custom code, no replication, and no external aggregation. It also scales cleanly across many buckets and many objects.","explanation_zh":"Amazon Macie 提供兩種偵測方式。Automated sensitive data discovery（自動化敏感資料偵測）每天評估 S3 bucket 清單，並使用抽樣（sampling）技術挑選代表性物件進行分析，能以最小管理成本廣泛掌握哪些 bucket 可能含有敏感資料。Sensitive data discovery jobs（敏感資料偵測工作）則對你指定的特定 bucket 做更深入、完整的掃描。選項 C 正好把這兩個原生功能串接起來，符合 AWS 建議的做法：先啟用自動化偵測（單一開關、持續抽樣）找出含敏感資料的 bucket，再只對這些 bucket 執行完整的 discovery job 掃描。此做法不需自訂程式碼、不需跨區複製、也不需外部彙整，因此管理成本最低，並能在大量 bucket 與物件的情境下良好擴展。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"Configuring Cross-Region Replication to a second Region and scanning the replicated copies doubles storage cost and adds significant setup/operational overhead. Macie is a regional service; there is no need to replicate objects to another Region to scan them, so this is far from the least overhead.","why_zh":"設定跨區複製（CRR）到第二個 Region 並掃描複製副本會使儲存成本翻倍並大幅增加設定與維運負擔。Macie 是區域性服務，掃描資料根本不需要複製到另一個 Region，因此完全不是管理成本最低的方案。"},{"letter":"B","why_en":"Building a Lambda function as an S3 event destination to trigger a per-object Macie scan on upload requires custom code and event wiring, scans object-by-object, and does not cleanly identify which buckets already contain sensitive data across a large existing estate. This is high, not least, administrative overhead.","why_zh":"建立 Lambda 作為 S3 事件目的地、在物件上傳時逐一觸發 Macie 掃描，需要自訂程式碼與事件串接，且是逐物件掃描，也無法乾淨地在龐大既有資料中辨識哪些 bucket 已含敏感資料。這屬於高（而非最低）管理成本。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"Running Macie scans and then aggregating results into a DynamoDB table for querying adds a custom data pipeline that must be built and maintained. Macie already exposes bucket sensitivity scores, findings, and results natively, so DynamoDB aggregation is unnecessary overhead and does not, by itself, drive additional targeted scans of the flagged buckets.","why_zh":"執行 Macie 掃描後再把結果彙整到 DynamoDB 供查詢，需要自行建置並維護一條自訂資料管線。Macie 本身已原生提供 bucket 敏感度分數、findings 與 results，因此 DynamoDB 彙整是多餘的負擔，且本身並不會驅動對被標記 bucket 的後續針對性掃描。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/macie/latest/user/data-classification.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/macie/latest/user/discovery-asdd.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/macie/latest/user/discovery-jobs.html"]}},{"id":134,"question_en":"A company runs a public web application on Amazon EKS behind Amazon CloudFront and an Application Load Balancer (ALB). A security engineer must send a notification to an existing Amazon SNS topic when the application receives 10,000 requests from the same end-user IP address within any 5-minute period. Which solution will meet these requirements?","question_zh":"一家公司在 Amazon EKS 上运行一个公共网络应用，该应用位于 Amazon CloudFront 和 Application Load Balancer（ALB）之后。安 全工程师需要在应用在任意 5 分钟内从同一终端用户 IP 地址收到 10,000 次请求时，向现有的 Amazon SNS 主题发送通知。 哪种解决方案能满足这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Configure CloudFront standard logging and CloudWatch Logs metric filters.","B":"Configure VPC Flow Logs and CloudWatch Logs metric filters.","C":"Configure an AWS WAF web ACL with an ASN match rule and CloudWatch alarms.","D":"Configure an AWS WAF web ACL with a rate-based rule. Associate it with CloudFront. Create a CloudWatch alarm to notify SNS."},"options_zh":{"A":"配置 CloudFront 标准日志和 CloudWatch Logs 指标过滤器。","B":"配置 VPC 流日志和 CloudWatch 日志指标过滤器。","C":"配置一个带有ASN匹配规则和CloudWatch告警的AWS WAF网络ACL。","D":"配置一个基于速率的 AWS WAF 网站访问控制列表（web ACL），并将其与 CloudFront 关联。创建一个 CloudWatch 警报以通知 SNS。"},"answer":["D"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Networking/DNS","Security/IAM","Compute","Serverless/Integration","Monitoring/Ops","Containers"],"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選","research":{"verdict":["D"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"both","explanation_en":"AWS WAF rate-based rules count incoming requests aggregated by end-user IP address (the default aggregation key) over an evaluation window, and 300 seconds (5 minutes) is a valid, default evaluation-window setting. The rate limit can be set to 10,000 (minimum is 10), so the rule precisely expresses '10,000 requests from the same IP within any 5-minute period.' Because the app sits behind CloudFront, you create a CloudFront-scope (global) web ACL and associate it with the distribution; AWS WAF publishes per-rule metrics to the AWS/WAFV2 CloudWatch namespace, so a CloudWatch alarm on that metric can notify the existing SNS topic. This is the only option that natively provides per-IP request counting over a sliding 5-minute window with a threshold and an alarm path to SNS.","explanation_zh":"AWS WAF 的 rate-based rule（速率型規則）會依 end-user IP address（預設彙總鍵）在一段評估視窗內累計請求數，而 300 秒（5 分鐘）正是有效且預設的評估視窗設定。速率上限可設為 10,000（最小為 10），因此該規則精確對應「同一 IP 在任意 5 分鐘內達 10,000 次請求」的需求。由於應用位於 CloudFront 之後，需建立 CloudFront 範圍（全域）的 web ACL 並關聯到該 distribution；AWS WAF 會將各規則的指標發佈到 AWS/WAFV2 CloudWatch namespace，於是可用 CloudWatch alarm 監控該指標並通知既有的 SNS topic。這是唯一能原生提供「以 IP 為單位、滑動 5 分鐘視窗計數 + 門檻 + 觸發 SNS 告警」的選項。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"CloudFront standard (access) logs plus CloudWatch Logs metric filters cannot aggregate requests per distinct source IP and alarm at a 10,000-per-IP threshold across a rolling 5-minute window. Metric filters match log patterns; they have no per-IP counting or dynamic top-talker logic.","why_zh":"CloudFront 標準（存取）日誌加上 CloudWatch Logs metric filter 無法針對「各別來源 IP」累計並在滑動 5 分鐘視窗達到每 IP 10,000 次時告警。Metric filter 只是比對日誌樣式，沒有依 IP 計數或動態辨識高流量 IP 的能力。"},{"letter":"B","why_en":"VPC Flow Logs record network-flow metadata (5-tuple, bytes/packets), not HTTP request counts. Behind CloudFront and an ALB, the source IP seen at the VPC is CloudFront's, not the true end-user IP, so per-end-user-IP HTTP request counting is impossible.","why_zh":"VPC Flow Logs 記錄的是網路流量中繼資料（5-tuple、位元組/封包數），並非 HTTP 請求數。位於 CloudFront 與 ALB 之後時，VPC 端看到的來源 IP 是 CloudFront 的位址，而非真正的 end-user IP，因此無法依實際使用者 IP 計算 HTTP 請求數。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"An ASN match rule filters by Autonomous System Number (an entire ISP/network), not by an individual end-user IP request rate. It cannot express 'the same IP address exceeding 10,000 requests in 5 minutes,' so it does not meet the requirement.","why_zh":"ASN match rule 是依 Autonomous System Number（整個 ISP／網路）過濾，而非依單一 end-user IP 的請求速率。它無法表達「同一 IP 在 5 分鐘內超過 10,000 次請求」，故不符合需求。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/waf/latest/developerguide/waf-rule-statement-type-rate-based-high-level-settings.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/waf/latest/developerguide/waf-rule-statement-type-rate-based-aggregation-options.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/waf/latest/developerguide/waf-metrics.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/waf/latest/developerguide/how-aws-waf-works.html"]}},{"id":135,"question_en":"A company runs several applications on Amazon Elastic Kubernetes Service (Amazon EKS). The company needs a solution to detect any Kubernetes security risks by monitoring Amazon EKS audit logs in addition to operating system, networking, and file events. The solution must send email alerts for any identified risks to a mailing list that is associated with a security team. Which solution will meet these requirements?","question_zh":"一家公司在 Amazon 弹性 Kubernetes 服务（Amazon EKS）上运行多个应用程序。该公司需要一种解决方案，通过监控 Amazon EKS 审计日志以及操作系统、网络和文件事件来检测任何 Kubernetes 安全风险。该解决方案必须将识别出的风险以电 子邮件形式发送给与安全团队关联的邮件列表。 哪种解决方案能满足这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Deploy AWS Security Hub and enable security standards that contain EKS controls. Create an Amazon Simple Notification Service (Amazon SNS) topic and set the security team ' s mailing list as a subscriber. Use an Amazon EventBridge rule to send relevant Security Hub events to the SNS topic.","B":"Enable Amazon Inspector container image scanning. Configure Amazon Detective to analyze EKS security logs. Create Amazon CloudWatch log groups for EKS audit logs. Use an AWS Lambda function to process the logs and to send email alerts to the security team.","C":"Enable Amazon GuardDuty. Enable EKS Protection and Runtime Monitoring for Amazon EKS in GuardDuty. Create an Amazon Simple Notification Service (Amazon SNS) topic and set the security team ' s mailing list as a subscriber. Use an Amazon EventBridge rule to send relevant GuardDuty events to the SNS topic.","D":"Install the AWS Systems Manager Agent (SSM Agent) on all EKS nodes. Configure Amazon CloudWatch Logs to collect EKS audit logs. Create an Amazon Simple Notification Service (Amazon SNS) topic and set the security team ' s mailing list as a subscriber. Configure a CloudWatch alarm to publish a message to the SNS topic when new audit logs are generated."},"options_zh":{"A":"部署 AWS Security Hub 并启用包含 EKS 控制项的安全标准。创建一个 Amazon 简单通知服务（Amazon SNS）主题，并 将安全团队的邮件列表设置为订阅者。使用 Amazon EventBridge 规则将相关的 Security Hub 事件发送到该 SNS 主题。","B":"启用 Amazon Inspector 对容器镜像进行扫描。配置 Amazon Detective 以分析 EKS 安全日志。为 EKS 审计日志创建 Amazon CloudWatch 日志组。使用 AWS Lambda 函数处理日志，并向安全团队发送电子邮件告警。","C":"启用 Amazon GuardDuty。在 GuardDuty 中启用 Amazon EKS 的保护和运行时监控功能。创建一个 Amazon 简单通知服 务（Amazon SNS）主题，并将安全团队的邮件列表设置为订阅者。使用 Amazon EventBridge 规则将相关的 GuardDuty 事件发送到该 SNS 主题。","D":"在所有 EKS 节点上安装 AWS Systems Manager Agent（SSM Agent）。配置 Amazon CloudWatch Logs 以收集 EKS 审计 日志。创建 Amazon 简单通知服务（Amazon SNS） 创建一个SNS主题，并将安全团队的邮件列表设置为订阅者。配置CloudWatch告警，以便在生成新的审计日志时向该 SNS主题发布消息。"},"answer":["C"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Security/IAM","Compute","Serverless/Integration","Monitoring/Ops","Containers"],"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選","research":{"verdict":["C"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"both","explanation_en":"The requirement has two distinct detection needs: (1) monitor Amazon EKS audit logs for Kubernetes security risks, and (2) monitor operating system, networking, and file events. Amazon GuardDuty covers both with two features. GuardDuty EKS Protection uses EKS audit logs to analyze the activities of users and applications and detect Kubernetes security risks (it uses its own independent stream of audit logs, no extra config needed). GuardDuty Runtime Monitoring (which includes EKS Runtime Monitoring via the aws-guardduty-agent EKS add-on) collects runtime events at the node/container level: Process events (operating system / process execution), DNS events (networking), and Open events (file access and modification). GuardDuty findings are automatically sent to EventBridge, so an EventBridge rule targeting an SNS topic with the security team's mailing list as an email subscriber delivers the alerts. This is exactly option C. The dump suggested answer C is correct.","explanation_zh":"此題有兩個偵測需求：(1) 監控 Amazon EKS audit logs 以偵測 Kubernetes 安全風險；(2) 監控作業系統、網路與檔案事件。Amazon GuardDuty 以兩項功能同時滿足。GuardDuty EKS Protection 使用 EKS audit logs 分析使用者與應用程式活動、偵測 Kubernetes 風險（GuardDuty 以自有獨立串流擷取 audit logs，無需額外設定）。GuardDuty Runtime Monitoring（透過 aws-guardduty-agent EKS add-on 涵蓋 EKS Runtime Monitoring）在節點／容器層級蒐集執行期事件：Process events（作業系統／程序執行）、DNS events（網路）、Open events（檔案存取與修改）。GuardDuty findings 會自動送到 EventBridge，因此以 EventBridge rule 將相關事件送到 SNS topic、並將安全團隊郵件群組設為 email 訂閱者，即可寄出告警。此即選項 C，dump 建議答案 C 正確。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"Security Hub EKS/GuardDuty controls perform posture/configuration checks (CSPM) against best practices; they do not monitor node-level operating system, networking, and file events. Security Hub is a findings aggregator, not a runtime threat detector, so it cannot satisfy the OS/network/file requirement.","why_zh":"Security Hub 的 EKS/GuardDuty controls 做的是組態／態勢檢查（CSPM），不會監控節點層級的作業系統、網路與檔案事件。Security Hub 是 findings 聚合器而非執行期威脅偵測器，無法滿足 OS/網路/檔案需求。"},{"letter":"B","why_en":"Inspector container image scanning finds vulnerabilities/CVEs in images, not runtime Kubernetes risks. Detective is for investigation, not primary detection, and does not 'analyze EKS security logs' as its detection engine. The Lambda-parses-logs-and-emails design is high operational overhead and still lacks OS/network/file runtime event coverage.","why_zh":"Inspector 容器映像掃描找的是映像中的漏洞/CVE，而非執行期 Kubernetes 風險。Detective 用於調查而非主要偵測，且不會作為偵測引擎去『分析 EKS security logs』。Lambda 解析 log 再寄信的設計運維負擔高，仍缺乏 OS/網路/檔案執行期事件覆蓋。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"This only ships EKS audit logs to CloudWatch Logs and fires an alarm when new logs arrive — it does no security analysis and does not detect Kubernetes risks or OS/network/file events. An alarm on 'new audit logs generated' would alert on all normal activity, not identified risks.","why_zh":"此方案只是把 EKS audit logs 送到 CloudWatch Logs，並在有新 log 時觸發 alarm——完全沒有安全分析，無法偵測 Kubernetes 風險或 OS/網路/檔案事件。以『產生新 audit log』為條件的 alarm 會對所有正常活動發告警，而非已識別的風險。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/guardduty/latest/ug/kubernetes-protection.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/guardduty/latest/ug/runtime-monitoring.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/guardduty/latest/ug/runtime-monitoring-collected-events.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/guardduty/latest/ug/how-runtime-monitoring-works-eks.html"]}},{"id":136,"question_en":"A company is using AWS to run a long-running analysis process on data that is stored in Amazon S3 buckets. The process runs on a fleet of Amazon EC2 instances in an Auto Scaling group. The EC2 instances are deployed in a private subnet that does not have internet access. The EC2 instances access Amazon S3 through an S3 gateway endpoint that has the default access policy. Each EC2 instance uses an instance profile role that allows s3:GetObject and s3:PutObject only for required S3 buckets. The company learns that one or more EC2 instances are compromised and are exfiltrating data to an S3 bucket that isoutside the company’s AWS Organization. The processing job must continue to function. Which solution will meet these requirements?","question_zh":"一家公司正在使用 AWS 在 Amazon S3 存储桶中存储的数据上运行一个长期分析流程。该流程在 Auto Scaling 组中的多个 Amazon EC2 实例上运行，这些 EC2 实例部署在没有互联网访问权限的私有子网中。 EC2 实例通过具有默认访问策略的 S3 网关端点访问 Amazon S3。每个 EC2 实例使用实例配置文件角色，该角色仅允许对所需 的 S3 存储桶执行 s3:GetObject 和 s3:PutObject 操作。 公司发现一个或多个EC2实例已被入侵，并正在将数据外泄至公司AWS组织之外的S3存储桶。处理任务必须继续正常运行。 哪种解决方案能满足这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Update the policy on the S3 gateway endpoint to allow S3 actions only if aws:ResourceOrgId and aws: PrincipalOrgId match the company’s organization.","B":"Update the instance profile role policy to require aws:ResourceOrgId.","C":"Add a network ACL rule to block outbound traffic on port 443.","D":"Apply an SCP that restricts S3 actions using organization condition keys."},"options_zh":{"A":"更新 S3 网关端点的策略，仅当 aws:ResourceOrgId 和 aws:PrincipalOrgId 与公司组织匹配时，才允许执行 S3 操作。","B":"更新实例配置文件角色策略，要求包含 aws:ResourceOrgId。","C":"添加一条网络ACL规则，以阻止443端口的出站流量。","D":"应用一个使用组织条件键来限制 S3 操作的 SCP。"},"answer":["A"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Organizations/Governance","Storage","Compute"],"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選","research":{"verdict":["A"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"Because the EC2 instances are in a private subnet with no internet access, the S3 gateway endpoint is the ONLY path to Amazon S3, so its endpoint policy is the always-on network chokepoint for every S3 request. This is the AWS-documented resource-perimeter control: 'Only trusted resources can be accessed from your network' is enforced with a VPC endpoint policy using aws:ResourceOrgId. Setting the endpoint policy to allow S3 only when aws:ResourceOrgId matches the company organization means the exfiltration bucket (which lives outside the organization, so its owning account has a different ResourceOrgId) is denied at the endpoint, while the company's own buckets remain reachable. Adding aws:PrincipalOrgId (the calling instance-profile role belongs to the company org) still evaluates true for legitimate traffic, so the processing job continues to function. This exactly matches the AWS 'Preventing data exfiltration in a private VPC' guidance, which uses a restrictive S3 VPC endpoint policy as the mechanism.","explanation_zh":"由於 EC2 執行個體位於沒有網際網路存取的私有子網路，S3 gateway endpoint 是通往 Amazon S3 的唯一路徑，因此該 endpoint policy 就是每一個 S3 請求都必經、always-on 的網路收斂點。這正是 AWS 文件所述的 resource perimeter 控制：『只有受信任的資源能從你的網路被存取』是透過 VPC endpoint policy 搭配 aws:ResourceOrgId 來強制執行。將 endpoint policy 設為只有當 aws:ResourceOrgId 等於公司組織時才允許 S3，代表外洩目標 bucket（位於組織之外、擁有帳號的 ResourceOrgId 不同）會在 endpoint 被拒絕，而公司自有 buckets 仍可存取。再加上 aws:PrincipalOrgId（呼叫端的 instance profile role 屬於本公司組織）對合法流量仍為 true，因此處理作業可持續運作。此做法完全符合 AWS『Preventing data exfiltration in a private VPC』指引，該指引正是以限制性的 S3 VPC endpoint policy 作為機制。","distractors":[{"letter":"B","why_en":"The instance-profile role already scopes GetObject/PutObject to the specific required (in-org) buckets, so adding aws:ResourceOrgId to the role adds no new protection against the described exfiltration; the identity-policy layer is not the effective chokepoint here. The always-on network control is the VPC endpoint policy, not per-instance IAM edits.","why_zh":"instance profile role 早已把 GetObject/PutObject 限縮到特定（組織內）必要 buckets，因此在 role 上再加 aws:ResourceOrgId 對所述外洩並無新增防護；identity policy 這一層並非有效收斂點。always-on 的網路控制是 VPC endpoint policy，而非逐台修改 IAM。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"S3 gateway endpoint traffic stays on the AWS private network via route tables and is not governed by a blanket outbound port-443 NACL rule; moreover S3 uses HTTPS/443, so blocking outbound 443 would break the legitimate processing job (violating 'must continue to function') and cannot distinguish in-org from out-of-org buckets.","why_zh":"S3 gateway endpoint 流量經路由表走 AWS 私有網路，並不受一條泛用的出向 443 NACL 規則管轄；且 S3 使用 HTTPS/443，封鎖出向 443 會中斷合法處理作業（違反『必須持續運作』），也無法區分組織內外的 buckets。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"An SCP with organization condition keys is a valid resource-perimeter approach, but it is a broad account-wide guardrail affecting all identities and is not tailored to the described architecture. The question centers on the single S3 path (the gateway endpoint with its default policy), for which the VPC endpoint policy is the precise, network-level, always-on control that blocks exfiltration while leaving legitimate access intact.","why_zh":"帶組織 condition keys 的 SCP 是有效的 resource perimeter 做法，但它是影響整個帳號所有身分的粗粒度護欄，並未針對所述架構量身打造。題目聚焦於唯一的 S3 路徑（帶預設政策的 gateway endpoint），對此 VPC endpoint policy 才是精準、網路層、always-on 的控制，能封鎖外洩同時保留合法存取。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/res/latest/ug/S3-buckets-preventing-exfiltration.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/IAM/latest/UserGuide/access_policies_data-perimeters.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/awsconsolehelpdocs/latest/gsg/trusted-resources.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonS3/latest/userguide/example-policies-s3.html"]}},{"id":137,"question_en":"CloudFormation stack deployments fail for some users due to permission inconsistencies.Which combination of steps will ensure consistent deployments MOST securely? (Select THREE.)","question_zh":"由于权限不一致，部分用户的 CloudFormation 堆栈部署失败。 以下哪三个步骤的组合能最安全地确保部署的一致性？（选择三项。）","options_en":{"A":"Create a composite principal service role.","B":"Create a service role with cloudformation.amazonaws.com as the principal.","C":"Attach scoped policies to the service role.","D":"Attach service ARNs in policy resources.","E":"Update each stack to use the service role.","F":"Allow iam:PassRole to the service role."},"options_zh":{"A":"创建一个组合主服务角色。","B":"创建一个服务角色，将 cloudformation.amazonaws.com 作为主体。","C":"将作用域策略附加到服务角色。","D":"在策略资源中附加服务 ARN。","E":"更新每个堆栈以使用服务角色。","F":"允许服务角色使用 iam:PassRole。"},"answer":["B","E","F"],"multi":true,"vote":{},"tags":["Security/IAM","Monitoring/Ops"],"difficulty":2,"diff_why":"複選","research":{"verdict":["B","E","F"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"CORRECTED to B, E, F (confirming the dump/community answer). AWS's CloudFormation service-role documentation lays out the workflow in three concrete steps that map directly to B, E, and F. First, you create the IAM role and its trust policy specifies cloudformation.amazonaws.com as the trusted principal so CloudFormation itself can assume the role (B) -- this is the foundational step that lets CloudFormation, rather than each individual user's own credentials, perform the stack operations. Second, you associate that service role with each stack: 'To associate a service role with a stack, specify the role when you create the stack, or you can also change the service role when you update the stack' -- once attached, 'CloudFormation always uses that role for all operations that are performed on that stack,' which is exactly the mechanism that eliminates per-user permission inconsistencies (E), since every user who operates on that stack now deploys under the same fixed role regardless of their own IAM permissions. Third, the same doc explicitly gates the ability to specify a service role behind a permission: 'Before you specify a service role, ensure that you have permission to pass it (iam:PassRole).' The IAM PassRole documentation confirms this is a real, required, and security-relevant control: 'To pass a role to an AWS service, a user must have permissions to pass the role to the service. This helps administrators ensure that only approved users can configure a service with a role that grants permissions' (F). This is precisely how the 'MOST securely' qualifier is satisfied here -- without iam:PassRole scoped to specific approved users, any user could attach an arbitrary, over-permissioned role to a stack. Attaching generic 'scoped least-privilege policies' (C) is good general security hygiene for any IAM role, but the CloudFormation documentation does not call it out as one of the specific enumerated steps for setting up and enforcing a service role for consistent deployments; the actual documented control that governs who may attach which role to a stack is PassRole, not the policy-scoping step in isolation. Option A (composite principal) is not needed since the trust policy only requires a single principal, cloudformation.amazonaws.com. Option D ('attach service ARNs in policy resources') is not a real CloudFormation service-role step; it garbles the least-privilege phrasing without matching any documented action.","explanation_zh":"更正為 B、E、F（確認社群/題庫答案）。AWS 的 CloudFormation service role 文件描述的流程正好對應 B、E、F 三個具體步驟。首先，建立 IAM role 並在其信任政策中指定 cloudformation.amazonaws.com 為受信任的 principal，讓 CloudFormation 本身可以扮演該角色（B）——這是讓 CloudFormation（而非每個使用者各自的憑證）執行 stack 操作的基礎步驟。第二，將該 service role 與每個 stack 關聯：文件指出「若要將 service role 與 stack 關聯，需在建立 stack 時指定該角色，也可以在更新 stack 時變更 service role」，一旦附加後「CloudFormation 會針對該 stack 的所有操作永遠使用該角色」，這正是消除各使用者權限不一致問題的機制（E），因為所有操作該 stack 的使用者，現在都會在同一個固定角色下部署，不受各自 IAM 權限影響。第三，同一份文件明確將「指定 service role」的能力綁定在一項權限之後：「在指定 service role 之前，請確保你有權限傳遞它（iam:PassRole）。」IAM PassRole 文件證實這是一項真實、必要且與安全性相關的控制：「若要將角色傳遞給 AWS 服務，使用者必須擁有將該角色傳遞給該服務的權限。這有助於管理員確保只有經核准的使用者才能以授予權限的角色來設定服務」（F）。這正是滿足「MOST securely」這一限定詞的關鍵——如果沒有將 iam:PassRole 限定給經核准的使用者，任何使用者都可能將任意、過度授權的角色附加到 stack 上。附加通用的「範圍化最小權限政策」（C）對任何 IAM 角色而言都是良好的一般安全做法，但 CloudFormation 文件並未將其列為設定並強制執行 service role 以達成一致部署的特定列舉步驟之一；真正記載於文件中、用來管控「誰可以將哪個角色附加到 stack」的控制機制是 PassRole，而不是單獨的政策範圍化步驟。選項 A（composite principal）並不需要，因為信任政策只需要單一 principal，即 cloudformation.amazonaws.com。選項 D（『在政策 Resource 中附加 service ARN』）並非真實的 CloudFormation service role 步驟，只是含糊地套用最小權限用語，並不對應任何文件記載的動作。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"A 'composite principal' (multiple principals combined in one trust policy) is neither required nor documented as a best practice for a CloudFormation service role; the role's trust policy only needs a single principal, cloudformation.amazonaws.com, to allow CloudFormation to assume it.","why_zh":"『composite principal』（在單一信任政策中合併多個 principal）並非 CloudFormation service role 所需要或文件記載的最佳實務；該角色的信任政策只需要單一 principal，即 cloudformation.amazonaws.com，即可讓 CloudFormation 扮演該角色。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"Attaching scoped least-privilege policies to the role is generally good practice, but it is not one of the specific steps the CloudFormation service-role documentation enumerates for setting up and securing service-role-based deployments; the documented control that actually governs who can attach which role to a stack is iam:PassRole (F), not policy scoping in isolation.","why_zh":"為角色附加範圍化的最小權限政策整體上是良好做法，但這並非 CloudFormation service role 文件中列舉、用於建立並強化以 service role 為基礎部署安全性的特定步驟之一；文件實際記載、真正管控『誰可以將哪個角色附加到 stack』的控制機制是 iam:PassRole（F），而非單獨的政策範圍化。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"'Attach service ARNs in policy resources' does not correspond to any documented CloudFormation service-role step; the actual least-privilege practice is scoping the policy's Resource element to the specific resource ARNs the stack manages, which this option garbles into non-standard phrasing.","why_zh":"『在政策 Resource 中附加 service ARN』並不對應任何文件記載的 CloudFormation service role 步驟；實際的最小權限做法是將政策的 Resource 元素範圍限定在該 stack 所管理的特定資源 ARN，而此選項將其誤植為不標準的說法。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AWSCloudFormation/latest/UserGuide/using-iam-servicerole.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/IAM/latest/UserGuide/id_roles_use_passrole.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/IAM/latest/UserGuide/id_roles_create_for-service.html"]}},{"id":138,"question_en":"A company uploads data files as objects into an Amazon S3 bucket. A vendor downloads the objects to perform data processing. A security engineer must implement a solution that prevents objects from residing in the S3 bucket for longer than 72 hours.","question_zh":"一家公司将数据文件作为对象上传到 Amazon S3 存储桶中，供应商则下载这些对象以进行数据处理。 安全工程师必须实施一项解决方案，以防止对象在S3存储桶中保留超过72小时。","options_en":{"A":"Configure S3 Versioning to expire object versions that have been in the bucket for 72 hours.","B":"Configure an S3 Lifecycle configuration rule on the bucket to expire objects after 72 hours.","C":"Use the S3 Intelligent-Tiering storage class and configure expiration after 72 hours.","D":"Generate presigned URLs that expire after 72 hours."},"options_zh":{"A":"配置 S3 版本控制，使在存储桶中保留超过 72 小时的对象版本自动过期。","B":"在存储桶上配置 S3 生命周期规则，使对象在 72 小时后过期。","C":"使用 S3 智能分层存储类别，并设置 72 小时后过期。","D":"生成在72小时后过期的预签名URL。"},"answer":["B"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Storage"],"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選","research":{"verdict":["B"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"The requirement is that objects must not RESIDE in the bucket for longer than 72 hours, which means the objects themselves must be deleted. An S3 Lifecycle configuration rule with an Expiration action deletes objects based on their age (72 hours = 3 days). Per AWS docs, the Expiration action tells Amazon S3 to delete objects at the end of their lifetime, and for a nonversioned bucket it permanently removes the object. This is the only option that actually removes objects from the bucket automatically on a schedule.","explanation_zh":"需求是物件不得在儲存貯體中停留超過 72 小時，也就是物件本身必須被刪除。S3 Lifecycle configuration 規則搭配 Expiration 動作會根據物件存在天數（72 小時＝3 天）自動刪除物件。根據 AWS 文件，Expiration 動作會告訴 Amazon S3 在物件生命週期結束時刪除該物件；對於未啟用版本控制的貯體，會永久移除物件。這是唯一能真正依排程自動從貯體移除物件的選項。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"S3 Versioning by itself does not delete objects; it retains multiple versions. Expiring versions is a Lifecycle action (NoncurrentVersionExpiration), not a Versioning feature, and it only affects noncurrent versions, not the current object residing in the bucket.","why_zh":"S3 Versioning 本身不會刪除物件，而是保留多個版本。讓版本過期是 Lifecycle 動作（NoncurrentVersionExpiration），並非 Versioning 功能，且只影響非目前版本，無法移除貯體中的目前物件。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"S3 Intelligent-Tiering is a storage class that moves objects between access tiers to optimize cost; it never deletes or expires objects. Expiration requires a Lifecycle rule, not the storage class itself.","why_zh":"S3 Intelligent-Tiering 是一種儲存類別，用於在存取層之間移動物件以最佳化成本，永遠不會刪除或使物件過期。物件過期需要 Lifecycle 規則，而非儲存類別本身。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"Presigned URLs only limit how long a download link is valid for access; they expire the URL, not the object. The object still resides in the bucket indefinitely regardless of URL expiration, so this does not meet the 72-hour residence requirement.","why_zh":"預簽章 URL 僅限制下載連結的有效存取時間，過期的是 URL 而非物件。無論 URL 是否過期，物件仍會無限期停留在貯體中，因此無法滿足 72 小時停留限制的需求。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonS3/latest/userguide/lifecycle-expire-general-considerations.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonS3/latest/userguide/object-lifecycle-mgmt.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonS3/latest/userguide/using-presigned-url.html"]}},{"id":139,"question_en":"A company ' s security engineer receives an abuse notification from AWS indicating that malware is being hosted from the company’s AWS account. The security engineer discovers that an IAM user created a new Amazon S3 bucket without authorization. Which combination of steps should the security engineer take to MINIMIZE the consequences of this compromise? (Select THREE.)","question_zh":"一家公司的安全工程师收到 AWS 发来的滥用通知，提示有恶意软件正从该公司的 AWS 账户托管。 安全工程师发现，一名 IAM 用户未经授权创建了一个新的 Amazon S3 存储桶。 安全工程师应采取哪些步骤组合来最小化此次泄露事件的后果？（选择三项。）","options_en":{"A":"Encrypt all AWS CloudTrail logs.","B":"Turn on Amazon GuardDuty.","C":"Change the password for all IAM users.","D":"Rotate or delete all AWS access keys.","E":"Take snapshots of all Amazon Elastic Block Store (Amazon EBS) volumes.","F":"Delete any resources that are unrecognized or unauthorized."},"options_zh":{"A":"加密所有 AWS CloudTrail 日志。","B":"启用 Amazon GuardDuty。","C":"更改所有 IAM 用户的密码。","D":"旋转或删除所有 AWS 访问密钥。","E":"对所有 Amazon 弹性块存储（Amazon EBS）卷进行快照。","F":"删除任何无法识别或未经授权的资源。"},"answer":["B","D","F"],"multi":true,"vote":{},"tags":["Security/IAM","Storage","Monitoring/Ops"],"difficulty":3,"diff_why":"複選・官方文件判定需斟酌・題庫與社群皆錯","research":{"verdict":["C","D","F"],"confidence":"medium","agrees_with":"neither","explanation_en":"The qualifier is to MINIMIZE the consequences of THIS compromise, i.e. contain and remediate an active breach where IAM credentials were used to create an unauthorized S3 bucket hosting malware. AWS incident-response guidance (the 'My AWS account may be compromised' article referenced directly by the GuardDuty 'Remediating potentially compromised AWS credentials' doc) prescribes a consistent trio: rotate/delete the compromised access keys, change the IAM console passwords, and remove any unauthorized/unrecognized resources the attacker created. D (rotate or delete all access keys) revokes the programmatic AccessKey credentials the attacker is using. C (change the password for all IAM users) cuts off console access, which is required because the credentials themselves are compromised and you don't yet know which user is affected. F (delete unrecognized/unauthorized resources) removes the malicious S3 bucket and stops the malware hosting. B (turn on GuardDuty) is a DETECTIVE, forward-looking control that does nothing to undo or contain the compromise that already happened, so it does not minimize the consequences of this incident. The dump answer B/D/F is wrong on B for this reason.","explanation_zh":"題目限定詞是要「最小化這次入侵的後果」，也就是圍堵並修復一個已發生的入侵：IAM 憑證被用來建立未授權、託管惡意程式的 S3 儲存貯體。AWS 事件回應指引（GuardDuty『Remediating potentially compromised AWS credentials』文件直接引用的『My AWS account may be compromised』知識庫文章）給出一致的三步：輪替/刪除被洩漏的存取金鑰、變更 IAM 主控台密碼、刪除攻擊者建立的任何未授權/無法辨識資源。D（輪替或刪除所有 access key）撤銷攻擊者正在使用的 AccessKey 程式化憑證。C（變更所有 IAM 使用者密碼）切斷主控台存取，因為憑證本身已遭洩漏且尚不確定是哪個使用者受影響，必須全面撤銷。F（刪除無法辨識/未授權的資源）移除惡意 S3 儲存貯體，停止惡意程式託管。B（開啟 GuardDuty）屬於偵測型、面向未來的控制，無法回復或圍堵已發生的入侵，因此無法最小化這次事件的後果。dump 答案 B/D/F 在 B 上是錯的。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"Encrypting CloudTrail logs is a preventive/data-protection control. For this incident you would REVIEW CloudTrail to scope the activity, not encrypt it; encryption does nothing to contain or reverse the compromise.","why_zh":"加密 CloudTrail 日誌屬於預防/資料保護控制。此事件中你應該是「檢視」CloudTrail 以釐清活動範圍，而非加密它；加密無助於圍堵或回復入侵。"},{"letter":"B","why_en":"Turning on GuardDuty is a detective, forward-looking control. It helps detect FUTURE threats but does not revoke the attacker's existing access or remove damage from this already-occurred compromise, so it does not minimize the consequences.","why_zh":"開啟 GuardDuty 是偵測型、面向未來的控制。它有助偵測未來威脅，但無法撤銷攻擊者現有存取或移除此次已發生入侵造成的損害，因此無法最小化後果。"},{"letter":"E","why_en":"Taking EBS snapshots is a forensic-preservation action. There is no EBS in scope (the attack is an unauthorized S3 bucket), and snapshots preserve evidence rather than minimize the consequences of the compromise.","why_zh":"建立 EBS 快照屬於鑑識保存動作。此情境無 EBS 相關（攻擊是未授權 S3 儲存貯體），且快照是保存證據，並非最小化入侵後果。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/guardduty/latest/ug/compromised-creds.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/guardduty/latest/ug/compromised-s3.html","https://repost.aws/knowledge-center/potential-account-compromise","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/IAM/latest/UserGuide/id_credentials_access-keys.html"]}},{"id":140,"question_en":"A company uses AWS IAM Identity Center to manage access to its AWS accounts. The accounts are in an organization in AWS Organizations. A security engineer needs to set up delegated administration of IAM Identity Center in the organization’s management account. Which combination of steps should the security engineer perform in IAM Identity Center before configuring delegated administration? (Select THREE.)","question_zh":"一家公司使用 AWS IAM Identity Center 来管理其 AWS 账户的访问权限。这些账户位于 AWS Organizations 中的一个组织内。安全工程师需要在该组织的管理账户中设置 IAM Identity Center 的 委派管理。 在配置委派管理之前，安全工程师应在 IAM Identity Center 中执行哪些步骤组合？（选择三项。）","options_en":{"A":"Grant least privilege access to the organization ' s management account.","B":"Create a new IAM Identity Center directory in the organization ' s management account.","C":"Set up a second AWS Region in the organization’s management account.","D":"Create permission sets for use only in the organization ' s management account.","E":"Create IAM users for use only in the organization ' s management account.","F":"Create user assignments only in the organization ' s management account."},"options_zh":{"A":"为组织的管理账户授予最小权限访问。","B":"在组织的管理账户中创建一个新的 IAM 身份中心目录。","C":"设置一 个 组织管理账户中的第二个 AWS 区域。","D":"创建仅在组织的管理账户中使用的权限集。","E":"为仅在组织的管理账户中使用而创建 IAM 用户。","F":"仅在组织的管理账户中创建用户分配。"},"answer":["B","D","F"],"multi":true,"vote":{},"tags":["Organizations/Governance","Security/IAM"],"difficulty":3,"diff_why":"複選・題庫與社群皆錯","research":{"verdict":["A","D","F"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"neither","explanation_en":"The IAM Identity Center 'Delegated administration' page has a 'Best practices to consider before you configure delegated administration' section that lists exactly these recommendations. (1) Grant least privilege to the management account = Option A: because the management account is highly privileged, restrict access to as few people as possible. (2) Use dedicated permission sets for the management account = Option D: a permission set used for the management account can only be modified from the management account and the delegated admin cannot alter it. (3) Assign users only (not groups) to permission sets in the management account = Option F: assigning groups would let any group/IdP admin change who has management-account access, so assign users directly. B is wrong because the IAM Identity Center instance/directory already resides in the management account by default; you do not create a new directory as a delegated-admin prerequisite. C is wrong because there is no second-Region requirement. E is wrong because IAM Identity Center uses identity store users and permission sets, not IAM users. The dump answer [B,D,F] wrongly swaps A for B.","explanation_zh":"IAM Identity Center 的「Delegated administration」文件中「Best practices to consider before you configure delegated administration」一節，正好列出這三項建議：(1) 對 management account 採最小權限（選項 A）——management account 權限極高，應盡量限縮可存取人數；(2) 為 management account 使用專屬 permission sets（選項 D）——用於 management account 的 permission set 只能由 management account 內修改，delegated administrator 無法變更；(3) 在 management account 中只指派使用者（而非群組）到 permission sets（選項 F）——若指派群組，任何群組或 IdP 管理員都可改變誰能存取 management account，故應直接指派使用者。B 錯：IAM Identity Center 執行個體/目錄預設就在 management account，delegated administration 前不需要新建 directory。C 錯：無第二個 Region 的需求。E 錯：IAM Identity Center 使用 identity store 使用者與 permission sets，而非 IAM users。Dump 答案 [B,D,F] 錯在把 A 換成 B。","distractors":[{"letter":"B","why_en":"The IAM Identity Center instance (and its identity store/directory) already resides in the management account by default; creating a new directory there is not a delegated-administration prerequisite.","why_zh":"IAM Identity Center 執行個體（含 identity store/目錄）預設就已存在於 management account；delegated administration 前並不需要新建 directory。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"Delegated administration has no multi-Region requirement; IAM Identity Center operates in a single Region and a second Region is irrelevant to enabling delegation.","why_zh":"Delegated administration 沒有多 Region 需求；IAM Identity Center 在單一 Region 運作，第二個 Region 與啟用委派無關。"},{"letter":"E","why_en":"IAM Identity Center assigns identity store users to permission sets, not IAM users; creating IAM users is not part of the delegated-administration best practices.","why_zh":"IAM Identity Center 是把 identity store 使用者指派到 permission sets，而非 IAM users；建立 IAM users 不屬於 delegated administration 的最佳實務。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/singlesignon/latest/userguide/delegated-admin.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/singlesignon/latest/userguide/delegated-admin-how-to-register.html"]}},{"id":141,"question_en":"Notify when IAM roles are modified.","question_zh":"当 IAM 角色被修改时发出通知。","options_en":{"A":"Use Amazon Detective.","B":"Use EventBridge with CloudTrail events.","C":"Use CloudWatch metric filters.","D":"Use CloudWatch subscription filters."},"options_zh":{"A":"使用 Amazon Detective。","B":"使用 EventBridge 处理 CloudTrail 事件。","C":"使用 CloudWatch 指标过滤器。","D":"使用 CloudWatch 订阅筛选器。"},"answer":["B"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Security/IAM","Serverless/Integration","Monitoring/Ops"],"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選","research":{"verdict":["B"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"IAM management operations that modify roles (for example AttachRolePolicy, DetachRolePolicy, PutRolePolicy, DeleteRolePolicy, UpdateRole, UpdateAssumeRolePolicy, TagRole) are recorded by AWS CloudTrail, and CloudTrail delivers these as 'AWS API Call via CloudTrail' events (source aws.iam) to the Amazon EventBridge default event bus. You create an EventBridge rule with an event pattern matching those IAM API calls and set an Amazon SNS topic as the target, giving direct, real-time notification whenever a role is modified. This is the canonical, event-driven AWS pattern for 'notify when a specific API action happens.' Amazon Detective (A) is an investigation/root-cause tool for security findings, not a notification service. CloudWatch metric filters (C) can technically alert on IAM activity, but that requires the indirect CloudTrail to CloudWatch Logs to metric filter to alarm to SNS chain, adds latency, and the AWS-documented metric-filter example targets IAM policy changes rather than being the direct path for role modifications. CloudWatch subscription filters (D) only stream log data to a destination such as Lambda, Kinesis, or Firehose for processing and are not a notification mechanism.","explanation_zh":"修改 IAM role 的管理操作（例如 AttachRolePolicy、DetachRolePolicy、PutRolePolicy、DeleteRolePolicy、UpdateRole、UpdateAssumeRolePolicy、TagRole）都會被 AWS CloudTrail 記錄，且 CloudTrail 會把它們以「AWS API Call via CloudTrail」事件（source 為 aws.iam）送到 Amazon EventBridge 的 default event bus。你只要建立一條 EventBridge rule，用 event pattern 比對這些 IAM API 呼叫，並把 Amazon SNS topic 設為 target，就能在 role 被修改時取得直接、即時的通知，這正是 AWS 針對「當特定 API 動作發生時通知」的標準事件驅動作法。Amazon Detective（A）是安全發現的調查／根因分析工具，不是通知服務。CloudWatch metric filters（C）技術上可對 IAM 活動發出告警，但需要 CloudTrail 到 CloudWatch Logs 到 metric filter 到 alarm 到 SNS 的間接鏈路，延遲較高，且 AWS 文件的 metric-filter 範例針對的是 IAM policy 變更，而非 role 修改的直接路徑。CloudWatch subscription filters（D）只是把 log 串流到 Lambda、Kinesis 或 Firehose 等目的地做處理，並非通知機制。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"Amazon Detective is for security investigation and root-cause analysis of findings (visualizing GuardDuty/CloudTrail/VPC data); it does not emit notifications when IAM roles are modified.","why_zh":"Amazon Detective 用於安全事件的調查與根因分析（視覺化 GuardDuty/CloudTrail/VPC 資料），不會在 IAM role 被修改時發出通知。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"CloudWatch metric filters can alert on CloudTrail activity but only via the indirect CloudTrail to Logs to metric filter to alarm to SNS chain with added latency; the documented example targets IAM policy changes, so it is not the direct notification path for role modifications.","why_zh":"CloudWatch metric filters 可對 CloudTrail 活動告警，但需經 CloudTrail 到 Logs 到 metric filter 到 alarm 到 SNS 的間接鏈路且延遲較高；官方範例針對 IAM policy 變更，並非 role 修改的直接通知路徑。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"CloudWatch subscription filters only stream log events to destinations like Lambda, Kinesis, or Firehose for processing; they are a log-delivery pipe, not a notification service.","why_zh":"CloudWatch subscription filters 只是把 log 事件串流到 Lambda、Kinesis 或 Firehose 等目的地處理，是 log 傳輸管道，不是通知服務。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/eventbridge/latest/userguide/eb-service-event-cloudtrail.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/eventbridge/latest/userguide/eb-service-event-cloudtrail-management.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/awscloudtrail/latest/userguide/cloudwatch-alarms-for-cloudtrail.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/IAM/latest/UserGuide/cloudtrail-integration.html"]}},{"id":142,"question_en":"A company needs the ability to identify the root cause of security findings in an AWS account. The company has enabled VPC Flow Logs, Amazon GuardDuty, and AWS CloudTrail. The company must investigate any IAM roles that are involved in the security findings and must visualize the findings. Which solution will meet these requirements?","question_zh":"一家公司需要具备识别AWS账户中安全问题根本原因的能力。该公司已启用VPC流量日志、Amazon GuardDuty和AWS CloudTrail。 公司必须调查与安全发现相关的所有IAM角色，并对这些发现进行可视化分析。 哪种解决方案能满足这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Use Amazon Detective to run investigations on the IAM roles and to visualize the findings.","B":"Use Amazon Inspector to run investigations on the IAM roles and visualize the findings.","C":"Export GuardDuty findings to Amazon S3 and analyze them with Amazon Athena.","D":"Enable AWS Security Hub and use custom actions to investigate IAM roles."},"options_zh":{"A":"使用 Amazon Detective 对 IAM 角色进行调查并可视化分析结果。","B":"使用 Amazon Inspector 对 IAM 角色进行调查并可视化分析结果。","C":"将 GuardDuty 的检测结果导出到 Amazon S3，并使用 Amazon Athena 进行分析。","D":"启用 AWS Security Hub 并使用自定义操作来调查 IAM 角色。"},"answer":["A"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Security/IAM","Storage","Monitoring/Ops","Analytics"],"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選","research":{"verdict":["A"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"Amazon Detective is purpose-built to analyze, investigate, and identify the root cause of security findings. It automatically ingests exactly the three data sources the company enabled — VPC Flow Logs, Amazon GuardDuty findings, and AWS CloudTrail — into a behavior graph. The Detective Investigation feature specifically investigates IAM users and IAM roles using indicators of compromise to determine whether a resource is involved in a security incident, and Detective uses graph theory and machine learning to generate interactive visualizations (including finding groups) of the findings. This maps one-to-one to every requirement: root-cause analysis, investigation of IAM roles, and visualization of findings.","explanation_zh":"Amazon Detective 專門用來分析、調查並找出安全發現（findings）的根本原因。它會自動將公司已啟用的三種資料來源——VPC Flow Logs、Amazon GuardDuty findings 與 AWS CloudTrail——匯入其 behavior graph。Detective Investigation 功能可針對 IAM users 與 IAM roles，依據入侵指標（indicators of compromise）進行調查，判斷資源是否牽涉於安全事件，並運用圖論與機器學習產生互動式視覺化（含 finding groups）。這與題目每一項需求（找出根本原因、調查 IAM roles、視覺化 findings）完全對應。","distractors":[{"letter":"B","why_en":"Amazon Inspector is a vulnerability management service that scans EC2, Lambda, and container images for CVEs and unintended network exposure. It does not investigate IAM roles involved in security findings and does not consume VPC Flow Logs/GuardDuty/CloudTrail for root-cause investigation or visualization.","why_zh":"Amazon Inspector 是漏洞管理服務，掃描 EC2、Lambda 與容器映像的 CVE 與網路暴露。它不會調查牽涉於安全發現的 IAM roles，也不會使用 VPC Flow Logs/GuardDuty/CloudTrail 進行根本原因調查或視覺化。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"Exporting GuardDuty findings to S3 and querying with Athena lets you analyze finding records, but it does not correlate cross-source activity to determine root cause, does not investigate IAM role behavior across CloudTrail/VPC Flow Logs, and provides no built-in visualization. It is a manual, high-effort approach that misses the investigation and visualization requirements.","why_zh":"將 GuardDuty findings 匯出到 S3 並用 Athena 查詢可分析發現記錄，但無法跨來源關聯以判定根本原因，也無法調查 IAM role 在 CloudTrail/VPC Flow Logs 中的行為，且沒有內建視覺化。這是手動、高工作量的做法，未滿足調查與視覺化需求。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"AWS Security Hub aggregates and prioritizes findings; its custom actions merely send selected findings to EventBridge targets for automation. Security Hub itself does not investigate the IAM roles' behavior across data sources or visualize the root cause — that investigative pivot is precisely what Amazon Detective provides.","why_zh":"AWS Security Hub 匯總並排序 findings；其 custom actions 只是把選定的 findings 送到 EventBridge 目標以觸發自動化。Security Hub 本身不會跨資料來源調查 IAM roles 的行為或視覺化根本原因——這正是 Amazon Detective 提供的調查樞紐功能。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/detective/latest/userguide/what-is-detective.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/detective/latest/userguide/investigations-about.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/detective/latest/userguide/detective-source-data-about.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/detective/latest/userguide/detective-investigation-about.html"]}},{"id":143,"question_en":"A company has enabled AWS Config for its organization in AWS Organizations. The company has deployed hundreds of Amazon S3 buckets across the organization. A security engineer needs to identify any S3 buckets that are not encrypted with AWS Key Management Service (AWS KMS). The security engineer also must prevent objects that are not encrypted with AWS KMS from being uploaded to the S3 buckets. Which solution will meet these requirements?","question_zh":"一家公司已在 AWS Organizations 中为其组织启用了 AWS Config。该公司在组织内部署了数百个 Amazon S3 存储桶。安全工程师需要 识别所有未使用 AWS Key Management Service（AWS KMS）加密的 S3 存储桶，同时还必须阻止未使用 AWS KMS 加密的对象上传 至这些 S3 存储桶。 哪种解决方案能满足这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Use thes3-default-encryption-kmsAWS Config managed rule to identify unencrypted S3 buckets. Create an SCP to allow thes3:PutObjectaction only when the object is encrypted with AWS KMS.","B":"Use thes3-default-encryption-kmsAWS Config managed rule to identify unencrypted S3 buckets. Create bucket policies for each S3 bucket to deny thes3:PutObjectaction only when the object has server-side encryption with S3 managed keys (SSE-S3).","C":"Use thes3-bucket-ssl-requests-onlyAWS Config managed rule to identify unencrypted S3 buckets. Create an SCP to allow thes3:PutObjectaction only when the object is encrypted with AWS KMS.","D":"Use thes3-bucket-ssl-requests-onlyAWS Config managed rule to identify unencrypted S3 buckets. Create bucket policies for each S3 bucket to allow thes3:PutObjectaction only when the object is encrypted with AWS KMS."},"options_zh":{"A":"使用 AWS Config 管理规则 thes3-default-encryption-kms 来识别未加密的 S3 存储桶。创建一个 SCP，仅允许在对象使用 AWS KMS 加密时执行 s3:PutObject 操作。","B":"使用 AWS Config 管理规则 thes3-default-encryption-kms 来识别未加密的 S3 存储桶。为每个 S3 存储桶创建存储桶策略， 仅当对象使用 S3 管理密钥（SSE-S3）进行服务器端加密时，拒绝 s3:PutObject 操作。","C":"使用 AWS Config 管理规则 thes3-bucket-ssl-requests-only 来识别未加密的 S3 存储桶。创建一个 SCP，仅允许在对象使用 AWS KMS 加密时执行 s3:PutObject 操作。","D":"使用 AWS Config 管理规则 thes3-bucket-ssl-requests-only 来识别未加密的 S3 存储桶。为每个 S3 存储桶创建存储桶策略， 仅允许在对象使用 AWS KMS 加密时执行 s3:PutObject 操作。"},"answer":["A"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Organizations/Governance","Security/IAM","Storage"],"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選","research":{"verdict":["A"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"The requirement has two parts: (1) identify S3 buckets not encrypted with AWS KMS, and (2) prevent uploads of objects not encrypted with KMS. For part 1, the s3-default-encryption-kms (S3_DEFAULT_ENCRYPTION_KMS) managed rule 'checks if the S3 buckets are encrypted with AWS KMS' and is NON_COMPLIANT if a bucket is not encrypted with a KMS key -- exactly what is needed. The s3-bucket-ssl-requests-only rule only checks whether bucket policies require SSL/TLS for requests (in-transit), which has nothing to do with KMS at-rest encryption, so options C and D are eliminated on part 1. For part 2, the company enabled Config for its whole organization and has hundreds of buckets across the organization, so an SCP that permits s3:PutObject only when the object is encrypted with AWS KMS enforces the control org-wide across all accounts and buckets in one place (AWS documents this org-level pattern, e.g. the managed SCP that restricts unencrypted S3 uploads). Option B is wrong because denying PutObject only when the object uses SSE-S3 does not block uploads that have no encryption header or use SSE-C, so it fails to require KMS and does not fully prevent non-KMS uploads, while also requiring edits to hundreds of individual bucket policies. Option A is the only choice that both correctly identifies non-KMS buckets and fully prevents non-KMS uploads at organization scale.","explanation_zh":"需求有兩部分：(1) 找出未以 AWS KMS 加密的 S3 儲存貯體；(2) 阻擋未以 KMS 加密的物件上傳。第一部分中，s3-default-encryption-kms（S3_DEFAULT_ENCRYPTION_KMS）受管規則的定義正是「檢查 S3 儲存貯體是否以 AWS KMS 加密」，若未以 KMS 金鑰加密即為 NON_COMPLIANT，完全符合需求。s3-bucket-ssl-requests-only 只檢查儲存貯體政策是否要求以 SSL/TLS（傳輸中）發出請求，與 KMS 靜態加密無關，因此選項 C、D 在第一部分即被排除。第二部分中，該公司在 AWS Organizations 為整個組織啟用 Config，且組織內有數百個貯體，因此以 SCP 僅允許在物件以 AWS KMS 加密時執行 s3:PutObject，可在單一位置對所有帳戶與貯體套用此管控（AWS 有此組織層級模式的文件，例如限制未加密 S3 上傳的受管 SCP）。選項 B 錯誤：僅在物件使用 SSE-S3 時拒絕 PutObject，並不會阻擋沒有加密標頭或使用 SSE-C 的上傳，無法強制 KMS，也未能完整阻擋非 KMS 上傳，且須逐一修改數百個貯體政策。選項 A 是唯一能同時正確辨識非 KMS 貯體並在組織規模下完整阻擋非 KMS 上傳的選項。","distractors":[{"letter":"B","why_en":"Denying PutObject only when the object uses SSE-S3 does not block uploads with no encryption header or SSE-C, so it does not require KMS or fully prevent non-KMS uploads; it also demands editing hundreds of individual bucket policies.","why_zh":"僅在物件使用 SSE-S3 時拒絕 PutObject，並未阻擋無加密標頭或 SSE-C 的上傳，無法強制 KMS 或完整阻擋非 KMS 上傳；且須逐一修改數百個貯體政策。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"s3-bucket-ssl-requests-only only checks whether bucket policies enforce SSL/TLS for requests (in-transit encryption), not whether buckets are KMS-encrypted at rest, so it cannot identify buckets that are not KMS-encrypted.","why_zh":"s3-bucket-ssl-requests-only 只檢查儲存貯體政策是否強制以 SSL/TLS 發出請求（傳輸中加密），並非檢查貯體是否以 KMS 靜態加密，無法辨識未以 KMS 加密的貯體。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"Uses the wrong Config rule (s3-bucket-ssl-requests-only, which checks SSL/TLS, not KMS at-rest encryption), so it fails part 1 despite a reasonable bucket-policy approach for part 2.","why_zh":"使用了錯誤的 Config 規則（s3-bucket-ssl-requests-only 檢查的是 SSL/TLS 而非 KMS 靜態加密），儘管第二部分的貯體政策做法尚可，仍在第一部分失敗。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/config/latest/developerguide/s3-default-encryption-kms.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/config/latest/developerguide/s3-bucket-ssl-requests-only.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonS3/latest/userguide/UsingKMSEncryption.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/managedservices/latest/userguide/scp-library-compliance.html"]}},{"id":144,"question_en":"A company wants to store all objects that contain sensitive data in an Amazon S3 bucket. The company will use server-side encryption to encrypt the S3 bucket. The company ' s operations team manages access to the company’s S3 buckets. The company ' s security team manages access to encryption keys. The company wants to separate the duties of the two teams to ensure that configuration errors by only one of these teams will not compromise the data by granting unauthorized access to plaintext data. Which solution will meet this requirement?","question_zh":"一家公司希望将所有包含敏感数据的对象存储在 Amazon S3 存储桶中，并使用服务器端加密来保 护该 S3 存储桶。公司的运维团队负责管理对 S3 存储桶的访问权限，而安全团队则负责管理加密密 钥的访问权限。公司希望将这两个团队的职责分开，以确保仅其中一个团队出现配置错误时，不会 因授予未授权方对明文数据的访问而导致数据泄露。 哪种解决方案能满足这一要求？","options_en":{"A":"Ensure that the operations team configures default bucket encryption on the S3 bucket to use server- side encryption with Amazon S3 managed encryption keys (SSE-S3). Ensure that the security team creates an IAM policy that controls access to use the encryption keys.","B":"Ensure that the operations team creates a bucket policy that requires requests to use server-side encryption with AWS KMS keys (SSE-KMS) that are customer managed. Ensure that the security team creates a key policy that controls access to the encryption keys.","C":"Ensure that the operations team creates a bucket policy that requires requests to use server-side encryption with Amazon S3 managed keys (SSE-S3). Ensure that the security team creates an IAM policy that controls access to the encryption keys.","D":"Ensure that the operations team creates a bucket policy that requires requests to use server-side encryption with customer-provided encryption keys (SSE-C). Ensure that the security team stores the customer-provided keys in AWS Key Management Service (AWS KMS). Ensure that the security team creates a key policy that controls access to the encryption keys."},"options_zh":{"A":"确保运维团队在S3存储桶上配置默认的存储桶加密，使用Amazon S3托管加密密钥（SSE-S3） 进行服务器端加密。确保安全团队创建一个IAM策略，以控制对加密密钥的访问权限。","B":"确保运维团队创建一个存储桶策略，要求请求必须使用客户管理的 AWS KMS 密钥（SSE-KMS） 进行服务器端加密。确保安全团队创建密钥策略，以控制对加密密钥的访问权限。","C":"确保运维团队创建一个存储桶策略，要求请求必须使用 Amazon S3 管理的密钥（SSE-S3） 进行服务器端加密。确保安全团队创建一个 IAM 策略，以控制对加密密钥的访问权限。","D":"确保运维团队创建一个存储桶策略，要求请求必须使用客户提供的加密密钥进行服务器端加密 （SSE-C）。确保安全团队将客户提供的密钥存储在 AWS 密钥管理服务（AWS KMS）中。 确保安全团队创建密钥策略，以控制对加密密钥的访问权限。"},"answer":["B"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Security/IAM","Storage"],"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選","research":{"verdict":["B"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"The requirement is true separation of duties: a misconfiguration by only one team must not, by itself, expose plaintext. That demands two independent access-control layers each owned by a different team. SSE-KMS with a customer managed key delivers this: reading plaintext requires BOTH s3:GetObject on the bucket (controlled by the operations team's bucket policy) AND kms:Decrypt on the CMK (controlled by the security team's KMS key policy). If operations mistakenly grants bucket access, the requester still cannot decrypt without key-policy access; if security mistakenly grants key access, the requester still cannot reach the objects without bucket access. So option B is correct. SSE-S3 (options A and C) fails because Amazon S3 fully manages those keys and exposes no customer-controllable key access policy at all, so the security team has no independent key-access control to manage and there is no dual control. SSE-C (option D) is technically invalid: customer-provided keys are supplied on each request and are NOT stored in AWS KMS (S3 keeps only a salted HMAC), so 'store the customer-provided keys in AWS KMS' and a KMS 'key policy' cannot exist for SSE-C.","explanation_zh":"本題要求真正的職責分離：任一團隊單獨的設定錯誤都不得自行導致明文外洩，因此需要兩層由不同團隊各自掌控的獨立存取控制。SSE-KMS 搭配 customer managed key 正好符合：讀取明文同時需要 bucket 的 s3:GetObject（由 operations 團隊的 bucket policy 控制）以及 CMK 的 kms:Decrypt（由 security 團隊的 KMS key policy 控制）。若 operations 誤放行 bucket 存取，沒有 key policy 授權仍無法解密；若 security 誤放行金鑰存取，沒有 bucket 存取仍拿不到物件。故選 B。SSE-S3（A、C）不行，因為金鑰完全由 Amazon S3 管理，不對外提供可由客戶控制的金鑰存取策略，security 團隊沒有可獨立掌控的金鑰存取層，無法形成雙重控制。SSE-C（D）在技術上不成立：客戶提供的金鑰是每次請求隨附、並不儲存於 AWS KMS（S3 僅保存加鹽 HMAC），因此 SSE-C 根本沒有『把金鑰存進 KMS』或 KMS『key policy』這回事。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"SSE-S3 keys are entirely managed by Amazon S3; there is no customer-controllable IAM or key policy governing use of SSE-S3 keys, so the security team has no independent key-access layer to manage and no dual control exists.","why_zh":"SSE-S3 金鑰完全由 Amazon S3 管理，客戶無法用 IAM 或 key policy 控管其使用，security 團隊沒有可獨立管理的金鑰存取層，形不成雙重控制。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"Same core flaw as A: SSE-S3 gives no customer access control over the keys, so an 'IAM policy that controls access to the encryption keys' is not possible; a single team's error could expose plaintext, defeating separation of duties.","why_zh":"與 A 同一根本問題：SSE-S3 不提供客戶對金鑰的存取控制，所謂『控管金鑰存取的 IAM policy』不存在；單一團隊的錯誤即可能外洩明文，達不到職責分離。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"SSE-C uses customer-provided keys sent with each request; AWS KMS does not store SSE-C keys (S3 keeps only a salted HMAC), so 'store the customer-provided keys in AWS KMS' and a KMS 'key policy' for SSE-C are technically impossible.","why_zh":"SSE-C 使用每次請求隨附的客戶提供金鑰；AWS KMS 不儲存 SSE-C 金鑰（S3 只保存加鹽 HMAC），因此『把客戶金鑰存進 KMS』及為 SSE-C 建立 KMS key policy 技術上不可能。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonS3/latest/userguide/UsingKMSEncryption.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonS3/latest/userguide/ServerSideEncryptionCustomerKeys.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/kms/latest/developerguide/key-policies.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonS3/latest/userguide/specifying-s3-c-encryption.html"]}},{"id":145,"question_en":"A company ' s web application is hosted on Amazon EC2 instances running behind an Application Load Balancer (ALB) in an Auto Scaling group. An AWS WAF web ACL is associated with the ALB. AWS CloudTrail is enabled and stores logs in Amazon S3 and Amazon CloudWatch Logs. The operations team has observed some EC2 instances reboot at random. After rebooting, all access logs on the instances have been deleted. During an investigation, the operations team found that each reboot happened just after a PHP error occurred on the new-user-creation.php file. The operations team needs to view log information to determine if the company is being attacked. Which set of actions will identify the suspect attacker ' s IP address for future occurrences?","question_zh":"一家公司的Web应用程序托管在Amazon EC2实例上，这些实例位于自动扩展组中，并运行在应用负载均衡器（ALB）之后。 一个AWS WAF网络ACL已与该ALB关联。AWS CloudTrail已启用，并将日志存储在Amazon S3和Amazon CloudWatch Logs中。 运维团队发现部分EC2实例出现随机重启现象。重启后，实例上的所有访问日志均被删除。在调查过程中，运维团队发现每次重启 都发生在new-user-creation.php文件发生PHP错误之后。运维团队需要查看日志信息，以判断公司是否正遭受攻击。 哪一组操作可以识别嫌疑攻击者的IP地址，以便在将来发生类似事件时使用？","options_en":{"A":"Configure VPC Flow Logs on the subnet where the ALB is located and stream the data to CloudWatch. Search for the new-user-creation.php occurrences in CloudWatch.","B":"Configure the CloudWatch agent on the ALB and send application logs to CloudWatch Logs.","C":"Configure the ALB to export access logs to an Amazon OpenSearch Service cluster and search for the new-user-creation.php occurrences.","D":"Configure the web ACL to send logs to Amazon Data Firehose, which delivers the logs to an S3 bucket. Use Amazon Athena to query the logs and find the new-user-creation.php occurrences."},"options_zh":{"A":"在ALB所在的子网中配置VPC流量日志，并将数据流式传输到CloudWatch。在CloudWatch中搜索new-user-creation.php的出现情 况。","B":"在ALB上配置CloudWatch代理，并将应用程序日志发送到CloudWatch Logs。","C":"配置 ALB 将访问日志导出到 Amazon OpenSearch 服务集群，并搜索 new-user-creation.php 的出现情况。","D":"配置网络ACL，将日志发送至Amazon Data Firehose，由其将日志传递到S3存储桶。使用Amazon Athena查询日志，查找new- user-creation.php的出现情况。"},"answer":["D"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Networking/DNS","Security/IAM","Storage","Compute","Monitoring/Ops","Analytics"],"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選","research":{"verdict":["D"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"The instances reboot and wipe their local access logs, so the only reliable way to capture the attacker's IP for future occurrences is an off-instance, durable Layer-7 log source. The web ACL is already associated with the ALB, so AWS WAF logging is the natural fit. AWS WAF supports sending web ACL logs to an Amazon Data Firehose delivery stream, which can deliver to an S3 bucket, and WAF logs include the client/source IP address and full HTTP request details (including the requested URI). Storing the logs in S3 and querying them with Amazon Athena lets the team search for new-user-creation.php occurrences and correlate them to the attacker's IP, and this data survives instance reboots. This is a documented, natively supported pattern, which makes D the only fully valid choice.","explanation_zh":"受攻擊的 EC2 執行個體會重啟並清除本機 access log，因此要在未來持續辨識攻擊者 IP，必須使用不在執行個體上、且能保存第七層 (L7) HTTP 內容的持久性 log 來源。由於 web ACL 已關聯到 ALB，AWS WAF logging 正是最合適的方案。AWS WAF 支援將 web ACL log 傳送到 Amazon Data Firehose delivery stream，再交付到 S3 bucket；WAF log 內含 client/source IP 位址與完整 HTTP 請求細節（包含請求的 URI）。將 log 存到 S3 並用 Amazon Athena 查詢，團隊即可搜尋 new-user-creation.php 出現的紀錄並比對出攻擊者 IP，且此資料不會因執行個體重啟而遺失。這是有官方文件支持且原生支援的作法，因此 D 是唯一完全成立的選項。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"VPC Flow Logs capture only IP-layer metadata (source/dest IP, ports, protocol, bytes, ACCEPT/REJECT). They contain no Layer-7/HTTP content, so the URI string new-user-creation.php never appears and cannot be searched in CloudWatch.","why_zh":"VPC Flow Logs 只記錄 IP 層 metadata（來源/目的 IP、port、protocol、位元組數、ACCEPT/REJECT），完全不含第七層 HTTP 內容，因此 new-user-creation.php 這個 URI 字串根本不會出現，無法在 CloudWatch 中搜尋到。"},{"letter":"B","why_en":"You cannot install the CloudWatch agent on an ALB. The ALB is a fully managed AWS service with no OS-level access, so running an agent on it is technically impossible.","why_zh":"無法在 ALB 上安裝 CloudWatch agent。ALB 是完全託管的 AWS 服務，使用者沒有作業系統層級的存取權，因此在其上執行 agent 在技術上不可行。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"ALB access logs can be delivered only to an Amazon S3 bucket; there is no native ALB option to export access logs directly to an Amazon OpenSearch Service cluster. Getting logs into OpenSearch requires extra plumbing (e.g., S3 -> Lambda/Firehose), so the option as written is not a valid ALB configuration.","why_zh":"ALB access logs 只能交付到 Amazon S3 bucket；ALB 並沒有原生選項可將 access logs 直接匯出到 Amazon OpenSearch Service cluster。要把 log 送進 OpenSearch 需額外串接（例如 S3 -> Lambda/Firehose），因此此選項所述並非有效的 ALB 設定。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/waf/latest/developerguide/logging.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/waf/latest/developerguide/logging-destinations.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/athena/latest/ug/waf-logs.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/elasticloadbalancing/latest/application/load-balancer-access-logs.html"]}},{"id":146,"question_en":"A company is expanding its group of stores. On the day that each new store opens, the company wants to launch a customized web application for that store. Each store ' s application will have a non-production environment and a production environment. Each environment will be deployed in a separate AWS account. The company uses AWS Organizations and has an OU that is used only for these accounts. The company distributes most of the development work to third-party development teams. A security engineer needs to ensure that each team follows the company ' s deployment plan for AWS resources. The security engineer also must limit access to the deployment plan to only the developers who need access. The security engineer already has created an AWS CloudFormation template that implements the deployment plan. What should the security engineer do next to meet the requirements in theMOST secureway?","question_zh":"一家公司正在扩展其门店网络。在每家新店开业当天，公司希望为该门店推出一个定制的网络应用 程序。每家门店的应用程序都将包含一个非生产环境和一个生产环境，且每个环境都将部署在独立 的 AWS 账户中。该公司使用 AWS Organizations，并已设置了一个仅用于这些账户的组织单元 （OU）。 该公司将大部分开发工作分配给第三方开发团队。安全工程师需要确保每个团队都遵循公司针对AWS 资源的部署计划，同时必须将部署计划的访问权限限制在仅需访问的开发人员范围内。安全工程师已 创建了一个实现该部署计划的AWS CloudFormation模板。 安全工程师接下来应采取什么措施，才能以最安全的方式满足要求？","options_en":{"A":"Create an AWS Service Catalog portfolio in the organization ' s management account. Upload the CloudFormation template. Add the template to the portfolio ' s product list. Share the portfolio with the OU.","B":"Use the CloudFormation CLI to create a module from the CloudFormation template. Register the module as a private extension in the CloudFormation registry. Publish the extension. Create an SCP that allows access to the extension.","C":"Create an AWS Service Catalog portfolio and create an IAM role for cross-account access. Attach the AWSServiceCatalogEndUserFullAccess managed policy to the role.","D":"Use the CloudFormation CLI to create a module and share the extension directly with the OU."},"options_zh":{"A":"在组织的管理账户中创建一个 AWS 服务目录组合，上传 CloudFormation 模板，将模板添加到 组合的产品列表中，并与 OU 共享该组合。","B":"使用 CloudFormation CLI 从 CloudFormation 模板创建模块。将该模块注册为 CloudFormation 注 册表中的私有扩展。发布该扩展。创建允许访问该扩展的 SCP。","C":"创建一个 AWS 服务目录组合，并创建一个用于跨账户访问的 IAM 角色。将 AWSServiceCatal ogEndUserFullAccess 管理策略附加到该角色。","D":"使用 CloudFormation CLI 创建模块，并直接与组织单元共享扩展。"},"answer":["A"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Organizations/Governance","Security/IAM","Monitoring/Ops"],"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選","research":{"verdict":["A"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"AWS Service Catalog is the purpose-built service for distributing a pre-approved, governed CloudFormation template as a 'product' so that third-party teams can only deploy resources that follow the company's approved deployment plan, and access can be scoped with IAM to only the developers who need it. The security engineer uploads the existing CloudFormation template as a product in a portfolio, then shares the portfolio with the OU using AWS Organizations integration; recipients cannot alter the products/constraints but can grant end-user IAM access, which enforces the plan while limiting who can use it. Option A is the only choice that both enforces the deployment plan and correctly distributes it to all accounts in the OU. Options B and D misuse CloudFormation modules/private extensions: modules are per-account/per-Region reusable building blocks included inside a parent template and do not force teams to follow a deployment plan, there is no mechanism to 'share an extension with an OU,' and an SCP is a deny/guardrail control that does not 'allow access' to a registry extension. Option C never shares the portfolio with the OU (so the third-party accounts cannot receive the product) and attaches the broad AWSServiceCatalogEndUserFullAccess policy, violating the requirement to limit access to only the developers who need it.","explanation_zh":"AWS Service Catalog 是專門用來將已核准、受治理的 CloudFormation 範本以「產品(product)」形式散布的服務,可確保第三方開發團隊只能部署符合公司核准部署計畫的資源,並透過 IAM 將存取範圍限縮到真正需要的開發者。安全工程師將既有的 CloudFormation 範本以產品形式上傳到投資組合(portfolio),再透過 AWS Organizations 整合把該 portfolio 分享給該 OU;接收端無法變更產品或約束條件,但可自行授予終端使用者的 IAM 存取權,如此既能強制執行部署計畫,又能限制使用者範圍。選項 A 是唯一同時「強制執行部署計畫」且「正確散布到 OU 內所有帳戶」的做法。選項 B 與 D 誤用 CloudFormation 模組/私有擴充功能:模組是以帳戶/區域為單位、被包含在父範本內的可重用建構區塊,並不會強制團隊遵循部署計畫;也沒有「把擴充功能分享給 OU」的機制;而 SCP 是拒絕/護欄型控制,並不會「允許存取」註冊表擴充功能。選項 C 從未把 portfolio 分享給 OU(第三方帳戶因此無法取得該產品),又附加了範圍過大的 AWSServiceCatalogEndUserFullAccess 政策,違反了將存取限縮到必要開發者的要求。","distractors":[{"letter":"B","why_en":"CloudFormation modules are per-account/per-Region private-registry building blocks included inside a parent template; registering/publishing one does not force teams to follow a deployment plan, and an SCP is a deny/guardrail control that cannot 'allow access' to a registry extension.","why_zh":"CloudFormation 模組是以帳戶/區域為單位、放在私有註冊表中並被父範本引用的建構區塊;註冊/發佈它並不會強制團隊遵循部署計畫,而且 SCP 是拒絕/護欄型控制,無法用來「允許存取」註冊表擴充功能。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"It never shares the portfolio with the OU, so third-party accounts cannot receive the product, and it grants the broad AWSServiceCatalogEndUserFullAccess policy, which contradicts limiting access to only the developers who need it.","why_zh":"它完全沒有把 portfolio 分享給 OU,第三方帳戶因此拿不到產品;又授予範圍過大的 AWSServiceCatalogEndUserFullAccess 政策,與「僅限必要開發者存取」的要求相牴觸。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"There is no mechanism to 'share a CloudFormation module/private extension directly with an OU'; private extensions are registered per account and Region, and modules do not enforce a deployment plan on distributed teams.","why_zh":"並不存在「把 CloudFormation 模組/私有擴充功能直接分享給 OU」的機制;私有擴充功能是以帳戶與區域為單位註冊的,而且模組無法對外部團隊強制執行部署計畫。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/servicecatalog/latest/adminguide/catalogs_portfolios_sharing_how-to-share.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/organizations/latest/userguide/services-that-can-integrate-servicecatalog.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AWSCloudFormation/latest/UserGuide/modules.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AWSCloudFormation/latest/UserGuide/modules-using.html"]}},{"id":147,"question_en":"A security engineer has designed a VPC to segment private traffic from public traffic. The VPC includes two Availability Zones. Each Availability Zone contains one public subnet and one private subnet. Three route tables exist: one for the public subnets and one for each private subnet. The security engineer discovers that all four subnets are routing traffic through the internet gateway that is attached to the VPC. Which combination of steps should the security engineer take to remediate this scenario? (Select TWO.)","question_zh":"一名安全工程师设计了一个VPC，用于将私有流量与公共流量进行隔离。该VPC包含两个可用区，每个可用区包含一个 公共子网和一个私有子网。共有三个路由表：一个用于公共子网，另外两个分别用于每个私有子网。 安全工程师发现，所有四个子网的流量都通过连接到VPC的互联网网关进行路由。 安全工程师应采取哪些步骤组合来解决此情况？（选择两项。）","options_en":{"A":"Verify that a NAT gateway has been provisioned in the public subnet in each Availability Zone.","C":"Modify the route tables for the public subnets to add a local route to the VPC CIDR range.","D":"Modify the route tables for the private subnets to route 0.0.0.0/0 to the NAT gateway in the public subnet of the same Availability Zone.","E":"Modify the route tables for the private subnets to route 0.0.0.0/0 to the internet gateway.","B":"Verify that a NAT gateway has been provisioned in the private subnet in each Availability Zone."},"options_zh":{"A":"验证每个可用区的公共子网中是否已配置了NAT网关。","B":"验证每个可用区的私有子网中是否已配置了NAT网关。","C":"修改公共子网的路由表，添加一条指向VPC CIDR范围的本地路由。","D":"修改私有子网的路由表，将 0.0.0.0/0 路由到同一可用区中公共子网的 NAT 网关。","E":"修改私有子网的路由表，将 0.0.0.0/0 路由到互联网网关。"},"answer":["A","D"],"multi":true,"vote":{},"tags":["Networking/DNS"],"difficulty":2,"diff_why":"複選","research":{"verdict":["A","D"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"The design goal is a standard public/private VPC where only public subnets route 0.0.0.0/0 to the internet gateway, and private subnets reach the internet outbound-only through a NAT gateway. The bug is that all four route tables send 0.0.0.0/0 to the IGW, so the two private subnets are effectively public. AWS docs specify that a NAT gateway must live in a PUBLIC subnet (it needs its own IGW route to function), so step A (verify a NAT gateway exists in the public subnet of each AZ) is the required prerequisite. Then per the routing docs you 'add a route for the private subnet's route table that routes IPv4 internet traffic (0.0.0.0/0) to the NAT device' — step D fixes the private route tables to target the same-AZ NAT gateway (same-AZ placement is best practice for resiliency and to avoid cross-AZ NAT data charges). Together A and D restore private/public segmentation.","explanation_zh":"此設計目標是標準的 public/private VPC：只有 public 子網的路由表把 0.0.0.0/0 指向 internet gateway，private 子網則透過 NAT gateway 進行僅出站的網際網路存取。問題在於四張路由表都把 0.0.0.0/0 指向 IGW，導致兩個 private 子網實質上變成 public。AWS 文件明確指出 NAT gateway 必須位於 PUBLIC 子網（它本身需要一條指向 IGW 的路由才能運作），因此步驟 A（確認每個 AZ 的 public 子網已佈署 NAT gateway）是必要前提。接著依路由文件，需在 private 子網路由表加入將 0.0.0.0/0 導向 NAT device 的路由——步驟 D 將 private 路由表改為指向同 AZ 的 NAT gateway（同 AZ 佈署是韌性最佳實務，並可避免跨 AZ 的 NAT 資料處理費用）。A 與 D 共同還原 private/public 分段。","distractors":[{"letter":"B","why_en":"A NAT gateway placed in a private subnet cannot reach the internet itself, because a private subnet has no route to the internet gateway. The NAT gateway must sit in a public subnet, so verifying it is in the private subnet is incorrect.","why_zh":"放在 private 子網的 NAT gateway 本身無法連上網際網路，因為 private 子網沒有指向 IGW 的路由。NAT gateway 必須位於 public 子網，故「確認 NAT gateway 在 private 子網」是錯的。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"The local route for the VPC CIDR is created automatically in every route table and cannot be manually added or removed. Adding a local route does nothing to remediate the private subnets wrongly routing to the IGW.","why_zh":"VPC CIDR 的 local 路由在每張路由表中都自動存在，無法手動新增或刪除。加入 local 路由完全無法修正 private 子網錯誤指向 IGW 的問題。"},{"letter":"E","why_en":"Routing the private subnets' 0.0.0.0/0 to the internet gateway is exactly the broken current state — it makes the private subnets public, the opposite of the required segmentation.","why_zh":"把 private 子網的 0.0.0.0/0 指向 internet gateway 正是目前壞掉的狀態——這會讓 private 子網變成 public，與所需的分段目標相反。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/vpc/latest/userguide/vpc-example-private-subnets-nat.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/vpc/latest/userguide/route-table-options.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/vpc/latest/userguide/vpc-nat-gateway.html"]}},{"id":148,"question_en":"A company is attempting to conduct forensic analysis on an Amazon EC2 instance, but the company is unable to connect to the instance by using AWS Systems Manager Session Manager. The company has installed AWS Systems Manager Agent (SSM Agent) on the EC2 instance. The EC2 instance is in a subnet in a VPC that does not have an internet gateway attached. The company has associated a security group with the EC2 instance. The security group does not have inbound or outbound rules. The subnet’s network ACL allows all inbound and outbound traffic. Which combination of actions will allow the company to conduct forensic analysis on the EC2 instance without compromising forensic data? (Select THREE.)","question_zh":"一家公司正尝试对 Amazon EC2 实例进行取证分析，但无法通过 AWS Systems Manager Session Manager 连接到该实例。该公司已在 EC2 实例上安装了 AWS Systems Manager Agent（SSM Agent）。 EC2 实例位于一个未连接互联网网关的 VPC 子网中。公司已为该 EC2 实例关联了一个安全组， 但该安全组没有入站或出站规则。子网的网络 ACL 允许所有入站和出站流量。 哪些操作组合可使公司在不损害取证数据的前提下对EC2实例进行取证分析？（选择三项。）","options_en":{"A":"Update the EC2 instance security group to add a rule that allows outbound traffic on port 443 for 0.0.0.0 /0.","B":"Update the EC2 instance security group to add a rule that allows inbound traffic on port 443 to the VPC ' s CIDR range.","C":"Create an EC2 key pair. Associate the key pair with the EC2 instance.","D":"Create a VPC interface endpoint for Systems Manager in the VPC where the EC2 instance is located.","E":"Attach a security group to the VPC interface endpoint. Allow inbound traffic on port 443 to the VPC ' s CIDR range.","F":"Create a VPC interface endpoint for the EC2 instance in the VPC where the EC2 instance is located."},"options_zh":{"A":"更新 EC2 实例的安全组，添加一条规则，允许 0.0.0.0/0 的出站流量通过端口 443。","B":"更新 EC2 实例的安全组，添加一条规则，允许从 VPC 的 CIDR 范围进入的 443 端口流量。","C":"创建一个 EC2 密钥对，并将该密钥对与 EC2 实例关联。","D":"在 EC2 实例所在的 VPC 中为 Systems Manager 创建一个 VPC 接口端点。","E":"将安全组附加到 VPC 接口端点。允许从 VPC 的 CIDR 范围进入的 443 端口流量。","F":"为 EC2 实例所在 VPC 中的 EC2 实例创建一个 VPC 接口端点。"},"answer":["A","D","E"],"multi":true,"vote":{},"tags":["Compute","Monitoring/Ops"],"difficulty":2,"diff_why":"複選","research":{"verdict":["A","D","E"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"The EC2 instance is in a private subnet with no internet gateway (and no NAT), so the SSM Agent cannot reach the Session Manager service over the internet. To fix this without touching the instance (which would compromise forensic data), you route Systems Manager traffic privately: (D) create VPC interface endpoints for Systems Manager (ssm, ssmmessages, ec2messages) so SSM Agent can reach the service over PrivateLink with private IPs; (E) attach a security group to those interface endpoints that allows inbound 443 from the VPC CIDR, because the docs state 'the security group attached to the VPC endpoint must allow incoming connections on port 443 from the private subnet of the managed instance'; and (A) update the instance security group to allow OUTBOUND 443, because SSM Agent always initiates connections outbound and the instance security group currently has no outbound rule, so the agent cannot reach the endpoints. These three are network/endpoint changes that do not alter the instance's disk or memory state, preserving forensic integrity.","explanation_zh":"EC2 執行個體位於沒有 internet gateway（也沒有 NAT）的私有子網，因此 SSM Agent 無法透過網際網路連到 Session Manager 服務。要在不動到執行個體本身（以免破壞鑑識資料）的前提下修復，必須讓 Systems Manager 流量走私有路徑：(D) 為 Systems Manager 建立 VPC interface endpoints（ssm、ssmmessages、ec2messages），讓 SSM Agent 透過 PrivateLink 以私有 IP 連到服務；(E) 為這些 interface endpoint 掛上安全群組並允許來自 VPC CIDR 的 443 入站，因為官方文件明載『掛在 VPC endpoint 上的安全群組必須允許來自受管節點私有子網的 443 埠入站連線』；(A) 更新執行個體安全群組允許 443『出站』，因為 SSM Agent 一律主動發起出站連線，而目前執行個體安全群組沒有任何出站規則，agent 無法到達 endpoint。這三項都是網路／端點層級變更，不會改動執行個體的磁碟或記憶體狀態，可保全鑑識完整性。","distractors":[{"letter":"B","why_en":"SSM Agent initiates all connections outbound; the instance does not need any inbound rule for Session Manager. AWS docs state you 'don't need to configure your firewall to allow inbound traffic to your instances for Systems Manager.' Inbound 443 to the instance is unnecessary and the missing rule is the OUTBOUND one (option A).","why_zh":"SSM Agent 一律主動發起出站連線，執行個體不需要任何入站規則即可用 Session Manager。AWS 文件明載『Systems Manager 不需要設定防火牆允許入站到執行個體』。入站 443 到執行個體多餘，真正缺的是出站規則（選項 A）。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"Session Manager does not use SSH key pairs at all, and you cannot associate a new key pair with an already-running instance. Modifying the instance to add a key would also risk compromising forensic data, which the question explicitly forbids.","why_zh":"Session Manager 完全不使用 SSH key pair，且無法把新的 key pair 掛到已在執行中的執行個體。為加金鑰而改動執行個體還會有破壞鑑識資料的風險，正是題目明令避免的。"},{"letter":"F","why_en":"An interface endpoint 'for the EC2 instance' is not what enables Session Manager. Session Manager connectivity is provided by the Systems Manager endpoints (ssm/ssmmessages/ec2messages) in option D. The EC2 API endpoint is only needed for extras like VSS snapshots, not for establishing the session, so F is redundant/incorrect here.","why_zh":"為『EC2 執行個體』建立 interface endpoint 並不能啟用 Session Manager。Session Manager 連線由選項 D 的 Systems Manager 端點（ssm/ssmmessages/ec2messages）提供。EC2 API 端點只在 VSS 快照等額外功能才需要，與建立工作階段無關，故 F 在此多餘且錯誤。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/systems-manager/latest/userguide/session-manager-getting-started-privatelink.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/systems-manager/latest/userguide/setup-create-vpc.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/systems-manager/latest/userguide/systems-manager-setting-up-messageAPIs.html"]}},{"id":149,"question_en":"A company is developing an application that runs across a combination of Amazon EC2 On-Demand Instances and Spot Instances. A security engineer needs to provide a logging solution that makes logs for all instances available from a single location. The solution must allow only a specific set of users to analyze the logs for event patterns. The users must be able to use SQL queries on the logs to perform root cause analysis. Which solution will meet these requirements?","question_zh":"一家公司正在开发一个应用程序，该应用运行在 Amazon EC2 按需实例和竞价实例的组合上。安全 工程师需要提供一种日志解决方案，使所有实例的日志都能从单一位置访问。该方案必须仅允许特 定的一组用户分析日志中的事件模式，并且这些用户应能够使用 SQL 查询对日志进行根因分析。 哪种解决方案能满足这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Configure the EC2 instances to send application logs to a single Amazon CloudWatch Logs log group. Allow only specific users to access the log group. Use CloudWatch Logs Insights to query the log group.","B":"Configure the EC2 instances to send application logs to a single Amazon S3 bucket. Allow only specific users to access the S3 bucket. Use Amazon CloudWatch Logs Insights to query the log files in the S3 bucket.","C":"Configure each EC2 instance to send its application logs to its own specific Amazon CloudWatch Logs log group. Allow only specific users to access the log groups. Use Amazon Athena to query all the log groups.","D":"Configure the EC2 instances to send application logs to a single Amazon CloudWatch Logs log group. Grant Amazon Detective access to the log group. Allow only specific users to use Detective to analyze the logs."},"options_zh":{"A":"配置 EC2 实例将应用程序日志发送到一个 Amazon CloudWatch Logs 日志组，并仅允许特定用 户访问该日志组。使用 CloudWatch Logs Insights 查询该日志组。","B":"配置 EC2 实例将应用程序日志发送到一个 Amazon S3 存储桶，并仅允许特定用户访问该 S3 存 储桶。使用 Amazon CloudWatch Logs Insights 查询存储桶中的日志文件。","C":"配置每个EC2实例将其应用程序日志发送到各自独立的Amazon CloudWatch Logs日志组，并仅 允许特定用户访问这些日志组。使用Amazon Athena查询所有日志组。","D":"配置 EC2 实例将应用程序日志发送到一个 Amazon CloudWatch Logs 日志组。授予 Amazon Detective 访问该日志组的权限，并仅允许特定用户使用 Detective 分析日志。"},"answer":["A"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Storage","Compute","Monitoring/Ops","Analytics"],"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選","research":{"verdict":["A"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"both","explanation_en":"The requirements are: (1) a single location holding logs from all instances (both On-Demand and Spot), (2) access restricted to a specific set of users, and (3) the ability to run SQL queries on the logs for root cause analysis. Option A sends all instance application logs (via the CloudWatch agent) to one CloudWatch Logs log group, restricts access to that log group with IAM, and queries it with CloudWatch Logs Insights. CloudWatch Logs Insights now supports OpenSearch Structured Query Language (SQL) directly against log groups, with SELECT, FROM, WHERE, GROUP BY, HAVING, JOINs, and subqueries, so the SQL requirement is met natively with no data movement. Option B is technically invalid because CloudWatch Logs Insights queries CloudWatch Logs log groups, not arbitrary log files stored in an S3 bucket (Athena, not Logs Insights, would query S3). Option C breaks the single-location requirement by giving each instance its own log group (unmanageable for ephemeral Spot instances) and incorrectly claims Athena can query CloudWatch Logs log groups, whereas Athena queries data in S3. Option D fails because Amazon Detective ingests CloudTrail, VPC Flow Logs, GuardDuty findings, and Security Lake data (not custom EC2 application logs) and analyzes them with a graph-based model, not SQL for root cause analysis of application logs.","explanation_zh":"需求為：(1) 單一位置集中所有執行個體（On-Demand 與 Spot）的日誌，(2) 僅限特定使用者存取分析，(3) 使用者能對日誌執行 SQL 查詢做根因分析。選項 A 透過 CloudWatch agent 將所有執行個體的應用日誌送到單一 CloudWatch Logs log group，用 IAM 限制特定使用者存取該 log group，並以 CloudWatch Logs Insights 查詢。CloudWatch Logs Insights 現已支援 OpenSearch Structured Query Language (SQL)，可直接對 log group 執行 SELECT、FROM、WHERE、GROUP BY、HAVING、JOIN 與子查詢，因此 SQL 需求原生滿足且不需搬移資料。選項 B 技術上不成立，因為 CloudWatch Logs Insights 查詢的是 CloudWatch Logs log group，而非 S3 bucket 中的日誌檔案（查 S3 應該用 Athena 而非 Logs Insights）。選項 C 違反單一位置需求（每個執行個體各有 log group，對短暫的 Spot 執行個體難以管理），且錯誤地宣稱 Athena 可直接查詢 CloudWatch Logs log group（Athena 查的是 S3 中的資料）。選項 D 不成立，因為 Amazon Detective 攝取的是 CloudTrail、VPC Flow Logs、GuardDuty findings 與 Security Lake 資料（非自訂 EC2 應用日誌），且以行為圖模型分析，並非以 SQL 對應用日誌做根因分析。","distractors":[{"letter":"B","why_en":"CloudWatch Logs Insights cannot query log files stored in an S3 bucket; it only queries CloudWatch Logs log groups. Querying SQL over logs in S3 would require Amazon Athena, so this option pairs the wrong tool with the wrong store.","why_zh":"CloudWatch Logs Insights 無法查詢儲存在 S3 bucket 中的日誌檔案，它只能查詢 CloudWatch Logs log group。對 S3 中的日誌做 SQL 查詢應使用 Amazon Athena，此選項把工具與儲存位置錯配。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"Giving each instance its own log group violates the single-location requirement and is unmanageable for ephemeral Spot instances. Also, Amazon Athena queries data in Amazon S3, not CloudWatch Logs log groups directly.","why_zh":"讓每個執行個體各自使用一個 log group 違反單一位置需求，且對短暫的 Spot 執行個體難以管理。此外，Amazon Athena 查詢的是 Amazon S3 中的資料，無法直接查詢 CloudWatch Logs log group。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"Amazon Detective consumes CloudTrail, VPC Flow Logs, GuardDuty findings, and Security Lake data, not custom EC2 application logs from a log group, and it analyzes data via a behavior graph rather than SQL queries for root cause analysis.","why_zh":"Amazon Detective 攝取的是 CloudTrail、VPC Flow Logs、GuardDuty findings 與 Security Lake 資料，而非 log group 中的自訂 EC2 應用日誌，且它是以行為圖分析而非用 SQL 查詢做根因分析。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonCloudWatch/latest/logs/CWL_AnalyzeLogData_Languages.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonCloudWatch/latest/logs/CWL_AnalyzeLogData_SQL.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonCloudWatch/latest/logs/CloudWatchLogs-Insights-Query-Assist.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/athena/latest/ug/cloudtrail-logs.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/detective/latest/userguide/detective-source-data-about.html"]}},{"id":150,"question_en":"A company has AWS accounts in an organization in AWS Organizations. An Amazon S3 bucket in one account is publicly accessible. A security engineer must remove public access and ensure the bucket cannot be made public again. Which solution will meet these requirements?","question_zh":"一家公司在 AWS Organizations 中拥有一个组织内的多个 AWS 账户。其中一个账户中的 Amazon S3 存储桶可被公开访问。安全 工程师必须移除公共访问权限，并确保该存储桶无法再次被设置为公开。 哪种解决方案能满足这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Enforce KMS encryption and deny s3:GetObject by SCP.","B":"Enable PublicAccessBlock and deny s3:GetObject by SCP.","C":"Enable PublicAccessBlock and deny s3:PutPublicAccessBlock by SCP.","D":"Enable Object Lock governance and deny s3:PutPublicAccessBlock by SCP."},"options_zh":{"A":"强制实施KMS加密，并通过SCP拒绝s3:GetObject权限。","B":"启用 PublicAccessBlock 并通过 SCP 拒绝 s3:GetObject 权限。","C":"启用 PublicAccessBlock 并通过 SCP 拒绝 s3:PutPublicAccessBlock。","D":"启用对象锁定治理，并通过SCP拒绝s3:PutPublicAccessBlock权限。"},"answer":["C"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Organizations/Governance","Security/IAM","Storage"],"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選","research":{"verdict":["C"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"The question has two requirements: (1) remove existing public access, and (2) ensure the bucket can never be made public again. Enabling S3 Block Public Access (the PublicAccessBlock configuration) satisfies requirement 1 by overriding any ACLs or bucket policies that grant public access. To satisfy requirement 2, you must stop anyone from turning that protection back off. The API action that modifies these settings is s3:PutBucketPublicAccessBlock (account-level: s3:PutAccountPublicAccessBlock). Denying this action in a Service Control Policy prevents any principal in the account from disabling Block Public Access, so the bucket cannot be re-exposed. This is exactly the AWS-documented pattern (SCP-AMS-018 'Prevent disabling S3 account public access block'). Option C enables PublicAccessBlock and denies s3:PutPublicAccessBlock via SCP, meeting both requirements.","explanation_zh":"本題有兩個要求：(1) 移除現有的公開存取，(2) 確保該 bucket 之後無法再被設為公開。啟用 S3 Block Public Access（PublicAccessBlock 設定）可覆寫任何授予公開存取的 ACL 或 bucket policy，滿足要求 1。要滿足要求 2，必須阻止任何人把這個保護關掉；修改這些設定的 API 動作是 s3:PutBucketPublicAccessBlock（帳戶層級為 s3:PutAccountPublicAccessBlock）。在 SCP 中 Deny 這個動作，帳戶內任何 principal 都無法停用 Block Public Access，bucket 就無法再被重新公開。這正是 AWS 官方文件記載的做法（SCP-AMS-018『Prevent disabling S3 account public access block』）。選項 C 啟用 PublicAccessBlock 並以 SCP Deny s3:PutPublicAccessBlock，同時滿足兩項要求。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"KMS encryption is unrelated to public access, and a blanket deny of s3:GetObject does not remove or lock public-access configuration; it breaks all legitimate reads without preventing the bucket from being made public.","why_zh":"KMS 加密與公開存取無關，全面 Deny s3:GetObject 既不移除也不鎖定公開存取設定，只會阻斷所有正常讀取，且無法防止 bucket 被設為公開。"},{"letter":"B","why_en":"Enabling PublicAccessBlock removes public access, but denying s3:GetObject does not prevent someone from later disabling Block Public Access; it fails the 'cannot be made public again' requirement and also blocks all legitimate object reads.","why_zh":"啟用 PublicAccessBlock 可移除公開存取，但 Deny s3:GetObject 無法阻止之後有人停用 Block Public Access，未達成『不能再被設為公開』的要求，且會阻斷所有正常物件讀取。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"S3 Object Lock (governance mode) provides WORM protection against object deletion/overwrite, not public-access control, so it does not remove existing public access; denying s3:PutPublicAccessBlock alone without first enabling BPA leaves the bucket publicly accessible.","why_zh":"S3 Object Lock（governance 模式）提供 WORM 防刪改保護，並非公開存取控制，無法移除既有公開存取；僅 Deny s3:PutPublicAccessBlock 而未先啟用 BPA，bucket 仍維持公開。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonS3/latest/userguide/access-control-block-public-access.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/managedservices/latest/userguide/scp-library-compliance.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonS3/latest/API/API_control_PutPublicAccessBlock.html"]}},{"id":151,"question_en":"A company has several Amazon S3 buckets that do not enforce encryption in transit. A security engineer must implement a solution that enforces encryption in transit for all the company ' s existing and future S3 buckets. Which solution will meet these requirements?","question_zh":"一家公司拥有多个Amazon S3存储桶，这些存储桶未强制实施传输过程中的加密。安全工程师必须实施一项解决方案，以确保公司所有 现有及未来的S3存储桶在传输过程中均启用加密。 哪种解决方案能满足这些要求","options_en":{"A":"Enable AWS Config. Create a proactive AWS Config Custom Policy rule. Create a Guard clause to evaluate the S3 bucket policies to check for a value of True for the aws:SecureTransport condition key. If the AWS Config rule evaluates to NON_COMPLIANT, block resource creation.","B":"Enable AWS Config. Configure the s3-bucket-ssl-requests-only AWS Config managed rule and set the rule trigger type to Hybrid. Create an AWS Systems Manager Automation runbook that applies a bucket policy to deny requests when the value of the aws:SecureTransport condition key is False. Configure automatic remediation. Set the runbook as the target of the rule.","C":"Enable Amazon Inspector. Create a custom AWS Lambda rule. Create a Lambda function that applies a bucket policy to deny requests when the value of the aws:SecureTransport condition key is False. Set the Lambda function as the target of the rule.","D":"Create an AWS CloudTrail trail. Enable S3 data events on the trail. Create an AWS Lambda function that applies a bucket policy to deny requests when the value of the aws:SecureTransport condition key is False. Configure the CloudTrail trail to invoke the Lambda function."},"options_zh":{"B":"启用 AWS Config。配置 s3-bucket-ssl-requests-only 这条 AWS Config 管理规则，并将规则触发类型设置为混合模式。创建一个 AWS Systems Manager Automation 自动化运行手册，用于在 aws:SecureTransport 条件键的值为 False 时，应用拒绝请求的存储 桶策略。配置自动修复功能，并将该运行手册设为规则的目标。","C":"启用 Amazon Inspector。创建自定义的 AWS Lambda 规则。创建一个 Lambda 函数，用于在 aws:SecureTransport 条件键的值为 False 时，拒绝请求并应用存储桶策略。将该 Lambda 函数设置为规则的目标。","D":"创建一个 AWS CloudTrail 跟踪，启用该跟踪上的 S3 数据事件。创建一个 AWS Lambda 函数，用于在 aws:SecureTransport 条件 键的值为 False 时，应用存储桶策略以拒绝请求。配置 CloudTrail 跟踪以调用该 Lambda 函数。","A":"启用 AWS Config。创建一个主动的 AWS Config 自定义策略规则。创建一个 Guard 语句，用于评估 S3 存储桶策略，检查 aws: SecureTransport 条件键的值是否为 True。如果 AWS Config 规则评估结果为“不合规”，则阻止资源创建。"},"answer":["B"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Organizations/Governance","Security/IAM","Storage","Compute","Monitoring/Ops"],"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選","research":{"verdict":["B"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"The AWS-documented pattern to enforce encryption in transit across existing and future S3 buckets is a detective AWS Config managed rule with auto-remediation. Option B uses the real managed rule s3-bucket-ssl-requests-only (which flags buckets whose policy does not deny requests where aws:SecureTransport is false) and wires it to automatic remediation via the AWS-provided Systems Manager Automation runbook AWSConfigRemediation-RestrictBucketSSLRequestsOnly, which applies a bucket policy that explicitly denies HTTP (non-SSL) requests. Because the Config rule is triggered by configuration changes, it evaluates and remediates both currently existing buckets and any new bucket that is created, satisfying the 'existing and future' requirement. Option A is wrong because AWS Config proactive rules do NOT block or prevent resource creation: the docs explicitly state 'Proactive rules do not remediate resources that are flagged as NON_COMPLIANT or prevent them from being deployed' - proactive mode only lets you check a resource via the StartResourceEvaluation API before deployment. The only blemish in B is the phrase 'set the rule trigger type to Hybrid' (the managed rule's actual trigger type is Configuration changes), but that is a minor descriptive inaccuracy; B's overall architecture is the correct, canonical AWS solution while A's core mechanism is factually impossible.","explanation_zh":"在既有與未來的 S3 buckets 上強制傳輸中加密，AWS 官方建議的做法是使用偵測型 AWS Config 受管規則搭配自動修復。選項 B 使用真實存在的受管規則 s3-bucket-ssl-requests-only（會標記 bucket policy 未拒絕 aws:SecureTransport 為 false 之請求的 bucket），並串接 AWS 官方提供的 Systems Manager Automation runbook AWSConfigRemediation-RestrictBucketSSLRequestsOnly 進行自動修復，該 runbook 會套用一條明確拒絕 HTTP（非 SSL）請求的 bucket policy。由於此 Config 規則由組態變更觸發，會對現有 bucket 及任何新建 bucket 進行評估與修復，滿足『既有與未來』的需求。選項 A 錯誤，因為 AWS Config 的 proactive 規則不會封鎖或阻止資源建立：官方文件明確指出『Proactive rules do not remediate resources that are flagged as NON_COMPLIANT or prevent them from being deployed』，proactive 模式僅能透過 StartResourceEvaluation API 在部署前檢查資源。B 唯一瑕疵是『set the rule trigger type to Hybrid』一詞（該受管規則的實際觸發類型是 Configuration changes），但屬輕微描述不精確；B 的整體架構是正確且標準的 AWS 解法，而 A 的核心機制在事實上不可能成立。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"AWS Config proactive/Custom Policy (Guard) rules do NOT block resource creation. The docs explicitly state proactive rules 'do not remediate resources that are flagged as NON_COMPLIANT or prevent them from being deployed' - proactive mode only enables pre-deployment checks via StartResourceEvaluation, so it cannot enforce/block creation as the option claims.","why_zh":"AWS Config 的 proactive/Custom Policy（Guard）規則不會封鎖資源建立。官方文件明確指出 proactive 規則『不會修復被標記為 NON_COMPLIANT 的資源，也不會阻止其部署』；proactive 模式僅能透過 StartResourceEvaluation 進行部署前檢查，無法如選項所述強制封鎖建立。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"Amazon Inspector is a vulnerability scanner (EC2/ECR/Lambda code), not a compliance-remediation engine. It has no concept of 'custom Lambda rules' that target a Lambda to reapply bucket policies - that mechanism belongs to AWS Config, not Inspector. The service choice is fundamentally wrong.","why_zh":"Amazon Inspector 是弱點掃描服務（EC2/ECR/Lambda 程式碼），並非合規修復引擎。它沒有『custom Lambda rules』去觸發 Lambda 重新套用 bucket policy 的機制，那是 AWS Config 的功能，非 Inspector。服務選擇根本錯誤。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"CloudTrail S3 data events + Lambda is an event-driven reaction to API activity; it does not systematically evaluate and remediate all existing buckets and is a non-standard, brittle pattern. CloudTrail cannot 'invoke a Lambda function' directly on data events for enforcement in the way described, and it fails to guarantee coverage of pre-existing buckets.","why_zh":"CloudTrail S3 data events + Lambda 是針對 API 活動的事件驅動反應，無法系統性地評估與修復所有既有 bucket，是非標準且脆弱的做法。CloudTrail 也無法如描述般直接『呼叫 Lambda』對 data events 進行強制執行，且無法保證涵蓋既有 bucket。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/config/latest/developerguide/s3-bucket-ssl-requests-only.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/systems-manager-automation-runbooks/latest/userguide/automation-aws-s3-deny-http.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/config/latest/developerguide/evaluating-your-resources.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/config/latest/developerguide/evaluate-config_develop-rules_cfn-guard.html"]}},{"id":152,"question_en":"A company runs workloads in an AWS account. A security engineer observes some unusual findings in Amazon GuardDuty. The security engineer wants to investigate a specific IAM role and generate an investigation report. The report must contain details about anomalous behavior and any indicators of compromise. Which solution will meet these requirements?","question_zh":"一家公司在AWS账户中运行工作负载。安全工程师在Amazon GuardDuty中发现了一些异常情况，希望调查某个特定的 IAM角色并生成一份调查报告。该报告必须包含有关异常行为以及任何入侵迹象的详细信息。 哪种解决方案能满足这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Use Amazon Detective to perform an investigation on the IAM role.","B":"Use AWS Audit Manager to create an assessment. Specify the IAM role. Run an assessment report.","C":"Use Amazon Inspector to create an assessment. Specify the IAM role. Run an assessment report.","D":"Use Amazon Inspector to run an on-demand scan of the IAM role."},"options_zh":{"A":"使用 Amazon Detective 对 IAM 角色进行调查。","B":"使用 AWS 审计管理器创建评估，指定 IAM 角色，并运行评估报告。","C":"使用 Amazon Inspector 创建评估任务，指定 IAM 角色，运行评估报告。","D":"使用 Amazon Inspector 对 IAM 角色运行按需扫描。"},"answer":["A"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Security/IAM"],"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選","research":{"verdict":["A"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"Amazon Detective Investigation is purpose-built for exactly this scenario. Per the AWS docs, 'You can use Amazon Detective Investigation to investigate IAM users and IAM roles using indicators of compromise (IOCs), which can help you determine if a resource is involved in a security incident.' It uses machine learning models and threat intelligence built on Detective's behavioral graph to identify anomalous behavior (attack tactics, impossible travel, flagged IP addresses, finding groups) and 'generates a report highlighting the risks.' You can start an investigation against a specific IAM role via the console, the StartInvestigation API, or the start-investigation CLI (using --entity-arn arn:aws:iam::...:role/rolename). Detective also integrates directly with GuardDuty for pivoting from a finding. This satisfies every requirement: investigate a specific IAM role, produce an investigation report, and surface anomalous behavior plus indicators of compromise.","explanation_zh":"Amazon Detective Investigation 正是為此情境設計。根據 AWS 文件：『You can use Amazon Detective Investigation to investigate IAM users and IAM roles using indicators of compromise (IOCs)』，它利用建立在 Detective behavioral graph 上的機器學習模型與威脅情資，找出異常行為（attack tactics、impossible travel、flagged IP addresses、finding groups），並『generates a report highlighting the risks』。可透過 Console、StartInvestigation API 或 start-investigation CLI（--entity-arn arn:aws:iam::...:role/rolename）針對特定 IAM role 啟動調查，且能與 GuardDuty finding 直接 pivot 整合。完全符合題目所有需求：調查特定 IAM role、產生調查報告、呈現異常行為與 indicators of compromise。","distractors":[{"letter":"B","why_en":"AWS Audit Manager collects evidence and produces compliance assessment reports against frameworks (e.g., CIS, PCI DSS, SOC 2). It does not investigate anomalous behavior or indicators of compromise for a specific IAM role, and it does not take an IAM role as an assessment target.","why_zh":"AWS Audit Manager 用於依合規框架（CIS、PCI DSS、SOC 2 等）蒐集證據並產出合規評估報告，不會針對特定 IAM role 調查異常行為或 indicators of compromise，也無法把 IAM role 當作評估對象。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"Amazon Inspector is a vulnerability management service that assesses EC2 instances, ECR container images, and Lambda functions for software vulnerabilities and network exposure. It cannot 'specify an IAM role' as an assessment target and has no IOC/anomalous-behavior investigation report.","why_zh":"Amazon Inspector 是弱點管理服務，掃描 EC2、ECR 容器映像與 Lambda 的軟體弱點與網路暴露，無法以 IAM role 作為評估對象，也沒有 IOC 或異常行為的調查報告。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"Amazon Inspector on-demand scans target compute resources (EC2/ECR/Lambda) for CVEs, not IAM roles. Inspector has no concept of scanning an IAM role or reporting indicators of compromise.","why_zh":"Amazon Inspector 的 on-demand scan 針對運算資源（EC2/ECR/Lambda）掃 CVE，並非 IAM role；Inspector 沒有掃描 IAM role 或回報 indicators of compromise 的能力。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/detective/latest/userguide/investigations-about.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/detective/latest/userguide/run-investigations.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/detective/latest/userguide/investigations-report-understand.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/guardduty/latest/ug/detective-integration.html"]}},{"id":153,"question_en":"A company begins to use AWS WAF after experiencing an increase in traffic to the company’s public web applications. A security engineer needs to determine if the increase in traffic is because of application-layer attacks. The security engineer needs a solution to analyze AWS WAF traffic. Which solution will meet this requirement?","question_zh":"一家公司在其公共网络应用流量增加后开始使用 AWS WAF。安全工程师需要确定流量增长是否由应用层攻击引起，并 需要一种解决方案来分析 AWS WAF 的流量。 哪种解决方案能满足这一要求？","options_en":{"A":"Send AWS WAF logs to AWS CloudTrail and analyze them with OpenSearch.","B":"Send AWS WAF logs to Amazon S3 and query them directly with OpenSearch.","C":"Send AWS WAF logs to Amazon S3. Create an Amazon Athena table with partition projection. Use Athena to query the logs.","D":"Send AWS WAF logs to AWS CloudTrail and analyze them with Amazon Athena."},"options_zh":{"A":"将 AWS WAF 日志发送到 AWS CloudTrail，并使用 OpenSearch 进行分析。","B":"将 AWS WAF 日志发送到 Amazon S3，并通过 OpenSearch 直接查询。","C":"将 AWS WAF 日志发送到 Amazon S3。创建一个带有分区投影的 Amazon Athena 表，并使用 Athena 查询日志。","D":"将 AWS WAF 日志发送到 AWS CloudTrail，并使用 Amazon Athena 进行分析。"},"answer":["C"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Security/IAM","Storage","Monitoring/Ops","Analytics"],"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選","research":{"verdict":["C"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"both","explanation_en":"AWS WAF supports exactly three logging destinations: Amazon CloudWatch Logs, Amazon S3, and Amazon Data Firehose. AWS CloudTrail is NOT a valid AWS WAF log destination (CloudTrail records API/management-plane events, not WAF web-request traffic logs), which eliminates options A and D. Between the two S3-based options, Amazon Athena is the AWS-documented, serverless service for querying WAF logs directly in place in S3 using SQL; the Athena User Guide even provides CREATE TABLE statements specifically for AWS WAF logs using partition projection, which improves performance and lowers cost for time-partitioned log data. Option B is wrong because Amazon OpenSearch Service cannot query objects in S3 'directly' — logs must be ingested/indexed into OpenSearch first (typically via Firehose or a pipeline), so it does not query S3 directly as stated. Therefore option C (S3 + Athena table with partition projection) is the correct and directly supported solution for analyzing WAF traffic to determine if application-layer attacks are occurring.","explanation_zh":"AWS WAF 只支援三種日誌目的地：Amazon CloudWatch Logs、Amazon S3、以及 Amazon Data Firehose。AWS CloudTrail 並不是有效的 WAF 日誌目的地（CloudTrail 記錄的是 API/管理層級事件，而非 WAF 的 web 請求流量日誌），因此可直接刪除選項 A 與 D。在兩個以 S3 為基礎的選項中，Amazon Athena 是 AWS 官方文件所記載、可直接在 S3 原地以 SQL 查詢 WAF 日誌的無伺服器服務；Athena 使用者指南甚至專門為 AWS WAF 日誌提供使用 partition projection 的 CREATE TABLE 範例，對於依時間分割的日誌資料能提升效能並降低成本。選項 B 錯誤，因為 Amazon OpenSearch Service 無法『直接』查詢 S3 中的物件——日誌必須先被匯入/索引到 OpenSearch（通常透過 Firehose 或資料管線），並非如題所述直接查詢 S3。因此選項 C（S3 + 使用 partition projection 的 Athena 資料表）才是分析 WAF 流量以判斷是否發生應用層攻擊的正確且有官方支援的方案。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"AWS CloudTrail is not a valid AWS WAF logging destination (only CloudWatch Logs, S3, and Firehose are). CloudTrail records API events, not WAF web-request traffic. You also cannot point OpenSearch at CloudTrail this way.","why_zh":"AWS CloudTrail 不是有效的 AWS WAF 日誌目的地（只有 CloudWatch Logs、S3、Firehose）。CloudTrail 記錄的是 API 事件，而非 WAF 的 web 請求流量，且無法以此方式讓 OpenSearch 分析。"},{"letter":"B","why_en":"Amazon OpenSearch Service cannot query logs 'directly' in S3; WAF logs must first be ingested and indexed into OpenSearch (e.g., via Firehose). Athena, not OpenSearch, is the native serverless tool that queries S3 data in place.","why_zh":"Amazon OpenSearch Service 無法『直接』查詢 S3 中的日誌；WAF 日誌必須先被匯入並索引到 OpenSearch（例如透過 Firehose）。能直接原地查詢 S3 資料的原生無伺服器工具是 Athena，而非 OpenSearch。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"Same fatal flaw as A: AWS WAF cannot send logs to AWS CloudTrail. Even though Athena is the right query tool, the log destination is invalid, so this solution cannot be implemented.","why_zh":"與 A 相同的致命缺陷：AWS WAF 無法將日誌送到 AWS CloudTrail。即使 Athena 是正確的查詢工具，但日誌目的地無效，此方案根本無法實作。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/waf/latest/developerguide/logging-destinations.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/athena/latest/ug/waf-logs.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/athena/latest/ug/create-waf-table.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/waf/latest/developerguide/logging-s3.html"]}},{"id":154,"question_en":"A company uses AWS Organizations. The company subscribes to AWS Shield Advanced. The company must share third-party firewall logs from all its accounts with the Shield Response Team. The company stores the logs in an Amazon S3 bucket that uses server-side encryption with S3 managed keys (SSE-S3). Which combination of steps will meet these requirements? (Select TWO.)","question_zh":"一家公司使用 AWS Organizations，并订阅了 AWS Shield Advanced 服务。该公司需要将其所有账户 中的第三方防火墙日志共享给 Shield 响应团队。这些日志存储在使用 S3 管理密钥（SSE-S3）进行服 务器端加密的 Amazon S3 存储桶中。 哪两个步骤的组合可以满足这些要求？（选择两项。）","options_en":{"A":"Use the aws shield associate-drt-log-bucket command to grant the Shield Response Team access to the bucket.","B":"Configure multi-account support by creating a delegated administrator account for Shield Advanced.","C":"In the delegated administrator account, configure Shield Advanced to forward events to AWS Security Hub CSPM.","D":"Create an IAM role and attach the AWSShieldDRTAccessPolicy policy. Create a trust policy with the drt.shield.amazonaws.com service principal.","E":"Configure auto-enable preferences in Organizations to enable Shield Advanced as the organization adds new member accounts."},"options_zh":{"A":"使用 aws shield associate-drt-log-bucket 命令授予 Shield 响应团队对存储桶的访问权限。","B":"通过为 Shield Advanced 创建委派管理员账户来配置多账户支持。","C":"在委派管理员账户中，配置 Shield Advanced 将事件转发至 AWS Security Hub CSPM。","D":"创建一个 IAM 角色并附加 AWSShieldDRTAccessPolicy 策略。创建一个信任策略，其中包含 服务主体 drt.shield.amazonaws.com。","E":"在组织中配置自动启用偏好设置，以便在组织添加新成员账户时自动启用 Shield Advanced。"},"answer":["A","D"],"multi":true,"vote":{},"tags":["Organizations/Governance","Security/IAM","Storage"],"difficulty":2,"diff_why":"複選","research":{"verdict":["A","D"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"both","explanation_en":"To share third-party firewall logs stored in S3 with the Shield Response Team (SRT/DRT), two things are required. First (D), you must authorize the SRT at the account level by creating an IAM role, attaching the AWS managed policy AWSShieldDRTAccessPolicy, and giving it a trust policy for the drt.shield.amazonaws.com service principal; this is the AssociateDRTRole operation that lets the SRT act in your account. Second (A), you grant the SRT read access to the specific S3 bucket holding the non-WAF logs (packet captures, ALB/CloudFront, or third-party logs) using the AssociateDRTLogBucket API / the 'aws shield associate-drt-log-bucket --log-bucket <name>' CLI command, which adds s3:GetBucketLocation, s3:GetObject, and s3:ListBucket for the SRT. The AWS docs explicitly state the log bucket can be plaintext or SSE-S3 encrypted (but NOT AWS KMS encrypted), which exactly matches the SSE-S3 bucket in the question, so the log-bucket association approach works. Options B, C, and E concern Shield Advanced organization-wide management (delegated admin, Security Hub event forwarding, and auto-enable for new member accounts) and have nothing to do with granting the SRT access to logs.","explanation_zh":"要把存放在 S3 的第三方防火牆日誌分享給 Shield Response Team（SRT/DRT），需要兩個步驟。第一（D）：先在帳戶層級授權 SRT——建立一個 IAM role、附掛 AWS 受管政策 AWSShieldDRTAccessPolicy，並設定信任 drt.shield.amazonaws.com service principal 的信任政策；這對應 AssociateDRTRole 操作，讓 SRT 能在你的帳戶內代為操作。第二（A）：用 AssociateDRTLogBucket API（或 CLI 指令 'aws shield associate-drt-log-bucket --log-bucket <名稱>'）授予 SRT 對特定 S3 bucket 的讀取權限（封包擷取、ALB/CloudFront、或第三方日誌），此動作會加上 s3:GetBucketLocation、s3:GetObject、s3:ListBucket。AWS 官方文件明確指出該日誌 bucket 可以是純文字或 SSE-S3 加密（但不可用 AWS KMS 加密），這正好符合題目中的 SSE-S3 bucket，因此此方法可行。B、C、E 屬於 Shield Advanced 組織層級管理（delegated admin、Security Hub 事件轉發、對新成員帳戶自動啟用），與授權 SRT 存取日誌無關。","distractors":[{"letter":"B","why_en":"Creating a Shield Advanced delegated administrator enables centralized organization-wide management of Shield Advanced subscriptions/protections; it does not share firewall logs with the Shield Response Team.","why_zh":"建立 Shield Advanced delegated administrator 是為了集中管理整個組織的 Shield Advanced 訂閱與防護，並不會把防火牆日誌分享給 Shield Response Team。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"Forwarding Shield Advanced events to AWS Security Hub CSPM aggregates findings for the customer's own visibility; it does not grant the SRT access to the S3 firewall logs.","why_zh":"把 Shield Advanced 事件轉發到 AWS Security Hub CSPM 只是為了客戶自己彙整檢視結果，並不會讓 SRT 取得 S3 中的防火牆日誌存取權。"},{"letter":"E","why_en":"Configuring auto-enable in Organizations automatically turns on Shield Advanced for newly added member accounts (onboarding automation); it is unrelated to giving the SRT access to logs.","why_zh":"在 Organizations 設定 auto-enable 只是讓新加入的成員帳戶自動啟用 Shield Advanced（自動導入），與授予 SRT 日誌存取權無關。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/waf/latest/developerguide/ddos-srt-access.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/waf/latest/developerguide/authorize-srt.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/waf/latest/developerguide/shd-security-iam-awsmanpol.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/cli/v1/userguide/cli_shield_code_examples.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/waf/latest/DDOSAPIReference/API_AssociateDRTRole.html"]}},{"id":155,"question_en":"A security engineer recently rotated the host keys for an Amazon EC2 instance. The security engineer is trying to access the EC2 instance by using the EC2 Instance Connect feature. However, the security engineer receives an error for failed host key validation. Before the rotation of the host keys, EC2 Instance Connect worked correctly with this EC2 instance. What should the security engineer do to resolve this error?","question_zh":"一名安全工程师最近轮换了Amazon EC2实例的主机密钥。该工程师尝试使用EC2实例连接功能访问该EC2实例，但收到了主 机密钥验证失败的错误信息。在轮换主机密钥之前，EC2实例连接功能可以正常用于此EC2实例。 安全工程师应采取什么措施来解决此错误？","options_en":{"A":"Import the key material into AWS Key Management Service (AWS KMS).","B":"Manually upload the new host key to the AWS trusted host keys database.","C":"Ensure that the AmazonSSMManagedInstanceCore policy is attached to the EC2 instance profile.","D":"Create a new SSH key pair for the EC2 instance."},"options_zh":{"A":"将密钥材料导入 AWS 密钥管理服务（AWS KMS）。","B":"手动将新的主机密钥上传至 AWS 可信主机密钥数据库。","C":"确保将 AmazonSSMManagedInstanceCore 策略附加到 EC2 实例配置文件。","D":"为 EC2 实例创建新的 SSH 密钥对。"},"answer":["B"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Security/IAM","Compute","Database"],"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選","research":{"verdict":["B"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"This is a textbook scenario documented verbatim in the EC2 troubleshooting guide under 'Error: Host key validation failed for EC2 Instance Connect'. When you rotate an instance's host keys, the new host keys are NOT automatically uploaded to the AWS trusted host keys database, so EC2 Instance Connect's host key validation fails on subsequent connections. The remedy is to get the new host key into that trusted host keys database (AWS provides the eic_harvest_hostkeys script to do this automatically). Option B captures exactly this root cause and fix: upload the new host key to the AWS trusted host keys database. The other options address unrelated mechanisms - KMS key material, SSM Session Manager IAM permissions, and user-authentication SSH key pairs - none of which affect instance host key validation.","explanation_zh":"這是 EC2 疑難排解文件中「Error: Host key validation failed for EC2 Instance Connect」段落逐字記載的典型情境。當你輪替(rotate)執行個體的 host key 後，新的 host key 不會自動上傳到 AWS trusted host keys database，因此 EC2 Instance Connect 在後續連線時 host key 驗證會失敗。解法就是把新的 host key 送進該 trusted host keys database(AWS 提供 eic_harvest_hostkeys 指令稿自動完成此動作)。選項 B 正好對應這個根因與修法:把新的 host key 上傳到 AWS trusted host keys database。其餘選項涉及無關的機制 - KMS 金鑰材料、SSM Session Manager 的 IAM 權限、以及用於使用者驗證的 SSH key pair - 都與執行個體的 host key 驗證無關。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"Importing key material into AWS KMS is for envelope encryption / customer-managed KMS keys and has nothing to do with SSH host keys or EC2 Instance Connect host key validation.","why_zh":"把金鑰材料匯入 AWS KMS 是用於信封加密/客戶管理的 KMS 金鑰,與 SSH host key 或 EC2 Instance Connect 的 host key 驗證毫無關係。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"The AmazonSSMManagedInstanceCore policy enables AWS Systems Manager Session Manager, a different connection method. It does not affect EC2 Instance Connect's host key validation against the AWS trusted host keys database.","why_zh":"AmazonSSMManagedInstanceCore 政策是啟用 AWS Systems Manager Session Manager(另一種連線方式),不影響 EC2 Instance Connect 對 AWS trusted host keys database 的 host key 驗證。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"An SSH key pair is used for USER authentication (client identity), not the instance's HOST key (server identity). Creating a new key pair does not update the rotated host key in the AWS trusted host keys database, so the validation error would persist.","why_zh":"SSH key pair 是用於「使用者」驗證(用戶端身分),不是執行個體的「host key」(伺服器身分)。建立新的 key pair 不會更新 AWS trusted host keys database 中被輪替的 host key,驗證錯誤仍會持續。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AWSEC2/latest/UserGuide/TroubleshootingInstancesConnecting.html"]}},{"id":156,"question_en":"A company has contracted with a third party to audit several AWS accounts. To enable the audit, cross- account IAM roles have been created in each account targeted for audit. The auditor is having trouble accessing some of the accounts. Which of the following may be causing this problem? (Select THREE.)","question_zh":"一家公司已与第三方签订合同，对其多个AWS账户进行审计。为便于审计，已在每个目标账户中创建了跨账户的IAM 角色。但审计人员在访问部分账户时遇到了问题。 以下哪几项可能导致此问题？（选择三项。）","options_en":{"A":"The external ID used by the auditor is missing or incorrect.","B":"The auditor is using the incorrect password.","C":"The auditor has not been grantedsts:AssumeRolefor the role in the destination account.","D":"The Amazon EC2 role used by the auditor must be set to the destination account role.","E":"The secret key used by the auditor is missing or incorrect.","F":"The role ARN used by the auditor is missing or incorrect."},"options_zh":{"A":"审计员使用的外部ID缺失或错误。","B":"审计员使用了错误的密码。","C":"审计员未被授予目标账户中该角色的 AssumeRole 权限。","D":"审计员使用的 Amazon EC2 角色必须设置为目标账户的角色。","E":"审计员使用的密钥缺失或错误。","F":"审计师使用的ARN角色缺失或错误。"},"answer":["A","C","F"],"multi":true,"vote":{},"tags":["Security/IAM","Compute"],"difficulty":2,"diff_why":"複選","research":{"verdict":["A","C","F"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"For a third party (the auditor) to assume a cross-account IAM role, AWS documentation identifies exactly the pieces that A, C, and F address. (A) The external ID: the account owner puts an sts:ExternalId condition in the role's trust policy to prevent the confused-deputy problem, and 'the third party must provide this ID when they assume the role' - if it is missing or wrong, AssumeRole is denied. (F) The role ARN: 'After you create the role, you must provide the role's ARN to the third party. They require your role's ARN in order to assume the role' - a missing/incorrect ARN means the auditor cannot target the correct role. (C) The sts:AssumeRole permission: assuming a cross-account role requires BOTH a trust policy on the destination role AND an identity-based policy on the auditor's source-account principal granting sts:AssumeRole on that role; without it the call fails. Because these three items are configured per target account, they cleanly explain why the auditor can reach some accounts but not others.","explanation_zh":"第三方稽核員要 assume 跨帳號 IAM 角色時，AWS 官方文件所列的必要條件正好對應 A、C、F。(A) External ID：帳號擁有者在角色的 trust policy 加上 sts:ExternalId 條件以防止 confused deputy 問題，第三方 assume 角色時必須提供此 ID，缺少或錯誤會被拒絕。(F) 角色 ARN：文件明確指出建立角色後必須把角色的 ARN 提供給第三方，他們需要此 ARN 才能 assume 角色，ARN 缺漏或錯誤就無法指向正確角色。(C) sts:AssumeRole 權限：跨帳號 assume 角色同時需要目標角色的 trust policy 以及來源帳號 principal 的 identity-based policy 授予 sts:AssumeRole，缺少此權限呼叫即失敗。這三項都是逐一針對每個目標帳號設定，正好解釋為何稽核員能存取部分帳號卻無法存取其他帳號。","distractors":[{"letter":"B","why_en":"Cross-account role assumption uses the caller's existing IAM credentials/session to call sts:AssumeRole; there is no password entered against the destination account, so an 'incorrect password' is not a cause.","why_zh":"跨帳號 assume 角色是用呼叫者現有的 IAM 憑證/session 呼叫 sts:AssumeRole，並不會對目標帳號輸入密碼，因此『密碼錯誤』不是原因。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"This is a fabricated requirement. There is no rule that an EC2 instance role must be 'set to' the destination account role; cross-account access is governed by trust policy + sts:AssumeRole permission, not by pointing an EC2 role at another role.","why_zh":"此為杜撰的需求。並無『EC2 執行個體角色必須設定為目標帳號角色』的規則；跨帳號存取是由 trust policy 與 sts:AssumeRole 權限控制，而非把 EC2 角色指向另一角色。"},{"letter":"E","why_en":"The auditor authenticates with their own source-account credentials to call AssumeRole; you never supply the destination account's secret key. A globally missing secret key would break all calls, whereas the scenario is failure on only some accounts, which is explained by the per-account items (external ID, role ARN, AssumeRole permission).","why_zh":"稽核員是用自己來源帳號的憑證呼叫 AssumeRole，從不需要提供目標帳號的 secret key。若 secret key 全面缺失會導致所有呼叫失敗，但題目是只在部分帳號失敗，這由逐帳號設定的項目（external ID、角色 ARN、AssumeRole 權限）來解釋。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/IAM/latest/UserGuide/id_roles_common-scenarios_third-party.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/IAM/latest/UserGuide/confused-deputy.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/IAM/latest/UserGuide/tutorial_cross-account-with-roles.html"]}},{"id":157,"question_en":"A company wants to establish separate AWS Key Management Service (AWS KMS) keys to use for different AWS services. The company ' s security engineer created the following key policy to allow the infrastructure deployment team to create encrypted Amazon Elastic Block Store (Amazon EBS) volumes by assuming the InfrastructureDeployment IAM role: { \" Version \" : \" 2012-10-17 \" , \" Id \" : \" key-policy-ebs \" , \" Statement \" : [ { \" Sid \" : \" Enable IAM User Permissions \" , \" Effect \" : \" Allow \" , \" Principal \" : { \" AWS \" : \" arn:aws:iam::123456789012:root \" }, \" Action \" : \" kms:* \" , \" Resource \" : \" * \" }, { \" Sid \" : \" Allow use of the key \" , \" Effect \" : \" Allow \" , \" Principal \" : { \" AWS \" : \" arn:aws:iam::123456789012:role/aws-reserved/sso.amazonaws.com/InfrastructureDeployment \" }, \" Action \" : [ \" kms:Encrypt \" , \" kms:Decrypt \" , \" kms:ReEncrypt* \" ,\" kms:GenerateDataKey* \" , \" kms:DescribeKey \" , \" kms:CreateGrant \" , \" kms:ListGrants \" , \" kms:RevokeGrant \" ], \" Resource \" : \" * \" , \" Condition \" : { \" StringEquals \" : { \" kms:ViaService \" : \" ec2.us-west-2.amazonaws.com \" } } } ] } The security engineer recently discovered that IAM rolesother thanthe InfrastructureDeployment role used this key for other services. Which change to the policy should the security engineer make to resolve these issues?","question_zh":"一家公司希望为不同的 AWS 服务建立独立的 AWS 密钥管理服务（AWS KMS）密钥。该公司的安全工程师创建了以下密钥 策略，以允许基础设施部署团队通过担任 InfrastructureDeployment IAM 角色来创建加密的 Amazon 弹性块存储（Amazon EBS） 卷： } ] } 安全工程师最近发现，除基础设施部署角色外，其他IAM角色也使用了此密钥来访问其他服务。 安全工程师应做出哪项策略调整来解决这些问题？","options_en":{"A":"In the statement block that contains the Sid \" Allow use of the key \" , under theConditionblock, change StringEquals to StringLike.","B":"In the policy document, remove the statement block that contains the Sid \" Enable IAM User Permissions \" . Add key management policies to the KMS policy.","C":"In the statement block that contains the Sid \" Allow use of the key \" , under theConditionblock, change the kms:ViaService value to ec2.us-east-1.amazonaws.com.","D":"In the policy document, add a new statement block that grants the kms:Disable* permission to the security engineer ' s IAM role."},"options_zh":{"A":"在包含 Sid “允许使用密钥”的语句块中，将 Condition 块下的 StringEquals 改为 StringLike。","B":"在策略文档中，移除包含 Sid “Enable IAM User Permissions”的语句块。将密钥管理 策略添加到 KMS 策略中。","C":"在包含“允许使用密钥”这一语句块的条件块下，将 kms:ViaService 的值更改为 ec2.us-east-1. amazonaws.com。","D":"在策略文档中添加一个新的声明块，授予安全工程师的 IAM 角色 kms:Disable* 权限。"},"answer":["A"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Security/IAM","Storage","Compute"],"difficulty":2,"diff_why":"題庫與社群皆錯","research":{"verdict":["B"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"neither","explanation_en":"The root cause is the first statement, 'Enable IAM User Permissions', which sets the principal to the account root ARN (arn:aws:iam::123456789012:root) with Action kms:*. Per the AWS KMS default key policy documentation, this statement does not grant any specific principal access; instead it enables the account to use IAM policies to DELEGATE access to the key. That means any IAM role in the account whose IAM policy allows KMS actions on this key can use it - which is exactly why 'IAM roles other than InfrastructureDeployment' are using it. To restrict the key to only the InfrastructureDeployment role, you must remove (or scope down) this broad root-delegation statement so that authorization comes only from the explicit key-policy statements, while re-adding proper key management statements so the key does not become unmanageable. Option B does this. Option A (StringEquals -> StringLike) only touches the second, InfrastructureDeployment-specific statement and actually LOOSENS the kms:ViaService match; it does nothing to the root-delegation statement that grants the unwanted access. The dump's suggested answer A is therefore wrong.","explanation_zh":"問題根源是第一個語句 'Enable IAM User Permissions'，其 Principal 設為帳戶 root ARN（arn:aws:iam::123456789012:root）且 Action 為 kms:*。依 AWS KMS 預設金鑰政策文件，此語句本身不授予任何特定 principal 存取權，而是讓帳戶得以透過 IAM policy 來『委派（delegate）』對此金鑰的存取。因此帳戶內任何在 IAM policy 中被允許操作此金鑰的角色都能使用它，這正是『InfrastructureDeployment 以外的 IAM 角色』能使用此金鑰的原因。要讓金鑰僅限 InfrastructureDeployment 角色，必須移除（或收斂）這條寬鬆的 root 委派語句，讓授權只來自明確列出 principal 的金鑰政策語句，同時補回適當的金鑰管理語句以免金鑰變得無法管理。選項 B 正是如此。選項 A（StringEquals 改 StringLike）只動到第二個 InfrastructureDeployment 專用語句，且實際上還放寬了 kms:ViaService 的比對，對造成非預期存取的 root 委派語句毫無作用。因此 dump 建議答案 A 是錯的。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"This changes only the second (InfrastructureDeployment) statement's condition from StringEquals to StringLike, which loosens the kms:ViaService match rather than tightening it. The unwanted access comes from the first root-delegation statement, which this change does not touch, so it does not stop other roles from using the key.","why_zh":"此選項只把第二個（InfrastructureDeployment）語句的條件由 StringEquals 改為 StringLike，實際是放寬 kms:ViaService 比對而非收緊。非預期存取源自第一個 root 委派語句，此變更完全沒碰到，故無法阻止其他角色使用金鑰。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"Changing the kms:ViaService value to ec2.us-east-1.amazonaws.com only alters the region in the second statement and would actually break legitimate us-west-2 usage. It does nothing about the root-delegation statement that grants the unwanted cross-role access.","why_zh":"把 kms:ViaService 改為 ec2.us-east-1.amazonaws.com 只是更動第二個語句的區域，反而會破壞合法的 us-west-2 使用，且對造成非預期跨角色存取的 root 委派語句毫無影響。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"Granting kms:Disable* to the security engineer's role is unrelated to the problem. It gives an admin the ability to disable the key but does nothing to prevent other IAM roles from using the key via IAM-policy delegation.","why_zh":"授予安全工程師角色 kms:Disable* 與問題無關；它只是讓管理者能停用金鑰，完全無法阻止其他 IAM 角色透過 IAM policy 委派使用此金鑰。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/kms/latest/developerguide/key-policy-default.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/kms/latest/developerguide/key-policies.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/kms/latest/developerguide/conditions-kms.html#conditions-kms-via-service"]}},{"id":158,"question_en":"A company runs an application on a fleet of Amazon EC2 instances. The company can remove instances from the fleet without risk to the application. All EC2 instances use the same security group named ProdFleet. Amazon GuardDuty and AWS Config are active in the company ' s AWS account. A security engineer needs to provide a solution that will prevent an EC2 instance from sending outbound traffic if GuardDuty generates a cryptocurrency finding event. The security engineer creates a new security group named Isolate that contains no outbound rules. The security engineer configures an AWS Lambda function to remove an EC2 instance from the ProdFleet security group and add it to the Isolate security group. Which additional step will meet this requirement?","question_zh":"一家公司在一个由多个Amazon EC2实例组成的机群上运行应用程序。该公司可以安全地从机群中移除实例，而不会影响应用程序的 正常运行。所有EC2实例均使用名为ProdFleet的相同安全组。该公司的AWS账户已启用Amazon GuardDuty和AWS Config服务。 安全工程师需要提供一种解决方案，以防止当 GuardDuty 生成加密货币发现事件时，EC2 实例发送出站流量。该安全工程师创建了一 个名为 Isolate 的新安全组，其中不包含任何出站规则，并配置了一个 AWS Lambda 函数，用于将 EC2 实例从 ProdFleet 安全组中移除， 并添加到 Isolate 安全组中。 哪一步额外操作可以满足这一要求？","options_en":{"A":"Configure GuardDuty to directly invoke the Lambda function if GuardDuty generates a CryptoCurrency:EC2/* finding event.","B":"Configure an AWS Config rule that invokes the Lambda function if a CryptoCurrency:EC2/* configuration change event occurs for an EC2 instance.","C":"Configure an Amazon EventBridge rule that invokes the Lambda function if GuardDuty generates a CryptoCurrency:EC2/* finding event.","D":"Configure an Amazon EventBridge rule that invokes the Lambda function if AWS Config detects a CryptoCurrency:EC2/* configuration change event for an EC2 instance."},"options_zh":{"A":"配置 GuardDuty，当 GuardDuty 生成 CryptoCurrency:EC2/* 类型的发现事件时，直接调用 Lambda 函数。","B":"配置一个 AWS Config 规则，当 EC2 实例发生 CryptoCurrency:EC2/* 配置变更事件时，调用该 Lambda 函数。","C":"配置一个 Amazon EventBridge 规则，当 GuardDuty 生成 CryptoCurrency:EC2/* 类型的发现事件时，调用该 Lambda 函数。","D":"配置一个 Amazon EventBridge 规则，当 AWS Config 检测到 EC2 实例发生 CryptoCurrency:EC2/* 配置变更事件时，调用该 Lambda 函数。"},"answer":["C"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Organizations/Governance","Security/IAM","Compute","Serverless/Integration"],"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選","research":{"verdict":["C"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"both","explanation_en":"GuardDuty does not invoke Lambda directly; it automatically publishes every finding (including CryptoCurrency:EC2/* finding types) as an event to Amazon EventBridge with source 'aws.guardduty' and detail-type 'GuardDuty Finding'. To automate a response, you create an EventBridge rule whose event pattern matches the desired GuardDuty finding type and whose target is the Lambda function that swaps the instance from the ProdFleet security group into the Isolate security group. Option C describes exactly this supported integration. AWS Config only tracks resource configuration changes and compliance state; a cryptocurrency finding is a GuardDuty threat detection, not a Config configuration-change event, so there is no such thing as a 'CryptoCurrency:EC2/* configuration change event' in AWS Config.","explanation_zh":"GuardDuty 不會直接呼叫 Lambda；它會自動將每一筆 finding（包含 CryptoCurrency:EC2/* 類型）以 source 為 'aws.guardduty'、detail-type 為 'GuardDuty Finding' 的事件發布到 Amazon EventBridge。要自動化回應，須建立一條 EventBridge rule，其 event pattern 比對目標 GuardDuty finding 類型，target 設為那個把執行個體從 ProdFleet security group 換到 Isolate security group 的 Lambda function。選項 C 正是這個受支援的整合方式。AWS Config 只追蹤資源設定變更與合規狀態；cryptocurrency finding 是 GuardDuty 的威脅偵測結果，而非 Config 的組態變更事件，因此 AWS Config 根本不存在所謂的 'CryptoCurrency:EC2/* configuration change event'。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"GuardDuty has no capability to directly invoke a Lambda function based on a finding type. Its documented automation path is to publish findings to EventBridge and let an EventBridge rule target Lambda.","why_zh":"GuardDuty 沒有依 finding 類型直接呼叫 Lambda function 的功能。官方記載的自動化路徑是將 findings 發布到 EventBridge，再由 EventBridge rule 以 Lambda 為 target。"},{"letter":"B","why_en":"AWS Config detects resource configuration changes and evaluates compliance rules; it does not receive or act on GuardDuty finding types. There is no 'CryptoCurrency:EC2/* configuration change event' in AWS Config.","why_zh":"AWS Config 偵測資源組態變更並評估合規規則，並不會接收或處理 GuardDuty 的 finding 類型。AWS Config 中不存在 'CryptoCurrency:EC2/* configuration change event'。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"AWS Config does not detect GuardDuty findings; a cryptocurrency finding is a GuardDuty threat detection, not a Config configuration-change event. The correct event source is GuardDuty via EventBridge, not AWS Config.","why_zh":"AWS Config 不會偵測 GuardDuty findings；cryptocurrency finding 是 GuardDuty 的威脅偵測，而非 Config 的組態變更事件。正確的事件來源是透過 EventBridge 的 GuardDuty，而非 AWS Config。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/guardduty/latest/ug/guardduty_findings_eventbridge.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/guardduty/latest/ug/guardduty_finding-types-active.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/config/latest/developerguide/WhatIsConfig.html"]}},{"id":159,"question_en":"A company is operating an open-source software platform that is internet facing. The legacy software platform no longer receives security updates. The software platform operates using Amazon Route 53 weighted load balancing to send traffic to two Amazon EC2 instances that connect to an Amazon RDS cluster. A recent report suggests this software platform is vulnerable to SQL injection attacks, with samples of attacks provided. The company’s security engineer must secure this system against SQL injection attacks within 24 hours. The security engineer’s solution must involve the least amount of effort and maintain normal operations during implementation. What should the security engineer do to meet these requirements?","question_zh":"一家公司正在运营一个面向互联网的开源软件平台。该旧版软件平台已不再接收安全更新。该平台通 过 Amazon Route 53 的加权负载均衡，将流量分发至两个连接到 Amazon RDS 集群的 Amazon EC2 实 例。最近的一份报告指出，该软件平台存在 SQL 注入攻击漏洞，并提供了攻击示例。公司的安全工 程师必须在 24 小时内保护该系统免受 SQL 注入攻击。安全工程师的解决方案需以最小的工作量实现， 并确保实施过程中业务正常运行。 安全工程师应采取哪些措施来满足这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Create an Application Load Balancer with the existing EC2 instances as a target group. Create an AWS WAF web ACL containing rules that protect the application from this attack, then apply it to the ALB. Test to ensure the vulnerability has been mitigated, then redirect the Route 53 records to point to the ALB. Update security groups on the EC2 instances to prevent direct access from the internet.","B":"Create an Amazon CloudFront distribution specifying one EC2 instance as an origin. Create an AWS WAF web ACL containing rules that protect the application from this attack, then apply it to the distribution. Test to ensure the vulnerability has been mitigated, then redirect the Route 53 records to point to CloudFront.","C":"Obtain the latest source code for the platform and make the necessary updates. Test the updated code to ensure that the vulnerability has been mitigated, then deploy the patched version of the platform to the EC2 instances.","D":"Update the security group that is attached to the EC2 instances, removing access from the internet to the TCP port used by the SQL database. Create an AWS WAF web ACL containing rules that protect the application from this attack, then apply it to the EC2 instances. Test to ensure the vulnerability has been mitigated, then restore the security group to the original setting."},"options_zh":{"A":"创建一个应用负载均衡器（ALB），并将现有的 EC2 实例作为目标组。创建一个包含防护规则 的 AWS WAF 网站访问控制列表（web ACL），以保护应用程序免受此类攻击，然后将其应 用于 ALB。测试以确保漏洞已被缓解，随后将 Route 53 记录指向该 ALB。更新 EC2 实例的 安全组，防止互联网直接访问。","B":"创建一个 Amazon CloudFront 分发，指定一个 EC2 实例作为源站。创建一个 AWS WAF 网络 ACL，并包含保护应用程序免受此类攻击的规则，然后将其应用到该分发上。测试以确保 漏洞已得到缓解，随后将 Route 53 记录指向 CloudFront。","C":"获取平台的最新源代码并进行必要的更新。测试更新后的代码，确保漏洞已得到缓解，然后将 修复后的平台版本部署到EC2实例上。","D":"更新附加到 EC2 实例的安全组，移除互联网对 SQL 数据库所用 TCP 端口的访问权限。创建一 个包含保护应用程序免受此类攻击规则的 AWS WAF 网站 ACL，然后将其应用到 EC2 实例上。 测试以确保漏洞已得到缓解，再将安全组恢复至原始设置。"},"answer":["A"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Networking/DNS","Security/IAM","Compute","Database"],"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選","research":{"verdict":["A"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"AWS WAF provides SQL injection protection through the AWSManagedRulesSQLiRuleSet managed rule group and SQLi match rule statements, so a WAF-based mitigation is the fastest, lowest-effort fix for a legacy platform that can no longer be patched. The decisive constraint is that an AWS WAF web ACL can only be associated with a fixed set of resources: CloudFront distributions, Application Load Balancers, API Gateway REST APIs, AppSync GraphQL APIs, Cognito user pools, App Runner services, Bedrock AgentCore Gateway, Verified Access instances, and Amplify. EC2 instances are NOT in that list, so WAF cannot be attached directly to EC2. Option A fronts the existing two EC2 instances with an Application Load Balancer (a supported WAF target), attaches a web ACL with SQLi rules, tests it, then repoints Route 53 to the ALB and locks the EC2 security groups so the internet can only reach the app through the WAF-protected ALB. This maintains normal operations (the ALB path is built and validated before the Route 53 cutover, and both instances stay in service) with the least effort. Option A is correct.","explanation_zh":"AWS WAF 透過 AWSManagedRulesSQLiRuleSet 受管規則群組與 SQLi match rule statement 提供 SQL injection 防護，對於已無法再套用安全更新的老舊平台而言，這是最快、最省力的緩解方式。決定性限制在於：AWS WAF web ACL 只能關聯到固定的資源清單——CloudFront distribution、Application Load Balancer、API Gateway REST API、AppSync GraphQL API、Cognito user pool、App Runner service、Bedrock AgentCore Gateway、Verified Access instance 與 Amplify。EC2 instance 不在此清單內，因此 WAF 無法直接套用到 EC2。選項 A 用 Application Load Balancer（WAF 支援的目標）承接現有兩台 EC2 instance，掛上含 SQLi 規則的 web ACL，測試後再把 Route 53 指向 ALB，並收緊 EC2 security group，使外網只能經由受 WAF 保護的 ALB 進入應用。此作法在維持正常運作（先建置並驗證 ALB 路徑再切換 Route 53，兩台 instance 皆持續服務）下所需工作量最少。正解為 A。","distractors":[{"letter":"B","why_en":"CloudFront does support WAF and SQLi rules, but specifying only ONE EC2 instance as the origin discards the existing Route 53 weighted load balancing across two instances, breaking high availability and creating a single point of failure. It does not maintain normal operations and is inferior to the ALB approach that keeps both instances in service.","why_zh":"CloudFront 確實支援 WAF 與 SQLi 規則，但只指定「一台」EC2 instance 為 origin，會放棄現有橫跨兩台 instance 的 Route 53 加權負載平衡，破壞高可用性並造成單點故障，無法維持正常運作，劣於同時保留兩台 instance 的 ALB 方案。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"The platform is legacy and no longer receives security updates. Obtaining source, patching, testing and redeploying is high effort and high risk, and is unlikely to be feasible within 24 hours. It directly violates the 'least amount of effort' requirement.","why_zh":"該平台為老舊系統且已不再收到安全更新。取得原始碼、修補、測試再重新部署工作量與風險都高，且不太可能在 24 小時內完成，直接違反「工作量最少」的要求。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"Technically impossible: a WAF web ACL cannot be associated directly with an EC2 instance (EC2 is not a supported WAF resource). Also, removing the SQL DB port from the security group does nothing against SQL injection, which enters through the web application layer, not by connecting to the DB port; temporarily toggling then restoring the security group is meaningless.","why_zh":"技術上不可行：WAF web ACL 無法直接關聯到 EC2 instance（EC2 不是 WAF 支援的資源）。此外，從 security group 移除 SQL 資料庫連接埠對 SQL injection 毫無作用，因為 SQLi 是經由 Web 應用層進入，而非直接連到資料庫連接埠；暫時調整後又還原 security group 也毫無意義。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/waf/latest/developerguide/how-aws-waf-works-resources.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/waf/latest/developerguide/web-acl-associating-aws-resource.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/waf/latest/developerguide/aws-managed-rule-groups-use-case.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/waf/latest/developerguide/waf-rule-statement-type-sqli-match.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/elasticloadbalancing/latest/application/load-balancer-integrations.html"]}},{"id":160,"question_en":"A company is operating an open-source software platform that is internet facing. The legacy software platform no longer receives security updates. The software platform operates using Amazon Route 53 weighted load balancing to send traffic to two Amazon EC2 instances that connect to an Amazon RDS cluster. A recent report suggests this software platform is vulnerable to SQL injection attacks, with samples of attacks provided. The company ' s security engineer must secure this system against SQL injection attacks within 24 hours. The solution must involve the least amount of effort and maintain normal operations during implementation. What should the security engineer do to meet these requirements?","question_zh":"一家公司正在运营一个面向互联网的开源软件平台。该旧版软件平台已不再接收安全更新。该平台通 过 Amazon Route 53 的加权负载均衡，将流量分发至两个连接到 Amazon RDS 集群的 Amazon EC2 实 例。最近的一份报告指出，该软件平台存在 SQL 注入攻击漏洞，并提供了攻击示例。公司的安全工 程师必须在 24 小时内保护该系统免受 SQL 注入攻击。解决方案需尽可能减少工作量，并在实施期间 保持正常运行。 安全工程师应采取哪些措施来满足这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Create an Application Load Balancer with the existing EC2 instances as a target group. Create an AWS WAF web ACL containing rules that protect the application from this attack, then apply it to the ALB. Test to ensure the vulnerability has been mitigated, then redirect the Route 53 records to point to the ALB. Update security groups on the EC2 instances to prevent direct access from the internet.","B":"Create an Amazon CloudFront distribution specifying one EC2 instance as an origin. Create an AWS WAF web ACL containing rules that protect the application from this attack, then apply it to the distribution. Test to ensure the vulnerability has been mitigated, then redirect the Route 53 records to point to CloudFront.","C":"Obtain the latest source code for the platform and make the necessary updates. Test the updated code to ensure that the vulnerability has been mitigated, then deploy the patched version of the platform to the EC2 instances.","D":"Update the security group that is attached to the EC2 instances, removing access from the internet to the TCP port used by the SQL database. Create an AWS WAF web ACL containing rules that protect the application from this attack, then apply it to the EC2 instances."},"options_zh":{"A":"创建一个应用负载均衡器（ALB），并将现有的 EC2 实例作为目标组。创建一个包含防护规则 的 AWS WAF 网站访问控制列表（web ACL），以保护应用程序免受此类攻击，然后将其应 用于 ALB。测试以确保漏洞已得到缓解，随后将 Route 53 记录指向该 ALB。更新 EC2 实例 的安全组，防止互联网直接访问。","B":"创建一个 Amazon CloudFront 分发，指定一个 EC2 实例作为源。创建一个 AWS WAF 网站访 问控制列表（web ACL），包含保护应用程序免受此类攻击的规则，然后将其应用到该分发 上。测试以确保漏洞已得到缓解，随后将 Route 53 记录指向 CloudFront。","C":"获取平台的最新源代码并进行必要的更新。测试更新后的代码，确保漏洞已得到缓解，然后将 修复后的平台版本部署到EC2实例上。","D":"更新附加到 EC2 实例的安全组，移除互联网对 SQL 数据库所用 TCP 端口的访问权限。创建一 个包含保护应用程序免受此类攻击规则的 AWS WAF 网络 ACL，然后将其应用到 EC2 实例上。"},"answer":["A"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Networking/DNS","Security/IAM","Compute","Database"],"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選","research":{"verdict":["A"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"AWS WAF provides SQL injection protection through the AWSManagedRulesSQLiRuleSet managed rule group and SQLi match rule statements, so a WAF-based mitigation is the fastest, lowest-effort fix for a legacy platform that can no longer be patched. The decisive constraint is that an AWS WAF web ACL can only be associated with a fixed set of resources: CloudFront distributions, Application Load Balancers, API Gateway REST APIs, AppSync GraphQL APIs, Cognito user pools, App Runner services, Bedrock AgentCore Gateway, Verified Access instances, and Amplify. EC2 instances are NOT in that list, so WAF cannot be attached directly to EC2. Option A fronts the existing two EC2 instances with an Application Load Balancer (a supported WAF target), attaches a web ACL with SQLi rules, tests it, then repoints Route 53 to the ALB and locks the EC2 security groups so the internet can only reach the app through the WAF-protected ALB. This maintains normal operations (the ALB path is built and validated before the Route 53 cutover, and both instances stay in service) with the least effort. Option A is correct.","explanation_zh":"AWS WAF 透過 AWSManagedRulesSQLiRuleSet 受管規則群組與 SQLi match rule statement 提供 SQL injection 防護，對於已無法再套用安全更新的老舊平台而言，這是最快、最省力的緩解方式。決定性限制在於：AWS WAF web ACL 只能關聯到固定的資源清單——CloudFront distribution、Application Load Balancer、API Gateway REST API、AppSync GraphQL API、Cognito user pool、App Runner service、Bedrock AgentCore Gateway、Verified Access instance 與 Amplify。EC2 instance 不在此清單內，因此 WAF 無法直接套用到 EC2。選項 A 用 Application Load Balancer（WAF 支援的目標）承接現有兩台 EC2 instance，掛上含 SQLi 規則的 web ACL，測試後再把 Route 53 指向 ALB，並收緊 EC2 security group，使外網只能經由受 WAF 保護的 ALB 進入應用。此作法在維持正常運作（先建置並驗證 ALB 路徑再切換 Route 53，兩台 instance 皆持續服務）下所需工作量最少。正解為 A。","distractors":[{"letter":"B","why_en":"CloudFront does support WAF and SQLi rules, but specifying only ONE EC2 instance as the origin discards the existing Route 53 weighted load balancing across two instances, breaking high availability and creating a single point of failure. It does not maintain normal operations and is inferior to the ALB approach that keeps both instances in service.","why_zh":"CloudFront 確實支援 WAF 與 SQLi 規則，但只指定「一台」EC2 instance 為 origin，會放棄現有橫跨兩台 instance 的 Route 53 加權負載平衡，破壞高可用性並造成單點故障，無法維持正常運作，劣於同時保留兩台 instance 的 ALB 方案。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"The platform is legacy and no longer receives security updates. Obtaining source, patching, testing and redeploying is high effort and high risk, and is unlikely to be feasible within 24 hours. It directly violates the 'least amount of effort' requirement.","why_zh":"該平台為老舊系統且已不再收到安全更新。取得原始碼、修補、測試再重新部署工作量與風險都高，且不太可能在 24 小時內完成，直接違反「工作量最少」的要求。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"Technically impossible: a WAF web ACL cannot be associated directly with an EC2 instance (EC2 is not a supported WAF resource). Also, removing the SQL DB port from the security group does nothing against SQL injection, which enters through the web application layer, not by connecting to the DB port; this action does not mitigate the reported attack vector at all.","why_zh":"技術上不可行：WAF web ACL 無法直接關聯到 EC2 instance（EC2 不是 WAF 支援的資源）。此外，從 security group 移除 SQL 資料庫連接埠對 SQL injection 毫無作用，因為 SQLi 是經由 Web 應用層進入，而非直接連到資料庫連接埠，此動作完全無法緩解所回報的攻擊向量。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/waf/latest/developerguide/how-aws-waf-works-resources.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/waf/latest/developerguide/web-acl-associating-aws-resource.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/waf/latest/developerguide/aws-managed-rule-groups-use-case.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/waf/latest/developerguide/waf-rule-statement-type-sqli-match.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/elasticloadbalancing/latest/application/load-balancer-integrations.html"]}},{"id":161,"question_en":"A company uses an incident response team to troubleshoot incidents. The incident response team must use temporary credentials from AWS STS for cross-account IAM role access when troubleshooting. Occasionally, each team member will need to respond to multiple different types of incidents simultaneously. Based on the type of incident, the company wants to dynamically assign minimal permissions to whichever team member responds. Which solution will meet these requirements?","question_zh":"一家公司使用事件响应团队来排查故障。在排查问题时，该团队必须使用 AWS STS 提供的临时凭证，通过跨账户 IAM 角色 进行访问。有时，每位团队成员需要同时处理多个不同类型的问题。根据事件类型，公司希望动态地为响应人员分配最小权 限。 哪种解决方案能满足这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Attach a policy to the cross-account role that grants the appropriate permissions for all types of incidents. Reduce the scope of those permissions by using a session policy.","B":"Attach a policy to the cross-account role that grants the appropriate permissions for all types of incidents. Reduce the scope of those permissions by using a permissions boundary.","C":"Do not assign any permissions to the cross-account role initially. Assign a session policy to the role being assumed with the required permission for that type of incident.","D":"Use an AWS Lambda function for each incident. Configure the function to create a temporary cross- account role that uses the AWS managed policy AWSSecurityIncidentResponseServiceRolePolicy. Reduce the scope of those permissions by using a permissions boundary."},"options_zh":{"A":"将策略附加到跨账户角色，以授予所有类型事件所需的适当权限，并通过使用会话策略来缩小这些权限的范 围。","B":"为跨账户角色附加策略，授予处理各类事件所需的适当权限，并通过使用权限边界来缩小这些权限的范围。","C":"初始时不要为跨账户角色分配任何权限。在承担该角色时，应为其指定包含所需权限的会话策略，以应对特定类型 的事件。","D":"为每个事件使用一个 AWS Lambda 函数。配置该函数以创建一个临时的跨账户角色，并使用 AWS 管理策略 AWSSecurityIncidentResponseServiceRolePolicy。通过权限边界来缩小这些权限的范围。"},"answer":["A"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Security/IAM","Compute"],"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選","research":{"verdict":["A"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"both","explanation_en":"The correct approach is A. AWS IAM documentation on AssumeRole is explicit: 'you can pass inline or managed session policies as parameters of the AssumeRole... API operations. Session policies limit the permissions for the role's temporary credential session. The resulting session's permissions are the intersection of the role's identity-based policy and the session policies. You can use the role's temporary credentials... You cannot use session policies to grant more permissions than those allowed by the identity-based policy of the role that is being assumed.' Because a session policy can only narrow (intersect with) permissions the role already has — never add permissions the role lacks — the cross-account role must first carry a broad identity-based policy covering every incident type the team might handle. Each time a responder calls sts:AssumeRole for a specific incident, they attach a session policy scoped to just that incident type, and the resulting temporary credentials are the intersection: minimal, incident-specific permissions. Because each AssumeRole call produces an independent temporary-credential session, the same team member can hold several concurrently-active sessions — one per incident, each scoped by its own session policy — satisfying the 'multiple different types of incidents simultaneously' requirement. Option C fails on the documented intersection rule: if the role starts with no permissions attached, intersecting 'nothing' with any session policy yields an empty effective permission set, so the responder would get zero access regardless of what the session policy says. Option B's permissions boundary is a static ceiling set on the role itself (or the underlying IAM principal) — it does not vary per AssumeRole call/session and is not the documented mechanism for per-session, per-incident scoping, so it can't dynamically narrow permissions per incident on the fly. Option D references AWSSecurityIncidentResponseServiceRolePolicy, which is the AWS-managed policy tied to the dedicated AWS Security Incident Response service's own service-linked role — it is not a general-purpose cross-account troubleshooting mechanism, and having Lambda dynamically create new IAM roles per incident is unnecessarily complex, slow, and not how AWS documents scoping temporary cross-account access. Session policies are precisely AWS's documented feature for this dynamic, per-session least-privilege use case.","explanation_zh":"正確答案是 A。AWS IAM 官方文件對 AssumeRole 講得很明確:「您可以在呼叫 AssumeRole... 等 API 時,以參數方式傳入 inline 或 managed 的 session policy。Session policy 會限制該角色暫時憑證工作階段的權限。最終工作階段的權限,是角色身分型政策(identity-based policy)與 session policy 的交集(intersection)。您無法使用 session policy 授予超出被擔任角色身分型政策所允許的權限。」由於 session policy 只能『縮小』(取交集)角色原本已具備的權限,絕不能新增角色本身沒有的權限,因此跨帳戶角色必須先掛載一個涵蓋所有可能事故類型的廣泛身分型政策。每當應變人員針對特定事故呼叫 sts:AssumeRole 時,附加一個僅涵蓋該事故類型所需權限的 session policy,產生的暫時憑證即為交集結果:僅具備該事故所需的最小權限。由於每次 AssumeRole 呼叫都會產生獨立的暫時憑證工作階段,同一名團隊成員可以同時持有多個作用中的工作階段——每個事故一個,各自由其專屬的 session policy 限縮權限——滿足題目「同時應對多種不同類型事故」的需求。選項 C 違反了文件明訂的交集規則:若角色一開始未掛載任何權限,則『無』與任何 session policy 的交集必為空集合,因此不論 session policy 內容為何,應變人員都會得到零權限。選項 B 的 permissions boundary 是設定在角色(或底層 IAM 主體)上的靜態上限,不會隨每次 AssumeRole 呼叫/工作階段而變動,也不是 AWS 文件中用於「依工作階段、依事故類型」動態限縮權限的機制,因此無法即時依事故動態縮小權限範圍。選項 D 提到的 AWSSecurityIncidentResponseServiceRolePolicy,是專屬於 AWS Security Incident Response 這項特定服務之服務連結角色(service-linked role)的 AWS 受管政策,並非通用的跨帳戶疑難排解機制;讓 Lambda 為每個事故動態建立全新 IAM 角色也過於複雜、緩慢,也不是 AWS 文件所記載限縮跨帳戶暫時存取權限的方式。Session policy 正是 AWS 官方文件針對此種「動態、依工作階段、最小權限」使用情境所設計的功能。","distractors":[{"letter":"B","why_en":"Permissions boundaries set a static maximum permission ceiling on an IAM entity (user or role) and are configured on the role itself, not passed dynamically per AssumeRole call. They don't let the same role be assumed with a different, incident-specific effective permission set on each call the way session policies do, so they can't satisfy 'dynamically assign minimal permissions... based on the type of incident' per session.","why_zh":"Permissions boundary 是設定在 IAM 實體(使用者或角色)上的靜態最大權限上限,是配置在角色本身,而非在每次 AssumeRole 呼叫時動態傳入。它無法像 session policy 那樣讓同一個角色在每次擔任時獲得依事故類型而異的有效權限組合,因此無法滿足「依事故類型動態指派最小權限」這項逐工作階段的需求。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"Contradicts AWS's documented policy evaluation logic: the effective session permissions are always the intersection of the role's identity-based policy and the session policy. If the role has no permissions attached, the intersection with any session policy is empty, so the responder ends up with no access at all — this option cannot actually grant the needed permissions.","why_zh":"違反 AWS 文件記載的政策評估邏輯:有效的工作階段權限永遠是角色身分型政策與 session policy 的交集。若角色未掛載任何權限,則與任何 session policy 的交集必為空集合,應變人員最終將完全沒有存取權——此選項實際上無法授予所需權限。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"AWSSecurityIncidentResponseServiceRolePolicy is the AWS managed policy used by the dedicated AWS Security Incident Response service's service-linked role, not a general mechanism for scoping ad-hoc cross-account troubleshooting access. Dynamically spinning up a new IAM role per incident via Lambda is unnecessarily complex and slow compared to the built-in session-policy mechanism, and is not how AWS documents least-privilege temporary cross-account access.","why_zh":"AWSSecurityIncidentResponseServiceRolePolicy 是專屬於 AWS Security Incident Response 這項特定服務之服務連結角色所使用的受管政策,並非用於限縮臨時跨帳戶疑難排解存取的通用機制。透過 Lambda 為每個事故動態建立新的 IAM 角色,相較於內建的 session policy 機制過於複雜且緩慢,也不是 AWS 文件記載用於實現最小權限暫時跨帳戶存取的方式。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/IAM/latest/UserGuide/id_credentials_temp_control-access_assumerole.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/IAM/latest/UserGuide/access_policies.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/IAM/latest/UserGuide/access_policies_boundaries.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/IAM/latest/UserGuide/reference_policies_evaluation-logic.html"]}},{"id":162,"question_en":"A company uses Amazon API Gateway to present REST APIs to users. An API developer wants to analyze API access patterns without the need to parse the log files. Which combination of steps will meet these requirements with the LEAST effort? (Select TWO.)","question_zh":"一家公司使用 Amazon API Gateway 向用户公开 REST API。一位 API 开发人员希望在无需解析日志文件的情况下分析 API 的访问模式。 哪两个步骤的组合能以最少的努力满足这些要求？（选择两项。）","options_en":{"A":"Configure access logging for the required API stage.","B":"Configure an AWS CloudTrail trail destination for API Gateway events. Configure filters on the userIdentity, userAgent, and sourceIPAddress fields.","C":"Configure an Amazon S3 destination for API Gateway logs. Run Amazon Athena queries to analyze API access information.","D":"Use Amazon CloudWatch Logs Insights to analyze API access information.","E":"Select the Enable Detailed CloudWatch Metrics option on the required API stage."},"options_zh":{"A":"为所需的 API 阶段配置访问日志。","B":"为 API 网关事件配置 AWS CloudTrail 跟踪目的地，并在 userIdentity、userAgent 和 sourceIPAddress 字段上设置 过滤器。","C":"为 API Gateway 日志配置 Amazon S3 目标。运行 Amazon Athena 查询以分析 API 访问信息。","D":"使用 Amazon CloudWatch Logs Insights 分析 API 访问信息。","E":"在所需的 API 阶段上选择“启用详细的 CloudWatch 指标”选项。"},"answer":["D","E"],"multi":true,"vote":{},"tags":["Storage","Serverless/Integration","Monitoring/Ops","Analytics"],"difficulty":3,"diff_why":"複選・題庫與社群皆錯","research":{"verdict":["A","D"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"neither","explanation_en":"The goal is to analyze API access patterns (who called the API, from where, how) without manually parsing log files. AWS documentation for API Gateway logging explicitly distinguishes execution logging from access logging, stating: 'In access logging, you, as an API developer, want to log who has accessed your API and how the caller accessed the API' — this is exactly the requirement, and it is enabled per-stage via accessLogSettings (option A). Once access logs land in a CloudWatch Logs log group (the lowest-effort destination, no additional infrastructure required), CloudWatch Logs Insights lets you interactively query and analyze that log data — filtering, aggregating, and extracting fields like source IP, identity, and method — without writing a parser or standing up any additional service (option D). Option E (Enable Detailed CloudWatch Metrics) only adds extra per-method numeric CloudWatch metrics (call count, latency, integration latency, error counts); it produces no log data at all and cannot reveal caller identity, source IP, or request paths, so it does not satisfy 'analyze API access patterns' and pairing it with D leaves nothing for Logs Insights to query. Option C (S3 + Athena) can technically analyze access data but requires provisioning an S3 export pipeline and writing/running Athena SQL against raw files — strictly more setup effort than A+D. Option B (CloudTrail) records control-plane/management events on the API Gateway service (e.g., CreateRestApi, UpdateStage) and is not designed to capture end-user data-plane invocations of the deployed API's execute-api endpoint, so it cannot show per-caller access patterns to the API itself.","explanation_zh":"本題目標是分析 API 存取模式（誰呼叫了 API、從哪裡呼叫、如何呼叫），且不需要手動解析日誌檔案。AWS 官方文件在說明 API Gateway 日誌時明確區分了 execution logging 與 access logging，並指出：「在 access logging 中，身為 API 開發者，你想要記錄誰存取了你的 API，以及呼叫者是如何存取 API 的」——這正好對應題目需求，且此功能是透過 stage 的 accessLogSettings 啟用（選項 A）。一旦 access log 送進 CloudWatch Logs 的 log group（這是最省力的目的地，不需額外建置基礎設施），CloudWatch Logs Insights 就能讓你以互動方式查詢、分析這些日誌資料——篩選、聚合並擷取來源 IP、身分、方法等欄位——完全不必自己寫 parser 或架設額外服務（選項 D）。選項 E（啟用 Detailed CloudWatch Metrics）只是新增每個方法的額外數值型 CloudWatch 指標（呼叫次數、延遲、整合延遲、錯誤數），完全不會產生任何日誌資料，也無法顯示呼叫者身分、來源 IP 或請求路徑，因此無法滿足「分析 API 存取模式」的需求；若搭配選項 D，Logs Insights 也將無日誌可查。選項 C（S3 + Athena）雖然技術上可行，但需要額外建置 S3 匯出管線並撰寫、執行 Athena SQL 查詢原始檔案，其設置成本明顯高於 A+D 的組合。選項 B（CloudTrail）記錄的是 API Gateway 服務本身的控制平面／管理事件（例如 CreateRestApi、UpdateStage），並非設計來擷取最終使用者對已部署 API 的 execute-api 端點所做的資料平面呼叫，因此無法呈現對該 API 本身的逐次存取模式。","distractors":[{"letter":"B","why_en":"AWS CloudTrail captures management/control-plane API calls to the API Gateway service (creating, updating, deleting APIs and stages), not the runtime invocations that end users make against the deployed execute-api endpoint, so it cannot reveal end-user access patterns to the API.","why_zh":"AWS CloudTrail 擷取的是對 API Gateway 服務本身的管理／控制平面呼叫（建立、更新、刪除 API 與 stage），而不是終端使用者對已部署 execute-api 端點所做的執行期呼叫，因此無法呈現終端使用者對該 API 的存取模式。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"Exporting logs to S3 and querying with Athena can work, but it requires setting up an export/delivery pipeline plus writing and running SQL queries against raw files — substantially more setup and operational effort than enabling access logging and querying directly with CloudWatch Logs Insights.","why_zh":"將日誌匯出到 S3 並用 Athena 查詢雖然可行，但需要建立匯出／傳送管線，並撰寫、執行 SQL 查詢原始檔案——比起啟用 access logging 後直接用 CloudWatch Logs Insights 查詢，設置與維運成本明顯更高。"},{"letter":"E","why_en":"Detailed CloudWatch Metrics only adds extra numeric, per-method CloudWatch metrics (call counts, latency, errors); it does not generate any log entries and cannot show caller identity, source IP, or request details, so it cannot be used to analyze access patterns and gives CloudWatch Logs Insights nothing to query.","why_zh":"Detailed CloudWatch Metrics 只是新增每個方法的額外數值型 CloudWatch 指標（呼叫次數、延遲、錯誤數），並不會產生任何日誌條目，也無法顯示呼叫者身分、來源 IP 或請求細節，因此無法用來分析存取模式，也讓 CloudWatch Logs Insights 無日誌可查。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/apigateway/latest/developerguide/set-up-logging.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/apigateway/latest/developerguide/http-api-logging.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonCloudWatch/latest/logs/AnalyzingLogData.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/apigateway/latest/developerguide/api-gateway-metrics-and-dimensions.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/apigateway/latest/developerguide/set-up-stages.html"]}},{"id":163,"question_en":"A development team is creating an open source toolset to manage a company’s software as a service (SaaS) application. The company stores the code in a public repository so that anyone can view and download the toolset’s code. The company discovers that the code contains an IAM access key and secret key that provide access to internal resources in the company ' s AWS environment. A security engineer must implement a solution to identify whether unauthorized usage of the exposed credentials has occurred. The solution also must prevent any additional usage of the exposed credentials. Which combination of steps will meet these requirements? (Select TWO.)","question_zh":"一个开发团队正在创建一套开源工具集，用于管理公司的软件即服务（SaaS）应用程序。该公司将代码存储在公共代码库 中，以便任何人都可以查看和下载。 工具集的代码。公司发现该代码中包含一个IAM访问密钥和秘密密钥，可访问公司AWS环境中的内部资源。安全工程师 必须实施一项解决方案，以确定是否发生了对暴露凭证的未授权使用，并且该方案还必须阻止任何进一步使用这些暴露 的凭证。 哪两个步骤的组合可以满足这些要求？（选择两项。）","options_en":{"A":"Use AWS Identity and Access Management Access Analyzer to determine which resources the exposed credentials accessed and who used them.","B":"Deactivate the exposed IAM access key from the user ' s IAM account.","C":"Create a rule in Amazon GuardDuty to block the access key in the source code from being used.","D":"Create a new IAM access key and secret key for the user whose credentials were exposed.","E":"Generate an IAM credential report. Check the report to determine when the user that owns the access key last logged in."},"options_zh":{"A":"使用 AWS 身份和访问管理访问分析器来确定暴露的凭据访问了哪些资源以及谁使用了这些凭据。","B":"从用户的IAM账户中停用已暴露的IAM访问密钥。","C":"在 Amazon GuardDuty 中创建规则，阻止源代码中的访问密钥被使用。","D":"为凭据已泄露的用户创建新的 IAM 访问密钥和秘密密钥。","E":"生成 IAM 凭据报告。查看报告以确定拥有该访问密钥的用户上次登录的时间。"},"answer":["B","E"],"multi":true,"vote":{},"tags":["Security/IAM"],"difficulty":2,"diff_why":"複選","research":{"verdict":["B","E"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"The two required outcomes are (1) determine whether the exposed access key was already misused, and (2) stop it from being used again. Deactivating the exposed IAM access key (B) immediately invalidates it for all future API calls, satisfying the prevention requirement (IAM lets an administrator deactivate/delete a user's access key at any time). Generating an IAM credential report (E) gives a CSV per IAM user with fields such as password_last_used and access_key_N_last_used_date/region/service, which lets the security engineer see whether the account/key was used (e.g., after the code was published) as a first-pass indicator of unauthorized activity. Option A is wrong because IAM Access Analyzer's actual capabilities are external-access analysis (finding resources shared outside the account) and unused-access analysis (unused roles/keys/passwords/permissions) — it does not track which resources a specific credential accessed or who used it; that is a CloudTrail/Access Advisor function, not Access Analyzer. Option C is wrong because GuardDuty is a detection service (it can raise a CredentialAccess:IAMUser/CompromisedCredentials finding) but has no mechanism to create a 'rule' that blocks an access key from being used — remediation still requires the administrator to deactivate/rotate the key. Option D (issuing a new key) is a business-continuity step for the legitimate user, but it neither identifies past unauthorized usage nor by itself prevents continued use of the leaked key (that only happens once the old key is deactivated/deleted, i.e., option B) — so it's not required to meet the two stated goals.","explanation_zh":"題目要求同時達成兩件事：(1) 判斷外洩的 access key 是否已遭未授權使用、(2) 阻止該 key 再被使用。停用外洩的 IAM access key（B）可立即讓該金鑰失效，滿足「阻止再被使用」的需求（IAM 管理員可隨時停用/刪除使用者的 access key）。產生 IAM credential report（E）會輸出每個 IAM 使用者的 CSV，內含 password_last_used 以及 access_key_N_last_used_date/region/service 等欄位，可讓安全工程師檢視該帳號/金鑰是否被使用過（例如程式碼公開後），作為判斷是否有未授權使用的初步依據。選項 A 錯誤：IAM Access Analyzer 的實際功能是外部存取分析（找出被分享到帳號外部的資源）與未使用存取分析（未使用的角色/金鑰/密碼/權限），並不會追蹤「某組憑證存取了哪些資源、被誰使用」，這是 CloudTrail／Access Advisor 的功能，不是 Access Analyzer。選項 C 錯誤：GuardDuty 是偵測服務（會產生 CredentialAccess:IAMUser/CompromisedCredentials 這類 finding），但沒有可以「建立規則封鎖某組 access key」的機制，補救仍須由管理員自行停用/輪替金鑰。選項 D（建立新金鑰）只是讓合法使用者能持續使用服務的維運步驟，本身既無法判斷過去是否有未授權使用，也無法單獨阻止舊外洩金鑰被繼續使用（那要靠停用/刪除舊金鑰，也就是選項 B），因此並非達成題目兩項需求所必需。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"IAM Access Analyzer only performs external-access analysis (resources shared outside the account) and unused-access analysis (unused roles/keys/passwords/permissions); it does not report which resources a given credential accessed or who used them.","why_zh":"IAM Access Analyzer 只做外部存取分析（分享到帳號外的資源）與未使用存取分析（未使用的角色/金鑰/密碼/權限），不會回報某組憑證存取了哪些資源或被誰使用。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"GuardDuty is a detection/monitoring service that generates findings (e.g., CredentialAccess:IAMUser/CompromisedCredentials); it has no 'rule' feature to block or deny use of a specific access key.","why_zh":"GuardDuty 是偵測/監控服務，只會產生 finding（例如 CredentialAccess:IAMUser/CompromisedCredentials），並沒有可以封鎖或拒絕特定 access key 使用的『規則』功能。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"Creating a new key for the user restores legitimate access but does not identify past unauthorized usage and does not by itself stop the old exposed key from being used — that requires deactivating/deleting it (option B).","why_zh":"為使用者建立新金鑰只是恢復合法存取，並不能判斷過去是否有未授權使用，也無法單獨阻止舊的外洩金鑰繼續被使用——那需要停用/刪除舊金鑰（選項 B）。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/IAM/latest/UserGuide/access-keys-admin-managed.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/IAM/latest/UserGuide/id_credentials_getting-report.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/IAM/latest/UserGuide/what-is-access-analyzer.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/guardduty/latest/ug/guardduty_finding-types-iam.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/guardduty/latest/ug/guardduty-finding-types-eks-audit-logs.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/IAM/latest/UserGuide/securing_access-keys.html"]}},{"id":164,"question_en":"A company’s application uses standard tier SecureString parameters from AWS Systems Manager Parameter Store. The application is receiving error messages when the company tries to update a parameter. The parameter uses an AWS KMS customer managed key for encryption and decryption. What are the reasons for the error messages? (Select TWO.)","question_zh":"一家公司的应用程序使用了 AWS Systems Manager 参数存储中的标准层级 SecureString 参数。当公司尝试更新该参数时， 应用程序会收到错误消息。该参数使用 AWS KMS 客户管理密钥进行加密和解密。 错误消息的原因是什么？（选择两项。）","options_en":{"A":"The application does not have the kms:Encrypt permission for the customer managed key.","B":"The customer managed key is already being used to encrypt another SecureString parameter.","C":"Standard tier SecureString parameters cannot use a customer managed key for encryption.","D":"The customer managed key that is specified in the application has its key state set to Disabled.","E":"The customer managed key that is specified in the application is using a key alias instead of a key ID."},"options_zh":{"A":"应用程序没有客户管理密钥的 kms:Encrypt 权限。","B":"客户管理的密钥已用于加密另一个 SecureString 参数。","C":"标准层级的 SecureString 参数无法使用客户管理的密钥进行加密。","D":"应用程序中指定的客户管理密钥的状态已设置为“已禁用”。","E":"应用程序中指定的客户管理密钥使用的是密钥别名，而不是密钥ID。"},"answer":["A","D"],"multi":true,"vote":{},"tags":["Security/IAM","Monitoring/Ops"],"difficulty":2,"diff_why":"複選","research":{"verdict":["A","D"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"AWS's own Parameter Store documentation lists the exact failure causes for KMS-related errors when creating or updating a SecureString parameter, and A and D map directly onto the first two of them. First, for a standard-tier SecureString, Parameter Store does not use envelope encryption — when you call PutParameter, Parameter Store sends the plaintext value straight to the AWS KMS Encrypt API using the specified customer managed key. The documentation states explicitly: 'To encrypt a standard SecureString parameter value, the user needs kms:Encrypt permission.' If the calling application/role lacks kms:Encrypt on that CMK's key policy or IAM policy, PutParameter fails with an AccessDenied-type error — this is option A. Second, AWS's dedicated 'Troubleshooting KMS key issues in Parameter Store' section states that 'the KMS key is not enabled' is a leading cause of failures, adding: 'When this occurs, Parameter Store returns an InvalidKeyId exception... If the KMS key state is Disabled, enable it.' A CMK in the Disabled state cannot be used for any cryptographic operation (Encrypt/Decrypt/GenerateDataKey), so PutParameter/GetParameter against it fails — this is option D. The remaining options are all false on technical merit: C is wrong because the documentation explicitly confirms standard SecureString parameters CAN use a customer managed key ('If you do not specify a KMS key, Parameter Store uses the AWS managed key... you can specify your own customer managed key'). B is wrong because there is no limit or restriction preventing a single customer managed key from encrypting multiple SecureString parameters (each parameter simply has a distinct encryption context of its own ARN — no exclusivity requirement exists). E is wrong because Parameter Store's KeyId parameter explicitly accepts a key ID, key ARN, alias name, or alias ARN interchangeably — using an alias is fully supported and is not an error condition (the 'KMS key is not found' failure mode refers to using an incorrect/nonexistent identifier, not to using an alias per se).","explanation_zh":"AWS 官方 Parameter Store 文件明確列出了建立或更新 SecureString 參數時,與 KMS 相關錯誤的具體成因,而 A 和 D 正好對應清單中的前兩項。首先,對於標準層級的 SecureString,Parameter Store 並不使用信封加密——當呼叫 PutParameter 時,Parameter Store 會直接以指定的 customer managed key 呼叫 AWS KMS 的 Encrypt API 來加密明文值。文件明確指出:「要加密標準 SecureString 參數值,使用者需要 kms:Encrypt 權限。」若呼叫的應用程式/角色在該 CMK 的金鑰政策或 IAM 政策中缺少 kms:Encrypt 權限,PutParameter 就會因存取被拒而失敗——這正是選項 A。其次,AWS 專門的「Parameter Store 中的 KMS 金鑰問題疑難排解」章節指出,「KMS 金鑰未啟用」是失敗的主要原因之一,並補充說明:「發生此情況時,Parameter Store 會傳回 InvalidKeyId 例外……若 KMS 金鑰狀態為 Disabled,請將其啟用。」處於 Disabled 狀態的 CMK 無法用於任何加密操作(Encrypt/Decrypt/GenerateDataKey),因此對其執行 PutParameter/GetParameter 會失敗——這正是選項 D。其餘選項在技術上皆不成立:C 錯誤,因為文件明確確認標準層級 SecureString 參數「可以」使用 customer managed key(「若未指定 KMS 金鑰,Parameter Store 會使用 AWS managed key……您也可以指定自己的 customer managed key」)。B 錯誤,因為並不存在限制單一 customer managed key 只能加密一個 SecureString 參數的規定(每個參數僅擁有各自 ARN 作為獨立的加密內容,並無互斥要求)。E 錯誤,因為 Parameter Store 的 KeyId 參數明確支援金鑰 ID、金鑰 ARN、別名名稱或別名 ARN 可互換使用——使用別名完全受支援,並非錯誤情況(「找不到 KMS 金鑰」的失敗情境指的是使用了錯誤或不存在的識別碼,而非單純使用別名本身)。","distractors":[{"letter":"C","why_en":"Directly contradicted by AWS documentation: standard-tier SecureString parameters are explicitly allowed to use a customer managed key ('you can specify your own customer managed key'); the only tier-based encryption difference is that standard uses direct KMS Encrypt while advanced uses envelope encryption via the AWS Encryption SDK — both tiers support customer managed keys.","why_zh":"與 AWS 文件直接矛盾:標準層級的 SecureString 參數明確允許使用 customer managed key(「您也可以指定自己的 customer managed key」);唯一與層級相關的加密差異在於標準層級直接呼叫 KMS Encrypt,而進階層級透過 AWS Encryption SDK 使用信封加密——兩種層級皆支援 customer managed key。"},{"letter":"B","why_en":"There is no documented restriction limiting a customer managed key to encrypting only one SecureString parameter; it is common and supported practice to use the same CMK across many parameters, each distinguished by its own PARAMETER_ARN encryption context. This is not listed among AWS's documented causes of KMS-related Parameter Store failures.","why_zh":"並無任何文件記載限制 customer managed key 只能加密一個 SecureString 參數;使用同一個 CMK 加密多個參數是常見且受支援的做法,每個參數會以自己的 PARAMETER_ARN 作為加密內容加以區分。這也不在 AWS 文件所列出的 KMS 相關 Parameter Store 失敗原因之中。"},{"letter":"E","why_en":"Parameter Store's KeyId parameter accepts a key ID, key ARN, alias name, or alias ARN interchangeably by design — using an alias instead of a key ID is fully supported and does not cause an error. AWS's troubleshooting guide attributes 'key not found' failures to using an incorrect/invalid identifier, not to the mere choice of alias vs. key ID.","why_zh":"Parameter Store 的 KeyId 參數在設計上可互換接受金鑰 ID、金鑰 ARN、別名名稱或別名 ARN——使用別名而非金鑰 ID 完全受支援,不會導致錯誤。AWS 的疑難排解指南將「找不到金鑰」的失敗歸因於使用了不正確或無效的識別碼,而非單純選擇別名或金鑰 ID 的差異。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/systems-manager/latest/userguide/secure-string-parameter-kms-encryption.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/systems-manager/latest/userguide/sysman-paramstore-access.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/kms/latest/developerguide/key-state.html"]}},{"id":165,"question_en":"A security engineer is responding to an incident that is affecting an AWS account. The ID of the account is 123456789012. The attack created workloads that are distributed across multiple AWS Regions. The security engineer contains the attack and removes all compute and storage resources from all affected Regions. However, the attacker also created an AWS KMS key. The key policy on the KMS key explicitly allows IAM principal kms:* permissions. The key was scheduled to be deleted the previous day. However, the key is still enabled and usable. The key has an ARN of arn:aws:kms:us-east-2:123456789012:key/mrk-0bb0212cd9864fdea0dcamzo26efb5670. The security engineer must delete the key as quickly as possible. Which solution will meet this requirement?","question_zh":"安全工程师正在响应影响一个AWS账户的事件，该账户的ID为123456789012。此次攻击创建了分 布在多个AWS区域的工作负载。 安全工程师成功遏制了攻击，并移除了所有受影响区域中的计算和存储资源。然而，攻击者还创 建了一个 AWS KMS 密钥，该密钥的策略明确允许 IAM 主体拥有 kms:* 权限。 该密钥原定于前一天删除，但目前密钥仍然处于启用状态并可正常使用。该密钥的ARN为 arn:aws:kms:us-east-2:123456789012:key/mrk-0bb0212cd9864fdea0dcamzo26efb5670 安全工程师必须尽快删除该密钥。 哪种解决方案能满足这一要求？","options_en":{"A":"Log in to the account by using the account root user credentials. Re-issue the deletion request for the KMS key with a waiting period of 7 days.","B":"Identify the other Regions where the KMS key ID is present and schedule the key for deletion in 7 days.","C":"Update the IAM principal to allow kms:* permissions on the KMS key ARN. Re-issue the deletion request for the KMS key with a waiting period of 7 days.","D":"Disable the KMS key. Re-issue the deletion request for the KMS key in 30 days."},"options_zh":{"A":"使用账户根用户凭据登录账户，重新提交KMS密钥的删除请求，并设置7天的等待期。","B":"识别KMS密钥ID所在的其他区域，并安排在7天后删除该密钥。","C":"更新 IAM 主体，使其对 KMS 密钥 ARN 拥有 kms:* 权限。重新提交删除 KMS 密钥的请求， 并设置 7 天的等待期。","D":"禁用KMS密钥。30天后重新提交删除该KMS密钥的请求。"},"answer":["A"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Security/IAM"],"difficulty":2,"diff_why":"題庫與社群皆錯","research":{"verdict":["B"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"neither","explanation_en":"The decisive clue is the key ID itself: 'mrk-0bb0212cd9864fdea0dcamzo26efb5670' carries the 'mrk-' prefix, which AWS KMS uses exclusively to identify multi-Region keys (both primary and replica keys share this ID format across Regions). Combined with the scenario stating the attacker's workloads were 'distributed across multiple AWS Regions,' this signals the attacker likely created replica keys of this same multi-Region key in other Regions besides us-east-2. AWS's own KMS documentation on ScheduleKeyDeletion is explicit about the exact symptom described: 'You can schedule the deletion of a multi-Region primary key and its replica keys at any time. However, AWS KMS will not delete a multi-Region primary key with existing replica keys. If you schedule the deletion of a primary key with replicas, its key state changes to PendingReplicaDeletion... This status can continue indefinitely. When the last of its replica keys is deleted (not just scheduled), the key state of the primary key changes to PendingDeletion and its waiting period begins.' This is precisely why the key 'was scheduled to be deleted the previous day' yet 'is still enabled and usable' the attack's replica keys elsewhere are blocking the primary from ever entering its real deletion countdown. The KMS Developer Guide's 'Deleting multi-Region keys' section confirms the remedy: 'To delete a primary key, you must schedule the deletion [of] all of its replica keys, and then wait for the replica keys to be deleted.' Therefore the security engineer must find every Region where a replica of this key ID exists and schedule each replica's deletion with the minimum allowed waiting period (7 days) option B is the only choice that targets the actual root cause (existing replicas) rather than re-issuing a no-op deletion request against the already-scheduled, already-permission-unrestricted primary key. The key policy already grants the IAM principal kms:* (full permissions), so permission-focused options (A and C, which fixate on re-authenticating as root or re-granting kms:* that is already granted) address a problem that does not exist and leave the true blocker (replicas) untouched. Option D's 30-day wait is both slower than the 7-day minimum and, like A and C, ignores the replica-key blocker entirely, so disabling and re-scheduling the primary alone would still leave it stuck in PendingReplicaDeletion.","explanation_zh":"決定性線索在金鑰 ID 本身:'mrk-0bb0212cd9864fdea0dcamzo26efb5670' 帶有 'mrk-' 前綴,這是 AWS KMS 專門用來識別多重區域金鑰(multi-Region key)的格式(主要金鑰與複本金鑰在各區域共用相同的金鑰 ID)。再搭配題目說明攻擊者的工作負載『分散在多個 AWS 區域』,可推斷攻擊者很可能在 us-east-2 以外的其他區域也建立了此同一把多重區域金鑰的複本(replica)。AWS KMS 官方文件在 ScheduleKeyDeletion API 說明中明確描述了題目所述的確切現象:『您可以隨時排程刪除多重區域主要金鑰及其複本金鑰。但是,只要存在複本金鑰,AWS KMS 就不會刪除多重區域主要金鑰。如果您排程刪除仍有複本存在的主要金鑰,其金鑰狀態會變更為 PendingReplicaDeletion……此狀態可能無限期持續。當其最後一個複本金鑰被刪除(而非僅是排程)時,主要金鑰的狀態才會變更為 PendingDeletion,其等待期才會開始。』這正是為何該金鑰『前一天已排程刪除』卻『仍處於啟用且可用狀態』的原因——攻擊者在其他區域建立的複本金鑰,阻擋了主要金鑰真正進入刪除倒數。KMS 開發人員指南『刪除多重區域金鑰』一節也確認了解法:『若要刪除主要金鑰,您必須先排程刪除其所有複本金鑰,然後等待這些複本金鑰被刪除。』因此,安全工程師必須找出此金鑰 ID 存在複本的所有區域,並以允許的最短等待期(7 天)排程刪除每一個複本——選項 B 是唯一真正針對根本原因(既存複本)下手的選項,而不是對已排程、權限本就暢通的主要金鑰重複發出無效的刪除請求。金鑰政策本已授予 IAM 主體 kms:*(完整權限),因此聚焦於權限的選項(A 使用 root 使用者重新登入、C 重新授予本已存在的 kms:* 權限)是在解決一個根本不存在的問題,完全沒有處理真正的阻塞點(複本金鑰)。選項 D 的 30 天等待期不僅比最短的 7 天更慢,而且和 A、C 一樣完全忽略複本金鑰這個阻塞因素,因此僅停用並重新排程主要金鑰,仍會卡在 PendingReplicaDeletion 狀態。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"Using root credentials to re-issue ScheduleKeyDeletion on the same primary key does not fix anything: the key policy already grants the IAM principal kms:* permissions, so there is no permission barrier to route around with root. The real blocker is that AWS KMS refuses to actually delete a multi-Region primary key while replica keys exist elsewhere it moves to PendingReplicaDeletion and 'can continue indefinitely' per AWS docs. Re-issuing the same deletion request (from root or anyone) against the primary without first deleting its replicas leaves it stuck in the same blocked state.","why_zh":"使用 root 憑證對同一把主要金鑰重新發出 ScheduleKeyDeletion 請求並不能解決問題:金鑰政策本已授予 IAM 主體 kms:* 權限,所以並不存在需要用 root 繞過的權限障礙。真正的阻塞點在於:只要其他區域仍存在複本金鑰,AWS KMS 就會拒絕真正刪除多重區域主要金鑰,金鑰狀態會轉為 PendingReplicaDeletion,且依 AWS 文件『可能無限期持續』。在未先刪除複本的情況下,對主要金鑰重複發出相同的刪除請求(不論由 root 或任何人執行),都只會讓它停留在同樣的阻塞狀態。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"This option assumes a permissions problem that does not exist the scenario explicitly states the key policy already 'explicitly allows IAM principal kms:* permissions,' so granting kms:* again is a no-op. It also fails to address the actual root cause: AWS KMS will not delete a multi-Region primary key while its replica keys in other Regions still exist, regardless of what permissions the IAM principal holds on the primary key's ARN.","why_zh":"此選項假設存在一個實際上不存在的權限問題——題目已明確說明金鑰政策『明確允許 IAM 主體 kms:* 權限』,因此再次授予 kms:* 毫無作用。它也未觸及真正的根本原因:無論 IAM 主體對主要金鑰 ARN 擁有何種權限,只要其他區域仍存在該金鑰的複本,AWS KMS 就不會刪除這把多重區域主要金鑰。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"Disabling the primary key does not remove the replica-key blocker documented by AWS for multi-Region primary keys, so re-scheduling deletion of the primary would still land it in the indefinite PendingReplicaDeletion state until replicas elsewhere are deleted. It also chooses the maximum 30-day waiting period rather than the minimum 7-day period, directly contradicting the requirement to delete the key 'as quickly as possible.'","why_zh":"停用主要金鑰並不能移除 AWS 文件所述、專屬於多重區域主要金鑰的複本阻塞問題,因此重新排程刪除主要金鑰,仍會使其停留在無限期的 PendingReplicaDeletion 狀態,直到其他區域的複本被刪除為止。此外,它選擇了最長的 30 天等待期,而非最短的 7 天,直接違背『盡快刪除該金鑰』的要求。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/kms/latest/APIReference/API_ScheduleKeyDeletion.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/kms/latest/developerguide/deleting-keys.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/kms/latest/developerguide/deleting-keys.html#deleting-mrks","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/kms/latest/developerguide/multi-region-keys-overview.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/kms/latest/developerguide/multi-region-keys-delete.html"]}},{"id":166,"question_en":"A company experienced a security incident caused by a vulnerable container image that was pushed from an external CI/CD pipeline into Amazon ECR. Which solution will prevent vulnerable images from being pushed?","question_zh":"一家公司因外部CI/CD流水线推送了一个存在漏洞的容器镜像至Amazon ECR，从而引发了一起安全事件。 哪种解决方案可以防止易受攻击的镜像被推送？","options_en":{"A":"Enable ECR enhanced scanning with Lambda blocking.","B":"Use Amazon Inspector with EventBridge and Lambda.","C":"Integrate Amazon Inspector into the CI/CD pipeline using SBOM generation and fail the pipeline on critical findings.","D":"Enable basic continuous ECR scanning."},"options_zh":{"A":"启用 ECR 增强扫描并使用 Lambda 进行阻断。","B":"使用 Amazon Inspector 与 EventBridge 和 Lambda。","C":"使用SBOM生成将Amazon Inspector集成到CI/CD流水线中，并在发现关键问题时使流水线失败。","D":"启用基本的持续ECR扫描。"},"answer":["C"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Compute","Serverless/Integration","Containers"],"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選","research":{"verdict":["C"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"The requirement is to PREVENT a vulnerable image from ever being pushed to ECR, which means the vulnerability check must happen before/during the CI/CD build, not after the image already exists in the registry. Amazon Inspector's CI/CD integration works by generating a CycloneDX SBOM for the container image (via the Inspector SBOM Generator) and submitting it to the Inspector Scan API as a pipeline build step; AWS documentation states this lets teams 'investigate and remediate risks before deployment,' and the pipeline can be configured to fail the build on critical findings, blocking the push entirely. Options A, B, and D all rely on ECR image scanning (basic or enhanced), which only scans images that have already been pushed into the repository — by definition this is detection-after-the-fact, not prevention, even if EventBridge/Lambda automation later quarantines or deletes the non-compliant image. Since the incident specifically involved an image already reaching ECR from an external pipeline, the fix must move the gate upstream into the CI/CD process itself, which only option C does.","explanation_zh":"題目要求「防止」有漏洞的映像檔被推送到 ECR，這代表漏洞檢查必須發生在 CI/CD 建置階段之前/期間，而不是映像檔已經進入 registry 之後。Amazon Inspector 的 CI/CD 整合做法是在管線的建置步驟中，透過 Inspector SBOM Generator 為容器映像產生 CycloneDX 格式的 SBOM，再呼叫 Inspector Scan API 進行掃描；AWS 官方文件明確指出這能讓團隊「在部署前調查並修復風險」，且管線可設定在出現 critical 等級發現時使 pipeline 失敗，從而完全阻擋推送動作。選項 A、B、D 都是依賴 ECR 映像掃描（basic 或 enhanced），這類掃描只會對已經推送進 repository 的映像檔進行掃描——本質上是事後偵測，即使搭配 EventBridge/Lambda 自動化後續隔離或刪除不合規映像，也無法阻止映像檔一開始就被推送進去。既然事故本身就是外部管線已把映像推入 ECR 造成的，修補點必須往前移到 CI/CD 流程本身，只有選項 C 做到這點。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"ECR enhanced scanning only scans images that are already stored in the repository (on push or continuously); adding a Lambda to react to findings can quarantine/delete an image afterward but cannot stop the initial push from succeeding, so it does not 'prevent' the push.","why_zh":"ECR enhanced scanning 只會掃描已經存放在 repository 中的映像檔（推送時或持續掃描）；即使加上 Lambda 對發現結果做反應，頂多是事後隔離或刪除映像，無法阻止最初的推送成功，因此不算「防止」推送。"},{"letter":"B","why_en":"This is the classic 'detect and react' pattern: Inspector scans images already in ECR, EventBridge captures the finding event, and Lambda takes remedial action — all of which happens after the vulnerable image has already been pushed, not before.","why_zh":"這是典型的「偵測後反應」模式：Inspector 掃描已存在 ECR 的映像檔，EventBridge 擷取發現事件，Lambda 執行補救動作——這一切都發生在有漏洞的映像檔已經被推送之後，而非之前。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"Basic continuous ECR scanning is even more limited (OS package CVEs only via Clair-based scanning) and, like enhanced scanning, only operates on images already pushed to the registry — it cannot block a push from completing.","why_zh":"Basic continuous ECR scanning 功能更有限（僅透過 Clair 型引擎掃描作業系統套件的 CVE），且與 enhanced scanning 一樣，只能作用在已經推送到 registry 的映像檔上——無法阻擋推送動作完成。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/inspector/latest/user/scanning-cicd.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/inspector/latest/user/cicd-custom.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/inspector/latest/user/configure-cicd-account.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonECR/latest/userguide/image-scanning.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonECR/latest/userguide/image-scanning-basic-enabling.html"]}},{"id":167,"question_en":"A company has a platform that is divided into 12 AWS accounts under the same organization in AWS Organizations. Many of these accounts use Amazon API Gateway to expose APIs to the company ' s frontend applications. The company needs to protect the existing APIs and any resources that will be deployed in the future against common SQL injection and bot attacks. Which solution will meet these requirements with the LEAST operational overhead?","question_zh":"一家公司拥有一个平台，该平台在 AWS Organizations 中的同一组织下划分为 12 个 AWS 账户。其中 许多账户使用 Amazon API Gateway 将 API 暴露给公司的前端应用程序。该公司需要保护现有的 API 以及未来部署的任何资源，使其免受常见的 SQL 注入和机器人攻击。 哪种解决方案能在最少的操作开销下满足这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Create an AWS WAF web ACL for each API. Include managed rules to block SQL injection and bot attacks. Use AWS Config to detect new resources that do not have a web ACL. Configure a remediation action to provision a web ACL for these resources.","B":"Use AWS Firewall Manager to create an AWS WAF policy. Configure the policy to include the AWS Bot Control and SQL database managed rule groups. Set the policy scope to include the API Gateway stage as the resource type.","C":"Create an AWS Service Catalog product for an AWS WAF web ACL that includes rules to block SQL injection and bot attacks. Use AWS Config to detect new resources that do not have this product applied. Configure a remediation action to provision a web ACL for these resources.","D":"Use AWS Security Hub to detect unprotected resources and to send the findings as custom action events to Amazon EventBridge. Create an AWS Lambda function for these events to provision an AWS WAF web ACL for the unprotected resources. Include managed rules to block SQL injection and bot attacks."},"options_zh":{"A":"为每个API创建一个AWS WAF网络ACL，包含用于阻止SQL注入和机器人攻击的托管规则。 使用AWS Config检测未配置网络ACL的新资源，并设置修复操作，自动为这些资源创建网 络ACL。","B":"使用 AWS Firewall Manager 创建 AWS WAF 策略。配置该策略以包含 AWS Bot Control 和 SQL 数据库托管规则组，并将策略范围设置为包含 API Gateway 阶段作为资源类型。","C":"创建一个 AWS 服务目录产品，用于 AWS WAF 网站访问控制列表（web ACL），其中包含阻 止 SQL 注入和机器人攻击的规则。使用 AWS Config 检测未应用此产品的新增资源，并配置 修复操作，为这些资源自动创建网站访问控制列表。","D":"使用 AWS Security Hub 检测未受保护的资源，并将发现结果作为自定义操作事件发送至 Amazon EventBridge。为这些事件创建一个 AWS Lambda 函数，用于为未受保护的资源配置 AWS WAF 网站访问控制列表（web ACL），并包含托管规则以阻止 SQL 注入和机器人攻击。"},"answer":["B"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Organizations/Governance","Security/IAM","Compute","Database","Serverless/Integration","Monitoring/Ops"],"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選","research":{"verdict":["B"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"community","explanation_en":"B is correct. The scenario's decisive features are: (1) 12 accounts under one AWS Organization, (2) a requirement to protect both existing APIs AND any future/not-yet-deployed resources, and (3) the qualifier 'LEAST operational overhead.' AWS Firewall Manager is purpose-built for exactly this combination. Per AWS's Firewall Manager documentation, a Firewall Manager AWS WAF policy lets an administrator specify rule groups once and Firewall Manager then centrally creates and manages web ACLs for all in-scope resources across the organization's accounts (docs: waf-policies.html). Critically, the policy scope documentation states: 'When you add a new account or resource to your organization, Firewall Manager automatically assesses it against your settings for each policy and applies the policy based on these settings' and 'Firewall Manager manages them continuously and applies them to new AWS accounts and resources as they are added' (docs: policy-scope.html). This means new API Gateway APIs deployed later are automatically protected with zero extra steps -- satisfying 'any resources that will be deployed in the future' with essentially no ongoing operational work. The policy can include the AWS-managed Bot Control rule group (for bot attacks) and the SQL database managed rule group (AWSManagedRulesSQLiRuleSet, for SQL injection) as a single set of rule groups applied org-wide, and API Gateway stages are a documented Firewall Manager/WAF resource type (confirmed by the AWS Config managed rule fms-webacl-resource-policy-check, which checks web ACL association for ALB, API Gateway stage, or CloudFront distribution). Options A, C, and D all require building and operating custom detect-and-remediate pipelines (AWS Config + remediation, Service Catalog + Config, or Security Hub + EventBridge + Lambda) that must be created, maintained, and kept correct across 12 accounts -- each is real, recurring engineering and operational burden compared to Firewall Manager's single centrally-managed policy that AWS itself keeps continuously enforced.","explanation_zh":"正確答案為 B。本題的關鍵線索是:(1) 12 個帳戶同屬一個 AWS Organization、(2) 需求同時涵蓋既有 API 與『未來部署』的資源、(3) 限定詞為『最少維運負擔』。AWS Firewall Manager 正是為此組合情境而設計。根據 AWS Firewall Manager 官方文件,Firewall Manager 的 AWS WAF policy 讓管理者只需設定一次規則群組,Firewall Manager 便會集中為 organization 中所有納入範圍(in-scope)的資源建立並管理 web ACL(文件:waf-policies.html)。更關鍵的是,policy scope 文件明確指出:『當您的 organization 新增帳戶或資源時,Firewall Manager 會自動依您為每個 policy 設定的條件進行評估,並依此套用 policy』,且『Firewall Manager 會持續管理這些 policy,並在新帳戶與資源加入時自動套用』(文件:policy-scope.html)。這代表日後新部署的 API Gateway API 會自動受到保護,完全不需要額外步驟——完美對應『未來部署的資源』這項需求,且幾乎沒有持續性維運工作。該 policy 可同時納入 AWS 受管的 Bot Control 規則群組(防禦機器人攻擊)與 SQL database 受管規則群組(AWSManagedRulesSQLiRuleSet,防禦 SQL injection),以單一組規則群組套用至整個組織;而 API Gateway stage 也確實是 Firewall Manager/WAF 文件記載的資源類型(可由 AWS Config 受管規則 fms-webacl-resource-policy-check 佐證,該規則會檢查 web ACL 是否已關聯至 ALB、API Gateway stage 或 CloudFront distribution)。選項 A、C、D 都需要自行建置並維運一套『偵測後補救』的客製化管線(AWS Config + 補救動作、Service Catalog + Config,或 Security Hub + EventBridge + Lambda),這些管線必須在 12 個帳戶間建立、維護並確保正確運作——相較於 Firewall Manager 這種由 AWS 原生持續強制執行的單一集中式 policy,前述方案都帶來真實且持續的工程與維運負擔。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"Creating a separate web ACL per API (across 12 accounts) plus a custom AWS Config rule and remediation action to catch and fix new unprotected resources is a self-built detect-and-remediate pipeline that must be deployed and maintained per account. It technically can work, but it duplicates functionality that Firewall Manager already provides natively and centrally, so it fails the 'LEAST operational overhead' bar.","why_zh":"為每個 API(跨 12 個帳戶)個別建立 web ACL,再加上自訂的 AWS Config 規則與補救動作來偵測並修復未受保護的新資源,等於自行打造一套『偵測後補救』管線,且必須在每個帳戶部署與維護。技術上可行,但重複了 Firewall Manager 原生集中提供的功能,無法滿足『最少維運負擔』的要求。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"Building and maintaining an AWS Service Catalog product for a WAF web ACL, plus AWS Config detection and remediation to enforce its use, is even more custom engineering than option A -- it requires provisioning portfolios/products across 12 accounts and a separate compliance-check/remediation loop. This is more operational overhead, not less, than a single Firewall Manager policy.","why_zh":"建置並維護一個包含 WAF web ACL 的 AWS Service Catalog 產品,再搭配 AWS Config 偵測與補救動作強制套用,比選項 A 需要更多客製化工程——必須在 12 個帳戶中佈建 portfolio/product,並建立另一套合規檢查與補救迴圈。相較於單一 Firewall Manager policy,這是更多而非更少的維運負擔。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"Using Security Hub findings routed through EventBridge to trigger a custom Lambda function that provisions web ACLs is a fully custom, reactive automation pipeline that the company must design, code, test, and operate itself across the organization. It depends on Security Hub first generating a finding (a lag/detection gap) and on custom Lambda logic staying correct as APIs change, making it substantially higher operational overhead than a native, continuously-enforced Firewall Manager policy.","why_zh":"透過 Security Hub 的發現事件經由 EventBridge 觸發自訂 Lambda 函式來佈建 web ACL,是一套完全客製化的被動式自動化管線,公司必須自行設計、撰寫、測試並在整個組織中維運。此方案仰賴 Security Hub 先產生發現事件(存在偵測延遲/落差),且自訂 Lambda 邏輯須隨 API 變動持續保持正確,相較於原生且持續強制執行的 Firewall Manager policy,維運負擔明顯更高。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/waf/latest/developerguide/waf-policies.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/waf/latest/developerguide/policy-scope.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/waf/latest/developerguide/create-policy.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/waf/latest/developerguide/aws-managed-rule-groups-bot.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/waf/latest/developerguide/aws-managed-rule-groups-list.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/config/latest/developerguide/fms-webacl-resource-policy-check.html"]}},{"id":168,"question_en":"A company ' s security engineer is designing an isolation procedure for Amazon EC2 instances as part of an incident response plan. The security engineer needs to isolate a target instance to block any traffic to and from the target instance, except for traffic from the company ' s forensics team. Each of the company ' s EC2 instances has its own dedicated security group. The EC2 instances are deployed in subnets of a VPC. A subnet can contain multiple instances. The security engineer is testing the procedure for EC2 isolation and opens an SSH session to the target instance. The procedure starts to simulate access to the target instance by an attacker. The security engineerremoves the existing security group rules and adds security group rules to give the forensics team access to the target instance on port 22. After these changes, the security engineer notices that the SSH connection is still active and usable. When the security engineer runs a ping command to the public IP address of the target instance, the ping command is blocked. What should the security engineer do to isolate the target instance?","question_zh":"一家公司的安全工程师正在为亚马逊EC2实例设计隔离流程，作为事件响应计划的一部分。该安全工程师需要将目标实例隔 离，以阻止除公司取证团队外的所有进出该实例的流量。公司每台EC2实例都有其专用的安全组，这些实例部署在VPC的子 网中，一个子网可包含多台实例。 安全工程师正在测试EC2隔离流程，并通过SSH会话连接到目标实例。该流程开始模拟攻击者对目标实例的访问。安全 工程师删除现有的安全组规则，并添加新的安全组规则，以便取证团队能够通过22端口访问目标实例。 经过这些更改后，安全工程师发现SSH连接仍然处于活动状态且可用。但当安全工程师向目标实例的公网IP地址执行ping 命令时，该ping命令被阻止了。 安全工程师应采取什么措施来隔离目标实例？","options_en":{"A":"Add an inbound rule to the security group to allow traffic from 0.0.0.0/0 for all ports. Add an outbound rule to the security group to allow traffic to 0.0.0.0/0 for all ports. Then immediately delete these rules.","B":"Remove the port 22 security group rule. Attach an instance role policy that allows AWS Systems Manager Session Manager connections so that the forensics team can access the target instance.","C":"Create a network ACL that is associated with the target instance ' s subnet. Add a rule at the top of the inbound rule set to deny all traffic from 0.0.0.0/0. Add a rule at the top of the outbound rule set to deny all traffic to 0.0.0.0/0.","D":"Create an AWS Systems Manager document that adds a host-level firewall rule to block all inbound traffic and outbound traffic. Run the document on the target instance."},"options_zh":{"A":"向安全组添加入站规则，允许来自 0.0.0.0/0 的所有端口流量；向安全组添加出站规则，允许去往 0.0.0.0/0 的所有端 口流量。然后立即删除这些规则。","B":"删除端口22的安全组规则。附加一个允许AWS Systems Manager Session Manager连接的实例角色策略，以便取 证团队能够访问目标实例。","C":"创建一个与目标实例所在子网关联的网络ACL。在入站规则集顶部添加一条规则，拒绝来自0.0.0.0/0的所有流量；在 出站规则集顶部添加一条规则，拒绝发往0.0.0.0/0的所有流量。","D":"创建一个 AWS Systems Manager 文档，用于添加主机级防火墙规则以阻止所有传入和传出流量，并在目标实例上 运行该文档。"},"answer":["C"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Compute","Monitoring/Ops"],"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選","research":{"verdict":["C"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"both","explanation_en":"Security groups use connection tracking and are stateful: per the EC2 User Guide, 'When you change a security group rule, its tracked connections are not immediately interrupted. The security group continues to allow packets until existing connections time out.' This is exactly what the engineer observed — removing/re-adding SG rules blocked the NEW ping (untracked) attempt but did not kill the already-tracked SSH session. The same doc gives the fix verbatim: 'To ensure that traffic is immediately interrupted... you can use a network ACL for your subnet. Network ACLs are stateless and therefore do not automatically allow response traffic. Adding a network ACL that blocks traffic in either direction breaks existing connections.' Option C applies exactly that documented remedy — a deny-all NACL on the instance's subnet — which forcibly terminates the already-open SSH session because NACLs evaluate every packet (including return packets of established flows) with no connection-state exemption. Option A never isolates anything (it briefly opens 0.0.0.0/0 both ways, the opposite of isolation, and still wouldn't force-close the tracked session). Option B only changes the future access method (SSM Session Manager) but does nothing to the already-tracked, currently-open SSH connection since SG edits don't retroactively affect tracked flows. Option D depends on unconfirmed prerequisites (SSM Agent + instance role already present) and operates inside the guest OS, which is not the AWS-documented mechanism for this specific SG-connection-tracking gap — the VPC networking layer (NACL) is the sanctioned tool.","explanation_zh":"Security group 使用 connection tracking，屬於 stateful:EC2 使用者指南明白寫道:「When you change a security group rule, its tracked connections are not immediately interrupted. The security group continues to allow packets until existing connections time out.」這正是題目情境——移除/重建 SG 規則後，「新」的 ping(未被追蹤)被擋下，但已經被追蹤的既有 SSH 連線並未中斷。同一份文件也給出明確解法:「To ensure that traffic is immediately interrupted... you can use a network ACL for your subnet. Network ACLs are stateless and therefore do not automatically allow response traffic. Adding a network ACL that blocks traffic in either direction breaks existing connections.」選項 C 正是套用這個官方解法——在該 instance 所在 subnet 建立 deny-all 的 NACL——因為 NACL 針對每個封包(含已建立連線的回應封包)逐一評估、沒有連線狀態豁免，所以能強制中斷已開啟的 SSH session。選項 A 完全沒有做到隔離(短暫開放 0.0.0.0/0 雙向等於隔離的反面)，且仍無法強制關閉已被追蹤的連線。選項 B 只是改變「未來」的存取方式(改用 SSM Session Manager)，對已經被追蹤、目前仍開著的 SSH 連線毫無作用，因為修改 SG 規則本就不會回溯影響已追蹤流量。選項 D 依賴未經確認的前提(instance 需已安裝 SSM Agent 並具備對應 IAM role)，且作用在 guest OS 層級，並非 AWS 文件針對這個 SG connection-tracking 缺口所指定的官方解法——VPC 網路層(NACL)才是官方認可的工具。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"Temporarily opening all inbound/outbound traffic to 0.0.0.0/0 is the opposite of isolation and creates a security exposure window; deleting the rules afterward still leaves any connections established during that window subject to the same stateful connection-tracking persistence problem, so it does not solve the observed issue.","why_zh":"暫時開放全部進出流量給 0.0.0.0/0 正好與隔離目的相反，會製造一段安全暴露空窗;之後刪除規則，在該空窗期間建立的連線一樣會遇到相同的 stateful connection-tracking 持續存在問題，並未解決題目觀察到的現象。"},{"letter":"B","why_en":"Switching future access to SSM Session Manager is good practice for avoiding open inbound ports, but it does not address why the already-open SSH connection from before the SG change is still usable — that persistence is due to security-group connection tracking, which SG rule edits (including removing port 22) do not retroactively affect.","why_zh":"改用 SSM Session Manager 作為未來存取方式雖是避免開放 inbound port 的良好作法，但完全沒有處理「SG 變更前就已建立的 SSH 連線為何仍可用」這個核心問題——那是 security group connection tracking 造成的持續性，修改 SG 規則(含移除 port 22)並不會回溯影響已追蹤的流量。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"Pushing a host-level (OS) firewall rule via an SSM document requires the SSM Agent and an IAM instance profile with SSM permissions to already be configured on the instance — not stated in the scenario — and it operates at the guest-OS layer rather than using the VPC-level tool (network ACL) that AWS documentation specifically prescribes for forcing an end to security-group-tracked connections.","why_zh":"透過 SSM document 下發 host-level(作業系統層)防火牆規則，前提是該 instance 已安裝 SSM Agent 且已附加具備 SSM 權限的 IAM instance profile——題目情境並未確認具備此前提;而且此法作用在 guest OS 層，並非 AWS 文件針對強制中斷 security-group 已追蹤連線所明確指定的 VPC 層工具(network ACL)。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AWSEC2/latest/UserGuide/security-group-connection-tracking.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/vpc/latest/userguide/infrastructure-security.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/vpc/latest/userguide/vpc-network-acls.html"]}},{"id":169,"question_en":"A company uses several AWS CloudFormation stacks to handle the deployment of a suite of applications. The leader of the company ' s application development team notices that the stack deployments fail with permission errors when some team members try to deploy the stacks. However, other team members can deploy the stacks successfully. The team members access the account by assuming a role that has a specific set of permissions. All team members have permissions to perform operations on the stacks. Which combination of steps will ensure consistent deployment of the stacksMOST securely? (Select THREE.)","question_zh":"一家公司使用多个 AWS CloudFormation 堆栈来部署一套应用程序。该公司应用开发团队的负责 人注意到，当部分团队成员尝试部署这些堆栈时，会因权限错误导致部署失败，而其他团队成员 却能成功部署。 团队成员通过承担具有特定权限集的角色来访问该账户。所有团队成员都拥有对堆栈执行操作 的权限。 以下哪三个步骤的组合能最安全地确保堆栈的一致部署？（选择三项。）","options_en":{"A":"Create a service role that has a composite principal that contains each service that needs the necessary permissions.","B":"Create a service role that has cloudformation.amazonaws.com as the service principal.","C":"Add policies that reference each CloudFormation stack ARN.","D":"Add policies that reference the ARNs of each AWS service that requires permissions.","E":"Update each stack to use the service role.","F":"Add a policy to each member role to allow the iam:PassRole action for the service role."},"options_zh":{"A":"创建一个服务角色，该角色包含一个复合主体，其中涵盖所有需要必要权限的服务。","B":"创建一个服务角色，其服务主体为 cloudformation.amazonaws.com。","C":"添加引用每个 CloudFormation 堆栈 ARN 的策略。","D":"添加引用每个需要权限的 AWS 服务 ARN 的策略。","E":"更新每个堆栈以使用服务角色。","F":"为每个成员角色添加策略，允许其执行 iam:PassRole 操作以用于服务角色。"},"answer":["B","E","F"],"multi":true,"vote":{},"tags":["Security/IAM","Monitoring/Ops"],"difficulty":2,"diff_why":"複選","research":{"verdict":["B","E","F"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"both","explanation_en":"The root cause is that CloudFormation, by default, uses the caller's own IAM credentials to perform stack operations, so deployments succeed or fail depending on the permissions of whichever team member's assumed role triggers them. The documented fix is a CloudFormation service role: an IAM role that CloudFormation itself assumes to perform all stack actions, decoupling the outcome from the caller's permission set. Per AWS docs (using-iam-servicerole.html), you (1) create the service role with cloudformation.amazonaws.com as the trusted service principal (option B), (2) associate/update each stack to use that service role so CloudFormation consistently uses its credentials for every operation on the stack (option E), and (3) grant the calling principals (team members) the iam:PassRole permission on that service role, because AWS requires a user to have PassRole before they can specify a role for a service to assume, per id_roles_use_passrole.html (option F). This is the most secure approach because it enforces least privilege: team members keep their own limited roles for everyday work, while the fixed, explicitly-scoped service role determines exactly what CloudFormation can provision, and PassRole with a resource ARN condition lets you tightly control who may attach that specific role to a stack. Option A (composite principal across multiple AWS services) is unnecessary and wrong—the service role's trust policy only needs cloudformation.amazonaws.com as principal, not every downstream service. Option C (policies referencing stack ARNs) doesn't grant CloudFormation any ability to create/manage the actual AWS resources (EC2, S3, etc.) inside the stack, so it does not solve the permission-consistency problem. Option D ('ARNs of each AWS service that requires permissions') is a plausible-sounding but technically muddled distractor: IAM permission policies authorize actions/resources, not 'AWS service ARNs' as a category, and the docs describe creating the service role's permission policy as part of role creation (bundled into B), not as an independent named step tested here.","explanation_zh":"根本原因在於 CloudFormation 預設會用呼叫者本身的 IAM 憑證來執行堆疊操作，因此部署成功與否取決於觸發部署的團隊成員所擔任角色的權限——這就是為何某些成員能成功、某些卻遇到權限錯誤。AWS 官方文件（using-iam-servicerole.html）記載的解法是使用 CloudFormation service role：一個由 CloudFormation 本身擔任（assume）以執行所有堆疊操作的 IAM role，讓結果與呼叫者的權限脫鉤。具體步驟為：(1) 建立 service role，並以 cloudformation.amazonaws.com 作為受信任的服務主體（選項 B）；(2) 將每個堆疊更新為使用該 service role，讓 CloudFormation 在該堆疊的所有操作中一致地使用此角色的憑證（選項 E）；(3) 授予呼叫的團隊成員角色 iam:PassRole 權限，因為根據 id_roles_use_passrole.html，使用者必須先擁有 PassRole 權限，才能指定要讓服務擔任的角色（選項 F）。這是最安全的做法，因為它落實最小權限原則：團隊成員平時仍使用自己受限的角色，而由這個範圍明確、固定的 service role 決定 CloudFormation 究竟能佈建什麼，並且可用附帶資源 ARN 條件的 PassRole 嚴格控管誰能把該特定角色指派給堆疊。選項 A（跨多個 AWS 服務的複合主體）是不必要且錯誤的——service role 的信任政策只需要 cloudformation.amazonaws.com 作為主體，不需要涵蓋每個下游服務。選項 C（參照堆疊 ARN 的政策）並未賦予 CloudFormation 建立/管理堆疊內實際 AWS 資源（如 EC2、S3 等）的能力，因此無法解決權限不一致的問題。選項 D（『參照每個需要權限之 AWS 服務的 ARN』）看似合理但技術上含糊：IAM 權限政策授權的是動作／資源，而非以『AWS 服務 ARN』作為分類單位；且文件將建立 service role 的權限政策視為建立角色（選項 B）的一部分，而非此處測驗的獨立步驟。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"A composite principal spanning multiple AWS services is unnecessary; the service role's trust policy only needs cloudformation.amazonaws.com as the principal, since CloudFormation itself is what assumes the role and then acts on the various downstream services.","why_zh":"涵蓋多個 AWS 服務的複合主體並非必要；service role 的信任政策只需要 cloudformation.amazonaws.com 作為主體，因為是 CloudFormation 本身擔任該角色後再去操作各下游服務。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"Policies referencing CloudFormation stack ARNs would control who can operate on the stack resource itself, but they grant no ability to create/modify the underlying AWS resources (EC2, S3, etc.) the stack provisions, so this does not fix the inconsistent-permission problem.","why_zh":"參照 CloudFormation 堆疊 ARN 的政策只能控制誰能操作堆疊資源本身,但無法賦予建立/修改堆疊所佈建之底層 AWS 資源（如 EC2、S3）的能力,因此無法解決權限不一致的問題。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"IAM permission policies are built around actions and resource ARNs, not 'ARNs of AWS services'; this option misdescribes how the service role's permission policy is structured and is not one of the three discrete steps AWS documents for setting up and using a CloudFormation service role.","why_zh":"IAM 權限政策是以動作與資源 ARN 為核心建構,而非『AWS 服務的 ARN』;此選項對 service role 權限政策的結構描述有誤,也不是 AWS 文件中設定與使用 CloudFormation service role 的三個具體步驟之一。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AWSCloudFormation/latest/UserGuide/using-iam-servicerole.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/IAM/latest/UserGuide/id_roles_use_passrole.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AWSCloudFormation/latest/UserGuide/security-best-practices.html"]}},{"id":170,"question_en":"A startup company is using a single AWS account that has resources in a single AWS Region. A security engineer configures an AWS CloudTrail trail in the same Region to deliver log files to an Amazon S3 bucket by using the AWS CLI. Because of expansion, the company adds resources in multiple Regions. The security engineer notices that the logs from the new Regions are not reaching the S3 bucket. What should the security engineer do to fix this issue with the LEAST amount of operational overhead?","question_zh":"一家初创公司正在使用一个AWS账户，其资源位于单一的AWS区域。安全工程师在同一个区域配置了AWS CloudTrail追踪， 通过AWS CLI将日志文件发送到Amazon S3存储桶。由于业务扩展，该公司在多个区域添加了资源。但安全工程师发现，来 自新区域的日志未能传送到S3存储桶。 安全工程师应采取什么措施来解决此问题，且以最少的操作开销？","options_en":{"A":"Create a new CloudTrail trail. Select the new Regions where the company added resources.","B":"Change the S3 bucket to receive notifications to track all actions from all Regions.","C":"Create a new CloudTrail trail that applies to all Regions.","D":"Change the existing CloudTrail trail so that it applies to all Regions."},"options_zh":{"A":"创建一个新的 CloudTrail 跟踪，选择公司新增资源所在的区域。","B":"将S3存储桶更改为接收通知，以跟踪所有区域中的所有操作。","C":"创建一个适用于所有区域的新 CloudTrail 跟踪。","D":"修改现有的 CloudTrail 跟踪，使其适用于所有区域。"},"answer":["D"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Storage","Monitoring/Ops"],"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選","research":{"verdict":["D"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"AWS CloudTrail documentation explicitly covers this exact scenario: converting an existing single-Region trail into a multi-Region trail using the AWS CLI. The official guide 'Receiving CloudTrail log files from multiple Regions' states: 'To change an existing trail so that it applies to all enabled Regions, add the --is-multi-region-trail option to the update-trail command' (e.g., `aws cloudtrail update-trail --name my-trail --is-multi-region-trail`). A multi-Region trail automatically logs events from all Regions enabled in the account — including any Region added later — and delivers them all to the same existing S3 bucket, with zero need to create new trails, new buckets, or new notification pipelines. This is the textbook least-operational-overhead fix: one CLI update command on the existing trail. Creating a brand-new trail (option A, limited to the new Regions, or option C, a new all-Region trail) would work technically but means managing a second trail/duplicated global service events and more resources to maintain — strictly more operational overhead than simply flipping the existing trail to multi-Region. Option B (S3 notifications) doesn't create CloudTrail logs at all and is a non-solution.","explanation_zh":"AWS CloudTrail 官方文件明確涵蓋此情境：使用 AWS CLI 將既有的單一 Region trail 轉換成多 Region trail。官方指南〈Receiving CloudTrail log files from multiple Regions〉指出：「若要讓既有 trail 套用到所有已啟用的 Region，在 update-trail 指令加上 --is-multi-region-trail 選項」（例如 `aws cloudtrail update-trail --name my-trail --is-multi-region-trail`）。多 Region trail 會自動記錄帳戶中所有已啟用 Region（包含之後新增的 Region）的事件，並全部送到同一個既有 S3 儲存貯體，完全不需要建立新 trail、新儲存貯體或新的通知管線。這正是「最少維運負擔」的標準解法——只需對既有 trail 下一個 CLI 更新指令。建立新 trail（選項 A 僅涵蓋新 Region，或選項 C 建立涵蓋所有 Region 的新 trail）在技術上雖可行，但代表要維護第二個 trail、重複的全域服務事件與更多資源，維運負擔嚴格高於直接把既有 trail 改成多 Region。選項 B（S3 通知）根本不會產生 CloudTrail 記錄，並非解法。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"Creating a new trail limited only to the new Regions works but adds a second trail to manage, duplicates global service event handling, and doesn't consolidate logging as cleanly — more operational overhead than updating the existing trail in place.","why_zh":"建立僅涵蓋新 Region 的新 trail雖可行，但會多一個 trail 要維護，且會重複處理全域服務事件，記錄也無法乾淨地整合——維運負擔高於直接就地更新既有 trail。"},{"letter":"B","why_en":"S3 event notifications track object-level actions on the bucket itself; they do not capture AWS API activity across Regions and are unrelated to CloudTrail's region coverage problem — this does not solve the issue at all.","why_zh":"S3 事件通知追蹤的是該儲存貯體本身的物件層級操作，並不會擷取跨 Region 的 AWS API 活動，與 CloudTrail 的 Region 涵蓋問題無關——根本無法解決此問題。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"Creating a brand-new multi-Region trail would fix the coverage gap but leaves the original trail still running (duplicate logs/cost) unless manually deleted, requiring more steps than simply converting the existing trail with update-trail --is-multi-region-trail.","why_zh":"建立全新的多 Region trail 確實能補上涵蓋缺口，但除非手動刪除原本的 trail，否則舊 trail 仍會繼續運作（重複記錄、增加成本），所需步驟比直接用 update-trail --is-multi-region-trail 轉換既有 trail 更多。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/awscloudtrail/latest/userguide/receive-cloudtrail-log-files-from-multiple-regions.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/awscloudtrail/latest/userguide/cloudtrail-create-and-update-a-trail-by-using-the-aws-cli-update-trail.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/awscloudtrail/latest/userguide/cloudtrail-multi-region-trails.html"]}},{"id":171,"question_en":"A company is using an organization in AWS Organizations that contains 100 accounts. The company hasconfigured trusted access for Amazon GuardDuty to AWS Organizations within the management account. The company has designated a member account to be the GuardDuty administrator for the organization. GuardDuty is working properly and reports findings for the organization in the GuardDuty console. The company wants a SecOps team to receive real-time email alerts from any GuardDuty finding within the organization that is high severity according to GuardDuty severity levels. Which solution will meet these requirements?","question_zh":"一家公司正在使用 AWS Organizations 中包含 100 个账户的组织。该公司已在管理账户中为 Amazon GuardDuty 配置了对 AWS Organizations 的受信任访问权限，并指定一个成员账户作为该组织的 GuardDuty 管理员。 GuardDuty 运行正常，并在 GuardDuty 控制台中为该组织报告发现的异常情况。公司希望安全运维团队能够实时收到邮件告 警，以便及时了解组织内根据 GuardDuty 严重性等级判定为高风险的任何发现。 哪种解决方案能满足这些要求","options_en":{"A":"In the management account, create a rule in Amazon EventBridge that will react to a GuardDuty finding that has a high severity level. Configure the rule to notify an Amazon SNS topic. Subscribe the SecOps team’s email addresses to the SNS topic.","B":"Configure trusted access for AWS Config within the organization. Create a rule in AWS Config to monitor for any non-archived findings in GuardDuty. Create a rule in Amazon EventBridge that will react if AWS Config detects a compliance change for the AWS Config rule. Configure the EventBridge rule to target an Amazon SNS topic. Subscribe the SecOps team’s email addresses to the SNS topic.","C":"In the GuardDuty delegated administrator account, configure a rule in Amazon EventBridge that will react to a GuardDuty finding that has a high severity level. Configure the rule to notify an Amazon SNS topic. Subscribe the SecOps team’s email addresses to the SNS topic.","D":"Configure AWS CloudTrail for the organization in the management account. Create a rule in Amazon EventBridge that will run on a ListFindings API call. Configure the rule to notify an Amazon SNS topic. Subscribe the SecOps team’s email addresses to the SNS topic."},"options_zh":{"B":"在组织内为 AWS Config 配置可信访问。在 AWS Config 中创建规则，用于监控 GuardDuty 中任何未归档的发现项。在 Amazon EventBridge 中创建规则，当 AWS Config 检测到 AWS Config 规则的合规性变更时触发响应。将 EventBridge 规则配置为目标 为 Amazon SNS 主题。将 SecOps 团队的电子邮件地址订阅到该 SNS 主题。","C":"在 GuardDuty 委托管理员账户中，配置 Amazon EventBridge 的一条规则，用于响应严重级别为“高”的 GuardDuty 发现项。将 该规则设置为通知一个 Amazon SNS 主题，并将 SecOps 团队的电子邮件地址订阅到该 SNS 主题。","D":"在管理账户中为组织配置 AWS CloudTrail。在 Amazon EventBridge 中创建一个规则，使其在 执行 ListFindings API 调用时触发，并将该规则配置为通知一个 Amazon SNS 主题。然后将 安全运维团队的电子邮件地址订阅到该 SNS 主题。","A":"在管理账户中，于 Amazon EventBridge 创建一条规则，用于响应严重级别为高的 GuardDuty 发现项。将该规则配置为通知一个 Amazon SNS 主题，并将 SecOps 团队的电子邮件地址订阅到该 SNS 主题。"},"answer":["C"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Organizations/Governance","Security/IAM","Serverless/Integration","Monitoring/Ops"],"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選","research":{"verdict":["C"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"both","explanation_en":"AWS GuardDuty documentation explicitly states that in a multi-account (AWS Organizations) setup, EventBridge rules configured in the delegated GuardDuty administrator account trigger based on applicable findings from all associated member accounts: \"EventBridge rules in your administrator account will trigger based on applicable findings from your member accounts. If you set up finding notifications through EventBridge in your administrator account, you will receive notifications of findings from both your account and member accounts.\" Since the company designated a member account (not the management account) as the GuardDuty delegated administrator, that delegated administrator account is the only place where a single EventBridge rule can see findings aggregated across the entire organization. Building the rule there with an event pattern matching high-severity findings (detail.severity in the high range) and targeting an SNS topic with email subscriptions satisfies the real-time, org-wide, high-severity-only alerting requirement with a single rule.","explanation_zh":"AWS GuardDuty 官方文件明確指出，在多帳戶（AWS Organizations）架構下，設在 GuardDuty 委派管理帳戶（delegated administrator account）中的 EventBridge 規則，會針對所有成員帳戶產生的相符 findings 觸發：「EventBridge rules in your administrator account will trigger based on applicable findings from your member accounts...you will receive notifications of findings from both your account and member accounts.」由於題目中公司是指定「某個成員帳戶」（而非管理帳戶）作為 GuardDuty 委派管理員，因此唯有在該委派管理帳戶建立 EventBridge 規則，才能用單一規則涵蓋整個組織所有帳戶的 findings。在該帳戶建立比對高嚴重度（detail.severity 落在 high 範圍）的事件規則，並將目標設為 SNS 主題、訂閱 SecOps 團隊 email，即可滿足即時、全組織、僅高嚴重度的警報需求。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"The management account only has trusted access configured for GuardDuty; it is not the GuardDuty delegated administrator (a member account was designated for that role). Per AWS docs, only the delegated administrator account's EventBridge rules aggregate findings across all member accounts, so a rule in the management account would not reliably receive findings events from every member account.","why_zh":"管理帳戶只是設定了 GuardDuty 的信任存取（trusted access），並非 GuardDuty 的委派管理帳戶（該角色已指派給某個成員帳戶）。根據 AWS 文件，只有委派管理帳戶的 EventBridge 規則才會匯總所有成員帳戶的 findings，因此在管理帳戶建立規則無法可靠地收到所有成員帳戶的 finding 事件。"},{"letter":"B","why_en":"GuardDuty findings are not evaluated or represented as AWS Config compliance items, and there is no native AWS Config rule type that monitors 'non-archived GuardDuty findings.' This option describes an integration that does not exist and adds unnecessary complexity and latency versus GuardDuty's native, purpose-built EventBridge finding events.","why_zh":"GuardDuty findings 並不會被評估或呈現為 AWS Config 的合規項目，也沒有原生的 AWS Config 規則類型可監控『未封存的 GuardDuty findings』。此選項描述了一個不存在的整合方式，相較於 GuardDuty 原生、專門設計的 EventBridge finding 事件，徒增不必要的複雜度與延遲。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"Reacting to a ListFindings CloudTrail API call is not equivalent to reacting to an actual finding's severity — ListFindings is just a read/query call that could return zero or many findings of any severity, and does not carry severity in a way EventBridge can filter on. This does not reliably produce real-time, severity-filtered alerts.","why_zh":"對 ListFindings 這個 CloudTrail API 呼叫做出反應，並不等於對實際 finding 的嚴重度做出反應——ListFindings 只是一個查詢/讀取呼叫，可能回傳零筆或多筆任意嚴重度的 findings，且其呼叫事件本身不含可供 EventBridge 篩選的嚴重度欄位。此作法無法可靠地產生即時且依嚴重度篩選的警報。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/guardduty/latest/ug/guardduty_findings_eventbridge.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/guardduty/latest/ug/administrator_member_relationships.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/guardduty/latest/ug/guardduty_accounts.html"]}},{"id":172,"question_en":"A company manages multiple AWS accounts through an organization in AWS Organizations. The company enables all features in the organization. A security team must implement a solution to centrally manage VPC security groups across the accounts. The company uses an existing reference security group with the required configuration. The solution must detect if security group rules have been modified to deviate from the reference security group. The solution must automatically restore any noncompliant security groups to match the reference security group. The security team needs to select a solution that does not require custom development or scripting. Which solution will meet these requirements?","question_zh":"一家公司通过 AWS Organizations 中的组织来管理多个 AWS 账户，并在该组织中启用了所有功能。 安全团队必须实施一种解决方案，以集中管理跨账户的VPC安全组。公司已使用一个具有所需配置的 现有参考安全组。该解决方案需检测安全组规则是否被修改，从而偏离了参考安全组。同时，解决方 案必须自动将任何不符合要求的安全组恢复为与参考安全组一致的状态。 安全团队需要选择一种无需自定义开发或脚本的解决方案。 哪种解决方案能满足这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Use AWS Firewall Manager to manage security group rules through security group policy rules.","B":"Create an AWS Systems Manager Automation runbook to identify and align noncompliant security groups with the reference security group.","C":"Use a custom AWS Config rule with auto remediation. Compare to the reference security group for compliance.","D":"Manage security groups through AWS CloudFormation StackSets. Use the reference security group for the initial rules."},"options_zh":{"A":"使用 AWS Firewall Manager 通过安全组策略规则来管理安全组规则。","B":"创建一个 AWS Systems Manager 自动化运行手册，用于识别并使不符合要求的安全组与参 考安全组保持一致。","C":"使用带有自动修复功能的自定义 AWS Config 规则，与参考安全组进行比较以确保合规性。","D":"通过 AWS CloudFormation StackSets 管理安全组。使用参考安全组作为初始规则。"},"answer":["A"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Organizations/Governance","Monitoring/Ops"],"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選","research":{"verdict":["A"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"AWS Firewall Manager security group policies include a \"content audit\" policy type that uses custom policy rules: you designate an existing security group as the \"audit security group\" (reference), and Firewall Manager compares all in-scope security groups across the AWS Organizations accounts against it, flagging any that deviate as noncompliant. When automatic remediation is enabled on the policy, Firewall Manager modifies the noncompliant security group to bring it back into compliance with the reference — exactly the detect-and-auto-restore behavior the question requires, centrally and organization-wide, with no Lambda functions, scripts, or runbooks to build. Option C is explicitly disqualified because it requires writing a *custom* AWS Config rule (and typically a Lambda-backed SSM Automation document for remediation), which violates the \"no custom development or scripting\" constraint. Option B (a Systems Manager Automation runbook) likewise requires building custom automation logic to compare against the reference and isn't a built-in, centrally managed detection mechanism. Option D (CloudFormation StackSets) can deploy the reference security group's initial rules, but it does not continuously detect drift or automatically revert out-of-band rule changes — CloudFormation drift detection is an on-demand, non-automatic operation, and StackSets does not re-apply the template unless you manually run an update. Only Firewall Manager's security group content audit policy natively satisfies continuous cross-account detection plus automatic remediation without custom code.","explanation_zh":"AWS Firewall Manager 的 security group policy 提供「content audit」政策類型，可使用 custom policy rules：指定一個既有的安全群組作為「audit security group」（參考基準），Firewall Manager 會將組織內所有納入範圍帳戶的安全群組與此參考基準比對，找出偏離設定的即標記為不合規。當政策啟用自動修復（automatic remediation）後，Firewall Manager 會修改不合規的安全群組，使其恢復符合參考基準——這正是題目要求的「偵測偏離＋自動還原」，而且是跨帳戶集中管理，完全不需要撰寫 Lambda、腳本或 runbook。選項 C 明確要求撰寫「custom」AWS Config rule（通常還需搭配 Lambda 或 SSM Automation 進行修復），違反「不得自訂開發或撰寫腳本」的限制。選項 B（Systems Manager Automation runbook）同樣需要自行建置比對與修復邏輯，並非內建的集中管理偵測機制。選項 D（CloudFormation StackSets）可用參考安全群組的規則做初始部署，但無法持續偵測 drift 並自動還原被人為修改的規則——CloudFormation 的 drift detection 是隨選（on-demand）且非自動的操作，StackSets 也不會在偵測到手動變更後自動重新套用範本。只有 Firewall Manager 的 security group content audit policy 能原生滿足「持續跨帳戶偵測＋自動修復」且不需自訂程式碼。","distractors":[{"letter":"B","why_en":"A Systems Manager Automation runbook to detect and align security groups is itself a piece of custom automation logic that the team would need to author and maintain — it fails the \"no custom development or scripting\" requirement and is not a purpose-built, centrally managed cross-account compliance mechanism.","why_zh":"用 Systems Manager Automation runbook 去偵測並校正安全群組，本身就是需要自行撰寫與維護的客製化自動化邏輯，違反「不得自訂開發或撰寫腳本」的要求，也不是專為跨帳戶集中合規管理設計的工具。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"The option explicitly calls for a *custom* AWS Config rule, which requires developing (typically Lambda-based) compliance-evaluation code and a remediation action — directly violating the stated constraint of no custom development or scripting.","why_zh":"此選項明確要求撰寫「custom」AWS Config rule，需要開發（通常是以 Lambda 為基礎）的合規評估程式碼與修復動作，直接違反題目「不得自訂開發或撰寫腳本」的限制。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"CloudFormation StackSets can push out the reference security group's initial configuration to multiple accounts, but it has no continuous, automatic drift-detection-and-revert capability; drift detection must be run on demand and does not by itself remediate manual rule changes.","why_zh":"CloudFormation StackSets 可以把參考安全群組的初始設定部署到多個帳戶，但它沒有持續且自動的 drift 偵測與還原能力；drift detection 必須手動觸發，且本身並不會自動修復被手動更動的規則。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/waf/latest/developerguide/security-group-policies-audit.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/waf/latest/developerguide/security-group-policies.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/waf/latest/developerguide/security-group-content-audit-policy-findings.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/waf/latest/developerguide/security-group-policies-common.html"]}},{"id":173,"question_en":"A company uses AWS Organizations and has an SCP at the root that prevents sharing resources with external accounts. The company now needs to allow only the marketing account to share resources externally while preventing all other accounts from doing so. All accounts are in the same OU. Which solution will meet these requirements?","question_zh":"一家公司使用 AWS Organizations，并在根目录下设置了一个 SCP，禁止与外部账户共享资源。现在该公司需要仅允许营销 账户对外部共享资源，同时阻止所有其他账户进行此类操作。所有账户均位于同一个组织单元（OU）中。 哪种解决方案能满足这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Create a new SCP in the marketing account to explicitly allow sharing.","B":"Edit the existing SCP to add a condition that excludes the marketing account.","C":"Edit the SCP to include an Allow statement for the marketing account.","D":"Use a permissions boundary in the marketing account."},"options_zh":{"A":"在营销账户中创建一个新的 SCP，以明确允许共享。","B":"编辑现有的SCP，添加一个排除营销账户的条件。","C":"编辑SCP，添加允许营销账户的语句。","D":"在营销账户中使用权限边界。"},"answer":["B"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Organizations/Governance"],"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選","research":{"verdict":["B"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"AWS Organizations SCP evaluation is deny-dominant: for a permission to be denied to an account, any single SCP anywhere in the path from the organization root through each OU down to the account (including the account itself) only needs to contain a Deny for that permission to apply — it cannot be overridden by an Allow statement elsewhere in the hierarchy (see 'How SCPs work with Deny' in AWS docs). Since the restrictive SCP is attached at the root and all accounts (including marketing) sit in the same OU beneath it, the only way to carve out an exception for the marketing account is to modify that existing Deny statement itself so it no longer applies when the principal is the marketing account — typically by adding a Condition such as StringNotEquals on aws:PrincipalAccount (or an equivalent exclusion) to the Deny. This is exactly option B. Option A (a new SCP in the marketing account with an Allow) and Option C (adding an Allow statement into the same SCP) both fail because the pre-existing Deny at the root still applies to marketing and Deny always wins over any Allow found elsewhere in the evaluation path. Option D (a permissions boundary) is an IAM construct scoped to a single account's identities; it cannot override or exempt an account from an organization-wide SCP Deny, since SCPs and permissions boundaries are evaluated independently and a boundary never loosens an SCP's restriction. Therefore only editing the existing SCP to exclude the marketing account via a condition achieves the requirement with a single, correctly-scoped change.","explanation_zh":"AWS Organizations 的 SCP 評估邏輯是「Deny 優先」：只要在從 root 經過各層 OU 到帳戶（含帳戶本身）的路徑上，任何一個 SCP 含有 Deny，該權限就會被拒絕，且無法被階層中其他地方的 Allow 敘述覆蓋（見 AWS 文件「How SCPs work with Deny」）。由於這個限制性 SCP 掛在 root，且所有帳戶（含 marketing）都在同一個 OU 下，唯一能為 marketing 帳戶開例外的方法，就是直接修改既有的 Deny 敘述本身，讓其在 principal 為 marketing 帳戶時不再套用——通常做法是在 Deny 的 Condition 中加入類似 StringNotEquals 搭配 aws:PrincipalAccount（或等效的排除條件）。這正是選項 B。選項 A（在 marketing 帳戶新增一個含 Allow 的 SCP）與選項 C（在同一個 SCP 中加入 Allow 敘述）都行不通，因為 root 上原本的 Deny 仍會套用到 marketing 帳戶，而 Deny 在評估路徑中永遠贏過任何地方的 Allow。選項 D（permissions boundary）是侷限在單一帳戶內 IAM 身分的機制，無法覆蓋或豁免組織層級 SCP 的 Deny，因為 SCP 與 permissions boundary 是各自獨立評估的，boundary 從不會放寬 SCP 的限制。因此，只有編輯既有 SCP、以條件排除 marketing 帳戶，才能用一個範圍精準的變更滿足需求。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"A new SCP attached to (or in) the marketing account can only add another Allow/Deny layer for that account, but it cannot cancel the Deny already inherited from the root-level SCP — SCP evaluation requires a Deny anywhere in the path to win, so the root Deny still blocks marketing regardless of any new Allow SCP.","why_zh":"在 marketing 帳戶新增的 SCP，只能為該帳戶疊加另一層 Allow/Deny，卻無法取消從 root SCP 繼承下來的 Deny——SCP 評估規則是路徑上任何一處的 Deny 都會生效，所以無論新增什麼 Allow SCP，root 的 Deny 仍會擋下 marketing。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"Adding an Allow statement into the same SCP does not neutralize the existing Deny statement in that policy (or any other SCP in the path); explicit Deny always takes precedence over Allow during policy evaluation, so the sharing restriction for marketing would remain in effect.","why_zh":"在同一份 SCP 中加入 Allow 敘述，並不會抵銷該政策（或路徑上其他 SCP）裡既有的 Deny 敘述；在政策評估中明確的 Deny 永遠優先於 Allow，因此 marketing 帳戶的分享限制依然會生效。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"A permissions boundary is an IAM feature that caps the maximum permissions of IAM users/roles inside a single account; it operates independently of, and cannot override, an AWS Organizations SCP. It cannot exempt an account from an org-wide Deny.","why_zh":"Permissions boundary 是 IAM 的功能，用來限制單一帳戶內 IAM 使用者／角色的最大權限上限；它與 AWS Organizations 的 SCP 各自獨立運作，無法覆蓋 SCP，也無法讓某帳戶豁免於組織層級的 Deny。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/organizations/latest/userguide/orgs_manage_policies_scps_evaluation.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/managedservices/latest/userguide/scp-library-compliance.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/ram/latest/userguide/security-iam-policies-examples.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/organizations/latest/userguide/orgs_manage_policies_authorization_policies.html"]}},{"id":174,"question_en":"A company uses an organization in AWS Organizations and AWS IAM Identity Center to manage its AWS environment. The company configures IAM Identity Center to access the company’s on-premises Active Directory through a properly configured AD Connector. All the company’s employees are in an Active Directory group namedCloud. The employees can view and access nearly all the AWS accounts in the organization, and the employees have the permissions that they require. However, the employees cannot access an account namedAccount A. The company verifies that Account A exists in the organization. What is the likely reason that the employees are unable to access Account A?","question_zh":"一家公司使用 AWS Organizations 和 AWS IAM Identity Center 来管理其 AWS 环境。该公司配置 IAM Identity Center 通过正确设置的 AD Connector 访问其本地 Active Directory。所有员工均属于名 为 Cloud 的 Active Directory 组。 员工可以查看和访问组织中的几乎所有AWS账户，并且拥有所需的权限。然而，员工无法访问名为 “Account A”的账户。公司已确认该账户确实存在于组织中。 员工无法访问账户A的可能原因是什么？","options_en":{"A":"The company did not add Account A to an organizational unit (OU) within the organization.","B":"The company has not synchronized the Cloud Active Directory group with the on-premises Active Directory.","C":"The company did not assign the Cloud Active Directory group to Account A in IAM Identity Center with a valid permission set.","D":"The company applied an IAM permissions boundary to Account A that is denying access to the account."},"options_zh":{"A":"该公司未将账户A添加到组织内的某个组织单位（OU）中。","B":"该公司尚未将云活动目录组与本地活动目录同步。","C":"该公司未在 IAM 身份中心中为账户 A 分配有效的权限集来关联云 Active Directory 组。","D":"该公司为账户A应用了IAM权限边界，该边界拒绝了对该账户的访问。"},"answer":["C"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Organizations/Governance","Security/IAM"],"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選","research":{"verdict":["C"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"both","explanation_en":"IAM Identity Center grants access to an AWS account only through an explicit assignment: an administrator must select that specific account under Multi-account permissions > AWS accounts, choose the user or group, and attach a permission set. This assignment is per-account and is not inherited from Organizational Unit membership, from directory group existence, or from any org-wide setting — so a group can have full access to 'nearly all' accounts and still be missing access to one account simply because no assignment (group + permission set) was ever created for that account. Since the Cloud group already works correctly for the rest of the organization, the AD Connector sync and directory configuration are proven functional, ruling out a sync problem (B). Moving Account A into an OU (A) has no bearing on Identity Center account assignments, which are made at the account level regardless of OU placement (OUs matter for SCPs/Control Tower guardrails, not for IAM Identity Center permission-set assignment). IAM permissions boundaries (D) are attached to individual IAM users/roles to cap their maximum permissions; there is no construct for applying a 'permissions boundary to an account,' making D not a real mechanism. Therefore the likely cause is C: the Cloud group was never assigned to Account A with a valid permission set.","explanation_zh":"IAM Identity Center 對 AWS 帳戶的存取權限,一定要透過明確指派才會生效:管理者必須在 Multi-account permissions > AWS accounts 選取該特定帳戶,選擇使用者或群組,並附加一個 permission set。這個指派是「逐帳戶」的,不會因為 OU 成員關係、目錄群組存在、或任何組織層級設定而自動繼承——所以一個群組可以對「幾乎所有」帳戶都有完整存取權,卻唯獨少了某一個帳戶,原因就只是從未替該帳戶建立(群組+permission set)的指派。既然 Cloud 群組在組織其餘帳戶都運作正常,代表 AD Connector 同步與目錄設定已證實可用,排除同步問題(B)。把 Account A 加入 OU(A)與 Identity Center 的帳戶指派無關,指派是在帳戶層級進行,與 OU 歸屬無關(OU 影響的是 SCP/Control Tower 防護機制,而非 IAM Identity Center 的 permission set 指派)。IAM permissions boundary(D)是附加在個別 IAM 使用者/角色上,用來限制其最大權限上限;並不存在「對整個帳戶套用 permissions boundary」這種機制,因此 D 並非真實可行的做法。因此最可能的原因是 C:公司從未在 IAM Identity Center 中把 Cloud 群組指派給 Account A 並賦予有效的 permission set。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"OU placement in AWS Organizations affects SCPs and Control Tower guardrails, not IAM Identity Center account assignments; access is still granted per-account via explicit group+permission-set assignment regardless of which OU the account sits in.","why_zh":"AWS Organizations 中的 OU 歸屬影響的是 SCP 與 Control Tower 防護機制,而非 IAM Identity Center 的帳戶指派;無論帳戶位於哪個 OU,存取權仍須透過逐帳戶的群組+permission set 明確指派才會生效。"},{"letter":"B","why_en":"The scenario states AD Connector is properly configured and the Cloud group already grants access to nearly all other accounts, proving the AD-to-Identity-Center group sync/lookup is working correctly — so a sync failure cannot explain access failing for just one account.","why_zh":"題目說明 AD Connector 已正確設定,且 Cloud 群組已能存取幾乎所有其他帳戶,證明 AD 與 Identity Center 之間的群組同步/查詢運作正常——因此同步失敗無法解釋為何唯獨一個帳戶存取失敗。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"IAM permissions boundaries are attached to specific IAM users or roles to cap their maximum permissions; AWS provides no feature to attach a permissions boundary to an entire account, so this is not a valid mechanism for blocking account-wide access.","why_zh":"IAM permissions boundary 是附加在特定 IAM 使用者或角色上,用來限制其最大權限;AWS 並未提供可對整個帳戶套用 permissions boundary 的功能,因此這不是能封鎖整個帳戶存取的有效機制。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/singlesignon/latest/userguide/assignusers.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/singlesignon/latest/userguide/manage-your-accounts.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/singlesignon/latest/userguide/permissionsetsconcept.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/singlesignon/latest/userguide/manage-sync-configurable-ADsync.html"]}},{"id":175,"question_en":"A company stores infrastructure and application code in web-based, third-party, Git-compatible code repositories outside of AWS. The company wants to give the code repositories the ability to securely authenticate and assume an existing IAM role within the company ' s AWS account by using OpenID Connect (OIDC). Which solution will meet these requirements?","question_zh":"一家公司将其基础设施和应用程序代码存储在 AWS 之外的基于网络的第三方 Git 兼容代码仓库中。 该公司希望使用 OpenID Connect（OIDC）使这些代码仓库能够安全地进行身份验证，并在公司的 AWS 账户中担任现有的 IAM 角色。 哪种解决方案能满足这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Create an OIDC identity provider (IdP) by using AWS Identity and Access Management (IAM) federation. Modify the trust policy of the IAM role to allow the code repositories to assume the IAM role.","B":"Use AWS Identity and Access Management (IAM) Roles Anywhere to create a trust anchor that uses OIDC. Modify the trust policy of the IAM role to allow the code repositories to assume the IAM role.","C":"Set up an account instance of AWS IAM Identity Center. Configure access to the code repositories as a customer managed OIDC application. Grant the application access to the IAM role.","D":"Use AWS Resource Access Manager (AWS RAM) to create a new resource share that uses OIDC. Limit the resource share to the specified code repositories. Grant the IAM role access to the resource share."},"options_zh":{"A":"使用 AWS 身份和访问管理（IAM）联合功能创建一个 OIDC 身份提供商（IdP），并修改 IAM 角色的信任策略，以允许代码仓库承担该 IAM 角色。","B":"使用 AWS 身份和访问管理（IAM）的 Anywhere 角色创建一个使用 OIDC 的信任锚点。修改 IAM 角色的信任策略，以允许代码仓库承担该 IAM 角色。","C":"创建 AWS IAM Identity Center 的账户实例。将对代码仓库的访问配置为由客户管理的 OIDC 应 用程序，并授予该应用程序对 IAM 角色的访问权限。","D":"使用 AWS 资源访问管理器（AWS RAM）创建一个使用 OIDC 的新资源共享，并将资源共享 限制为指定的代码仓库。授予 IAM 角色对资源共享的访问权限。"},"answer":["A"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Security/IAM"],"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選","research":{"verdict":["A"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"AWS's documented pattern for letting an external, OIDC-compatible identity provider (e.g., a third-party Git repository/CI system such as GitHub Actions or GitLab) securely obtain temporary AWS credentials is to register the provider as an IAM OIDC identity provider (IdP) using IAM federation, then edit the target IAM role's trust policy to trust that OIDC provider (specifying allowed audiences/subject claims). The external system then calls sts:AssumeRoleWithWebIdentity using its OIDC token to assume the role — no long-lived AWS credentials need to be stored in the repository. This is exactly option A. Option B is wrong because IAM Roles Anywhere trust anchors are built on X.509 certificates issued by a CA (AWS Private CA or an external CA) for workloads outside AWS, not on OIDC. Option C is wrong because IAM Identity Center's customer-managed OIDC applications provide workforce single sign-on into SaaS applications, not a mechanism for an external service to assume an IAM role via OIDC federation. Option D is wrong because AWS RAM shares native AWS resources (e.g., subnets, transit gateways) across accounts within an organization and has no OIDC-based mechanism for granting role-assumption to external Git providers.","explanation_zh":"AWS 官方文件所記載的做法是：讓外部、相容 OIDC 的身分提供者(例如第三方 Git 儲存庫/CI 系統，如 GitHub Actions 或 GitLab)安全取得暫時性 AWS 憑證的方式,是透過 IAM federation 建立一個 IAM OIDC identity provider (IdP),然後修改目標 IAM 角色的信任政策(trust policy),允許該 OIDC 提供者(指定允許的 audience/subject claim)。外部系統之後使用其 OIDC token 呼叫 sts:AssumeRoleWithWebIdentity 來承擔該角色,不需要在儲存庫中儲存長期有效的 AWS 憑證。這正是選項 A 所描述的做法。選項 B 錯誤,因為 IAM Roles Anywhere 的 trust anchor 是建立在 X.509 憑證(AWS Private CA 或外部 CA 簽發)之上,用於 AWS 以外的工作負載,而非 OIDC。選項 C 錯誤,因為 IAM Identity Center 的 customer managed OIDC application 提供的是員工對 SaaS 應用程式的單一登入(SSO),並非讓外部服務透過 OIDC federation 承擔 IAM 角色的機制。選項 D 錯誤,因為 AWS RAM 是在組織內跨帳戶共享原生 AWS 資源(例如子網路、transit gateway),沒有基於 OIDC 授予外部 Git 提供者角色承擔權限的機制。","distractors":[{"letter":"B","why_en":"IAM Roles Anywhere trust anchors are based on X.509 certificates from a CA (AWS Private CA or an external CA), not OIDC — it is designed for on-premises/non-AWS workloads authenticating with certificates, not OIDC-based code repositories.","why_zh":"IAM Roles Anywhere 的 trust anchor 是基於 CA(AWS Private CA 或外部 CA)簽發的 X.509 憑證,而非 OIDC——它是為了讓地端或非 AWS 工作負載透過憑證驗證,而非給 OIDC 型的程式碼儲存庫使用。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"IAM Identity Center customer managed OIDC applications configure workforce SSO access into third-party SaaS applications for human users, not a mechanism for a code repository service to assume an IAM role via OIDC.","why_zh":"IAM Identity Center 的 customer managed OIDC application 是用來設定員工對第三方 SaaS 應用程式的 SSO 存取,服務對象是人類使用者,而非讓程式碼儲存庫服務透過 OIDC 承擔 IAM 角色的機制。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"AWS RAM is used to share native AWS resources (subnets, transit gateways, license configurations, etc.) across accounts/organizations; it has no OIDC trust or role-assumption capability for external non-AWS systems.","why_zh":"AWS RAM 是用來在帳戶/組織間共享原生 AWS 資源(子網路、transit gateway、授權設定等),並沒有 OIDC 信任或讓外部非 AWS 系統承擔角色的能力。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/IAM/latest/UserGuide/id_roles_providers_create_oidc.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/IAM/latest/UserGuide/id_roles_providers_oidc.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/IAM/latest/UserGuide/id_roles_create_for-idp.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/rolesanywhere/latest/userguide/introduction.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/rolesanywhere/latest/userguide/public-key-infrastructure.html"]}},{"id":176,"question_en":"A company’s security engineer receives an alert that indicates that an unexpected principal is accessing a company-owned Amazon Simple Queue Service (Amazon SQS) queue. All the company’s accounts are within an organization in AWS Organizations. The security engineer must implement a mitigation solution that minimizes compliance violations and investment in tools outside of AWS. What should the security engineer do to meet these requirements?","question_zh":"一家公司的安全工程师收到一条告警，提示有未预期的主体正在访问公司拥有的 Amazon Simple Queue Service（Amazon SQS） 队列。该公司所有账户均位于 AWS Organizations 中的一个组织内。该安全工程师必须实施一项缓解方案，以尽量减少合规性违 规，并降低对 AWS 以外工具的投资。 安全工程师应采取哪些措施来满足这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Create security groups and attach them to all SQS queues.","B":"Modify network ACLs in all VPCs to restrict inbound traffic.","C":"Create interface VPC endpoints for Amazon SQS. Restrict access using aws:SourceVpce and aws: PrincipalOrgId conditions.","D":"Use a third-party cloud access security broker (CASB)."},"options_zh":{"A":"创建安全组并将其附加到所有 SQS 队列。","B":"修改所有VPC中的网络ACL，以限制入站流量。","C":"为 Amazon SQS 创建接口型 VPC 终端节点，并使用 aws:SourceVpce 和 aws:PrincipalOrgId 条件限制访问。","D":"使用第三方云访问安全代理（CASB）。"},"answer":["C"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Organizations/Governance","Serverless/Integration"],"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選","research":{"verdict":["C"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"both","explanation_en":"Option C is correct and is confirmed by official AWS documentation. Amazon SQS is a public AWS service accessed over its HTTPS API endpoint, but AWS provides interface VPC endpoints (AWS PrivateLink) so traffic from a VPC never traverses the public internet. AWS's SQS documentation states you can 'use queue policies to control access to queues from specific Amazon VPC endpoints or from specific VPCs,' and shows example policies using the aws:SourceVpce condition key to deny/allow requests that don't come through a specific VPC endpoint. Layering aws:PrincipalOrgId on top restricts access to only principals belonging to the company's AWS Organization, directly addressing the 'unexpected principal' alert — this mirrors AWS's own documented pattern (see the API Gateway/organization VPC endpoint policy example and the aws:PrincipalOrgID condition key reference) for confining access to an org's own principals via VPC endpoint or resource policies. This is a fully native, AWS-managed control (no third-party tooling, so no added compliance surface or external tool investment) and directly targets the actual attack vector (an unauthorized IAM principal calling the SQS API), satisfying both stated requirements. Options A, B, and D either don't apply to SQS's control plane at all or explicitly violate the 'minimize third-party tooling' requirement.","explanation_zh":"選項 C 正確,並獲得官方 AWS 文件證實。Amazon SQS 是透過 HTTPS API 端點存取的公開 AWS 服務,但 AWS 提供 interface VPC endpoint(AWS PrivateLink),讓來自 VPC 的流量完全不經過公開網際網路。AWS 的 SQS 文件明確指出可以「使用佇列政策(queue policies)來控制特定 Amazon VPC 端點或特定 VPC 對佇列的存取」,並展示了使用 aws:SourceVpce 條件鍵來拒絕/允許非經特定 VPC 端點的請求的範例政策。再疊加 aws:PrincipalOrgId 條件,可將存取限制在僅屬於公司 AWS Organization 的主體(principal),直接對應「非預期主體」警示這個問題——這與 AWS 官方文件中的模式一致(參見 API Gateway 的組織 VPC 端點政策範例及 aws:PrincipalOrgID 條件鍵參考文件),用於將存取限制在組織自身的主體範圍內,無論是透過 VPC 端點政策或資源政策。這是完全原生、由 AWS 管理的控制措施(不需第三方工具,因此不會增加合規面向或外部工具投資),且直接針對實際的攻擊向量(未經授權的 IAM 主體呼叫 SQS API),同時滿足題目提出的兩項需求。選項 A、B、D 要不是完全不適用於 SQS 的控制平面,就是明顯違反「最小化第三方工具投資」的需求。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"Security groups are a VPC networking construct that control traffic to/from elastic network interfaces (e.g., EC2 instances, interface VPC endpoints). Amazon SQS is a serverless, account-level AWS service with no ENI of its own to attach a security group to — 'attach a security group to an SQS queue' is not a supported or meaningful operation. Security groups also filter by IP/port/protocol, not by IAM principal, so they cannot address an 'unexpected principal' issue even conceptually.","why_zh":"安全群組(security group)是 VPC 網路層的機制,用於控制進出彈性網路介面(ENI,例如 EC2 執行個體、interface VPC endpoint)的流量。Amazon SQS 是無伺服器、帳戶層級的 AWS 服務,本身沒有可供附加安全群組的 ENI——「將安全群組附加到 SQS 佇列」並非受支援或有意義的操作。此外安全群組是依 IP/連接埠/通訊協定過濾,而非依 IAM 主體過濾,因此即使概念上也無法解決「非預期主體」的問題。"},{"letter":"B","why_en":"Network ACLs operate at the VPC subnet level, filtering traffic by IP address/protocol/port for resources inside a VPC. Amazon SQS's control plane (queue access) is governed by IAM/queue policies evaluating the calling principal's identity, not by subnet-level packet filtering. Modifying NACLs would not restrict which IAM principal can call the SQS API and does not address the alert's root cause.","why_zh":"網路 ACL(NACL)運作於 VPC 子網路層級,依 IP 位址/通訊協定/連接埠過濾 VPC 內資源的流量。Amazon SQS 的控制平面(佇列存取)是由 IAM/佇列政策依呼叫主體的身分來判斷,而非依子網路層級的封包過濾。修改 NACL 並不能限制哪個 IAM 主體可以呼叫 SQS API,也無法解決此警示的根本原因。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"A third-party CASB directly contradicts the stated requirement to 'minimize... investment in tools outside of AWS.' It would also add licensing cost, integration overhead, and a new external system in the compliance/audit scope, whereas AWS-native VPC endpoint + queue policy conditions achieve the same principal-restriction outcome using only AWS-managed controls.","why_zh":"第三方 CASB 直接牴觸題目明確要求的「最小化投資於 AWS 以外工具」。它還會增加授權成本、整合負擔,以及在合規/稽核範圍內引入新的外部系統,而 AWS 原生的 VPC 端點加上佇列政策條件,僅使用 AWS 自身管理的控制項就能達成相同的主體限制效果。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AWSSimpleQueueService/latest/SQSDeveloperGuide/sqs-internetwork-traffic-privacy.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AWSSimpleQueueService/latest/SQSDeveloperGuide/sqs-security-best-practices.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AWSSimpleQueueService/latest/SQSDeveloperGuide/sqs-creating-custom-policies-access-policy-examples.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/apigateway/latest/developerguide/apigateway-vpc-endpoint-policies.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/vpc/latest/userguide/vpc-endpoints-access.html"]}},{"id":177,"question_en":"A company is using Amazon Elastic Container Service (Amazon ECS) to deploy an application that deals with sensitive data. During a recent security audit, the company identified a security issue in which Amazon RDS credentials were stored with the application code in the company ' s source code repository. A security engineer needs to develop a solution to ensure that database credentials are stored securely and rotated periodically. The credentials should be accessible to the application only. The engineer also needs to prevent database administrators from sharing database credentials as plaintext with other teammates. The solution must also minimize administrative overhead. Which solution meets these requirements?","question_zh":"一家公司正在使用 Amazon 弹性容器服务（Amazon ECS）部署一个处理敏感数据的应用程序。在最近的一次安全审计中，该公 司发现了一个安全问题：Amazon RDS 的凭据被存储在公司源代码仓库的应用程序代码中。安全工程师需要设计一个解决方案， 以确保数据库凭据能够安全地存储并定期轮换，且仅允许应用程序访问这些凭据。同时，工程师还需防止数据库管理员将数据库 凭据以明文形式与其他团队成员共享。该解决方案还必须尽量减少管理开销。 哪种解决方案符合这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Use the AWS Systems Manager Parameter Store to generate database credentials. Use an IAM profile for ECS tasks to restrict access to database credentials to specific containers only.","B":"Use AWS Secrets Manager to store database credentials. Use an IAM inline policy for ECS tasks to restrict access to database credentials to specific containers only.","C":"Use the AWS Systems Manager Parameter Store to store database credentials. Use IAM roles for ECS tasks to restrict access to database credentials to specific containers only.","D":"Use AWS Secrets Manager to store database credentials. Use IAM roles for ECS tasks to restrict access to database credentials to specific containers only."},"options_zh":{"A":"使用 AWS Systems Manager 参数存储生成数据库凭据，并为 ECS 任务使用 IAM 角色，以限制对数据库凭据的访问仅限于 特定容器。","B":"使用 AWS Secrets Manager 存储数据库凭据，并为 ECS 任务使用 IAM 内联策略，将对数据库凭据的访问权限限制在特定 容器上。","C":"使用 AWS Systems Manager 参数存储来保存数据库凭据，并通过 IAM 角色为 ECS 任务限制对数据库凭据的访问，仅允许特 定容器访问。","D":"使用 AWS Secrets Manager 存储数据库凭据，并通过 IAM 角色为 ECS 任务限制对数据库凭据的访问，仅允许特定容器访问。"},"answer":["D"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Security/IAM","Compute","Database","Monitoring/Ops","Containers"],"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選","research":{"verdict":["D"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"both","explanation_en":"AWS Secrets Manager is purpose-built for this scenario: it stores the RDS credentials encrypted with KMS and, unlike Systems Manager Parameter Store, natively supports automatic periodic rotation of database credentials (via a built-in or custom Lambda rotation function) with minimal administrative overhead. Parameter Store (options A and C) has no built-in rotation mechanism for database credentials — you would have to build and manage your own rotation Lambda and scheduling, which fails the 'minimize administrative overhead' requirement. For access control, ECS tasks retrieve secrets using the 'IAM roles for tasks' feature: a task IAM role is attached to the task definition, and only that role (used by the specific containers in that task) is granted an IAM policy allowing secretsmanager:GetSecretValue on the specific secret — this both restricts credential access to the application and prevents developers/DBAs from having to share plaintext credentials. Option B describes an 'IAM inline policy for ECS tasks' — but ECS tasks do not attach IAM policies directly; access is granted through an IAM role (the task role) referenced by the task definition, to which policies (inline or managed) are attached. The standard AWS terminology and mechanism for this restriction is 'IAM roles for tasks,' making D's phrasing correct and B's phrasing an incorrect description of how ECS grants task-level AWS permissions. Option A also incorrectly says Parameter Store 'generates' database credentials, which is not a native capability (Secrets Manager can generate random secrets; Parameter Store cannot). Therefore D — Secrets Manager for storage/rotation plus IAM roles for ECS tasks for access restriction — meets all stated requirements.","explanation_zh":"AWS Secrets Manager 專為此情境設計:它使用 KMS 加密儲存 RDS 憑證,且與 Systems Manager Parameter Store 不同,原生支援資料庫憑證的定期自動輪替(透過內建或自訂的 Lambda 輪替函式),行政管理負擔最小。Parameter Store(選項 A、C)並沒有內建的資料庫憑證輪替機制——你必須自行建置並維運輪替用的 Lambda 與排程,這違反「將行政管理負擔降到最低」的要求。在存取控管方面,ECS 任務透過「IAM roles for tasks」功能取得密鑰:將 task IAM role 附加到任務定義,只有該角色(供該任務中特定容器使用)被授予允許 secretsmanager:GetSecretValue 存取特定密鑰的 IAM 政策——這既限制了應用程式對憑證的存取,也避免開發人員/資料庫管理員需要以明文分享憑證。選項 B 描述的是「ECS 任務的 IAM inline policy」——但 ECS 任務並不會直接附加 IAM 政策;存取權限是透過任務定義所參照的 IAM 角色(task role)授予,政策(不論 inline 或 managed)則附加在該角色上。AWS 針對此存取限制的標準術語與機制正是「IAM roles for tasks」,因此 D 的敘述正確,而 B 對 ECS 如何授予任務層級 AWS 權限的描述並不精確。選項 A 也錯誤地宣稱 Parameter Store 能「產生」資料庫憑證,這並非 Parameter Store 的原生能力(能產生隨機密鑰的是 Secrets Manager,而非 Parameter Store)。因此 D——使用 Secrets Manager 儲存並輪替憑證,搭配 IAM roles for ECS tasks 限制存取——完全符合題目所有要求。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"Systems Manager Parameter Store cannot 'generate' database credentials natively (that is a Secrets Manager capability), and Parameter Store has no built-in automatic rotation for database credentials, so it fails the periodic-rotation and low-administrative-overhead requirements. It also references an 'IAM profile' loosely rather than the correct task role mechanism.","why_zh":"Systems Manager Parameter Store 本身無法「產生」資料庫憑證(這是 Secrets Manager 的能力),且 Parameter Store 沒有內建的資料庫憑證自動輪替功能,因此無法滿足定期輪替與低行政負擔的要求。此選項也籠統地提到「IAM profile」,而非正確的 task role 機制。"},{"letter":"B","why_en":"While Secrets Manager is the right storage choice, ECS tasks do not attach an 'IAM inline policy' directly to themselves; access is granted via an IAM role (the ECS task role) referenced in the task definition, to which a policy is attached. This mislabels the actual AWS access-control mechanism used to scope secret access to specific tasks/containers.","why_zh":"雖然 Secrets Manager 是正確的儲存選擇,但 ECS 任務並不會直接對自己附加「IAM inline policy」;存取權限是透過任務定義中參照的 IAM 角色(ECS task role)授予,政策則附加在該角色上。此選項誤植了 AWS 用來限定特定任務/容器存取密鑰的實際存取控制機制。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"Parameter Store correctly pairs with IAM roles for tasks for access control, but Parameter Store lacks native automatic rotation for database credentials — achieving rotation requires custom Lambda functions and EventBridge scheduling that you must build and maintain yourself, increasing administrative overhead and failing that explicit requirement.","why_zh":"Parameter Store 搭配 IAM roles for tasks 做存取控管的部分是正確的,但 Parameter Store 缺乏原生的資料庫憑證自動輪替功能——要達成輪替必須自行建置並維護自訂 Lambda 函式與 EventBridge 排程,這會增加行政管理負擔,無法滿足題目明確提出的要求。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonECS/latest/developerguide/specifying-sensitive-data.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/secretsmanager/latest/userguide/rotate-secrets_turn-on-for-db.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/secretsmanager/latest/userguide/tutorials_rotation-single.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonECS/latest/developerguide/task_definition_parameters.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonECS/latest/developerguide/security-iam-roles.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonECS/latest/developerguide/ecs-iam-role-overview.html"]}},{"id":178,"question_en":"A company stores sensitive data in an Amazon S3 bucket. The company encrypts the data at rest by using server-side encryption with Amazon S3 managed keys (SSE-S3). A security engineer must prevent any modifications to the data in the S3 bucket. Which solution will meet this requirement?","question_zh":"一家公司将其敏感数据存储在 Amazon S3 存储桶中，并使用 Amazon S3 管理的密钥（SSE-S3） 进行静态数据加密。安全工程师必须防止对 S3 存储桶中的数据进行任何修改。 哪种解决方案能满足这一要求？","options_en":{"A":"Configure S3 bucket policies to deny DELETE and PUT object permissions.","B":"Configure S3 Object Lock in compliance mode with S3 bucket versioning enabled.","C":"Change the encryption on the S3 bucket to use AWS Key Management Service (AWS KMS) customer managed keys.","D":"Configure the S3 bucket with multi-factor authentication (MFA) delete protection."},"options_zh":{"A":"配置 S3 存储桶策略，拒绝 DELETE 和 PUT 对象权限。","B":"在启用 S3 存储桶版本控制的情况下，以合规模式配置 S3 对象锁定。","C":"将 S3 存储桶的加密方式更改为使用 AWS 密钥管理服务（AWS KMS）的客户托管密钥。","D":"配置 S3 存储桶以启用多因素认证（MFA）删除保护。"},"answer":["B"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Security/IAM","Storage"],"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選","research":{"verdict":["B"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"AWS S3 Object Lock is purpose-built to prevent an object from being deleted or overwritten for a fixed period or indefinitely, implementing a write-once-read-many (WORM) model. AWS documentation states Object Lock requires S3 Versioning to be enabled on the bucket, and that in Compliance mode 'a protected object version can't be overwritten or deleted by any user, including the root user in your AWS account' — the only way to remove it before the retention period expires is to delete the whole AWS account. This directly satisfies 'prevent any modifications to the data,' independent of the SSE-S3 encryption already in use (encryption and immutability are orthogonal concerns). Option A (bucket policy denying DELETE/PUT) is an IAM-based control that any principal with sufficient permissions (e.g., an account admin) can simply edit or remove, so it does not durably prevent modification — it is access control, not object-level immutability. Option C (switching to KMS customer managed keys) changes how data is encrypted at rest but has no bearing on whether the object can be overwritten or deleted; it does not address the modification-prevention requirement at all. Option D (MFA Delete) only adds an MFA requirement for permanently deleting an object version or changing the bucket's versioning state — it does not block ordinary PUT (overwrite) operations, and the requirement here is broader ('prevent any modifications'), which only Object Lock's WORM enforcement satisfies.","explanation_zh":"Amazon S3 Object Lock 專門設計用來讓物件在固定期間內、或永久地無法被刪除或覆寫,採用 write-once-read-many(WORM)模型。AWS 官方文件說明 Object Lock 必須先在儲存貯體上啟用 S3 Versioning,且在 Compliance 模式下「受保護的物件版本無法被任何使用者覆寫或刪除,包括 AWS 帳戶的 root 使用者」——在保留期限到期前,唯一能移除物件的方式是刪除整個 AWS 帳戶。這正好滿足「防止資料被任何修改」的要求,且與目前使用的 SSE-S3 加密無關(加密與不可變性是彼此正交的兩個議題)。選項 A(以 bucket policy 拒絕 DELETE/PUT 權限)只是一種 IAM 型存取控制,任何有足夠權限的主體(例如帳戶管理員)都能直接修改或移除該政策,因此無法持久地防止修改——這是存取控制,而非物件層級的不可變性。選項 C(改用 KMS customer managed keys)只改變資料靜態加密的方式,與物件能否被覆寫或刪除毫無關係,完全沒有解決「防止修改」的需求。選項 D(MFA Delete)只在永久刪除物件版本或變更儲存貯體版本控制狀態時,額外要求 MFA 驗證——它並不會阻擋一般的 PUT(覆寫)操作,而題目要求的是更廣泛的「防止任何修改」,只有 Object Lock 的 WORM 強制機制才能滿足此需求。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"A bucket policy denying DELETE and PUT is an IAM-based access control that can be edited or removed by any principal with sufficient permissions (e.g., an administrator); it provides no durable, tamper-resistant guarantee against modification the way Object Lock's WORM enforcement does.","why_zh":"以 bucket policy 拒絕 DELETE 和 PUT 只是一種 IAM 型存取控制,任何具備足夠權限的主體(例如管理員)都能修改或移除該政策,無法像 Object Lock 的 WORM 機制那樣提供持久且防竄改的保護。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"Switching from SSE-S3 to SSE-KMS with customer managed keys only changes the encryption-at-rest mechanism and key management/auditing capabilities; it has no effect on whether an object can be overwritten or deleted.","why_zh":"把 SSE-S3 改成使用 customer managed key 的 SSE-KMS,只是改變靜態加密機制與金鑰管理/稽核能力,對物件是否能被覆寫或刪除完全沒有影響。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"MFA Delete only requires MFA to permanently delete an object version or to disable/suspend bucket versioning; it does not prevent ordinary object overwrites (PUT requests), so it does not satisfy a requirement to prevent 'any modifications.'","why_zh":"MFA Delete 只在永久刪除物件版本,或停用/暫停儲存貯體版本控制時,才要求 MFA 驗證;它並不會阻止一般的物件覆寫(PUT 請求),因此無法滿足「防止任何修改」的要求。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonS3/latest/userguide/object-lock.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonS3/latest/userguide/batch-ops-compliance-mode.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonS3/latest/userguide/Versioning.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonS3/latest/userguide/MultiFactorAuthenticationDelete.html"]}},{"id":179,"question_en":"A company needs to implement DNS Security Extensions (DNSSEC) for a specific subdomain. The subdomain is already registered with Amazon Route 53. A security engineer has enabled DNSSEC signing and has created a key-signing key (KSK). When the security engineer tries to test the configuration, the security engineer receives an error for a broken trust chain. What should the security engineer do to resolve this error?","question_zh":"一家公司需要为某个特定的子域名实施DNS安全扩展（DNSSEC）。该子域名已注册到Amazon Route 53。安全工程师已启用DNSSEC签名，并创建了密钥签名密钥（KSK）。但当安全工程师尝 试测试配置时，却收到了信任链断裂的错误提示。 安全工程师应采取什么措施来解决此错误？","options_en":{"A":"Replace the KSK with a zone-signing key (ZSK).","B":"Deactivate and then activate the KSK.","C":"Create a Delegation Signer (DS) record in the parent hosted zone.","D":"Create a Delegation Signer (DS) record in the subdomain."},"options_zh":{"A":"将KSK替换为区域签名密钥（ZSK）。","B":"先停用，然后重新启用KSK。","C":"在父级托管区域中创建一个委托签名者（DS）记录。","D":"在子域名中创建一个委托签名者（DS）记录。"},"answer":["C"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Networking/DNS"],"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選","research":{"verdict":["C"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"both","explanation_en":"DNSSEC establishes a chain of trust from the parent zone down to the child zone via a Delegation Signer (DS) record. After you enable DNSSEC signing on a hosted zone and create a KSK, Route 53 signs the zone's records, but validating resolvers still see a 'broken chain of trust' until a DS record — derived from the KSK's public key — is published in the PARENT hosted zone that delegates to this subdomain. The DS record proves to resolvers that the parent zone vouches for the child zone's KSK. Per AWS's own three-step DNSSEC setup process, Step 3 (\"Establish chain of trust\") is exactly this: create the DS record in the parent hosted zone (in Route 53 or wherever the parent domain's DNS is hosted) using the KSK information Route 53 provides. Placing the DS record in the subdomain itself (option D) would not be validated by anyone, since resolvers walk down from the parent to establish trust, not sideways within the child zone. Options A and B address key type/state issues, not the actual missing link (the DS record) that causes a broken trust chain.","explanation_zh":"DNSSEC 的信任鏈是由父區域向下延伸到子區域，透過在父區域建立 Delegation Signer (DS) 記錄來達成。當你在某個 hosted zone 啟用 DNSSEC 簽章並建立 KSK 之後，Route 53 會對該區域的記錄進行簽章，但驗證中的解析器仍會出現「信任鏈中斷」，直到在委派此子網域的「父」hosted zone 中發布一筆衍生自 KSK 公鑰的 DS 記錄為止。DS 記錄的作用是向解析器證明父區域為子區域的 KSK 背書。依照 AWS 官方的 DNSSEC 三步驟設定流程，第三步「建立信任鏈」正是：使用 Route 53 提供的 KSK 資訊，在父 hosted zone（無論是在 Route 53 或其他機構管理該父網域的 DNS）建立 DS 記錄。若把 DS 記錄放在子網域本身（選項 D），則不會有任何人去驗證它，因為解析器是從父區域向下走以建立信任，而非在子區域內部橫向查找。選項 A、B 處理的是金鑰類型／狀態問題，並未解決造成信任鏈中斷的真正缺口（缺少 DS 記錄）。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"A ZSK (zone-signing key) signs the zone's individual resource records; it is not what forms the parent-child trust link. Replacing the KSK with a ZSK would not create the missing DS record and would not fix a broken chain of trust — in fact a hosted zone needs both a KSK and ZSKs, and the KSK specifically is what the DS record references.","why_zh":"ZSK（zone-signing key）用來簽署區域內個別的資源記錄，並非用來建立父子信任連結的元件。把 KSK 換成 ZSK 並不會產生缺少的 DS 記錄，也無法修復信任鏈中斷——事實上 hosted zone 同時需要 KSK 與 ZSK，而 DS 記錄所參照的正是 KSK。"},{"letter":"B","why_en":"Deactivating and reactivating the KSK only toggles its operational state; it does not publish anything in the parent zone. Since the broken trust chain is caused by the absence of a DS record at the parent, cycling the KSK's status has no effect on establishing the chain of trust.","why_zh":"停用再啟用 KSK 只是切換其運作狀態，並不會在父區域發布任何東西。既然信任鏈中斷的原因是父區域缺少 DS 記錄，反覆切換 KSK 狀態對建立信任鏈毫無幫助。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"Creating the DS record in the subdomain's own hosted zone does not help — DNSSEC validation walks the chain top-down from the parent zone, so the parent must hold the DS record pointing to the child's KSK. A DS record placed in the child zone itself is not consulted by resolvers validating the delegation and would not resolve the broken trust chain.","why_zh":"把 DS 記錄建立在子網域自己的 hosted zone 中並無幫助——DNSSEC 驗證是由父區域由上而下走訪信任鏈，因此必須是父區域持有指向子網域 KSK 的 DS 記錄。放在子區域本身的 DS 記錄不會被驗證委派的解析器參考，也無法解決信任鏈中斷的問題。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/Route53/latest/DeveloperGuide/dns-configuring-dnssec-enable-signing.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/Route53/latest/DeveloperGuide/ResourceRecordTypes.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/Route53/latest/DeveloperGuide/domain-configure-dnssec.html"]}},{"id":180,"question_en":"A company’s developers are using AWS Lambda function URLs to invoke functions directly. Thecompany must ensure that developers cannot configure or deploy unauthenticated functions in production accounts. The company wants to meet this requirement by using AWS Organizations. The solution must not require additional work for the developers. Which solution will meet these requirements?","question_zh":"公司开发人员正在使用 AWS Lambda 函数 URL 直接调用函数。公司必须确保开发人员无法在生产账户中配置或部署未经身 份验证的函数。公司希望通过使用 AWS Organizations 来满足这一要求，且解决方案不得给开发人员增加额外的工作负担。 哪种解决方案能满足这些要求","options_en":{"A":"Require the developers to configure all function URLs to support cross-origin resource sharing (CORS) when the functions are called from a different domain.","B":"Use an AWS WAF delegated administrator account to view and block unauthenticated access to function URLs in production accounts, based on the OU of accounts that are using the functions.","C":"Use SCPs to allow all lambda:CreateFunctionUrlConfig and lambda:UpdateFunctionUrlConfig actions that have a lambda:FunctionUrlAuthType condition key value of AWS_IAM.","D":"Use SCPs to deny all lambda:CreateFunctionUrlConfig and lambda:UpdateFunctionUrlConfig actions that have a lambda:FunctionUrlAuthType condition key value of NONE."},"options_zh":{"B":"使用 AWS WAF 委托管理员账户，根据使用函数的账户所属的组织单元（OU），查看并阻止对生产环境账户 中函数 URL 的未认证访问。","C":"使用 SCP 允许所有具有 lambda:FunctionUrlAuthType 条件键值为 AWS_IAM 的 lambda:CreateFunctionUrlConfig 和 lambda:UpdateFunctionUrlConfig 操作。","D":"使用 SCP 拒绝所有具有 lambda:FunctionUrlAuthType 条件键值为 NONE 的 lambda:CreateFunctionUrlConfig 和 lambda: UpdateFunctionUrlConfig 操作。","A":"要求开发者在函数从不同域名调用时，配置所有函数URL以支持跨域资源共享（CORS）。"},"answer":["D"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Organizations/Governance","Security/IAM","Compute"],"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選","research":{"verdict":["D"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"both","explanation_en":"AWS Lambda's own documentation on function URL governance shows exactly this pattern: use an SCP with an explicit Deny on lambda:CreateFunctionUrlConfig and lambda:UpdateFunctionUrlConfig, keyed on the lambda:FunctionUrlAuthType condition, to stop accounts in an OU from creating/updating unauthenticated function URLs org-wide, with zero extra steps for developers (the guardrail is invisible unless violated). The condition key lambda:FunctionUrlAuthType only ever takes two enum values, AWS_IAM or NONE, so an explicit Deny keyed on NONE (option D) blocks exactly the unauthenticated configuration path while leaving AWS_IAM-authenticated function URLs untouched — this mirrors AWS's own documented SCP example (which denies when the value is 'StringNotEquals AWS_IAM', logically equivalent given the two-value enum). Option C is the trap: an SCP with only an Allow statement scoped to the AWS_IAM condition does not, by itself, deny the NONE case — SCPs work by intersection, and a non-FullAWSAccess SCP that has no matching Allow statement for an action implicitly excludes that action from the effective permission set for every API call in the account, not just Lambda's. Using Allow-only SCPs like this is an AWS-documented anti-pattern that silently breaks every other unrelated permission in the account unless you exhaustively enumerate all other allowed actions too, so it is not a safe or correct way to build this guardrail. Option A (CORS) governs cross-origin browser requests, not authentication of the function URL invocation itself, and does not touch the AuthType at all. Option B (WAF delegated admin) can inspect/block HTTP traffic to a function URL after it exists, but it cannot prevent developers from creating or updating a function URL configuration with AuthType=NONE in the first place, and doesn't operate on IAM/Organizations OU-based preventive controls at the API-call level the way SCPs do. Therefore D is the only solution that is both preventive (blocks the CreateFunctionUrlConfig/UpdateFunctionUrlConfig API call itself), org-wide via OU-scoped SCP, and requires no developer behavior change.","explanation_zh":"AWS Lambda 官方文件在 function URL 治理章節中示範的正是這個模式：用 SCP 對 lambda:CreateFunctionUrlConfig 與 lambda:UpdateFunctionUrlConfig 動作加上明確 Deny，並以 lambda:FunctionUrlAuthType condition key 作為判斷條件，藉此在整個 OU／組織層級阻擋建立或更新未經驗證的 function URL，且對開發者完全零額外負擔（除非違規否則不會察覺此護欄存在）。lambda:FunctionUrlAuthType 這個 condition key 只有兩個列舉值：AWS_IAM 或 NONE，因此針對 NONE 值做明確 Deny（選項 D）恰好能封鎖未驗證的設定路徑，同時完全不影響 AWS_IAM 驗證的 function URL——這與 AWS 官方文件範例（用 StringNotEquals AWS_IAM 做 Deny）在邏輯上完全等價（因為只有兩個可能值）。選項 C 是陷阱：只用 Allow 陳述式、並以 AWS_IAM 條件限定範圍的 SCP，本身並不會 Deny NONE 的情況——SCP 是採交集（intersection）方式運作，一個非 FullAWSAccess 的 SCP 若對某個動作沒有對應的 Allow 陳述式，就會在該帳戶「所有」API 呼叫的有效權限交集中隱性排除該動作，而不僅限於 Lambda 相關動作。這種只用 Allow 的 SCP 寫法是 AWS 文件明確警示的反模式，除非把帳戶內所有其他允許的動作也鉅細靡遺列舉清楚，否則會在無聲無息間破壞帳戶內所有其他不相關的權限，因此並非建立此護欄的安全或正確做法。選項 A（CORS）管的是瀏覽器跨來源請求的行為，與 function URL 呼叫本身的身分驗證無關，完全不涉及 AuthType 設定。選項 B（WAF 委派管理員）只能在 function URL 已經存在之後，檢查／封鎖進入的 HTTP 流量，無法從源頭阻止開發者建立或更新 AuthType=NONE 的 function URL 設定，也不像 SCP 那樣能在 API 呼叫層級、依 Organizations 的 OU 做預防性控管。因此 D 是唯一同時具備「預防性（直接封鎖 CreateFunctionUrlConfig/UpdateFunctionUrlConfig API 呼叫）」「組織層級（透過 OU 範圍的 SCP）」且「不需開發者改變行為」三項要求的解法。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"CORS controls which browser origins may call the function URL; it has nothing to do with authenticating/authorizing the invocation itself, and doesn't touch AuthType at all.","why_zh":"CORS 控制的是哪些瀏覽器來源可以呼叫 function URL，與呼叫本身的身分驗證／授權完全無關，也不涉及 AuthType 設定。"},{"letter":"B","why_en":"AWS WAF (even via a delegated administrator) can only inspect/block HTTP requests to a function URL that already exists with a public endpoint; it cannot prevent the CreateFunctionUrlConfig/UpdateFunctionUrlConfig API calls from ever setting AuthType=NONE, so it's reactive traffic filtering, not a preventive Organizations-level guardrail on configuration.","why_zh":"即使透過 WAF 委派管理員帳戶，AWS WAF 也只能在 function URL 已存在且對外公開後，檢查／封鎖進來的 HTTP 請求，無法阻止 CreateFunctionUrlConfig/UpdateFunctionUrlConfig 這類 API 呼叫一開始就把 AuthType 設成 NONE，因此只是被動的流量過濾，並非在 Organizations 層級對設定動作做預防性管控。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"An Allow-only SCP scoped to the AWS_IAM condition does not implicitly Deny the NONE case for just those two Lambda actions — because SCPs combine via intersection, an SCP lacking an Allow statement for any other unrelated action would exclude that action from the account's effective permissions entirely, silently breaking every other unrelated API call unless exhaustively enumerated; this is a documented SCP anti-pattern, not a safe targeted guardrail.","why_zh":"只用 Allow、並以 AWS_IAM 條件限定範圍的 SCP，並不會針對這兩個 Lambda 動作隱性 Deny NONE 的情況——因為 SCP 是以交集方式合併，若某個 SCP 對其他不相關動作沒有對應的 Allow 陳述，就會把該動作整個排除在帳戶的有效權限之外，除非鉅細靡遺列出所有其他允許動作，否則會無聲破壞其他所有不相關的 API 呼叫，這是文件明確指出的 SCP 反模式，並非安全的針對性護欄做法。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/lambda/latest/dg/urls-auth.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/organizations/latest/userguide/orgs_manage_policies_scps.html"]}},{"id":181,"question_en":"A company is running a containerized application on an Amazon Elastic Container Service (Amazon ECS) cluster that uses AWS Fargate. The application runs as several ECS services. The ECS services are in individual target groups for an internet-facing Application Load Balancer (ALB). The ALB is the origin for an Amazon CloudFront distribution. An AWS WAF web ACL is associated with the CloudFront distribution. Web clients access the ECS services through the CloudFront distribution. The company learns that the web clients can bypass the web ACL and can access the ALB directly. Which solution will prevent the web clients from directly accessing the ALB?","question_zh":"一家公司正在使用 AWS Fargate 的 Amazon 弹性容器服务（Amazon ECS）集群上运行一个容器化应用程序。该应用程 序以多个 ECS 服务的形式运行。 ECS 服务位于面向互联网的应用负载均衡器（ALB）的独立目标组中。该 ALB 是 Amazon CloudFront 分发的源。一个 AWS WAF 网络 ACL 与 CloudFront 分发相关联。 Web客户端通过CloudFront分发访问ECS服务。公司发现，这些Web客户端可以绕过Web ACL，直接访问ALB。 哪种解决方案可以防止网络客户端直接访问ALB？","options_en":{"A":"Create an AWS PrivateLink endpoint and set it as the CloudFront origin.","B":"Create a new internal ALB and delete the internet-facing ALB.","C":"Modify the ALB listener rules to allow only CloudFront IP ranges.","D":"Add a custom X-Shared-Secret header in CloudFront and configure the ALB listener rules to allow requests only when the header value matches."},"options_zh":{"A":"创建一个 AWS PrivateLink 端点，并将其设置为 CloudFront 的源站。","B":"创建一个新的内部ALB并删除面向互联网的ALB。","C":"修改 ALB 监听器规则，仅允许 CloudFront 的 IP 范围。","D":"在 CloudFront 中添加自定义的 X-Shared-Secret 请求头，并配置 ALB 监听器规则，仅允许请求头值匹配时的请求通过。"},"answer":["D"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Networking/DNS","Security/IAM","Compute","Containers"],"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選","research":{"verdict":["D"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"both","explanation_en":"AWS's documented pattern for exactly this scenario (CloudFront in front of an internet-facing ALB, with WAF attached to the CloudFront distribution) is to configure CloudFront to inject a secret custom HTTP header (e.g., X-Shared-Secret / X-Custom-Header) into every origin request, and then add an ALB listener rule that only forwards requests containing the correct header value to the target group (return a fixed 403 response otherwise). This ensures every request that reaches the ECS services has passed through CloudFront (and therefore through the associated AWS WAF web ACL), because only CloudFront knows the secret header value. AWS explicitly documents this as the way to 'prevent users from directly accessing an Application Load Balancer, and allow access only through CloudFront.' Option C (allow-list CloudFront's IP ranges on the ALB) is explicitly called out by AWS as only a supplementary/optional hardening step, not a substitute for the header check, because IP ranges are shared across all CloudFront customers, change over time, and don't prove the request logically flowed through your specific distribution/WAF. Option B (switch to an internal ALB and delete the internet-facing one) would break CloudFront's ability to reach the origin at all under the classic architecture in this question (no VPC origin/PrivateLink is configured), so it does not preserve the working solution. Option A (PrivateLink endpoint as a CloudFront origin) is not a supported/documented CloudFront-to-ALB origin-access pattern for this architecture (the actual AWS feature for private origins, CloudFront VPC origins, works differently and isn't what's described). Therefore D is correct and matches the ExamTopics-suggested answer.","explanation_zh":"針對「CloudFront 位於 internet-facing ALB 前，且 WAF 掛在 CloudFront 上」這個情境，AWS 官方文件明確記載的作法是：讓 CloudFront 在送往 origin 的每個請求中加入一個秘密的自訂 HTTP 標頭（例如 X-Shared-Secret），再於 ALB 的 listener 規則設定「只有帶有正確標頭值的請求才轉發到 target group」，否則回傳固定的 403。這樣可確保所有能到達 ECS 服務的流量都必然經過 CloudFront（進而經過關聯的 AWS WAF web ACL），因為只有 CloudFront 知道這個秘密標頭值。AWS 文件明確把這個方法列為「防止使用者直接存取 ALB、只允許透過 CloudFront 存取」的標準做法。選項 C（在 ALB 上只允許 CloudFront 的 IP 範圍）被 AWS 文件明確定位為附加/選用的強化措施，而非取代標頭檢查的方案，因為 IP 範圍是所有 CloudFront 客戶共用、會變動，也無法證明請求確實經過你自己的 distribution／WAF。選項 B（改用 internal ALB 並刪除 internet-facing ALB）在題目描述的傳統架構下（未設定 VPC origin／PrivateLink）會讓 CloudFront 完全無法連到 origin，等於破壞了原本可運作的架構。選項 A（將 PrivateLink endpoint 設為 CloudFront origin）並非 CloudFront 對 ALB 這種架構下受支援、有文件記載的 origin 存取方式（AWS 真正的私有 origin 功能是 CloudFront VPC origins，運作方式不同，也不是題目所描述的做法）。因此正確答案是 D，與 ExamTopics 建議答案一致。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"CloudFront does not support a 'PrivateLink endpoint' as a documented origin-access mechanism for an ALB in this way; the actual AWS feature for keeping an ALB private while used as a CloudFront origin (CloudFront VPC origins) works differently and is not what this option describes.","why_zh":"CloudFront 並不支援以此方式將「PrivateLink endpoint」作為 ALB 的 origin 存取機制；AWS 真正讓 ALB 保持私有並作為 CloudFront origin 的功能（CloudFront VPC origins）運作方式不同，也不是此選項所描述的做法。"},{"letter":"B","why_en":"Switching to an internal ALB and deleting the internet-facing one would sever CloudFront's connectivity to the origin entirely under the classic architecture described (no VPC origin configured), breaking the application rather than fixing the security gap.","why_zh":"在題目描述的傳統架構下（未設定 VPC origin），改用 internal ALB 並刪除 internet-facing ALB 會讓 CloudFront 完全無法連到 origin，等於直接讓應用程式失效，而非修補安全漏洞。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"AWS documentation lists allow-listing CloudFront's managed prefix list on the ALB only as an optional supplementary control, not a reliable primary defense, since the IP ranges are shared by all CloudFront customers and change periodically, so it does not guarantee the request came through this specific distribution/WAF.","why_zh":"AWS 文件將在 ALB 上允許 CloudFront 受管理前綴清單列為選用的補充控制，而非可靠的主要防禦手段，因為該 IP 範圍由所有 CloudFront 客戶共用且會定期變動，無法保證請求確實經過這個特定的 distribution／WAF。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonCloudFront/latest/DeveloperGuide/restrict-access-to-load-balancer.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonCloudFront/latest/DeveloperGuide/add-origin-custom-headers.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonCloudFront/latest/DeveloperGuide/data-protection-summary.html"]}},{"id":182,"question_en":"A company is running an application in the eu-west-1 Region. The application uses an AWS Key Management Service (AWS KMS) customer managed key to encrypt sensitive data. The company plans to deploy the application in the eu-north-1 Region. A security engineer needs to implement a key management solution for the application deployment in the new Region. The security engineer must minimize changes to the application code. Which change should the security engineer make to the AWS KMS configuration to meet these requirements?","question_zh":"一家公司在 eu-west-1 区域运行一个应用程序，该应用使用 AWS 密钥管理服务（AWS KMS）的客户托管密钥来加密敏感数据。 公司计划将该应用程序部署到 eu-north-1 区域。安全工程师需要为新区域的应用程序部署实施密钥管理解决方案，且必须尽量 减少对应用程序代码的修改。 安全工程师应如何修改AWS KMS配置以满足这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Update the key policies in eu-west-1. Point the application in eu-north-1 to use the same customer managed key as the application in eu-west-1.","B":"Allocate a new customer managed key to eu-north-1 to be used by the application that is deployed in that Region.","C":"Allocate a new customer managed key to eu-north-1. Create the same alias name for both keys. Configure the application deployment to use the key alias.","D":"Allocate a new customer managed key to eu-north-1. Create an alias for eu--1. Change the application code to point to the alias for eu--1."},"options_zh":{"A":"更新 eu-west-1 中的关键策略。将 eu-north-1 中的应用程序指向使用与 eu-west-1 中应用程序相同的客户管理密钥。","B":"为 eu-north-1 分配一个新的客户管理密钥，供部署在该区域的应用程序使用。","C":"为 eu-north-1 分配一个新的客户管理密钥。为两个密钥创建相同的别名。配置应用程序部署以使用该密钥别名。","D":"为 eu-north-1 分配一个新的客户管理密钥。为 eu-north-1 创建一个别名。修改应用程序代码，使其指向 eu-north-1 的别名。"},"answer":["C"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Security/IAM"],"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選","research":{"verdict":["C"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"AWS KMS keys are strictly regional resources: a customer managed key created in eu-west-1 cannot be used natively by a workload deployed in eu-north-1 unless it is explicitly created as a multi-Region key (which this scenario never mentions), and AWS KMS documentation states plainly that 'an alias and its KMS key must be in the same account and Region.' Because the company is deploying the application into a brand-new Region, the security engineer must provision a brand-new, Region-local customer managed key in eu-north-1 — this rules out option A outright, since no key-policy edit in eu-west-1 can make that key a first-class resource usable directly inside eu-north-1. Given that a new key is mandatory, the remaining design decision is how the application discovers which key ID/ARN to call, and this is exactly the problem AWS KMS aliases exist to solve. The AWS KMS Developer Guide's 'Learn how to use aliases in your applications' page describes this exact multi-Region pattern: 'One of the most powerful uses of aliases is in applications that run in multiple AWS Regions... it's much easier to create an alias with the same alias name in each Region... Then, use the alias in your code. When your code runs in each Region, the alias will refer to its associated KMS key in that Region... You don't need to change your code.' This maps precisely onto option C: allocate the new eu-north-1 key, give it the identical alias name already used in eu-west-1, and have the application call the alias (e.g., alias/finance) rather than a hardcoded key ARN — the SDK/CLI call resolves the alias to whichever key exists in the calling Region, so zero application code changes are needed. Option B fails the 'minimize changes to application code' requirement because a bare new key with no matching alias forces the application to be reconfigured with a new, Region-specific key ID/ARN. Option D also fails that requirement on its face — it explicitly directs the engineer to 'change the application code to point to the alias,' which is the exact change the requirement says to avoid, whereas the correct design (C) lets the same alias-referencing code run unmodified in both Regions.","explanation_zh":"AWS KMS 金鑰嚴格來說是區域性資源:在 eu-west-1 建立的客戶受管金鑰,除非明確建立為多區域金鑰(本情境完全未提及此點),否則無法讓部署在 eu-north-1 的工作負載直接原生使用。AWS KMS 文件明確指出「別名與其 KMS 金鑰必須位於相同的帳戶與區域」。由於公司要將應用程式部署到全新的區域,安全工程師必須在 eu-north-1 佈建一把全新的、該區域專屬的客戶受管金鑰——這直接排除選項 A,因為在 eu-west-1 修改金鑰政策,無法讓那把金鑰成為可在 eu-north-1 內直接使用的一級資源。既然必須建立新金鑰,剩下的設計重點就是應用程式如何得知該呼叫哪個金鑰 ID/ARN,而這正是 AWS KMS 別名(alias)機制的設計目的。AWS KMS 開發人員指南的「了解如何在應用程式中使用別名」頁面描述了完全相同的跨區域模式:「別名最強大的用途之一,就是用在跨多個 AWS 區域執行的應用程式中……在每個區域建立相同別名名稱的別名會容易得多……接著在程式碼中使用該別名。當程式碼在每個區域執行時,該別名會參照該區域中與其關聯的 KMS 金鑰……您不需要變更程式碼。」這與選項 C 完全吻合:在 eu-north-1 配置新金鑰,賦予與 eu-west-1 相同的別名名稱,並讓應用程式呼叫該別名(例如 alias/finance)而非寫死金鑰 ARN——SDK/CLI 呼叫會依據所在區域解析別名指向的對應金鑰,因此完全不需要修改應用程式程式碼。選項 B 不符合「最小化應用程式程式碼變更」的要求,因為單純建立新金鑰而未配置對應別名,會迫使應用程式必須重新設定成使用新的、該區域專屬的金鑰 ID/ARN。選項 D 同樣明顯不符此要求——它明確指示工程師「變更應用程式程式碼以指向該別名」,這正是題目要求避免的變更,而正確做法(C)則是讓同樣參照別名的程式碼在兩個區域中原封不動地執行。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"KMS keys are Region-scoped resources. Editing the key policy in eu-west-1 does not make that customer managed key a native, directly usable resource in eu-north-1 (that capability requires an explicit multi-Region key setup, which is not described here). Pointing the eu-north-1 deployment at the eu-west-1 key also reintroduces cross-Region dependency and latency, defeating the purpose of deploying the application into a second, independent Region.","why_zh":"KMS 金鑰是區域範圍的資源。修改 eu-west-1 的金鑰政策,並不會讓那把客戶受管金鑰成為可在 eu-north-1 原生直接使用的資源(要具備此能力需要明確設定多區域金鑰,而題目並未描述此設定)。讓 eu-north-1 的部署指向 eu-west-1 的金鑰,也會重新引入跨區域相依性與延遲問題,違背將應用程式部署到第二個獨立區域的初衷。"},{"letter":"B","why_en":"Creating a new customer managed key in eu-north-1 is necessary, but without an alias the application must be reconfigured to call a new, Region-specific key ID or ARN — this directly violates the requirement to minimize changes to the application code.","why_zh":"在 eu-north-1 建立新的客戶受管金鑰確實是必要的,但若沒有搭配別名,應用程式就必須重新設定以呼叫新的、該區域專屬的金鑰 ID 或 ARN——這直接違反了『最小化應用程式程式碼變更』的要求。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"This option explicitly requires changing the application code to point to the new alias, which is precisely the outcome the requirement says to avoid. It ignores the documented AWS pattern of reusing an identical alias name across Regions so the existing alias-referencing code needs no modification at all.","why_zh":"此選項明確要求變更應用程式程式碼以指向新別名,這正是題目要求要避免的結果。它忽略了 AWS 文件記載的做法——在各區域使用相同的別名名稱,讓既有參照該別名的程式碼完全不需修改。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/kms/latest/developerguide/alias-using.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/kms/latest/developerguide/kms-alias.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/kms/latest/developerguide/multi-region-keys-overview.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/kms/latest/developerguide/rotate-keys-manually.html"]}},{"id":183,"question_en":"A company is building a secure solution that relies on an AWS Key Management Service (AWS KMS) customer managed key. The company wants to allow AWS Lambda to use the KMS key. However, the company wants to prevent Amazon EC2 from using the key. Which solution will meet these requirements?","question_zh":"一家公司正在构建一个依赖于 AWS 密钥管理服务（AWS KMS）客户管理密钥的安全解决方案。该公司希望允许 AWS Lambda 使用该 KMS 密钥，但同时希望阻止 Amazon EC2 使用该密钥。 哪种解决方案能满足这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Use IAM explicit deny for EC2 instance profiles and allow for Lambda roles.","B":"Use a KMS key policy with kms:ViaService conditions to allow Lambda usage and deny EC2 usage.","C":"Use aws:SourceIp and aws:AuthorizedService condition keys in the KMS key policy.","D":"Use an SCP to deny EC2 and allow Lambda."},"options_zh":{"A":"对 EC2 实例配置文件使用 IAM 显式拒绝，对 Lambda 角色使用允许。","B":"使用带有 kms:ViaService 条件的 KMS 密钥策略，允许 Lambda 使用并拒绝 EC2 使用。","C":"在KMS密钥策略SourceIp和aws:AuthorizedService条件键。","D":"使用安全组规则拒绝 EC2，允许 Lambda。"},"answer":["B"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Organizations/Governance","Security/IAM","Compute"],"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選","research":{"verdict":["B"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"both","explanation_en":"AWS KMS provides the kms:ViaService condition key specifically to restrict use of a KMS key to requests made through (or on behalf of a principal by) one or more specified AWS services, using values like \"lambda.<region>.amazonaws.com\" or \"ec2.<region>.amazonaws.com\". A key policy statement can Allow kms:ViaService = lambda.*.amazonaws.com and a separate Deny statement can target kms:ViaService = ec2.*.amazonaws.com, which is exactly the documented pattern AWS shows for restricting key usage to one service (e.g. EC2/EBS) via kms:CallerAccount + kms:ViaService in the AWS KMS developer guide. This is a key-policy (resource-based) control, so it is centrally enforced for every principal and role regardless of how many IAM roles or instance profiles exist, unlike identity-based denies which must be replicated across every EC2 role/instance profile and don't scale as new roles are created. aws:SourceIp is explicitly discouraged by AWS for KMS policies (source IP is unreliable/absent for calls forwarded on a principal's behalf via a service), and 'aws:AuthorizedService' is not a real documented AWS global condition key. SCPs operate at the IAM-permission level for accounts/OUs and are not the natural or documented mechanism for this service-vs-service KMS restriction. Therefore B is the correct, AWS-documented solution.","explanation_zh":"AWS KMS 提供 kms:ViaService 條件鍵，專門用來將 KMS 金鑰的使用限制在透過（或代表主體、由）特定 AWS 服務發出的請求，值如 \"lambda.<region>.amazonaws.com\" 或 \"ec2.<region>.amazonaws.com\"。金鑰政策（key policy）中可以用一個 Allow 陳述式設定 kms:ViaService = lambda.*.amazonaws.com，並用另一個 Deny 陳述式設定 kms:ViaService = ec2.*.amazonaws.com，這正是 AWS KMS 開發人員指南中示範的、以 kms:CallerAccount + kms:ViaService 限制金鑰只能透過某一服務（例如 EC2/EBS）使用的官方範例模式。這是資源型（金鑰政策）控制，會對所有主體與角色集中生效，不論有多少 IAM 角色或執行個體設定檔（instance profile），而不像身分型（identity-based）明確拒絕那樣，必須套用到每一個 EC2 角色/執行個體設定檔，且無法自動涵蓋未來新建的角色。AWS 官方文件明確建議在 KMS 政策中謹慎使用甚至避免依賴 aws:SourceIp（因為透過服務代為發出的請求，來源 IP 不可靠或不存在），而 'aws:AuthorizedService' 並非真實存在的 AWS 全域條件鍵。SCP 是在帳戶/OU 層級控管 IAM 權限的機制，並非官方文件針對「服務對服務」KMS 使用限制所建議的做法。因此 B 是正確且有官方文件依據的解法。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"An IAM explicit deny on every EC2 instance profile role is an identity-based control that must be replicated across all current and future EC2 roles/instance profiles; it does not centrally protect the key itself and does not scale, unlike a key-policy-level kms:ViaService restriction.","why_zh":"在每個 EC2 執行個體設定檔角色上設定 IAM 明確拒絕屬於身分型控制，必須套用到所有現有及未來的 EC2 角色/執行個體設定檔，無法在金鑰本身層級集中防護，也無法隨新角色自動擴展，不如金鑰政策層級的 kms:ViaService 限制。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"aws:SourceIp is explicitly called out in AWS KMS documentation as unreliable/risky to combine with KMS permission conditions (source IP may not propagate as expected for service-forwarded requests), and 'aws:AuthorizedService' is not a documented AWS global or KMS condition key at all.","why_zh":"AWS KMS 文件明確指出，將 aws:SourceIp 與 KMS 權限條件併用有風險/不可靠（對於由服務代為轉發的請求，來源 IP 不會如預期傳遞），而 'aws:AuthorizedService' 根本不是任何官方文件記載的 AWS 全域或 KMS 條件鍵。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"SCPs manage the maximum available IAM permissions for accounts/OUs across an AWS Organization; they are not the documented mechanism for restricting a specific KMS key to one AWS service versus another, and applying an SCP is a much blunter, organization-wide control than a resource-level key policy condition.","why_zh":"SCP 是用來管理 AWS Organizations 中帳戶/OU 可用的最大 IAM 權限範圍，並非官方文件針對「限制特定 KMS 金鑰只給某一 AWS 服務使用、禁止另一服務使用」所提供的機制，且套用 SCP 是組織層級的粗略控制，遠不如資源層級（金鑰政策）條件精確。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/kms/latest/developerguide/conditions-kms.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/kms/latest/developerguide/conditions-aws.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/kms/latest/developerguide/policy-conditions.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/amazondynamodb/latest/developerguide/encryption.usagenotes.html"]}},{"id":184,"question_en":"A company has an AWS account that hosts a production application. The company receives an email notification that Amazon GuardDuty has detected an Impact:IAMUser/AnomalousBehavior finding in the account. A security engineer needs to run the investigation playbook for this security incident and must collect and analyze the information without affecting the application.Which solution will meet these requirements MOST quickly?","question_zh":"一家公司拥有一个用于托管生产应用的 AWS 账户。该公司收到一封电子邮件通知，提示 Amazon GuardDuty 在该账户 中检测到一条“影响：IAM 用户/异常行为”的发现项。安全工程师需要针对此次安全事件执行调查流程，并在不影响 应用程序运行的前提下收集和分析相关信息。 哪种解决方案能最快满足这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Log in to the AWS account by using read-only credentials. Review the GuardDuty finding for details about the IAM credentials that were used. Use the IAM console to add a DenyAll policy to the IAM principal.","B":"Log in to the AWS account by using read-only credentials. Review the GuardDuty finding to determine which API calls initiated the finding. Use Amazon Detective to review the API calls in context.","C":"Log in to the AWS account by using administrator credentials. Review the GuardDuty finding for details about the IAM credentials that were used. Use the IAM console to add a DenyAll policy to the IAM principal.","D":"Log in to the AWS account by using read-only credentials. Review the GuardDuty finding to determine which API calls initiated the finding. Use AWS CloudTrail Insights and AWS CloudTrail Lake to review the API calls in context."},"options_zh":{"A":"使用只读凭据登录 AWS 账户。查看 GuardDuty 发现的详细信息，了解所使用的 IAM 凭据。通过 IAM 控制台为该 IAM 主体添加 DenyAll 策略。","B":"使用只读凭据登录 AWS 账户。查看 GuardDuty 的发现信息，以确定是哪些 API 调用触发了该发现。使用 Amazon Detective 在上下文中审查这些 API 调用。","C":"使用管理员凭据登录 AWS 账户。查看 GuardDuty 的发现信息，以了解所使用的 IAM 凭据的详细情况。然后通过 IAM 控制台为该 IAM 主体添加一个拒绝所有权限的策略。","D":"使用只读凭证登录 AWS 账户。查看 GuardDuty 的发现信息，以确定是哪些 API 调用触发了该发现。使用 AWS CloudTrail Insights 和 AWS CloudTrail Lake 在上下文中审查这些 API 调用。"},"answer":["B"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Security/IAM","Monitoring/Ops"],"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選","research":{"verdict":["B"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"community","explanation_en":"B is correct. The task has two hard constraints: (1) do not affect the running application, and (2) do it MOST quickly. Constraint 1 rules out C (administrator credentials are unnecessary for read-only investigation and violate least privilege/blast-radius principles) and rules out A and C together, since both jump straight to applying a DenyAll policy to the IAM principal before the investigation is even complete — that is a remediation action, not investigation, and risks breaking legitimate application functionality if the finding turns out to involve a role the application also uses, or if it is a false positive. That leaves B and D, which both correctly start with read-only credentials and reviewing the GuardDuty finding for the API calls that triggered it. The deciding factor is speed of correlating those API calls 'in context.' Amazon Detective is purpose-built for exactly this: GuardDuty findings integrate with Detective via a one-click 'Investigate with Detective' pivot directly from the finding details pane, and Detective has already ingested and pre-organized CloudTrail management/data events, VPC Flow Logs, EKS audit logs, and GuardDuty findings into a behavior graph with prebuilt entity profiles and visualizations — so an analyst instantly sees related API calls, entities, and timelines without writing any queries. AWS Detective's own documentation frames its triage/scoping/response phases as starting directly from a GuardDuty finding for this reason. CloudTrail Insights (D) is a baseline-anomaly-detection feature for unusual API call volume/rate, not an ad hoc forensic tool for a specific already-identified finding, and CloudTrail Lake requires the analyst to author and run SQL queries against event data stores to reconstruct context manually — both are slower and more manual than Detective's pre-built, point-and-click correlation. Hence B best satisfies 'MOST quickly' while keeping actions read-only and non-disruptive to the application.","explanation_zh":"正確答案是 B。題目有兩個硬性條件:(1) 不能影響正在運行的應用程式,(2) 要用「最快」的方式完成。條件 (1) 排除了 C(調查階段使用管理員憑證並非必要,違反最小權限原則),也排除了 A 與 C 的共同做法——兩者都在調查尚未完成前就直接對 IAM 主體套用 DenyAll 政策,這是「補救措施」而非「調查」,若該角色其實也被應用程式使用,或該發現其實是誤判,就可能直接打斷應用程式運作。剩下 B 與 D,兩者都正確地以唯讀憑證登入並先檢視 GuardDuty finding 找出觸發的 API 呼叫。決勝點在於「用情境（in context）關聯這些 API 呼叫」的速度。Amazon Detective 正是為此設計:GuardDuty 主控台可直接從發現詳情窗格一鍵「Investigate with Detective」跳轉,Detective 已預先擷取並整理好 CloudTrail 管理/資料事件、VPC Flow Logs、EKS 稽核日誌與 GuardDuty 發現,建構成行為圖(behavior graph),並提供現成的實體檔案與視覺化圖表,分析師無需撰寫任何查詢即可立即看到相關 API 呼叫、實體與時間軸。AWS Detective 官方文件也明確將其分診(triage)、範圍界定(scoping)、回應(response)三階段流程設計為直接從 GuardDuty finding 開始。相較之下,CloudTrail Insights(D)是針對 API 呼叫量/頻率異常的基準偵測功能,並非為特定已知發現做即時鑑識分析而設計;CloudTrail Lake 則需要分析師自行撰寫並執行 SQL 查詢來手動重建情境——兩者都比 Detective 現成、點選式的關聯分析來得慢且繁瑣。因此在維持唯讀、不干擾應用程式的前提下,B 最能滿足「最快」的要求。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"Applying a DenyAll policy to the IAM principal is a remediation/containment action taken before the investigation is complete, not an investigation step, and directly risks affecting the application if the principal is shared with or used by production workloads — violating the 'without affecting the application' requirement.","why_zh":"對 IAM 主體套用 DenyAll 政策是在調查完成前就採取的補救/圍堵措施,而非調查步驟,若該主體也被生產環境的應用程式共用或使用,將直接違反「不影響應用程式」的要求。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"Using administrator credentials for a read-only investigation is unnecessary and violates least privilege, and it pairs with the same premature DenyAll remediation action as A that risks disrupting the application before scoping is complete.","why_zh":"在只需唯讀存取的調查階段使用管理員憑證既無必要也違反最小權限原則,且與 A 一樣在範圍界定完成前就採取 DenyAll 補救動作,可能中斷應用程式運作。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"CloudTrail Insights is designed to surface unusual API call volume/rate patterns over a rolling baseline, not to provide instant contextual correlation for one already-identified finding; CloudTrail Lake requires the analyst to write and run SQL queries to manually reconstruct the context, which is slower than Detective's prebuilt, point-and-click entity profiles and visualizations for the same GuardDuty finding.","why_zh":"CloudTrail Insights 是設計來偵測相對於滾動基準的異常 API 呼叫量/頻率模式,而非為單一已知發現提供即時情境關聯;CloudTrail Lake 則需要分析師自行撰寫並執行 SQL 查詢來手動重建情境,相較 Detective 針對同一 GuardDuty finding 提供的現成、點選式實體檔案與視覺化圖表,速度更慢。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/detective/latest/userguide/detective-investigation-about.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/guardduty/latest/ug/detective-integration.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/guardduty/latest/ug/guardduty_finding-types-iam.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/awscloudtrail/latest/userguide/cloudtrail-insights-events-with-cloudtrail.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/awscloudtrail/latest/userguide/query-event-data-store.html"]}},{"id":185,"question_en":"A company sends Apache logs from EC2 Auto Scaling instances to a CloudWatch Logs log group with 1-year retention. A suspicious IP address appears in logs. A security engineer needs to analyze the past week of logs to count requests from that IP and list requested URLs. What should the engineer do with the LEAST effort?","question_zh":"一家公司将其EC2自动扩展实例的Apache日志发送到保留期为一年的CloudWatch Logs日志组中。日志中出现了一个可疑的IP地 址。安全工程师需要分析过去一周的日志，统计该IP的请求次数并列出所请求的URL。 工程师最少需要做什么？","options_en":{"A":"Export to S3 and use Macie.","B":"Stream to OpenSearch and analyze.","C":"Use CloudWatch Logs Insights with queries.","D":"Export to S3 and use AWS Glue."},"options_zh":{"A":"导出到 S3 并使用 Macie。","B":"流式传输至 OpenSearch 并进行分析。","C":"使用 CloudWatch Logs Insights 进行查询。","D":"导出到 S3 并使用 AWS Glue。"},"answer":["C"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Security/IAM","Storage","Compute","Monitoring/Ops","Analytics"],"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選","research":{"verdict":["C"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"both","explanation_en":"The logs are already sitting in a CloudWatch Logs log group, and the task is a one-off, time-bounded investigation (last 7 days) to count requests from one IP and list the URLs it hit. CloudWatch Logs Insights is purpose-built for exactly this: you run an ad-hoc query language (filter, stats count(), sort, limit) directly against the existing log group over a chosen time range, with no data export, no new infrastructure, and no ongoing cost — results return in seconds. AWS documentation describes Logs Insights as letting you 'interactively search and analyze your log data in Amazon CloudWatch Logs' and 'perform queries to help you more efficiently and effectively respond to operational issues,' which is precisely this use case. All other options require standing up or feeding a separate analytics/classification service (Macie, OpenSearch, Glue) purely to answer a narrow, short-term question, which is strictly more effort for no added benefit here.","explanation_zh":"日誌已經存在 CloudWatch Logs 的 log group 中，且需求只是針對過去 7 天做一次性、有時間範圍限制的調查：統計來自某個 IP 的請求數並列出被存取的 URL。CloudWatch Logs Insights 正是為此設計——直接對既有 log group 執行 filter、stats count()、sort、limit 等查詢語言，指定時間範圍即可，不需匯出資料、不需建置新基礎設施、也沒有額外持續性成本，結果幾秒內就能拿到。AWS 文件說明 Logs Insights 可以「互動式地搜尋與分析 Amazon CloudWatch Logs 中的日誌資料」，並「執行查詢以更有效率地回應維運問題」，完全對應此情境。其餘選項都需要另外架設或餵資料給獨立的分析／分類服務（Macie、OpenSearch、Glue），只為了回答一個範圍狹窄的短期問題，明顯是更多的工作量卻沒有額外效益。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"Amazon Macie is a data-classification and PII-discovery service for S3 objects; it has no concept of counting requests by source IP or enumerating requested URLs from Apache access logs, and using it here would require exporting the logs to S3 first for a capability Macie doesn't even provide.","why_zh":"Amazon Macie 是針對 S3 物件的資料分類與 PII 探索服務，並不具備依來源 IP 統計請求數或列出 Apache access log 中被請求 URL 的能力；要用它還得先把日誌匯出到 S3，而且 Macie 根本沒有這項功能。"},{"letter":"B","why_en":"Streaming to OpenSearch (via subscription filter/Kinesis Firehose) works for analysis but requires provisioning and configuring an OpenSearch domain/ingestion pipeline — a standing piece of infrastructure — for a single ad-hoc investigation, which is far more setup effort than Logs Insights.","why_zh":"把日誌串流到 OpenSearch（透過訂閱過濾器／Kinesis Firehose）確實可以分析，但需要建置並設定 OpenSearch 網域與擷取管線——一個常駐的基礎設施——只為了一次性的調查，設定成本遠高於直接使用 Logs Insights。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"Exporting to S3 and using AWS Glue (crawler + ETL job + Athena/other query engine) is a batch, multi-step pipeline meant for ongoing or large-scale data processing; it adds export lag, job setup, and schema/catalog work that is unnecessary for a quick one-week IP/URL lookup.","why_zh":"匯出到 S3 再用 AWS Glue（crawler、ETL job，再搭配 Athena 等查詢引擎）是一套批次、多步驟的管線，適合長期或大規模資料處理；對於只是查一週內某 IP 的請求與 URL，這會多出匯出延遲、job 設定與 schema/catalog 建置等不必要的工作。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonCloudWatch/latest/logs/AnalyzingLogData.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonCloudWatch/latest/logs/CWL_QuerySyntax.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonCloudWatch/latest/logs/CWL_AnalyzeLogData_LogsInsights.html"]}},{"id":186,"question_en":"A security engineer for a company is investigating suspicious traffic on a web application in the AWS Cloud. The web application is protected by an Application Load Balancer (ALB) behind an Amazon CloudFront distribution. There is an AWS WAF web ACL associated with the ALB. The company stores AWS WAF logs in an Amazon S3 bucket. The engineer notices that all incoming requests in the AWS WAF logs originate from a small number of IP addresses that correspond to CloudFront edge locations. The security engineer must identify the source IP addresses of the clients that are initiating the suspicious requests. Which solution will meet this requirement?","question_zh":"一家公司的安全工程师正在调查 AWS 云中某个 Web 应用程序上的可疑流量。该 Web 应用程序由一 个位于 Amazon CloudFront 分发后的 Application Load Balancer（ALB）进行保护，并关联了一个 AWS WAF 网站访问控制列表（web ACL）。该公司将 AWS WAF 日志存储在 Amazon S3 存储桶中。 工程师注意到，AWS WAF 日志中的所有传入请求均来自少量与 CloudFront 边缘位置对应的 IP 地 址。安全工程师必须确定发起可疑请求的客户端的真实源 IP 地址。 哪种解决方案能满足这一要求？","options_en":{"A":"Enable VPC Flow Logs in the VPC where the ALB is deployed. Examine the source field to capture the client IP addresses.","B":"Inspect the X-Forwarded-For header in the AWS WAF logs to determine the original client IP addresses.","C":"Modify the CloudFront distribution to disable ALB connection reuse. Examine the clientIp field in the AWS WAF logs to identify the original client IP addresses.","D":"Configure CloudFront to add a custom header named Client-IP to origin requests that are sent to the ALB."},"options_zh":{"A":"在部署ALB的VPC中启用VPC流量日志，检查源字段以捕获客户端IP地址。","B":"检查 AWS WAF 日志中的 X-Forwarded-For 请求头，以确定原始客户端的 IP 地址。","C":"修改 CloudFront 分发设置，以禁用 ALB 连接复用。检查 AWS WAF 日志中的 clientIp 字段， 以识别原始客户端 IP 地址。","D":"配置 CloudFront，以便在发送到 ALB 的源请求中添加名为 Client-IP 的自定义标头。"},"answer":["B"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Networking/DNS","Security/IAM","Storage"],"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選","research":{"verdict":["B"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"community","explanation_en":"AWS WAF is attached to the ALB, not to CloudFront, so the WAF log's clientIp field always records the IP address of whatever made the TCP connection to the ALB — which is a CloudFront edge server, not the original viewer. This is expected behavior, not a misconfiguration: AWS WAF documentation defines clientIp simply as 'The IP address of the client sending the request,' i.e., the immediate peer. However, CloudFront documentation confirms that when it forwards a viewer request to a custom origin (here, the ALB) it automatically adds an X-Forwarded-For header containing the viewer's real IP address if one isn't already present, or appends the viewer IP it read from the TCP connection to an existing X-Forwarded-For chain. That header travels with the request all the way to the ALB/WAF. AWS WAF's log format captures the full list of request headers in httpRequest.headers, so the X-Forwarded-For header — and the true client IP it carries — is already present in the existing WAF logs with zero infrastructure changes; the engineer just needs to inspect it. This is the lowest-effort, immediately-available solution and requires no reconfiguration of CloudFront, ALB, or logging pipelines.","explanation_zh":"AWS WAF 是掛在 ALB 上，而不是掛在 CloudFront 上，所以 WAF log 的 clientIp 欄位永遠記錄的是「直接跟 ALB 建立 TCP 連線的來源」——也就是 CloudFront edge server 的 IP，而不是原始使用者的 IP。這是預期行為，不是設定錯誤：AWS WAF 文件把 clientIp 定義為「發出請求的 client 的 IP 位址」，也就是直接對接的那一端。但 CloudFront 文件證實，當它把 viewer 請求轉發給 custom origin（此處即 ALB）時，若請求原本沒有 X-Forwarded-For 標頭，CloudFront 會自動加上一個內含 viewer 真實 IP 的 X-Forwarded-For 標頭；若已存在，則會把從 TCP 連線讀到的 viewer IP 附加到既有的 X-Forwarded-For 鏈尾端。這個標頭會一路跟著請求送到 ALB／WAF。AWS WAF 的 log 格式會把完整的請求標頭清單記錄在 httpRequest.headers 中，因此 X-Forwarded-For 標頭（及其攜帶的真實 client IP）早已存在於現有的 WAF logs 裡，不需要任何基礎設施異動；工程師只需要去檢視它即可。這是成本最低、立即可用的解法，不需要重新設定 CloudFront、ALB 或日誌管線。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"VPC Flow Logs capture IP-layer (Layer 3/4) connection metadata for the ALB's elastic network interfaces — source/destination IP, ports, protocol, bytes. Since the TCP connection to the ALB is established by the CloudFront edge server, the 'source' field in Flow Logs will show the CloudFront edge IP, exactly the same limitation seen in the WAF clientIp field. Flow Logs do not parse HTTP headers like X-Forwarded-For, so they cannot reveal the original viewer's IP address here.","why_zh":"VPC Flow Logs 擷取的是 ALB 彈性網路介面上的第 3/4 層連線metadata（來源／目的 IP、埠、協定、位元組數）。由於與 ALB 建立 TCP 連線的是 CloudFront edge server，Flow Logs 的 source 欄位一樣只會顯示 CloudFront edge 的 IP，跟 WAF clientIp 欄位遇到的限制完全相同。Flow Logs 不會解析 X-Forwarded-For 這類 HTTP 標頭，因此無法揭露原始 viewer 的 IP。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"CloudFront's origin 'connection reuse' setting (persistent/keep-alive connections to the origin) only affects whether CloudFront reuses TCP connections to the origin for efficiency; it has no effect on which IP address is recorded as the TCP peer. The WAF clientIp field will still show the CloudFront edge server's IP regardless of this setting, so disabling connection reuse does not make clientIp show the true viewer IP — the premise of this option is technically false.","why_zh":"CloudFront 對 origin 的「connection reuse」（持久連線／keep-alive）設定，只影響 CloudFront 是否重複使用與 origin 的 TCP 連線以提升效率，並不會改變被記錄為 TCP 對端的 IP 位址。不論此設定為何，WAF 的 clientIp 欄位都還是會顯示 CloudFront edge server 的 IP，所以關閉 connection reuse 並不會讓 clientIp 顯示真實 viewer IP——這個選項的前提在技術上就不成立。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"CloudFront's 'add custom header to origin requests' feature (documented under origin custom headers) lets you attach a fixed, statically-configured name/value pair to every request sent to the origin — it cannot dynamically populate a header with each request's actual viewer IP through simple configuration. Also unnecessary: CloudFront already automatically forwards the viewer's real IP via X-Forwarded-For to custom origins by default, so inventing a new 'Client-IP' header duplicates functionality that already exists and is already visible in the WAF logs.","why_zh":"CloudFront 的『在 origin 請求加自訂標頭』功能（origin custom headers）只能替每個送往 origin 的請求附加固定、靜態設定的 name/value，無法透過簡單設定就動態帶入每個請求各自的真實 viewer IP。而且這也沒有必要：CloudFront 預設本來就會透過 X-Forwarded-For 自動把 viewer 真實 IP 轉發給 custom origin，新增一個『Client-IP』標頭只是重複已存在、且已經在 WAF logs 裡看得到的功能。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/waf/latest/developerguide/logging-fields.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonCloudFront/latest/DeveloperGuide/RequestAndResponseBehaviorCustomOrigin.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonCloudWatch/latest/logs/CloudWatch-Logs-Transformation-BuiltIn.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonCloudFront/latest/DeveloperGuide/add-origin-custom-headers.html"]}},{"id":187,"question_en":"A security engineer needs to configure DDoS protection for a Network Load Balancer (NLB) with an Elastic IP address. The security engineer wants to set up an AWS WAF web ACL with a rate-based rule statement to protect the NLB. The security engineer needs to determine a rate limit that will not block legitimate traffic. The securityengineer has configured the rule statement to aggregate based on the source IP address. How should the security engineer configure the rule to protect the NLB?","question_zh":"安全工程师需要为带有弹性IP地址的网络负载均衡器（NLB）配置DDoS防护。该安全工程师希望设置一个基于速率规则的 AWS WAF网络ACL，以保护NLB。 安全工程师需要确定一个不会阻断合法流量的速率限制。该安全工程师已将规则语句配置为基于源IP地址进行聚合。 安全工程师应如何配置规则以保护NLB？","options_en":{"A":"Configure the rule to use theCountaction.","B":"Configure the rule to use theBlockaction.","C":"Configure the rule to use theMonitoraction.","D":"Configure the rule to use theAllowaction."},"options_zh":{"A":"配置规则以使用计数操作。","B":"配置规则以使用“阻止”操作。","C":"配置规则以使用“监控”操作。","D":"配置规则以使用“允许”操作。"},"answer":["A"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Networking/DNS","Security/IAM"],"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選","research":{"verdict":["A"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"both","explanation_en":"The scenario's key requirement is to 'determine a rate limit that will not block legitimate traffic' — i.e., the engineer does not yet know the correct threshold and must validate it safely. AWS WAF's documented best practice for rolling out any new rule, including rate-based rules, is to first set the rule action to Count. In Count mode, AWS WAF evaluates the rule and increments a counter/emits CloudWatch metrics and sampled logs for every request that would have matched, but it does not actually restrict or block traffic. This lets the engineer observe real traffic volume per source IP against the configured rate threshold, tune the threshold using CloudWatch metrics, and confirm no legitimate clients would be caught, before ever risking a false-positive block. Only after the threshold is validated should the action be changed to Block. Monitor and Allow are not valid AWS WAF rule actions (the actual actions are Allow, Block, Count, and CAPTCHA/Challenge — 'Monitor' is not one of them, and 'Allow' would defeat the purpose of rate limiting since it never restricts anything even after validation). Therefore Count (A) is correct for this determine-safely step.","explanation_zh":"題目的關鍵需求是「找出一個不會誤擋合法流量的速率限制值」——也就是工程師尚未確定正確的門檻值，必須先安全地驗證。AWS WAF 官方建議在部署任何新規則（包含 rate-based rule）時，應先將規則動作設為 Count。在 Count 模式下，WAF 會正常評估規則、對符合條件的請求計數並產生 CloudWatch 指標與取樣日誌，但『不會』實際限制或封鎖流量。這讓工程師可以觀察每個來源 IP 的真實流量相對於設定門檻的情況，透過 CloudWatch 指標調整門檻，並在真正冒著誤擋合法用戶的風險之前先行確認。等門檻驗證無誤後，才將動作改為 Block。Monitor 與 Allow 都不是 AWS WAF 規則的有效動作（WAF 的動作只有 Allow、Block、Count 與 CAPTCHA/Challenge；'Monitor' 根本不存在；而 'Allow' 即使驗證完成後也永遠不會限制流量，違背 rate limiting 的目的）。因此本題（先安全地找出門檻）正確答案是 Count（A）。","distractors":[{"letter":"B","why_en":"Block is the enforcement action used only after the correct rate limit has already been validated. Configuring Block first, while the threshold is still unverified, risks blocking legitimate traffic — the exact outcome the engineer is trying to avoid.","why_zh":"Block 是門檻確認無誤『之後』才使用的強制動作。若在門檻尚未驗證時就直接設為 Block，就有可能誤擋合法流量，恰好是工程師想避免的結果。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"'Monitor' is not an actual AWS WAF rule action. The valid rule actions in AWS WAF are Allow, Block, Count, and CAPTCHA/Challenge — Monitor does not exist as a configurable action.","why_zh":"'Monitor' 並非 AWS WAF 真實存在的規則動作。WAF 有效的規則動作為 Allow、Block、Count 與 CAPTCHA/Challenge，並沒有 Monitor 這個可設定的動作。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"Allow would let all requests through regardless of rate, providing no rate-limiting or DDoS protection at all — it does not help determine or enforce a safe rate limit.","why_zh":"Allow 會讓所有請求無論流量高低都直接放行，完全沒有速率限制或 DDoS 防護效果——無法幫助判斷或落實安全的速率限制。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/waf/latest/developerguide/web-acl-testing.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/waf/latest/developerguide/classic-web-acl-testing.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/waf/latest/developerguide/waf-rule-action.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/waf/latest/developerguide/ddos-app-layer-rbr.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/waf/latest/developerguide/waf-rule-statement-type-rate-based-request-limiting.html"]}},{"id":188,"question_en":"A company has an AWS Lambda function that requires access to an Amazon S3 bucket. The company’ssecurity policy requires that connections to Amazon S3 are over a private network and are secure. The company has configured a gateway VPC endpoint in the VPC to allow access to Amazon S3. The company has configured the Lambda function to run inside the VPC. Additionally, the company has configured the Lambda function to use a private subnet that has a route to the internet through a NAT gateway. Other resources in the VPC use this private subnet to access the internet successfully. When the Lambda function runs, it uses the NAT gateway instead of the gateway VPC endpoint to access Amazon S3. What can a security engineer do to ensure that the Lambda function uses the gateway VPC endpoint for Amazon S3?","question_zh":"一家公司有一个 AWS Lambda 函数，需要访问 Amazon S3 存储桶。公司的安全策略要求对 Amazon S3 的连接必须通过私有网络进行，并且确保安全。 该公司已在VPC中配置了网关VPC端点，以允许访问Amazon S3。公司还配置Lambda函数在VPC内 部运行，并且将Lambda函数设置为使用一个私有子网，该子网通过NAT网关路由到互联网。VPC中 的其他资源均通过此私有子网成功访问互联网。当Lambda函数运行时，它会使用NAT网关而非网关 VPC端点来访问Amazon S3。 安全工程师可以采取哪些措施来确保Lambda函数使用Amazon S3的网关VPC端点？","options_en":{"A":"Remove the route to the NAT gateway within the route table of the private subnet that the Lambda function uses.","B":"Associate the gateway VPC endpoint with the route table of the private subnet that the Lambda function uses.","C":"Adjust the gateway VPC endpoint policy to allow access from the Lambda function’s network interface address.","D":"Configure the Lambda function’s security group to allow connections to the S3 network address space."},"options_zh":{"A":"从Lambda函数所使用的私有子网的路由表中移除通往NAT网关的路由。","B":"将网关VPC端点关联到Lambda函数所使用的私有子网的路由表。","C":"调整网关VPC端点策略，以允许从Lambda函数的网络接口地址进行访问。","D":"配置 Lambda 函数的安全组，以允许连接到 S3 的网络地址空间。"},"answer":["B"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Networking/DNS","Storage","Compute"],"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選","research":{"verdict":["B"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"both","explanation_en":"A gateway VPC endpoint (unlike an interface endpoint) is not an ENI with an IP address — it works purely through route tables. AWS automatically inserts a route with a target of the endpoint (via the AWS-managed prefix list for the service) only into the specific route tables you explicitly associate with the endpoint when you create or edit it. If the Lambda function's private subnet uses a route table that was never associated with the S3 gateway endpoint, that route table still only has the 0.0.0.0/0 -> NAT gateway route for internet-bound traffic, so all S3 traffic (which uses public IP ranges) matches the NAT route instead, even though the endpoint exists elsewhere in the VPC. Associating the gateway endpoint with the private subnet's route table adds the prefix-list route that takes priority (more specific route) over the NAT gateway's 0.0.0.0/0 route, causing traffic to Amazon S3 to flow over the private AWS network path through the endpoint instead of the NAT gateway. Removing the NAT route (A) would break other traffic that legitimately needs internet access via that subnet and doesn't guarantee endpoint usage if the endpoint isn't associated with the route table. Endpoint policies (C) and security groups (D) control authorization/traffic filtering, not path selection — they never change which target (NAT vs. endpoint) is chosen for routing, and gateway endpoints don't even have their own security groups or ENI addresses to reference from a Lambda security group.","explanation_zh":"Gateway VPC endpoint（不同於 interface endpoint）並非帶有 IP 位址的 ENI，而是純粹透過路由表運作。AWS 只會在你建立或編輯 endpoint 時明確關聯的路由表中，自動加入一條以該 endpoint 為目標（透過該服務的 AWS 受管前綴清單）的路由。如果 Lambda 函數所在私有子網使用的路由表從未與 S3 gateway endpoint 建立關聯，該路由表就只會有 0.0.0.0/0 -> NAT gateway 這條供對外流量使用的路由，導致所有前往 S3（使用公開 IP 範圍）的流量都符合 NAT 路由，即使 VPC 內其他地方已有此 endpoint 存在。將 gateway endpoint 與該私有子網的路由表建立關聯，會加入前綴清單路由，其優先權（較精確的路由）高於 NAT gateway 的 0.0.0.0/0 路由，使前往 Amazon S3 的流量改走 endpoint 的私有 AWS 網路路徑，而非經過 NAT gateway。移除 NAT 路由（A）會破壞該子網其他合法需要對外連線的流量，且若 endpoint 未與路由表關聯，也無法保證流量會改走 endpoint。Endpoint 政策（C）與安全群組（D）控制的是授權/流量過濾，並不會改變路由選擇（NAT 或 endpoint）；況且 gateway endpoint 本身並沒有可供 Lambda 安全群組參照的安全群組或 ENI 位址。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"Removing the NAT route would stop Lambda's S3 traffic from defaulting to NAT, but it breaks all other legitimate internet-bound traffic from the subnet (which the question says other resources rely on), and does not by itself guarantee S3 traffic uses the endpoint if the endpoint isn't associated with that route table.","why_zh":"移除 NAT 路由雖然能阻止 S3 流量預設走 NAT，但也會破壞該子網其他資源合法需要的對外流量（題目提到其他資源仰賴此路由），且如果 endpoint 未與該路由表關聯，也無法確保 S3 流量會改走 endpoint。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"Endpoint policies are IAM-style authorization documents that control which principals/actions/resources are allowed through the endpoint; they have no effect on network routing/path selection between NAT and the endpoint, and a Lambda ENI address isn't something an endpoint policy references.","why_zh":"Endpoint 政策是類 IAM 的授權文件，控制哪些主體/動作/資源可透過該 endpoint 存取；它對 NAT 與 endpoint 之間的網路路由選擇毫無影響，而且 endpoint 政策也不會參照 Lambda 的 ENI 位址。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"Security groups filter allowed traffic on a resource's ENI; they don't influence which route (NAT gateway vs. gateway endpoint) is selected for outbound packets, and gateway endpoints don't expose a network address space that a security group rule would reference.","why_zh":"安全群組是過濾資源 ENI 上允許的流量，並不會影響對外封包選擇哪一條路由（NAT gateway 或 gateway endpoint），而且 gateway endpoint 也沒有可供安全群組規則參照的網路位址範圍。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/vpc/latest/privatelink/vpc-endpoints-s3.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/vpc/latest/userguide/create-a-vpc-with-private-subnets-and-nat-gateways-using-aws-cli.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/vpc/latest/userguide/route-table-options.html"]}},{"id":189,"question_en":"A company has the following security policy for its Amazon Aurora MySQL databases for a single AWS account: • Database storage must be encrypted at rest. • Deletion protection must be enabled. • Databases must not be publicly accessible. • Database audit logs must be published to Amazon CloudWatch Logs. A security engineer must implement a solution thatcontinuously monitorsall Aurora MySQL resources for compliance with this policy. The solution must be able todisplay a database ' s compliance state for each part of the policy at any time. Which solution will meet these requirements?","question_zh":"一家公司为其单个AWS账户中的Amazon Aurora MySQL数据库制定了以下安全策略： • 数据库存储在静态状态下必须进行加密。 • 必须启用删除保护。 数据库不得对外公开访问。 • 数据库审计日志必须发布到 Amazon CloudWatch Logs。 安全工程师必须实施一种解决方案，持续监控所有 Aurora MySQL 资源是否符合此策略。该解决方案必须能够随时显示数据 库在策略各个部分上的合规状态。 哪种解决方案能满足这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Enable AWS Audit Manager. Configure Audit Manager to use a custom framework that matches the security requirements. Create an assessment report to view the compliance state.","B":"Enable AWS Config. Implement AWS Config managed rules that monitor all Aurora MySQL resources for the security requirements. View the compliance state in the AWS Config dashboard.","C":"Enable AWS Security Hub. Create a configuration policy that includes the security requirements. Apply the configuration policy to all Aurora MySQL resources. View the compliance state in Security Hub.","D":"Create an Amazon EventBridge rule that runs when an Aurora MySQL resource is created or modified. Create an AWS Lambda function to verify the security requirements and to send the compliance state to a CloudWatch custom metric."},"options_zh":{"A":"启用 AWS 审计管理器。配置审计管理器使用符合安全要求的自定义框架。创建评估报告以查看合规状态。","B":"启用 AWS Config。实施 AWS Config 管理规则，以监控所有 Aurora MySQL 资源是否符合安全要求，并在 AWS Config 控制台中查看合规状态。","C":"启用 AWS Security Hub。创建包含安全要求的配置策略，并将其应用于所有 Aurora MySQL 资源。在 Security Hub 中查 看合规状态。","D":"创建一个 Amazon EventBridge 规则，当 Aurora MySQL 资源被创建或修改时触发该规则。创建一个 AWS Lambda 函数， 用于验证安全要求，并将合规状态发送到 CloudWatch 自定义指标。"},"answer":["B"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Organizations/Governance","Security/IAM","Compute","Database","Serverless/Integration","Monitoring/Ops"],"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選","research":{"verdict":["B"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"both","explanation_en":"AWS Config is purpose-built for exactly this requirement: continuous, resource-level configuration compliance monitoring with a persistent, queryable compliance state per rule and per resource, viewable at any time in the AWS Config dashboard. Critically, AWS Config already ships managed rules that map one-to-one onto every clause of this security policy: rds-storage-encrypted (storage encrypted at rest), rds-cluster-deletion-protection-enabled / rds-instance-deletion-protection-enabled (deletion protection), rds-instance-public-access-check (not publicly accessible), and rds-logging-enabled (which accepts an 'additionalLogs' parameter, e.g. 'aurora: audit, error, general, slowquery', to verify Aurora audit logs are being published). Once these managed rules are enabled and scoped to AWS::RDS::DBInstance/DBCluster resources, AWS Config evaluates every Aurora MySQL resource on every configuration change (and on a periodic schedule) and continuously exposes a COMPLIANT/NON_COMPLIANT state per rule per resource in the Config console — satisfying both 'continuously monitors' and 'display compliance state for each part of the policy at any time' with zero custom code. Option A (Audit Manager) is designed for audit-evidence collection and generating point-in-time assessment reports for auditors, not for continuous per-resource compliance display. Option C describes Security Hub 'configuration policies,' which in AWS's actual central-configuration feature exist to turn on/off existing Security Hub standards and controls across an organization — they are not a mechanism for encoding a bespoke, arbitrary security policy like this one. Option D reinvents functionality (EventBridge + Lambda + custom CloudWatch metric) that AWS Config managed rules already provide out of the box, adding unnecessary custom code and operational overhead. Therefore B is correct, matching the dump's suggested answer.","explanation_zh":"AWS Config 正是為此需求而生:它針對資源設定持續進行合規監控,為每條規則、每個資源維護一個可隨時查詢的合規狀態,並可在 AWS Config 主控台隨時檢視。關鍵在於,AWS Config 已提供與此安全政策每一條要求一一對應的受管規則:rds-storage-encrypted(儲存體靜態加密)、rds-cluster-deletion-protection-enabled / rds-instance-deletion-protection-enabled(刪除保護)、rds-instance-public-access-check(不可公開存取)、以及 rds-logging-enabled(可透過 additionalLogs 參數,例如 'aurora: audit, error, general, slowquery',驗證 Aurora 稽核日誌是否已發佈)。只要啟用這些受管規則並將範圍設定於 AWS::RDS::DBInstance/DBCluster 資源,AWS Config 便會在每次設定變更時(以及定期排程)評估每個 Aurora MySQL 資源,並在 Config 主控台中持續顯示每條規則、每個資源的 COMPLIANT/NON_COMPLIANT 狀態——完全不需自訂程式碼即可同時滿足「持續監控」與「隨時顯示政策各部分合規狀態」兩項需求。選項 A(Audit Manager)是為蒐集稽核證據、產出供稽核人員使用的時間點評估報告而設計,並非用於持續的逐資源合規顯示。選項 C 所描述的 Security Hub「配置政策」,在 AWS 實際的集中設定功能中,是用來在整個組織中開關既有的 Security Hub 標準與控制項——並非用來編碼像本題這種客製化、任意的安全政策的機制。選項 D 則是重新發明 AWS Config 受管規則已經原生提供的功能(EventBridge + Lambda + 自訂 CloudWatch 指標),徒增不必要的自訂程式碼與維運負擔。因此答案為 B,與題庫建議答案相符。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"AWS Audit Manager is designed to continuously collect evidence and generate assessment reports mapped to a framework for audit purposes, but it is not built to give a real-time, per-resource, per-control compliance dashboard that can be checked 'at any time' the way AWS Config's compliance dashboard does; it is oriented toward periodic audit reporting, not live continuous resource monitoring.","why_zh":"AWS Audit Manager 設計目的是持續蒐集證據並產出對應框架的評估報告以供稽核使用,但並非設計用來提供像 AWS Config 合規儀表板那樣可『隨時』查詢的即時逐資源、逐控制項合規狀態;它偏向定期稽核報告,而非即時持續的資源監控。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"Security Hub 'configuration policies' (central configuration) are a mechanism for enabling/disabling existing Security Hub standards (e.g., AWS FSBP, CIS, PCI DSS) and their built-in controls consistently across an AWS Organization — they do not let you define an arbitrary custom security policy like 'deletion protection enabled' or 'audit logs published to CloudWatch Logs' as new controls; the built-in Security Hub controls for RDS do not cover this exact custom checklist item-for-item.","why_zh":"Security Hub 的『配置政策』(central configuration)機制,是用來在整個 AWS Organization 中一致地啟用/停用既有的 Security Hub 標準(如 AWS FSBP、CIS、PCI DSS)及其內建控制項——並不能讓你將任意的自訂安全政策(例如『已啟用刪除保護』或『稽核日誌已發佈至 CloudWatch Logs』)定義為新的控制項;Security Hub 內建的 RDS 控制項並未逐項對應本題這份客製化檢查清單。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"This is a workable but needlessly heavy custom-built solution: it requires writing and maintaining Lambda code to re-implement checks (encryption, deletion protection, public access, logging) that AWS Config managed rules already perform natively, and a custom CloudWatch metric is a weaker, less structured way to expose per-resource/per-requirement compliance state than AWS Config's built-in compliance dashboard, which already shows this out of the box.","why_zh":"此方案雖然可行,但是不必要地笨重的自建方案:需要撰寫並維護 Lambda 程式碼,重新實作 AWS Config 受管規則已原生提供的檢查(加密、刪除保護、公開存取、日誌記錄),而以自訂 CloudWatch 指標呈現逐資源/逐要求的合規狀態,也遠不如 AWS Config 內建合規儀表板來得結構化、開箱即用。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/config/latest/developerguide/rds-storage-encrypted.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/config/latest/developerguide/rds-cluster-deletion-protection-enabled.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/config/latest/developerguide/rds-instance-deletion-protection-enabled.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/config/latest/developerguide/rds-instance-public-access-check.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/config/latest/developerguide/rds-logging-enabled.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/config/latest/developerguide/managed-rules-by-aws-config.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/securityhub/latest/userguide/central-configuration-intro.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/securityhub/latest/userguide/securityhub-settingup.html"]}},{"id":190,"question_en":"A company wants to remove all SSH keys permanently from a specific subset of its Amazon Linux 2 Amazon EC2 instances that are using the same IAM instance profile. However, three individuals who have IAM user accounts will need to access these instances by using an SSH session to perform critical duties. How can a security engineer provide the access to meet these requirements?","question_zh":"一家公司希望永久移除其部分使用相同IAM实例配置文件的Amazon Linux 2 Amazon EC2实例上的所 有SSH密钥。然而，有三名拥有IAM用户账户的人员仍需通过SSH会话访问这些实例，以执行关键任 务。 安全工程师如何提供满足这些要求的访问权限？","options_en":{"A":"Assign an IAM policy to the instance profile to allow the EC2 instances to be managed by AWS Systems Manager. Provide the IAM user accounts with permission to use Systems Manager. Remove the SSH keys from the EC2 instances. Use Systems Manager Inventory to select the EC2 instance and connect.","B":"Assign an IAM policy to the IAM user accounts to provide permission to use AWS Systems Manager Run Command. Remove the SSH keys from the EC2 instances. Use Run Command to open an SSH connection to the EC2 instance.","C":"Assign an IAM policy to the instance profile to allow the EC2 instances to be managed by AWS Systems Manager. Provide the IAM user accounts with permission to use Systems Manager. Remove the SSH keys from the EC2 instances. Use Systems Manager Session Manager to select the EC2 instance and connect.","D":"Assign an IAM policy to the IAM user accounts to provide permission to use the EC2 service in the AWS Management Console. Remove the SSH keys from the EC2 instances. Connect to the EC2 instance as the ec2-user through the AWS Management Console’s EC2 SSH client method."},"options_zh":{"A":"为实例配置文件分配 IAM 策略，以允许 EC2 实例由 AWS Systems Manager 进行管理。授予 IAM 用户账户使用 Systems Manager 的权限。从 EC2 实例中移除 SSH 密钥。使用 Systems Manager 清单选择 EC2 实例并建立连接。","B":"为 IAM 用户账户分配 IAM 策略，以授予使用 AWS Systems Manager Run Command 的权限。 从 EC2 实例中移除 SSH 密钥，并使用 Run Command 建立与 EC2 实例的 SSH 连接。","C":"为实例配置文件分配 IAM 策略，以允许 EC2 实例由 AWS Systems Manager 进行管理。授予 IAM 用户账户使用 Systems Manager 的权限。从 EC2 实例中移除 SSH 密钥。使用 Systems Manager Session Manager 选择 EC2 实例并建立连接。","D":"为 IAM 用户账户分配 IAM 策略，以授予其在 AWS 管理控制台中使用 EC2 服务的权限。从 EC2 实例中移除 SSH 密钥。通过 AWS 管理控制台的 EC2 SSH 客户端方式，以 ec2-user 身 份连接到 EC2 实例。"},"answer":["C"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Security/IAM","Compute","Monitoring/Ops"],"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選","research":{"verdict":["C"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"both","explanation_en":"Option C is correct. AWS Systems Manager Session Manager is the AWS-documented capability purpose-built for exactly this scenario: it provides 'browser-based or CLI-based shell access without requiring SSH keys, bastion hosts, or open inbound ports.' The setup described in C matches AWS's own procedure: attach an IAM policy (e.g., the AmazonSSMManagedInstanceCore managed policy) to the EC2 instance profile so the SSM Agent can register the instances as managed nodes, grant the three IAM user accounts IAM permissions to use Systems Manager (ssm:StartSession and related actions), remove the SSH keys, and then have the users select the instance in the Session Manager console/CLI and 'connect' to open an interactive shell session. This satisfies both stated requirements simultaneously: SSH key material is permanently removed from the instances, and the three named IAM principals retain full interactive shell access for their critical duties, with the connection logged/auditable via CloudTrail and optionally Session Manager logging. Option A fails because Systems Manager Inventory is a metadata-collection feature (it catalogs installed applications, network configuration, Windows updates, etc.) — it has no 'connect to a shell' capability at all; you cannot use Inventory to open a session. Option B fails because Run Command is designed to execute one-time commands or scripts across managed nodes (patch, install software, run scripts) — it does not open an interactive SSH/shell session; there is no Run Command feature that 'opens an SSH connection.' Option D fails because there is no native AWS Management Console 'EC2 SSH client method' that works once SSH keys are removed — regular EC2 console access and permissions to use the EC2 service do not, by themselves, provide any mechanism to open a shell into an instance without either an SSH key, EC2 Instance Connect (a separate, unmentioned feature that pushes ephemeral public keys), or Session Manager. Only Session Manager (C) meets the 'permanently remove SSH keys yet retain SSH-like access for specific IAM users' requirement as documented by AWS.","explanation_zh":"正確答案為 C。AWS Systems Manager Session Manager 是 AWS 官方文件明確記載、專為此情境設計的功能:它提供「透過瀏覽器或 CLI 的 shell 存取,不需要 SSH 金鑰、堡壘主機或開放的輸入埠」。選項 C 描述的設定完全符合 AWS 官方流程:在 EC2 執行個體設定檔上附加 IAM 政策(例如 AmazonSSMManagedInstanceCore 受管政策),讓 SSM Agent 能將執行個體註冊為受管節點;授予三個 IAM 使用者帳戶使用 Systems Manager 的 IAM 權限(ssm:StartSession 等動作);移除 SSH 金鑰;接著讓使用者在 Session Manager 主控台/CLI 中選取執行個體並「連線」以開啟互動式 shell 工作階段。這同時滿足兩項需求:SSH 金鑰材料已從執行個體永久移除,而三位指定的 IAM 主體仍保有完整的互動式 shell 存取權以執行其關鍵職責,且連線可透過 CloudTrail 記錄與稽核(並可選擇啟用 Session Manager 記錄)。選項 A 錯誤,因為 Systems Manager Inventory 是中繼資料蒐集功能(用於編目已安裝的應用程式、網路組態、Windows 更新等)——它完全沒有「連線至 shell」的能力,無法用 Inventory 開啟工作階段。選項 B 錯誤,因為 Run Command 是設計用來在受管節點上執行一次性命令或指令碼(修補、安裝軟體、執行指令碼)——它不會開啟互動式 SSH/shell 工作階段;Run Command 並沒有「開啟 SSH 連線」這項功能。選項 D 錯誤,因為在移除 SSH 金鑰後,並不存在原生的 AWS Management Console「EC2 SSH 用戶端方法」可運作——單純具備使用 EC2 服務的主控台存取權限,本身並不提供任何在沒有 SSH 金鑰、EC2 Instance Connect(另一項未被提及、會推送臨時公開金鑰的獨立功能)或 Session Manager 的情況下開啟執行個體 shell 的機制。只有 Session Manager(C)符合 AWS 文件所述「永久移除 SSH 金鑰,同時保留特定 IAM 使用者類 SSH 存取權」的需求。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"Systems Manager Inventory is a metadata-collection feature that catalogs installed applications, network configurations, Windows updates, and other instance metadata for visibility and compliance purposes. It has no session/connect capability whatsoever — you cannot 'select the EC2 instance and connect' from Inventory. The option conflates Inventory with Session Manager's actual connect functionality.","why_zh":"Systems Manager Inventory 是中繼資料蒐集功能,用於編目已安裝的應用程式、網路組態、Windows 更新等執行個體中繼資料,以利可視性與合規性。它完全沒有工作階段/連線能力——無法從 Inventory「選取 EC2 執行個體並連線」。此選項將 Inventory 與 Session Manager 實際的連線功能混淆。"},{"letter":"B","why_en":"AWS Systems Manager Run Command is designed for executing one-time commands or scripts across managed nodes at scale (patching, installing software, running scripts) — per AWS documentation it 'allows you to automate common administrative tasks.' It does not provide an interactive SSH/shell session; there is no documented Run Command feature that 'opens an SSH connection to the EC2 instance.' Interactive shell access is Session Manager's role, not Run Command's.","why_zh":"AWS Systems Manager Run Command 是設計用來大規模地在受管節點上執行一次性命令或指令碼(修補、安裝軟體、執行指令碼)——依 AWS 文件所述,它「讓您能夠自動化常見的管理任務」。它並不提供互動式 SSH/shell 工作階段;沒有任何文件記載 Run Command 具備「開啟 SSH 連線至 EC2 執行個體」的功能。互動式 shell 存取是 Session Manager 的職責,而非 Run Command。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"There is no native AWS Management Console 'EC2 SSH client method' that functions once SSH keys are removed from the instance. Ordinary EC2 console permissions do not grant any mechanism to open a shell without an SSH key — that would require either EC2 Instance Connect (a separate, unmentioned feature involving ephemeral public key push) or Session Manager. As worded, D describes a non-existent capability once the SSH keys are gone.","why_zh":"在執行個體的 SSH 金鑰被移除後,並不存在可運作的原生 AWS Management Console「EC2 SSH 用戶端方法」。一般的 EC2 主控台權限並不提供任何在沒有 SSH 金鑰的情況下開啟 shell 的機制——那需要 EC2 Instance Connect(另一項未被提及、涉及推送臨時公開金鑰的獨立功能)或 Session Manager。就選項 D 的敘述而言,一旦 SSH 金鑰移除,它所描述的是一項不存在的能力。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/systems-manager/latest/userguide/session-manager.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AWSEC2/latest/UserGuide/connect-with-systems-manager-session-manager.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/systems-manager/latest/userguide/session-manager-getting-started-enable-ssh-connections.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/systems-manager/latest/userguide/run-command.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/systems-manager/latest/userguide/sysman-inventory.html"]}},{"id":191,"question_en":"A company must inventory sensitive data across all Amazon S3 buckets in all accounts from a single security account.","question_zh":"一家公司必须从一个安全账户中，对所有账户中的所有Amazon S3存储桶内的敏感数据进行盘点。","options_en":{"A":"Delegate Amazon Macie and Security Hub administration.","B":"Use Amazon Inspector with Security Hub.","C":"Use Inspector with Trusted Advisor.","D":"Use Macie with Trusted Advisor."},"options_zh":{"A":"委托管理 Amazon Macie 和 Security Hub。","B":"使用 Amazon Inspector 与 Security Hub。","C":"使用 Inspector 配合 Trusted Advisor。","D":"使用 Macie 与可信顾问配合。"},"answer":["A"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Security/IAM","Storage"],"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選","research":{"verdict":["A"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"Amazon Macie is the AWS service purpose-built to discover and inventory sensitive data (PII, credentials, financial data, etc.) in Amazon S3 buckets; its console/API exposes an 'S3 buckets' inventory view with sensitivity scores. To do this across every account in an AWS Organization from one central security account, you designate that account as the delegated Macie administrator, which lets it enable Macie for member accounts and view aggregated S3 bucket inventory and sensitive-data findings for the whole organization. Pairing this with a delegated Security Hub administrator lets the same central account also aggregate the Macie findings (and other security findings) across accounts into one dashboard, which is the standard AWS multi-account security-tooling pattern. Amazon Inspector, by contrast, does vulnerability/CVE scanning of EC2 instances, Lambda functions, and ECR container images — it has no capability to classify or inventory sensitive data inside S3 objects, so any option built on Inspector (B, C) is the wrong service for this requirement. AWS Trusted Advisor provides cost/performance/security/fault-tolerance best-practice checks (e.g., flags publicly-readable S3 buckets) but does not scan object content for sensitive data and has no organization-wide delegated-administrator inventory capability, so pairing Macie with Trusted Advisor (D) does not satisfy 'inventory sensitive data ... from a single security account' either. Therefore A is the only option that uses the correct service (Macie) with the correct multi-account delegation mechanism.","explanation_zh":"Amazon Macie 是專門用來探索並盤點 Amazon S3 儲存貯體中敏感資料（PII、憑證、財務資料等）的服務，其主控台/API 提供帶有敏感度分數的「S3 buckets」庫存檢視。若要從單一安全帳戶對整個 AWS Organizations 中所有帳戶執行此盤點，需將該帳戶指定為 Macie 委派管理員帳戶，使其能為成員帳戶啟用 Macie，並檢視整個組織彙總後的 S3 儲存貯體庫存與敏感資料探索結果。再搭配委派 Security Hub 管理員帳戶，同一個中央帳戶就能將 Macie 的發現（以及其他安全發現）彙整到單一儀表板，這正是 AWS 多帳戶安全工具的標準作法。相對地，Amazon Inspector 是對 EC2 執行個體、Lambda 函式與 ECR 容器映像進行弱點／CVE 掃描，完全沒有能力對 S3 物件內容做敏感資料分類或盤點，因此任何以 Inspector 為基礎的選項（B、C）都用錯了服務。AWS Trusted Advisor 提供成本／效能／安全／容錯最佳實務檢查（例如標記公開可讀的 S3 儲存貯體），但不會掃描物件內容找敏感資料，也沒有跨組織的委派管理員式庫存能力，因此 Macie 搭配 Trusted Advisor（D）同樣無法滿足「從單一安全帳戶盤點敏感資料」的需求。因此 A 是唯一使用正確服務（Macie）並搭配正確多帳戶委派機制的選項。","distractors":[{"letter":"B","why_en":"Amazon Inspector performs vulnerability/CVE scanning for EC2, ECR container images, and Lambda functions — it has no ability to discover or inventory sensitive data inside S3 objects, so it cannot fulfill the requirement regardless of Security Hub integration.","why_zh":"Amazon Inspector 是對 EC2、ECR 容器映像與 Lambda 函式做弱點／CVE 掃描，完全無法探索或盤點 S3 物件內的敏感資料，因此無論是否搭配 Security Hub 都無法滿足需求。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"Same core flaw as B (Inspector cannot inspect S3 object content for sensitive data), and Trusted Advisor also does not provide sensitive-data discovery or an org-wide delegated inventory mechanism.","why_zh":"與 B 相同的核心缺陷（Inspector 無法檢查 S3 物件內容中的敏感資料），且 Trusted Advisor 同樣不提供敏感資料探索或跨組織委派式庫存機制。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"Macie is the right service, but Trusted Advisor only flags S3 bucket-level misconfigurations (e.g., public access) via best-practice checks — it does not analyze object content for sensitive data and has no delegated-administrator model to centralize this across every account in an organization from one security account.","why_zh":"Macie 是正確的服務，但 Trusted Advisor 只是透過最佳實務檢查標記 S3 儲存貯體層級的錯誤設定（例如公開存取），並不會分析物件內容中的敏感資料，也沒有委派管理員模型可讓單一安全帳戶集中管理整個組織。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/macie/latest/user/accounts-mgmt-ao-integrate.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/macie/latest/user/macie-accounts.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/macie/latest/user/discovery-asdd-account-manage.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/macie/latest/user/accounts-mgmt-ao-administer.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/securityhub/latest/userguide/designate-orgs-admin-account.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/inspector/latest/user/what-is-inspector.html"]}},{"id":192,"question_en":"A company is running a new workload across accounts that are in an organization in AWS Organizations. All running resources must have a tag ofCostCenter, and the tag must have one of three approved values. The company must enforce this policy and must prevent any changes of the CostCenter tag to a non-approved value. Which solution will meet these requirements?","question_zh":"一家公司正在 AWS Organizations 中的组织内跨多个账户运行一项新的工作负载。所有正在运行的资源都必须包含名为 CostCenter 的标签，且该标签的值必须为三个批准值之一。公司必须强制执行此策略，并防止将 CostCenter 标签更改为未经批准的值。 哪种解决方案能满足这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Create an AWS Config Custom Policy rule by using AWS CloudFormation Guard. Include the tag key of CostCenter and the approved values. Create an SCP that denies the creation of resources when the value of the aws:RequestTag/CostCenter condition key is not one of the three approved values.","B":"Create an AWS CloudTrail trail. Create an Amazon EventBridge rule that includes a rule statement that matches the creation of new resources. Configure the EventBridge rule to invoke an AWS Lambda function that checks for the CostCenter tag. Program the Lambda function to block creation in case of a noncompliant value.","C":"Enable tag policies for the organization. Create a tag policy that specifies a tag key of CostCenter and the approved values. Configure the policy to enforce noncompliant operations. Create an SCP that denies the creation of resources when the aws:RequestTag/CostCenter condition key has a null value.","D":"Enable tag policies for the organization. Create a tag policy that specifies a tag key of CostCenter and the approved values. Create an Amazon EventBridge rule that invokes an AWS Lambda function when a noncompliant tag is created. Program the Lambda function to block changes to the tag."},"options_zh":{"A":"使用 AWS CloudFormation Guard 创建一个 AWS Config 自定义策略规则，包含 CostCenter 标签键及其批准的取值。创建一 个服务控制策略（SCP），当 aws:RequestTag/CostCenter 条件键的值不是三个批准值之一时，拒绝资源的创建。","B":"创建一个 AWS CloudTrail 跟踪。创建一个 Amazon EventBridge 规则，其中包含匹配新资源创建的规则语句。配置该 EventBridge 规则以调用一个 AWS Lambda 函数，用于检查 CostCenter 标签。编程 Lambda 函数，当标签值不符合要求时， 阻止资源创建。","C":"为组织启用标签策略。创建一个标签策略，指定标签键 CostCenter 及其允许的值，并配置该策略以强制执行合规操作。创 建一个服务控制策略（SCP），当 aws:RequestTag/CostCenter 条件键的值为空时，拒绝创建资源。","D":"为组织启用标签策略。创建一个标签策略，指定标签键为 CostCenter 并定义允许的值。创建一个 Amazon EventBridge 规则， 当创建不符合要求的标签时触发 AWS Lambda 函数。编程该 Lambda 函数以阻止对标签的修改。"},"answer":["A"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Organizations/Governance","Compute","Serverless/Integration","Monitoring/Ops"],"difficulty":2,"diff_why":"題庫與社群皆錯","research":{"verdict":["C"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"neither","explanation_en":"The requirement has two distinct parts that no single AWS mechanism covers alone: (1) every resource must HAVE a CostCenter tag, and (2) the tag's value must be one of three approved values, with changes to non-approved values blocked. AWS's own tag-policies documentation states this split explicitly: 'Basic compliance rules do not enforce tag compliance on resources that are created without tags. This capability does not enforce missing tag keys... Use SCPs to prevent IAM users and roles in target accounts from creating certain resource types if the request doesn't include the specified tags' (orgs_manage_policies_tag-policies-enforcement.html). In other words, tag policies with 'Prevent noncompliant operations for this tag' (the enforced_for field) are the AWS-native, documented preventive control for value compliance — they block CreateTags/TagResource/resource-creation calls whose CostCenter value isn't in the approved list, for supported services — but they never catch a resource created with no CostCenter tag at all, because there's nothing to evaluate. To close that presence gap, AWS explicitly recommends an SCP using the Null condition operator against aws:RequestTag/CostCenter (deny when null/true, i.e., the tag key is absent from the request) — this is the standard, documented IAM/SCP pattern for mandating a tag key at resource-creation time (docs.aws.amazon.com/IAM/latest/UserGuide/access_tags.html; orgs_manage_policies_tag-policies-best-practices.html, 'Consider creating an SCP to set guardrails around resource creation requests'). Option C combines exactly these two documented, complementary preventive controls: a tag policy enforcing the three approved CostCenter values, plus an SCP denying creation when CostCenter is null (missing). Option A substitutes an AWS Config custom Guard rule for the tag-policy half, but AWS Config is a detective/evaluation service that assesses resource configuration after a resource exists (or on a scheduled/change-triggered basis) — it cannot itself block an API call in real time, so it cannot 'prevent' creation the way the question demands; the SCP in A also only checks for a StringNotEquals mismatch on value and never enforces that the tag exists at all (a request lacking aws:RequestTag/CostCenter simply never matches that condition), so A leaves the missing-tag case completely uncovered. Options B and D are both reactive, event-driven (CloudTrail/EventBridge + Lambda) architectures that act only after the tagging API call has already succeeded and been logged — by design they cannot prevent the noncompliant state from ever existing, they can only detect and remediate afterward, which fails 'must prevent' as stated in the requirement. Therefore C is the only option built entirely from documented, genuinely preventive AWS controls that together cover both the required-tag-key gap and the approved-value gap.","explanation_zh":"此需求包含兩個各自獨立、沒有單一 AWS 機制可同時涵蓋的部分:(1) 每個資源都必須「擁有」CostCenter 標籤;(2) 標籤值必須是三個核准值之一,且不允許改成不核准的值。AWS 官方 tag policies 文件明確指出這種區分:「Basic compliance rules 不會對建立時未加標籤的資源強制執行合規性。此功能不會強制要求缺少的標籤金鑰……請使用 SCP 來防止目標帳戶中的 IAM 使用者與角色在請求未包含指定標籤時建立特定資源類型」(orgs_manage_policies_tag-policies-enforcement.html)。換言之,啟用「Prevent noncompliant operations for this tag」(即 enforced_for 欄位)的 tag policies,是 AWS 原生、有文件記載、用於「值合規性」的預防性控制——它會針對支援的服務,阻擋 CostCenter 值不在核准清單內的 CreateTags/TagResource/資源建立呼叫——但它永遠無法攔截「完全沒有加上 CostCenter 標籤」的資源建立,因為根本沒有值可供評估。為了補上這個「是否存在標籤」的缺口,AWS 明確建議使用 SCP 搭配 Null 條件運算子,針對 aws:RequestTag/CostCenter(當該值為 null/true,亦即請求中完全缺少該標籤金鑰時予以拒絕)——這是標準且有文件記載的 IAM/SCP 模式,用於在資源建立當下強制要求某個標籤金鑰必須存在(docs.aws.amazon.com/IAM/latest/UserGuide/access_tags.html;orgs_manage_policies_tag-policies-best-practices.html 中的「Consider creating an SCP to set guardrails around resource creation requests」)。選項 C 正好結合了這兩項有文件依據、互補的預防性控制:一個強制執行三個核准 CostCenter 值的 tag policy,加上一個在 CostCenter 缺失(null)時拒絕建立的 SCP。選項 A 用 AWS Config 自訂 Guard 規則取代 tag policy 的那一半,但 AWS Config 是偵測性/評估性服務,是在資源已存在之後(或依排程/變更觸發)才評估其組態——它本身無法即時阻擋 API 呼叫,因此無法如題目要求般「防止」資源被建立;A 中的 SCP 也僅檢查 StringNotEquals 的值不符情形,完全沒有強制標籤必須存在(缺少 aws:RequestTag/CostCenter 的請求根本不會符合該條件),因此 A 完全沒有涵蓋「缺少標籤」這個情境。選項 B 與 D 皆為反應式、事件驅動(CloudTrail/EventBridge + Lambda)架構,只會在標籤 API 呼叫已經成功執行並被記錄之後才採取行動——依其設計,它們無法防止不合規狀態一開始就發生,只能事後偵測與補救,這無法滿足題目所述的「必須防止」要求。因此,C 是唯一完全由有文件記載、真正具預防性的 AWS 控制所組成、且同時涵蓋「必須有標籤」與「值須核准」兩個缺口的選項。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"AWS Config (even a Custom Policy rule authored with CloudFormation Guard) is a detective/evaluation control that assesses resource configuration after the fact or on a change/periodic trigger — it cannot itself block an API call in real time, so pairing it with an SCP does not add real preventive value for values and leaves the SCP alone to do the work, but that SCP only tests StringNotEquals on aws:RequestTag/CostCenter and never fires when the tag is absent entirely (a missing condition key simply doesn't match), so the 'must have a CostCenter tag' presence requirement is left completely unenforced.","why_zh":"AWS Config(即使是以 CloudFormation Guard 撰寫的 Custom Policy rule)屬於偵測性/評估性控制,是在資源建立之後或依變更/排程觸發才進行評估——它本身無法即時阻擋 API 呼叫,因此搭配 SCP 並不會為「值的合規性」帶來額外的預防效果,實際上仍只能靠該 SCP 單獨運作;但該 SCP 僅檢查 aws:RequestTag/CostCenter 是否 StringNotEquals,當標籤完全缺失時根本不會觸發(缺少的條件金鑰本就不會匹配),因此「必須有 CostCenter 標籤」這項存在性要求完全沒有被強制執行。"},{"letter":"B","why_en":"CloudTrail + EventBridge + Lambda is a reactive, after-the-fact pattern: the resource (and its noncompliant tag) already exists and has been logged by the time the Lambda function runs, so at best it can remediate (e.g., delete the resource or fix the tag) — it cannot 'prevent' creation as CloudTrail only records API calls that have already completed, and there is no supported way for an EventBridge-triggered Lambda to synchronously block an in-flight CreateTags/RunInstances call.","why_zh":"CloudTrail + EventBridge + Lambda 屬於事後反應式模式:當 Lambda 函式執行時,該資源(與其不合規標籤)早已建立並被記錄下來,因此頂多只能做事後補救(例如刪除資源或修正標籤)——它無法「防止」建立行為,因為 CloudTrail 只會記錄已經完成的 API 呼叫,也沒有受支援的方式能讓 EventBridge 觸發的 Lambda 同步攔截一個正在進行中的 CreateTags/RunInstances 呼叫。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"Same reactive flaw as B: tag policies here only report/flag noncompliance (no enforced_for/'Prevent noncompliant operations' is mentioned), and the EventBridge rule fires only after a noncompliant tag has already been created/changed, so the Lambda function is 'blocking' something that has already happened — it can at best revert or remediate, not prevent, failing the question's explicit 'must prevent' requirement.","why_zh":"與 B 有相同的反應式缺陷:此處的 tag policy 只做回報/標記不合規(並未提及 enforced_for 或『Prevent noncompliant operations』的設定),且 EventBridge 規則是在不合規標籤已經被建立/變更之後才觸發,因此 Lambda 函式所『阻擋』的其實是已經發生過的事——它頂多只能還原或補救,而無法防止,不符合題目明確要求的『必須防止』。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/organizations/latest/userguide/orgs_manage_policies_tag-policies-enforcement.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/organizations/latest/userguide/orgs_manage_policies_tag-policies-best-practices.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/organizations/latest/userguide/orgs_manage_policies_example-tag-policies.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/IAM/latest/UserGuide/access_tags.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/organizations/latest/userguide/orgs_manage_policies_tag-policies-getting-started.html"]}},{"id":193,"question_en":"An application is running on an Amazon EC2 instance that has an IAM role attached. The IAM role provides access to an AWS Key Management Service (AWS KMS) customer managed key and an Amazon S3 bucket. The key is used to access 2 TB of sensitive data that is stored in the S3 bucket. A security engineer discovers a potential vulnerability on the EC2 instance that could result in the compromise of the sensitive data. Due to other critical operations, the security engineer cannot immediately shut down the EC2 instance for vulnerability patching. What is the FASTEST way to prevent the sensitive data from being exposed?","question_zh":"一个应用程序正在运行于一台附加了 IAM 角色的 Amazon EC2 实例上。该 IAM 角色提供了对 AWS 密钥管理服务（AWS KMS）客户托管密钥以及一个 Amazon S3 存储桶的访问权限。该密钥用于访问存储在 S3 存储桶中的 2 TB 敏感数据。安全工 程师发现 EC2 实例上存在一个潜在漏洞，可能导致敏感数据泄露。但由于其他关键操作正在进行，安全工程师无法立即关闭 该 EC2 实例以进行漏洞修补。 防止敏感数据泄露的最快方法是什么？","options_en":{"A":"Download the data from the existing S3 bucket to a new EC2 instance. Then delete the data from the S3 bucket. Re-encrypt the data with a client-based key. Upload the data to a new S3 bucket.","B":"Block access to the public range of S3 endpoint IP addresses by using a host-based firewall. Ensure that internet-bound traffic from the affected EC2 instance is routed through the host-based firewall.","C":"Revoke the IAM role’s active session permissions. Update the S3 bucket policy to deny access to the IAM role. Remove the IAM role from the EC2 instance profile.","D":"Disable the current key. Create a new KMS key that the IAM role does not have access to, and re- encrypt all the data with the new key. Schedule the compromised key for deletion."},"options_zh":{"A":"从现有的 S3 存储桶下载数据到新的 EC2 实例，然后删除 S3 存储桶中的数据。使用客户端密钥重新加密数据，并将数据 上传至新的 S3 存储桶。","B":"使用基于主机的防火墙阻止对S3端点IP地址公共范围的访问。确保受影响的EC2实例发出的互联网流量通过该基于主机的 防火墙进行路由。","C":"撤销 IAM 角色的活动会话权限。更新 S3 存储桶策略，拒绝该 IAM 角色的访问权限。将 IAM 角色从 EC2 实例配置文 件中移除。","D":"禁用当前密钥。创建一个 IAM 角色无法访问的新 KMS 密钥，并使用新密钥重新加密所有数据。安排删除已泄露 的密钥。"},"answer":["C"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Security/IAM","Storage","Compute"],"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選","research":{"verdict":["C"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"both","explanation_en":"AWS IAM provides a documented, near-instant mechanism for exactly this scenario: revoking an IAM role's active session permissions. When you choose 'Revoke active sessions' on a role, IAM attaches an AWSRevokeOlderSessions inline deny-all policy scoped by aws:TokenIssueTime, which immediately invalidates every temporary credential issued to that role before that moment — even ones already cached/exfiltrated from the EC2 instance metadata service — without needing to know which sessions exist or waiting for natural expiry. Combining that with denying the role in the S3 bucket policy (defense in depth, since bucket policies are evaluated on every request) and detaching the role from the instance profile (stops the instance from minting new credentials) fully cuts off access to the sensitive data in seconds, with zero data movement. This is dramatically faster than options that require processing the entire 2 TB dataset: re-encrypting or moving 2 TB (options A and D) takes substantial time proportional to object count/size, and disabling/deleting the KMS key (D) doesn't even revoke credentials the attacker may already hold from IMDS, nor does it stop S3 access via a different key path. Option B (host-based firewall blocking S3 IP ranges) is unreliable because a compromised instance's own firewall/OS cannot be trusted to enforce the block, S3 also has non-public VPC-endpoint paths, and it does nothing to invalidate credentials that could be used from outside the instance. Only option C directly and immediately severs the compromised principal's access at the IAM/S3 policy layer, which is the fastest and most robust containment step.","explanation_zh":"AWS IAM 針對此情境提供了官方記載、幾乎即時生效的機制：撤銷 IAM role 的現行工作階段權限（Revoke active sessions）。對 role 執行此動作後，IAM 會附加一個以 aws:TokenIssueTime 為條件的 AWSRevokeOlderSessions 內嵌 deny-all 政策，立即讓該時間點之前核發給此 role 的所有臨時憑證失效——即使是已經被 EC2 instance metadata service 快取或已外洩的憑證也一併失效，且不需要知道確切有哪些工作階段存在，也不必等待憑證自然過期。再搭配修改 S3 bucket policy 明確拒絕該 IAM role（縱深防禦，因為 bucket policy 在每次請求都會被評估）、以及從 instance profile 移除該 role（阻止該執行個體再核發新憑證），可在數秒內完全切斷對敏感資料的存取，且完全不需搬動任何資料。相較之下，需要處理整整 2TB 資料的做法明顯慢得多：重新加密或搬移 2TB 資料（選項 A、D）所需時間與物件數量/大小成正比；停用並刪除 KMS 金鑰（選項 D）甚至無法撤銷攻擊者可能已經從 IMDS 取得的既有憑證，也無法阻止透過其他金鑰路徑存取 S3。選項 B（以主機防火牆封鎖 S3 IP 範圍）並不可靠，因為已遭入侵的主機，其作業系統/防火牆本身已不可信任、無法保證會確實執行封鎖，且 S3 也存在非公開的 VPC endpoint 路徑，此法也完全無法讓憑證失效、無法阻止憑證被搬到別處使用。只有選項 C 能在 IAM／S3 政策層直接且立即切斷已遭入侵主體的存取權，是最快也最穩健的圍堵措施。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"Downloading, deleting, re-encrypting client-side, and re-uploading 2 TB of data is a lengthy data-movement operation (hours, not seconds) and does nothing to immediately cut off the compromised role's access during that window — it is the opposite of 'fastest'.","why_zh":"下載、刪除、以用戶端金鑰重新加密再重新上傳 2TB 資料是耗時的資料搬移作業（要花數小時而非數秒），且在搬移期間完全沒有立即阻斷該遭入侵 role 的存取，與『最快』完全背道而馳。"},{"letter":"B","why_en":"A host-based firewall runs on the potentially compromised instance itself, so an attacker with OS-level access could disable or bypass it; it also does not stop the stolen IAM credentials from being used outside the instance, and S3 traffic may not even traverse the public IP range if VPC endpoints are used.","why_zh":"主機式防火牆是跑在可能已遭入侵的執行個體本身上，攻擊者若已取得作業系統層級的存取權，就能停用或繞過它；此法也無法阻止被竊取的 IAM 憑證在該執行個體之外被使用，且若使用 VPC endpoint，S3 流量甚至不會經過公開 IP 範圍。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"Disabling/scheduling deletion of the KMS key does not revoke any temporary credentials already obtained by the instance (they could still call other permitted actions), and re-encrypting 2 TB of S3 objects with a new CMK requires rewriting every object, which is slow — not the fastest containment step.","why_zh":"停用並排程刪除 KMS 金鑰並不會撤銷該執行個體已經取得的任何臨時憑證（攻擊者仍可能呼叫其他被允許的操作），而以新 CMK 重新加密 2TB 的 S3 物件需要逐一重寫每個物件，速度緩慢，並非最快的圍堵手段。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/IAM/latest/UserGuide/id_roles_use_revoke-sessions.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/IAM/latest/UserGuide/id_credentials_temp_control-access_disable-perms.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/IAM/latest/UserGuide/id_credentials_temp_control-access.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/guardduty/latest/ug/compromised-ec2.html"]}},{"id":194,"question_en":"A company ' s security engineer receives an alert that indicates that an unexpected principal is accessing a company-owned Amazon Simple Queue Service (Amazon SQS) queue. All the company ' s accounts are within an organization in AWS Organizations. The security engineer must implement a mitigation solution that minimizes compliance violations and investment in tools that are outside of AWS. What should the security engineer do to meet these requirements?","question_zh":"一家公司的安全工程师收到一条告警，提示有未预期的主体正在访问公司拥有的 Amazon Simple Queue Service（Amazon SQS）队列。该公司所有账户均位于 AWS Organizations 中的一个组织内。该安全工程师必须实施一项缓解方案，以尽 量减少合规性违规，并降低对 AWS 以外工具的投资。 安全工程师应采取哪些措施来满足这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Create security groups that only accept inbound traffic from the CIDR blocks of all the VPCs in the organization. Attach the security groups to all the SQS queues in all the VPCs in the organization.","B":"In all the VPCs in the organization, adjust the network ACLs to only accept inbound traffic from the CIDR blocks of all the VPCs in the organization. Attach the network ACLs to all the subnets in all the VPCs in the organization.","C":"Create interface VPC endpoints for Amazon SQS in all the VPCs in the organization. Set the aws: SourceVpce condition to the VPC endpoint identifier on the SQS policy. Add the aws:PrincipalOrgId condition to the VPC endpoint policy.","D":"Use a cloud access security broker (CASB) to maintain a list of managed resources. Configure the CASB to check the API and console access against that list on a web proxy."},"options_zh":{"A":"创建仅允许来自组织内所有VPC的CIDR块的入站流量的安全组，并将这些安全组附加到组织内所有VPC中的所 有SQS队列。","B":"在组织内的所有VPC中，调整网络ACL，使其仅接受来自组织内所有VPC的CIDR地址块的入站流量，并将这些网络 ACL关联到组织内所有VPC中的所有子网。","C":"在组织内的所有 VPC 中为 Amazon SQS 创建接口型 VPC 终端节点。在 SQS 策略中将 aws:SourceVpce 条件设置为 VPC 终端节点标识符，并在 VPC 终端节点策略中添加 aws:PrincipalOrgId 条件。","D":"使用云访问安全代理（CASB）来维护受管资源列表，并配置CASB在Web代理上检查API和控制台访问是否与 该列表匹配。"},"answer":["C"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Organizations/Governance","Serverless/Integration"],"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選","research":{"verdict":["C"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"both","explanation_en":"C is correct. This scenario is the textbook \"unexpected principal accessed a resource\" trigger for building an AWS-native data perimeter around Amazon SQS, entirely with AWS-managed controls (no third-party investment). The fix layers two perimeters: (1) a network perimeter — deploy interface VPC endpoints for Amazon SQS in every VPC in the organization so traffic to the queue never has to leave AWS's private network, and put an `aws:SourceVpce` condition on the SQS queue's resource-based policy so the queue only accepts requests that arrive through that expected VPC endpoint (or set of endpoint IDs); and (2) an identity perimeter — attach a VPC endpoint policy to the interface endpoint(s) that uses `aws:PrincipalOrgID` to allow only principals that belong to the company's AWS Organization to use the endpoint at all. Both condition keys and this exact resource-policy/endpoint-policy combination are documented by AWS for restricting SQS and other services to expected identities and expected networks (see the SQS custom access-policy examples and the SQS least-privilege guide, which explicitly calls out `aws:PrincipalOrgID` as a global condition key for this purpose, plus the general `aws:SourceVpce`/VPC-endpoint-policy pattern used across services). This directly stops an \"unexpected principal\" — whether from outside the org or from an unapproved network path — from reaching the queue, using nothing but native IAM/VPC-endpoint mechanics, so it satisfies both \"minimize compliance violations\" and \"minimize non-AWS tooling.\" Options A and B fail on a basic technical point: Amazon SQS is a fully managed service with no elastic network interface of its own to attach a security group to, and it is not addressed by subnet-level network ACLs unless all traffic is already forced through VPC endpoints — neither security groups nor NACLs can be attached to or meaningfully gate an SQS queue directly, and CIDR-based VPC filtering does nothing to stop a compromised/unexpected IAM principal that is already inside an allowed VPC or reaching SQS over the public endpoint. Option D explicitly requires a CASB, a non-AWS tool, which directly violates the \"minimizes investment in tools that are outside of AWS\" requirement, so it is disqualified regardless of technical merit. The dump's suggested answer C is confirmed as genuinely correct.","explanation_zh":"正確答案是 C。這個情境是典型的「非預期主體存取到資源」觸發情境,解法是完全用 AWS 原生控制項在 Amazon SQS 周圍建立資料邊界(data perimeter),不需要投資任何第三方工具。此解法疊加兩層邊界:(1) 網路邊界——在組織中所有 VPC 建立 Amazon SQS 的 interface VPC endpoint,讓前往佇列的流量不必離開 AWS 私有網路,並在 SQS 佇列的資源型政策(queue policy)上設定 `aws:SourceVpce` 條件,使佇列只接受經由該預期 VPC endpoint(或一組 endpoint ID)傳入的請求;(2) 身分邊界——在該 interface endpoint 上附加 VPC endpoint policy,使用 `aws:PrincipalOrgID` 條件,只允許屬於公司 AWS Organization 的主體使用該端點。這兩個條件金鑰以及「資源政策 + endpoint 政策」的組合模式,都記載於 AWS 官方文件中,用於將 SQS 及其他服務的存取限制在預期身分與預期網路範圍內(參見 SQS 自訂存取政策範例,以及 SQS 最小權限指南——該指南明確將 `aws:PrincipalOrgID` 列為用於此目的的全域條件金鑰,再加上跨服務通用的 `aws:SourceVpce` / VPC endpoint policy 模式)。這能直接阻擋「非預期主體」——無論是來自組織外部,還是經由未經核准的網路路徑——存取該佇列,且僅使用原生 IAM / VPC endpoint 機制,因此同時滿足「將合規違規降到最低」與「將非 AWS 工具投資降到最低」的需求。選項 A 與 B 在基本技術層面就站不住腳:Amazon SQS 是完全託管服務,本身沒有可供附加安全群組的彈性網路介面,若非強制所有流量都經過 VPC endpoint,子網層級的網路 ACL 也管不到它——安全群組與 NACL 都無法直接附加或有效控管 SQS 佇列,而以 CIDR 為基礎的 VPC 過濾,對於一個已經身處允許的 VPC 內、或透過公開端點存取 SQS 的遭入侵/非預期 IAM 主體,完全無法阻止。選項 D 明確要求使用 CASB(非 AWS 工具),直接違反「將非 AWS 工具投資降到最低」的需求,因此無論技術上是否可行都應被排除。此題 dump 建議答案 C 經確認為真正正確答案。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"Security groups attach to elastic network interfaces (e.g., EC2 instances or interface VPC endpoints); Amazon SQS itself is a fully managed service with no ENI of its own, so you cannot 'attach security groups to SQS queues' as the option describes. Even if applied to the endpoint ENIs, VPC-CIDR-based security groups only filter by source network, not by AWS principal identity, so they cannot stop an unexpected principal that already has network reachability (e.g., a compromised role inside an allowed VPC, or any caller via the public SQS endpoint).","why_zh":"安全群組是附加在彈性網路介面上的(例如 EC2 執行個體或 interface VPC endpoint);Amazon SQS 本身是完全託管服務,並沒有自己的 ENI,因此無法像選項所述那樣『將安全群組附加到 SQS 佇列』。即使將其套用在端點的 ENI 上,以 VPC CIDR 為基礎的安全群組也只能依來源網路過濾,無法依 AWS 主體身分過濾,因此無法阻止一個已具備網路可達性的非預期主體(例如允許的 VPC 內遭入侵的角色,或透過公開 SQS 端點呼叫的任何呼叫者)。"},{"letter":"B","why_en":"Network ACLs operate at the subnet boundary and filter by IP/CIDR and port, not by AWS principal identity. Unless all SQS traffic is already forced through VPC endpoints, standard SQS API calls go to a public AWS endpoint that NACLs on the org's own subnets have no control over, so this does nothing to stop an unexpected IAM principal (which may not even be calling from inside the organization's VPCs) from reaching the queue.","why_zh":"網路 ACL 是在子網邊界運作,依 IP/CIDR 與連接埠過濾,並非依 AWS 主體身分過濾。除非所有 SQS 流量已強制經由 VPC endpoint,否則標準 SQS API 呼叫會前往公開的 AWS 端點,組織自有子網上的 NACL 對此毫無控制力,因此無法阻止一個非預期的 IAM 主體(甚至可能根本不是從組織 VPC 內部呼叫)存取該佇列。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"A CASB is a third-party (non-AWS) tool and requires ongoing licensing/operational investment outside the AWS ecosystem, directly contradicting the stated requirement to 'minimize investment in tools that are outside of AWS.' It is disqualified on that requirement alone, independent of whether it could technically detect the access pattern.","why_zh":"CASB 是第三方(非 AWS)工具,需要持續在 AWS 生態系之外投入授權與維運成本,直接牴觸題目明確要求的『將投資在 AWS 以外工具的成本降到最低』。單就這項需求即應被排除,無論它在技術上是否能偵測到該存取模式。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AWSSimpleQueueService/latest/SQSDeveloperGuide/sqs-least-privilege-policy.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AWSSimpleQueueService/latest/SQSDeveloperGuide/sqs-creating-custom-policies-access-policy-examples.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/IAM/latest/UserGuide/access_policies_data-perimeters.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/IAM/latest/UserGuide/reference_policies_condition-keys.html#condition-keys-principalorgid","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/apigateway/latest/developerguide/apigateway-vpc-endpoint-policies.html"]}},{"id":195,"question_en":"A company’s platform has grown rapidly over the past 6 months. The company’s platform architecture evolved quickly to accommodate the growth. The company’s development team has been deploying features quickly by using different AWS services. The development team has not performed formal architecture reviews. The company needs to evaluate its security posture against AWS security best practices. Which solution will meet these requirements?","question_zh":"过去6个月中，该公司的平台迅速发展。为适应增长，平台架构也快速演进。开发团队通过使用不 同的AWS服务快速部署功能，但尚未进行正式的架构评审。 公司需要根据 AWS 安全最佳实践来评估自身的安全状况。 哪种解决方案能满足这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Create a new workload in the AWS Well-Architected Tool. Work with the development team to answer security questions based on the team’s current state. Use the save milestone feature to track improvements against identified high-risk items.","B":"Use the cost recommendations in AWS Cost Explorer. Analyze the cost implications of security misconfigurations. Prioritize architectural changes based on potential cost savings as a result of implementing AWS security best practices.","C":"Enable AWS Security Hub CSPM. Create a Security Hub CSPM automation rule to map existing services to approved architecture patterns. Use the data to identify non-compliance against AWS best practices and generate a compliance report.","D":"Enable Amazon Detective. Create a Detective investigation for AWS security best practices. Use a behavior graph to visualize the data. Analyze the entities to identify architectural components that do not follow AWS security best practices."},"options_zh":{"A":"在 AWS Well-Architected 工具中创建一个新的工作负载。与开发团队合作，根据团队当前状态 回答安全相关问题。使用“保存里程碑”功能来跟踪针对已识别高风险项目的改进情况。","B":"使用 AWS 成本探索器中的成本建议，分析安全配置错误带来的成本影响，并根据实施 AWS 安全最佳实践可能节省的成本，优先推进架构调整。","C":"启用 AWS Security Hub 的云服务管理（CSPM）功能。创建一个 Security Hub CSPM 自动化规 则，将现有服务映射到已批准的架构模式。利用这些数据识别不符合 AWS 最佳实践的情况， 并生成合规性报告。","D":"启用 Amazon Detective。为 AWS 安全最佳实践创建 Detective 调查。使用行为图可视化数据， 并分析实体以识别不符合 AWS 安全最佳实践的架构组件。"},"answer":["A"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Security/IAM","Cost Optimization"],"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選","research":{"verdict":["A"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"A is correct. The scenario describes exactly the use case AWS designed the Well-Architected Tool for: an architecture that evolved rapidly without formal reviews, needing to be evaluated against AWS best practices. Per AWS documentation, the AWS Well-Architected Tool lets you 'document the state of your workloads and compare them to the latest AWS architectural best practices' by answering a set of questions organized by pillar (including the Security pillar), and it produces a plan for architectural improvements by generating high-risk issues (HRIs) and medium-risk issues (MRIs) on a dashboard. The 'save milestone' feature referenced in option A is a real, documented capability: as you make improvements, you record milestones to track your progress addressing identified risks over time (docs.aws.amazon.com/wellarchitected/latest/userguide/getting-started.html and dashboard.html describe HRIs/MRIs; workload review flow is in start-workflow-review.html and continue-workflow-review.html). This directly matches 'work with the development team to answer security questions based on current state' and 'track improvements against identified high-risk items.' Option C is a distractor built on a fabricated capability: real Security Hub CSPM automation rules (docs.aws.amazon.com/securityhub/latest/userguide/automation-rules.html and create-automation-rules.html) automatically update finding severity/status/note fields or create tickets for findings that match criteria — they do not 'map existing services to approved architecture patterns' or perform an architecture review; Security Hub CSPM's real strength is continuous compliance checks against specific frameworks (AWS FSBP, CIS, PCI-DSS, NIST), not a holistic best-practices architecture review of a still-evolving, ad hoc platform. Option B (Cost Explorer) addresses cost optimization, not security posture, and cost is not a reliable proxy for security risk. Option D (Amazon Detective) is a forensic/investigative tool for analyzing already-flagged suspicious activity via a behavior graph built from VPC Flow Logs, CloudTrail, and GuardDuty findings — it has no concept of 'architecture best-practice compliance' and cannot evaluate whether services are configured/architected per AWS best practices. Therefore, the Well-Architected Tool (A) is the only option that both technically performs a best-practices architecture assessment and tracks remediation progress as described.","explanation_zh":"答案為 A。此情境正是 AWS Well-Architected Tool 設計要解決的典型用例:架構在缺乏正式審查的情況下快速演變,現在需要對照 AWS 最佳實踐進行評估。根據 AWS 文件,AWS Well-Architected Tool 讓您「記錄工作負載的現狀,並與最新的 AWS 架構最佳實踐進行比對」,做法是回答依支柱(pillar,包含安全支柱)分類的一組問題,並透過儀表板產生高風險項目(HRI)與中風險項目(MRI),形成架構改善計畫。選項 A 提到的「save milestone」功能是真實存在且有文件記載的能力:當您進行改善時,可記錄里程碑以追蹤處理已識別風險的進度(參見 dashboard.html 說明 HRI/MRI;審查流程見 start-workflow-review.html 與 continue-workflow-review.html)。這與「與開發團隊合作,依現況回答安全問題」及「追蹤針對已識別高風險項目的改善進度」完全吻合。選項 C 則建立在虛構的功能上:真正的 Security Hub CSPM automation rules(見 automation-rules.html 及 create-automation-rules.html)只會自動更新符合條件之發現項目的嚴重性/狀態/備註欄位,或建立工單——並不會「將現有服務對應到核准的架構模式」,也不執行架構審查;Security Hub CSPM 真正的強項是針對特定框架(AWS FSBP、CIS、PCI-DSS、NIST)進行持續合規檢查,而非對一個仍在演變、缺乏規劃的平台做全面性最佳實踐架構審查。選項 B(Cost Explorer)處理的是成本優化而非安全態勢,成本並非安全風險的可靠代理指標。選項 D(Amazon Detective)是鑑識/調查工具,用於透過由 VPC Flow Logs、CloudTrail 與 GuardDuty 發現項目建構的行為圖(behavior graph)來分析已被標記的可疑活動——它沒有「架構最佳實踐合規性」的概念,無法評估服務是否依 AWS 最佳實踐配置或架構設計。因此,Well-Architected Tool(A)是唯一能同時執行最佳實踐架構評估、並如題目所述追蹤修復進度的選項。","distractors":[{"letter":"B","why_en":"AWS Cost Explorer analyzes spend and cost trends, not security configuration or architectural risk. Prioritizing security fixes by 'potential cost savings' is not how AWS best-practice evaluation works, and Cost Explorer has no mechanism to assess compliance with AWS security best practices.","why_zh":"AWS Cost Explorer 分析的是支出與成本趨勢,而非安全設定或架構風險。以「潛在成本節省」來排序安全修復的優先順序,並非 AWS 最佳實踐評估的方式,且 Cost Explorer 沒有任何機制可用來評估是否符合 AWS 安全最佳實踐。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"Security Hub CSPM automation rules are documented to automatically modify finding fields (severity, workflow status, notes) or trigger ticketing integrations when findings match criteria — they do not 'map existing services to approved architecture patterns.' Security Hub's real best-practices evaluation comes from its compliance standards/controls (e.g., AWS Foundational Security Best Practices), not from automation rules, making this option's described mechanism inaccurate.","why_zh":"根據文件,Security Hub CSPM 的 automation rules 是在發現項目符合條件時,自動修改欄位(嚴重性、工作流程狀態、備註)或觸發工單整合——並不會「將現有服務對應到核准的架構模式」。Security Hub 真正的最佳實踐評估來自其合規標準/控制項(例如 AWS Foundational Security Best Practices),而非 automation rules,因此此選項所描述的機制並不正確。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"Amazon Detective builds a behavior graph from VPC Flow Logs, CloudTrail, and GuardDuty findings to help investigate and root-cause already-suspected security incidents. It is not designed to assess whether a platform's overall architecture follows AWS best practices, and it has no 'architecture best practices' investigation type.","why_zh":"Amazon Detective 透過 VPC Flow Logs、CloudTrail 與 GuardDuty 發現項目建構行為圖,協助調查並找出已被懷疑之安全事件的根本原因。它並非設計用來評估平台整體架構是否符合 AWS 最佳實踐,也沒有『架構最佳實踐』這種調查類型。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/wellarchitected/latest/userguide/getting-started.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/wellarchitected/latest/userguide/dashboard.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/wellarchitected/latest/userguide/start-workflow-review.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/wellarchitected/latest/userguide/continue-workflow-review.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/securityhub/latest/userguide/automation-rules.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/securityhub/latest/userguide/create-automation-rules.html"]}},{"id":196,"question_en":"A company is using an organization with all features enabled in AWS Organizations. The organization contains OUs. The company has configured a delegated administrator account for AWS IAM Identity Center. In this delegated administrator account, the company has deployed an AWS CloudFormation stack that contains permission sets. A security engineer must implement a solution to prevent the deletion of the CloudFormation stack. Which solution will meet this requirement?","question_zh":"一家公司正在使用启用了所有功能的 AWS Organizations 组织。该组织包含多个组织单元（OUs）。该公司已为 AWS IAM Identity Center 配置了一个委托管理员账户。在该委托管理员账户中，公司部署了一个包含权限集的 AWS CloudFormation 堆栈。 安全工程师必须实施一项解决方案，以防止删除 CloudFormation 堆栈。 哪种解决方案能满足这一要求？","options_en":{"A":"Enable termination protection for the CloudFormation stack. Create an SCP that denies the cloudformation:UpdateTerminationProtection action for the stack’s ARN. Apply the SCP to the root of the organization.","B":"Enable termination protection for the CloudFormation stack. Create an SCP that denies the cloudformation:DeleteStack action for the stack’s ARN. Apply the SCP to all OUs except the OU that contains the delegated administrator account.","C":"Set the DeletionPolicy attribute to Retain for all resources in the CloudFormation stack. Create an IAM policy that denies the cloudformation:DeleteStack action for the stack’s ARN. Attach the IAM policy to all IAM users and roles in the organization’s management account.","D":"Assign a stack policy to deny updates to stack resources. Create an SCP that denies the cloudformation: UpdateStack action for the stack’s ARN. Apply the SCP to all OUs and the organization’s management account."},"options_zh":{"A":"为 CloudFormation 堆栈启用终止保护。创建一个 SCP，拒绝针对该堆栈 ARN 的 cloudformation: UpdateTerminationProtection 操作，并将该 SCP 应用到组织的根目录。","B":"为 CloudFormation 堆栈启用终止保护。创建一个 SCP，拒绝针对该堆栈 ARN 的 cloudformation:DeleteStack 操作，并 将此 SCP 应用于除包含委派管理员账户的组织单元（OU）之外的所有 OU。","C":"将 CloudFormation 堆栈中所有资源的 DeletionPolicy 属性设置为 Retain。创建一个 IAM 策略，拒绝针对该堆栈 ARN 的 cloudformation:DeleteStack 操作，并将此 IAM 策略附加到组织管理账户中的所有 IAM 用户和角色。","D":"分配一个堆栈策略以拒绝对堆栈资源的更新。创建一个服务控制策略（SCP），拒绝针对该堆栈ARN执行 cloudformation:UpdateStack操作，并将此SCP应用于所有组织单元（OU）以及组织的管理账户。"},"answer":["A"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Organizations/Governance","Security/IAM","Monitoring/Ops"],"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選","research":{"verdict":["A"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"Option A is the only option that both correctly blocks the deletion mechanism and correctly targets the account where the stack actually lives. CloudFormation's own documentation states that termination protection causes any deletion attempt on a protected stack to fail outright, and that changing this setting requires the cloudformation:UpdateTerminationProtection permission. So the two-layer defense is: (1) termination protection stops direct cloudformation:DeleteStack calls, and (2) an SCP denying cloudformation:UpdateTerminationProtection on the stack's ARN stops anyone — including an account administrator — from first disabling that protection and then deleting the stack. This closes the loophole that a plain 'deny DeleteStack' policy alone would not, since IAM/Organizations administrators could otherwise just flip termination protection off before deleting. Crucially, AWS Organizations documentation explicitly confirms: 'SCPs don't affect users or roles in the management account. They affect only the member accounts in your organization. This also means that SCPs apply to member accounts that are designated as delegated administrators.' The IAM Identity Center delegated administrator account is a member account (not the management account), so an SCP attached at the organization root does propagate down and does restrict it — making Option A's placement valid and effective. Option B is a trap: it applies the SCP to 'all OUs except the OU that contains the delegated administrator account,' which explicitly excludes the one account where the stack (and the DeleteStack risk) actually exists, leaving the stack completely unprotected. Option C relies on DeletionPolicy=Retain, which only preserves underlying resources after a stack deletion — it does not stop the stack itself from being deleted — and an IAM policy on the management account's principals does nothing to restrain principals in the delegated administrator (member) account where the stack resides. Option D uses a stack policy (which governs updates to resources, not stack deletion) and an SCP that denies cloudformation:UpdateStack (the wrong action — it doesn't block DeleteStack at all), so the stack could still be deleted outright. Therefore A is the technically correct, fully closed-loop solution.","explanation_zh":"選項 A 是唯一同時正確阻斷刪除機制、又正確鎖定堆疊實際所在帳戶的選項。CloudFormation 官方文件指出,啟用終止保護後,任何對受保護堆疊的刪除嘗試都會直接失敗;而要變更此設定,需要 cloudformation:UpdateTerminationProtection 權限。因此這是雙層防禦:(1) 終止保護阻擋直接的 cloudformation:DeleteStack 呼叫;(2) 一條針對該堆疊 ARN 拒絕 cloudformation:UpdateTerminationProtection 的 SCP,則阻止任何人(包括該帳戶的管理員)先關閉終止保護、再刪除堆疊。這正好補上單純「拒絕 DeleteStack」政策的漏洞——否則 IAM/Organizations 管理員仍可先關閉終止保護再刪除。關鍵是,AWS Organizations 文件明確指出:「SCP 不會影響管理帳戶中的使用者或角色,只會影響組織中的成員帳戶;這也表示 SCP 適用於被指定為委派管理員的成員帳戶。」IAM Identity Center 的委派管理員帳戶本身就是一個成員帳戶(而非管理帳戶),因此附加在組織根層級的 SCP 會往下套用並確實限制該帳戶——這使選項 A 的套用位置是有效且正確的。選項 B 是陷阱:它將 SCP 套用到「除了包含委派管理員帳戶的 OU 以外的所有 OU」,這正好排除了堆疊(以及刪除風險)實際存在的那個帳戶,導致堆疊完全未受保護。選項 C 依賴 DeletionPolicy=Retain,但這只在堆疊被刪除「之後」保留底層資源,並不能阻止堆疊本身被刪除;而將 IAM 政策附加到管理帳戶的主體上,對位於委派管理員(成員)帳戶中、實際持有該堆疊的主體毫無限制作用。選項 D 使用堆疊政策(僅管控資源更新,而非堆疊刪除)以及拒絕 cloudformation:UpdateStack 的 SCP(動作用錯,完全不會阻擋 DeleteStack),因此堆疊仍可被直接刪除。綜上,A 是技術上正確且形成完整防護迴路的解法。","distractors":[{"letter":"B","why_en":"The SCP is applied to 'all OUs except the OU that contains the delegated administrator account' — meaning the one account that actually hosts the CloudFormation stack is explicitly excluded from the deny rule. Principals in the delegated administrator account would therefore still be permitted to call cloudformation:DeleteStack (after disabling termination protection, since nothing blocks UpdateTerminationProtection there either), so the stack remains unprotected. This inverts the intended targeting.","why_zh":"該 SCP 套用於「除了包含委派管理員帳戶的 OU 以外的所有 OU」,也就是說,真正持有該 CloudFormation 堆疊的那個帳戶被明確排除在拒絕規則之外。委派管理員帳戶中的主體因此仍可呼叫 cloudformation:DeleteStack(而且也沒有東西阻擋該帳戶關閉終止保護的 UpdateTerminationProtection),導致堆疊完全未受保護。這正好把目標套用方向弄反了。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"Setting DeletionPolicy to Retain only controls what happens to the underlying resources (e.g., they are kept, not deleted) when a stack deletion succeeds — it does not prevent the stack itself, or the CloudFormation stack resource/entry, from being deleted. Additionally, attaching the IAM deny policy only to principals in the organization's management account does nothing to restrict principals in the delegated administrator (member) account, which is where the stack and the deletion risk actually reside.","why_zh":"將 DeletionPolicy 設為 Retain,只控制堆疊刪除成功後底層資源的處置方式(例如保留而非刪除),並不會阻止堆疊本身被刪除。此外,只把 IAM 拒絕政策附加到組織管理帳戶中的主體,對真正持有堆疊、實際存在刪除風險的委派管理員(成員)帳戶中的主體完全沒有限制作用。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"A stack policy governs which update operations are allowed on stack resources during a stack update — it has no bearing on whether the stack itself can be deleted. The SCP in this option denies cloudformation:UpdateStack, the wrong action entirely for this requirement; it does nothing to block cloudformation:DeleteStack, so the stack can still be deleted outright regardless of the stack policy or this SCP.","why_zh":"堆疊政策(stack policy)管控的是堆疊更新期間允許對哪些資源執行哪些更新操作,與堆疊本身是否能被刪除完全無關。此選項中的 SCP 拒絕的是 cloudformation:UpdateStack,這與本題需求完全用錯動作;它無法阻擋 cloudformation:DeleteStack,因此無論堆疊政策或此 SCP 為何,堆疊仍可被直接刪除。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AWSCloudFormation/latest/UserGuide/using-cfn-protect-stacks.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/organizations/latest/userguide/orgs_manage_policies_scps.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AWSCloudFormation/latest/UserGuide/protect-stack-resources.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/cur/latest/userguide/cur-consolidated-billing.html"]}},{"id":197,"question_en":"A company runs a global ecommerce website using Amazon CloudFront. The company must block traffic from specific countries to comply with data regulations. Which solution will meet these requirements MOST cost-effectively?","question_zh":"一家公司使用 Amazon CloudFront 运营全球电子商务网站，为遵守数据法规，必须屏蔽来自特定国家的流量。 哪种解决方案能以最具成本效益的方式满足这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Use AWS WAF IP match rules.","B":"Use AWS WAF geo match rules.","C":"Use CloudFront geo restriction to deny the countries.","D":"Use geolocation headers in CloudFront."},"options_zh":{"A":"使用 AWS WAF IP 匹配规则。","B":"使用 AWS WAF 地理位置匹配规则。","C":"使用 CloudFront 地理限制来阻止特定国家。","D":"在 CloudFront 中使用地理位置头信息。"},"answer":["C"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Networking/DNS","Security/IAM","Cost Optimization"],"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選","research":{"verdict":["C"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"both","explanation_en":"CloudFront geographic restriction is a built-in, no-additional-charge feature of every CloudFront distribution: on the distribution's Security tab you configure an allow list or block list of countries, and CloudFront (using its own IP-to-country database, ~99.8% accuracy) returns HTTP 403 to blocked requests at the edge before they even reach your origin or AWS WAF. Because this requires no separate service, no Web ACL, and no per-rule/per-request charges, it is the most cost-effective way to satisfy a pure 'block specific countries' requirement across the whole distribution. AWS WAF geo match rules (option B) do the same country-level blocking logically, but AWS WAF is a distinct, separately billed service — you pay a monthly fee per Web ACL, a monthly fee per rule, and a per-million-requests inspection fee — so it is strictly more expensive for this exact use case and is documented as being useful mainly when you need finer-grained combinations (e.g., geo + rate-based rules, geo + label matching for sub-country regions, or restricting only part of a distribution's content) rather than a flat country-level block/allow across an entire distribution. AWS WAF IP match rules (option A) require the company to build and continuously maintain per-country IP CIDR lists, which is both operationally heavier and still incurs AWS WAF's per-Web-ACL/per-rule/per-request charges — clearly not the most cost-effective or accurate option, since IP-to-country mapping changes over time and isn't something WAF IP sets track for you. CloudFront 'geolocation headers' (option D, i.e., the CloudFront-Viewer-Country header) only informs the origin or a CloudFront Function/Lambda@Edge of the viewer's country for routing/personalization decisions — it does not itself block anything, so a functioning block would require the company to write and maintain custom edge code, adding complexity and cost that native geo restriction avoids entirely. This matches the dump's suggested answer and AWS's own guidance that recommends the native CloudFront geographic restrictions feature specifically for whole-distribution, country-level blocking.","explanation_zh":"CloudFront 地理限制（geographic restriction）是每個 CloudFront distribution 內建、不額外收費的功能：只要在 distribution 的 Security 分頁設定國家的 allow list 或 block list，CloudFront 就會用自己的 IP 對應國家資料庫（準確度約 99.8%）在邊緣節點直接對被封鎖的請求回傳 HTTP 403，甚至不會傳到你的來源伺服器或 AWS WAF。因為這完全不需要額外服務、不需要建立 Web ACL、也沒有按規則或按請求計費的費用，對於單純「封鎖特定國家」且套用到整個 distribution 的需求而言，是最具成本效益的做法。AWS WAF geo match 規則（選項 B）在邏輯上能做到相同的國家層級封鎖，但 AWS WAF 是獨立、另外計費的服務——需按 Web ACL 每月計費、按規則每月計費、並依檢查的請求數以百萬次計費——因此就這個確切情境而言必然更昂貴；官方文件也指出 AWS WAF geo match 主要適用於需要更精細組合的情境（例如地理比對加上速率限制規則、地理比對加上 label 比對以鎖定次國家層級的地區，或只想限制 distribution 中部分內容），而非對整個 distribution 做單純的國家層級封鎖/允許。AWS WAF IP match 規則（選項 A）需要公司自行建立並持續維護各國的 IP CIDR 清單，操作負擔更重，而且仍會產生 AWS WAF 的 Web ACL／規則／請求計費——顯然不是最具成本效益也不夠準確的選項，因為 IP 對應國家的關係會隨時間變動，WAF 的 IP set 並不會自動幫你追蹤更新。CloudFront 的「地理位置標頭」（選項 D，即 CloudFront-Viewer-Country header）只是把訪客所在國家的資訊提供給來源伺服器或 CloudFront Function／Lambda@Edge 做路由或個人化決策用——它本身並不會封鎖任何請求，若要真正實現封鎖，公司還得自行撰寫並維護邊緣運算的自訂程式碼，增加了原生地理限制功能完全不需要的複雜度與成本。此結論與題庫建議答案一致，也符合 AWS 官方文件建議：針對整個 distribution 的國家層級封鎖，應使用原生的 CloudFront geographic restrictions 功能。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"AWS WAF IP match rules block by IP address/CIDR, not by country directly — the company would have to source, build, and continually maintain accurate per-country IP range lists themselves (IP-to-country mappings change over time), which is far more operational overhead than a native country dropdown. It also still incurs AWS WAF's Web ACL, rule, and per-request charges, making it more expensive than CloudFront's built-in geo restriction for the same outcome.","why_zh":"AWS WAF 的 IP match 規則是依 IP 位址／CIDR 封鎖，而非直接依國家封鎖——公司得自行取得、建立並持續維護準確的各國 IP 範圍清單（IP 對應國家的關係會隨時間改變），比起原生的國家下拉選單需要更多維運心力。而且仍會產生 AWS WAF 的 Web ACL、規則與按請求計費的費用，對相同目標而言比 CloudFront 內建的地理限制更昂貴。"},{"letter":"B","why_en":"AWS WAF geo match rules can technically block by country, but AWS WAF is a separately billed service (monthly per-Web-ACL fee, per-rule fee, and per-million-requests inspection fee) on top of CloudFront. For a simple whole-distribution country block with no other WAF requirement (e.g., no need to combine with rate limiting or other managed rule groups), this is strictly less cost-effective than the free, native CloudFront geographic restriction feature.","why_zh":"AWS WAF 的 geo match 規則技術上確實能依國家封鎖，但 AWS WAF 是在 CloudFront 之上另外計費的服務（每月 Web ACL 費用、每條規則費用，以及按百萬次請求計費的檢查費用）。若只是單純針對整個 distribution 做國家封鎖、並無其他 WAF 需求（例如不需搭配速率限制或其他受管規則群組），這個做法在成本效益上必然不如免費的原生 CloudFront 地理限制功能。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"The CloudFront-Viewer-Country geolocation header only tells the origin (or edge compute like CloudFront Functions/Lambda@Edge) which country a viewer is in — it is informational and used for routing/personalization, not enforcement. Using it to actually block traffic would require the company to design, write, and operate custom edge logic themselves, which is more complex and costly than simply enabling CloudFront's built-in geographic restriction toggle.","why_zh":"CloudFront-Viewer-Country 這類地理位置標頭只是告訴來源伺服器（或 CloudFront Functions／Lambda@Edge 等邊緣運算）訪客所在國家，屬於資訊性用途，用於路由或個人化，並非強制封鎖機制。若要用它真正封鎖流量，公司得自行設計、撰寫並維運自訂的邊緣程式邏輯,這比直接開啟 CloudFront 內建的地理限制開關更複雜、成本更高。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonCloudFront/latest/DeveloperGuide/georestrictions.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonCloudFront/latest/DeveloperGuide/DownloadDistValuesEnableGeoRestriction.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/waf/latest/developerguide/waf-rule-statement-type-geo-match.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/waf/latest/developerguide/classic-aws-waf-pricing.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonCloudFront/latest/DeveloperGuide/header-caching.html"]}},{"id":198,"question_en":"A company has an encrypted Amazon Aurora DB cluster in the us-east-1 Region. The DB cluster is encrypted with an AWS Key Management Service (AWS KMS) customer managed key. To meet compliance requirements, the company needs to copy a DB snapshot to the us-west-1 Region. However, when the company tries to copy the snapshot to us-west-1, the company cannot access the key that was used to encrypt the original database. What should the company do to set up the snapshot in us-west-1 with proper encryption?","question_zh":"一家公司在 us-east-1 区域拥有一个加密的 Amazon Aurora 数据库集群，该数据库集群使用 AWS 密钥管理服务（AWS KMS）的 客户托管密钥进行加密。为满足合规要求，该公司需要将数据库快照复制到 us-west-1 区域。然而，当公司尝试将快照复制到 us- west-1 时，无法访问用于加密原始数据库的密钥。 公司应采取哪些措施，才能在 us-west-1 区域创建带有适当加密的快照？","options_en":{"A":"Use AWS Secrets Manager to store the customer managed key in us-west-1 as a secret. Use this secret to encrypt the snapshot in us-west-1.","B":"Create a new customer managed key in us-west-1. Use this new key to encrypt the snapshot in us-west- 1.","C":"Create an IAM policy that allows access to the customer managed key in us-east-1. Specify arn:aws: kms:us-west-1:* as the principal.","D":"Create an IAM policy that allows access to the customer managed key in us-east-1. Specify arn:aws:rds: us-west-1:* as the principal."},"options_zh":{"A":"使用 AWS Secrets Manager 将客户管理的密钥以密钥形式存储在 us-west-1 区域，然后使用该密钥对 us-west-1 区域中的快 照进行加密。","B":"在 us-west-1 区域创建一个新的客户管理密钥，并使用该新密钥对 us-west-1 区域中的快照进行加密。","C":"创建一个 IAM 策略，允许访问位于 us-east-1 的客户管理密钥，并将 arn:aws:kms:us-west-1:* 指定为 principal。","D":"创建一个 IAM 策略，允许访问位于 us-east-1 的客户管理密钥，并将 arn:aws:rds:us-west-1:* 指定为 principal。"},"answer":["B"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Security/IAM","Database"],"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選","research":{"verdict":["B"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"AWS KMS customer managed keys are regional resources: a key created in us-east-1 cannot be used to encrypt resources in us-west-1 (aside from the separate multi-Region key feature, which none of the options describe). AWS documentation for copying an encrypted Aurora/RDS DB cluster snapshot across Regions states explicitly that you MUST specify a KMS key for the destination Region when copying an encrypted snapshot cross-Region — the source key cannot be reused. Therefore the company must create a new customer managed key in us-west-1 and use it (via --kms-key-id / KmsKeyId in the destination Region) to encrypt the copied snapshot. IAM policies (options C and D) cannot make a KMS key usable outside its home Region, and the ARNs given (arn:aws:kms:us-west-1:* or arn:aws:rds:us-west-1:* as a 'principal') are not valid IAM principal formats and would not solve the cross-region key limitation regardless. Storing the key material as a Secrets Manager secret (option A) is not how RDS/Aurora snapshot encryption is configured — RDS references a KMS key ID directly, not a Secrets Manager secret.","explanation_zh":"AWS KMS 的客戶自管金鑰（customer managed key）是區域性資源：在 us-east-1 建立的金鑰無法用於加密 us-west-1 的資源（多區域金鑰 multi-Region key 是另一項需明確設定的功能，題目選項均未描述此情境）。AWS 官方文件針對跨區複製已加密的 Aurora/RDS DB cluster 快照明確指出：跨區複製加密快照時「必須」指定目的地區域的 KMS 金鑰，無法沿用來源區域的金鑰。因此該公司應在 us-west-1 建立新的客戶自管金鑰，並在目的地區域執行複製時使用該金鑰（--kms-key-id / KmsKeyId）加密快照複本。選項 C、D 透過 IAM 政策授予存取權限並不能讓 KMS 金鑰跨區域可用，且其中作為「principal」的 ARN 格式（arn:aws:kms:us-west-1:* 或 arn:aws:rds:us-west-1:*）本身也不是有效的 IAM principal 格式。選項 A 將金鑰儲存於 Secrets Manager 作為密鑰的做法，並非 RDS/Aurora 快照加密的運作方式——RDS 是直接參照 KMS 金鑰 ID，而非透過 Secrets Manager 密鑰。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"RDS/Aurora snapshot encryption works by referencing a KMS Key ID directly (KmsKeyId parameter); it does not use AWS Secrets Manager secrets to hold or apply encryption keys for snapshots. This option describes a mechanism RDS snapshot copy does not support.","why_zh":"RDS/Aurora 快照加密是直接參照 KMS Key ID（KmsKeyId 參數）運作，並不會透過 AWS Secrets Manager 的密鑰來持有或套用加密金鑰於快照上。此選項描述的機制並非 RDS 快照複製所支援的方式。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"KMS keys cannot be made accessible cross-Region merely via an IAM policy; the key material and the key itself only exist in its home Region (excluding explicit multi-Region keys). Additionally, 'arn:aws:kms:us-west-1:*' is not a valid IAM policy Principal element format.","why_zh":"僅靠 IAM 政策無法讓 KMS 金鑰跨區域可被存取；金鑰本身（及其金鑰材料）只存在於其所屬區域（明確設定的多區域金鑰除外）。此外，'arn:aws:kms:us-west-1:*' 也不是有效的 IAM 政策 Principal 元素格式。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"Same core flaw as option C: an IAM policy granting an RDS-service principal in us-west-1 access to a us-east-1 KMS key does not overcome the fundamental Regional scoping of KMS keys, and the given ARN is not a valid Principal format.","why_zh":"與選項 C 相同的根本缺陷：即使以 IAM 政策授予 us-west-1 的 RDS 服務 principal 存取 us-east-1 KMS 金鑰的權限，也無法克服 KMS 金鑰在區域範圍上的根本限制，且所給的 ARN 也不是有效的 Principal 格式。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonRDS/latest/AuroraUserGuide/USER_CopyDBClusterSnapshot.Encrypted.CrossRegion.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonRDS/latest/UserGuide/USER_CopySnapshot.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/kms/latest/developerguide/multi-region-keys-overview.html"]}},{"id":199,"question_en":"A company uses AWS Organizations. The company has teams that use an AWS CloudHSM hardware security module (HSM) that is hosted in a central AWS account. One of the teams creates its own new dedicated AWS account and wants to use the HSM that is hosted in the central account. How should a security engineer share the HSM that is hosted in the central account with the new dedicated account?","question_zh":"一家公司使用 AWS Organizations。该公司有多个团队，他们使用托管在中央 AWS 账户中的 AWS CloudHSM 硬件安全模 块（HSM）。其中一个团队创建了自己的专用 AWS 账户，并希望使用托管在中央账户中的 HSM。 安全工程师应如何将托管在中央账户中的HSM共享给新的专用账户？","options_en":{"A":"Use AWS Resource Access Manager (AWS RAM) to share the VPC subnet ID of the HSM that is hosted in the central account with the new dedicated account. Configure the CloudHSM security group to accept inbound traffic from the private IP addresses of client instances in the new dedicated account.","B":"Use AWS Identity and Access Management (IAM) to create a cross-account role to access the CloudHSM cluster that is in the central account. Create a new IAM user in the new dedicated account. Assign the cross-account role to the new IAM user.","C":"Use AWS IAM Identity Center to create an AWS Security Token Service (AWS STS) token to authenticate from the new dedicated account to the central account. Use the cross-account permissions that are assigned to the STS token to invoke an operation on the HSM in the central account.","D":"Use AWS Resource Access Manager (AWS RAM) to share the ID of the HSM that is hosted in the central account with the new dedicated account. Configure the CloudHSM security group to accept inbound traffic from the private IP addresses of client instances in the new dedicated account."},"options_zh":{"A":"使用 AWS 资源访问管理器（AWS RAM）将托管在中央账户中的 HSM 的 VPC 子网 ID 与新的专用账户共享。配置 CloudHSM 安全组，以接受来自新专用账户中客户端实例私有 IP 地址的入站流量。","B":"使用 AWS 身份和访问管理（IAM）创建一个跨账户角色，以访问位于中央账户中的 CloudHSM 集群。在新的专用账 户中创建一个新的 IAM 用户，并将该跨账户角色分配给此新 IAM 用户。","C":"使用 AWS IAM Identity Center 创建一个 AWS 安全令牌服务（AWS STS）令牌，以便从新的专用账户认证到中央账户。 然后利用分配给该 STS 令牌的跨账户权限，在中央账户中的 HSM 上执行操作。","D":"使用 AWS 资源访问管理器（AWS RAM）将托管在中央账户中的 HSM ID 与新的专用账户共享。配置 CloudHSM 安全组，以接受来自新专用账户中客户端实例私有 IP 地址的入站流量。"},"answer":["D"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Organizations/Governance","Security/IAM"],"difficulty":2,"diff_why":"題庫與社群皆錯","research":{"verdict":["A"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"neither","explanation_en":"AWS CloudHSM places an elastic network interface (ENI) for each HSM inside a subnet in the customer's own VPC; the HSM device itself lives in an AWS-owned VPC, and clients reach it only by having network-level access to that ENI's subnet (documented options are being in the same VPC, VPC peering, Direct Connect, or VPN). AWS Resource Access Manager's VPC-subnet-sharing feature lets an account owner share a subnet with another account in the same AWS Organization; the participant account can then launch its own EC2 client instances directly into that shared subnet, giving them the required network path to the HSM ENIs. Because CloudHSM's own console/CLI does not always allow cross-account security-group-ID referencing for the cluster's default security group, the documented workaround is to allow inbound HSM traffic by the private IP addresses of the client instances in the participant account — exactly what option A describes. Option D is a distractor: AWS RAM's list of CloudHSM-shareable resources contains only the 'AWS CloudHSM Backup' resource type (used to restore a new cluster from a shared backup in another account) — there is no shareable 'HSM ID' resource that grants live network/API access to an existing cluster, so D does not correspond to any real RAM capability. Options B and C are irrelevant because CloudHSM key/crypto operations are performed over a dedicated network protocol authenticated by HSM users/crypto officers on the device itself, not via IAM roles or STS tokens — no IAM or STS mechanism substitutes for the required network reachability to the ENI.","explanation_zh":"AWS CloudHSM 會把每顆 HSM 的彈性網路介面(ENI)放進客戶自己 VPC 中的某個 subnet;HSM 硬體本身則位於 AWS 自有的 VPC 內,用戶端只能透過取得該 ENI 所在 subnet 的網路層存取權來連線(官方文件列出的方式為:同一 VPC、VPC peering、Direct Connect 或 VPN)。AWS Resource Access Manager 的 VPC subnet 共享功能,可讓帳號擁有者把某個 subnet 分享給同一 AWS Organizations 下的另一個帳號;取得分享的帳號即可直接在該共享 subnet 中啟動自己的 EC2 用戶端執行個體,取得連到 HSM ENI 所需的網路路徑。由於 CloudHSM 叢集預設的安全群組不一定支援跨帳號以安全群組 ID 互相參照,官方作法是改用來源私有 IP 位址的方式放行新帳號用戶端執行個體的流量——這正是選項 A 所描述的做法。選項 D 是陷阱:AWS RAM 可分享的 CloudHSM 資源類型清單中只有『AWS CloudHSM Backup』(備份)這一種資源,用途是讓其他帳號用該備份還原出一個新叢集,並不存在可分享『HSM ID』來讓其他帳號直接取得現有叢集網路/API 存取權的資源類型,因此 D 並不對應任何真實的 RAM 功能。選項 B、C 則不相關,因為 CloudHSM 的金鑰/加密操作是透過專屬網路協定、由裝置上的 HSM 使用者/密碼官身分驗證完成,並非透過 IAM 角色或 STS token;沒有任何 IAM 或 STS 機制能取代連到 ENI 所需的網路可達性。","distractors":[{"letter":"B","why_en":"An IAM cross-account role only grants AWS API-level (control-plane) permissions; it does not establish the network path to the HSM's ENI, and CloudHSM data-plane crypto operations are authenticated by HSM crypto users, not IAM identities.","why_zh":"IAM 跨帳號角色只能授予 AWS API(control plane)層級的權限,無法建立到 HSM ENI 的網路路徑;CloudHSM 的資料層(data plane)加密操作是由 HSM 上的 crypto user 身分驗證,而非 IAM 身分。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"CloudHSM does not expose its cryptographic operations as an STS-authenticated service API that IAM Identity Center federation could invoke; access still requires direct network reachability to the HSM ENIs.","why_zh":"CloudHSM 並未將其加密運算功能以可用 STS 驗證呼叫的服務 API 形式提供,IAM Identity Center 聯合登入的 STS token 無法解決這個問題;存取仍需要直接連到 HSM ENI 的網路可達性。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"AWS RAM's shareable CloudHSM resource type is only 'AWS CloudHSM Backup' (for restoring a cluster in another account), not a live HSM/cluster ID; sharing a backup does not give the new account access to the existing running HSM, and there is no RAM resource type that shares an active HSM's ID for network access.","why_zh":"AWS RAM 可分享的 CloudHSM 資源類型只有『AWS CloudHSM Backup』(供其他帳號還原出新叢集用),並非現有 HSM/叢集的 ID;分享備份無法讓新帳號存取既有運行中的 HSM,也沒有任何 RAM 資源類型是用來分享現有 HSM ID 以取得網路存取權的。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/cloudhsm/latest/userguide/cluster-architecture.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/cloudhsm/latest/userguide/launch-client-instance.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/cloudhsm/latest/userguide/bp-cluster-management.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/ram/latest/userguide/shareable.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/cloudhsm/latest/userguide/sharing.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/vpc/latest/userguide/vpc-share-limitations.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/vpc/latest/userguide/vpc-share-prerequisites.html"]}},{"id":200,"question_en":"A company is investigating an increase in its AWS monthly bill. The company discovers that bad actors compromised some Amazon EC2 instances and served webpages for a large email phishing campaign. A security engineer must implement a solution to monitor for cost increases in the future to help detect malicious activity. Which solution will offer the company the EARLIEST detection of cost increases?","question_zh":"一家公司正在调查其AWS月度账单的上涨情况。该公司发现，攻击者已入侵部分Amazon EC2实例，并利用这些实例为 大规模电子邮件钓鱼活动提供网页服务。安全工程师需要实施一项解决方案，以监控未来成本增长，从而帮助检测恶 意活动。 哪种解决方案能为公司提供最早的成本上涨预警？","options_en":{"A":"Create an Amazon EventBridge rule that invokes an AWS Lambda function hourly. Program the Lambda function to download an AWS usage report from AWS Data Exports about usage of all services. Program the Lambda function to analyze the report and to send a notification when anomalies are detected.","B":"Create a cost monitor in AWS Cost Anomaly Detection. Configure an individual alert to notify an Amazon Simple Notification Service (Amazon SNS) topic when the percentage above the expected cost exceeds a threshold.","C":"Review AWS Cost Explorer daily to detect anomalies in cost from prior months. Review the usage of any services that experience a significant cost increase from prior months.","D":"Capture VPC flow logs from the VPC where the EC2 instances run. Use a third-party network analysis tool to analyze the flow logs and to detect anomalies in network traffic that might increase cost."},"options_zh":{"A":"创建一个 Amazon EventBridge 规则，每小时触发一次 AWS Lambda 函数。将 Lambda 函数编程为从 AWS 数据导出服 务下载所有服务的使用情况报告，并分析该报告，一旦检测到异常即发送通知。","B":"在 AWS 成本异常检测中创建成本监控器。配置单独的告警，当实际成本超出预期成本的百分比超过阈值时，通知 Amazon 简单通知服务（Amazon SNS）主题。","C":"每日查看 AWS 成本探索器，以检测与之前月份相比的成本异常情况。审查任何服务的使用情况，这些服务的成本相较 于之前月份有显著增长。","D":"从运行 EC2 实例的 VPC 中捕获 VPC 流日志。使用第三方网络分析工具分析这些流日志，以检测可能导致成本增加的网络 流量异常。"},"answer":["B"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Compute","Cost Optimization","Serverless/Integration"],"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選","research":{"verdict":["B"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"AWS Cost Anomaly Detection is a purpose-built, machine-learning-based service that continuously evaluates net unblended cost data and, per AWS documentation, runs approximately three times a day and offers an 'Individual alerts' subscription option that 'notifies recipients immediately when an anomaly is detected' (as opposed to daily or weekly digest summaries). Configuring a cost monitor with an individual alert routed to an SNS topic is the fastest built-in, fully-managed path from anomaly-to-notification that AWS offers, and it uses ML to reduce false positives from normal seasonality/growth. Option A (hourly Lambda parsing AWS Data Exports) is bounded by the same or worse underlying data latency — Data Exports/CUR refresh on a daily cadence, and Cost Explorer-derived cost data (which both Cost Anomaly Detection and any custom report-based solution rely on) has up to a 24-hour delay — so polling hourly does not yield earlier detection than the native service, while also requiring the company to build and tune custom anomaly-detection logic from scratch, which is slower to deliver and less reliable than AWS's managed ML detector. Option C is a manual, human-driven daily review process, which is inherently slower and less consistent than an automated real-time alert. Option D uses VPC Flow Logs and a third-party network tool to infer cost impact indirectly from network traffic anomalies; it does not measure cost directly at all and requires extra correlation work, making it the least direct and generally slowest way to detect a cost increase. Therefore option B, using AWS Cost Anomaly Detection's individual (immediate) alert subscription, offers the earliest detection of cost increases.","explanation_zh":"AWS Cost Anomaly Detection 是專為此用途打造、以機器學習為基礎的服務，官方文件說明它會持續評估淨無折扣後成本資料，大約每天執行三次，並提供「Individual alerts（個別警示）」訂閱選項，此選項會在「偵測到異常時立即通知收件者」（相對於每日或每週彙總摘要）。建立成本監控（cost monitor）並設定個別警示、透過 SNS 主題通知，是 AWS 提供的、從偵測異常到發出通知最快的原生全代管路徑，且透過 ML 降低季節性/自然成長造成的誤判。選項 A（每小時執行 Lambda 分析 AWS Data Exports）受限於相同甚至更差的底層資料延遲——Data Exports/CUR 是以每日頻率更新，而 Cost Explorer 衍生的成本資料（Cost Anomaly Detection 與任何自建報表方案都仰賴此資料）本身就有最多 24 小時的延遲，因此每小時輪詢並不會比原生服務更早偵測到異常，還需要公司從零打造並調校自訂的異常偵測邏輯，交付速度更慢、可靠度也不如 AWS 代管的 ML 偵測器。選項 C 是人工每日手動檢視流程，本質上比自動化即時警示更慢也更不一致。選項 D 使用 VPC flow logs 搭配第三方網路分析工具，是從網路流量異常「間接推論」成本影響，並非直接量測成本，還需要額外的關聯分析，是最不直接、通常也最慢偵測到成本增加的方式。因此選項 B——使用 AWS Cost Anomaly Detection 的個別（即時）警示訂閱——能提供最早的成本增加偵測。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"A custom hourly Lambda check does not beat the underlying billing data latency: AWS Data Exports/CUR data refreshes on a daily cadence and Cost Explorer-sourced cost data has up to a 24-hour delay, the same constraint Cost Anomaly Detection operates under. Polling more often than the data updates provides no earlier detection, while requiring the company to design, build, and validate custom anomaly-detection logic instead of using AWS's proven managed ML detector.","why_zh":"自建的每小時 Lambda 檢查無法克服底層帳單資料的延遲：AWS Data Exports/CUR 資料是以每日頻率更新，而 Cost Explorer 來源的成本資料最多有 24 小時延遲，這與 Cost Anomaly Detection 所受的限制相同。輪詢頻率高於資料更新頻率並不會帶來更早的偵測，反而需要公司自行設計、建置並驗證客製化的異常偵測邏輯，而非使用 AWS 已驗證的代管 ML 偵測器。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"Manually reviewing Cost Explorer once a day is a human-driven, reactive process dependent on an engineer's schedule and diligence; it lacks the automated, immediate, ML-based alerting that Cost Anomaly Detection's individual alert subscription provides, making it slower and less reliable for early detection.","why_zh":"每天手動檢視 Cost Explorer 是仰賴人工、被動反應的流程，取決於工程師的排程與細心程度；它缺乏 Cost Anomaly Detection 個別警示訂閱所提供的自動化、即時、以 ML 為基礎的警示能力，因此在早期偵測上更慢也更不可靠。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"VPC Flow Logs capture network traffic metadata, not cost/billing data; using a third-party tool to infer cost anomalies from network patterns is an indirect proxy that requires extra correlation logic and does not directly or promptly surface AWS bill cost increases across all services (e.g., non-network cost drivers would be missed entirely).","why_zh":"VPC flow logs 擷取的是網路流量中繼資料，而非成本／帳單資料；使用第三方工具從網路流量模式推論成本異常只是間接的代理指標，需要額外的關聯邏輯，且無法直接、即時地反映所有服務的 AWS 帳單成本增加（例如非網路相關的成本驅動因素將完全被忽略）。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/cost-management/latest/userguide/manage-ad.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/cost-management/latest/userguide/getting-started-ad.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/cur/latest/userguide/dataexports-create-standard.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/cur/latest/userguide/dataexports-export-delivery.html"]}},{"id":201,"question_en":"A security engineer must investigate an Amazon GuardDuty finding. The finding indicates potential cryptocurrency mining activity on an Amazon EC2 instance. The security engineer must validate the finding and assess the impact. Which data sources should the security engineer analyze to meet these requirements?","question_zh":"安全工程师必须调查一项 Amazon GuardDuty 的发现，该发现表明在 Amazon EC2 实例上可能存在加密货币挖矿活动。安全工 程师需要验证该发现并评估其影响。 安全工程师应分析哪些数据源以满足这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Check the instance’s CPU utilization metrics in Amazon CloudWatch. Examine the finding’s MITRE ATT & CK tactic classification. Review any associated IAM role permissions.","B":"Count the number of GuardDuty findings associated with the instance. Verify the instance’s launch time. Check AWS Security Hub CSPM for any related alerts.","C":"Review the instance’s process details that relate to the finding. Examine DNS queries to known mining domains. Analyze the instance’s outbound network connections by using VPC Flow Logs.","D":"Examine the instance’s AWS Systems Manager session history. Verify Amazon Route 53 DNS records. Review GuardDuty severity levels."},"options_zh":{"A":"在 Amazon CloudWatch 中检查实例的 CPU 使用率指标。查看该发现项的 MITRE ATT&CK 技术分类。审查相关的 IAM 角色权限。","B":"统计与该实例相关的 GuardDuty 发现数量。验证实例的启动时间。检查 AWS Security Hub 的 CSPM 是否存在相关告 警。","C":"检查与发现结果相关的实例进程详情。检查对已知挖矿域名的DNS查询。使用VPC流量日志分析实例的出站网络连接。","D":"检查实例的 AWS Systems Manager 会话历史记录，验证 Amazon Route 53 DNS 记录，并查看 GuardDuty 的严重性级别。"},"answer":["C"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Networking/DNS","Security/IAM","Compute","Monitoring/Ops"],"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選","research":{"verdict":["C"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"both","explanation_en":"GuardDuty's cryptocurrency-mining findings (the CryptoCurrency:EC2/BitcoinTool.B family, plus its DNS and Runtime Monitoring variants) are generated from exactly three underlying signal types: process/execution activity captured by Runtime Monitoring, DNS query logs showing lookups to known cryptocurrency-mining pool domains, and VPC Flow Logs showing outbound connections to known mining-pool IP addresses/ports. To validate a GuardDuty crypto-mining finding and assess its blast radius, a security engineer must go to these actual data sources referenced by the finding: the instance's running processes (to confirm a miner binary/process is active), the DNS resolution history (to confirm the domain is a known mining pool), and VPC Flow Logs (to confirm and scope outbound connections to the mining infrastructure, which shows impact/data exfil scale). AWS's own EC2-compromise remediation runbook centers on exactly this kind of evidence gathering (process/malware inspection, network isolation, source-of-activity identification) rather than metadata like CloudWatch CPU graphs, finding counts, launch times, or MITRE ATT&CK tags. Option A's CPU metrics and MITRE tactic tag are indirect/contextual, not the actual forensic evidence, and IAM role permissions are irrelevant to a compute/network-based mining finding. Option B (finding count, launch time, Security Hub CSPM alerts) and Option D (SSM session history, Route 53 DNS records, GuardDuty severity levels) are largely administrative or unrelated metadata, not the process/DNS/network telemetry that actually confirms mining behavior and its impact.","explanation_zh":"GuardDuty 的加密貨幣挖礦類 finding(CryptoCurrency:EC2/BitcoinTool.B 家族,及其 DNS 與 Runtime Monitoring 變體)是根據三種底層訊號產生的:Runtime Monitoring 擷取的行程/執行活動、顯示查詢已知挖礦礦池網域的 DNS 查詢紀錄,以及顯示對外連線到已知礦池 IP/連接埠的 VPC Flow Logs。要驗證 GuardDuty 的挖礦 finding 並評估影響範圍,安全工程師必須檢視 finding 實際引用的這些資料來源:執行個體上的行程(確認是否有挖礦程式在執行)、DNS 解析紀錄(確認網域是否為已知礦池)、以及 VPC Flow Logs(確認並界定對外連線到挖礦基礎設施的範圍,藉此了解影響/資料外洩規模)。AWS 官方的 EC2 疑似受駭修復手冊本身就是圍繞這類證據蒐集(行程/惡意程式檢查、網路隔離、找出可疑活動來源),而非 CloudWatch CPU 圖表、finding 數量、啟動時間或 MITRE ATT&CK 標籤這類中繼資料。選項 A 的 CPU 指標與 MITRE 戰術標籤只是間接/情境資訊,並非實際鑑識證據,而 IAM 角色權限與運算/網路型挖礦 finding 無關。選項 B(finding 數量、啟動時間、Security Hub CSPM 警示)與選項 D(SSM session 歷史、Route 53 DNS 紀錄、GuardDuty 嚴重性等級)大多是管理性或不相關的中繼資料,並非真正能確認挖礦行為及其影響的行程/DNS/網路遙測資料。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"CloudWatch CPU metrics only hint at high load and don't confirm mining; the MITRE ATT&CK tactic tag is just a classification label attached to the finding, not investigative evidence; IAM role permissions are unrelated to a compute/network-based cryptocurrency finding.","why_zh":"CloudWatch CPU 指標只能暗示負載偏高,無法確認是挖礦;MITRE ATT&CK 戰術標籤只是附加在 finding 上的分類標籤,並非調查證據;IAM 角色權限與運算/網路型的加密貨幣 finding 無關。"},{"letter":"B","why_en":"Counting related GuardDuty findings, checking launch time, and looking at Security Hub CSPM (configuration posture) alerts do not provide the process, DNS, or network evidence needed to confirm active mining behavior or its scope.","why_zh":"計算相關 GuardDuty finding 數量、檢查啟動時間、查看 Security Hub CSPM(組態態勢)警示,都無法提供確認挖礦行為是否存在及其影響範圍所需的行程、DNS 或網路證據。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"SSM session history shows administrative access history (not mining activity), Route 53 DNS records describe your own hosted zones (not the instance's outbound lookups to mining pools), and GuardDuty severity levels are just a priority score, not forensic data.","why_zh":"SSM session 歷史顯示的是管理性存取紀錄(非挖礦活動),Route 53 DNS 紀錄描述的是自己託管區域的設定(而非該執行個體對外查詢礦池的紀錄),GuardDuty 嚴重性等級只是優先順序分數,並非鑑識資料。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/guardduty/latest/ug/compromised-ec2.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/guardduty/latest/ug/guardduty_finding-types-retired.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/guardduty/latest/ug/lambda-protection-finding-types.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/guardduty/latest/ug/guardduty_findings-summary.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/guardduty/latest/ug/runtime-monitoring-collected-events.html"]}},{"id":202,"question_en":"A company is running a dynamic website by using an Application Load Balancer (ALB). A security engineer notices that bots from different IP addresses are using brute-force attacks to invoke a service endpoint frequently. What is the FASTEST way to mitigate this problem?","question_zh":"一家公司正在使用应用负载均衡器（ALB）运行一个动态网站。安全工程师发现，来自不同IP地址 的机器人正频繁地通过暴力攻击调用服务端点。 解决这个问题的最快方法是什么？","options_en":{"A":"Create an AWS Lambda function to process ALB logs. Block the bots’ IP addresses in the ALB’s security group.","B":"Create an AWS WAF web ACL for the ALB. Add a rate-based rule to the web ACL to block the bots.","C":"Create an ALB listener rule. Combine source-ip and path-pattern as the conditions to match bots. Specify a fixed-response action to return an HTTP 403 status.","D":"Create an AWS WAF web ACL for the ALB. Add a rate-based rule to a rule group to block the bots. Attach the rule to the web ACL."},"options_zh":{"A":"创建一个 AWS Lambda 函数来处理 ALB 日志，并在 ALB 的安全组中屏蔽机器人 IP 地址。","B":"为ALB创建一个AWS WAF网络ACL，并在该网络ACL中添加基于速率的规则以阻止机器人。","C":"创建一个 ALB 监听器规则，将源 IP 和路径模式作为匹配机器人流量的条件，并指定返回 HTTP 403 状态码的固定响应操作。","D":"为ALB创建一个AWS WAF网络ACL。将基于速率的规则添加到规则组中以阻止机器人，然 后将该规则附加到网络ACL。"},"answer":["B"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Networking/DNS","Security/IAM","Compute"],"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選","research":{"verdict":["B"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"both","explanation_en":"AWS WAF rate-based rules are purpose-built to counter this exact scenario: bots hammering an endpoint from many different source IPs. A rate-based rule statement tracks the number of requests from each IP (or another aggregation key) in a rolling 5-minute (or 10-minute, depending on version) window and automatically blocks any IP that exceeds the configured threshold — no need to know the offending IPs in advance, unlike option C's static source-ip listener rule. Per AWS documentation, a rate-based rule statement 'can [be included] directly in a protection pack (web ACL) or rule group' — both are valid places to define it. Because the question asks for the FASTEST mitigation, adding the rate-based rule directly to the web ACL (option B) requires fewer resources and steps than first creating a separate rule group, adding the rate-based rule to it, and then attaching that rule group to the web ACL (option D) — an unnecessary extra layer of indirection when a rule group isn't needed for reuse across multiple web ACLs. Option A (Lambda parsing ALB access logs to update the ALB security group) is slow and reactive: logs must be delivered, processed, and security-group rules updated, plus security groups have IP-range limits and don't rate-limit — this takes minutes to hours, not the fastest path. Option C's ALB listener rule with a fixed source-ip condition cannot scale to bots rotating across many/unknown IP addresses. Therefore B is the fastest, purpose-fit, and directly documented mitigation.","explanation_zh":"AWS WAF 的 rate-based rule（速率規則）正是為了對付「多個不同來源 IP 對端點進行暴力嘗試」這種情境而設計：它會在滾動的評估窗口（預設 5 分鐘）內追蹤每個來源 IP（或其他聚合鍵）的請求數，一旦超過門檻就自動封鎖該來源，完全不需要像選項 C 那樣事先知道具體的 bot IP。根據 AWS 官方文件，rate-based rule statement「可以直接加入 protection pack（web ACL）或 rule group」，兩者皆為合法位置。但題目問的是「最快」的緩解方式：直接把 rate-based rule 加到 web ACL（選項 B）比選項 D 多繞一層——先建立獨立的 rule group、在其中加入規則、再把該 rule group 附加到 web ACL——多了不必要的中間層，除非需要跨多個 web ACL 重複使用規則，否則沒有必要。選項 A 用 Lambda 解析 ALB 存取日誌再更新安全群組屬於被動且延遲的做法（日誌傳遞、處理、更新安全群組規則都要時間，且安全群組不支援速率限制、也有規則數量上限），並非最快方案。選項 C 的 ALB 監聽器規則搭配固定 source-ip 條件，無法應對來源 IP 不斷變動、數量龐大的 bot 攻擊。因此選項 B 是最快、最貼合官方文件建議的緩解方式。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"Building a Lambda function to parse ALB logs and then update the ALB's security group is a slow, custom, reactive pipeline (log delivery + processing + security-group updates), and security groups don't support rate-limiting or wildcard/CIDR-based dynamic blocking at the scale of many rotating bot IPs — far from 'fastest'.","why_zh":"自建 Lambda 解析 ALB 日誌再更新安全群組是緩慢的自訂被動流程（日誌傳遞、處理、更新安全群組規則都要時間），且安全群組不支援速率限制，也難以應付大量、不斷變動的 bot IP，並非最快做法。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"An ALB listener rule using a fixed source-ip condition requires knowing the bots' IP addresses ahead of time and manually maintaining the list; it cannot adapt to bots using many different/changing IP addresses, which is exactly the scenario described.","why_zh":"ALB 監聽器規則使用固定的 source-ip 條件，需要事先知道 bot 的 IP 並手動維護清單，無法應付題目描述中「來自不同 IP 位址的 bot」這種持續變動的情境。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"Technically works (rate-based rules can live in a rule group), but routing through a separate rule group that is then attached to the web ACL adds an unnecessary extra resource and step compared to adding the rate-based rule directly to the web ACL, making it slower to set up than option B for this one-off mitigation.","why_zh":"技術上可行（rate-based rule 可以放在 rule group 中），但多繞過一個獨立的 rule group 再附加到 web ACL，比起直接把 rate-based rule 加到 web ACL 多了一道不必要的步驟與資源，對於這種一次性緩解措施而言設定速度較慢，不如選項 B 直接。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/waf/latest/developerguide/waf-rule-statement-type-rate-based.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/waf/latest/developerguide/waf-rule-statement-type-rate-based-high-level-settings.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/waf/latest/developerguide/waf-rule-statement-type-rate-based-examples.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/waf/latest/developerguide/waf-chapter.html"]}},{"id":203,"question_en":"A company runs ECS services behind an internet-facing ALB that is the origin for CloudFront. An AWS WAF web ACL is associated with CloudFront, but clients can bypass it by accessing the ALB directly. Which solution will prevent direct access to the ALB?","question_zh":"一家公司通过面向互联网的ALB运行ECS服务，该ALB作为CloudFront的源站。虽然CloudFront已关联了AWS WAF网络ACL， 但客户端仍可通过直接访问ALB绕过该防护。 哪种解决方案可以防止直接访问ALB？","options_en":{"A":"Use AWS PrivateLink with the ALB.","B":"Replace the ALB with an internal ALB.","C":"Restrict ALB listener rules to CloudFront IP ranges.","D":"Require a custom header from CloudFront and validate it at the ALB."},"options_zh":{"A":"使用 AWS PrivateLink 与 ALB。","B":"将 ALB 替换为内部 ALB。","C":"将 ALB 监听器规则限制为 CloudFront IP 范围。","D":"要求 CloudFront 提供自定义标头，并在 ALB 处验证该标头。"},"answer":["D"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Networking/DNS","Security/IAM","Compute","Containers"],"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選","research":{"verdict":["D"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"both","explanation_en":"AWS's official documented mitigation for exactly this scenario (internet-facing ALB used as a CloudFront origin) is to have CloudFront insert a secret custom HTTP header on origin requests, and configure the ALB listener rules to forward traffic only when that header/value is present (returning a fixed 403 response otherwise). AWS explicitly titles the relevant guide 'Restrict access to Application Load Balancers' and lists the custom-header-plus-listener-rule steps as the core solution, with HTTPS required to keep the header confidential in transit. Restricting the ALB to CloudFront's IP ranges (option C) is presented in that same doc only as an OPTIONAL supplementary layer, because CloudFront IP ranges are shared across all CloudFront customers — anyone with their own CloudFront distribution pointed at your ALB's DNS name could still get through an IP-only restriction. PrivateLink (A) is not the mechanism used to expose a public/internet-facing ALB behind CloudFront for this pattern, and converting to an internal ALB (B) would sever CloudFront's ability to reach the origin at all in the standard internet-facing setup described. Therefore D is both the ExamTopics-suggested answer and the technically correct one per AWS documentation.","explanation_zh":"針對「internet-facing ALB 作為 CloudFront 來源」這個情境，AWS 官方文件明確記載的防護做法是：讓 CloudFront 在轉發到源站的請求中加入一個秘密的自訂 HTTP 標頭，並在 ALB 的 listener 規則設定為「只有帶有此標頭/值的請求才轉發到目標群組」（否則回傳固定的 403）。AWS 文件標題即為「Restrict access to Application Load Balancers」，把自訂標頭 + listener 規則列為核心解法，並建議搭配 HTTPS 以保護標頭在傳輸中的機密性。將 ALB 限制為僅接受 CloudFront IP 範圍（選項 C）在同一篇文件中僅被列為「可選的」補充層，因為 CloudFront 的 IP 範圍是所有 CloudFront 客戶共用的——任何人只要建立自己的 CloudFront distribution 指向你的 ALB DNS 名稱，仍可繞過純 IP 限制。PrivateLink（A）並非此情境中用來讓 CloudFront 存取公開型 ALB 的機制；把 ALB 改成 internal（B）在標準的 internet-facing 架構下會直接讓 CloudFront 無法連到源站。因此 D 同時是題庫建議答案，也是依據 AWS 文件技術上正確的答案。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"AWS PrivateLink is used for private cross-VPC/cross-account service exposure, not as the documented mechanism to let CloudFront exclusively reach a public-facing ALB origin in this pattern; it is not part of AWS's published guidance for this exact problem.","why_zh":"AWS PrivateLink 是用於跨 VPC/跨帳戶的私有服務曝露，並非 AWS 官方文件中針對『讓 CloudFront 專屬存取公開型 ALB 源站』這個問題所記載的機制。"},{"letter":"B","why_en":"Making the ALB internal would prevent CloudFront (in the standard internet-facing setup described) from reaching the origin at all, breaking the architecture rather than securing it; internal ALBs require the newer CloudFront VPC origins feature and a different setup than what's described.","why_zh":"把 ALB 改成 internal，在題目描述的標準 internet-facing 架構下會讓 CloudFront 根本無法連到源站，等於破壞架構而非強化安全；internal ALB 需搭配較新的 CloudFront VPC origins 功能與不同的設定方式。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"AWS documentation explicitly lists IP-range restriction via the CloudFront managed prefix list as an OPTIONAL supplementary control, not the primary fix, because those IP ranges are shared by all CloudFront customers and don't verify the request actually came from your specific distribution.","why_zh":"AWS 文件明確將透過 CloudFront managed prefix list 限制 IP 範圍列為『可選』的補充控制，而非主要解法，因為這些 IP 範圍是所有 CloudFront 客戶共用的，無法驗證請求確實來自你自己的 distribution。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonCloudFront/latest/DeveloperGuide/restrict-access-to-load-balancer.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonCloudFront/latest/DeveloperGuide/add-origin-custom-headers.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonCloudFront/latest/DeveloperGuide/data-protection-summary.html"]}},{"id":204,"question_en":"A security engineer is troubleshooting an AWS Lambda function that is namedMyLambdaFunction. The function is encountering an error when the function attempts to read the objects in an Amazon S3 bucket that is namedDOC-EXAMPLE-BUCKET. The S3 bucket has the following bucket policy: { \" Effect \" : \" Allow \" , \" Principal \" : { \" Service \" : \" lambda.amazonaws.com \" }, \" Action \" : \" s3:GetObject \" , \" Resource \" : \" arn:aws:s3:::DOC-EXAMPLE-BUCKET \" , \" Condition \" : { \" ArnLike \" : { \" aws:SourceArn \" : \" arn:aws:lambda:::function:MyLambdaFunction \" } } } Which change should the security engineer make to the policy to ensure that the Lambda function can read the bucket objects?","question_zh":"一名安全工程师正在排查一个名为 MyLambdaFunction 的 AWS Lambda 函数。当该函数尝试读取名为 DOC-EXAMPLE-BUCKET 的 Amazon S3 存储桶中的对象时，会遇到错误。该 S3 存储桶具有以下存储桶策略： 安全工程师应如何修改策略，以确保Lambda函数能够读取存储桶中的对象？","options_en":{"A":"Remove the Condition element. Change the Principal element to the following:{ \" AWS \" : \" arn:aws: lambda:::function:MyLambdaFunction \" }","B":"Change the Action element to the following:[ \" s3:GetObject* \" , \" s3:GetBucket* \" ]","C":"Change the Resource element to \" arn:aws:s3:::DOC-EXAMPLE-BUCKET/* \" .","D":"Change the Resource element to \" arn:aws:lambda:::function:MyLambdaFunction \" . Change the Principal element to the following:{ \" Service \" : \" s3.amazonaws.com \" }"},"options_zh":{"A":"删除 Condition 元素。将 Principal 元素更改为以下内容：{ \" AWS \" : \" arn:aws： lambda：：：function: MyLambdaFunction \" }","B":"将操作元素更改为以下内容：[\"s3:GetObject*\"， \"s3:GetBucket*\"]","C":"将资源元素更改为“arn:aws:s3:::DOC-EXAMPLE-BUCKET/*”。","D":"将 Resource 元素更aws:lambda:::function：MyLambdaFunction\"。将 Principal 元素更改为以下内容：{ \"Service \": \"s3.amazonaws.com\" }"},"answer":["C"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Storage","Compute"],"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選","research":{"verdict":["C"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"The bucket policy grants the action `s3:GetObject`, which is an object-level S3 action. Object-level actions require the `Resource` element to be an object ARN in the form `arn:aws:s3:::bucket-name/*` (or a specific key), not the bucket ARN alone (`arn:aws:s3:::bucket-name`). As written, the policy's `Resource` is `arn:aws:s3:::DOC-EXAMPLE-BUCKET` — the bucket ARN — which is a resource-type mismatch for `s3:GetObject` (that bare bucket ARN is only valid for bucket-level actions like `s3:ListBucket` or `s3:GetBucketLocation`). This mismatch causes the policy statement to not apply to any actual object, so Lambda's read attempts fail. The fix is to change `Resource` to `arn:aws:s3:::DOC-EXAMPLE-BUCKET/*`, matching AWS's documented S3 object ARN format used in the `Resource` element of IAM and bucket policies. This is a well-known, frequently-tested S3 IAM gotcha (bucket ARN vs. object ARN) and does not require touching Principal, Action, or Condition, which are otherwise valid for a Lambda-execution-role-based cross-service read (invoked via SourceArn condition tying to the specific function).","explanation_zh":"此 bucket policy 授予的 action 是 `s3:GetObject`，這是一個「物件層級（object-level）」的 S3 action。物件層級的 action 要求 `Resource` 元素必須是物件 ARN 格式，即 `arn:aws:s3:::bucket-name/*`（或指定的 key），而不能只是 bucket ARN（`arn:aws:s3:::bucket-name`）。目前 policy 中的 `Resource` 是 `arn:aws:s3:::DOC-EXAMPLE-BUCKET`，也就是 bucket ARN——這與 `s3:GetObject` 所需的資源型別不符（該裸 bucket ARN 只適用於 bucket 層級的 action，例如 `s3:ListBucket` 或 `s3:GetBucketLocation`）。這種不匹配會導致該 policy 陳述式無法套用到任何實際物件，因此 Lambda 的讀取請求會失敗。修正方式是把 `Resource` 改成 `arn:aws:s3:::DOC-EXAMPLE-BUCKET/*`，這正好符合 AWS 官方文件中 IAM／bucket policy 的 `Resource` 元素所使用的 S3 物件 ARN 格式。這是一個常見且經常在考試中出現的 S3 IAM 陷阱（bucket ARN vs. 物件 ARN），且不需要更動 Principal、Action 或 Condition——這些元素對於透過 SourceArn 條件綁定特定函式的跨服務讀取情境本身是合理的。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"Removing the Condition and setting Principal to an AWS-type principal pointing at the Lambda function ARN is invalid: a bucket policy's `Principal` for cross-service access should be the service principal (`lambda.amazonaws.com`, scoped safely via `aws:SourceArn`/`aws:SourceAccount`) or an IAM user/role/account ARN — a Lambda function ARN is not a valid IAM principal identity and cannot be used as an `AWS` principal value. It also doesn't address the actual root cause (the Resource ARN format mismatch for GetObject).","why_zh":"移除 Condition 並將 Principal 改為 AWS 型別、指向 Lambda function ARN，這是無效的做法：bucket policy 中用於跨服務存取的 `Principal` 應該是服務主體（`lambda.amazonaws.com`，並透過 `aws:SourceArn`/`aws:SourceAccount` 安全地限縮範圍）或是 IAM 使用者／角色／帳號 ARN——Lambda function ARN 本身並不是有效的 IAM 主體身分，不能作為 `AWS` principal 的值。而且這個做法也沒有解決真正的根本原因（GetObject 所需的 Resource ARN 格式不匹配）。"},{"letter":"B","why_en":"Expanding the Action list to include `s3:GetObject*` and `s3:GetBucket*` does not fix the problem: the existing `Resource` is still the bare bucket ARN, which remains invalid for any object-level action (including the wildcard `s3:GetObject*` variants). The error is about resource-type mismatch, not insufficient action coverage.","why_zh":"把 Action 清單擴充為 `s3:GetObject*` 與 `s3:GetBucket*` 並不能解決問題：現有的 `Resource` 仍然是裸的 bucket ARN，對任何物件層級的 action（包括 `s3:GetObject*` 這類萬用字元變體）依然無效。問題出在資源型別不匹配，而不是 action 涵蓋範圍不足。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"This inverts the entire access model: making the Resource a Lambda function ARN and the Principal `s3.amazonaws.com` would turn this into a resource-based policy on the Lambda function granting S3 permission to invoke Lambda — the opposite of what's needed (Lambda reading from S3). This does not grant the Lambda function any S3 read permission at all.","why_zh":"此選項完全顛倒了存取模型：把 Resource 改成 Lambda function ARN、Principal 改成 `s3.amazonaws.com`，會變成一個附加在 Lambda function 上的資源型 policy，授權 S3 去呼叫（invoke）該 Lambda——這與題目需求（Lambda 讀取 S3）完全相反。這個做法完全沒有賦予 Lambda function 任何讀取 S3 的權限。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonS3/latest/userguide/security_iam_service-with-iam.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonS3/latest/userguide/using-with-s3-actions.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/IAM/latest/UserGuide/reference_policies_elements_resource.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonS3/latest/userguide/access-management.html"]}},{"id":205,"question_en":"A company has an organization in AWS Organizations. The company’s security team is developing automation to capture Amazon EC2 forensic evidence within any AWS account in the organization. The company has encrypted the Amazon EBS volumes of all the EC2 instances in the organization by default by using the AWS managed key. The automation consists of AWS Lambda functions and AWS Step Functions state machines. The automation assumes an IAM role in the target AWS account. The automation takes snapshots of suspicious EC2 instances and assigns permissions to allow the security team’s account to copy the snapshots. The security team has an AWS KMS key to encrypt the snapshots. During testing, the automation fails to copy the snapshots into the security team’s AWS account. Which combination of steps should the security team take so that the automation can capture EC2 forensic evidence in all AWS accounts in the organization? (Select THREE.)","question_zh":"一家公司在 AWS Organizations 中拥有一个组织架构。该公司的安全团队正在开发自动化流程，以 在组织内的任何 AWS 账户中收集 Amazon EC2 的取证证据。该公司默认使用 AWS 管理的密钥对 组织内所有 EC2 实例的 Amazon EBS 卷进行了加密。该自动化流程由 AWS Lambda 函数和 AWS Step Functions 状态机组成。 自动化流程在目标AWS账户中假设了一个IAM角色。该自动化会为可疑的EC2实例创建快照，并分 配权限，允许安全团队的账户复制这些快照。安全团队拥有一个AWS KMS密钥用于加密快照。但在 测试过程中，自动化未能成功将快照复制到安全团队的AWS账户中。 安全团队应采取哪些步骤组合，才能使自动化系统能够捕获组织内所有AWS账户中的EC2取证证 据？（选择三项。）","options_en":{"A":"In the target AWS account, update the KMS key policy on the AWS managed key to explicitly allow the kms:Decrypt and kms:CreateGrant actions to the automation’s IAM role.","B":"In the target AWS account, create a customer managed KMS key. Update the automation’s IAM role to allow the kms:Encrypt, kms:Decrypt, kms:GenerateDataKey*, and kms:CreateGrant actions.","C":"In the security team’s AWS account, update the automation’s IAM role to allow the kms:Encrypt, kms: Decrypt, and kms:CreateGrant actions for the AWS managed key.","D":"In the security team’s AWS account, update the automation’s IAM role to allow the kms:Encrypt, kms: Decrypt, kms:GenerateDataKey*, and kms:CreateGrant actions for the customer managed KMS key.","F":"In the security team’s AWS account, update the automation code to take EBS snapshots and to use the customer managed KMS key.","E":"In the security team’s AWS account, update the automation code to take EBS snapshots and to use the AWS managed key."},"options_zh":{"A":"在目标 AWS 账户中，更新 AWS 托管密钥的 KMS 密钥策略，明确允许自动化流程的 IAM 角 色执行 kms:Decrypt 和 kms:CreateGrant 操作。","B":"在目标 AWS 账户中创建一个客户管理的 KMS 密钥。更新自动化流程的 IAM 角色，以允许执 行 kms:Encrypt、kms:Decrypt、kms：GenerateDataKey* 和 kms:CreateGrant 操作。","C":"在安全团队的 AWS 账户中，更新自动化流程的 IAM 角色，以允许对 AWS 管理密钥执行 kms: Encrypt、kms:Decrypt 和 kms:CreateGrant 操作。","D":"在安全团队的 AWS 账户中，更新自动化流程的 IAM 角色，以允许对客户管理的 KMS 密钥执 行 kms:Encrypt、kms：Decrypt、kms：GenerateDataKey* 和 kms:CreateGrant 操作。","E":"在安全团队的 AWS 账户中，更新自动化代码以创建 EBS 快照并使用 AWS 管理的密钥。","F":"在安全团队的 AWS 账户中，更新自动化代码以创建 EBS 快照，并使用客户管理的 KMS 密钥。"},"answer":["B","D","F"],"multi":true,"vote":{},"tags":["Organizations/Governance","Security/IAM","Storage","Compute","Serverless/Integration"],"difficulty":2,"diff_why":"複選","research":{"verdict":["B","D","F"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"AWS documentation is explicit and decisive here: \"You can't share snapshots that are encrypted with the default AWS managed key. You can only share snapshots that are encrypted with a customer managed key\" (EBS user guide, ebs-modifying-snapshot-permissions.html). Since the company encrypts all EBS volumes by default with the AWS managed key (aws/ebs), any snapshot the automation takes inherits that AWS managed key encryption and can never be shared cross-account, no matter what IAM or key-policy permissions are granted — the API rejects the ModifySnapshotAttribute/share operation outright for AWS-managed-key-encrypted snapshots, and AWS managed key policies cannot be edited by customers to add outside principals anyway. The only fix is to move to customer managed keys (CMKs), which support cross-account key policies and grants (ebs/latest/userguide/share-kms-key.html lists the required actions: kms:CreateGrant, kms:Decrypt, kms:GenerateDataKey*, kms:DescribeKey, kms:ReEncrypt). Concretely: (B) in the target account, provision a CMK and grant the automation's assumed role there kms:Encrypt/Decrypt/GenerateDataKey*/CreateGrant so it can re-encrypt the snapshot with a shareable key instead of the AWS managed key; (D) in the security team's account, grant the automation's home role the same actions on the security team's own CMK, which is required to receive/re-encrypt the copy once it lands in that account (CopySnapshot into a destination account needs kms:CreateGrant/Decrypt/GenerateDataKey* on the destination key); and (F) update the automation code so the snapshot-copy step in the security account actually specifies the customer managed key rather than relying on the source's (unshareable) AWS managed key. Together these three changes replace the AWS-managed-key-based flow with a fully cross-account-capable CMK-based flow, which is the documented pattern for sharing/copying encrypted EBS snapshots between accounts.","explanation_zh":"AWS 官方文件在這點上講得非常明確：「You can't share snapshots that are encrypted with the default AWS managed key. You can only share snapshots that are encrypted with a customer managed key」（EBS 使用者指南 ebs-modifying-snapshot-permissions.html）。由於該公司預設用 AWS managed key（aws/ebs）加密所有 EBS 磁碟區，自動化程式產生的快照也會繼承這個 AWS managed key 加密，因此無論授予什麼 IAM 或 key policy 權限，這類快照永遠無法跨帳號分享——API 會直接拒絕對 AWS managed key 加密快照執行 ModifySnapshotAttribute／分享操作，而且客戶本來就無法編輯 AWS managed key 的 key policy 去加入外部帳號主體。唯一的解法是改用 customer managed key（CMK），因為 CMK 才支援跨帳號 key policy 與 grant（ebs/latest/userguide/share-kms-key.html 列出所需 action：kms:CreateGrant、kms:Decrypt、kms:GenerateDataKey*、kms:DescribeKey、kms:ReEncrypt）。具體而言：(B) 在目標帳號中建立一把 CMK，並授予自動化程式在該帳號中所扮演角色 kms:Encrypt/Decrypt/GenerateDataKey*/CreateGrant 權限，使其能用可分享的金鑰重新加密快照，而非繼續使用 AWS managed key；(D) 在安全團隊帳號中，授予自動化程式的主要角色對安全團隊自有 CMK 相同的權限，這是快照複製進入該帳號時（CopySnapshot 到目的帳號）所需的權限（需要對目的金鑰有 kms:CreateGrant/Decrypt/GenerateDataKey*）；(F) 更新自動化程式碼，讓在安全團隊帳號執行的快照複製步驟確實指定使用該 customer managed key，而不是依賴來源那把（無法分享的）AWS managed key。這三項變更合起來，把原本以 AWS managed key 為基礎、無法跨帳號運作的流程，改造成完整支援跨帳號的 CMK 流程，這正是 AWS 文件記載的加密 EBS 快照跨帳號分享／複製標準做法。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"This is not achievable and would not work even if attempted: AWS managed key (aws/ebs) policies are owned and controlled entirely by AWS and cannot be edited by customers to add external principals or actions. More fundamentally, per AWS documentation snapshots encrypted with the AWS managed key cannot be shared with other accounts at all — the restriction is enforced at the EC2/snapshot-sharing level, not merely at the KMS permission level, so granting kms:Decrypt/CreateGrant on the AWS managed key (even if it were possible) would not unblock cross-account copying.","why_zh":"此做法根本不可行，就算真的嘗試也不會成功：AWS managed key（aws/ebs）的 key policy 完全由 AWS 擁有並控管，客戶無法編輯它去加入外部主體或 action。更根本的是，根據 AWS 文件，用 AWS managed key 加密的快照本來就無法分享給其他帳號——這個限制是在 EC2／快照分享層級強制執行的，而不僅僅是 KMS 權限層級的問題，因此就算能對 AWS managed key 授予 kms:Decrypt/CreateGrant（實際上不可能），也無法解除跨帳號複製的封鎖。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"Granting the security team's role permissions on the AWS managed key does not help: that key belongs to and is scoped to the target account, its policy cannot be modified to add the security team's account as a principal, and — as with option A — snapshots encrypted with an AWS managed key cannot be shared cross-account regardless of any IAM policy granted in the recipient account. The bottleneck is the encryption key type on the snapshot itself, not which account's IAM role is being edited.","why_zh":"在安全團隊帳號中授予其角色對 AWS managed key 的權限並無幫助：該金鑰屬於且僅限於目標帳號，其 key policy 無法被修改以加入安全團隊帳號作為主體；而且如同選項 A，用 AWS managed key 加密的快照無論在接收端帳號授予何種 IAM 權限都無法跨帳號分享。問題瓶頸在於快照本身使用的加密金鑰類型，而不是在哪個帳號編輯 IAM 角色。"},{"letter":"E","why_en":"Continuing to use the AWS managed key perpetuates exactly the root cause of the failure. Per AWS documentation, snapshots encrypted with the default AWS managed key can never be shared with another account; keeping this design means the security team's automation will keep failing to copy the snapshots regardless of any other fix applied.","why_zh":"繼續使用 AWS managed key 恰恰延續了造成失敗的根本原因。根據 AWS 文件，用預設 AWS managed key 加密的快照永遠無法分享給其他帳號；維持這種設計代表無論再做任何其他修正，安全團隊的自動化程式仍會持續複製快照失敗。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/ebs/latest/userguide/ebs-modifying-snapshot-permissions.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/ebs/latest/userguide/share-kms-key.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/ebs/latest/userguide/ebs-encryption-requirements.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/ebs/latest/userguide/data-protection.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/systems-manager-automation-runbooks/latest/userguide/awssupport-share-encrypted-ami-or-ebs-snapshot.html"]}},{"id":206,"question_en":"A company uses AWS Organizations to manage the company’s AWS accounts. The company’s security team needs to implement preventive controls to deny the use of account-level root credentials. The solution must minimize the risk that an AWS account root user could be compromised. The solution must also minimize the effort needed to manage root access. Which solution will meet these requirements?","question_zh":"一家公司使用 AWS Organizations 来管理其 AWS 账户。公司的安全团队需要实施预防性控制措施， 以禁止使用账户级别的根凭据。该解决方案必须最大限度降低 AWS 账户根用户被泄露的风险，同时 也要尽量减少管理根访问所需的工作量。 哪种解决方案能满足这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Create an AWS Lambda function to disable the root user in every member account. Enable the root account only if the company needs it to modify settings related to centralized billing or the recovery of AWS KMS keys.","B":"Enable centralized root access management in IAM. Remove long-term root credentials in the member accounts. Create a company policy that requires employees to use Organizations to create new accounts.","C":"Enable centralized root access management through AWS Security Hub CSPM. Remove long-term root credentials in the member accounts. Configure new accounts to be created without root credentials in Security Hub CSPM.","D":"Configure an SCP to explicitly deny all actions when the principal is the root user of an account for all member accounts. Require that member account root users have MFA enabled. Require that root credentials are rotated on a regular schedule."},"options_zh":{"A":"创建一个 AWS Lambda 函数，用于在每个成员账户中禁用根用户。仅当公司需要修改与集中 计费或 AWS KMS 密钥恢复相关的设置时，才启用根账户。","B":"在 IAM 中启用集中式根访问管理。移除成员账户中的长期根凭据。制定公司政策，要求员工使 用 Organizations 创建新账户。","C":"通过 AWS Security Hub CSPM 启用集中化的根访问权限管理。在成员账户中移除长期有效的根 凭据。在 Security Hub CSPM 中配置新创建的账户时不包含根凭据。","D":"配置一个 SCP，明确拒绝所有成员账户中以账户根用户作为主体的操作。要求成员账户的根用 户启用多因素认证（MFA）。要求定期轮换根用户凭证。"},"answer":["B"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Organizations/Governance","Security/IAM","Compute","Cost Optimization"],"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選","research":{"verdict":["B"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"both","explanation_en":"AWS's official guidance for multi-account root-user security is the IAM 'centralized root access management' feature, which integrates with AWS Organizations. Per AWS docs: 'For multiple AWS accounts managed through AWS Organizations, we recommend removing root user credentials from member accounts to help prevent unauthorized use... For more information, see Centrally manage root access for member accounts.' Enabling this feature lets the management account (or a delegated administrator for IAM) delete the root password, access keys, signing certificates, and MFA devices in every member account, and it performs any rare privileged root task (e.g., fixing a bucket policy that locks everyone out) via short-term STS sessions instead of root sign-in — eliminating standing root credentials that could be compromised while requiring no per-account manual work. AWS Organizations also creates new member accounts with no root credentials by default, so a company policy mandating account creation through Organizations preserves that credential-free state going forward with essentially zero ongoing effort. This combination (enable the IAM feature + remove existing root credentials + require Organizations-based account creation) directly matches option B and is AWS's documented best-practice pattern, minimizing both compromise risk (no credentials exist to steal) and management overhead (centralized, not per-account). Option D (SCP deny-all-root + MFA + periodic rotation) is a legitimate secondary control AWS also documents, but it leaves root credentials in place (so they can still be stolen/phished) and adds recurring operational burden (scheduled rotation across every account), failing the 'minimize effort' requirement. Option A (Lambda-based toggling of root) and Option C (attributing this capability to Security Hub CSPM) misstate or overcomplicate the actual AWS mechanism, which lives in IAM/Organizations, not Security Hub.","explanation_zh":"AWS 官方針對多帳戶 root 使用者安全性的建議做法，是 IAM 的「集中管理 root 存取」(centralized root access management) 功能，該功能與 AWS Organizations 整合。根據 AWS 文件：「對於透過 AWS Organizations 管理的多個 AWS 帳戶，我們建議從成員帳戶中移除 root 使用者憑證，以防止未經授權的使用……詳情請參閱『集中管理成員帳戶的 root 存取』。」啟用此功能後，管理帳戶（或 IAM 的委派管理員）可以刪除每個成員帳戶中的 root 密碼、存取金鑰、簽署憑證與 MFA 裝置，並透過短期 STS 工作階段（而非 root 登入）執行極少數需要 root 權限的特殊任務（例如修復鎖死所有人的儲存貯體政策）——這樣就消除了可能被入侵的長期 root 憑證，且不需要逐帳戶手動操作。AWS Organizations 建立的新成員帳戶預設也沒有 root 憑證，因此若公司政策要求一律透過 Organizations 建立新帳戶，就能以幾乎零額外成本持續維持這種「無憑證」狀態。這樣的組合（啟用 IAM 功能＋移除既有 root 憑證＋要求透過 Organizations 建立帳戶）正好對應選項 B，也是 AWS 文件記載的最佳實務模式，同時將「遭入侵風險」（根本沒有憑證可偷）與「管理成本」（集中式而非逐帳戶）降到最低。選項 D（SCP 全面拒絕 root 動作＋MFA＋定期輪換）雖然也是 AWS 文件提到的合法輔助控制，但它仍保留 root 憑證本身（因此仍可能被竊取或釣魚），且需要在每個帳戶上持續執行排程輪換，增加了經常性維運負擔，不符合「最小化管理成本」的要求。選項 A（用 Lambda 切換 root 啟用/停用）與選項 C（把此能力歸於 Security Hub CSPM）則是誤植或過度複雜化了實際機制——這項功能其實位於 IAM／Organizations，而非 Security Hub。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"Building a custom Lambda function to disable/enable root, and periodically re-enabling root for billing or KMS key recovery, reintroduces standing root credentials and requires ongoing custom automation to maintain — higher operational effort and higher compromise risk than using the native centralized root access management feature, which removes credentials entirely and handles rare privileged tasks via temporary sessions without ever re-enabling root sign-in.","why_zh":"自行建置 Lambda 函數來停用/啟用 root，並為了帳單或 KMS 金鑰復原而定期重新啟用 root，等於重新引入常駐的 root 憑證，還需要持續維護自訂自動化——比起原生的集中式 root 存取管理功能（該功能徹底移除憑證，並以臨時工作階段處理罕見的特殊任務、無需重新啟用 root 登入），管理成本與遭入侵風險都更高。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"There is no 'centralized root access management' capability in AWS Security Hub CSPM; that capability is an IAM feature that integrates with AWS Organizations trusted access (id_root-enable-root-access.html), not something configured through Security Hub's CSPM console. This option misattributes the mechanism to the wrong service.","why_zh":"AWS Security Hub CSPM 並沒有「集中管理 root 存取」這項功能；該功能其實是 IAM 與 AWS Organizations 信任存取整合的功能（見 id_root-enable-root-access.html），並非透過 Security Hub 的 CSPM 主控台設定。此選項把機制誤植到錯誤的服務上。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"An SCP denying all actions for the root principal, plus mandatory MFA and scheduled credential rotation, is a documented secondary hardening layer, but it keeps long-term root credentials (password/keys/MFA) alive in every member account — they remain a target for phishing/compromise — and scheduled rotation across all accounts is exactly the kind of recurring manual effort the question asks to minimize, unlike centrally removing credentials once via IAM/Organizations.","why_zh":"以 SCP 拒絕 root 主體的所有動作，並強制 MFA 與排程輪換憑證，雖是文件記載的次要強化層，但這仍讓每個成員帳戶的長期 root 憑證（密碼／金鑰／MFA）繼續存在——依然可能成為釣魚或入侵的目標，而且要在所有帳戶上排程輪換，正是題目要求盡量避免的持續性人工負擔，遠不如透過 IAM／Organizations 一次性集中移除憑證來得省力。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/IAM/latest/UserGuide/id_root-user.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/IAM/latest/UserGuide/id_root-enable-root-access.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/IAM/latest/UserGuide/root-user-best-practices.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/organizations/latest/userguide/services-that-can-integrate-iam.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/organizations/latest/userguide/orgs_best-practices_member-acct.html"]}},{"id":207,"question_en":"A company is using Amazon EC2 instances to host an application in a private subnet in a VPC. The application needs to use AWS KMS. What is the MOST secure way for a security engineer to meet this requirement?","question_zh":"一家公司正在使用 Amazon EC2 实例在 VPC 的私有子网中托管一个应用程序，该应用程序 需要使用 AWS KMS。 安全工程师满足此要求的最安全方法是什么？","options_en":{"A":"Attach an internet gateway to the VPC. Move the EC2 instances to a public subnet. Use the internet gateway to connect to AWS KMS.","B":"Create a gateway VPC endpoint. Use the endpoint to connect to AWS KMS.","C":"Attach a NAT gateway to the VPC. Leave the EC2 instances in the private subnet. Use the NAT gateway to connect to AWS KMS.","D":"Create an interface VPC endpoint. Use the endpoint to connect to AWS KMS."},"options_zh":{"A":"将互联网网关附加到VPC，将EC2实例移至公共子网，并使用该互联网网关连接到AWS KMS。","B":"创建一个网关型VPC端点，并使用该端点连接到AWS KMS。","C":"将 NAT 网关附加到 VPC。将 EC2 实例保留在私有子网中，并使用 NAT 网关连接到 AWS KMS。","D":"创建一个接口型 VPC 终端节点，并使用该终端节点连接到 AWS KMS。"},"answer":["D"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Networking/DNS","Security/IAM","Compute"],"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選","research":{"verdict":["D"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"both","explanation_en":"AWS KMS only supports Amazon VPC private connectivity through an interface VPC endpoint powered by AWS PrivateLink — it does not support gateway VPC endpoints at all (gateway endpoints exist only for Amazon S3 and DynamoDB). An interface endpoint places an Elastic Network Interface with a private IP directly in the subnet, letting EC2 instances in a private subnet call the AWS KMS API entirely within the AWS network, without an internet gateway, NAT device, VPN, or Direct Connect connection and without the instances needing public IP addresses. This is both the most secure (traffic never traverses the public internet, and endpoint policies can restrict access) and the only technically valid option for KMS among the four choices. Options A and C route traffic out to the internet or through a NAT gateway, which is less secure and unnecessary since KMS is a regional AWS service reachable via PrivateLink. Option B is simply invalid because gateway endpoints do not support KMS.","explanation_zh":"AWS KMS 在 VPC 內僅支援透過 AWS PrivateLink 提供的 interface VPC endpoint 進行私有連線，完全不支援 gateway VPC endpoint（gateway endpoint 僅支援 Amazon S3 與 DynamoDB）。Interface endpoint 會在子網路中建立帶有私有 IP 的彈性網路介面（ENI），讓私有子網路中的 EC2 執行個體能在 AWS 網路內部直接呼叫 AWS KMS API，不需要 internet gateway、NAT 裝置、VPN 或 Direct Connect 連線，執行個體也不需要公有 IP。這不僅是四個選項中最安全的做法（流量完全不經過公網，且可用 endpoint policy 限制存取），也是唯一技術上對 KMS 有效的選項。選項 A、C 讓流量經由網際網路或 NAT gateway 路由，較不安全且沒必要，因為 KMS 是可透過 PrivateLink 存取的區域性 AWS 服務。選項 B 直接無效，因為 gateway endpoint 不支援 KMS。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"Attaching an internet gateway and moving instances to a public subnet exposes them to the internet and requires public IP addresses, which is far less secure and unnecessary since KMS is reachable privately via PrivateLink.","why_zh":"附加 internet gateway 並將執行個體搬到公有子網路會讓它們暴露在網際網路上，且需要公有 IP，這遠不如透過 PrivateLink 私下連線安全，也沒有必要。"},{"letter":"B","why_en":"Gateway VPC endpoints only support Amazon S3 and DynamoDB; AWS KMS is not a supported gateway endpoint service, so this option is technically invalid.","why_zh":"Gateway VPC endpoint 只支援 Amazon S3 與 DynamoDB，AWS KMS 並非支援的 gateway endpoint 服務，因此此選項在技術上不成立。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"A NAT gateway lets private-subnet instances reach KMS over the public AWS service endpoint via the internet path, which works but is less secure and less direct than a private interface endpoint that never leaves the AWS network.","why_zh":"NAT gateway 可讓私有子網路的執行個體透過網際網路路徑存取 KMS 的公有服務端點，雖然可行，但不如完全不離開 AWS 網路的私有 interface endpoint 安全與直接。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/kms/latest/developerguide/kms-vpc-endpoint.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/kms/latest/developerguide/vpce-create-endpoint.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/kms/latest/developerguide/vpce-connect.html"]}},{"id":208,"question_en":"A company ' s data scientists want to create artificial intelligence and machine learning (AI/ML) training models by using Amazon SageMaker. The training models will use large datasets in an Amazon S3 bucket. The datasets contain sensitive information. On average, the data scientists need 30 days to train models. The S3 bucket has been secured appropriately. The company ' s data retention policy states that all data that is older than 45 days must be removed from the S3 bucket. Which action should a security engineer take to enforce this data retention policy?","question_zh":"一家公司的数据科学家希望使用 Amazon SageMaker 创建人工智能和机器学习（AI/ML）训练模型。 这些训练模型将使用存储在 Amazon S3 存储桶中的大型数据集，而这些数据集包含敏感信息。 数据科学家平均需要30天来训练模型。S3存储桶已得到妥善保护。公司的数据保留政策规定，所有 超过45天的数据必须从S3存储桶中删除。 安全工程师应采取什么措施来执行此数据保留政策？","options_en":{"A":"Configure an S3 Lifecycle rule on the S3 bucket to delete objects after 45 days.","B":"Create an AWS Lambda function to check the last-modified date of the S3 objects and delete objects that are older than 45 days. Create an S3 event notification to invoke the Lambda function for each PutObject operation.","C":"Create an AWS Lambda function to check the last-modified date of the S3 objects and delete objects that are older than 45 days. Create an Amazon EventBridge rule to invoke the Lambda function each month.","D":"Configure S3 Intelligent-Tiering on the S3 bucket to automatically transition objects to another storage class."},"options_zh":{"A":"在S3存储桶上配置S3生命周期规则，以在45天后删除对象。","B":"创建一个 AWS Lambda 函数，用于检查 S3 对象的最后修改日期，并删除超过 45 天的对象。 创建一个 S3 事件通知，以便在每次执行 PutObject 操作时触发该 Lambda 函数。","C":"创建一个 AWS Lambda 函数，用于检查 S3 对象的最后修改日期，并删除超过 45 天的对象。 创建一个 Amazon EventBridge 规则，每月调用该 Lambda 函数。","D":"在S3存储桶上配置S3智能分层，以自动将对象迁移至其他存储类别。"},"answer":["A"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Storage","Compute","Serverless/Integration"],"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選","research":{"verdict":["A"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"both","explanation_en":"S3 Lifecycle configuration is the native, serverless mechanism purpose-built for this exact use case: automatically deleting (expiring) objects after a specified number of days from an S3 bucket. Configuring an Expiration action with Days=45 requires zero custom code, zero compute infrastructure, and no ongoing maintenance — Amazon S3 itself enforces the retention policy. This directly satisfies the requirement to remove data older than 45 days with the least operational overhead. Option B (Lambda triggered on every PutObject) is inefficient and unnecessary — checking object age on every upload event to decide on deletion of unrelated older objects makes no logical sense and adds needless custom code and invocation costs. Option C (Lambda + monthly EventBridge schedule) reinvents lifecycle expiration with custom code, introduces a maintenance burden, and a monthly cadence is too coarse to reliably enforce a 45-day boundary. Option D (S3 Intelligent-Tiering) only changes storage class for cost optimization based on access patterns — it never deletes objects, so it cannot fulfill a data retention/deletion requirement at all.","explanation_zh":"S3 Lifecycle 設定是 AWS 原生、無伺服器的機制，正是為此情境打造：可自動在物件超過指定天數後刪除（到期）。只要設定 Expiration 動作、Days=45，完全不需自訂程式碼、不需管理運算資源、也不需持續維運——由 Amazon S3 本身強制執行保留政策。這直接滿足「移除超過 45 天資料」且維運負擔最低的需求。選項 B（每次 PutObject 都觸發 Lambda）沒有效率也不合理——在每次上傳事件時去檢查並刪除其他不相關的舊物件毫無邏輯，還增加不必要的自訂程式碼與呼叫成本。選項 C（Lambda + 每月 EventBridge 排程）等於用自訂程式碼重造 Lifecycle 到期機制，增加維運負擔，且每月一次的頻率太粗糙，無法可靠地精準執行 45 天的界線。選項 D（S3 Intelligent-Tiering）僅根據存取模式自動轉換儲存層級以節省成本，從不會刪除物件，因此完全無法滿足資料保留／刪除的需求。","distractors":[{"letter":"B","why_en":"Invoking a Lambda function on every PutObject to scan for and delete unrelated 45-day-old objects is inefficient, illogical (an upload event has no relation to which old objects should be purged), and adds unnecessary custom code and operational overhead compared to native Lifecycle expiration.","why_zh":"在每次 PutObject 時觸發 Lambda 去掃描並刪除其他不相關的 45 天舊物件既沒效率又不合邏輯（上傳事件與該刪除哪些舊物件毫無關聯），相較原生 Lifecycle 到期機制增加了不必要的自訂程式碼與維運負擔。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"This reimplements object-age-based deletion with custom Lambda code and a monthly EventBridge schedule, which duplicates functionality S3 Lifecycle already provides natively, adds maintenance burden, and a monthly check cannot precisely enforce a 45-day cutoff.","why_zh":"此方案用自訂 Lambda 程式碼加上每月一次的 EventBridge 排程來重新實作依物件存留天數刪除的邏輯，這與 S3 Lifecycle 原生已提供的功能重複，增加維護負擔，且每月檢查一次無法精準落實 45 天的界線。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"S3 Intelligent-Tiering automatically moves objects between access tiers to optimize storage cost based on access patterns; it does not delete objects, so it cannot enforce a data retention/removal policy at all.","why_zh":"S3 Intelligent-Tiering 是根據存取模式自動在不同儲存層級間轉換物件以優化成本，並不會刪除物件，因此完全無法用來落實資料保留（刪除）政策。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonS3/latest/userguide/intro-lifecycle-rules.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonS3/latest/userguide/lifecycle-expire-general-considerations.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonS3/latest/userguide/object-lifecycle-mgmt.html"]}},{"id":209,"question_en":"A company recently set up Amazon GuardDuty and is receiving a high number of findings from IP addresses within the company. A security engineer has verified that these IP addresses are trusted and allowed. Which combination of steps should the security engineer take to configure GuardDuty so that it does not produce findings for these IP addresses? (Select TWO.)","question_zh":"一家公司最近启用了 Amazon GuardDuty，但收到了大量来自公司内部 IP 地址的告警信息。安全工程师已确认这些 IP 地址 是可信且被允许的。 安全工程师应采取哪些步骤组合来配置 GuardDuty，使其不对这些 IP 地址生成检测结果？（选择两项。）","options_en":{"A":"Create a plaintext configuration file that contains the trusted IP addresses.","B":"Create a JSON configuration file that contains the trusted IP addresses.","C":"Upload the configuration file directly to GuardDuty.","D":"Upload the configuration file to Amazon S3. Add a new trusted IP list to GuardDuty that points to the file.","E":"Manually copy and paste the configuration file data into the trusted IP list in GuardDuty."},"options_zh":{"A":"创建一个包含可信IP地址的纯文本配置文件。","B":"创建一个包含可信IP地址的JSON配置文件。","C":"直接将配置文件上传到 GuardDuty。","D":"将配置文件上传至 Amazon S3，并在 GuardDuty 中添加一个新的受信任 IP 列表，指向该文件。","E":"手动将配置文件数据复制并粘贴到 GuardDuty 的可信 IP 列表中。"},"answer":["A","D"],"multi":true,"vote":{},"tags":["Security/IAM","Storage"],"difficulty":2,"diff_why":"複選","research":{"verdict":["A","D"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"GuardDuty trusted IP lists (and threat lists) are defined as plain text files containing one IP address or CIDR range per line — not JSON. This file must be uploaded to an Amazon S3 bucket (GuardDuty does not accept a direct upload of the file, nor manual paste of its contents into the console) and then you add a trusted IP list in GuardDuty whose 'Location' field points to that S3 object (accepted formats include s3://bucket.name/file.txt, https://s3.amazonaws.com/bucket.name/file.txt, etc.). The CLI example in AWS docs explicitly uses '--format TXT' when calling create-ip-set with an S3 location. Therefore the correct combination is: create a plaintext file with the trusted IPs (A), then upload it to S3 and add a trusted IP list in GuardDuty pointing to that S3 file (D).","explanation_zh":"GuardDuty 的 trusted IP list（及 threat list）格式規定為純文字檔（plaintext/TXT），每行一個 IP 位址或 CIDR 範圍——並非 JSON 格式。此檔案必須先上傳至 Amazon S3 儲存桶（GuardDuty 不支援直接上傳檔案本身，也不支援手動複製貼上內容到主控台），接著在 GuardDuty 新增一個 trusted IP list，其 Location 欄位指向該 S3 物件（可接受格式如 s3://bucket.name/file.txt、https://s3.amazonaws.com/bucket.name/file.txt 等）。AWS 文件中的 CLI 範例在呼叫 create-ip-set 並指定 S3 位置時明確使用 '--format TXT'。因此正確組合為：建立包含受信任 IP 的純文字設定檔（A），並將其上傳至 S3、在 GuardDuty 新增指向該 S3 檔案的 trusted IP list（D）。","distractors":[{"letter":"B","why_en":"GuardDuty trusted IP lists must be plain text (TXT) files with one IP/CIDR per line, not JSON. GuardDuty's create-ip-set API/console uses format TXT for these lists, so a JSON configuration file is not the supported format.","why_zh":"GuardDuty 的 trusted IP list 必須是純文字（TXT）檔案，每行一個 IP/CIDR，而非 JSON 格式。GuardDuty 的 create-ip-set API／主控台針對此類清單使用 TXT 格式，因此 JSON 設定檔並非支援的格式。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"GuardDuty does not support uploading a configuration file directly into the service; the file must first reside in an S3 bucket, and GuardDuty references it via a location URL (s3:// or https://s3...) rather than accepting a direct file upload.","why_zh":"GuardDuty 不支援將設定檔直接上傳至服務本身；檔案必須先存放於 S3 儲存桶，GuardDuty 透過 Location URL（s3:// 或 https://s3...）參照該檔案，而非接受直接檔案上傳。"},{"letter":"E","why_en":"There is no console option to manually copy/paste IP list contents into GuardDuty. The console 'Location' field only accepts a URL/URI pointing to an S3-hosted object, not inline pasted data.","why_zh":"GuardDuty 主控台並沒有可讓使用者手動複製貼上 IP 清單內容的選項。主控台的 Location 欄位只接受指向 S3 物件的 URL/URI，而非直接貼上的內嵌資料。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/guardduty/latest/ug/guardduty-lists-create-activate.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/guardduty/latest/ug/guardduty-lists-prerequisites.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/guardduty/latest/ug/guardduty_upload-lists.html"]}},{"id":210,"question_en":"A consultant agency needs to perform a security audit for a company ' s production AWS account. Several consultants need access to the account. The consultant agency already has its own AWS account. The company requires multi-factor authentication (MFA) for all access to its production account. The company also forbids the use of long-term credentials. Which solution will provide the consultant agency with access that meets these requirements?","question_zh":"一家咨询公司需要对某企业的生产环境AWS账户进行安全审计。多名顾问需要访问该账户。该咨询公司已拥有自己的AWS 账户。企业要求所有对生产账户的访问都必须启用多因素认证（MFA），并且禁止使用长期凭证。 哪种解决方案能为咨询机构提供满足这些要求的访问权限？","options_en":{"A":"Create an IAM group. Create an IAM user for each consultant. Add each user to the group. Turn on MFA for each consultant.","B":"Configure Amazon Cognito on the company’s production account to authenticate against the consultant agency ' s identity provider (IdP). Add MFA to a Cognito user pool.","C":"Create an IAM role in the consultant agency ' s AWS account. Define a trust policy that requires MFA. In the trust policy, specify the company ' s production account as the principal. Attach the trust policy to the role.","D":"Create an IAM role in the company’s production account. Define a trust policy that requires MFA. In the trust policy, specify the consultant agency ' s AWS account as the principal. Attach the trust policy to the role."},"options_zh":{"A":"创建一个 IAM 组。为每位顾问创建一个 IAM 用户，并将每位用户添加到该组中。为每位顾问启用多因素认证 （MFA）。","B":"在公司的生产账户上配置 Amazon Cognito，以对接咨询机构的身份提供商（IdP）进行身份验证。为 Cognito 用户池添加 多因素认证（MFA）。","C":"在顾问公司的 AWS 账户中创建一个 IAM 角色。定义一个要求使用多因素认证（MFA）的信任策略，在该信任策略中指 定公司生产账户作为主体，并将此信任策略附加到角色上。","D":"在公司的生产账户中创建一个 IAM 角色。定义一个要求使用多因素认证（MFA）的信任策略，在该信任策略中指定顾 问机构的 AWS 账户作为主体，并将此信任策略附加到角色上。"},"answer":["D"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Security/IAM"],"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選","research":{"verdict":["D"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"both","explanation_en":"This is the textbook 'MFA protection for cross-account delegation' pattern from the IAM documentation: to let users from another AWS account (the consultant agency's account) access resources in your account (the company's production account) without long-term credentials, you create an IAM role IN THE ACCOUNT WHOSE RESOURCES ARE BEING ACCESSED (production account), and its trust policy names the OTHER account (consultant agency) as the Principal, with a Condition requiring aws:MultiFactorAuthPresent = true. Consultants then call sts:AssumeRole from their own account's IAM users (who authenticate with MFA) to obtain short-lived temporary credentials scoped to the production account role — satisfying both the MFA requirement and the no-long-term-credentials requirement. Option C has the trust relationship backwards: a role created in the consultant agency's own account with the production account as principal would let the PRODUCTION account's principals assume a role in the CONSULTANTS' account — the opposite of what's needed, and it grants the consultants no access to production resources at all. Option A uses IAM users with long-term access keys/passwords, which the company explicitly forbids. Option B (Cognito) is designed for authenticating end users of consumer/web/mobile apps into federated identity pools, not for auditors/administrators needing temporary, role-based AWS API/console access to a production account — it's the wrong tool and adds unnecessary complexity for this cross-account human-access use case.","explanation_zh":"這是 IAM 文件中「MFA protection for cross-account delegation」的標準範式：若要讓另一個 AWS 帳戶（顧問公司帳戶）的使用者存取你帳戶（公司正式環境帳戶）中的資源、且不使用長期憑證，你必須在『資源所在的帳戶』(正式環境帳戶) 中建立 IAM 角色，其信任政策 (trust policy) 將『對方帳戶』(顧問公司) 指定為 Principal，並加上要求 aws:MultiFactorAuthPresent = true 的 Condition。顧問接著從他們自己帳戶內、已用 MFA 驗證的 IAM 使用者呼叫 sts:AssumeRole，取得僅適用於正式環境角色的短期臨時憑證——同時滿足 MFA 要求與『禁止長期憑證』要求。選項 C 的信任關係方向相反：在顧問公司自己的帳戶中建立角色、並將正式環境帳戶指定為 Principal，這會變成讓『正式環境帳戶』的主體去 assume『顧問公司帳戶』裡的角色，完全不是需要的方向，也無法讓顧問存取正式環境資源。選項 A 使用 IAM 使用者搭配長期存取金鑰/密碼，正是公司明文禁止的做法。選項 B（Cognito）是設計給消費者/網頁/行動應用程式的終端使用者身分聯合驗證，並不適合稽核人員/管理員需要對正式環境帳戶進行臨時、以角色為基礎的 AWS API/主控台存取的情境——對此跨帳戶人員存取用例而言是錯誤工具且徒增複雜度。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"Creates IAM users with long-term credentials (passwords/access keys) in the production account for each consultant, directly violating the company's explicit ban on long-term credentials, even though MFA can be added to IAM users.","why_zh":"在正式環境帳戶中為每位顧問建立帶有長期憑證（密碼/存取金鑰）的 IAM 使用者，即使能加上 MFA，仍直接違反公司明文禁止長期憑證的規定。"},{"letter":"B","why_en":"Amazon Cognito user pools/identity pools are built for authenticating end users of applications and vending temporary AWS credentials to them via identity pools; it is not the standard or appropriate mechanism for granting an external partner organization's staff role-based administrative/audit access to a production AWS account, and adds unneeded complexity versus a direct cross-account IAM role.","why_zh":"Amazon Cognito 使用者集區/身分集區是為應用程式終端使用者驗證身分、並透過身分集區發放臨時 AWS 憑證而設計；並非授予外部夥伴組織員工對正式環境帳戶進行角色型管理/稽核存取的標準或合適機制，相較直接的跨帳戶 IAM 角色徒增不必要的複雜度。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"Puts the role and trust policy in the wrong account: a role created in the consultant agency's account with the production account as principal would allow the production account to assume a role in the consultants' account, not the reverse — it does not grant consultants any access to the production account's resources.","why_zh":"角色與信任政策放錯帳戶：在顧問公司帳戶中建立角色、以正式環境帳戶作為 Principal，會變成允許正式環境帳戶去 assume 顧問公司帳戶裡的角色，而非相反方向——這完全無法讓顧問取得正式環境帳戶資源的存取權。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/IAM/latest/UserGuide/id_credentials_mfa_configure-api-require.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/IAM/latest/UserGuide/id_roles_common-scenarios_aws-accounts.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/IAM/latest/UserGuide/id_roles_create_policy-examples.html"]}},{"id":211,"question_en":"A company runs an online game on AWS. When players sign up for the game, their username and password credentials are stored in an Amazon Aurora database. The number of users has grown to hundreds of thousands of players. The number of requests for password resets and login assistance has become a burden for the company ' s customer service team. The company needs to implement a solution to give players another way to log in to the game. The solution must remove the burden of password resets and login assistance while securely protecting each player ' s credentials. Which solution will meet these requirements?","question_zh":"一家公司在 AWS 上运行一款在线游戏。当玩家注册游戏时，其用户名和密码凭据将存储在 Amazon Aurora 数据库中。 用户数量已增长至数十万玩家，密码重置和登录帮助的请求量给公司的客户服务团队带来了沉重负担。 公司需要实施一项解决方案，为玩家提供另一种登录游戏的方式。该方案必须在安全保护每位玩家账户信息的同时，免除密 码重置和登录协助带来的负担。 哪种解决方案能满足这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"When a new player signs up, use an AWS Lambda function to automatically create an IAM access key and a secret access key.","B":"Migrate the player credentials from the Aurora database to AWS Secrets Manager.","C":"Configure Amazon Cognito user pools to federate access to the game with third-party identity providers (IdPs), such as social IdPs. Migrate the game ' s authentication mechanism to Cognito.","D":"Issue API keys to new and existing players and use Amazon API Gateway for authentication."},"options_zh":{"A":"当新玩家注册时，使用 AWS Lambda 函数自动生成 IAM 访问密钥和秘密访问密钥。","B":"将玩家凭据从 Aurora 数据库迁移至 AWS Secrets Manager。","C":"配置 Amazon Cognito 用户池，通过第三方身份提供商（IdP），例如社交 IdP，实现游戏的联合访问。将游戏的身份验证 机制迁移至 Cognito。","D":"为新老玩家发放API密钥，并使用Amazon API Gateway进行身份验证。"},"answer":["C"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Migration","Security/IAM","Compute","Database","Serverless/Integration"],"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選","research":{"verdict":["C"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"C is correct. The company's core problem is that it self-manages username/password credentials in its own Aurora database, and the resulting password-reset and login-assistance load has become an operational burden at scale. Amazon Cognito user pools are purpose-built to solve exactly this: per AWS documentation, 'Your app users can either sign in directly through a user pool, or they can federate through a third-party identity provider (IdP). The user pool manages the overhead of handling the tokens that are returned from social sign-in through Facebook, Google, Amazon, and Apple, and from OpenID Connect (OIDC) and SAML IdPs' (Cognito Developer Guide, cognito-user-pools-identity-federation.html). By federating to social/third-party IdPs, the game offloads authentication, password recovery, and account management to identity providers players already use and trust (Google, Facebook/Meta, Apple, Amazon, etc.), which eliminates the flood of first-party password-reset tickets. For players who still authenticate natively in the user pool, Cognito itself securely stores and hashes credentials (never storing plaintext passwords) rather than the company managing raw credentials in Aurora, satisfying 'securely protecting each player's credentials.' This is the standard, AWS-recommended architecture for consumer-facing (CIAM) authentication at scale, unlike the other three options, none of which are designed as end-user authentication/identity systems.","explanation_zh":"答案為 C。這家公司的核心問題是自行在 Aurora 資料庫中管理帳號密碼憑證,導致大規模下密碼重設與登入協助的維運負擔過重。Amazon Cognito user pools 正是為解決此問題而設計:根據 AWS 官方文件,「您的應用程式使用者可以直接透過 user pool 登入,或是透過第三方身分提供者 (IdP) 進行聯合登入。User pool 會處理來自 Facebook、Google、Amazon、Apple 的社群登入,以及 OpenID Connect (OIDC) 與 SAML IdP 所回傳權杖的所有繁瑣工作」(Cognito Developer Guide, cognito-user-pools-identity-federation.html)。透過聯合至社群/第三方 IdP,遊戲可將驗證、密碼救援與帳號管理work外包給玩家原本就在使用且信任的身分提供者(Google、Facebook/Meta、Apple、Amazon 等),進而消除大量第一方密碼重設請求。對於仍在 user pool 中原生驗證的玩家,Cognito 本身會安全地儲存並雜湊憑證(絕不儲存明文密碼),而非由公司在 Aurora 中管理原始憑證,滿足「安全保護每位玩家憑證」的要求。這是 AWS 官方推薦、針對大規模消費者導向(CIAM)驗證的標準架構,其餘三個選項均非為終端使用者驗證/身分系統而設計。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"IAM users and access keys are designed for programmatic/API access to AWS resources by administrators, developers, or workloads — not as a consumer-facing login mechanism for hundreds of thousands of game players. AWS explicitly discourages creating IAM users at scale for end-user identity; IAM has account-level user limits, no built-in social login or self-service password recovery UX for consumers, and issuing long-lived AWS credentials to every player is a severe security anti-pattern (players would gain direct AWS credentials, not just game-login credentials).","why_zh":"IAM user 與存取金鑰是設計給管理員、開發者或工作負載用來對 AWS 資源進行程式化/API 存取,並非設計給數十萬名遊戲玩家使用的消費者登入機制。AWS 明確不建議為終端使用者身分大規模建立 IAM user;IAM 有帳戶層級的使用者數量限制,也沒有內建的社群登入或消費者自助密碼救援介面,且對每位玩家發放長期有效的 AWS 憑證是嚴重的安全反模式(玩家將取得的是直接的 AWS 憑證,而非單純的遊戲登入憑證)。"},{"letter":"B","why_en":"AWS Secrets Manager is designed to store, encrypt, and automatically rotate application/infrastructure secrets such as database credentials, API keys, and OAuth tokens — it is not a consumer identity or authentication service. It has no sign-in API, no MFA, no social-IdP federation, and no self-service password-reset flow for end users, so migrating player credentials there does nothing to reduce the customer service team's password-reset/login-assistance burden.","why_zh":"AWS Secrets Manager 是設計用來儲存、加密並自動輪換應用程式/基礎架構機密(例如資料庫憑證、API 金鑰、OAuth 權杖),並非消費者身分或驗證服務。它沒有登入 API、沒有 MFA、沒有社群 IdP 聯合登入,也沒有終端使用者的自助密碼重設流程,因此將玩家憑證遷移至此完全無法減輕客服團隊的密碼重設/登入協助負擔。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"API keys in Amazon API Gateway are intended to identify and throttle API clients under usage plans (e.g., for metering third-party developers calling an API) — they are not a user authentication mechanism and provide no identity assurance, MFA, or self-service credential recovery for individual human players. Distributing static API keys to hundreds of thousands of consumers as a 'login' method is both insecure (keys are easily leaked/shared) and does not solve password-reset support burden, since API keys still need to be issued, rotated, and recovered by the company itself.","why_zh":"Amazon API Gateway 的 API 金鑰是用來在使用量方案下識別與節流 API 呼叫者(例如計量第三方開發者呼叫 API 的次數),並非使用者驗證機制,對個別玩家也無法提供身分保證、MFA 或自助憑證救援。將靜態 API 金鑰發放給數十萬名消費者作為『登入』方式,既不安全(金鑰容易外洩或被共用),也無法解決密碼重設的客服負擔問題,因為 API 金鑰仍需由公司自行核發、輪換與救援。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/cognito/latest/developerguide/cognito-user-pools-identity-federation.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/cognito/latest/developerguide/cognito-user-pools-identity-provider.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/cognito/latest/developerguide/cognito-user-pools-social-idp.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/cognito/latest/developerguide/cognito-scenarios.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/IAM/latest/UserGuide/id_users.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/secretsmanager/latest/userguide/intro.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/apigateway/latest/developerguide/api-gateway-api-usage-plans.html"]}},{"id":212,"question_en":"A company needs to deploy AWS CloudFormation templates that configure sensitive database credentials.The company already uses AWS Key Management Service (AWS KMS) and AWS Secrets Manager. Which solution will meet the requirements?","question_zh":"一家公司需要部署 AWS CloudFormation 模板来配置敏感的数据库凭据。该公司已使用 AWS 密钥管理服务（AWS KMS） 和 AWS Secrets Manager。 哪种方案能满足要求？","options_en":{"A":"Use a dynamic reference in the CloudFormation template to reference the database credentials in Secrets Manager.","B":"Use encrypted parameters in the CloudFormation template.","C":"Use SecureString parameters to reference Secrets Manager.","D":"Use SecureString parameters encrypted by AWS KMS."},"options_zh":{"A":"在 CloudFormation 模板中使用动态引用，以引用 Secrets Manager 中的数据库凭据。","B":"在 CloudFormation 模板中使用加密参数。","C":"使用 SecureString 参数来引用 Secrets Manager。","D":"使用由 AWS KMS 加密的 SecureString 参数。"},"answer":["A"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Security/IAM","Database","Monitoring/Ops"],"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選","research":{"verdict":["A"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"community","explanation_en":"AWS CloudFormation's documented mechanism for referencing sensitive values held in Secrets Manager (or SSM Parameter Store) without embedding them in the template is the dynamic reference, using the pattern {{resolve:secretsmanager:secret-id:SecretString:json-key:version-stage:version-id}}. The AWS CloudFormation User Guide's 'Get values stored in other services using dynamic references' page states this is exactly how to 'decouple sensitive information from your infrastructure-as-code templates' and specifically documents 'Get a secret or secret value from Secrets Manager' as a supported dynamic-reference pattern. Critically, CloudFormation template Parameters do NOT support a 'SecureString' type at all — AWS's own CloudFormation-supplied parameter types documentation explicitly lists 'SecureString' as an Unsupported Systems Manager parameter type for template parameter definitions, which directly eliminates options C and D. There is also no CloudFormation feature called 'encrypted parameters' (option B) — CloudFormation only offers the NoEcho attribute (which merely masks console/CLI display, providing no actual encryption or Secrets Manager integration) and dynamic references for true secret retrieval. Since the company already uses both KMS (for encryption at rest of the secret) and Secrets Manager (to store the credentials), the dynamic reference in option A is the only mechanism that actually retrieves the KMS-encrypted secret from Secrets Manager at deploy/update time without ever exposing plaintext in the template or CloudFormation console/CLI output.","explanation_zh":"AWS CloudFormation 官方記載的機制，用來在不將機密值直接寫入範本的情況下參照存放在 Secrets Manager（或 SSM Parameter Store）中的敏感值，就是動態參照 (dynamic reference)，語法為 {{resolve:secretsmanager:secret-id:SecretString:json-key:version-stage:version-id}}。AWS CloudFormation 使用者指南「Get values stored in other services using dynamic references」頁面明確指出，這正是用來『將敏感資訊與基礎架構即程式碼範本解耦』的方法，並特別記載「Get a secret or secret value from Secrets Manager」為受支援的動態參照模式。關鍵是，CloudFormation 範本的 Parameters 根本不支援「SecureString」型別——AWS 官方的 CloudFormation-supplied parameter types 文件明文將「SecureString」列為範本參數定義中『不支援』的 Systems Manager 參數型別，這直接排除了選項 C 與 D。CloudFormation 也沒有所謂「encrypted parameters（加密參數）」這種功能（選項 B）——CloudFormation 只提供 NoEcho 屬性（僅遮蔽主控台/CLI 顯示，並非真正加密，也不與 Secrets Manager 整合）以及動態參照這種真正能取得機密值的方式。由於該公司已同時使用 KMS（用於加密靜態機密）與 Secrets Manager（用於儲存憑證），選項 A 的動態參照是唯一能在部署/更新時實際從 Secrets Manager 取出經 KMS 加密的機密值、且從不在範本或 CloudFormation 主控台/CLI 輸出中洩漏明文的機制。","distractors":[{"letter":"B","why_en":"CloudFormation has no feature literally called 'encrypted parameters.' The closest built-in mechanism is the NoEcho attribute on a template Parameter, which only masks the value from being displayed in the console, CLI describe-stacks output, and logs — it does not encrypt the value, does not integrate with Secrets Manager, and the plaintext value is still passed into and stored as part of the template/parameter values, unlike a dynamic reference which retrieves the value directly from Secrets Manager at runtime.","why_zh":"CloudFormation 並沒有字面上稱為「encrypted parameters」的功能。最接近的內建機制是範本 Parameter 上的 NoEcho 屬性，但它只是讓該值在主控台、CLI 的 describe-stacks 輸出與日誌中被遮蔽顯示——並不會加密該值，也不會與 Secrets Manager 整合，且明文值仍會被傳入並儲存為範本/參數值的一部分，不像動態參照是在執行時直接從 Secrets Manager 取值。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"There is no 'SecureString' CloudFormation parameter type that references Secrets Manager. SecureString is an SSM Parameter Store parameter type, and AWS's own CloudFormation-supplied parameter types documentation explicitly lists SecureString under 'Unsupported Systems Manager parameter types' for CloudFormation template parameter definitions — CloudFormation cannot resolve a SecureString value as a template parameter at all, let alone one 'referencing Secrets Manager,' which SecureString parameters have no relationship to.","why_zh":"並不存在會參照 Secrets Manager 的「SecureString」CloudFormation 參數型別。SecureString 是 SSM Parameter Store 的參數型別，而 AWS 官方的 CloudFormation-supplied parameter types 文件明確將 SecureString 列在「Unsupported Systems Manager parameter types」之下，代表 CloudFormation 範本參數定義根本無法解析 SecureString 值——更遑論它本來就與 Secrets Manager 毫無關聯。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"Same root problem as C: CloudFormation template Parameters do not support a SecureString type under any circumstances, regardless of which KMS key would supposedly encrypt it — this is explicitly documented as an unsupported Systems Manager parameter type in CloudFormation templates, so this option describes a capability that does not exist.","why_zh":"與選項 C 問題相同：無論宣稱由哪一把 KMS 金鑰加密，CloudFormation 範本 Parameters 在任何情況下都不支援 SecureString 型別——這在文件中被明確列為 CloudFormation 範本中不支援的 Systems Manager 參數型別，因此此選項描述的是一個並不存在的能力。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AWSCloudFormation/latest/UserGuide/dynamic-references.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AWSCloudFormation/latest/UserGuide/dynamic-references-secretsmanager.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/secretsmanager/latest/userguide/cfn-example_reference-secret.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AWSCloudFormation/latest/UserGuide/cloudformation-supplied-parameter-types.html"]}},{"id":213,"question_en":"A company is expanding its group of stores. On the day that each new store opens, the company wants to launch a customized web application for that store. Each store's application will have a non-production environment and a production environment. Each environment will be deployed in a separate AWS account. The company uses AWS Organizations and has an OU that is used only for these accounts. The company distributes most of the development work to third-party development teams. A security engineer needs to ensure that each team follows the company's deployment plan for AWS resources. The security engineer also must limit access to the deployment plan to only the developers who need access. The security engineer already has created an AWS CloudFormation template that implements the deployment plan. What should the security engineer do next to meet the requirements in the MOST secure way?","question_zh":"一家公司正在扩展其门店网络。每当新店开业时，公司希望为该门店推出一个定制的网络应用程序。每个门店的应用程序 都将包含一个非生产环境和一个生产环境，且每个环境都部署在独立的AWS账户中。该公司使用AWS Organizations，并设 有一个仅用于这些账户的组织单元（OU）。 该公司将大部分开发工作分配给第三方开发团队。安全工程师需要确保每个团队都遵循公司针对AWS资源的部署计划，同时 必须将部署计划的访问权限限制在仅需访问的开发人员范围内。安全工程师已创建了一个实现该部署计划的AWS CloudFormation模板。 安全工程师接下来应采取什么措施，才能以最安全的方式满足要求？","options_en":{"A":"Create an AWS Service Catalog portfolio in the organization's management account. Upload the CloudFormation template. Add the template to the portfolio's product list. Share the portfolio with the OU.","B":"Use the CloudFormation CLI to create a module from the CloudFormation template. Register the module as a private extension in the CloudFormation registry. Publish the extension. In the OU, create an SCP that allows access to the extension.","C":"Create an AWS Service Catalog portfolio in the organization's management account. Upload the CloudFormation template. Add the template to the portfolio's product list. Create an IAM role that has a trust policy that allows cross-account access to the portfolio for users in the OU accounts. Attach the AWSServiceCatalogEndUserFullAccess managed policy to the role.","D":"Use the CloudFormation CLI to create a module from the CloudFormation template. Register the module as a private extension in the CloudFormation registry. Publish the extension. Share the extension with the OU."},"options_zh":{"A":"在组织的管理账户中创建一个 AWS 服务目录组合，上传 CloudFormation 模板，将模板添加到组合的产品列表中，并 与 OU 共享该组合。","B":"使用 CloudFormation CLI 从 CloudFormation 模板创建模块。将该模块注册为 CloudFormation 注册表中的私有扩展， 然后发布该扩展。在组织单元（OU）中创建一个 SCP，以允许访问该扩展。","C":"在组织的管理账户中创建一个 AWS 服务目录组合，上传 CloudFormation 模板，并将该模板添加到组合的产品列表中。 创建一个 IAM 角色，其信任策略允许 OU 账户中的用户跨账户访问该组合。将 AWSServiceCatalogEndUserFullAcces s 管理策略附加到该角色。","D":"使用 CloudFormation CLI 从 CloudFormation 模板创建模块。将该模块注册为 CloudFormation 注册表中的私有扩 展。发布该扩展，并与组织单元（OU）共享。"},"answer":["A"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Organizations/Governance","Security/IAM","Monitoring/Ops"],"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選","research":{"verdict":["A"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"AWS Service Catalog is purpose-built for this exact scenario: centrally governing which CloudFormation templates ('products') third parties are allowed to deploy, while controlling who can launch them. The security engineer should create a portfolio in the management account, add the vetted CloudFormation template as a product, and share the portfolio with the OU using Service Catalog's native AWS Organizations integration (enable-aws-organizations-access + create-portfolio-share to an organization node/OU). This distributes the approved template to every account in the OU without manually copying portfolio IDs, and each account's administrators then use associate-principal-with-portfolio to grant only the specific developer IAM principals access to launch products — satisfying both 'follow the deployment plan' and 'limit access to only developers who need it.' Option C performs the same portfolio setup but then attaches the broad AWSServiceCatalogEndUserFullAccess managed policy to a single role with a cross-account trust policy for 'users in the OU accounts' — this is both non-standard (Service Catalog's documented access model is per-account principal association, not a shared cross-account role) and less secure, since it grants sweeping Service Catalog end-user rights to anyone who can assume that one role, rather than scoping access to specific developers. Options B and D repurpose CloudFormation modules/private extensions, which are reusable resource-type building blocks meant to be referenced inside other templates, not a governed self-service deployment mechanism; private extensions must be manually re-registered via register-type in every receiving account after being shared via RAM, offering no equivalent to Service Catalog's constraints, versioning, and principal-based access control. Hence A is the most secure and AWS-idiomatic choice.","explanation_zh":"AWS Service Catalog 正是為此情境設計:集中治理允許第三方部署哪些 CloudFormation 範本(『產品』),同時控制誰能啟動它們。安全工程師應在管理帳戶建立 portfolio、將已審核的 CloudFormation 範本加入產品清單,並利用 Service Catalog 原生的 AWS Organizations 整合(啟用 trusted access 後對組織節點/OU 執行 create-portfolio-share)將 portfolio 分享給該 OU。這樣可將核准的範本自動分發到 OU 內所有帳戶,而不需手動複製 portfolio ID;之後各帳戶管理員再用 associate-principal-with-portfolio,只把啟動產品的權限授予特定的開發者 IAM 主體——同時滿足『遵循部署計畫』與『僅限需要存取的開發者』兩項需求。選項 C 雖然也建立了相同的 portfolio,卻額外把範圍很廣的 AWSServiceCatalogEndUserFullAccess 受管政策,附加到一個對『OU 內帳戶的使用者』設有跨帳戶信任政策的單一角色上——這既不符合 Service Catalog 文件所述『以帳戶為單位做主體關聯』的存取模型,也較不安全,因為任何能夠 assume 該角色的人都會取得廣泛的 Service Catalog 終端使用者權限,而非侷限於特定開發者。選項 B、D 則是挪用 CloudFormation 模組/私有擴充功能,這類功能是設計給其他範本內部參照的可重複使用資源類型建構區塊,並非治理型自助部署機制;私有擴充功能透過 RAM 分享後,接收端的每個帳戶都得手動以 register-type 重新註冊,也沒有等同於 Service Catalog 的限制條件、版本控管與以主體為基礎的存取控制。因此 A 是最安全且最符合 AWS 慣例的做法。","distractors":[{"letter":"B","why_en":"CloudFormation modules are reusable resource-type fragments meant to be referenced inside other templates during authoring, not a self-service catalog mechanism for end users to launch full application stacks; SCPs also cannot 'allow access to' a CloudFormation extension — that is not how extension permissions or SCPs work.","why_zh":"CloudFormation 模組是設計給撰寫範本時內部參照的可重複使用資源片段,並非讓終端使用者啟動完整應用程式堆疊的自助式目錄機制;而且 SCP 本來就無法用來『允許存取』一個 CloudFormation extension,這不符合 extension 權限或 SCP 的運作方式。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"Attaching the broad AWSServiceCatalogEndUserFullAccess managed policy to one cross-account role that trusts users across the entire OU grants far more access than needed and abandons Service Catalog's intended per-principal, per-account access control (associate-principal-with-portfolio), making it less secure than option A.","why_zh":"把範圍很廣的 AWSServiceCatalogEndUserFullAccess 受管政策,附加到一個信任整個 OU 使用者的跨帳戶角色上,授予的權限遠超所需,也放棄了 Service Catalog 原本以帳戶為單位、以主體為基礎的存取控管機制(associate-principal-with-portfolio),因此比選項 A 更不安全。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"Private CloudFormation extensions are shared via AWS RAM to specific accounts and must be manually re-registered with register-type in each receiving account/region; there is no native 'share the extension with the OU' governance workflow equivalent to Service Catalog portfolio sharing, and modules are not the right artifact for distributing a full governed deployment plan to end users.","why_zh":"私有 CloudFormation extension 是透過 AWS RAM 分享給特定帳戶,接收端的每個帳戶/地區都必須手動以 register-type 重新註冊;並不存在等同於 Service Catalog portfolio 分享、原生『把 extension 分享給 OU』的治理流程,而且模組本來就不是用來向終端使用者分發完整治理型部署計畫的合適產物。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/organizations/latest/userguide/services-that-can-integrate-servicecatalog.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/servicecatalog/latest/adminguide/introduction.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/cli/latest/userguide/cli_service-catalog_code_examples.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AWSCloudFormation/latest/UserGuide/registry-register-private-extension.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AWSCloudFormation/latest/UserGuide/modules-using.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AWSCloudFormation/latest/UserGuide/registry-private.html"]}},{"id":214,"question_en":"A security engineer needs to build a solution to turn AWS CloudTrail back on in multiple AWS Regions in case it is ever turned off. What is the MOST efficient way to implement this solution?","question_zh":"安全工程师需要构建一个解决方案，以便在AWS CloudTrail被关闭的情况下，能够将其在多个AWS区域中重新启用。 实现此解决方案的最有效方法是什么？","options_en":{"A":"Use AWS Config with a managed rule to initiate the AWS-EnableCloudTrail remediation.","B":"Create an Amazon EventBridge event with a cloudtrail.amazonaws.com event source and a StartLogging event name to invoke an AWS Lambda function to call the StartLogging API.","C":"Create an Amazon CloudWatch alarm with a cloudtrail.amazonaws.com event source and a StopLogging event name to invoke an AWS Lambda function to call the StartLogging API.","D":"Monitor AWS Trusted Advisor to ensure CloudTrail logging is enabled."},"options_zh":{"A":"使用 AWS Config 配合托管规则来启动 AWS-EnableCloudTrail 的修复操作。","B":"创建一个 Amazon EventBridge 事件，使用 cloudtrail.amazonaws.com 作为事件源，并设置事件名称为 StartLogging，以触发 AWS Lambda 函数调用 StartLogging API。","C":"创建一个 Amazon CloudWatch 警报，使用 cloudtrail.amazonaws.com 作为事件源，并设置事件名称为 StopLogging，以触发 AWS Lambda 函数调用 StartLogging API。","D":"监控 AWS Trusted Advisor，确保已启用 CloudTrail 日志记录。"},"answer":["A"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Organizations/Governance","Compute","Serverless/Integration","Monitoring/Ops"],"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選","research":{"verdict":["A"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"AWS Config has a managed rule, cloudtrail-enabled (identifier CLOUD_TRAIL_ENABLED), that periodically checks whether a CloudTrail trail is enabled and marks the resource NON_COMPLIANT if it is not. AWS provides a purpose-built Systems Manager Automation runbook, AWS-EnableCloudTrail, that AWS Config's remediation feature can invoke automatically whenever the rule goes non-compliant — no custom code to write, test, or maintain. This is the officially documented, fully managed pattern for auto-remediating a disabled trail and can be rolled out to every Region (or centrally via an AWS Config aggregator/conformance pack across an organization), which is what makes it the MOST efficient option. Option B is invalid as written: it wires the EventBridge rule to the StartLogging event name, so it would fire only after logging is already restarted, never on the actual StopLogging incident it's supposed to catch — plus it requires you to build and operate a custom Lambda function. Option C compounds two errors: CloudWatch alarms are threshold-based metric alarms, not event-pattern matchers, so a 'CloudWatch alarm with a cloudtrail.amazonaws.com event source' is not a real, valid construct — event source/event name matching is an EventBridge (CloudWatch Events) concept, not a CloudWatch alarm concept — and it too needs custom Lambda code. Option D is purely observational: AWS Trusted Advisor can flag that CloudTrail logging is disabled but has no remediation action, requires manual intervention, and several relevant checks require a Business or Enterprise support plan. Therefore A is the correct, most efficient, fully-managed solution.","explanation_zh":"AWS Config 有一個受管規則 cloudtrail-enabled(識別碼 CLOUD_TRAIL_ENABLED),會定期檢查是否已啟用 CloudTrail 追蹤軌跡,若未啟用則標記為 NON_COMPLIANT。AWS 提供專門設計的 Systems Manager Automation 文件 AWS-EnableCloudTrail,可由 AWS Config 的自動修復(remediation)功能在規則變成不合規時自動呼叫——不需要撰寫、測試或維護任何自訂程式碼。這是官方文件記載、完全託管的自動修復模式,可以部署到每個 Region(或透過 AWS Config aggregator/conformance pack 在整個組織中集中部署),這正是它成為「最有效率」選項的原因。選項 B 就其描述而言是無效的:它把 EventBridge 規則綁定在 StartLogging 這個事件名稱上,這樣只會在記錄已經被重新啟動之後才觸發,永遠不會捕捉到它原本應該偵測的 StopLogging 事件——而且還需要自行建置與維運一個 Lambda 函式。選項 C 犯了兩個錯誤:CloudWatch 警示(alarm)是基於指標門檻值的機制,並不是事件模式比對機制,所以「帶有 cloudtrail.amazonaws.com 事件來源的 CloudWatch alarm」根本不是一個有效的架構——事件來源/事件名稱比對是 EventBridge(CloudWatch Events)的概念,不是 CloudWatch alarm 的概念——而且同樣需要自訂 Lambda 程式碼。選項 D 純粹只是觀察性質:AWS Trusted Advisor 可以標示 CloudTrail 記錄功能已停用,但沒有自動修復動作,需要人工介入,而且部分相關檢查項目需要 Business 或 Enterprise 支援方案才能使用。因此 A 是正確且最有效率的完全託管解決方案。","distractors":[{"letter":"B","why_en":"As literally described it listens for the StartLogging event name, so it would trigger after logging resumes rather than when CloudTrail is stopped, and it still requires writing/operating a custom Lambda function instead of using a managed remediation.","why_zh":"就字面描述而言,它監聽的是 StartLogging 事件名稱,因此只會在記錄恢復後才觸發,而不是在 CloudTrail 被停止時觸發;而且仍需自行撰寫並維運 Lambda 函式,而非使用受管的自動修復機制。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"CloudWatch alarms are metric-threshold based and cannot match an 'event source'/'event name' like cloudtrail.amazonaws.com StopLogging — that is an EventBridge event-pattern concept, so the described architecture is not technically valid; it also requires custom Lambda code.","why_zh":"CloudWatch alarm 是基於指標門檻值,無法比對像 cloudtrail.amazonaws.com StopLogging 這樣的「事件來源/事件名稱」——那是 EventBridge 事件模式的概念,所以此描述的架構在技術上並不成立;而且同樣需要自訂 Lambda 程式碼。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"Trusted Advisor only monitors and alerts; it has no built-in remediation action to turn CloudTrail back on, requiring manual follow-up, and relevant checks require Business/Enterprise support.","why_zh":"Trusted Advisor 只能監控與發出警示;它沒有內建的修復動作能重新開啟 CloudTrail,需要人工後續處理,且相關檢查項目需要 Business 或 Enterprise 支援方案。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/config/latest/developerguide/cloudtrail-enabled.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/systems-manager-automation-runbooks/latest/userguide/automation-aws-enablecloudtrail.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/config/latest/developerguide/remediation.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/awscloudtrail/latest/userguide/cloudtrail-concepts.html"]}},{"id":215,"question_en":"A company is developing an application that runs across a combination of Amazon EC2 On-Demand Instances and Spot Instances. A security engineer needs to provide a logging solution that makes logs for all instances available from a single location. The solution must allow only a specific set of users to analyze the logs for events patterns. The users must be able to use SQL queries on the logs to perform root cause analysis. Which solution will meet these requirements?","question_zh":"一家公司正在开发一个应用程序，该应用将运行在Amazon EC2按需实例和竞价实例的组合上。安全 工程师需要提供一种日志解决方案，使所有实例的日志都能在一个位置集中访问。该方案必须仅允许 特定的一组用户分析日志中的事件模式，并且这些用户应能够使用SQL查询对日志进行根因分析。 哪种解决方案能满足这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Configure the EC2 instances to send application logs to a single Amazon CloudWatch Logs log group. Allow only specific users to access the log group. Use CloudWatch Logs Insights to query the log group.","B":"Configure the EC2 instances to send application logs to a single Amazon S3 bucket. Allow only specific users to access the S3 bucket. Use Amazon CloudWatch Logs Insights to query the log files in the S3 bucket.","C":"Configure each EC2 instance to send its application logs to its own specific Amazon CloudWatch Logs log group. Allow only specific users to access the log groups. Use Amazon Athena to query all the log groups.","D":"Configure the EC2 instances to send application logs to a single Amazon CloudWatch Logs log group. Grant Amazon Detective access to the log group. Allow only specific users to use Detective to query the log group."},"options_zh":{"A":"配置 EC2 实例将应用程序日志发送到一个 Amazon CloudWatch Logs 日志组，并仅允许特定用 户访问该日志组。使用 CloudWatch Logs Insights 查询该日志组。","B":"配置 EC2 实例将应用程序日志发送到一个 Amazon S3 存储桶，并仅允许特定用户访问该 S3 存 储桶。使用 Amazon CloudWatch Logs Insights 查询存储桶中的日志文件。","C":"配置每个EC2实例将其应用程序日志发送到各自独立的Amazon CloudWatch Logs日志组，并仅 允许特定用户访问这些日志组。使用Amazon Athena查询所有日志组。","D":"配置 EC2 实例将应用程序日志发送到一个 Amazon CloudWatch Logs 日志组。授予 Amazon Detective 访问该日志组的权限，并仅允许特定用户使用 Detective 查询该日志组。"},"answer":["A"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Storage","Compute","Monitoring/Ops","Analytics"],"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選","research":{"verdict":["A"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"Option A is correct. The requirement has three parts: (1) a single, centralized location for logs from a heterogeneous fleet of On-Demand and Spot EC2 instances, (2) access restricted to a specific set of users, and (3) SQL-style querying for root-cause/event-pattern analysis. Amazon CloudWatch Logs is designed exactly for this: EC2 instances (via the unified CloudWatch agent) can all stream their application logs into one shared CloudWatch Logs log group regardless of purchasing option (On-Demand vs Spot has no bearing on the logging path since it is the agent/OS pushing logs, not the billing model). AWS's CloudWatch Logs access-control documentation confirms that IAM identity-based policies (scoped to the specific log group ARN) and/or log-group resource policies can be used to permit only a named set of IAM principals to read a given log group, satisfying the 'only a specific set of users' requirement without needing a separate service. For querying, CloudWatch Logs Insights is AWS's purpose-built interactive query engine for CloudWatch Logs: its native query language (Logs Insights QL) offers SQL-like constructs (fields, filter, stats, sort, parse, etc.) for aggregation and pattern discovery, and — as of the newer CloudWatch Logs Insights query-language options — you can additionally choose to write queries in true OpenSearch SQL syntax directly against the log group. Either way, the documented capability is 'use SQL(-like) queries directly on a CloudWatch Logs log group,' which is precisely what option A describes end-to-end (single log group -> IAM-restricted access -> Logs Insights queries). B is wrong because CloudWatch Logs Insights queries CloudWatch Logs log groups, not raw log objects sitting in an S3 bucket — there is no supported integration where Logs Insights reads S3 files directly. C is wrong because it re-fragments the logs into per-instance log groups (defeating the 'single location' requirement) and because Amazon Athena does not natively query CloudWatch Logs log groups — Athena queries data cataloged/stored in S3 (or via Athena federated query connectors), not log groups directly. D is wrong because Amazon Detective is a graph-based security-investigation and threat-analysis tool for exploring resource behavior over time; it does not expose a general-purpose SQL/QL interface for ad hoc root-cause analysis over arbitrary application log content, and it is not designed to be the query surface for a CloudWatch Logs log group. Therefore A is the only option that correctly pairs a single centralized log destination, IAM-based user restriction, and a native SQL-like query engine.","explanation_zh":"答案為 A。需求分三部分:(1) 讓混合使用 On-Demand 與 Spot EC2 執行個體的所有日誌集中到單一位置,(2) 僅限特定使用者存取,(3) 能用類似 SQL 的查詢語言做根因/事件模式分析。Amazon CloudWatch Logs 正是為此設計:所有 EC2 執行個體(透過統一 CloudWatch agent)都能將應用程式日誌串流到同一個共用的 CloudWatch Logs 日誌群組,採購選項(On-Demand 或 Spot)不影響日誌傳送路徑,因為推送日誌的是 agent/作業系統,而非計費模型。AWS 的 CloudWatch Logs 存取控管文件確認,可用 IAM 身分型政策(範圍限定在特定日誌群組 ARN)及/或日誌群組資源政策,只允許指定的一組 IAM 主體讀取該日誌群組,滿足「僅限特定使用者」的需求,且不需要額外服務。查詢方面,CloudWatch Logs Insights 是 AWS 專為 CloudWatch Logs 設計的互動式查詢引擎:其原生查詢語言(Logs Insights QL)提供類 SQL 的語法結構(fields、filter、stats、sort、parse 等)用於彙總與模式探索;而在較新版本中,CloudWatch Logs Insights 甚至可直接選用真正的 OpenSearch SQL 語法對日誌群組下查詢。無論哪一種,文件記載的能力都是「直接對 CloudWatch Logs 日誌群組使用 SQL(類)查詢」,這正是選項 A 從頭到尾所描述的流程(單一日誌群組 -> IAM 限制存取 -> Logs Insights 查詢)。B 錯誤,因為 CloudWatch Logs Insights 查詢的對象是 CloudWatch Logs 日誌群組,而非存放在 S3 儲存貯體中的原始日誌物件——沒有支援 Logs Insights 直接讀取 S3 檔案的整合方式。C 錯誤,因為它把日誌重新拆分成每個執行個體各自的日誌群組(違反「單一位置」需求),而且 Amazon Athena 並非原生查詢 CloudWatch Logs 日誌群組的工具——Athena 查詢的是已編目/儲存在 S3 中的資料(或透過 Athena 聯合查詢連接器),而非直接查詢日誌群組。D 錯誤,因為 Amazon Detective 是以圖形化方式進行安全調查與威脅分析的工具,用於探索資源隨時間的行為模式;它並未提供通用的 SQL/查詢語言介面,可對任意應用程式日誌內容做臨機根因分析,也不是設計來作為 CloudWatch Logs 日誌群組的查詢介面。因此,A 是唯一同時正確搭配「單一集中日誌目的地」、「以 IAM 限制使用者」與「原生類 SQL 查詢引擎」的選項。","distractors":[{"letter":"B","why_en":"CloudWatch Logs Insights queries CloudWatch Logs log groups, not objects stored directly in an S3 bucket; there is no AWS-documented mechanism for Logs Insights to query raw log files sitting in S3, so pairing 'S3 bucket' with 'CloudWatch Logs Insights' describes a nonexistent integration.","why_zh":"CloudWatch Logs Insights 查詢的對象是 CloudWatch Logs 日誌群組,而非直接存放在 S3 儲存貯體中的物件;AWS 文件中沒有讓 Logs Insights 直接查詢 S3 原始日誌檔案的機制,因此將『S3 bucket』與『CloudWatch Logs Insights』搭配描述的是一個不存在的整合方式。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"Sending each instance's logs to its own separate log group directly violates the 'single location' requirement, and Amazon Athena is a serverless SQL query service for data cataloged/stored in Amazon S3 (or via federated connectors) — it does not natively query CloudWatch Logs log groups without first exporting/streaming that data into S3.","why_zh":"讓每台執行個體的日誌各自送到獨立的日誌群組,直接違反『單一位置』的需求;而 Amazon Athena 是針對編目/儲存在 Amazon S3 中資料(或透過聯合查詢連接器)的無伺服器 SQL 查詢服務——若未先將 CloudWatch Logs 資料匯出/串流到 S3,Athena 並不能原生查詢 CloudWatch Logs 日誌群組。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"Amazon Detective is purpose-built for visualizing and investigating security findings and resource behavior graphs (e.g., from GuardDuty, VPC Flow Logs, CloudTrail) over time; it does not provide a general SQL/query-language interface for ad hoc root-cause analysis across arbitrary application logs, and CloudWatch Logs log groups are not a resource that Detective is granted 'access' to query in this way.","why_zh":"Amazon Detective 專門用於視覺化與調查安全發現及資源行為圖(例如來自 GuardDuty、VPC 流量日誌、CloudTrail 的資料)隨時間的變化;它並未提供通用的 SQL/查詢語言介面,可對任意應用程式日誌做臨機根因分析,而且 CloudWatch Logs 日誌群組也不是可以『授予 Detective 存取權』來以此方式查詢的資源。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonCloudWatch/latest/logs/AnalyzingLogData.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonCloudWatch/latest/logs/CWL_QuerySyntax.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonCloudWatch/latest/logs/CWL_AnalyzeLogData_Languages.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonCloudWatch/latest/logs/CWL_AnalyzeLogData_SQL.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonCloudWatch/latest/logs/auth-and-access-control-cwl.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonCloudWatch/latest/logs/iam-identity-based-access-control-cwl.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/athena/latest/ug/what-is.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/detective/latest/userguide/what-is-detective.html"]}},{"id":216,"question_en":"A company has a single AWS account and uses an Amazon EC2 instance to test application code. The company recently discovered that the instance was compromised and was serving malware. Analysis showed that the instance was compromised 35 days ago. A security engineer must implement a continuous monitoring solution that automatically notifies the security team by email for high severity findings as soon as possible. Which combination of steps should the security engineer take to meet these requirements? (Select THREE.)","question_zh":"一家公司只有一个AWS账户，并使用Amazon EC2实例来测试应用程序代码。该公司最近发现该实例已被入侵并正在分发恶意软件。 分析显示，该实例在35天前即已被入侵。安全工程师必须实施一种持续监控解决方案，以便在发现高严重性问题时，能尽快通过电 子邮件自动通知安全团队。 安全工程师应采取哪些步骤组合来满足这些要求？（选择三项。）","options_en":{"A":"Enable AWS Security Hub in the AWS account.","B":"Enable Amazon GuardDuty in the AWS account.","C":"Create an Amazon Simple Notification Service (Amazon SNS) topic. Subscribe the security team ' s email distribution list to the topic.","E":"Create an Amazon EventBridge rule for GuardDuty findings of high severity. Configure the rule to publish a message to the topic.","F":"Create an Amazon EventBridge rule for Security Hub findings of high severity. Configure the rule to publish a message to the queue.","D":"Create an Amazon Simple Queue Service (Amazon SQS) queue. Subscribe the security team ' s email distribution list to the queue."},"options_zh":{"A":"在 AWS 账户中启用 AWS Security Hub。","B":"在 AWS 账户中启用 Amazon GuardDuty。","C":"创建一个 Amazon 简单通知服务（Amazon SNS）主题，并将安全团队的电子邮件分发列表订阅到该主题。","D":"创建一个 Amazon 简单队列服务（Amazon SQS）队列，并将安全团队的电子邮件分发列表订阅到该队列。","E":"为严重程度较高的 GuardDuty 发现创建 Amazon EventBridge 规则，并配置该规则将消息发布到指定主题。","F":"为安全中心的高严重性发现创建一个 Amazon EventBridge 规则，并配置该规则将消息发布到队列中。"},"answer":["B","C","E"],"multi":true,"vote":{},"tags":["Security/IAM","Compute","Serverless/Integration"],"difficulty":2,"diff_why":"複選","research":{"verdict":["B","C","E"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"both","explanation_en":"GuardDuty is AWS's continuous threat-detection service that natively analyzes CloudTrail, VPC Flow Logs, and DNS logs to detect exactly this kind of scenario (a compromised EC2 instance serving malware, e.g. Backdoor:EC2/C&CActivity.B or Trojan findings) without needing any agent deployment, and it starts generating findings automatically once enabled (B). To get near-real-time email alerts, the standard AWS-documented pattern is: create an SNS topic and subscribe the security team's email address to it via the 'email' protocol (C), then create an EventBridge rule that matches GuardDuty finding events of high severity and targets that SNS topic (E). This exact three-step flow is documented by AWS itself in the GuardDuty 'Getting started' tutorial section 'Step 4: Set up GuardDuty finding alerts through SNS'. Security Hub (A) is a finding aggregator/dashboard across multiple accounts and services — it does not perform its own threat detection and is unnecessary for a single-account requirement to be notified of GuardDuty's own high-severity findings; adding it just adds delay and complexity without meeting the 'as soon as possible' requirement any better. SQS (D/F) is wrong because Amazon SQS does not support an email endpoint/protocol at all — only SNS supports the 'email' subscription protocol — so any option involving subscribing the email list directly to a queue, or routing EventBridge/Security Hub findings to a queue for email delivery, cannot actually deliver an email notification.","explanation_zh":"GuardDuty 是 AWS 的持續威脅偵測服務,原生分析 CloudTrail、VPC Flow Logs 與 DNS 記錄,能直接偵測「EC2 執行個體遭入侵並散布惡意軟體」這類情境(例如 Backdoor:EC2/C&CActivity.B 或 Trojan 類型的 finding),啟用後(B)無須部署任何 agent 即可自動產生 findings。要達成近乎即時的 email 告警,AWS 官方文件記載的標準做法是:建立一個 SNS 主題,並以 email 協定將資安團隊的信箱訂閱到該主題(C),接著建立一條 EventBridge 規則,比對高嚴重性(high severity)的 GuardDuty finding 事件,並將目標設為該 SNS 主題(E)。這正是 GuardDuty「Getting started」教學文件中「Step 4: Set up GuardDuty finding alerts through SNS」章節所描述的三步驟流程。Security Hub(A)只是跨帳戶/跨服務的 finding 彙整與儀表板服務,本身不做威脅偵測,在單一帳戶、只需要針對 GuardDuty 自身高嚴重性 finding 發送通知的需求下並非必要,加入它只會增加延遲與複雜度,無助於更快滿足「as soon as possible」的要求。SQS(D/F)則是錯誤選項,因為 Amazon SQS 完全不支援 email 端點/協定——只有 SNS 支援『email』訂閱協定——所以任何把 email 清單直接訂閱到佇列、或是把 EventBridge/Security Hub 的 finding 導向佇列以求寄送 email 的做法,實際上都無法真正送出 email 通知。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"Security Hub aggregates and normalizes findings across services/accounts but performs no threat detection of its own; it is unnecessary overhead for a single-account requirement to react to GuardDuty's own findings quickly, and does not by itself satisfy the notification requirement.","why_zh":"Security Hub 只彙整並正規化跨服務/跨帳戶的 findings,本身不做威脅偵測;在單一帳戶且只需快速回應 GuardDuty 自身 finding 的需求下屬於多餘的額外環節,單靠它也無法滿足通知需求。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"Amazon SQS does not support subscribing an email address directly — SQS has no email protocol/endpoint, so this step cannot deliver notifications to the security team's email distribution list at all.","why_zh":"Amazon SQS 不支援直接訂閱 email 地址——SQS 沒有 email 協定/端點,因此此步驟完全無法將通知送達資安團隊的 email 群組。"},{"letter":"F","why_en":"Routing Security Hub findings to an SQS queue still fails to produce an email notification since SQS cannot deliver to email endpoints, and it also depends on unnecessarily enabling Security Hub (A) first.","why_zh":"把 Security Hub 的 finding 導向 SQS 佇列仍然無法產生 email 通知,因為 SQS 無法送達 email 端點,且此路徑還得先多餘地啟用 Security Hub(A)。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/guardduty/latest/ug/guardduty_settingup.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/guardduty/latest/ug/guardduty_findings_eventbridge.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/sns/latest/dg/sns-email-notifications.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/guardduty/latest/ug/guardduty_sns.html"]}},{"id":217,"question_en":"A company in France uses Amazon Cognito with the Cognito Hosted UI as an identity broker for sign-in and sign-up processes. The company is marketing an application and expects that all the application ' s users will come from France. When the company launches the application, the company ' s security team observes fraudulent sign-ups for the application. Most of the fraudulent registrations are from users outside of France. The security team needs a solution to perform custom validation at sign-up. Based on the results of the validation, the solution must accept or deny the registration request. Which combination of steps will meet these requirements? (Select TWO.)","question_zh":"一家法国公司使用 Amazon Cognito 及其托管用户界面作为身份代理，来处理登录和注册流程。该公司正在推广一款应用程 序，并预计所有用户都将来自法国。然而，当应用上线后，安全团队发现存在大量欺诈性注册行为，其中大多数注册用户来 自法国境外。安全团队需要一种解决方案，在注册时执行自定义验证，并根据验证结果决定接受或拒绝注册请求。 哪两个步骤的组合可以满足这些要求？（选择两项。）","options_en":{"A":"Create a pre sign-up AWS Lambda trigger. Associate the Amazon Cognito function with the Amazon Cognito user pool.","B":"Use a geographic match rule statement to configure an AWS WAF web ACL. Associate the web ACL with the Amazon Cognito user pool.","C":"Configure an app client for the application ' s Amazon Cognito user pool. Use the app client ID to validate the requests in the hosted UI.","D":"Update the application ' s Amazon Cognito user pool to configure a geographic restriction setting.","E":"Use Amazon Cognito to configure a social identity provider (IdP) to validate the requests on the hosted UI."},"options_zh":{"A":"创建一个预注册的 AWS Lambda 触发器。将 Amazon Cognito 函数与 Amazon Cognito 用户池关联。","B":"使用地理位置匹配规则语句配置 AWS WAF 网站访问控制列表（web ACL），并将该 web ACL 与 Amazon Cognito 用 户池关联。","C":"为应用程序的 Amazon Cognito 用户池配置一个应用客户端。使用应用客户端 ID 来验证托管 UI 中的请求。","D":"更新应用程序的 Amazon Cognito 用户池，以配置地理限制设置。","E":"使用 Amazon Cognito 配置一个社交身份提供商（IdP），以验证托管 UI 上的请求。"},"answer":["A","B"],"multi":true,"vote":{},"tags":["Security/IAM","Compute"],"difficulty":2,"diff_why":"複選","research":{"verdict":["A","B"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"Two complementary controls are needed: a pre sign-up Lambda trigger (A) and an AWS WAF web ACL with a geographic match rule associated with the user pool (B). Amazon Cognito's pre sign-up Lambda trigger fires immediately before a new user is created and lets you 'analyze the sign-in event with custom logic, and modify or deny the new user' — this is exactly the 'perform custom validation ... accept or deny the registration request' requirement in the question (e.g., inspect the request's source IP/country and return an error to reject non-France sign-ups). Separately, Amazon Cognito user pools support associating an AWS WAF web ACL to protect the classic hosted UI, managed login, and API endpoints; AWS WAF's geographic match rule statement can block requests based on the country derived from the source IP, stopping fraudulent registration traffic from outside France before it even reaches the sign-up flow. Together these give defense in depth: WAF filters at the edge by geography, and the Lambda trigger enforces custom business validation logic at the application layer. Option D is a distractor — Amazon Cognito user pools have no native 'geographic restriction' setting; geographic control for a user pool must be implemented via an associated AWS WAF web ACL (option B), not a built-in Cognito setting. Option C (app client ID validation) and option E (social IdP) do not address geographic fraud validation at all.","explanation_zh":"本題需要兩個互補的控制項:pre sign-up Lambda trigger(A)以及在 user pool 上關聯一個含地理比對規則的 AWS WAF web ACL(B)。Amazon Cognito 的 pre sign-up Lambda trigger 會在建立新使用者「之前」立即觸發,可讓你「以自訂邏輯分析登入事件,並修改或拒絕新使用者」——這正好對應題目「執行自訂驗證,並依驗證結果接受或拒絕註冊請求」的需求(例如檢查來源 IP/國別,對非法國的註冊回傳錯誤以拒絕)。另一方面,Amazon Cognito user pool 支援關聯 AWS WAF web ACL,以保護 classic hosted UI、managed login 與 API 端點;AWS WAF 的 geographic match rule statement 可依來源 IP 推斷出的國別封鎖請求,在請求抵達註冊流程前就先阻擋來自法國以外的詐騙註冊流量。兩者合併形成縱深防禦:WAF 在邊界依地理位置過濾,Lambda trigger 則在應用層執行自訂商業驗證邏輯。選項 D 是陷阱——Amazon Cognito user pool 並沒有原生的「地理限制」設定,user pool 的地理控制必須透過關聯 AWS WAF web ACL(選項 B)來實作,而非內建 Cognito 設定。選項 C(app client ID 驗證)與選項 E(社群 IdP)都完全無法解決地理詐騙驗證的需求。","distractors":[{"letter":"C","why_en":"An app client ID identifies which client is calling the user pool APIs; it is not a mechanism for validating the geographic origin of a sign-up request, and Cognito does not use app client IDs to perform country-based accept/deny logic in the hosted UI.","why_zh":"App client ID 只是用來識別哪個用戶端在呼叫 user pool API,並非用來驗證註冊請求地理來源的機制,Cognito 也不會用 app client ID 在 hosted UI 中執行依國別接受/拒絕的邏輯。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"Amazon Cognito user pools have no built-in 'geographic restriction' configuration setting. Geographic filtering for a user pool must be implemented externally via an associated AWS WAF web ACL with a geo match rule (option B), so this option describes a non-existent feature.","why_zh":"Amazon Cognito user pool 並沒有內建的「地理限制」設定選項。User pool 的地理過濾必須透過外部關聯的 AWS WAF web ACL 搭配 geo match 規則(選項 B)來實作,因此此選項描述的是一個不存在的功能。"},{"letter":"E","why_en":"Configuring a social identity provider (e.g., Google, Facebook) changes how users federate into the hosted UI; it provides no capability to validate or restrict sign-ups by geographic location and does not address the fraud pattern described.","why_zh":"設定社群身分提供者(如 Google、Facebook)只是改變使用者如何透過聯合登入進入 hosted UI,並不具備依地理位置驗證或限制註冊的能力,也無法解決題目描述的詐騙模式。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/cognito/latest/developerguide/user-pool-lambda-pre-sign-up.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/cognito/latest/developerguide/user-pool-waf.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/waf/latest/developerguide/waf-rule-statement-type-geo-match.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/cognito/latest/developerguide/managing-security.html"]}},{"id":218,"question_en":"A systems administrator was attempting to launch a new Amazon EC2 instance with an encrypted boot volume using a new AWS KMS customer managed key. The EC2 console initially stated the launch was successful, but the instance was subsequently terminated. The IAM role used by the systems administrator has the following IAM permissions: • ec2:Describe* • ec2:AuthorizeSecurityGroupIngress • kms:Encrypt • kms:Decrypt • kms:ReEncrypt* • kms:GenerateDataKey*• kms:DescribeKey Which IAM permission is the systems administrator missing?","question_zh":"一名系统管理员尝试使用新的 AWS KMS 客户管理密钥，启动一个带有加密启动卷的 Amazon EC2 实例。EC2 控制台最初显示启 动成功，但该实例随后被终止。系统管理员所使用的 IAM 角色具有以下 IAM 权限： •ec2:Describe* •ec2：授权安全组入站规则 •kms：加密 •kms：解密 •kms：重新加密* •kms：生成数据密钥* •kms：描述密钥 系统管理员缺少哪个IAM权限？","options_en":{"A":"kms:GetKeyRotationStatus","B":"kms:CreateGrant","C":"kms:GenerateRandom","D":"kms:EnableKey"},"options_zh":{"A":"kms：获取密钥轮换状态","B":"kms：创建授权","C":"kms：生成随机数","D":"kms：启用密钥"},"answer":["B"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Security/IAM","Compute"],"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選","research":{"verdict":["B"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"both","explanation_en":"Per official AWS documentation, when using a KMS customer managed key for Amazon EBS encryption, the calling IAM principal must have permission to call: kms:CreateGrant, kms:Decrypt, kms:DescribeKey, kms:GenerateDataKeyWithoutPlaintext (covered by kms:GenerateDataKey*), and kms:ReEncrypt (covered by kms:ReEncrypt*). EBS needs a grant on the CMK to generate and use the volume key that encrypts the EBS volume; without kms:CreateGrant the administrator's role cannot delegate this permission to the EBS service, so the encrypted-volume launch silently fails and EC2 terminates the instance after the console reports apparent success (a classic symptom of a missing KMS grant permission). The administrator's role already has kms:Encrypt, kms:Decrypt, kms:ReEncrypt*, kms:GenerateDataKey*, and kms:DescribeKey, but is missing kms:CreateGrant, which is exactly the gap that causes this failure mode.","explanation_zh":"根據 AWS 官方文件,使用 AWS KMS 客戶受管金鑰進行 Amazon EBS 加密時,呼叫的 IAM 主體(principal)必須具備下列動作的權限:kms:CreateGrant、kms:Decrypt、kms:DescribeKey、kms:GenerateDataKeyWithoutPlaintext(已涵蓋於 kms:GenerateDataKey*)以及 kms:ReEncrypt(已涵蓋於 kms:ReEncrypt*)。EBS 需要在該 CMK 上取得一個 grant,才能產生並使用加密該 EBS 磁碟區的 volume key;若缺少 kms:CreateGrant,系統管理員的角色便無法將此權限委派給 EBS 服務,導致加密磁碟區的啟動在主控台顯示「成功」後又被 EC2 靜默終止實例——這正是缺少 KMS grant 權限的典型症狀。該管理員角色已具備 kms:Encrypt、kms:Decrypt、kms:ReEncrypt*、kms:GenerateDataKey* 與 kms:DescribeKey,唯獨缺少 kms:CreateGrant,正是造成此故障的關鍵缺口。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"kms:GetKeyRotationStatus only allows checking whether automatic key rotation is enabled on a CMK; it is unrelated to EBS's need to create a volume key and has no bearing on instance launch or termination.","why_zh":"kms:GetKeyRotationStatus 僅用於查詢 CMK 是否啟用自動金鑰輪替,與 EBS 建立 volume key 的需求無關,對實例啟動或終止沒有任何影響。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"kms:GenerateRandom generates a random byte string using AWS KMS as a secure random number source; it is not used in the EBS volume encryption workflow and is not part of the documented required permission set for EBS encryption.","why_zh":"kms:GenerateRandom 是使用 AWS KMS 作為安全亂數來源產生隨機位元組字串,並不用於 EBS 磁碟區加密流程,也不在官方文件列出的 EBS 加密所需權限清單中。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"kms:EnableKey is used to re-enable a previously disabled CMK; the scenario does not indicate the key is disabled, and this permission is not part of the documented set of actions users need for EBS encryption.","why_zh":"kms:EnableKey 用於重新啟用先前被停用的 CMK;題目情境並未顯示金鑰被停用,而且此權限也不在官方文件所列使用者進行 EBS 加密所需的動作清單中。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/ebs/latest/userguide/ebs-encryption-requirements.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/kms/latest/cryptographic-details/ebs-volume-encryption.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/autoscaling/ec2/userguide/ec2-auto-scaling-data-protection.html"]}},{"id":219,"question_en":"A company uses AWS IAM Identity Center to manage access to its AWS accounts. The accounts are in an organization in AWS Organizations. A security engineer needs to set up delegated administration of IAM Identity Center in the organization ' s management account. Which combination of steps should the security engineer perform in IAM Identity Center before configuring delegated administration? (Select THREE.)","question_zh":"一家公司使用 AWS IAM Identity Center 来管理其 AWS 账户的访问权限。这些账户位于 AWS Organizations 中的一个组织 内。安全工程师需要在该组织的管理账户中设置 IAM Identity Center 的委派管理。 在配置委派管理之前，安全工程师应在 IAM Identity Center 中执行哪些步骤组合？（选择三项。）","options_en":{"A":"Grant least privilege access to the organization ' s management account.","B":"Create a new IAM Identity Center directory in the organization ' s management account.","C":"Set up a second AWS Region in the organization ' s management account.","D":"Create permission sets for use only in the organization ' s management account.","E":"Create IAM users for use only in the organization ' s management account.","F":"Create user assignments only in the organization ' s management account."},"options_zh":{"A":"为组织的管理账户授予最小权限访问。","B":"在组织的管理账户中创建一个新的 IAM 身份中心目录。","C":"在组织的管理账户中设置第二个 AWS 区域。","D":"创建仅在组织的管理账户中使用的权限集。","E":"为仅在组织的管理账户中使用而创建 IAM 用户。","F":"仅在组织的管理账户中创建用户分配。"},"answer":["A","D","F"],"multi":true,"vote":{},"tags":["Organizations/Governance","Security/IAM"],"difficulty":2,"diff_why":"複選","research":{"verdict":["A","D","F"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"AWS's official IAM Identity Center documentation has a dedicated 'Best practices' section titled 'Here are some best practices to consider before you configure delegated administration' that lists exactly this kind of guidance, and three of its bullets map directly onto three of the six options. First, 'Grant least privilege to the management account' — AWS states the management account is highly privileged and recommends restricting access to it to as few people as possible before delegating, which is option A verbatim. Second, 'Use dedicated permission sets for the management account' — AWS explains a permission set used for management-account access should only ever be modified by an administrator working from the management account and the delegated administrator can't alter it, i.e., permission sets intended for the management account should be created/used only there, which is option D. Third, 'Assign users only (not groups) to permission sets in the management account' — AWS warns that assigning groups to management-account permission sets lets any group/IdP admin indirectly grant management-account access by editing group membership, so you should assign individual users directly (create user assignments, not group assignments) for the management account, which is option F. The other three options are not part of this guidance and are technically off: B is wrong because an IAM Identity Center instance/directory already exists by default in the management account when you enable the service — there is no 'create a new directory in the management account' step, and the doc's actual identity-source guidance is about where to locate an Active Directory relative to the delegated admin account, not creating a second directory in the management account. C is nonsensical — IAM Identity Center is a single-instance, single-Region-per-organization service; you don't 'set up a second Region in the management account' as part of delegating administration. E conflates IAM Identity Center identity-store users with IAM (identity) users — the best practice is about assigning existing IAM Identity Center users (not groups) to management-account permission sets, not about creating standalone IAM users, so E misstates the mechanism AWS actually documents. The dump's suggested answer (A, D, F) is confirmed by the AWS documentation's own three matching best-practice bullets.","explanation_zh":"AWS 官方 IAM Identity Center 文件有一個專門的「Best practices」章節,標題正是「在設定委派管理之前應考慮的最佳實務」,其中三條建議恰好一一對應六個選項中的三個。第一,「對管理帳戶授予最小權限」——AWS 說明管理帳戶是高度特權帳戶,建議在委派管理之前先將能存取管理帳戶的人數限制到最少,這正是選項 A 的原文重述。第二,「為管理帳戶使用專屬的權限集」——AWS 說明用於管理帳戶存取的權限集只能由在管理帳戶中操作的 IAM Identity Center 管理員修改,委派管理員無法變更它,也就是說專供管理帳戶使用的權限集應只在管理帳戶中建立/使用,這正是選項 D。第三,「僅將使用者(而非群組)指派給管理帳戶中的權限集」——AWS 警告若將群組指派給管理帳戶的權限集,任何有權修改該群組成員的群組/IdP 管理員都能間接取得管理帳戶存取權,因此應直接指派個別使用者(建立使用者指派,而非群組指派)給管理帳戶,這正是選項 F。其餘三個選項並非此份指引的內容,且技術上站不住腳:B 錯誤,因為啟用 IAM Identity Center 時,其執行個體/目錄預設就已存在於管理帳戶中——並沒有「在管理帳戶中建立新目錄」這個步驟;文件中實際的身分來源指引談的是 Active Directory 應相對於委派管理帳戶放在哪裡,而非在管理帳戶中建立第二個目錄。C 不合理——IAM Identity Center 是每個組織單一執行個體、單一 Region 的服務,委派管理的準備工作中並不包含「在管理帳戶中設定第二個 Region」。E 把 IAM Identity Center 身分存放區的使用者與 IAM(身分)使用者混為一談——該最佳實務談的是把既有的 IAM Identity Center 使用者(而非群組)指派給管理帳戶的權限集,而不是建立獨立的 IAM 使用者,因此 E 對 AWS 實際記載的機制描述有誤。題庫建議答案(A、D、F)已由 AWS 文件中恰好對應的三條最佳實務條目所證實。","distractors":[{"letter":"B","why_en":"An IAM Identity Center directory (identity store) already exists by default in the management account the moment you enable the service — there is no separate 'create a new directory in the management account' action to perform before delegating administration. AWS's actual guidance about directories concerns where to locate an external Active Directory relative to the delegated administrator account, not creating an additional directory in the management account itself.","why_zh":"啟用 IAM Identity Center 的當下,管理帳戶中預設就已存在一個目錄(身分存放區)——在委派管理之前並不需要另外執行「在管理帳戶中建立新目錄」的動作。AWS 實際對目錄的指引,講的是外部 Active Directory 應相對於委派管理帳戶放在哪個位置,而不是在管理帳戶本身另外建立一個目錄。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"IAM Identity Center operates as a single instance in a single, chosen AWS Region per organization; there is no concept of 'setting up a second Region in the management account' as a prerequisite for, or step related to, delegated administration. This option does not correspond to anything in AWS's delegated-administration guidance.","why_zh":"IAM Identity Center 在每個組織中是以單一執行個體、單一指定 AWS Region 的方式運作,並不存在「在管理帳戶中設定第二個 Region」這種作為委派管理前置作業或相關步驟的概念。此選項在 AWS 委派管理指引中找不到對應內容。"},{"letter":"E","why_en":"This conflates IAM (identity) users with IAM Identity Center's own identity-store users. AWS's best practice is to assign existing IAM Identity Center users directly (not groups) to permission sets that grant management-account access — it is not a recommendation to create standalone IAM users in the management account, which is a different, unrelated resource type and not part of the IAM Identity Center delegated-administration workflow at all.","why_zh":"此選項把 IAM(身分)使用者與 IAM Identity Center 自身身分存放區中的使用者混淆了。AWS 的最佳實務是直接將既有的 IAM Identity Center 使用者(而非群組)指派給授予管理帳戶存取權的權限集,而不是建議在管理帳戶中建立獨立的 IAM 使用者——那是完全不同、不相關的資源類型,也完全不屬於 IAM Identity Center 委派管理的工作流程。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/singlesignon/latest/userguide/delegated-admin.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/singlesignon/latest/userguide/delegated-admin-how-to-register.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/organizations/latest/userguide/services-that-can-integrate-sso.html"]}},{"id":220,"question_en":"A company uses an organization in AWS Organizations to manage multiple AWS accounts. The company wants to centrally give users the ability to access Amazon Q Developer. Which solution will meet this requirement?","question_zh":"一家公司使用 AWS Organizations 中的组织来管理多个 AWS 账户。该公司希望集中授予用户访问 Amazon Q Developer 的 权限。 哪种解决方案能满足这一要求？","options_en":{"A":"Enable AWS IAM Identity Center and set up Amazon Q Developer as an AWS managed application.","B":"Enable Amazon Cognito and create a new identity pool for Amazon Q Developer.","C":"Enable Amazon Cognito and set up Amazon Q Developer as an AWS managed application.","D":"Enable AWS IAM Identity Center and create a new identity pool for Amazon Q Developer."},"options_zh":{"A":"启用 AWS IAM Identity Center，并将 Amazon Q Developer 配置为 AWS 托管应用程序。","B":"启用 Amazon Cognito 并为 Amazon Q 开发者创建一个新的身份池。","C":"启用 Amazon Cognito，并将 Amazon Q Developer 配置为 AWS 托管应用程序。","D":"启用 AWS IAM Identity Center，并为 Amazon Q 开发者创建一个新的身份池。"},"answer":["A"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Organizations/Governance","Security/IAM"],"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選","research":{"verdict":["A"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"AWS IAM Identity Center is the centralized identity/access management service for AWS Organizations, and Amazon Q Developer Pro is designed to be enabled organization-wide through IAM Identity Center as an AWS managed application. AWS documentation states that administrators who want to set up multiple users with Amazon Q Developer at the Pro tier should get started with IAM Identity Center, which provides enterprise controls such as bulk subscription management, cancellation, and usage tracking across the organization. When enabled, Amazon Q Developer appears as an IAM Identity Center managed application (e.g., the 'QDevProfile-region' application shared among Pro subscribers), and access is granted to IAM Identity Center users/groups rather than through a separate identity store. Amazon Cognito (options B and C) is designed for building custom authentication into applications (via user pools and identity pools) and federating access to AWS resources for app users — it is not the mechanism AWS uses for organization-wide, centralized enablement of AWS managed applications like Amazon Q Developer. Option D incorrectly mixes IAM Identity Center with the Cognito concept of an 'identity pool,' which does not exist within IAM Identity Center. Therefore, the correct and AWS-documented solution is to enable IAM Identity Center and configure Amazon Q Developer as an AWS managed application (Option A).","explanation_zh":"AWS IAM Identity Center 是 AWS Organizations 中用來集中管理身份與存取的服務，而 Amazon Q Developer Pro 的設計就是要透過 IAM Identity Center 以「AWS managed application」的形式在整個組織中集中啟用。AWS 官方文件明確指出，想要為多位使用者設定 Amazon Q Developer Pro 的管理員應該從 IAM Identity Center 開始，因為它提供企業級控管能力，例如批次訂閱、取消訂閱、以及跨組織的使用量追蹤儀表板。啟用後，Amazon Q Developer 會以 IAM Identity Center 受管應用程式的形式出現（例如在成員帳戶中名為 'QDevProfile-region' 的應用程式，由所有 Pro 訂閱者共用），存取權限授予的對象是 IAM Identity Center 的使用者/群組,而非另外建立身份儲存區。Amazon Cognito（選項 B、C）則是用來為應用程式建立自訂身份驗證（透過 user pool 與 identity pool），並讓應用程式使用者聯合存取 AWS 資源，並不是 AWS 用來集中啟用像 Amazon Q Developer 這類受管應用程式的機制。選項 D 則錯誤地把 IAM Identity Center 與 Cognito 的「identity pool」概念混在一起，但 IAM Identity Center 本身並沒有 identity pool 這個概念。因此，根據 AWS 官方文件，正確做法是啟用 IAM Identity Center，並將 Amazon Q Developer 設定為 AWS managed application（選項 A）。","distractors":[{"letter":"B","why_en":"Amazon Cognito identity pools are used to grant app users (often unauthenticated or externally authenticated) temporary AWS credentials to access AWS resources directly from client applications — this is unrelated to centrally enabling a workforce-facing AWS managed application like Amazon Q Developer across an AWS Organization.","why_zh":"Amazon Cognito 的 identity pool 是用來讓應用程式使用者（通常是未經驗證或透過外部驗證的使用者）取得臨時 AWS 憑證，以便從用戶端應用程式直接存取 AWS 資源，這與在 AWS Organization 中集中為員工啟用像 Amazon Q Developer 這類受管應用程式毫無關係。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"Amazon Q Developer is not offered as an 'AWS managed application' concept under Amazon Cognito; that managed-application integration pattern belongs to IAM Identity Center, not Cognito, which has no equivalent managed-application catalog for organization-wide AWS service access.","why_zh":"Amazon Q Developer 並不是在 Amazon Cognito 底下以「AWS managed application」的概念提供；這種受管應用程式的整合模式屬於 IAM Identity Center，而 Cognito 並沒有對應的、可供組織層級啟用 AWS 服務的受管應用程式目錄。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"IAM Identity Center does not have a construct called an 'identity pool' — that terminology belongs to Amazon Cognito. Within IAM Identity Center, centralized access to services like Amazon Q Developer is granted by enabling the service as an AWS managed application and assigning users/groups, not by creating an identity pool.","why_zh":"IAM Identity Center 並沒有「identity pool」這個構件，那是 Amazon Cognito 的術語。在 IAM Identity Center 中，要集中授予像 Amazon Q Developer 這類服務的存取權，做法是將該服務啟用為 AWS managed application 並指派使用者/群組，而不是建立 identity pool。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/amazonq/latest/qdeveloper-ug/getting-started-idc.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/amazonq/latest/qdeveloper-ug/subscribe-member.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/amazonq/latest/qdeveloper-ug/subscribe-standalone.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/amazonq/latest/qdeveloper-ug/manage-account-details.html"]}},{"id":221,"question_en":"A security engineer needs to implement a solution to identify any sensitive data that is stored in an Amazon S3 bucket. The solution must report on sensitive data in the S3 bucket by using an existing Amazon Simple Notification Service (Amazon SNS) topic. Which solution will meet these requirements with the LEAST implementation effort?","question_zh":"安全工程师需要实施一项解决方案，以识别存储在 Amazon S3 存储桶中的任何敏感数据。该解决方案必须通过现有的 Amazon 简单通知服务（Amazon SNS）主题报告 S3 存储桶中的敏感数据。 哪种解决方案能在最少的实施工作量下满足这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Enable AWS Config. Configure AWS Config to monitor for sensitive data in the S3 bucket and to send notifications to the SNS topic.","B":"Create an AWS Lambda function to scan the S3 bucket for sensitive data that matches a pattern. Program the Lambda function to send notifications to the SNS topic.","C":"Configure Amazon Macie to use managed data identifiers to identify and categorize sensitive data. Create an Amazon EventBridge rule to send notifications to the SNS topic.","D":"Enable Amazon GuardDuty. Configure AWS CloudTrail S3 data events. Create an Amazon CloudWatch alarm that reacts to GuardDuty findings and sends notifications to the SNS topic."},"options_zh":{"A":"启用 AWS Config。配置 AWS Config 以监控 S3 存储桶中的敏感数据，并向 SNS 主题发送通知。","B":"创建一个 AWS Lambda 函数，用于扫描 S3 存储桶中符合特定模式的敏感数据，并将通知发送到 SNS 主题。","C":"配置 Amazon Macie 使用托管数据标识符来识别和分类敏感数据。创建一个 Amazon EventBridge 规则，将通知发送 到 SNS 主题。","D":"启用 Amazon GuardDuty，配置 AWS CloudTrail 的 S3 数据事件，并创建一个 Amazon CloudWatch 警报，用于 响应 GuardDuty 的发现结果并向 SNS 主题发送通知。"},"answer":["C"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Organizations/Governance","Security/IAM","Storage","Compute","Serverless/Integration","Monitoring/Ops"],"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選","research":{"verdict":["C"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"both","explanation_en":"Amazon Macie is the AWS service purpose-built to discover and classify sensitive data (PII, credentials, financial data, etc.) in S3 buckets, using built-in managed data identifiers that require no custom rule-writing. Macie automatically publishes findings as events to Amazon EventBridge; you simply create an EventBridge rule that matches Macie finding events and routes them to the existing SNS topic as the target — no custom code, no polling, no data pipeline to build. This is the documented, native integration path (Macie -> EventBridge -> SNS) and represents the least implementation effort of the four options.","explanation_zh":"Amazon Macie 是專門用來探索與分類 S3 儲存的機敏資料（PII、憑證、財務資料等）的服務，內建 managed data identifiers，不需要自訂規則。Macie 會自動將 finding 發布為 EventBridge 事件，只要建立一條 EventBridge rule 比對 Macie finding 事件，並將目標設為既有的 SNS 主題即可，完全不需寫程式、輪詢或建置資料管線。這是官方文件記載的原生整合路徑（Macie -> EventBridge -> SNS），在四個選項中實作工作量最小。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"AWS Config evaluates resource configuration compliance (e.g., bucket policy settings) — it has no capability to inspect object content for sensitive data patterns, so it cannot meet the core requirement at all.","why_zh":"AWS Config 只評估資源設定的合規性（例如 bucket policy 設定），完全沒有檢查物件內容是否含機敏資料的能力，因此根本無法滿足核心需求。"},{"letter":"B","why_en":"Building a custom Lambda function to scan S3 objects for sensitive-data patterns requires writing and maintaining detection logic, error handling, and scaling — far more implementation effort than using Macie's built-in managed data identifiers.","why_zh":"自建 Lambda 函式掃描 S3 物件比對機敏資料樣式，需要自行撰寫並維護偵測邏輯、錯誤處理與擴展性，遠比使用 Macie 內建的 managed data identifiers 費工。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"GuardDuty S3 Protection analyzes CloudTrail S3 data events for anomalous/malicious access behavior (e.g., unusual API calls, potential data exfiltration), not for classifying the content of objects as containing sensitive data — it does not perform data content inspection.","why_zh":"GuardDuty S3 Protection 是分析 CloudTrail S3 data events 找出異常或惡意存取行為（如異常 API 呼叫、疑似資料外洩），並非用來分類物件內容是否含機敏資料，它不做資料內容檢測。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/macie/latest/user/findings-monitor-events-eventbridge.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/macie/latest/user/managed-data-identifiers.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/macie/latest/user/what-is-macie.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/macie/latest/user/discovery-asdd.html"]}},{"id":222,"question_en":"A security engineer needs to prepare Amazon EC2 instances for quarantine during a security incident. AWS Systems Manager Agent (SSM Agent) is installed, and a script exists to install and update forensic tools. Which solution will quarantine EC2 instances during a security incident?","question_zh":"安全工程师需要在发生安全事件时，为Amazon EC2实例准备隔离措施。AWS Systems Manager Agent（SSM Agent）已安装， 并存在用于安装和更新取证工具的脚本。 在安全事件期间，哪种解决方案会隔离EC2实例？","options_en":{"A":"Track SSM Agent versions with AWS Config.","B":"Configure Session Manager to deny external connections.","C":"Store the script in Amazon S3 and grant read access.","D":"Configure IAM permissions for the SSM Agent to run the script as a Systems Manager Run Command document."},"options_zh":{"A":"使用 AWS Config 跟踪 SSM Agent 版本。","B":"配置会话管理器以拒绝外部连接。","C":"将脚本存储在 Amazon S3 中并授予读取权限。","D":"配置 IAM 权限，使 SSM Agent 能够以 Systems Manager 运行命令文档的形式执行脚本。"},"answer":["D"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Organizations/Governance","Security/IAM","Storage","Compute","Monitoring/Ops"],"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選","research":{"verdict":["D"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"The scenario already supplies two pieces of the incident-response setup — SSM Agent is installed on the instances, and a script exists that installs/updates forensic tools — and asks which solution actually lets the security engineer act on those instances (run the forensic script) during an incident. The missing piece is an execution mechanism, and AWS Systems Manager Run Command is the documented way to 'remotely and securely manage the configuration' of managed instances and execute commands/scripts on them without needing SSH/RDP or interactive login (see the EC2 user guide's Run Command page). To actually invoke a script as a Run Command document, you must configure IAM permissions on both sides: the instance's IAM role needs the SSM managed-instance permissions so the agent can receive and execute commands, and the calling principal needs ssm:SendCommand/RunCommand permissions to dispatch the document — this is exactly what option D describes. This pattern matches AWS's own documented incident-response capability, EC2 Triage (part of AWS Security Incident Response), which 'allows responders to execute Systems Manager Run Command on EC2 instances to gather investigative data without direct instance access,' and whose CloudFormation templates explicitly provision the 'additional permissions for EC2 Triage via AWS Systems Manager Run Command.' Without configuring those IAM permissions, having the script written (and even stored somewhere reachable) is not sufficient — the script never actually executes on the fleet of instances that need to be quarantined/triaged. So D is the step that turns the existing SSM Agent + script into an actionable quarantine/forensics capability, and it is confirmed as correct.","explanation_zh":"題目情境已經提供了事件回應設置中的兩個要素——EC2 執行個體已安裝 SSM Agent,且已存在一支用來安裝/更新鑑識工具的腳本——並詢問哪個方案能讓安全工程師在事件發生時真正對這些執行個體採取行動(執行該鑑識腳本)。缺少的環節是「執行機制」,而 AWS Systems Manager Run Command 正是官方文件記載的方式,可在不需要 SSH/RDP 或互動式登入的情況下,「遠端且安全地管理」受管執行個體並在其上執行命令/腳本(參見 EC2 使用者指南的 Run Command 頁面)。若要真正以 Run Command 文件的形式呼叫該腳本,必須在兩端都設定 IAM 權限:執行個體的 IAM 角色需要 SSM 受管執行個體所需的權限,讓 Agent 能接收並執行命令;而發出呼叫的主體則需要 ssm:SendCommand/RunCommand 權限才能派送該文件——這正是選項 D 所描述的內容。此模式與 AWS 官方記載的事件回應能力「EC2 Triage」(AWS Security Incident Response 的一部分)相符,該功能「允許回應人員在 EC2 執行個體上執行 Systems Manager Run Command,以在不直接存取執行個體的情況下蒐集調查資料」,其 CloudFormation 範本更明確布建了「透過 AWS Systems Manager Run Command 執行 EC2 Triage 所需的額外權限」。若未設定這些 IAM 權限,即使腳本已寫好(甚至已存放在可讀取的位置),也不足以讓腳本在需要被隔離/鑑識的執行個體群上實際執行。因此 D 正是讓現有的 SSM Agent + 腳本轉化為可執行的隔離/鑑識能力的關鍵步驟,確認為正確答案。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"AWS Config with a managed rule can track/report the SSM Agent version installed on instances for compliance visibility, but that is a passive monitoring/inventory capability. It does not execute the forensic script, does not grant any permission to run it, and does nothing to isolate or quarantine an instance during an active incident.","why_zh":"AWS Config 搭配受管規則可以追蹤/回報執行個體上安裝的 SSM Agent 版本,提供合規性可視性,但這只是被動的監控/盤點能力。它不會執行鑑識腳本,也不會授予任何執行權限,對於在事件發生當下隔離或圍堵執行個體毫無幫助。"},{"letter":"B","why_en":"Session Manager provides interactive, auditable shell access to managed instances without opening inbound ports; there is no documented Session Manager setting to 'deny external connections' as a quarantine mechanism, and even restricting Session Manager access would not run the forensic script or block the instance's own network traffic — it addresses administrator access to the instance, not incident containment of the instance itself.","why_zh":"Session Manager 提供的是對受管執行個體的互動式、可稽核的 shell 存取,且不需開放任何輸入連接埠;文件中並沒有『拒絕外部連線』這種可作為隔離機制的 Session Manager 設定,即使限制了 Session Manager 存取,也不會執行鑑識腳本或阻擋該執行個體本身對外的網路流量——它處理的是管理員對執行個體的存取,而非對執行個體本身的事件圍堵。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"Storing the script in S3 and granting read access only makes the script content retrievable — it does not provide any mechanism for the script to actually run on the target EC2 instances during an incident. Without a companion execution path (Run Command with the right IAM permissions), the script can be downloaded but never invoked at scale during the incident window.","why_zh":"把腳本存放到 S3 並授予讀取權限,只能讓腳本內容『可被取得』——並未提供任何機制讓該腳本在事件發生時實際於目標 EC2 執行個體上執行。若缺少對應的執行途徑(具備正確 IAM 權限的 Run Command),該腳本頂多能被下載,卻無法在事件期間對整批執行個體大規模呼叫執行。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AWSEC2/latest/UserGuide/ec2-stig-ssm-cmd-doc.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AWSEC2/latest/UserGuide/ec2rw-ssm.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/security-ir/latest/userguide/containment-with-ec2-triage-template.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/security-ir/latest/userguide/cloudformation-templates.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/systems-manager-automation-runbooks/latest/userguide/aws-quarantineec2instance.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/guardduty/latest/ug/compromised-ec2.html"]}},{"id":223,"question_en":"A company runs a web application on a fleet of Amazon EC2 instances in an Auto Scaling group. Amazon GuardDuty and AWS Security Hub are enabled. The security engineer needs an automated response to anomalous traffic that follows AWS best practices and minimizes application disruption. Which solution will meet these requirements?","question_zh":"一家公司在自动扩展组中的Amazon EC2实例集群上运行Web应用程序，已启用Amazon GuardDuty和AWS Security Hub。 安全工程师需要一种符合AWS最佳实践、并能最小化应用中断的自动化响应机制，以应对异常流量。 哪种解决方案能满足这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Use EventBridge to disable the instance profile access keys.","B":"Use EventBridge to invoke a Lambda function that removes the affected instance from the Auto Scaling group and isolates it with a restricted security group.","C":"Use Security Hub to update the subnet network ACL to block traffic.","D":"Send GuardDuty findings to Amazon SNS for email notification."},"options_zh":{"A":"使用 EventBridge 禁用实例配置文件的访问密钥。","B":"使用 EventBridge 调用一个 Lambda 函数，将受影响的实例从自动伸缩组中移除，并通过受限的安全组将其隔离。","C":"使用安全中心更新子网的网络ACL以阻止流量。","D":"将 GuardDuty 的发现结果发送到 Amazon SNS 以进行电子邮件通知。"},"answer":["B"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Security/IAM","Compute","Serverless/Integration"],"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選","research":{"verdict":["B"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"both","explanation_en":"B is correct and matches AWS's own documented remediation pattern for GuardDuty findings on EC2. AWS's guide 'Remediating a potentially compromised Amazon EC2 instance' (guardduty/latest/ug/compromised-ec2.html) prescribes exactly this two-part isolation: create a dedicated, tightly-restricted 'Isolation' security group with no 0.0.0.0/0 inbound/outbound rules, associate it with the flagged instance, and remove all other security-group associations — while the instance itself is kept running (not terminated) for forensic investigation. Pairing that with removing the instance from the Auto Scaling group is the standard EC2 Auto Scaling incident-response pattern: the ASG immediately launches a healthy replacement instance to maintain capacity/availability (minimizing application disruption), while the suspect instance is quarantined out-of-service for investigation rather than abruptly killed (which would destroy forensic evidence) or left in the group (where it keeps serving/receiving traffic). Driving this from an EventBridge rule matching the GuardDuty finding, invoking a Lambda function, is the AWS-documented automation pattern ('Creating an EventBridge rule for GuardDuty findings', guardduty_findings_eventbridge.html) for turning findings into an automatic, code-defined response — satisfying 'automated response' with no manual step. This combination is the only option that is both automated and follows the documented isolate-don't-destroy best practice while preserving application availability via the ASG's self-healing.","explanation_zh":"B 正確,且完全對應 AWS 官方針對 GuardDuty EC2 發現事項所記載的修復模式。AWS 指南《Remediating a potentially compromised Amazon EC2 instance》(guardduty/latest/ug/compromised-ec2.html)明確規定了這兩步驟的隔離做法:建立一個嚴格限制、不含 0.0.0.0/0 輸入/輸出規則的專用「Isolation」安全群組,將其套用到被標記的執行個體,並移除該執行個體上所有其他安全群組關聯——同時保留執行個體持續運行(而非終止),以利鑑識調查。搭配將該執行個體從 Auto Scaling 群組中移除,則是標準的 EC2 Auto Scaling 事件回應模式:ASG 會立即啟動一個健康的替代執行個體以維持容量/可用性(將應用程式中斷降到最低),而可疑執行個體則被隔離、退出服務以供調查,而非直接終止(這會摧毀鑑識證據)或留在群組中繼續提供/接收流量。透過 EventBridge 規則比對 GuardDuty 發現事項並觸發 Lambda 函式來執行此流程,正是 AWS 文件記載的自動化模式(《Creating an EventBridge rule for GuardDuty findings》,guardduty_findings_eventbridge.html),能將發現事項轉為自動化、程式碼定義的回應,滿足題目「自動化回應」且無需人工介入的要求。這個組合是唯一同時滿足自動化、遵循官方隔離而非銷毀鑑識證據的最佳實務,並透過 ASG 的自我修復能力維持應用程式可用性的選項。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"EC2 instance profiles grant temporary, automatically-rotated security credentials via the metadata service, not static 'access keys' that can simply be 'disabled' the way an IAM user's access key can. There is no such single action, and even if credentials could be revoked, this does nothing to stop the instance from sending or receiving anomalous network traffic — it addresses the wrong attack surface for a traffic-based finding.","why_zh":"EC2 執行個體設定檔是透過中繼資料服務提供暫時性、自動輪替的安全憑證,並非像 IAM 使用者存取金鑰那樣可以直接『停用』的靜態金鑰,因此不存在這樣單一的動作。即使能撤銷憑證,也無法阻止該執行個體傳送或接收異常網路流量——對於以流量為主的發現事項而言,這解決的是錯誤的攻擊面。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"AWS Security Hub is a findings aggregation and posture-management service; it does not have a native capability to modify network ACLs or any other resource configuration itself. Remediation actions must be performed by a separate compute/automation resource (e.g., Lambda via EventBridge or a Security Hub custom action invoking SSM/Lambda), not by Security Hub directly, making this option technically inaccurate.","why_zh":"AWS Security Hub 是發現事項彙整與安全態勢管理服務,本身並沒有原生能力可以修改網路 ACL 或任何其他資源設定。修復動作必須由另一個運算/自動化資源執行(例如透過 EventBridge 觸發 Lambda,或 Security Hub 自訂動作呼叫 SSM/Lambda),而非由 Security Hub 直接執行,因此此選項在技術上並不正確。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"Sending findings to SNS for email notification is purely a notification mechanism requiring a human to read the email and manually act — it is explicitly not an automated response, failing the question's core 'automated response' requirement, and leaves the anomalous traffic completely unmitigated during the delay.","why_zh":"將發現事項傳送至 SNS 進行電子郵件通知,純粹是一種通知機制,需要有人閱讀郵件並手動採取行動——這明顯不是自動化回應,無法滿足題目核心的「自動化回應」要求,且在等待期間異常流量完全未被緩解。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/guardduty/latest/ug/compromised-ec2.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/guardduty/latest/ug/guardduty_findings_eventbridge.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AWSEC2/latest/UserGuide/using-network-security.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/autoscaling/ec2/userguide/detach-instance-asg.html"]}},{"id":224,"question_en":"A company is migrating one of its legacy systems from an on-premises data center to AWS. The application server will run on AWS, but the database must remain in the on-premises data center for compliance reasons. The database is sensitive to network latency. Additionally, the data that travels between the on-premises data center and AWS must have IPsec encryption. Which combination of AWS solutions will meet these requirements? (Select TWO.)","question_zh":"一家公司正在将其一个遗留系统从本地数据中心迁移至 AWS。应用程序服务器将在 AWS 上运行，但由于合规性要求，数据库必 须保留在本地数据中心。该数据库对网络延迟较为敏感。此外，在本地数据中心与 AWS 之间传输的数据必须使用 IPsec 加密。 以下哪两种 AWS 解决方案的组合可以满足这些要求？（选择两项。）","options_en":{"A":"AWS Site-to-Site VPN","B":"AWS Direct Connect","C":"AWS VPN CloudHub","D":"VPC peering","E":"NAT gateway"},"options_zh":{"A":"AWS 站点到站点 VPN","B":"AWS Direct Connect","C":"AWS VPN CloudHub","D":"VPC 对等连接","E":"NAT网关"},"answer":["A","B"],"multi":true,"vote":{},"tags":["Networking/DNS","Security/IAM","Database"],"difficulty":2,"diff_why":"複選","research":{"verdict":["A","B"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"both","explanation_en":"The database is latency-sensitive, which rules out a VPN-only design (Site-to-Site VPN runs over the public internet with variable, higher latency), and the data in transit must be IPsec-encrypted, which AWS Direct Connect does not provide by default (DX is a private, dedicated, low-latency link but plaintext unless MACsec is separately enabled, and MACsec is not one of the listed options). AWS's own guidance is explicit: 'With AWS Direct Connect and AWS Site-to-Site VPN, you can combine one or more AWS Direct Connect dedicated network connections with the Amazon VPC VPN. This combination provides an IPsec-encrypted private connection that also reduces network costs, increases bandwidth throughput, and provides a more consistent network experience than internet-based VPN connections.' Running an IPsec Site-to-Site VPN over a Direct Connect (public or transit) virtual interface is the documented pattern for getting both a consistent, low-latency, high-bandwidth private path AND end-to-end IPsec encryption. Therefore A (Site-to-Site VPN) and B (Direct Connect), used together, is the combination that satisfies both requirements.","explanation_zh":"資料庫對延遲敏感，這排除了純 VPN 方案（Site-to-Site VPN 走公開網際網路,延遲較高且不穩定）；同時流量必須有 IPsec 加密，而 AWS Direct Connect 預設不加密（DX 是私有、專屬、低延遲的連線，但除非另外啟用 MACsec，否則是明文傳輸，而 MACsec 並不在此題選項中）。AWS 官方文件明確指出：「透過 AWS Direct Connect 與 AWS Site-to-Site VPN，您可以將一或多個 AWS Direct Connect 專屬網路連線與 Amazon VPC VPN 結合，此組合可提供 IPsec 加密的私有連線，同時降低網路成本、提升頻寬並提供比網際網路 VPN 更穩定的網路體驗。」在 Direct Connect（public 或 transit 虛擬介面）上疊加 IPsec Site-to-Site VPN，正是官方文件記載用來同時取得穩定低延遲高頻寬私有路徑「與」端對端 IPsec 加密的標準做法。因此 A（Site-to-Site VPN）與 B（Direct Connect）搭配使用，才是能同時滿足兩項需求的組合。","distractors":[{"letter":"C","why_en":"AWS VPN CloudHub is designed to provide secure communication between multiple remote sites (branch offices) using a hub-and-spoke model over Site-to-Site VPN connections to a single virtual private gateway; it is not the mechanism for combining low-latency and IPsec encryption for a single on-premises data center connection, and by itself is still internet-based (not low-latency).","why_zh":"AWS VPN CloudHub 設計用途是讓多個遠端站點（分支機構）透過 hub-and-spoke 模式,經由多條 Site-to-Site VPN 連線到單一 virtual private gateway 之間安全通訊；它並非用來為單一內部部署資料中心連線同時達成低延遲與 IPsec 加密的機制,且本身仍是基於網際網路的連線,不具備低延遲特性。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"VPC peering connects two VPCs to each other within AWS (or across accounts/Regions); it has no capability to connect to an on-premises data center at all, so it cannot satisfy either the latency or the IPsec encryption requirement in this hybrid scenario.","why_zh":"VPC peering 是用來連接 AWS 內兩個 VPC（可跨帳戶／跨區域）,完全沒有能力連接到內部部署資料中心,因此在此混合架構情境中,它無法滿足延遲或 IPsec 加密的任何一項需求。"},{"letter":"E","why_en":"A NAT gateway allows resources in a private subnet to initiate outbound traffic to the internet (or other networks) while remaining private; it is not a hybrid-connectivity or encryption solution and does not connect AWS to an on-premises data center.","why_zh":"NAT gateway 是讓私有子網路中的資源能夠對網際網路（或其他網路）發起出站流量,同時本身維持私有狀態；它並非混合雲連接或加密解決方案,也無法將 AWS 與內部部署資料中心連接起來。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/directconnect/latest/UserGuide/encryption-in-transit.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/directconnect/latest/UserGuide/WhatIsAWSDirectConnect.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/vpn/latest/s2svpn/VPC_VPN.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/vpn/latest/s2svpn/CloudHub.html"]}},{"id":225,"question_en":"A company that uses AWS Organizations is using AWS IAM Identity Center to administer access to AWS accounts. A security engineer is creating a custom permission set in IAM Identity Center. The company will use the permission set across multiple accounts. An AWS managed policy and a customer managed policy are attached to the permission set. The security engineer has full administrative permissions and is operating in the management account. When the security engineer attempts to assign the permission set to an IAM Identity Center user who has access to multiple accounts, the assignment fails. What should the security engineer do to resolve this failure?","question_zh":"一家使用 AWS Organizations 的公司正在使用 AWS IAM Identity Center 来管理对 AWS 账户的访问权 限。安全工程师正在 IAM Identity Center 中创建一个自定义权限集，该公司将在多个账户中使用该权 限集。该权限集已附加了 AWS 托管策略和客户托管策略。安全工程师拥有完全的管理权限，并在管 理账户中操作。 当安全工程师尝试将权限集分配给有权访问多个账户的 IAM Identity Center 用户时，分配操作会 失败。 安全工程师应采取什么措施来解决此故障？","options_en":{"A":"Create the customer managed policy in every account where the permission set is assigned. Give the customer managed policy the same name and same permissions in each account.","B":"Remove either the AWS managed policy or the customer managed policy from the permission set. Create a second permission set that includes the removed policy. Apply the permission sets separately to the user.","C":"Evaluate the logic of the AWS managed policy and the customer managed policy. Resolve any policy conflicts in the permission set before deployment.","D":"Do not add the new permission set to the user. Instead, edit the user ' s existing permission set to include the AWS managed policy and the customer managed policy."},"options_zh":{"A":"在分配权限集的每个账户中创建客户管理策略。在每个账户中，为该客户管理策略设置相同 的名称和相同的权限。","B":"从权限集中移除 AWS 管理的策略或客户管理的策略。创建第二个包含已移除策略的权限集， 并将这两个权限集分别应用到用户。","C":"评估 AWS 管理策略和客户管理策略的逻辑，在部署前解决权限集中的任何策略冲突。","D":"不要将新的权限集添加给用户，而是编辑用户现有的权限集，以包含 AWS 管理的策略和 客户管理的策略。"},"answer":["A"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Organizations/Governance","Security/IAM"],"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選","research":{"verdict":["A"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"IAM Identity Center never creates the actual customer managed policy content in member accounts. When you attach a customer managed policy to a permission set, you must pre-create an IAM customer managed policy with the exact same name (and path) in every target member account before the permission set can be provisioned/assigned there. If that policy does not already exist in the account, the assignment operation fails outright. AWS's own documentation states this as a required precondition, not just a best practice: 'IAM Identity Center fails to assign the permission set if the policy doesn't exist in your member account.' The permissions granted by the policy do not need to be byte-for-byte identical across accounts, but AWS recommends keeping them identical (e.g., via CloudFormation StackSets) for a consistent access experience — which matches option A's wording. Options B, C, and D misdiagnose the root cause: removing/splitting policies (B) or resolving policy 'conflicts' (C) does nothing because the failure is not about policy logic conflicts but about a missing named policy resource in the target account, and editing an unrelated existing permission set (D) doesn't address the actual assignment failure for the new permission set.","explanation_zh":"IAM Identity Center 本身不會在成員帳戶中建立 customer managed policy 的實際內容。當你把 customer managed policy 附加到 permission set 時，你必須事先在每個要指派該 permission set 的成員帳戶中，建立一個名稱（與路徑）完全相同的 IAM customer managed policy，之後才能佈建／指派該 permission set。如果該 policy 在該帳戶中不存在，指派操作就會直接失敗。AWS 官方文件明確將此列為必要前提條件，而非僅是最佳實務：「如果 policy 在成員帳戶中不存在，IAM Identity Center 會無法指派該 permission set。」policy 授予的權限內容不需要在各帳戶間完全一致，但 AWS 建議（例如透過 CloudFormation StackSets）保持一致以提供一致的存取體驗——這與選項 A 的敘述相符。選項 B、C、D 都誤判了根本原因：移除／拆分 policy（B）或解決 policy「衝突」（C）都無濟於事，因為失敗原因並非 policy 邏輯衝突，而是目標帳戶中缺少同名的 policy 資源；編輯另一個既有 permission set（D）也無法解決這個新 permission set 指派失敗的問題。","distractors":[{"letter":"B","why_en":"Splitting the policies into two permission sets does not solve anything — the customer managed policy still must exist by name in every target member account regardless of which permission set it is attached to. The failure is caused by a missing policy resource, not by combining an AWS managed and customer managed policy together.","why_zh":"把 policy 拆成兩個 permission set 並不能解決問題——不論 customer managed policy 附加在哪個 permission set 上，它仍然必須以相同名稱存在於每個目標成員帳戶中。失敗原因是缺少 policy 資源，而不是因為同時附加了 AWS managed policy 與 customer managed policy。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"There is no indication of a policy logic conflict in the scenario, and AWS documentation does not describe permission set assignment failures as being caused by conflicting policy statements between an AWS managed and customer managed policy. The documented failure mode is a missing customer managed policy in the target account.","why_zh":"情境中並無跡象顯示存在 policy 邏輯衝突，AWS 文件也未將 permission set 指派失敗歸因於 AWS managed policy 與 customer managed policy 之間的敘述衝突。文件記載的失敗原因是目標帳戶中缺少該 customer managed policy。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"Editing a different, existing permission set instead of fixing the new one does not resolve the assignment failure of the new permission set, and abandoning the new permission set entirely is not a real fix — it avoids the problem rather than solving it, and still would not let the company reuse a single custom permission set across multiple accounts as intended.","why_zh":"去編輯另一個既有的 permission set，而不修正新建立的這個，並不能解決新 permission set 的指派失敗問題；直接放棄新的 permission set 也不是真正的修正方式——這只是迴避問題，而且無法讓公司如預期般在多個帳戶中重複使用同一個自訂 permission set。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/singlesignon/latest/userguide/howtocmp.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/singlesignon/latest/userguide/permissionsetcustom.html"]}},{"id":226,"question_en":"A company’s application team needs a new AWS Key Management Service (AWS KMS) customer managed key to use with Amazon S3. The company’s security policy requires separate keys for different AWS services to limit security exposure. How can a security engineer limit the KMS customer managed key to work with only Amazon S3?","question_zh":"公司的应用团队需要一个新的 AWS 密钥管理服务（AWS KMS）客户托管密钥，用于与 Amazon S3 配合使用。根据公司的安全策略，不同 AWS 服务必须使用独立的密钥，以降低安全风险。 安全工程师如何限制KMS客户管理密钥仅与Amazon S3一起使用？","options_en":{"A":"Configure the key policy to allow only Amazon S3 to perform the kms:Encrypt action.","B":"Configure the key policy to allow KMS actions only when the value for the kms:ViaService condition key matches the Amazon S3 service name.","C":"Configure the application’s IAM role policy to allow Amazon S3 to perform the iam:PassRole action.","D":"Configure the application’s IAM role policy to allow only S3 operations when the operations are combined with the KMS customer managed key."},"options_zh":{"A":"配置密钥策略，仅允许 Amazon S3 执行 kms:Encrypt 操作。","B":"配置密钥策略，仅当 kms:ViaService 条件键的值与 Amazon S3 服务名称匹配时，才允许执行 KMS 操作。","C":"配置应用程序的 IAM 角色策略，以允许 Amazon S3 执行 iam:PassRole 操作。","D":"配置应用程序的 IAM 角色策略，仅允许在操作与 KMS 客户管理密钥结合时执行 S3 操作。"},"answer":["B"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Security/IAM","Storage"],"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選","research":{"verdict":["B"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"both","explanation_en":"The kms:ViaService condition key is the AWS-documented mechanism for scoping a KMS key's usable actions to requests that originate from a specific AWS service. AWS's own KMS Developer Guide states that 'kms:ViaService condition key limits use of a KMS key to requests from specified AWS services,' and its reference table explicitly lists Amazon S3 (ViaService name s3.<region>.amazonaws.com) as a supported service. This matches exactly how AWS managed keys are scoped: 'All AWS managed keys use a kms:ViaService condition key in their key policy document. This condition allows the KMS key to be used only for requests that come from the service that created the KMS key.' Option A is wrong because a key policy 'Principal' naming an S3 service principal is not how S3-KMS integration actually authorizes requests (the calling principal is the IAM role/user, not the S3 service, and restricting only kms:Encrypt leaves kms:Decrypt/GenerateDataKey/DescribeKey unrestricted) — it doesn't achieve 'only usable with S3' scoping. Option C (iam:PassRole) is unrelated to KMS-service restriction; PassRole governs passing a role to a service like EC2/Lambda, not KMS key usage scoping. Option D is vague IAM-side wording that doesn't actually constrain which service can invoke the KMS key at the key-policy/resource level, and combining IAM 'S3 operations' with a KMS key reference isn't a real, documented IAM policy construct for this purpose. Therefore B is the correct, docs-grounded answer, and it matches the dump's suggested answer.","explanation_zh":"kms:ViaService 條件鍵是 AWS 官方文件中用來把 KMS 金鑰的可用範圍限制在「特定 AWS 服務發出的請求」的機制。AWS KMS Developer Guide 明確指出:「kms:ViaService condition key limits use of a KMS key to requests from specified AWS services」,且其對照表明確列出 Amazon S3(ViaService 名稱為 s3.<region>.amazonaws.com)為受支援的服務之一。這與 AWS 管理金鑰(AWS managed key)的作法完全一致:「All AWS managed keys use a kms:ViaService condition key in their key policy document. This condition allows the KMS key to be used only for requests that come from the service that created the KMS key.」選項 A 錯誤,因為在金鑰政策中把 Principal 設為 S3 服務主體,並不是 S3 與 KMS 整合實際授權請求的方式(實際呼叫方是 IAM 角色/使用者,而非 S3 服務本身),且只限制 kms:Encrypt 動作也無法涵蓋 kms:Decrypt、GenerateDataKey、DescribeKey 等 S3 實際會用到的動作,無法達成「僅供 S3 使用」的限制效果。選項 C(iam:PassRole)與限制 KMS 金鑰服務範圍完全無關,PassRole 是用來把角色傳遞給像 EC2、Lambda 這類服務,與 KMS 金鑰使用範圍限制無關。選項 D 的敘述模糊,在 IAM 角色政策層級並不能真正限制哪個服務可以呼叫該 KMS 金鑰(這是資源層級/金鑰政策層級的控制),而且「IAM 政策中把 S3 操作與 KMS 金鑰結合」也不是文件中真實存在的政策寫法。因此 B 是有官方文件佐證的正確答案,也與題庫建議答案一致。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"Restricting only kms:Encrypt via a key policy 'Principal' of Amazon S3 does not match how S3-KMS integration actually works (the calling identity is the IAM principal, with S3 acting via a forwarded access session), and it ignores that S3 also needs kms:Decrypt, kms:GenerateDataKey*, and kms:DescribeKey, so it does not truly restrict the key to 'only' S3 usage.","why_zh":"透過金鑰政策把 Principal 設為 Amazon S3 並只限制 kms:Encrypt,並不符合 S3 與 KMS 實際整合的運作方式(實際呼叫身分是 IAM 主體,S3 透過 forwarded access session 代為呼叫),而且忽略了 S3 也需要 kms:Decrypt、kms:GenerateDataKey*、kms:DescribeKey 等動作,因此無法真正把金鑰限制為「僅」供 S3 使用。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"iam:PassRole controls granting a role to a service (e.g., EC2 or Lambda) so that service can assume it; it has no bearing on restricting which AWS service can use a given KMS key, so it does not solve the stated requirement.","why_zh":"iam:PassRole 是用來控制把角色授予某服務(例如 EC2 或 Lambda)以便該服務可以擔任該角色,與限制哪個 AWS 服務可以使用某個 KMS 金鑰完全無關,因此無法解決題目要求。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"An IAM role policy that allows 'only S3 operations when combined with the KMS key' is not a real, documented IAM/KMS policy construct, and IAM identity policies on the caller's role cannot enforce a resource-side restriction that the KMS key itself may only be invoked via S3 by any principal — that enforcement belongs in the key policy via kms:ViaService.","why_zh":"「IAM 角色政策僅允許『搭配該 KMS 金鑰時的 S3 操作』」並非真實存在、有文件依據的 IAM/KMS 政策寫法,且呼叫者角色上的 IAM 身分政策無法在資源端強制「此 KMS 金鑰只能經由 S3 被任何主體呼叫」這種限制,這種強制力必須寫在金鑰政策(key policy)中,透過 kms:ViaService 達成。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/kms/latest/developerguide/conditions-kms.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/kms/latest/developerguide/references.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/kms/latest/developerguide/service-integration.html"]}},{"id":227,"question_en":"A company runs an application on an Amazon EC2 instance. The application generates invoices and stores them in an Amazon S3 bucket. The instance profile that is attached to the instance has appropriate access to the S3 bucket. The company needs to share each invoice with multiple clients that do not have AWS credentials. Each client must be able to download only the client ' s own invoices. Clients must download their invoices within 1 hour of invoice creation. Clients must use only temporary credentials to access the company ' s AWS resources. Which additional step will meet these requirements?","question_zh":"一家公司在一个 Amazon EC2 实例上运行应用程序。该应用程序生成发票并将其存储在 Amazon S3 存储桶中。附加到该 实例的实例配置文件拥有对 S3 存储桶的适当访问权限。公司需要将每份发票与多个没有 AWS 凭据的客户共享。每个客 户只能下载属于自己的发票，且必须在发票创建后 1 小时内完成下载。客户只能使用临时凭据访问公司的 AWS 资源。 哪一步额外措施能够满足这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Update the S3 bucket policy to ensure that clients that use pre-signed URLs have the S3:Get* permission and the S3:List* permission to access S3 objects in the bucket.","B":"Add a StringEquals condition to the IAM role policy for the EC2 instance profile. Configure the policy condition to restrict access based on the s3:ResourceTag/ClientId tag of each invoice. Tag each generated invoice with the ID of its corresponding client.","C":"Update the script to use AWS Security Token Service (AWS STS) to obtain new credentials each time the script runs by assuming a new role that has S3:GetObject permissions. Use the credentials to generate the pre-signed URLs.","D":"Generate an access key and a secret key for an IAM user that has S3:GetObject permissions on the S3 bucket. Embed the keys into the script. Use the keys to generate the pre-signed URLs."},"options_zh":{"A":"更新 S3 存储桶策略，确保使用预签名 URL 的客户端拥有 S3:Get* 和 S3:List* 权限，以便访问存储桶中的 S3 对象。","B":"为 EC2 实例配置文件的 IAM 角色策略添加一个 StringEquals 条件。将策略条件设置为根据每张发票的 s3: ResourceTag/ClientId 标签限制访问权限。为每张生成的发票添加其对应客户的 ID 作为标签。","C":"更新脚本，使其每次运行时都通过 AWS 安全令牌服务（AWS STS）获取新的凭证，方法是假设一个具有 S3: GetObject 权限的新角色。然后使用这些凭证生成预签名 URL。","D":"为具有 S3 存储桶 S3:GetObject 权限的 IAM 用户生成访问密钥和秘密密钥，并将这些密钥嵌入脚本中。使用这些密 钥生成预签名 URL。"},"answer":["B"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Security/IAM","Storage","Compute"],"difficulty":2,"diff_why":"題庫與社群皆錯","research":{"verdict":["C"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"neither","explanation_en":"The scenario layers three constraints onto a presigned-URL solution: (1) credential-less clients can only be handed a presigned URL, since 'the credentials used by the presigned URL are those of the AWS Identity and Access Management (IAM) principal who generated the URL' (S3 User Guide, using-presigned-url.html); (2) only temporary credentials may be used; and (3) the link must stop working after exactly 1 hour. The same page's 'Who can create a presigned URL' table is decisive: for 'IAM role credentials used by Amazon EC2 instances,' a presigned URL is 'Valid for the duration of the role credentials (typically 6 hours),' and in general 'a presigned URL expires when the credential expires... even if the URL was created with a later expiration time.' So if the script just calls generate_presigned_url() straight off the EC2 instance profile's default session, the link inherits that session's ~6-hour lifetime — it cannot be reliably capped at 1 hour, violating the requirement even though the credentials are technically 'temporary.' Option C is the fix: have the script call AWS STS (e.g., AssumeRole with an explicit DurationSeconds, per docs.aws.amazon.com/IAM/latest/UserGuide/id_credentials_temp_request.html) each time it runs, obtaining a fresh, narrowly-scoped (S3:GetObject-only) temporary credential set whose own expiration is bounded to the desired ~1-hour window, and generating the presigned URL from that session. Because the URL's validity is hard-capped by 'the duration of the temporary credentials' (not just the Expires parameter, which the credential expiration can override downward), this is the only option that reliably enforces both 'temporary credentials only' and the 1-hour cutoff; per-invoice object keys already ensure each unique URL only reaches its own client. Option B never produces a shareable link at all — restricting the EC2 role's own IAM policy with a static s3:ResourceTag/ClientId condition only changes what objects that single instance role can touch (and, as a static, non-session-scoped condition, would break the app's ability to serve any client other than the one hardcoded ClientId), so it does not deliver anything to a credential-less client. Option A misreads presigned-URL authorization — it is the signer's (the instance role's) permissions that matter, not a bucket-policy grant to the anonymous downloading client, and adding S3:List* is both unneeded and a privilege-escalation risk (enumeration of other clients' invoices). Option D hardcodes a permanent IAM user access key/secret in the script, directly violating 'must use only temporary credentials.'","explanation_zh":"此情境同時對 pre-signed URL 方案疊加三個限制:(1) 沒有 AWS 憑證的客戶只能拿到 pre-signed URL,因為官方文件指出「the credentials used by the presigned URL are those of the AWS Identity and Access Management (IAM) principal who generated the URL」(S3 User Guide, using-presigned-url.html);(2) 只能使用臨時憑證;(3) 連結必須在剛好 1 小時後失效。同一頁「Who can create a presigned URL」的對照表給出關鍵依據:對於「IAM role credentials used by Amazon EC2 instances」,pre-signed URL「Valid for the duration of the role credentials (typically 6 hours)」,並且一般而言「a presigned URL expires when the credential expires... even if the URL was created with a later expiration time」。也就是說,若腳本只是直接拿 EC2 instance profile 預設 session 呼叫 generate_presigned_url(),連結會繼承該 session 約 6 小時的有效期——無法可靠地限制在 1 小時內,即使憑證本身技術上算「臨時」,仍不符合題目要求。選項 C 正是解方:讓腳本每次執行時呼叫 AWS STS(例如以明確的 DurationSeconds 呼叫 AssumeRole,參見 docs.aws.amazon.com/IAM/latest/UserGuide/id_credentials_temp_request.html),取得一組全新、範圍窄(僅 S3:GetObject)、且本身效期即被限制在約 1 小時視窗內的臨時憑證,再用這組 session 產生 pre-signed URL。由於 URL 的有效期會被「臨時憑證本身的效期」硬性封頂(而不只是 Expires 參數——憑證到期時間可以把它往下蓋過),這是唯一能同時可靠達成「僅用臨時憑證」與「1 小時內失效」兩項要求的選項;而每張 invoice 對應獨立的 S3 物件金鑰,也已確保每個獨一 URL 只會送到對應客戶手中。選項 B 從頭到尾都沒有產生任何可分享的連結——用靜態的 s3:ResourceTag/ClientId 條件限制 EC2 角色自身的 IAM 政策,只會改變這個單一 instance role 能碰到哪些物件(而且作為靜態、非隨 session 動態比對的條件,反而會讓應用程式除了寫死的那個 ClientId 外無法再服務任何其他客戶),因此完全沒有交付任何東西給沒有憑證的客戶。選項 A 誤解了 pre-signed URL 的授權機制——真正重要的是簽署者(instance role)本身的權限,而不是 bucket policy 授予匿名下載端客戶的權限,額外加上 S3:List* 既無必要,又有讓客戶列舉其他客戶 invoice 的權限擴大風險。選項 D 則是把永久性的 IAM user access key/secret 寫死在腳本中,直接違反「必須只使用臨時憑證」的要求。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"Presigned-URL authorization is governed by the permissions of the IAM principal who signs the URL (here, the EC2 instance role, which the scenario already says has 'appropriate access'), not by a bucket policy statement aimed at the anonymous, credential-less downloading client; adding S3:List* is unnecessary and risks letting a client enumerate/access other clients' invoices, breaking the 'own invoices only' requirement, and it does nothing to enforce the 1-hour or temporary-credential constraints.","why_zh":"pre-signed URL 的授權取決於簽署該 URL 的 IAM 主體(此處為題目已說明「已具備適當存取權」的 EC2 instance role)的權限,而不是靠 bucket policy 去對付根本沒有 AWS 身分的匿名下載端客戶;額外授予 S3:List* 既無必要,也可能讓客戶列舉/存取到其他客戶的 invoice,違反「僅限本人 invoice」的要求,且完全無助於滿足 1 小時或臨時憑證的限制。"},{"letter":"B","why_en":"A static s3:ResourceTag/ClientId condition on the EC2 instance profile's own IAM policy only constrains which objects that one shared application role can touch — it never generates or delivers a presigned URL to a credential-less client, and because it is a fixed condition value (not a per-request/session-scoped tag match), it would actually prevent the app from serving any client other than the single hardcoded ClientId, breaking the multi-client requirement outright.","why_zh":"在 EC2 instance profile 自身的 IAM 政策上加上靜態的 s3:ResourceTag/ClientId 條件,只會限制這個共用的單一應用程式角色能碰到哪些物件——它完全沒有產生或交付任何 pre-signed URL 給沒有憑證的客戶,而且由於這是固定值條件(而非隨請求/session 動態比對的標籤),實際上會讓應用程式除了那個寫死的 ClientId 外,無法再服務任何其他客戶,直接違背多客戶的需求。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"Embedding a long-lived IAM user access key and secret key directly in the script is exactly the permanent-credential pattern the scenario forbids ('must use only temporary credentials'), regardless of whether it can technically generate a working presigned URL.","why_zh":"把長期有效的 IAM user access key 與 secret key 直接寫死在腳本裡,正是題目明確禁止的永久憑證做法(「必須只使用臨時憑證」),無論它在技術上是否能產生可用的 pre-signed URL,都不符合要求。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonS3/latest/userguide/using-presigned-url.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonS3/latest/userguide/ShareObjectPreSignedURL.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/IAM/latest/UserGuide/id_credentials_temp_request.html"]}},{"id":228,"question_en":"A security engineer discovers that a company ' s user passwords have no required minimum length. The company uses the following identity providers (IdPs): • AWS Identity and Access Management (IAM) federated with on-premises Active Directory • Amazon Cognito user pools that contain the user database for an AWS Cloud application Which combination of actions should the security engineer take to implement a required minimum password length? (Select TWO.)","question_zh":"一名安全工程师发现，该公司用户的密码没有设置最低长度要求。该公司使用了以下身份提供商（IdP）： • AWS 身份和访问管理（IAM）与本地 Active Directory 实现联合 • 包含 AWS 云应用程序用户数据库的 Amazon Cognito 用户池 安全工程师应采取哪些操作组合来实施所需的最小密码长度？（选择两项。）","options_en":{"A":"Update the password length policy in the IAM configuration.","B":"Update the password length policy in the Amazon Cognito configuration.","C":"Update the password length policy in the on-premises Active Directory configuration.","D":"Create an SCP in AWS Organizations to enforce minimum password length.","E":"Create an IAM policy with a minimum password length condition."},"options_zh":{"A":"在 IAM 配置中更新密码长度策略。","B":"在 Amazon Cognito 配置中更新密码长度策略。","C":"更新本地 Active Directory 配置中的密码长度策略。","D":"在 AWS Organizations 中创建一个 SCP，以强制执行密码最小长度。","E":"创建一个包含最小密码长度条件的 IAM 策略。"},"answer":["B","C"],"multi":true,"vote":{},"tags":["Organizations/Governance","Security/IAM","Database"],"difficulty":2,"diff_why":"複選","research":{"verdict":["B","C"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"both","explanation_en":"Password length is enforced at the identity store that actually authenticates the user, not at IAM. For the AWS Cloud application, Amazon Cognito user pools store password hashes for local (non-federated) users and expose their own password policy setting (minimum length, complexity, history) in the user pool configuration — this must be updated directly in Cognito (Option B). For the on-premises Active Directory users who access AWS via IAM federation (e.g., SAML/AD Connector), those users authenticate against Active Directory itself; IAM never stores or validates their password, so the IAM account password policy (which only governs native IAM users' console passwords) has no effect on them. The minimum length requirement must instead be set in the on-premises AD password policy (Option C), which then flows through to federated sign-in. Options A and E both incorrectly assume IAM can control the password length for federated identities — IAM's password policy and IAM policy conditions only ever apply to IAM user credentials, never to externally-federated principals. Option D (SCP) is a permissions guardrail across AWS Organizations accounts/API actions and has no mechanism for password complexity/length enforcement at all.","explanation_zh":"密碼長度規則必須在真正驗證使用者身分的來源系統上設定,而非在 IAM 上設定。針對 AWS 雲端應用程式,Amazon Cognito 使用者集區會為本機(非聯合)使用者儲存密碼雜湊,並在使用者集區設定中提供自己的密碼原則(最小長度、複雜度、歷史紀錄)——必須直接在 Cognito 中更新(選項 B)。針對透過 IAM 聯合登入(例如 SAML/AD Connector)存取 AWS 的地端 Active Directory 使用者,這些使用者是向 Active Directory 本身進行驗證;IAM 從未儲存或驗證他們的密碼,因此 IAM 帳戶密碼原則(僅管控原生 IAM 使用者的主控台密碼)對他們毫無作用。最小長度要求必須改在地端 AD 密碼原則中設定(選項 C),之後才會套用到聯合登入。選項 A 與 E 都錯誤地假設 IAM 可以控制聯合身分的密碼長度——IAM 密碼原則與 IAM 政策條件永遠只適用於 IAM 使用者憑證,不適用於外部聯合的主體。選項 D(SCP)是跨 AWS Organizations 帳戶/API 動作的權限防護機制,完全沒有強制密碼複雜度或長度的機制。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"The IAM account password policy only governs passwords of native IAM users signing into the AWS Management Console; it does not apply to users federated in from an external IdP like on-premises Active Directory.","why_zh":"IAM 帳戶密碼原則只管控原生 IAM 使用者登入 AWS 管理主控台的密碼,不適用於從外部 IdP(如地端 Active Directory)聯合登入的使用者。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"SCPs in AWS Organizations restrict which API actions/permissions accounts can use; they have no capability to enforce password complexity or length requirements for any identity store.","why_zh":"AWS Organizations 的 SCP 是用來限制帳戶可使用的 API 動作/權限,並沒有能力對任何身分儲存庫強制執行密碼複雜度或長度要求。"},{"letter":"E","why_en":"There is no IAM policy condition key that enforces password minimum length; IAM policies control authorization to actions/resources, not authentication-time password complexity rules.","why_zh":"IAM 並沒有可強制密碼最小長度的政策條件鍵;IAM 政策管控的是對動作/資源的授權,而非驗證時的密碼複雜度規則。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/IAM/latest/UserGuide/id_credentials_passwords_account-policy.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/cognito/latest/developerguide/managing-users-passwords.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/cognito/latest/developerguide/how-to-create-user-accounts.html"]}},{"id":229,"question_en":"A company ' s public website consists of an Application Load Balancer (ALB), a set of Amazon EC2 instances that run a stateless application behind the ALB, and an Amazon DynamoDB table from which the application reads data. The company is concerned about malicious scanning and DDoS attacks. The company wants to impose a restriction in which each client IP address can read the data only3 times in any 5-minute period. Which solution will meet this requirement with the LEAST effort?","question_zh":"一家公司的公共网站由一个应用负载均衡器（ALB）、一组运行在ALB后的无状态应用程序的Amazon EC2实例，以及一个供应 用程序读取数据的Amazon DynamoDB表组成。该公司担心恶意扫描和DDoS攻击，希望实施一项限制措施：每个客户端IP地址 在任意5分钟内只能读取数据3次。 哪种解决方案能以最少的努力满足这一要求？","options_en":{"A":"Set up AWS WAF in front of the ALB. Create a rule that blocks requests that exceed the limit of 3 requests in any 5-minute period for each IP address.","B":"Create an AWS Lambda function based on an Amazon CloudWatch request. Configure the Lambda function to count the requests for each IP address in rolling 5-minute intervals and to provide notification if the count exceeds 3.","C":"Modify the EC2 application to count the source IP address of requests and calculate a rolling 5-minute sum. Return an error message if the count sum is greater than 3.","D":"Add source IP address and request time to the DynamoDB table. Add a 5-minute TTL setting based on request time. Change the read capacity of the DynamoDB table throughput to 3."},"options_zh":{"A":"在ALB前面设置AWS WAF，创建一条规则，阻止每个IP地址在任意5分钟内超过3次请求的访问。","B":"基于 Amazon CloudWatch 请求创建一个 AWS Lambda 函数。配置该 Lambda 函数，以滚动的 5 分钟间隔统计每个 IP 地址的请求数量，并在数量超过 3 时发出通知。","C":"修改EC2应用程序，统计请求的源IP地址数量，并计算滚动5分钟内的总和。如果计数总和大于3，则返回错误消息。","D":"将源IP地址和请求时间添加到DynamoDB表中。根据请求时间设置5分钟的TTL（生存时间）。将DynamoDB表的读取容 量调整为3。"},"answer":["A"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Networking/DNS","Security/IAM","Compute","Database","Monitoring/Ops"],"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選","research":{"verdict":["A"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"AWS WAF rate-based rule statements are purpose-built for exactly this scenario: they count incoming requests per client IP address (or other aggregation key) over a rolling evaluation window (60/120/300/600 seconds, with 300s/5 minutes as the default) and automatically apply an action (e.g., Block) once the count exceeds a configured threshold. Attaching a Web ACL with a rate-based rule to the ALB requires no code changes to the stateless EC2 application and no new infrastructure — this is the least-effort, purpose-built AWS feature for per-IP request throttling against scanning/DDoS. By contrast: Option B (Lambda + CloudWatch) only counts and notifies — it does not block or restrict traffic, so it fails the stated requirement, and it is far more custom engineering effort. Option C requires modifying the application code and, because the architecture is a stateless, multi-instance fleet behind an ALB, each EC2 instance would need a shared/centralized counter (e.g., ElastiCache or DynamoDB) to track a client's requests across all instances correctly — this is significantly more effort and still reinvents what WAF already provides. Option D is not a coherent rate-limiting mechanism at all: DynamoDB read capacity throttles the table's overall aggregate throughput, not per-source-IP request counts, so it cannot enforce a per-client limit. Note a documentation nuance: AWS WAF's rate-based rule enforces a rate limit no lower than 10 requests per evaluation window (and rate limiting is applied 'near' the limit, not with an exact guarantee), so an exact threshold of 3 is below the documented floor — but among the four options, A is still the only one that actually implements a per-IP, blocking rate restriction with minimal operational effort, which is what the question is testing.","explanation_zh":"AWS WAF 的 rate-based rule 正是為此情境設計:它會依用戶端 IP(或其他聚合鍵)在滾動的評估視窗(60/120/300/600 秒,預設 300 秒即 5 分鐘)內計算請求數,一旦超過設定門檻就自動套用動作(例如 Block)。只要在 ALB 前面的 Web ACL 加上一條 rate-based rule,完全不需要修改無狀態的 EC2 應用程式碼,也不需要新增基礎設施——這是針對「依 IP 限制存取次數以防掃描/DDoS」這個需求,AWS 原生且最省力的做法。相較之下:選項 B(Lambda + CloudWatch)只會計數並發出通知,並不會真的阻擋或限制流量,不符合題目「imposeを restriction」的要求,而且屬於高度客製化開發,效力遠不及原生功能。選項 C 需要修改應用程式碼,且因為架構是無狀態、多台 EC2 執行個體共同服務於 ALB 之後,每台執行個體若各自計數將無法正確彙總同一用戶端跨執行個體的請求數,必須另外導入共享儲存(如 ElastiCache 或 DynamoDB)才能正確運作,這遠比使用 WAF 費工。選項 D 完全不是合理的限流機制:DynamoDB 的讀取容量是控制資料表整體的總體吞吐量,並非依來源 IP 個別計數,無法達成「每個用戶端」的限制。需注意一個文件細節:AWS WAF 的 rate-based rule 所能設定的最低門檻是每個評估視窗 10 個請求(且限流是「接近」門檻值執行,並非精確保證),因此題目要求的「剛好 3 次」實際上低於文件記載的下限——但在四個選項中,A 仍是唯一真正以最少心力實作「依 IP 進行阻擋式限流」的方案,也正是本題想測試的重點。","distractors":[{"letter":"B","why_en":"A Lambda function driven by CloudWatch only counts requests and sends a notification when the threshold is exceeded — it does not block or throttle the client, so it fails to 'impose a restriction' as required, and it is substantially more custom effort than a managed WAF rule.","why_zh":"由 CloudWatch 觸發的 Lambda 只會計數並在超過門檻時發送通知,並不會阻擋或限制用戶端流量,無法滿足題目「施加限制」的要求,而且比起使用受管理的 WAF 規則需要更多客製化開發心力。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"Modifying the stateless EC2 application to track per-IP rolling counts requires either losing statelessness or adding a shared datastore (e.g., DynamoDB/ElastiCache) so all instances see a consistent count for each client IP — far more development and operational effort than a built-in WAF rate-based rule.","why_zh":"修改無狀態的 EC2 應用程式來追蹤每個 IP 的滾動計數,需要放棄無狀態設計或另外導入共享資料儲存(如 DynamoDB/ElastiCache)才能讓所有執行個體對同一用戶端 IP 有一致的計數,這比使用內建的 WAF rate-based rule 需要多得多的開發與維運心力。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"DynamoDB provisioned/read throughput settings and TTL govern the table's overall capacity and item expiration; they do not count or limit requests per source IP address, so this option cannot implement a per-client rate restriction at all.","why_zh":"DynamoDB 的讀取容量設定與 TTL 是用來控管資料表整體的容量與項目過期,並不能依來源 IP 計數或限制請求次數,因此此選項根本無法實作「每個用戶端」的限流需求。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/waf/latest/developerguide/waf-rule-statement-type-rate-based.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/waf/latest/developerguide/waf-rule-statement-type-rate-based-high-level-settings.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/waf/latest/developerguide/waf-rule-statement-type-rate-based-caveats.html"]}},{"id":230,"question_en":"A corporate cloud security policy states that communications between the company ' s VPC and KMS must travel entirely within the AWS network and not use public service endpoints. Which combination of the following actions MOST satisfies this requirement? (Select TWO.)","question_zh":"企业云安全策略规定，公司VPC与KMS之间的通信必须完全在AWS网络内部进行，不得使用公共服务端点。 以下哪两项操作的组合最能满足此要求？（选择两项。）","options_en":{"A":"Add theaws:sourceVpcecondition to the AWS KMS key policy referencing the company ' s VPC endpoint ID.","B":"Remove the VPC internet gateway from the VPC and add a virtual private gateway to the VPC to prevent direct, public internet connectivity.","C":"Create a VPC endpoint for AWS KMS withprivate DNS enabled.","D":"Use the KMS Import Key feature to securely transfer the AWS KMS key over a VPN.","E":"Add the following condition to the AWS KMS key policy: \" aws:SourceIp \" : \" 10.0.0.0/16 \" ."},"options_zh":{"A":"将 aws：sourceVpc 条件添加到引用公司 VPC 端点 ID 的 AWS KMS 密钥策略中。","B":"从VPC中移除互联网网关，并向VPC添加虚拟私人网关，以防止直接的公共互联网连接。","C":"创建一个启用了私有 DNS 的 AWS KMS VPC 终端节点。","D":"使用 KMS 导入密钥功能，通过 VPN 安全地传输 AWS KMS 密钥。","E":"向 AWS KMS 密钥策略中添加以下条件：“aws:SourceIp”：“10.0.0.0/16”。"},"answer":["A","C"],"multi":true,"vote":{},"tags":["Networking/DNS","Security/IAM"],"difficulty":2,"diff_why":"複選","research":{"verdict":["A","C"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"community","explanation_en":"The requirement is that all traffic between the VPC and AWS KMS stay entirely within the AWS network and never traverse a public service endpoint. AWS KMS documentation states this outcome directly and by name: 'You can connect directly to AWS KMS through a private interface endpoint in your virtual private cloud (VPC). When you use an interface VPC endpoint, communication between your VPC and AWS KMS is conducted entirely within the AWS network' (kms-vpc-endpoint.html). So option C — creating an interface VPC endpoint (PrivateLink) for AWS KMS — is the mechanism that actually removes the public endpoint from the data path. Enabling private DNS on that endpoint is what makes this transparent: it causes the standard public AWS KMS hostname (kms.<region>.amazonaws.com) used by the AWS SDK/CLI/KMS clients to resolve to the private VPC endpoint IP instead of a public IP, so existing application code and AWS service integrations automatically route over PrivateLink without being reconfigured to a vpce-specific hostname (vpce-create-endpoint.html, vpce-connect.html). Merely creating the endpoint without private DNS would still work but would require every caller to specify the VPC endpoint-specific DNS name explicitly — enabling private DNS is what makes the requirement met by default for all traffic. However, creating the VPC endpoint alone only makes the private path available; it does not force traffic to actually use it (VPC-wide, an admin, a NAT gateway path, or a resource without endpoint routing could still theoretically reach the public endpoint if IAM/network policy allows). That's where option A comes in: adding the aws:sourceVpce condition key to the KMS key policy, scoped to the company's specific VPC endpoint ID, denies/restricts KMS key operations unless the request arrives via that VPC endpoint. AWS's own KMS documentation gives this exact pattern: a key-policy Deny statement using 'Condition': {'StringNotEquals': {'aws:sourceVpce': 'vpce-...'}} to 'restrict usage to my VPC endpoint' (vpce-policy-condition.html). Together, C establishes the all-AWS-network path and A enforces that KMS only honors requests that actually traveled that path — which is the combination that MOST satisfies the stated policy.","explanation_zh":"此題要求 VPC 與 AWS KMS 之間的所有通訊完全留在 AWS 網路內,絕不經過公開的服務端點。AWS KMS 官方文件直接明確指出這個效果:「您可以透過虛擬私有雲 (VPC) 中的私有介面端點直接連線至 AWS KMS。使用介面 VPC 端點時,VPC 與 AWS KMS 之間的通訊完全在 AWS 網路內進行」(kms-vpc-endpoint.html)。因此選項 C——為 AWS KMS 建立介面 VPC 端點(PrivateLink)——正是真正將公開端點從資料路徑中移除的機制。在該端點上啟用私有 DNS,則是讓這件事對應用程式透明化的關鍵:它會讓 AWS SDK/CLI/KMS 用戶端所使用的標準公開 AWS KMS 主機名稱(kms.<region>.amazonaws.com)解析到私有 VPC 端點的 IP,而非公開 IP,使現有的應用程式碼與 AWS 服務整合自動改走 PrivateLink,而不需重新設定成 vpce 專屬主機名稱(vpce-create-endpoint.html、vpce-connect.html)。若只建立端點而不啟用私有 DNS,雖然仍可運作,但每個呼叫端都必須明確指定該 VPC 端點專屬的 DNS 名稱——啟用私有 DNS 才能讓「所有流量」預設就符合這項要求。然而,單純建立 VPC 端點只是讓私有路徑「可用」,並不會強制所有流量實際使用它(理論上,若 IAM/網路政策允許,VPC 內其他路徑、管理者操作或未經端點路由的資源仍可能觸及公開端點)。這正是選項 A 的作用所在:在 KMS 金鑰政策中加入 aws:sourceVpce 條件鍵,並指定該公司特定的 VPC 端點 ID,可拒絕/限制 KMS 金鑰操作,除非請求是透過該 VPC 端點送達。AWS 官方 KMS 文件正好給出這個模式:金鑰政策中使用 Deny 陳述式搭配 'Condition': {'StringNotEquals': {'aws:sourceVpce': 'vpce-...'}} 來「將使用限制在我的 VPC 端點」(vpce-policy-condition.html)。C 建立了完全在 AWS 網路內的路徑,A 則強制 KMS 只接受確實透過該路徑送達的請求——兩者合併正是最能滿足此政策要求的組合。","distractors":[{"letter":"B","why_en":"Removing the internet gateway and adding a virtual private gateway changes how the VPC reaches the public internet/on-premises network over VPN or Direct Connect, but it does nothing to change how traffic to AWS KMS is routed. Without a VPC interface endpoint for KMS, KMS API calls still resolve to KMS's public regional endpoint and traverse it (via NAT/VPN egress if internet access exists through another path, or fail if it doesn't) — a virtual private gateway is for VPC-to-corporate-network connectivity, not VPC-to-AWS-service PrivateLink connectivity, so it is irrelevant to keeping KMS traffic off public endpoints.","why_zh":"移除網際網路閘道並加入虛擬私有閘道,改變的是 VPC 透過 VPN 或 Direct Connect 連接公開網際網路/內部部署網路的方式,但完全不會改變前往 AWS KMS 的流量路由方式。若沒有為 KMS 建立 VPC 介面端點,KMS API 呼叫仍會解析到 KMS 的公開區域端點並經由該端點傳送(若透過其他路徑仍有網際網路存取則經 NAT/VPN 出口,若無則失敗)——虛擬私有閘道是用於 VPC 對企業網路的連線,而非 VPC 對 AWS 服務的 PrivateLink 連線,因此與讓 KMS 流量避開公開端點無關。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"KMS Import Key (Bring Your Own Key) lets you import your own cryptographic key material into a KMS key so AWS does not generate it, but it is unrelated to network path or endpoint routing — it does not use a VPN to 'transfer the AWS KMS key,' and the KMS key material itself never leaves AWS once imported (it stays in the KMS key store). This option misdescribes the feature and does not address whether API traffic to KMS travels over public or private network paths.","why_zh":"KMS Import Key(自帶金鑰,BYOK)功能是讓您將自有的加密金鑰材料匯入 KMS 金鑰,使該金鑰材料不是由 AWS 產生,但這與網路路徑或端點路由無關——它並不會透過 VPN 來「傳輸 AWS KMS 金鑰」,且金鑰材料一旦匯入後就留在 KMS 金鑰儲存區內、不會離開 AWS。此選項對該功能的描述有誤,也完全沒有解決 KMS API 流量究竟走公開還是私有網路路徑的問題。"},{"letter":"E","why_en":"AWS KMS documentation explicitly warns that the aws:sourceIp condition key 'is not effective when the request comes from an Amazon VPC endpoint' and directs readers to use aws:sourceVpce or aws:sourceVpc instead for restricting requests to a VPC endpoint (vpce-policy-condition.html). A private IP CIDR condition also does nothing to force traffic onto a private network path in the first place — it is a request-filtering condition, not a network-routing control, so it cannot satisfy 'travel entirely within the AWS network' on its own, and per AWS's own guidance it is the wrong condition key for VPC-endpoint-scoped enforcement.","why_zh":"AWS KMS 文件明確警告,aws:sourceIp 條件鍵「在請求來自 Amazon VPC 端點時無效」,並指示應改用 aws:sourceVpce 或 aws:sourceVpc 來限制請求必須透過 VPC 端點送達(vpce-policy-condition.html)。此外,私有 IP CIDR 條件本身也不會強制流量一開始就走私有網路路徑——它只是請求過濾條件,而非網路路由控制,因此單靠它無法滿足「完全在 AWS 網路內傳輸」的要求,而且依 AWS 官方指引,這也是用於 VPC 端點範圍限制時錯誤的條件鍵。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/kms/latest/developerguide/kms-vpc-endpoint.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/kms/latest/developerguide/vpce-policy-condition.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/kms/latest/developerguide/vpce-create-endpoint.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/kms/latest/developerguide/vpce-connect.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/kms/latest/developerguide/conditions-aws.html"]}},{"id":231,"question_en":"A company has configured an organization in AWS Organizations for its AWS accounts. AWS CloudTrail is enabled in all AWS Regions. A security engineer must implement a solution toprevent CloudTrail from being disabled. Which solution will meet this requirement?","question_zh":"一家公司已在 AWS Organizations 中为其 AWS 账户配置了组织结构，并在所有 AWS 区域启用了 AWS CloudTrail。 安全工程师必须实施一项解决方案，以防止CloudTrail被禁用。 哪种解决方案能满足这一要求？","options_en":{"A":"Enable CloudTrail log file integrity validation from the organization ' s management account.","B":"Enable server-side encryption with AWS KMS keys (SSE-KMS) for CloudTrail logs. Create a KMS key. Attach a policy to the key to prevent decryption of the logs.","C":"Create a service control policy (SCP) that includes an explicitDenyrule for the cloudtrail:StopLogging action and the cloudtrail:DeleteTrail action. Attach the SCP to the root OU.","D":"Create IAM policies for all the company ' s users to prevent the users from performing the DescribeTrails action and the GetTrailStatus action."},"options_zh":{"A":"从组织的管理账户启用 CloudTrail 日志文件完整性验证。","B":"为 CloudTrail 日志启用使用 AWS KMS 密钥的服务器端加密（SSE-KMS）。创建一个 KMS 密钥，并将策略附加到该 密钥，以防止日志被解密。","C":"创建一个服务控制策略（SCP），其中包含针对 cloudtrail：StopLogging 和 cloudtrail:DeleteTrail 操作的明确拒绝规则， 并将该 SCP 附加到根组织单元。","D":"为公司所有用户创建 IAM 策略，以防止用户执行 DescribeTrails 和 GetTrailStatus 操作。"},"answer":["C"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Organizations/Governance","Security/IAM","Monitoring/Ops"],"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選","research":{"verdict":["C"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"AWS's own AWS Organizations tutorial 'Creating and configuring an organization' builds exactly this scenario: it creates an SCP named 'Block CloudTrail Configuration Actions' that explicitly denies cloudtrail:DeleteTrail, cloudtrail:StopLogging (plus CreateTrail/UpdateTrail/StartLogging/AddTags/RemoveTags) on all CloudTrail resources, and attaches it to the organization's Root — with the doc stating verbatim that this is done 'so that it affects all member accounts to prevent anyone from altering the way that you configured CloudTrail.' A service control policy (SCP) is a preventive, organization-wide guardrail evaluated before IAM policy evaluation: it sets the maximum available permissions for every principal (including account administrators with AdministratorAccess) in every member account, and an explicit Deny in an SCP cannot be overridden by any identity-based or resource-based policy in that account. Attaching an SCP with an explicit Deny on cloudtrail:StopLogging and cloudtrail:DeleteTrail to the root OU cascades that restriction to every OU and account below it, which is exactly what the requirement — 'prevent CloudTrail from being disabled' organization-wide — calls for (SCPs never restrict the management account itself, which is the expected, standard caveat). This is the only option that actually removes the ability to disable CloudTrail at the API level across the whole organization. Option A (log file integrity validation) only lets you detect after the fact whether delivered log files were tampered with or deleted; it does nothing to stop someone from calling StopLogging or DeleteTrail in the first place. Option B (SSE-KMS with a restrictive key policy) protects confidentiality/decryptability of already-delivered log content, but has no bearing on the CloudTrail control-plane actions that start/stop logging or delete a trail. Option D (IAM policies denying DescribeTrails/GetTrailStatus) targets read-only status-check actions rather than the actual disable actions (StopLogging, DeleteTrail, UpdateTrail), applies only to the specific IAM identities you remember to attach it to (missing roles, other accounts, and the root user), and can be edited or detached by anyone with sufficient IAM permissions — unlike an SCP, which only the management account can manage.","explanation_zh":"AWS 官方 AWS Organizations 教學文件「Creating and configuring an organization」建立的正是這個情境:文件建立一個名為 'Block CloudTrail Configuration Actions' 的 SCP,明確拒絕 cloudtrail:DeleteTrail、cloudtrail:StopLogging(以及 CreateTrail/UpdateTrail/StartLogging/AddTags/RemoveTags)對所有 CloudTrail 資源的存取,並將此 SCP 附加到組織的 Root——文件原文明確指出這樣做是「so that it affects all member accounts to prevent anyone from altering the way that you configured CloudTrail(讓它影響所有成員帳戶,防止任何人變更你設定 CloudTrail 的方式)」。服務控制原則(SCP)是組織層級的預防性護欄,在 IAM 原則評估之前就會被評估:它為每個成員帳戶中的每個主體(包括擁有 AdministratorAccess 的帳戶管理員)設定可用權限的上限,且 SCP 中明確的 Deny 無法被該帳戶中任何身分型或資源型原則覆寫。將包含明確拒絕 cloudtrail:StopLogging 與 cloudtrail:DeleteTrail 動作的 SCP 附加到根 OU,會使此限制向下延伸至其下的每個 OU 與帳戶,這正好符合題目要求——在整個組織範圍內「防止 CloudTrail 被停用」(SCP 本身不限制管理帳戶,這是標準且預期的例外情況)。這是四個選項中唯一真正能在 API 層級移除整個組織停用 CloudTrail 能力的方案。選項 A(日誌檔案完整性驗證)只能在事後偵測已送達的日誌檔案是否遭竄改或刪除,無法阻止任何人一開始就呼叫 StopLogging 或 DeleteTrail。選項 B(以限制性金鑰原則設定 SSE-KMS)只保護已送達日誌內容的機密性/可解密性,與啟動/停止日誌記錄或刪除 trail 的 CloudTrail 控制平面動作無關。選項 D(拒絕 DescribeTrails/GetTrailStatus 的 IAM 原則)針對的是唯讀狀態查詢動作,而非真正的停用動作(StopLogging、DeleteTrail、UpdateTrail),且僅適用於你記得附加原則的特定 IAM 身分(遺漏角色、其他帳戶及 root 使用者),任何擁有足夠 IAM 權限的人都能編輯或移除該原則——這與只能由管理帳戶管理的 SCP 截然不同。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"CloudTrail log file integrity validation only lets you detect after the fact whether delivered log files in S3 have been tampered with or deleted; it does not prevent anyone from calling StopLogging or DeleteTrail to disable the trail in the first place.","why_zh":"CloudTrail 日誌檔案完整性驗證只能在事後偵測已送達 S3 的日誌檔案是否遭竄改或刪除,並無法阻止任何人一開始就呼叫 StopLogging 或 DeleteTrail 來停用 trail。"},{"letter":"B","why_en":"Enabling SSE-KMS and restricting decryption of already-delivered log content protects the confidentiality of the log files, but has no effect whatsoever on the CloudTrail control-plane actions (StopLogging, DeleteTrail, UpdateTrail) that actually disable the trail.","why_zh":"啟用 SSE-KMS 並限制已送達日誌內容的解密,只能保護日誌檔案的機密性,對於真正停用 trail 的 CloudTrail 控制平面動作(StopLogging、DeleteTrail、UpdateTrail)完全沒有作用。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"IAM policies denying DescribeTrails/GetTrailStatus target read-only status-check actions, not the actual disable actions, apply only to the specific IAM users you remember to attach them to (missing roles, other accounts, and the root user), and can be edited or detached by anyone with sufficient IAM permissions — unlike an org-wide SCP controlled solely from the management account.","why_zh":"拒絕 DescribeTrails/GetTrailStatus 的 IAM 原則針對的是唯讀狀態查詢動作,而非真正的停用動作,且僅適用於你記得附加的特定 IAM 使用者(遺漏角色、其他帳戶及 root 使用者),任何擁有足夠 IAM 權限的人都能編輯或移除該原則,與只能由管理帳戶控制的組織層級 SCP 不同。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/organizations/latest/userguide/orgs_tutorials_basic.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/organizations/latest/userguide/orgs_manage_policies_scps.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/awscloudtrail/latest/userguide/cloudtrail-turning-off-logging.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/managedservices/latest/userguide/scp-library-compliance.html"]}}];
